orkers in Colorado and Minnesota may embolden other states and cities to use pension reductions as a tool to help balance their budgets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/01/business/01pension.html', 'snippet': 'The dismissal of suits by retired public workers in Colorado and Minnesota may embolden other states and cities to use pension reductions as a tool to help balance their budgets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Judges in Colorado and Minnesota have dismissed court challenges by retired public workers whose pensions had been cut — developments that may embolden other states and cities to use pension reductions as a tool to help balance their budgets. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Rulings Find Cuts in Public Pensions Permissible', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Two Rulings Find Cuts In Pensions Permissible', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Employees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-01T00:22:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mary Williams Walsh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mary', 'middlename': 'Williams', 'lastname': 'Walsh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/638eb712-14c0-5997-9c1f-e17b7a91f15c', 'word_count': 673, 'uri': 'nyt://article/638eb712-14c0-5997-9c1f-e17b7a91f15c'}, {'abstract': 'Who should sacrifice now that the pension bill is coming due for state and local workers?', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/the-impossible-public-pensions-choices/', 'snippet': 'Who should sacrifice now that the pension bill is coming due for state and local workers?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last summer, I wrote about a brewing court battle in Colorado. At issue was the question of whether the state could reduce the annual cost-of-living adjustments for the pensions of state workers who were already retired.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Impossible Public Pensions Choices', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Retirement', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colorado', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wisconsin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-01T00:23:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Lieber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lieber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3d76333-b4d4-55ac-9b8a-2cd84533bb25', 'word_count': 262, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3d76333-b4d4-55ac-9b8a-2cd84533bb25'}, {'abstract': 'The Socialist legislator Pierre Moscovici, a close ally of Dominique Strauss-Kahn, said Thursday that he would support François Hollande for president.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/01/world/europe/01webbrfs-Moscovici.html', 'snippet': 'The Socialist legislator Pierre Moscovici, a close ally of Dominique Strauss-Kahn, said Thursday that he would support François Hollande for president.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The Socialist legislator Pierre Moscovici, a close ally of Dominique Strauss-Kahn, said Thursday that he would support François Hollande for president. Mr. Moscovici, 53, had been hesitating about whether to support the Socialist Party leader Martine Aubry or Mr. Hollande, a former party leader, or to run himself. Mr. Hollande is the current front-runner in opinion polls for the Socialist primaries scheduled for October. Another ally of Mr. Strauss-Kahn, Jean-Christophe Cambadélis, has decided to support Ms. Aubry. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France: Moscovici Backs Hollande for Socialists', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | EUROPE', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France: Legislator Backs Hollande for Socialists', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strauss-Kahn, Dominique', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Aubry, Martine', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-01T00:28:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Romain Parlier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Romain', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parlier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/60209f93-c095-5b31-b0eb-13ad6d59bb60', 'word_count': 78, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60209f93-c095-5b31-b0eb-13ad6d59bb60'}, {'abstract': 'The state said it issued the license to Planned Parenthood of Kansas and Mid-Missouri after previously denying it under new state regulations that two other clinics are challenging in federal court.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/01/us/01kansas.html', 'snippet': 'The state said it issued the license to Planned Parenthood of Kansas and Mid-Missouri after previously denying it under new state regulations that two other clinics are challenging in federal court.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KANSAS CITY, Mo. — Ending speculation that new regulations could make it the only state without an abortion provider, Kansas announced Thursday that it had issued a license that would allow one of three abortion clinics to continue operating. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kansas Gives License to One Abortion Clinic', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Kansas Gives License to One Abortion Clinic', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Planned Parenthood Federation of America', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kansas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-01T00:31:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By A. G. Sulzberger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'Sulzberger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b4fb240-48bd-5871-af30-8737ce4c2ca8', 'word_count': 450, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b4fb240-48bd-5871-af30-8737ce4c2ca8'}, {'abstract': 'When America won independence, the British left behind a covert occupation force in the shape of its streetwise, opportunistic weeds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/01/opinion/01mabey.html', 'snippet': 'When America won independence, the British left behind a covert occupation force in the shape of its streetwise, opportunistic we