s', '_id': 'nyt://article/a63ea0de-6b51-5983-a19b-a557850d04a2', 'word_count': 1341, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a63ea0de-6b51-5983-a19b-a557850d04a2'}, {'abstract': 'The legislature and state employee unions face a tough choice between a wage freeze and benefit cuts, or losing 7,500 jobs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/01/nyregion/with-mass-layoffs-looming-connecticut-unions-scramble-to-resurrect-a-deal.html', 'snippet': 'The legislature and state employee unions face a tough choice between a wage freeze and benefit cuts, or losing 7,500 jobs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HARTFORD — Connecticut legislators early Friday morning gave Gov. Dannel P. Malloy dramatically expanded authority to make radical cuts to programs and employment after state employee unions rejected a labor deal meant to balance the state’s $40.1 billion two-year budget.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/01/nyregion/CONNECTICUT1/CONNECTICUT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/01/nyregion/CONNECTICUT1/CONNECTICUT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/01/nyregion/CONNECTICUT1/CONNECTICUT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Connecticut Steps Closer to Widespread Layoffs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Connecticut Steps Closer to Mass Layoffs as the Unions&#8217; Next Move Is Awaited', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'