assroom time than other schools, actually have a lower percentage of students exceeding state standards.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/01/us/01cncisat.html', 'snippet': 'ISAT scores show that charter schools, which tend to offer more classroom time than other schools, actually have a lower percentage of students exceeding state standards.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mayor Rahm Emanuel and new leaders of Chicago Public Schools have been pushing for a longer school day and school year to help raise student performance. But last week’s state test results show that charter schools — which typically have more instructional time — actually have a lower percentage of students exceeding state standards. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17B', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/01/us/01CNCISAT/01CNCISAT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Test Results Raise Questions About Extending Days', 'kicker': 'Chicago News Cooperative', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Test Results Raise Questions About Extending Days', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago News Cooperative', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Standards and Standardization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests and Examinations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-01T05:19:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rebecca Vevea', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rebecca', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vevea', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', '