jor': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inventions and Patents', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nortel Networks Corp', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Research In Motion Ltd', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-01T08:58:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris V. Nicholson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': 'V.', 'lastname': 'Nicholson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7bacc7a-2a15-5ae4-94b1-372172522dfd', 'word_count': 616, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7bacc7a-2a15-5ae4-94b1-372172522dfd'}, {'abstract': 'What do you do when a starving woman asks for food you just don’t have to give?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/03/magazine/in-kenya-needy-refugees-outpace-food-supplies.html', 'snippet': 'What do you do when a starving woman asks for food you just don’t have to give?', 'lead_paragraph': 'One day each month in Eastleigh, a run-down suburb of Nairobi with dirt roads and rivering sewers, a young Kenyan woman named Dorothy Gakii starts calling out numbers. “Numbaa one!” she shouts, using slow and deliberate English. “Numbaa two!” Gathered before her on long wooden benches in a church meeting hall are several dozen refugees holding scraps of paper that mark their place in line. They are waiting for food — for the sacks of dried beans and rice and maize flour piled against one wall. For the seriously malnourished, there is a nutritional porridge mix labeled, “Pure Wimbi.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/magazine/03here_map/03here_map-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 837, 'width': 929, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/magazine/03here_map/03here_map-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/03/magazine/03here_map/03here_map-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'One Mouth Too Many', 'kicker': 'You Are Here', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'One Mouth Too Many', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nairobi (Kenya)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-01T09:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sara Corbett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Corbett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/850af4ac-f148-5f0f-9322-755b4ec50b25', 'word_count': 819, 'uri': 'nyt://article/850af4ac-f148-5f0f-9322-755b4ec50b25'}, {'abstract': 'Our Summer Reading Contest begins this week. Please come and post your answers to our question here, and we’ll choose a favorite answer at the end of each week.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/01/what-interested-you-most-in-the-times-this-week-2/', 'snippet': 'Our Summer Reading Contest begins this week. Please come and post your answers to our question here, and we’ll choose a favorite answer at the end of each week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Our Summer Reading Contest begins!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Interested You Most in The Times This Week?', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-01T09:07:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2784db0f-9498-5256-bef7-8ee28e8ac5a6', 'word_count': 329, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2784db0f-9498-5256-bef7-8ee28e8ac5a6'}, {'abstract': 'Gaby Dunn, New York-based journalist and proprietor of the Web project 100 Interviews, talks to Zak Bagans, host of Travel Channel’s “Ghost Adventures.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/03/magazine/bonus-feature-the-enthusiast.html', 'snippet': 'Gaby Dunn, New York-based journalist and proprietor of the Web project 100 Interviews, talks to Zak Bagans, host of Travel Channel’s “Ghost Adventures.”', 'lead_paragraph': ' The Enthusiast: Gaby Dunn, New York-based journalist and proprietor of the Web project 100 Interviews (100interviews.com).', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '45', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Enthusiast', 'kicker': 'Bonus Feature', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Enthusiast', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reality Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Travel Channel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-01T09:13:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d1c8d76-2180-589b-a714-a0a4223f3d33', 'word_count': 205, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d1c8d76-2180-589b-a714-a0a4223f3d33'}, {'abstract': 'We have had enough of strong female characters. What we need are more weak female characters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/03/magazine/a-plague-of-strong-female-characters.html', 'snippet': 'We have had enough of strong female characters. What we need are more weak female characters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every time I hear someone use the term “strong female character,” I want to punch them. The problem is, I hit like a girl. Before I go further, here’s an anecdote that might help set the tone for what I’m about to try to say, which I worry has the potential to come across all wrong unless I manage to dispel certain widely shared assumptions without unduly setting anyone off. ', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '44', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/magazine/03riff_span/03riff_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 103, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/03/magazine/03riff_span/03riff_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 103}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/magazine/03riff_span/mag-03Riff-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 209, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/magazine/03riff_span/03riff_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/03/magazine/03ri