dy-striped bracelet that he bought online. When the piece arrived, de Givenchy, a jeweler, was so taken with the quality of the plastic that he took it into in his workshop for further study, leaving it next to a pile of faceted lapis. The commingling was purely serendipitous. “I thought it would be so much fun,” de Givenchy said of the costume bauble-turned-fine jewelry. A very American transformation, don’t you think? $10,000. Go to taffin.com or call (212) 421-6222 for an appointment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Accidental Patriot', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-01T14:19:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie La Cava', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'La Cava', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e958e13-c64c-50ce-9b59-51b7cf087616', 'word_count': 93, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e958e13-c64c-50ce-9b59-51b7cf087616'}, {'abstract': 'Uno Roboto is an interactive, computerized version of the popular card game from Mattel that records and recites the names of the players and their house rule.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/01/a-high-tech-twist-on-a-classic-card-game/', 'snippet': 'Uno Roboto is an interactive, computerized version of the popular card game from Mattel that records and recites the names of the players and their house rule.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Remember the card game Uno? Now, Uno remembers you.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A High-Tech Twist on a Classic Card Game', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywo