one, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4616bac6-8b46-53d6-8f07-a8b64e82281a', 'word_count': 727, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4616bac6-8b46-53d6-8f07-a8b64e82281a'}, {'abstract': 'The bailout, worth $14.1 billion, raised the specter of balance sheet problems at other Russian banks, which had a tendency during the recession to roll over loans to struggling companies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/02/business/global/02ruble.html', 'snippet': 'The bailout, worth $14.1 billion, raised the specter of balance sheet problems at other Russian banks, which had a tendency during the recession to roll over loans to struggling companies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — Russian regulators said on Friday that they had averted the collapse of one of the largest Russian banks by providing a bailout package of 395 billion rubles to Bank of Moscow, suggesting the bank’s problems with bad loans were more severe than previously acknowledged.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Regulators Provide $14 Billion Bailout for Bank of Moscow', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Regulators Provide $14 Billion Bailout for Bank of Moscow', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-01T14:32:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew E. Kramer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Kramer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/edb449e9-