348710cf54ff', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/8087e98d-ca04-53da-a8bd-348710cf54ff'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo bowed to party bosses’ wishes by allowing them to pick the candidates to represent the Congressional district that includes parts of Queens and Brooklyn.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/01/sept-13-date-set-for-election-to-fill-weiners-seat/', 'snippet': 'Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo bowed to party bosses’ wishes by allowing them to pick the candidates to represent the Congressional district that includes parts of Queens and Brooklyn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fulfilling the wishes of local political leaders, Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo announced on Friday that a special election to fill the seat of former Representative Anthony D. Weiner would be held on Sept. 13.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Election to Replace Weiner Is Set for Sept. 13', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-01T16:51:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/abd88433-0b5b-5c35-b9c7-37d7645d2675', 'word_count': 596, 'uri': 'nyt://article/abd88433-0b5b-5c35-b9c7-37d7645d2675'}, {'abstract': 'Beginning on July 1, the Plaza Hotel will one again offer children’s bike rentals for hotel guests and a few lucky New Yorkers.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/01/the-plaza-hotel-reopens-its-tricycle-garage/', 'snippet': 'Beginning on July 1, the Plaza Hotel will one again offer children’s bike rentals for hotel guests and a few lucky New Yorkers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Plaza Hotel in New York City will revive its Tricycle Garage, which will be good news for “Eloise” fans — especially those lucky enough to stay at the renovated landmark hotel. Beginning on July 1, the Plaza will offer children’s bike rentals – including Radio Flyer tricycles, bicycles and scooters – for hotel guests and a few lucky New Yorkers. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Plaza Hotel Reopens Its Tricycle Garage', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Plaza Hotel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-01T16:51:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Danielle Belopotosky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Danielle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belopotosky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/afcba89d-b1db-58a3-b95f-19f4bc58f2cb', 'word_count': 138, 'uri': 'nyt://article/afcba89d-b1db-58a3-b95f-19f4bc58f2cb'}, {'abstract': 'A salad from the Minimalist column archives that combines sweet and savory, tender and crunchy.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/01/the-minimalist-watermelon-and-tomato-salad/', 'snippet': 'A salad from the Minimalist column archives that combines sweet and savory, tender and crunchy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I developed this recipe about five years into my stint as the Minimalist. By that point I had already exhausted (or thought I had; I was wrong) most of the obvious candidates for the column– five-ingredient pasta dishes, simple marinated meats, 10-minute green salads — and was forced to research and invent recipes that were less conventional but no more complicated. This salad is one of my favorite