ry allowed the United States to begin a siege of Santiago de Cuba, which led to Spanish surrender and the end of the Spanish-American War.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'July 1, 1898 | The Battle of San Juan Hill', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-01T17:15:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/373e201e-eddf-532c-9280-f47ea44873b3', 'word_count': 412, 'uri': 'nyt://article/373e201e-eddf-532c-9280-f47ea44873b3'}, {'abstract': '“Legion Lost,” a tale of the Legion of Super-Heroes, a group of champions from 1,000 years in the future, lands at No. 2 on the hardcover list this week.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/01/graphic-books-best-sellers-lost-in-space/', 'snippet': '“Legion Lost,” a tale of the Legion of Super-Heroes, a group of champions from 1,000 years in the future, lands at No. 2 on the hardcover list this week.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Legion Lost,” a tale of the Legion of Super-Heroes, a group of champions from 1,000 years in the future, lands at No. 2 on the hardcover list this week. The group, published by DC Comics, has had a bit of a confounding history. The Legion was created in 1958. They were time travelers from the future who had traveled to the past to meet their heroic inspiration: Superboy. Cut to 1985 when DC published Crisis on Infinite Earths, a limited series intended to streamline the decades of convoluted continuity of its heroes. It was decided that Superman never had costumed adventures as a youth, so the reason for the Legion’s founding had to be reconsidered. A lot of stories were crafted to give them a new reason for forming – until it was decided, 20 years later when DC published Infinite Crisis – that Superman did have a career as Superboy so the Legion could be inspired by him.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Graphic Books Best Sellers: Lost in Space', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comic Books and Strips', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'DC Comics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-01T17:15:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Gene Gustines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': 'Gene', 'lastname': 'Gustines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0af412dc-20fe-5c6d-9131-4d218c73bd59', 'word_count': 453, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0af412dc-20fe-5c6d-9131-4d218c73bd59'}, {'abstract': 'With the propeller shafts of two ships damaged, authorities holding others in port and an American boat turned back by the Greek Coast Guard, the international flotilla to Gaza has stalled.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/02/world/middleeast/02flotilla.html', 'snippet': 'With the propeller shafts of two ships damaged, authorities holding others in port and an American boat turned back by the Greek Coast Guard, the international flotilla to Gaza has stalled.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATHENS — With the propeller shafts of two ships mysteriously damaged, the Greek authorities holding other vessels in port on government orders and an American boat turned back by the Greek coast guard on Friday just 20 minutes off the coast, the international flotilla to Gaza has stalled.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 