ne}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0eac74ab-21b1-53c5-a212-c5d7113ea279', 'word_count': 1398, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0eac74ab-21b1-53c5-a212-c5d7113ea279'}, {'abstract': 'Colombia’s women’s national soccer team is playing in its first World Cup, but back home, the notion of women playing the sport still struggles for acceptance.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/01/in-colombia-a-soccer-paradox/', 'snippet': 'Colombia’s women’s national soccer team is playing in its first World Cup, but back home, the notion of women playing the sport still struggles for acceptance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'POPAYÁN, Colombia—The presence of Las Cafeteras, the national team from Colombia, in its first Women’s World Cup likely will pass with little comment here. (Colombia faces the United States in a first-round Group C match in Sinsheim, Germany on Saturday.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Colombia, a Soccer Paradox', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colombia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-01T18:35:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Turnbull', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Turnbull', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/efc7eeab-54f6-564a-ad96-633b415011d1', 'word_count': 1041, 'uri': 'nyt://article/efc7eeab-54f6-564a-ad96-633b415011d1'}, {'abstract': 'Others may control the copyrights, the royalties and the theme park receipts, but they can’t keep Harry Potter’s wizardry out of millions of hearts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/03/movies/the-fans-are-all-right-for-harry-potter.html', 'snippet': 'Others may control the copyrights, the royalties and the theme park receipts, but they can’t keep Harry Potter’s wizardry out of millions of hearts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HARRY POTTER’S final battle with Lord Voldemort will hit movie screens on July 15, but that young wizard has already scored a decisive victory where it counts: at the box office, on best-seller lists and in the crowded arena of fantasy-driven popular culture. J. K. Rowling, a single mother when she hatched a series of magical boarding-school novels, has ascended to an Oprah-like level of wealth and influence, while Harry, with more than $6 billion in tickets sold globally, has surpassed James Bond as the top-grossing movie-franchise hero.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/arts/CRITICS-Jp-1/CRITICS-Jp-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/arts/CRITICS-Jp-1/CRITICS-Jp-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/03/arts/CRITICS-Jp-1/CRITICS-Jp-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Fans Own the Magic', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Fans Own the Magic', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rowling, J K', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-01T18:36:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis and A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/703e9083-a8e7-5e73-8ccb-5112ab8f8d43', 'word_count': 2064, 'uri': 'nyt://article/703e9083-a8e7-5e73-8ccb-5112ab8f8d43'}, {'abstract': 'Kate Moss looks pretty great in the simple but elegant beaded gown she wore to wed Jamie Hince of the Kills in the Cotswolds in England.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/01/kate-moss-gets-married/', 'snippet': 'Kate Moss looks pretty great in the simple but elegant beaded gown she wore to wed Jamie Hince of the Kills in the Cotswolds in England.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kate Moss looks pretty great in the simple but elegant beaded gown she wore Friday afternoon to wed Jamie Hince of the Kills in the Cotswolds in England. The silk dress was apparently designed by her longtime friend John Galliano. I love her young bridesmaids’ plain shifts, with their bare legs and slippers. Nothing fussy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kate Moss Gets Married', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-01T18:39:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/adf8b1f4-7857-53ae-83e6-c69bccc07cf6', 'word_count': 99, 'uri': 'nyt://article/adf8b1f4-7857-53ae-83e6-c69bccc07cf6'}, {'abstract': 'Decision by federal appeals court is the latest round of the decade-long fight over the University of Michigan’s affirmative action policies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/02/education/02michigan.html', 'snippet': 'Decision by federal appeals court is the latest round of the decade-long fight over the University of Michigan’s affirmative action policies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A federal appeals court on Friday struck down Michigan’s 2006 ban on the consideration of race and gender in public-university admissions and government hiring in the latest round of the decade-long fight over the University of Michigan’s affirmative action policies. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/02/us/JP-MICHIGAN/JP-MICHIGAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/02/us/JP-MICHIGAN/JP-MICHIGAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/02/us/JP-MICHIGAN/JP-MICHIGAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 611, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/02/us/JP-MICHIGAN/JP-MICHIGAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/02/us/JP-MICHIGAN/JP-MICHIGAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Court Overturns Michigan Affirmative-Action Ban', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Michigan Rule On Admission To University Is Overturned', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AFFIRMATIVE ACTION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Michigan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADMISSIONS STANDARDS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-01T18:39:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tamar Lewin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tamar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lewin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18805da3-aef1-551f-9a4b-915192cf2291', 'word_count': 722, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18805da3-aef1-551f-9a4b-915192cf2291'}, {'abstract': 'Craig Taborn is one in a long line of jazz piano soloists, taking part in a revered tradition in jazz because solo piano was a mode of performance in ragtime before jazz existed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/03/arts/music/the-tradition-of-the-jazz-piano-solo.html', 'snippet': 'Craig Taborn is one in a long line of jazz piano soloists, taking part in a revered tradition in jazz because solo piano was a mode of performance in ragtime before jazz existed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CRAIG TABORN was deep into a solo expedition one recent evening at the Rubin Museum of Art in Manhattan, seeming for all the world like someone cracking a secret code. Poised for action at a grand piano, he disrupted an expectant stillness with a turbulent digression. With his left hand he formed the lopsided bass-clef vamp of a piece called “Avenging Angel”; with his right he improvised complex annotations, firing them off in boldface or sleek cursive. It was taut, transfixing music, sharpened by the austerity of the setting: just Mr. Taborn at the piano, on his own. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/arts/SOLOPIANO-1/SOLOPIANO-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/03/arts/SOLOPIANO-1/SOLOPIANO-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/arts/SOLOPIANO-1/SOLOPIANO-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 862, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/arts/SOLOPIANO-1/SOLOPIANO-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/03/arts/SOLOPIANO-1/SOLOPIANO-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lonely Voyage of Player, Piano and Audience', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lonely Voyage of Player,Piano and Audience', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rubin Museum of Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rubalcaba, Gonzalo', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jarrett, Keith', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taborn, Craig', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-01T18:41:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa21825b-325b-5b9d-8d3e-e61dc5d0c852', 'word_count': 1738, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa21825b-325b-5b9d-8d3e-e61dc5d0c852'}, {'abstract': 'Zynga, a game maker, is expected to raise about $1 billion in its initial public offering.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/01/dealbook-zynga-files-for-1-billion-i-p-o/', 'snippet': 'Zynga, a game maker, is expected to raise about $1 billion in its initial public offering.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With real-world profit and an inexhaustible supply of virtual cows, Zynga is gunning for a blockbuster debut on the public markets.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dealbook: Zynga Files for $1 Billion I.P.O.', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Zynga Game Network', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-01T18:43:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f21be3fd-dd1e-5f2f-9d20-69974cc7751e', 'word_count': 146, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f21be3fd-dd1e-5f2f-9d20-69974cc7751e'}, {'abstract': 'Inspired by swirling soap brushes at a car wash, the owner of a Houston dance studio took tin can, fishing line and a rotary lawn edger in hand, and the Weed Eater was born.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/02/business/02ballas.html', 'snippet': 'Inspired by swirling soap brushes at a car wash, the owner of a Houston dance studio took tin can, fishing line and a rotary lawn edger in hand, and the Weed Eater was born.', 'lead_paragraph': 'George C. Ballas loved tending to his lawn with meticulous care, but the 200 or more trees crowding a two-acre expanse behind his house in Houston posed a problem: how to get around the bulging roots and manicure close enough to achieve the near perfection he desired. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/02/business/02ballas-web/02ballas-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 475, 'width': 324, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/02/business/02ballas-web/02ballas-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/02/business/02ballas-web/02ballas-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'George Ballas, Inventor of the Weed Whacker, Dies at 85', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'George Ballas, 85, Inventor In 1971 of the Weed Whacker', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ballas, George C', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weeds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Botanic Garden', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lawns', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gardens and Gardening', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Emerson Electric Company', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-01T18:47:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Den