'web_url': 'https://scientistatwork.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/01/whats-in-a-name/', 'snippet': 'Naming conventions help scientists and even inexperienced observers keep track of hyenas and the relationships among them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kay E. Holekamp, a zoologist at Michigan State University, writes from the Masai Mara National Reserve in Kenya, where she is studying the behavior of spotted hyenas.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s in a Name?', 'kicker': 'Scientist at Work', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hyenas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Names, Personal', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kenya', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-01T19:40:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kay E. Holekamp', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kay', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Holekamp', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7b159db-c5a2-5b12-b0a3-339fbfedf643', 'word_count': 903, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7b159db-c5a2-5b12-b0a3-339fbfedf643'}, {'abstract': 'A former Lehman executive who went to a company winding down the bankrupt firm resigns from a corporate board because of a “material change” in his position.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/07/01/a-departure-at-long-last-from-lehman/', 'snippet': 'A former Lehman executive who went to a company winding down the bankrupt firm resigns from a corporate board because of a “material change” in his position.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Eric Salzman, a managing director and group head of Lamco, the company handling the wind-down of Lehman Brothers, seems to have finally cut his ties to the bankrupt firm. Mr. Salzman was previously a Lehman executive before the firm’s collapse in September 2008.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Departure, at Long Last, From Lehman', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Salzman, Eric', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lehman Brothers Holdings Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ShoreTel Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-01T19:46:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michelle Leder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michelle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/48f9c656-f409-5140-be22-820788293a24', 'word_count': 243, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48f9c656-f409-5140-be22-820788293a24'}, {'abstract': 'The Case-Shiller home price index managed a small gain in April, but most markets are still not as high as they were in 2004.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/02/business/02charts.html', 'snippet': 'The Case-Shiller home price index managed a small gain in April, but most markets are still not as high as they were in 2004.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IS your home worth as much as it was seven years ago? If so, you’ve done better than most Americans.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Home Prices, It’s Back to at Least 2004', 'kicker': 'Off the Charts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Home Prices, It’s Back to at Least 2004', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Standard & Poor's Case-Shiller Home Price Index", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-01T19:49:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Floyd Norris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Norris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af459d41-fb12-5750-91fc-8b2a2d7a4c91', 'word_count': 523, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af459d41-fb12-5750-91fc-8b2a2d7a4c91'}, {'abstract': 'The new Blu-ray releases of two films directed by Robert Aldrich are very different: “Vera Cruz,” and “Kiss Me Deadly.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/03/movies/homevideo/robert-aldrichs-vera-cruz-and-kiss-me-deadly-on-dvd.html', 'snippet': 'The new Blu-ray releases of two films directed by Robert Aldrich are very different: “Vera Cruz,” and “Kiss Me Deadly.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROBERT ALDRICH was still in his early 30s when he made, back to back, two of the most influential films of the 1950s, “Vera Cruz” (1954) and “Kiss Me Deadly” (1955). More remarkable still is that these films had their influence on two very different groups of filmmakers, at two very different periods.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/arts/KEHR/KEHR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 325, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/03/arts/KEHR/KEHR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 325}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/arts/