, discusses her long and still-evolving career.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Annie Sprinkle, who reviews Chester Brown’s “Paying for It: A Comic-Strip Memoir About Being a John” in this weekend’s Book Review, is no stranger to the documentary urge. “From the day I gave away my virginity at 17, I started documenting my sexual experiences,” Sprinkle told us recently. “I still am, 40 years later.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reviewer Spotlight: Annie Sprinkle on Sex, Art and Activism', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-01T19:55:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer B. McDonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c597748e-39ea-5ac7-b2df-04840d1b7802', 'word_count': 929, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c597748e-39ea-5ac7-b2df-04840d1b7802'}, {'abstract': 'The all-wheel-drive convertible continues Nissan’s recent flurry of risk-taking designs, but is that necessarily a good thing?', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/01/reviewing-the-nissan-murano-crosscabriolet/', 'snippet': 'The all-wheel-drive convertible continues Nissan’s recent flurry of risk-taking designs, but is that necessarily a good thing?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Sunday’s Automobiles section, Lawrence Ulrich reviews the 2011 Nissan Murano CrossCabriolet, a two-door, all-wheel-drive convertible based on the four-door Murano crossover.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reviewing the Nissan Murano CrossCabriolet