ure Spotted Owls', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forests and Forestry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Land Use Policies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Logging Industry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Owls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wood and Wood Products', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-01T21:16:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Yardley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yardley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/963a50c1-d392-500e-8acf-8d3a8e6489bf', 'word_count': 605, 'uri': 'nyt://article/963a50c1-d392-500e-8acf-8d3a8e6489bf'}, {'abstract': 'A videotape of the mass detonation by the Police Department of the 5,000 pounds of illegal fireworks it has seized over the year.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/01/gone-with-a-bang-bang-bang/', 'snippet': 'A videotape of the mass detonation by the Police Department of the 5,000 pounds of illegal fireworks it has seized over the year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'So far this year, the New York Police Department reports that it has confiscated more than 5,000 pounds of illegal fireworks, ranging from sparklers to professional pyrotechnics. But the scofflaws’ loss is your gain, kind of: the police released this video of the mass detonation of the entire stash, which was accomplished Friday morning at 11:05 a.m. at the firing range at Rodman’s Neck in the Bronx.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia':