op-weddings.html', 'snippet': 'An associate producer at “Soundcheck,” a talk show on the public radio station WNYC-FM, marries an associate online editor and producer for MarthaStewart.com.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Katherine Esther Macpherson and Eric Nathan Bishop are to be married Sunday evening by the Rev. Dr. Val Fowler at the First Presbyterian Church of Honeoye Falls in Honeoye Falls, N.Y. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/fashion/weddings/03MCPHERSON/03MCPHERSON-Specs-225-x-142-Caption-Katie-Macpherson-and-Eric-Bishop--NYTCREDIT--jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/fashion/weddings/03MCPHERSON/03MCPHERSON-Specs-225-x-142-Caption-Katie-Macpherson-and-Eric-Bishop--NYTCREDIT--thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/03/fashion/weddings/03MCPHERSON/03MCPHERSON-Specs-225-x-142-Caption-Katie-Macpherson-and-Eric-Bishop--NYTCREDIT--thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Katherine Macpherson, Eric Bishop', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Katherine Macpherson, Eric Bishop', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-01T23:09:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Society', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': 'Weddings', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/725f433d-e319-508f-9462-1c5ac052fa59', 'word_count': 179, 'uri': 'nyt://article/725f433d-e319-508f-9462-1c5ac052fa59'}, {'abstract': 'More on “Unnatural Selection” and abortion.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/01/a-response-to-mara-hvistendahl-ii/', 'snippet': 'More on “Unnatural Selection” and abortion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In her reply to my column, the author of “Unnatural Selection” also disputes my suggestion that her book’s tone of moral outrage depends on an (implicit) sympathy for aborted female fetuses as well as a concern for the societal impact of sex-selective abortion. “I make very clear in my book that the victim is women,” Hvistendahl writes — “women who in the 1960s and 1970s were used as pawns in a Western drive to reduce birth rates in Asia, women who later aborted female fetuses against the backdrop of patriarchy, and women who, now that they are scarce, find themselves at greater risk of being trafficked, kidnapped, or sold by their parents to men desperate to find wives. Sex-selective abortion is wrong because women should account for half of the human population, and in parts of the world they now account for far less. That alone justifies moral outrage.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Response to Mara Hvistendahl (II)', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-01T23:21:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/556ba8af-571b-5cf2-8ad1-26d598b1151e', 'word_count': 738, 'uri': 'nyt://article/556ba8af-571b-5cf2-8ad1-26d598b1151e'}, {'abstract': 'In this homemade video, Emily Schle