his life, when he suffered from depression and paranoia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/02/opinion/02hotchner.html', 'snippet': 'A friend of Ernest Hemingway recalls the last year of his life, when he suffered from depression and paranoia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EARLY one morning, 50 years ago today, while his wife, Mary, slept upstairs, Ernest Hemingway went into the vestibule of his Ketchum, Idaho, house, selected his favorite shotgun from the rack, inserted shells into its chambers and ended his life. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/01/opinion/0oped/0oped-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 819, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/01/opinion/0oped/0oped-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/01/opinion/0oped/0oped-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hemingway, Hounded by the Feds', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hemingway, Hounded By the Feds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hemingway, Ernest', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suicides and Suicide Attempts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-02T01:07:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By A. E. Hotchner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Hotchner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/d45cfcf8-1d9b-57b7-a42f-6e3ba68846bc', 'word_count': 1307, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d45cfcf8-1d9b-57b7-a42f-6e3ba68846bc'}, {'abstract': 'The Fourth of July fireworks show is a New York tradition, but where to locate it has been the subject of much wrangling over the years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/02/nyregion/spurned-by-lady-liberty-macys-fireworks-show-stays-put.html', 'snippet': 'The Fourth of July fireworks show is a New York tradition, but where to locate it has been the subject of much wrangling over the years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For this year’s Fourth of July celebration, Macy’s had hoped to turn its massive fireworks show into a birthday party for the Statue of Liberty, which was dedicated in New York harbor 125 years ago. The show’s planners wanted to surround the statue with barges loaded with shells, fire some others off from the base of the statue and even have Beyoncé perform on a stage there.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/02/nyregion/Y-FIREWORKS/Y-FIREWORKS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/02/nyregion/Y-FIREWORKS/Y-FIREWORKS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/02/nyregion/Y-FIREWORKS/Y-FIREWORKS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2