ol in New York in the 1960s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEING closely associated with Andy Warhol and his Factory during the 1960s has been perhaps both a blessing and a curse for Ultra Violet, the artist and writer who starred in many of his films. Without Warhol, she would quite likely be unknown today, but her history also gets in her way.', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/nyregion/03SPOTLI/03SPOTLI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 697, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A ‘Factory’ Worker Glances Back', 'kicker': 'Spotlight | Bridgehampton', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A ‘Factory’ Worker Glances Back', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Warhol, Andy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bridgehampton (NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-02T01:39:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven McElroy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McElroy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7805c956-7f34-5f7c-9953-cd407a38ad95', 'word_count': 440, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7805c956-7f34-5f7c-9953-cd407a38ad95'}, {'abstract': '“Legally Blonde: The Musical,” playing at the Gateway Playhouse, seems to say it’s good for a gal to be smart, but really wonderful if she’s also blond and beautiful.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/03/nyregion/legally-blonde-the-musical-in-bellport-review.html', 'snippet': '“Legally Blonde: The Musical,” playing at the Gateway Playhouse, seems to say it’s good for a gal to be smart, but really wonderful if she’s also blond and beautiful.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Legally Blonde: The Musical,” the lightweight confection now playing at the Gateway Playhouse in Bellport, overflows with fluffiness, which is just what is called for in the book by Heather Hach and the music and lyrics by Laurence O’Keefe and Nell Benjamin. ', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/nyregion/03ARTSLI_SPAN/03ARTSLI_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/03/nyregion/03ARTSLI_SPAN/03ARTSLI_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/nyregion/03ARTSLI_SPAN/03ARTSLI_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/nyregion/03ARTSLI_SPAN/03ARTSLI_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/03/nyregion/03ARTSLI_SPAN/03ARTSLI_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Succeed in a Pink Power Suit', 'kicker': 'Arts | Long Island', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How to Succeed in a Pink Power Suit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hach, Heather', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gateway Playhouse', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-02T01:39:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Aileen Jacobson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Aileen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jacobson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/397d47a0-6a9e-5728-a89e-de090e8d3539', 'word_count': 661, 'uri': 'nyt://article/397d47a0-6a9e-5728-a89e-de090e8d3539'}, {'abstract': 'A guide to cultural and recreational goings-on in and around Nassau and Suffolk Counties this week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/03/nyregion/events-on-long-island.html', 'snippet': 'A guide to cultural and recreational goings-on in and around Nassau and Suffolk Counties this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A guide to cultural and recreational goings-on in and around Nassau and Suffolk Counties. Items for the guide should be sent at least three weeks in advance to lical@nytimes.com, or by mail to Long Island Calendar, Metropolitan, 620 Eighth Avenue, New York, N.Y. 10018-1405.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Events on Long Island', 'kicker': 'Calendar', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Events on Long Island', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-02T01:40:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/acbc41ec-1945-56c8-9a06-29d68c4a9d3c', 'word_count': 3085, 'uri': 'nyt://article/acbc41ec-1945-56c8-9a06-29d68c4a9d3c'}, {'abstract': 'The chaos of life on the farm, with its overlapping settlements and empires, creates an almost perfect day.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/02/opinion/02sat4.html', 'snippet': 'The chaos of life on the farm, with its overlapping settlements and empires, creates an almost perfect day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week, there was a day I hesitate to call perfect only because I would hate it if the perfect day had already come and gone in my life. But when that perfect day comes at last it will probably resemble the one last week. The western breeze had cleaned the sun and purified the light, which fell moteless on the farm.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'One Fine Day', 'kicker': 'Editorial | The Rural Life', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'One Fine Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Farmers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-02T01:43:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Verlyn Klinkenborg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Verlyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Klinkenborg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/4acd9a42-2c21-508e-8c69-cd4be2139839', 'word_count': 341, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4acd9a42-2c21-508e-8c69-cd4be2139839'}, {'abstract': 'Al Foster, once a drummer with the Miles Davis band of the early 1970s, will mix straight-ahead standards and original pieces with harmonic substance at the festival.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/03/nyregion/al-foster-to-perform-at-hartford-festival.html', 'snippet': 'Al Foster, once a drummer with the Miles Davis band of the early 1970s, will mix straight-ahead standards and original pieces with harmonic substance at the festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AL FOSTER, a mild-mannered man with a perpetual smile, burst on the scene as the improbably fierce drummer with the Miles Davis band of the early 1970s. The job made his name; it even earned him a $200-a-week retainer, a benefit rare in the world of freelance musicians. But the band, heavy on rock vamps and light on harmonic progressions, was not really his style — and he let Davis know it. ', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/nyregion/03MUSICCT_SPAN/03MUSICCT_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/03/nyregion/03MUSICCT_SPAN/03MUSICCT_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/nyregion/03MUSICCT_SPAN/03MUSICCT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/nyregion/03MUSICCT_SPAN/03MUSICCT_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/03/nyregion/03MUSICCT_SPAN/03MUSICCT_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Drummer Goes Beyond a Legacy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Drummer Goes Beyond a Legacy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Foster, Al', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 