e and a favorite of daily hordes of burger and hot-dog fans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At a different time of year, the whitewashed shack that is Harry’s Place might be mistaken for a farm stand or carnival booth. But not between St. Patrick’s Day and Halloween, when the wooden panels of its hatch windows are slung open and customers line up for the burgers and dogs that have made Harry’s a drive-in destination. ', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Burgers, Dogs and History', 'kicker': 'Quick Bite | Colchester', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Burgers, Dogs and History', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-02T02:05:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Brooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/45679e7e-8c28-5547-b481-16c9b2da2599', 'word_count': 303, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45679e7e-8c28-5547-b481-16c9b2da2599'}, {'abstract': 'Kokoro tries to live up to its name, which means “from the heart,” and its menu, with mostly Asian entrees, includes its own take on some Western dishes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/03/nyregion/kokoro-bistro-isnt-limited-by-geography-review.html', 'snippet': 'Kokoro tries to live up to its name, which means “from the heart,” and its menu, with mostly Asian entrees, includes its own take on some Western dishes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN a long, narrow space a few steps below street level on Greenwich Avenue — a space once occupied by the admirable but relatively short-lived Solaia — is a self-described modern Asian bistro. But that phrase barely begins to capture the amazing dishes at Kokoro, whose name means “from the heart,” said Simon Chik, a co-owner, “which is how I would describe the cooking of our chef, Anan Tiwadom.”', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/nyregion/03DINECT1/03DINECT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 714, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/nyregion/03DINECT1/03DINECT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/03/nyregion/03DINECT1/03DINECT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Geography’s of No Matter in This Asian Bistro', 'kicker': 'Connecticut Dining | Greenwich', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Geography’s of No Matter In This Asian Bistro', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-02T02:06:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Brooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1466a4a5-bf1d-5d1d-80ee-6a15526d140e', 'word_count': 830, 'uri': 'ny