 died Wednesday in Kingston, N.Y. He was 55.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/02/nyregion/obit-costello/obit-costello-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 341, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/02/nyregion/obit-costello/obit-costello-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 341}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/02/nyregion/obit-costello/obit-costello-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 746, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/02/nyregion/obit-costello/obit-costello-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/02/nyregion/obit-costello/obit-costello-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Billy Costello, Who Won Light Welterweight Crown, Dies at 55', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Billy Costello, 55, Who Won Light Welterweight Crown', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Costello, Billy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boxing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-02T02:07:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Goldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1fa3ff4-ea26-56c0-86ab-6126abe53c50', 'word_count': 585, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1fa3ff4-ea26-56c0-86ab-6126abe53c50'}, {'abstract': 'Dave Robertson’s versatility has stabilized an injury-ravaged bullpen and his eighth-inning dependability has supplied a sturdy bridge to Mariano Rivera.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/03/sports/baseball/yankees-robertson-hitting-his-stride-setting-up-rivera.html', 'snippet': 'Dave Robertson’s versatility has stabilized an injury-ravaged bullpen and his eighth-inning dependability has supplied a sturdy bridge to Mariano Rivera.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The way Dave Robertson remembers it, no more than 150 people lined Broad Street in Rome, Ga., the night before the 2007 South Atlantic League All-Star Game. Sitting in the back of one of the vintage convertibles that ferried athletes along the parade route, Robertson waved to his parents. Then he felt a thud. He lurched forward. His car had collided with the car in front.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/sports/03reliever2/03reliever2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/03/sports/03reliever2/03reliever2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/sports/03reliever2/03reliever2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/sports/03reliever2/03reliever2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/03/sports/03reliever2/03reliever2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Yankees’ Robertson Making an All-Star Case', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hitting His Stride Setting Up Rivera', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rivera, Mariano', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Robertson, Dave', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-02T02:11:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af727824-c4a9-54af-8690-b9daf0eb216d', 'word_count': 1372, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af727824-c4a9-54af-8690-b9daf0eb216d'}, {'abstract': 'At Tommy 2 Scoops, the owner gives his staff a lot of creative freedom to make flavors, like ricotta honey and parmesan olive oil.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/03/nyregion/ingenious-gelato-at-tommy-2-scoops-in-jersey-city.html', 'snippet': 'At Tommy 2 Scoops, the owner gives his staff a lot of creative freedom to make flavors, like ricotta honey and parmesan olive oil.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tom Parisi offers 18 flavors of gelato daily at his tidy, 800-square-foot shop, Tommy 2 Scoops, in Jersey City. But he does not take credit for the ingenuity of those flavors, which include ricotta honey and parmesan olive oil and are made on the premises ($3.50 a scoop). ', 'print_section': 'NJ', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ingenious Gelato', 'kicker': 'Quick Bite | Jersey City', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ingenious Gelato', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gelato', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-02T02:11:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tammy La Gorce', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tammy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'La Gorce', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4dab0d5-d0c5-5ecd-b51c-e6863e3c7743', 'word_count': 313, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4dab0d5-d0c5-5ecd-b51c-e6863e3c7743'}, {'abstract': 'Niko’s Trapezi Greek Tavern caters to both beachgoers and regulars.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/03/nyregion/nikos-trapezi-offers-greek-food-in-long-branch-review.html', 'snippet': 'Niko’s Trapezi Greek Tavern caters to both beachgoers and regulars.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAKE a sweater and a good appetite for home-style Greek food to Niko’s Trapezi Greek Taverna; given the air-conditioning and the gargantuan portions, you will need both. This place, a narrow storefront in an L-shaped strip mall near the beach, is the work of two owners, who opened it in April 2009: Niko Katsilianos, the chef, and his brother-in-law, Jay Keating. Mr. Keating and his wife, Georgia, work the front of the house and handle the office chores and the marketing.', 'print_section': 'NJ', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/nyregion/03DINENJ1/03DINENJ1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 71