een the strain of bacteria that killed a woman at a Bordeaux hospital and the E. coli outbreak in Germany.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — A 78-year-old French woman died Saturday in Bordeaux from complications related to E. coli, a spokeswoman for a regional health authority said. Officials said there were no apparent links to the devastating E. coli outbreak in Germany that has killed dozens of people and sickened thousands more, despite that strain being implicated in another case in Bordeaux.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Woman Stricken With E. Coli Dies in France', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Woman Stricken With E. Coli Dies in France', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Contamination and Poisoning', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E Coli (Bacteria)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-02T11:14:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Jolly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jolly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9488f88-da8f-5ea4-8c7a-92acfb511912', 'word_count': 443, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9488f88-da8f-5ea4-8c7a-92acfb511912'}, {'abstract': 'In which Sam and Kate use humor and a sense of adventure to avoid confronting their horrible taste in cars.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/02/classic-ad-pontiac-aztek/', 'snippet': 'In which Sam and Kate use humor and a sense of adventure to avoid confronting their horrible taste in cars.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this Sunday’s Automobiles section, Lawrence Ulrich we