rnament', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-02T12:18:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Clarey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clarey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d4551b5-5fb9-5c06-ac53-264ff6278463', 'word_count': 1987, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d4551b5-5fb9-5c06-ac53-264ff6278463'}, {'abstract': 'A roundup of the week’s Formula One news.', 'web_url': 'https://formulaone.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/02/week-roundup-of-racing-news/', 'snippet': 'A roundup of the week’s Formula One news.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As we prepare for Formula One’s home race next week at Silverstone — I think it can be called a “home race” because most of the teams are based in Britain — there has been a lot of news to digest. Here are some of the highlights.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Roundup of the Week’s Racing News', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-02T12:45:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brad Spurgeon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spurgeon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4119d9e5-96bc-5073-888f-47aa12fff176', 'word_count': 110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4119d9e5-96bc-5073-888f-47aa12fff176'}, {'abstract': 'A roundup of the week’s Formula One news.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/02/week-roundup-of-racing-news/', 'snippet': 'A roundup of the week’s Formula One news.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As we prepare for Formula One’s home race next week at Silverstone — I think it can be called a “home race” because most of the teams are based in Britain — there has been a lot of news to digest. Here are some of the highlights.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Roundup of the Week’s Racing News', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-02T12:45:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brad Spurgeon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spurgeon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eaa4d528-e85d-527b-8d0c-e931635e0b97', 'word_count': 110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eaa4d528-e85d-527b-8d0c-e931635e0b97'}, {'abstract': 'One New Yorker’s quest to discover the story behind a weathered leather change purse found at a Chelsea flea market.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/02/chasing-a-name-lost-to-time-2/', 'snippet': 'One New Yorker’s quest to discover the story behind a weathered leather change purse found at a Chelsea flea market.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Benjamin P. Feldman, a retired real estate investor with the time and the money to chase his enthusiasms, was rummaging through a bin at a flea market in Chelsea last winter when he came across a weathered leather change purse with words engraved in gilt: “Compliments of Sol Goldberg’s Cafe, 71 Canal Street, Tel. 2111 Orchard.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chasing a Name Lost to Time', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank':