med at appeasing the protesters in Hama, where demonstrations have grown.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/03/world/middleeast/03syria.html', 'snippet': 'The move seemed to be aimed at appeasing the protesters in Hama, where demonstrations have grown.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — President Bashar al-Assad of Syria fired the governor responsible for the city of Hama on Saturday, a day after tens of thousands of protesters filled its streets in the largest demonstration since the uprising began in March.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Syrian President Fires Governor in Charge of a Restive City', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Syrian President Fires Governor in Charge of a Restive City', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-02T14:57:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Shadid', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shadid', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f15bb77d-eddc-5f38-957b-f77685f3047c', 'word_count': 778, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f15bb77d-eddc-5f38-957b-f77685f3047c'}, {'abstract': 'Neither at corporations nor at banks.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/02/cash-is-not-the-problem/', 'snippet': 'Neither at corporations nor at banks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A couple of followups to my repatriation post.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cash Is Not the Problem', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-02T14:58:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/83e84d44-be22-59f4-a406-e151ed9d20bf', 'word_count': 372, 'uri': 'nyt://article/83e84d44-be22-59f4-a406-e151ed9d20bf'}, {'abstract': 'Here is how the rosters should shape up, including representatives from every team but giving no regard to fan preferences or pitching rotations. Deserving starters are listed first.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/02/the-jigsaw-puzzle-of-picking-all-stars/', 'snippet': 'Here is how the rosters should shape up, including representatives from every team but giving no regard to fan preferences or pitching rotations. Deserving starters are listed first.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Until a few years ago, the manager of the All-Star team chose all of the pitchers and reserves for his league. The responsibilities are different now, and as much as the managers might prepare, they make only 16 selections: seven by the American League manager, nine by the National League manager.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Jigsaw Puzzle of Picking All-Stars', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALL STAR GAMES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-02T15:12:52+0000', 'doc