1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b931b959-a520-537e-9402-8bd4777c29ef', 'word_count': 609, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b931b959-a520-537e-9402-8bd4777c29ef'}, {'abstract': 'The death last week of Lorenzo Charles, who grew up in the relatively benign surroundings of Starrett City, cast a light on the area’s failure to produce many athletes of note.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/03/sports/ncaabasketball/lorenzo-charles-the-hero-of-starrett-city-in-brooklyn.html', 'snippet': 'The death last week of Lorenzo Charles, who grew up in the relatively benign surroundings of Starrett City, cast a light on the area’s failure to produce many athletes of note.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lorenzo Charles, not to put it unkindly, was known for exactly one basketball play. With the score tied and a few seconds left in the 1983 N.C.A.A. championship game against heavily favored Houston, his North Carolina State teammate Dereck Whittenburg heaved a prayer at the rim. Charles recognized the arc of a 30-foot air ball. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/sports/starrett2/starrett2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 758, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/sports/starrett2/starrett2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/03/sports/starrett2/starrett2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Lesson in Fleeting Fame From the Old Neighborhood', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Lesson in Fleeting Fame From the Old Neighborhood', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'key