roaded by untrained prosecutors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In an important prosecutorial-misconduct case this term, the Supreme Court’s conservative majority threw out a $14 million jury award for a New Orleans man who was imprisoned for 18 years, including 14 on death row, for a robbery and a murder he did not commit. One month before John Thompson’s scheduled execution, a private investigator discovered that prosecutors had hidden evidence that exonerated him.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The D.A. Stole His Life, Justices Took His Money', 'kicker': 'Editorial | Annotation', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The D.A. Stole His Life, Justices Took His Money', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thompson, John', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'District Attorneys', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'False Arrests, Convictions and Imprisonments', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Connick, Harry Sr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ginsburg, Ruth Bader', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-02T20:49:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lincoln Caplan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lincoln', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7e46b23-ffdd-57ad-9f83-b9e5f3a21864', 'word_count': 408, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7e46b23-ffdd-57ad-9f83-b9e5f3a21864'}, {'abstract': 'Readers continue a conversation about cuts in Social Security and Medicare.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/03/opinion/sunday/l03dialogue.html', 'snippet': 'Readers continue a conversation about cuts in Social Security and Medicare.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What’s in Medicare’s future? A letter on Wednesday calling for a sharp cut in benefits and a “sober dialogue” between the generations drew more than 100 responses. This is a sampling.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/sunday-review/0703letters/0703letters-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 852, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/sunday-review/0703letters/0703letters-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/03/sunday-review/0703letters/0703letters-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sunday Dialogue: The Old, the Young and Medicare', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sunday Dialogue: The Old, The Young and Medicare', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-02T20:50:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_n