ndstedt and Horia Tecau, 6-3, 6-4, 7-6 (2), in the Wimbledon men’s doubles final Saturday to tie Todd Woodbridge and Mark Woodforde’s record of 11 Grand Slam championships.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WIMBLEDON, England — History was never the carrot Bob and Mike Bryan were chasing. They weren’t fixated on records the way the golfer Tiger Woods is on Jack Nicklaus’s record of 18 major titles. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bryans Tie Record for Major Doubles Championships', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bryan, Bob', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bryan, Mike', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-02T20:57:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/15647da7-75dc-51fd-8de0-7251996a37f2', 'word_count': 461, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15647da7-75dc-51fd-8de0-7251996a37f2'}, {'abstract': 'Median pay for chief executives at 200 of the nation’s largest companies rose 23 percent last year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/07/03/business/20110703-executive-pay-revisited-even-higher-than-it-first-seemed.html', 'snippet': 'Median pay for chief executives at 200 of the nation’s largest companies rose 23 percent last year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Median pay for chief executives at 200 of the nation’s largest companies rose 23 percent last year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Executive Pay, Revisited: Even Higher Than It First Seemed', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-02T21:15:05+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/611fa6ee-40bb-59ba-97b7-2aae3de49b0d', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/611fa6ee-40bb-59ba-97b7-2aae3de49b0d'}, {'abstract': 'A look at how Equilar, the executive compensation data company, compiled pay data for its survey.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/03/business/03paybox.html', 'snippet': 'A look at how Equilar, the executive compensation data company, compiled pay data for its survey.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sunday Business asked Equilar, the executive compensation data company, to compile and analyze pay data from corporate filings. To be included in the revised study, a company must have been incorporated in the United States and must have filed a definitive proxy statement by June 23. The 200 highest-paid C.E.O.’s at companies with revenue of $10.78 billion or more were included.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How the Pay Figures Were Calculated', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How the Pay Figures Were Calculated', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Compensation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Equilar', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-02T21:15:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a72bad4-966b-5f58-9b45-a414f6fc7460', 'word_count': 253, '