h': 'It has been six months since Congress voted to allow military service by openly gay, lesbian and bisexual Americans, but the law banning their service is still in effect. The Pentagon has not certified that the military is ready for the change, and while that process needlessly drags on, soldiers continue to be discharged for acknowledging their sexuality. The full repeal of this discriminatory policy should be one of the highest priorities for the new defense secretary, Leon Panetta.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Unfinished Business: ‘Don’t Ask, Don’t Tell’', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Unfinished Business: The military has yet to be freed of ‘don’t ask, don’t tell’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Panetta, Leon V', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-02T21:17:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c5b4c73-7ef4-5815-b54b-e77adae5c799', 'word_count': 523, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c5b4c73-7ef4-5815-b54b-e77adae5c799'}, {'abstract': 'What happens in a he said-she said case, when he’s known to be a predator and she’s revealed to be a liar?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/03/opinion/sunday/03dowd.html', 'snippet': 'What happens in a he said-she said case, when he’s known