one, 'print_headline': 'Unfinished Business: Federal law undermines progress on same-sex marriage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense of Marriage Act (1996)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-02T21:24:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6528b5f-8b47-5233-a30d-84dc73d55fb2', 'word_count': 476, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6528b5f-8b47-5233-a30d-84dc73d55fb2'}, {'abstract': 'Inconsistent laws will make same-sex divorce difficult. But “straight” disunions were once a lot tougher too. No longer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/03/sunday-review/03divorce.html', 'snippet': 'Inconsistent laws will make same-sex divorce difficult. But “straight” disunions were once a lot tougher too. No longer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IF you thought the fight over same-sex marriage has been tumultuous, just wait for the era of same-sex divorce. With New York State’s new law allowing same-sex marriage, not just for residents but for out-of-staters as well, a bumper crop of weddings is sure to follow — and, eventually and inevitably, a sizable number of divorces. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Same-Sex Marriages End', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Same-Sex Marriages End', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Socarides, Richard', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Divorce, Separations and Annulments', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legal Profession', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duncan, William C', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abbott, Greg', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-02T21:30:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Schwartz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwartz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3aee5e2-946b-5474-89f9-47e937d0af19', 'word_count': 948, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3aee5e2-946b-5474-89f9-47e937d0af19'}, {'abstract': 'When Jo-Wilfried Tsonga fell behind love 40 while serving for the first set at 5-4, I remembered a story about Pancho Gonzalez. He had such confidence in his serve that he thought the odds of coming back and holding serve were still in his favor, even if faced with three straight break points.  Sure enough, Tsonga played a deft half volley to save the first break point, then uncorked two monstrous first serves to get back to deuce.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/02/analysis-tsonga-lost-on-his-own-terms/', 'snippet': 'When Jo-Wilfried Tsonga fell behind love 40 while serving for the first set at 5-4, I remembered a story about Pancho Gonzalez. He had such confidence in his serve that he thought the odds of coming back and holding serve were still in his favor, ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Jo-Wilfried Tsonga fell behind by 0-40 while serving for the first set at 5-4, I remembered a story about Pancho Gonzalez. He had such confidence in his serve that he thought the odds of coming back and holding serve were still in his favor, even if faced with three straight break points. Sure enough, Tsonga played a deft half volley to save the first break point, then uncorked two monstrous first serves to get back to deuce.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Analysis: Tsonga Lost, on His Own Terms', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-02T21:30:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Geoff Macdonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Geoff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macdonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e914cb8a-2e9c-5dcf-aae4-517815d01e2b', 'word_count': 488, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e914cb8a-2e9c-5dcf-aae4-517815d01e2b'}, {'abstract': 'By analyzing aggregated cellphone traffic interesting patterns emerge about how people connect.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/03/sunday-review/03phone-map.html', 'snippet': 'By analyzing aggregated cellphone traffic interesting patterns emerge about how people connect.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AMERICANS are more connected now than ever. Mobile phones allow people to maintain relationships with friends, family and colleagues across long distances. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Phone-Call Cartography', 'kicker': 'Data Points', 'conte