he war in Iraq will be a well-trained and well-equipped Iraqi special operations force.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the American military legacies of the war in Iraq will be a well-trained and well-equipped Iraqi special operations force.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/28/world/middleeast/20110629-IRAQ-slide-BKJ8/20110629-IRAQ-slide-BKJ8-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/28/world/middleeast/20110629-IRAQ-slide-BKJ8/20110629-IRAQ-slide-BKJ8-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/28/world/middleeast/20110629-IRAQ-slide-BKJ8/20110629-IRAQ-slide-BKJ8-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Teamwork and Training in Iraq', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Joint Special Operations Command (JSOC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Special Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Army Special Forces (Green Berets)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-02T21:57:30+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'World', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/5a01070e-d98e-5f33-b6d9-5d5d6e5fb6b8', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/5a01070e-d98e-5f33-b6d9-5d5d6e5fb6b8'}, {'abstract': 'Members of Iraq’s well-trained special operations force say that American troops must stay longer to continue training and advising.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/03/world/middleeast/03iraq.html', 'snippet': 'Members of Iraq’s well-trained special operations force say that American troops must stay longer to continue training and advising.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BAGHDAD — In darkness and dressed in black, the American and Iraqi Special Operations commandos navigated the dense urban neighborhood here in the capital and approached a house they believed to be a hide-out for two brothers suspected of carrying out assassinations and car-bomb attacks. As the Iraqis bashed in the door, the sound of glass shattering and screams pierced the nighttime stillness.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/world/03iraq-span/sub-jp03iraq1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 362, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/03/world/03iraq-span/sub-jp03iraq1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 362}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/world/03iraq-span/sub-jp03iraq1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/world/03iraq-span/sub-jp03iraq1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/03/world/03iraq-span/sub-jp03iraq1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Taking Lead, Iraqis Hope U.S. Special Operations Commandos Stay', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Taking Lead, Iraqis Hope U.S. Commandos Stay', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Special Operations Command', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-02T21:59:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Arango', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Arango', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a61f7bc1-5413-5bbe-8857-ed07950d96e9', 'word_count': 1159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a61f7bc1-5413-5bbe-8857-ed07950d96e9'}, {'abstract': 'That Pete Muller. What a heckuva nice guy he is.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/02/treat/', 'snippet': 'That Pete Muller. What a heckuva nice guy he is.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SUNDAY’S PUZZLE — Are you thirsty? I’ll bet you are. We’ve had two puzzles today, and as far as I’m concerned, that’s a full working day.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sunday: My Treat', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-02T22:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7fb42fa-2259-5b2b-bdeb-9bd9be70c64e', 'word_count': 350, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7fb42fa-2259-5b2b-bdeb-9bd9be70c64e'}, {'abstract': 'Michael Crosno and MyEdu, the Web company of which he is chief executive, are working to reduce the costs of college and lower the average time for getting a degree.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/03/us/03ttmyedu.html', 'snippet': 'Michael Crosno and MyEdu, the Web company of which he is chief executive, are working to reduce the costs of college and lower the average time for getting a degree.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If there was a theme to the just-concluded 82nd legislative session it was do more with less, and Representative Daniel Branch, Republican of Dallas and chairman of the House Higher Education Committee, embraced it by attacking the cost of college from multiple angles. He pushed through legislation to try to lower what students must spend on textbooks and to mandate that undergraduate students file — and stick to — degree plans.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/us/03TTMYEDU/03TTMYEDU-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/03/us/03TTMYEDU/03TTMYEDU-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/us/03TTMYEDU/03TTMYEDU-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/us/03TTMYEDU/03TTMYEDU-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/03/us/03TTMYEDU/03TTMYEDU-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Crusading From Outside to Lower College Costs', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Crusading From Outside To Lower College Costs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pick-a-Prof', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-02T22:04:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Reeve Hamilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Reeve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hamilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7c7157e-8bd3-51ab-a5ad-3327f71e4bab', 'word_count': 862, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7c7157e-8bd3-51ab-a5ad-3327f71e4bab'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Fellows worked with some of the biggest stars in Hollywood, including Bing Crosby, W. C. Fields and Gene Autry.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/03/arts/edith-fellows-child-star-shadowed-by-dickensian-troubles-dies-at-88.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Fellows worked with some of the biggest stars in Hollywood, including Bing Crosby, W. C. Fields and Gene Autry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Edith Fellows, a child star of the 1930s who was known for playing orphans and urchins but whose own life was more Dickensian than that of any character she portrayed, died on June 26 in Los Angeles. She was 88.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/02/arts/obit-fellows/obit-fellows-articleL