 Creation myths like that are powerful, even when they have no basis in fact.', 'lead_paragraph': 'San Francisco’s $1.6 billion Central Subway is finally arriving. After decades of planning, the city this week chose a construction company that will begin digging the tunnel from South of Market to Chinatown later this year. And it is all because former Mayor Willie Brown Jr., following the 1989 Loma Prieta earthquake, promised a subway to Chinatown leaders who feared that their community would suffer when the city tore down the Embarcadero Freeway. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Myths Get Trains Running', 'kicker': 'The Bay Citizen', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Myths Get Trains Running', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transit Systems', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Willie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bay Citizen, The', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-02T22:46:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zusha Elinson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zusha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elinson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6444ce9-75f0-5a03-9ec7-b6d2e10b2dbf', 'word_count': 489, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6444ce9-75f0-5a03-9ec7-b6d2e10b2dbf'}, {'abstract': 'The United States defeated Colombia, 3-0, and Sweden topped North Korea, 1-0, to advance to the quarterfinals of the Women’s World Cup in Germany.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/02/u-s-women-advance-to-quarterfinals/', 'snippet': 'The United States defeated Colombia, 3-0, and Sweden topped North Korea, 1-0, to advance to the quarterfinals of the Women’s World Cup in Germany.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The United States defeated Colombia, 3-0, and Sweden topped North Korea, 1-0, to advance to the quarterfinals of the Women’s World Cup in Germany. Neither team has allowed a goal through two games, but plenty will be at stake when they meet Wednesday in Wolfsburg: the group winner will most likely avoid a date with Brazil in the quarterfinals. Read the article here, and come back to comment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Women Advance to Quarterfinals', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's World Cup (Soccer)", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-02T22:51:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6d2977e-2367-555e-ba85-31df041c6f4a', 'word_count': 68, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6d2977e-2367-555e-ba85-31df041c6f4a'}, {'abstract': 'A clever network of pathways crisscrossing the Berkeley hills helped transform the bare brown hills into some of Berkeley’s most beautiful and romantic neighborhoods.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/03/us/03bcintel.html', 'snippet': 'A clever network of pathways crisscrossing the Berkeley hills helped transform the bare brown hills into some of Berkeley’s most beautiful and romantic neighborhoods.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A clever network of pathways crisscrossing the Berkeley hills helped transform the bare brown hills into some of Berkeley’s most beautiful and romantic neighborhoods. The pathways have made life easier for hill dwellers for more than 100 years.\xa0', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21B', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/us/03BCINTEL1/03BCINTEL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/03/us/03BCINTEL1/03BCINTEL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/us/03BCINTEL1/03BCINTEL1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 702, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/us/03BCINTEL1/03BCINTEL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/03/us/03BCINTEL1/03BCINTEL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pedestrian Pathways', 'kicker': 'The Bay Citizen', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pedestrian Pathways', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Volunteers and Community Service', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Berkeley (Calif)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bay Citizen, The', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Landscaping', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-02T22:52:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tasneem Raja', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tasneem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Raja', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 