': 'The Times it is a changing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The movie, which we just saw. It’s about the Times; and Robin and I, at least, found it fascinating. David Carr (whom I’ve never met) makes the film through his sheer quirkiness, although it jumps around a lot between the big question of whether news organizations as we know them can survive and smaller stories.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Page One', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-02T23:14:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/447647b1-a22c-5a87-b2b2-d6e7072b6641', 'word_count': 148, 'uri': 'nyt://article/447647b1-a22c-5a87-b2b2-d6e7072b6641'}, {'abstract': 'In losing their second straight game to the Yankees, the Mets also lost Reyes to tightness in his left hamstring. Reyes will undergo an M.R.I. on Sunday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/03/sports/baseball/mets-loss-to-yankees-is-compounded-by-reyess-early-exit.html', 'snippet': 'In losing their second straight game to the Yankees, the Mets also lost Reyes to tightness in his left hamstring. Reyes will undergo an M.R.I. on Sunday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For weeks now, Jose Reyes’s name has been a fixture in sentences bursting with superlatives. The best shortstop. The fastest leadoff hitter. The most exciting player in baseball. But on a muggy Saturday afternoon, a chill went through Mets fans as Reyes was linked with a familiar and discouraging concern — a hamstring injury.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/sports/YMETS1/YMETS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/03/sports/YMETS1/YMETS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/sports/YMETS1/YMETS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mets Hold Their Breath After Reyes Grabs His Hamstring', 'kicker': 'Yankees 5, Mets 2', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stop Sign', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reyes, Jose', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Colon, Bartolo', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-02T23:17:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/17e0aec7-5665-5aa7-9597-ef321a810992', 'word_count': 946, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17e0aec7-5665-5aa7-9597-ef321a810992'}, {'abstract': 'The United Neighborhood Organization, or UNO, steps in to guide Hispanic elementary school students in applying to high schools with favorable graduation and college-enrollment rates.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/03/us/03cncuno.html', 'snippet': 'The United Neighborhood Organization, or UNO, steps in to guide Hispanic elementary school students in applying to high schools with favorable graduation and college-enrollment rates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Amalia Lopez transferred to Tamayo Elementary charter school last year from a neighborhood school, where she says no one talked to her about high school options. It was assumed, said Amalia, 14, that she would attend her neighborhood high school. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/us/03CNCUNO/03CNCUNO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/03/us/03CNCUNO/03CNCUNO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/us/03CNCUNO/03CNCUNO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/us/03CNCUNO/03CNCUNO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/03/us/03CNCUNO/03CNCUNO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Expanding Hispanic Students’ Academic Horizons', 'kicker': 'Chicago News Cooperative', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Expanding Hispanic Students’ Academic Horizons', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12