 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/03/us/03CNCCENSUS/03CNCCENSUS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/us/03CNCCENSUS/03CNCCENSUS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Black Chicagoans Fuel Growth of South Suburbs', 'kicker': 'Chicago News Cooperative', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Black Chicagoans Fuel Growth of South Suburbs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Census', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Population', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-02T23:58:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Darnell Little and Dan Mihalopoulos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Darnell', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Little', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mihalopoulos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/24cd572f-bd0c-526e-8b12-14ffb0098f36', 'word_count': 1216, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24cd572f-bd0c-526e-8b12-14ffb0098f36'}, {'abstract': 'Gregory Young of San Francisco was ranked just seventh in the 10-player field at the United States Junior Closed Championship, and he had not competed in six months.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/03/crosswords/chess/chess-gregory-young-wins-us-junior-title.html', 'snippet': 'Gregory Young of San Francisco was ranked just seventh in the 10-player field at the United States Junior Closed Championship, and he had not competed in six months.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gregory Young is America’s newest junior champion, and an unlikely one.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '16-Year-Old Gets Aggressive, and Wins U.S. Junior Title', 'kicker': 'Chess', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '16-Year-Old Gets Aggressive, And Wins U.S. Junior Title', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chess', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-03T00:14:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'subsection_name': 'Chess', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dylan Loeb McClain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dylan', 'middlename': 'Loeb', 'lastname': 'McClain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf0ac828-cc1d-507c-be26-ab4b297cd7b9', 'word_count': 532, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf0ac828-cc1d-507c-be26-ab4b297cd7b9'}, {'abstract': 'The founder of Niche Media relaxes in Southampton on Sundays with his wife and two daughters, his “human alarm clock.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/03/nyregion/jason-binn-spends-summer-sundays-on-the-beach.html', 'snippet': 'The founder of Niche Media relaxes in Southampton on Sundays with his wife and two daughters, his “human alarm clock.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'An entrepreneur who markets luxury goods online and on paper, and himself on the cocktail party circuit, Jason Binn is the chairman and founder of Niche Media, an array of boutique magazines including Hamptons and Gotham. He is also chief adviser to Kevin Ryan, chief executive officer of the Gilt Groupe. Mr. Binn, 43, shares homes in TriBeCa; Southampton; Aspen, Colo.; and Los Angeles with his wife, Haley, 35, and their daughters, Penny, 5, and CeCe, 3. He often spends Friday and Saturday nights socializing with haute Hamptons luminaries like Christie Brinkley,\xa0but summer Sundays are for kicking back with the kids at the beach.  ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/nyregion/03ROUTINE_SPAN/03ROUTINE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 352, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/03/nyregion/03ROUTINE_SPAN/03ROUTINE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 352}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/nyregion/03ROUTINE_SPAN/03ROUTINE_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/nyregion/03ROUTINE_SPAN/03ROUTINE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/03/nyregion/03ROUTINE_SPAN/03ROUTINE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Saddling Up, and Hitting the Beach', 'kicker': 'Sunday Routine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Saddling Up, and Hitting the Beach', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Niche Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bridgehampton (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Binn, Jason', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-03T00:28:45+0000', 'documen