acy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/03/nyregion/03POETRY_span/03POETRY_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/nyregion/03POETRY_span/03POETRY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/nyregion/03POETRY_span/03POETRY_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/03/nyregion/03POETRY_span/03POETRY_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When Waves and Sand Evoke Summertime Lust', 'kicker': 'Poetic Connections | The Beach', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Waves and Sand Evoke Summertime Lust', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Craigslist', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beaches', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-03T00:29:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Feuer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Feuer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/94e11c00-a305-5fcd-b3ed-2b925a37b0ed', 'word_count': 458, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94e11c00-a305-5fcd-b3ed-2b925a37b0ed'}, {'abstract': 'Because Tim Pawlenty sits in the middle of the Republican presidential field, he has more competition to worry about. The types of voters who find him acceptable will also like a lot of other candidates.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/02/how-tim-pawlenty-is-like-rc-cola/', 'snippet': 'Because Tim Pawlenty sits in the middle of the Republican presidential field, he has more competition to worry about. The types of voters who find him acceptable will also like a lot of other candidates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Regular readers of this blog will know that I’ve been of mixed minds on the electoral prospects of former Gov. Tim Pawlenty of Minnesota. I’ve gone from initial skepticism about his chances to defending him as a “top-tier” candidate while some other analysts downgraded his status.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Tim Pawlenty Is Like RC Cola', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pawlenty, Tim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-03T00:45:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/328df0b9-6cd8-5bb2-ba5c-cce06a636625', 'word_count': 1032, 'uri': 'nyt://article/328df0b9-6cd8-5bb2-ba5c-cce06a636625'}, {'abstract': 'Noam Chomsky, whom President Hugo Chávez of Venezuela often cites as a source of inspiration, issued a call for clemency for a judge held under house arrest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/03/world/americas/03venezuela.html', 'snippet': 'Noam Chomsky, whom President Hugo Chávez of Venezuela often cites as a source of inspiration, issued a call for clemency for a judge held under house arrest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CARACAS, Venezuela — Even 