akes the game look easy, especially in pass protection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Friendly Disclaimer: The following list is influenced largely -– but not strictly -– by film study of all 32 teams from the 2010 season. Stats weren’t acknowledged, but players with poor numbers generally don’t make top 10 lists anyway. Vague enough for you? Criteria for top 10 lists tend to be. That’s why most of you will have no trouble finding some disagreement with what you’re about to read.  ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Top 10 Offensive Tackles in N.F.L.', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-03T10:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Benoit', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Benoit', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/04859543-03f9-5baf-96dd-473278e43506', 'word_count': 495, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04859543-03f9-5baf-96dd-473278e43506'}, {'abstract': 'In a rare display of cross-cultural cooperation between countries with a history of enmity, a new exhibition in Istanbul features antiquities from Greece.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/03/in-istanbul-greek-history-on-display/', 'snippet': 'In a rare display of cross-cultural cooperation between countries with a history of enmity, a new exhibition in Istanbul features antiquities from Greece.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a rare display of cross-cultural cooperation between countries with a history of enmity, a new exhibition in Istanbul features antiquities from Greece, including marble figurines, clay tankards, weapons, cooking utensils, jewelry and ancient idols.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Istanbul, Greek History on Display', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Istanbul (Turkey)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-03T10:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susanne Fowler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fowler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d620e978-a754-5bcf-aa7d-4c1908f3fb17', 'word_count': 212, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d620e978-a754-5bcf-aa7d-4c1908f3fb17'}, {'abstract': 'General Lee, I have no division.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/03/july-3-1863/', 'snippet': 'General Lee, I have no division.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Update: now that I have a few minutes, what I get from Stephen Sears is that the portrayal in this movie is fairly accurate. The main gap seems to be the thing about the fence: apparently the double fence at the Emmitsburg Road was a big obstacle on the left wing of the attack (Trimble and Pettigrew), where in fact the attack stopped dead right there; on Pickett’s wing, the fence was much further back and wasn’t a big deal.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'July 3, 1863', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-03T11:38:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By