nd Gorillaz) and Rufus Norris, opened at the Manchester International Festival in England.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/04/arts/music/damon-albarn-opera-dr-dee-at-manchester-festival-review.html', 'snippet': '“Dr Dee,” an opera set in Elizabethan times, by Damon Albarn (of Blur and Gorillaz) and Rufus Norris, opened at the Manchester International Festival in England.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MANCHESTER, England — What’s a rock songwriter — Damon Albarn, of Blur and Gorillaz — doing composing an opera about an Elizabethan alchemist? The best answer might be: conjuring. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/04/arts/04albern_395/04albern_395-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 664, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/04/arts/04albern_395/04albern_395-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/04/arts/04albern_395/04albern_395-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Alchemist Reaches Out Across Centuries', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Alchemist Reaches Out Across Centuries', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'English National Opera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Palace Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALBARN, DAMON', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Norris, Rufus', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Blur', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-03T19:14:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/3827f8f6-723d-5f1b-bb98-f81c2d13562a', 'word_count': 692, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3827f8f6-723d-5f1b-bb98-f81c2d13562a'}, {'abstract': 'Novak Djokovic defeated the defending champion Rafael Nadal for the fifth time this year, but for the first time in a Grand Slam event.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/04/sports/tennis/2011-wimbledon-mens-final-novak-djokovic-defeats-rafael-nadal.html', 'snippet': 'Novak Djokovic defeated the defending champion Rafael Nadal for the fifth time this year, but for the first time in a Grand Slam event.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WIMBLEDON, England — It was the final game of an era, and Rafael Nadal punched the strings of his racket as if it were the culprit instead of the faithful companion that had helped him win 2 Wimbledon titles and 20 straight matches here.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/04/sports/yyy-wimbledon1/yyy-wimbledon1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/04/sports/yyy-wimbledon1/yyy-wimbledon1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/04/sports/yyy-wimbledon1/yyy-wimbledon1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 705, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/04/sports/yyy-wimbledon1/yyy-wimbledon1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/04/sports/yyy-wimbledon1/yyy-wimbledon1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Djokovic’s Dream Made Real With Wimbledon Conquest', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Djokovic’s Dream Made Real With Wimbledon Conquest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nadal, Rafael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Djokovic, Novak', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-03T19:17:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Clarey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clarey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c11f256c-001d-5656-a85e-fff469637a13', 'word_count': 1081, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c11f256c-001d-5656-a85e-fff469637a13'}, {'abstract': '“The Devil’s Music” is a biographical musical about the life, loves and career of the blues singer Bessie Smith.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/04/theater/reviews/the-devils-music-at-st-lukes-theater-review.html', 'snippet': '“The Devil’s Music” is a biographical musical about the life, loves and career of the blues singer Bessie Smith.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Miche Braden plants herself at the front of the stage, shimmies a little and sings the blues, “The Devil’s Music: The Life and Blues of Bessie Smith” finds its reason for being. As Bessie, Ms. Braden has the requisite big voice — she knows when to let it soar and when to keep it at an insinuatingly low simmer — and her committed performance gives you glimmers of what the bawdy-talking, hooch-swilling (she hates the store-bought stuff), unapologetically bisexual Bessie must have been like. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/04/arts/devil/devil-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 957, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/04/arts/devil/devil-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/04/arts/devil/devil-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Big Voice Full of Blues, Bawdy and Unapologetic', 'kicker': "Theater Review | 'The Devil's Music'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Big Voice Full of Blues, Bawdy and Unapologetic', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Braden, Miche', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blues Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Penguin Repertory Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Bessie (1894-1937)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parra, Angelo', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "The Devil's Music (Play)", 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-03T19:41:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Saltz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saltz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf782a64-78e7-5d14-8abc-37f3cdf40d87', 'word_count': 362, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf782a64-78e7-5d14-8abc-37f3cdf40d87'}, {'abstract': '“The Greenwich Village Follies,” at Manhattan Theater Source, is a historical tour of the Village, with singing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/04/theater/reviews/greenwich-village-follies-at-theater-source-review.html', 'snippet': '“The Greenwich Village Follies,” at Manhattan Theater Source, is a historical tour of the Village, with singing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I lived on West 12th Street, I bought a coffee-table book called “Greenwich Village and How It Got That Way.” It turned out to be a rich, juicy history, starring American Indians, pirates, artists, anarchists and beatniks.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/04/arts/sub-green/sub-green-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 876, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From George Washington to Beatniks and Beyond', 'kicker': "Theater Review | 'The Greenwich Village Follies'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From George Washington to Beatniks and Beyond', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Manhattan Theatre Source', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greenwich Village (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-03T19:51:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': '