rticle', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/95caa021-7287-54b1-a452-4556eb3e364f', 'word_count': 353, 'uri': 'nyt://article/95caa021-7287-54b1-a452-4556eb3e364f'}, {'abstract': 'Politicians and Western diplomats here have said privately that they hope recent attacks, which have killed 42 Afghans, will stop before villagers in the attacked areas take up arms themselves.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/04/world/asia/04afghanistan.html', 'snippet': 'Politicians and Western diplomats here have said privately that they hope recent attacks, which have killed 42 Afghans, will stop before villagers in the attacked areas take up arms themselves.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — Rocket and artillery shells fired from Pakistan have killed 42 Afghans and wounded 48 in three provinces of eastern Afghanistan over the last five weeks, according to local Afghan security officials and tribal elders who have strongly protested the assaults over the last several days and demanded that the Afghan government protect them.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/04/world/04afghanistan/04afghanistan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/04/world/04afghanistan/04afghanistan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 340}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/04/world/04afghanistan/04afghanistan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/04/world/04afghanistan/04afghanistan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/04/world/04afghanistan/04afghanistan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Deadly Shelling by Pakistan Into Afghanistan Is Stoking Tensions', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Deadly Shelling by Pakistan Into Afghanistan Is Stoking Tensions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-04T01:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alissa J. Rubin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alissa', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Rubin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a21e6cb-24db-5c4a-b7b7-66aebc841ba5', 'word_count': 737, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a21e6cb-24db-5c4a-b7b7-66aebc841ba5'}, {'abstract': 'An animated film celebrating Sousa and the Fourth.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/03/stars-stripes/', 'snippet': 'An animated film celebrating Sousa and the Fourth.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve always liked John Philip Sousa’s “The Stars and Stripes Forever.” I first became aware of the song in Popeye cartoons from the 1930s and ’40s. It consistently accompanied his post-spinach trouncing of his rival, Bluto. The music gave Popeye strength, better posture, moral certainty and an aura of the American military’s invincibility. Battleships firing cannons even appeared in his muscles. I guess that’s what a good march does: it makes you stronger on your way to battle. This performance is excerpted from a 1906 Edison recording featuring Sousa’s band.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Stars & Stripes’', 'kicker': 'Jeff Scher', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holidays and Special Occasions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-04T01:00:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Scher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/54d976d2-d4d5-58aa-9779-927462149d67', 'word_count': 210, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54d976d2-d4d5-58aa-9779-927462149d67'}, {'abstract': 'The United States of America has requested your friendship on Facebook.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/04/opinion/04wayne.html', 'snippet': 'The United States of America has requested your friendship on Facebook.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AMERICA and Indigenous Peoples are now friends. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Like It or Unfriend It', 'kicker': 'Op-Art', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Like It or Unfriend It', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': '