Greatest of All Time conversation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Analysis: How Djokovic Beat Nadal', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-04T01:15:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Geoff Macdonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Geoff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macdonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f681f9b1-2a35-58e9-bff3-2dfbc46a5271', 'word_count': 751, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f681f9b1-2a35-58e9-bff3-2dfbc46a5271'}, {'abstract': 'The Dodgers’ financial problems highlights the expanding importance of television rights in sports.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/04/sports/baseball/dodgers-plight-highlights-influence-of-tv-in-sports.html', 'snippet': 'The Dodgers’ financial problems highlights the expanding importance of television rights in sports.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The fight for control of the Los Angeles Dodgers that reached United States Bankruptcy Court in Delaware on Tuesday pits Frank McCourt, an owner desperate to keep his team, against Commissioner Bud Selig, who believes that McCourt has turned the iconic team into a financial wreck.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/04/sports/JPDODGERS3/JPDODGERS3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 737, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/04/sports/JPDODGERS3/JPDODGERS3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/04/sports/JPDODGERS3/JPDODGERS3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'TV’s Supporting Role in Dodgers’ Drama', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'TV’s Supporting Role in Dodgers’ Drama', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Dodgers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox Sports', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCourt, Frank H Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Selig, Bud', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-04T01:17:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/391e0ce2-588a-5f98-a0ea-69013cffa1d9', 'word_count': 1041, 'uri': 'nyt://article/391e0ce2-588a-5f98-a0ea-69013cffa1d9'}, {'abstract': 'A dormant anti-Americanism has been reawakened, fueled by a sense that the media-driven culture of the United States has undermined justice and fair play in the case of Dominique Strauss-Kahn.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/04/world/europe/04france.html', 'snippet': 'A dormant anti-Americanism has been reawakened, fueled by a sense that the media-driven culture of the United States has undermined justice and fair play in the case of Dominique Strauss-Kahn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — The stunning reversals in the criminal case against Dominique Strauss-Kahn, a putative French presidential candidate, have reawakened a dormant anti-Americanism here, fueled by a sense that the raw, media-driven culture of the United States has undermined justice and fair play.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'French See Case Against Strauss-Kahn as American Folly', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'French See Strauss-Kahn Case as American Folly', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strauss-Kahn, Dominique', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-04T01:18:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Erlanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erlanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/60c6a01d-b47e-5c01-9043-ccdff142312c', 'word_count': 1292, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60c6a01d-b47e-5c01-9043-ccdff142312c'}, {'abstract': 'Supporters of both Mr. Strauss-Kahn and his accuser are questioning the assumptions they had made about race, sex and power.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/04/nyregion/as-strauss-kahn-case-falters-new-yorkers-reflect-on-the-citys-attitude.html', 'snippet': 'Supporters of both Mr. Strauss-Kahn and his accuser are questioning the assumptions they had made about race, sex and power.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The sexual assault case against Dominique Strauss-Kahn, with its deep undercurrents of international power, sex, race and political ambition, seemed a good Rorschach test for how New Yorkers see their city. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/04/nyregion/voices1/voices1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 782, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/04/nyregion/voices1/voices1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/04/nyregion/voices1/voices1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'With Each Twist in Strauss-Kahn Case, City Sees Further Reflections of Itself', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Each Twist in Strauss-Kahn Case, City Sees Further Reflections of Itself', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strauss-Kahn, Dominique', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-04T01:21:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Dolnick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dolnick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4dba12f6-7d23-5a64-85a2-79bf295c382a', 'word_count': 1125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4dba12f6-7d23-5a64-