nytimes.com/2011/07/05/world/europe/05union.html', 'snippet': 'Responding to the growing threat of a humanitarian crisis, the European Union said it would provide about $14.5 million in emergency aid.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRUSSELS — Responding to the growing threat of a humanitarian crisis in North Korea, the European Union announced on Monday that it will provide about $14.5 million in emergency aid to feed more than some 650,000 North Koreans.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'European Union to Send Food Aid to North Korea', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'European Union to Send Food Aid to North Korea', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Aid', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Humanitarian Aid', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-04T09:08:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Castle and Mark McDonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McDonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e689ceee-3a53-50ac-ac17-dff336401708', 'word_count': 825, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e689ceee-3a53-50ac-ac17-dff336401708'}, {'abstract': 'Ratko Mladic, the former Bosnian Serb military commander, challenged the legitimacy of the war crimes tribunal and repeatedly interrupted the proceedings at his trial.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/world/europe/05mladic.html', 'snippet': 'Ratko Mladic, the former Bosnian Serb military commander, challenged the legitimacy of the war crimes tribunal and repeatedly interrupted the proceedings at his trial.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — The wartime Bosnian Serb commander, Ratko Mladic, put on a show of belligerence at the United Nations war crimes tribunal on Monday, shouting and laughing at the bench, even taunting his judges, but he lost the first test of wills when the presiding judge abruptly expelled him from the court.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/05/world/MLADIC/MLADIC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/05/world/MLADIC/MLADIC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/05/world/MLADIC/MLADIC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hague Judge Orders Mladic Removed From Courtroom', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Judge Orders Mladic From Courtroom After Outbursts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mladic, Ratko', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Netherlands', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-04T09:21:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marlise Simons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marlise', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Simons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a12ad6e-ffec-5bd0-8a53-10b747f7db82', 'word_count': 639, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a12ad6e-ffec-5bd0-8a53-10b747f7db82'}, {'abstract': 'Construction of bike paths offers economic benefits in addition to improvements in health and the environment, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/04/the-bicycle-dividend/', 'snippet': 'Construction of bike paths offers economic benefits in addition to improvements in health and the environment, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nancy Folbre is an economics professor at the University of Massachusetts Amherst.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Bicycle Dividend', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bicycles and Bicycling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-04T10:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nancy Folbre', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nancy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Folbre', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6de2cbe-9f57-5223-b6d8-d86c40a6f059', 'word_count': 755, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6de2cbe-9f57-5223-b6d8-d86c40a6f059'}, {'abstract': 'With Nick Mangold, the Jets are the only team in the N.F.L. that doesn’t have to sacrifice a guard when facing an elite nose tackle.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/04/top-10-centers-in-n-f-l/', 'snippet': 'With Nick Mangold, the Jets are the only team in the N.F.L. that doesn’t have to sacrifice a guard when facing an elite nose tackle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Friendly Disclaimer: The following list is influenced largely -– but not strictly -– by film study of all 32 teams from the 2010 season. Stats weren’t acknowledged, but players with poor numbers generally don’t make top 10 lists anyway. Vague enough for you? Criteria for top 10 lists tend to be. That’s why most of you will have no trouble finding some disagreement with what you’re about to read. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Top 10 Centers in N.F.L.', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-04T10:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Benoit', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Benoit', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e78bf9e-e14b-5b35-b047-a32775894d91', 'word_count': 360, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e78bf9e-e14b-5b35-b047-a32775894d91'}, {'abstract': 'In this week’s Complaint Box: I had one good pickup line, and e-readers ruined it.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/04/complaint-box-how-e-readers-destroyed-my-love-life/', 'snippet': 'In this week’s Complaint Box: I had one good pickup line, and e-readers ruined it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I noticed his wavy hair, his feline eyes and his lips, which moved slightly as he read. But the first thing I noticed was his book: Philip Roth’s “Portnoy’s Complaint,” one of my favorites, was cradled in his palm. Between Delancey Street and Bryant Park on the uptown F train, I fell for him hard. It wasn’t the first time I’d flirted my way into a Saturday night date with a simple phrase: “I love that book.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Complaint Box | How E-Readers Destroyed My Love Life', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Amazon Kindle', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electronic Books and Readers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subways', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-04T10:00:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Lewis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lewis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4fbe297-06f9-5235-85bd-e8cc406cd10f', 'word_count': 676, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4fbe297-06f9-5235-85bd-e8cc406cd10f'}, {'abstract': 'Fifty dramatic color photographs by Anders Ryman will grace illuminated screens at More London Riverside, a development on the south bank of the River Thames, through Sept. 6.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/04/london-photo-display-celebrates-rites-of-life/', 'snippet': 'Fifty dramatic color photographs by Anders Ryman will grace illuminated screens at More London Riverside, a development on the south bank of the River Thames, through Sept. 6.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fifty dramatic color photographs of ceremonies and events, ranging from birth to death, as celebrated by the world’s modern and traditional societies will grace illuminated screens at More London Riverside, a development on the south bank of the River Thames, through Sept. 6.', 'source': 'The New York Tim