e more likely to die from them than people living elsewhere in the country. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In the ‘Stroke Belt,’ Erosion of Memory Is More Likely Too', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In the ‘Stroke Belt,’ Erosion of Memory Is More Likely Too', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Memory', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stroke', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-04T15:33:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pam Belluck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belluck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b613a55e-2c7f-5b36-bd14-c7bdd4eeeed1', 'word_count': 1222, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b613a55e-2c7f-5b36-bd14-c7bdd4eeeed1'}, {'abstract': 'At age 2, children identified as “late talkers” were more likely than other toddlers to have behavioral problems, but there was no difference between the groups at older ages.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/health/research/05patterns.html', 'snippet': 'At age 2, children identified as “late talkers” were more likely than other toddlers to have behavioral problems, but there was no difference between the groups at older ages.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Parents often worry when their toddlers are slow to start talking, but a long-term study has found that these children have no more emotional or behavioral problems than others by age 5 — as long as they are otherwise developing n