on, 17 minimal looks cut from men’s suiting, did not disappoint.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/04/just-one-look-bouchra-jarrar/', 'snippet': 'Jarrar’s collection, 17 minimal looks cut from men’s suiting, did not disappoint.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bouchra Jarrar is one of the few ready-to-wear designers to present a collection on the haute couture calendar. The Balenciaga-alum is beloved for the gamine simplicity of her silhouettes, the refinement of her hand (Jarrar’s clothes look as good inside as out), and her cool way with a slit. This collection she showed at the Odeon on Monday did not disappoint: 17 minimal looks cut from men’s suiting wools, tie silks and tuxedo satins. Here, her take on a smoking with an asymmetric collar and a slinky slash down the back.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Bouchra Jarrar', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-04T18:45:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sally Singer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sally', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Singer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f73cc016-fb81-5012-bbd8-53a4c1f40943', 'word_count': 96, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f73cc016-fb81-5012-bbd8-53a4c1f40943'}, {'abstract': 'There was a bit of anticipation about whether Mitt Romney and Jon Huntsman would interact at the Independence Day parade here in Amherst, N.H.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/04/mr-romney-say-hello-to-mr-huntsman/', 'snippet': 'There was a bit of anticipation about whether Mitt Romney and Jon Huntsman would interact at the Independence Day parade here in Amherst, N.H.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AMHERST, N.H. — There was a bit of anticipation about whether Mitt Romney and Jon Huntsman would interact at the Independence Day parade here in Amherst — at least as much anticipation as there can be for a parade route interaction. (Let’s face it, it’s a slow holiday weekend and the political press can get hungry for drama.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mr. Romney, Say Hello to Mr. Huntsman', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parades', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AMHERST (MASS)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beijing (China)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Hampshire', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-04T18:46:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Rutenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rutenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e465ac29-fd18-5118-8df4-631318f8436a', 'word_count': 165, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e465ac29-fd18-5118-8df4-631318f8436a'}, {'abstract': 'The Spanish sports newspaper Mundo Deportivo has reported that Rudy Fernandez, whom the Portland Trail Blazers traded on draft night to the newly crowned champion Dallas Mavericks, has a six-year contract offer to return to his native Spain and play for Real Madrid of the Spanish ACB, which is considered Europe’s top professional league.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/04/real-madrid-beckons-rudy-fernandez-with-offer/', 'snippet': 'The Spanish sports newspaper Mundo Deportivo has reported that Rudy Fernandez, whom the Portland Trail Blazers traded on draft night to the newly crowned champion Dallas Mavericks, has a six-year contract offer to return to his native Spain and pl...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The N.B.A. lockout may be in its infancy, but the immediate future is looking grim for a league that was forced to hold a shortened 50-game season in 1999 following a 204-day lockout.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Real Madrid Beckons Rudy Fernandez With Offer', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-04T19:00:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By JORGE CASTILLO', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jorge', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'CASTILLO', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e0e7e1d-a8fc-539d-9fb9-d1defe92147c', 'word_count': 350, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e0e7e1d-a8fc-539d-9fb9-d1defe92147c'}, {'abstract': 'For more than seven years, Roger Federer and Rafael Nadal have maintained a stranglehold on tennis’s top spot. Novak Djokovic changed that with his victory at Wimbledon.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/sports/tennis/novak-djokovic-finally-leads-the-pack-after-wimbledon.html', 'snippet': 'For more than seven years, Roger Federer and Rafael Nadal have maintained a stranglehold on tennis’s top spot. Novak Djokovic changed that with his victory at Wimbledon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WIMBLEDON, England — Novak Djokovic has been the hunter for years now, trying to chase down Roger Federer and Rafael Nadal. But he is No. 1 at last, and when he returned to Wimbledon as the new champion on Monday for his morning-after obligations with the news media, he was asked how it felt to be the rabbit, the one everyone else is chasing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/05/sports/tennis/05tennis1/05tennis1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 801, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/05/sports/tennis/05tennis1/05tennis1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/05/sports/tennis/05tennis1/05tennis1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After Years of Chasing, Djokovic Finally Leads the Pack', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Years of Chasing, Djokovic Finally Leads the Pack', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Federer, Roger', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nadal, Rafael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Djokovic, Novak', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-04T19:04:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Clarey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clarey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a486c83-0bf2-5f78-b376-625d51f45d3d', 'word_count': 1133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a486c83