le': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Landon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thomas', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2593d627-ead5-5ea2-850b-98883e48f854', 'word_count': 1630, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2593d627-ead5-5ea2-850b-98883e48f854'}, {'abstract': 'The effects of light on melatonin, which regulates our internal clocks, and our overall health are just beginning to be explored.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/health/05light.html', 'snippet': 'The effects of light on melatonin, which regulates our internal clocks, and our overall health are just beginning to be explored.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just as the ear has two purposes — hearing and telling you which way is up — so does the eye. It receives the input necessary for vision, but the retina also houses a network of sensors that detect the rise and fall of daylight. With light, the body sets its internal clock to a 24-hour cycle regulating an estimated 10 percent of our genes.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/05/science/05light/LIGHT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 922, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/05/science/05light/05light-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/05/science/05light/05light-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Eyes, a Clock Calibrated by Wavelengths of Light', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Eyes, a Clock Calibrated by Wavelengths of Light', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Light Bulbs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Melatonin (Hormone)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fluorescent Bulbs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-04T20:15:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laura Beil', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laura', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beil', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03e2b085-dd56-5dde-9fee-fedefb7c117f', 'word_count': 1119, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03e2b085-dd56-5dde-9fee-fedefb7c117f'}, {'abstract': 'A new study of twins released online on Monday marked an important shift in thinking about the causes of autism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/health/research/05autism.html', 'snippet': 'A new study of twins released online on Monday marked an important shift in thinking about the causes of autism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new study of twins suggests that environmental factors, including conditions in the womb, may be at least as important as genes in causing autism. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Study Implicates Environmental Factors in Autism', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Autism Study Finds Link to Environment', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Autism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Twins', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-