ht on weapons innovation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/science/05bomb.html', 'snippet': 'A trove of photographs reveals the casual approach to designing weapons that prevailed at Lawrence Livermore National Laboratory in the 1950s, and sheds light on weapons innovation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1952 the physicist Ernest O. Lawrence assembled a group of young scientists to design weapons that were radically different from those being designed at Los Alamos National Laboratory in New Mexico, the nation’s original nuclear weapons lab.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/05/science/05bomb/05bomb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 357, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/05/science/05bomb/05bomb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 357}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/05/science/05bomb/05bomb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/05/science/05bomb/05bomb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/05/science/05bomb/05bomb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Laid-Back in the Lab, Maybe, but They Spurred the Weapons Race', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Laid-Back in the Lab, Maybe, but They Spurred the Weapons Race', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photogra