'}, {'abstract': 'The New Haarlem Arts Theater makes its debut with a difficult James Baldwin drama from 1964.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/theater/reviews/blues-for-mister-charlie-by-james-baldwin-review.html', 'snippet': 'The New Haarlem Arts Theater makes its debut with a difficult James Baldwin drama from 1964.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Give credit where it’s due. In inaugurating its debut season with James Baldwin’s rarely staged play “Blues for Mister Charlie,” New Haarlem Arts Theater hardly played it safe. (Its second show, a revival of the toe-tapping revue “It Ain’t Nothin’ but the Blues” opening later this month, is another matter.) If theater were an Olympic sport, the degree of difficulty on display would earn New Haarlem several points, although not quite enough to offset the spotty execution.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/05/arts/Blues-1/Blues-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 889, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/05/arts/Blues-1/Blues-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/05/arts/Blues-1/Blues-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Murder, an Arrest and Racial Tensions', 'kicker': "Theater Review | 'Blues for Mister Charlie'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Murder, an Arrest and Racial Tensions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Haarlem Arts Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baldwin, James', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 