rk', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/fa747ecb-e147-5a84-a769-1c32742181ec', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/fa747ecb-e147-5a84-a769-1c32742181ec'}, {'abstract': 'The National Education Association on Monday affirmed for the first time that evidence of student learning must be considered in the evaluations of school teachers around the country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/us/05teachers.html', 'snippet': 'The National Education Association on Monday affirmed for the first time that evidence of student learning must be considered in the evaluations of school teachers around the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — Catching up to the reality already faced by many of its members, the nation’s largest teachers’ union on Monday affirmed for the first time that evidence of student learning must be considered in the evaluations of school teachers around the country.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Union Shifts Position on Teacher Evaluations', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Union Shifts Position On Teacher Evaluations', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Performance Evaluations (Labor)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Education Assn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests and Examinations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T01:57:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sharon Otterman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sharon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Otterman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8026d053-dc02-5405-a849-98c6cacb86bb', 'word_count': 1072, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8026d053-dc02-5405-a849-98c6cacb86bb'}, {'abstract': 'In the past two years at Dodger Stadium, the Mets have encountered more than their share of injuries.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/04/for-mets-los-angeles-holds-painful-memories/', 'snippet': 'In the past two years at Dodger Stadium, the Mets have encountered more than their share of injuries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Jason Bay sat at his locker Monday and went over the details of the season-ending injury he sustained at Dodger Stadium last year. While playing left field, Bay crashed into the bullpen fence and fell to the ground with a concussion that was not diagnosed until two days later.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mets Turn Bad Memories Around', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bay, Jason', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Collins, Terry L', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Ike', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reyes, Jose', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Dodgers', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T01:58:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cdee8b42-63c1-59c5-be7b-1c5b0436e2dc', 'word_count': 918, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cdee8b42-63c1-59c5-be7b-1c5b0436e2dc'}, {'abstract': 'Andrea Carla Michaels and Johanna Fenimore bring on the wordplay, and O, do they make us laugh.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/04/lanai/', 'snippet': 'Andrea Carla Michaels and Johanna Fenimore bring on the wordplay, and O, do they make us laugh.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TUESDAY’S PUZZLE — Well, this one just tickled me. The visuals evoked by the wordplay here are just great, and there were even a few entries that seemed like they were directed just at me, although there’s no way that Andrea Carla Michaels and Johanna Fenimore could have known that. That’s one of the nice things about puzzles. You never know when a word or phrase will trigger a particularly strong memory.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tuesday: Lanai Ladies', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T02:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef630928-392d-5139-ba47-32edcea26f2a', 'word_count': 529, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef630928-392d-5139-ba47-32edcea26f2a'}, {'abstract': 'The Yankees broke through with their first hits of the game in the seventh, taking a two-run lead that A. J. Burnett quickly turned into a 4-2 deficit in the bottom of the inning.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/sports/baseball/burnett-cools-just-as-yankees-offense-warms-up.html', 'snippet': 'The Yankees broke through with their first hits of the game in the seventh, taking a two-run lead that A. J. Burnett quickly turned into a 4-2 deficit in the bottom of the inning.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CLEVELAND — Of all the things that can happen on a baseball diamond, perhaps nothing infuriates A. J. Burnett more than his failure to preserve a lead. The circumstances are irrelevant; it is his job, and his only job, to uphold the covenant between a pitcher and his teammates, particularly in the sort of low-scoring game that developed Monday night.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/05/sports/subYANKEES1/subYANKEES1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/05/sports/subYANKEES1/subYANKEES1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/05/sports/subYANKEES1/subYANKEES1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Burnett Cools Just as Yanks Warm Up', 'kicker': 'Indians 6, Yankees 3', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Burnett Cools Just as Yanks Warm Up', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cleveland Indians', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burnett, A J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jeter, Derek', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T02:01:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1eae67da-e59d-5595-93e4-34cf7643c8e8', 'word_count': 865, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1eae67da-e59d-5595-93e4-34cf7643c8e8'}, {'abstract': 'Is the Republican Party so blinded by its tax-rate fixation that it misses the chance to exchange a few revenue increases for huge spending cuts?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/opinion/05brooks.html', 'snippet': 'Is the Republican Party so blinded by its tax-rate fixation that it misses the chance to exchange a few revenue increases for huge spending cuts?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Republicans have changed American politics since they took control of the House of Representatives. They have put spending restraint and debt reduction at the top of the national agenda. They have sparked a discussion on entitlement reform. They have turned a bill to raise the debt limit into an opportunity to put the U.S. on a stable fiscal course.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': '