 debt ceiling, Republicans now say they want a balanced budget amendment to the Constitution.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/opinion/05tue1.html', 'snippet': 'In addition to demanding spending cuts in exchange for raising the debt ceiling, Republicans now say they want a balanced budget amendment to the Constitution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Congressional Republicans have opened a new front in the deficit wars. In addition to demanding trillions of dollars in spending cuts in exchange for raising the nation’s debt limit, they are now vowing not to act without first holding votes in each chamber on a balanced budget amendment to the Constitution. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Folly in the Debt Limit Talks', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'More Folly in the Debt Limit Talks: Republicans now say they want a balanced budget amendment, too', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitutional Amendments', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitution (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T02:15:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ead486e1-d610-5be1-b645-88009482ddf5', 'word_count': 583, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ead486e1-d610-5be1-b645-88009482ddf5'}, {'abstract': 'In a fractious free-for-all, rival hackers engage in tit-for-tat attacks on each other, often for no better reason than to outwit the other guy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/technology/05hack.html', 'snippet': 'In a fractious free-for-all, rival hackers engage in tit-for-tat attacks on each other, often for no better reason than to outwit the other guy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The hackers, calling themselves the A-Team, assembled a trove of private information and put it online for all to see: names, aliases, addresses, phone numbers, even details about family members and girlfriends. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hackers Select a New Target: Other Hackers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hackers Select A New Target: Other Hackers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hackers (Computers)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lulz Security', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T02:15:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Somini Sengupta and Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Somini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sengupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/01433ec8-4569-586b-a9ef-fa0bfdf1ccde', 'word_count': 1087, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01433ec8-4569-586b-a9ef-fa0bfdf1ccde'}, {'abstract': 'Television set-top boxes are not really off when you think they are off.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/opinion/05tue2.html', 'snippet': 'Television set-top boxes are not really off when you think they are off.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Energy Department chimed in at just the right time when it announced that it might issue energy conservation requirements for cable boxes, digital recorders and the like. A voluntary conservation program run by the Environmental Protection Agency may not be enough to generate a commitment to energy efficiency among the companies that provide these power-hungry boxes.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/opinion/08fixesscreenshot/08fixesscreenshot-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 691, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Power-Hungry Devices', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Power-Hungry Devices: Television set-top boxes are not really off when you think they are off', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Energy Efficiency', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cable Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Digital Video Recorders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T02:21:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2c87d0b-a605-5be3-81db-2311e51dd81d', 'word_count': 364, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2c87d0b-a605-5be3-81db-2311e51dd81d'}, {'abstract': 'The Web search company is too important to most people’s Internet experience for regulators not to examine its behavior.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/opinion/05tue3.html', 'snippet': 'The Web search company is too important to most people’s Internet experience for regulators not to examine its behavior.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Federal Trade Commission’s decision to open an investigation into potential anticompetitive or deceptive practices at Google is a welcome move. While the Internet company has been a leader in innovation, giving consumers exciting new choices online, the public’s interest lies in ensuring fair competition in this fast-changing arena. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Investigating Google', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Investigating Google', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antitrust Laws and Competition Issues', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Trade Commission', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Android (Operating System)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Skyhook Wireless', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T02:23:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/dcc2e644-bb8b-5930-ba86-cbdc150777fd', 'word_count': 327, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dcc2e644-bb8b-5930-ba86-cbdc150777fd'}, {'abstract': 'Now that the governor has ordered special elections, party leaders, not the people, will get to choose the candidates to run for a House seat and six State Assembly seats.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/opinion/05tue4.html', 'snippet': 'Now that the governor has ordered special elections, party leaders, not the people, will get to choose the candidates to run for a House seat and six State Assembly seats.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Andrew Cuomo on Friday called for special elections on Sept. 13 to fill Anthony Weiner’s Congressional office and six vacant State Assembly seats. Party leaders will now get to choose the candidates to run. That is not the way a democracy is supposed to work. Unfortunately, it’s the way things are done in New York.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York’s Especially Undemocratic Elections', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New York’s Especially Undemocratic Elections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weiner, Anthony D', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crowley, Joseph', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T02:23:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/707b127b-317f-523d-9b55-1cf02b1e2ad9', 'word_count': 320, 'uri': 'nyt://article/707b127b-317f-523d-9b55-1cf02b1e2ad9'}, {'abstract': 'News of the World allegedly intercepted messages left for Milly Dowler, 13, and deleted them to make room for new ones, giving her family false hope.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/world/europe/05britain.html', 'snippet': 'News of the World allegedly intercepted messages left for Milly Dowler, 13, and deleted them to make room for new ones, giving her family false hope.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The voice-mail account of a British schoolgirl who went missing in 2002 and whose murdered body was discovered six months later was repeatedly hacked by the News of the World tabloid at a time