ill this week for what promises to be more saber rattling over the debt limit increase as well as debate over the role of the United States military in Libya and Afghanistan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Congressional Week Ahead: Debt Limit Deadline Approaches', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T12:31:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Hulse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hulse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/902b9d9e-08b1-5b8d-b08a-9be7e8dc5a49', 'word_count': 455, 'uri': 'nyt://article/902b9d9e-08b1-5b8d-b08a-9be7e8dc5a49'}, {'abstract': 'Family trees now have complex roots, new autism study implicates environmental factors, cancer scans can have false positive results and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/tuesday-reading-family-trees-now-have-complex-roots/', 'snippet': 'Family trees now have complex roots, new autism study implicates environmental factors, cancer scans can have false positive results and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and online in our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tuesday Reading: Family Trees Now Have Complex Roots', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T12:35:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1aa38aa-9142-52c6-af23-be0c8de4b7ae', 'word_count': 114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1aa38aa-9142-52c6-af23-be0c8de4b7ae'}, {'abstract': 'The private equity giant TPG Capital is acquiring a company that makes products which identify blood type and determine compatibility.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/tpg-capital-to-buy-immucor-for-1-97-billion/', 'snippet': 'The private equity giant TPG Capital is acquiring a company that makes products which identify blood type and determine compatibility.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Immucor, a maker of systems used in blood transfusions, said on Tuesday that it had agreed to be acquired by TPG Capital in a $1.97 billion deal. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'TPG to Buy Immucor for $1.97 Billion', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TPG Capital', 'rank': 3, '