By Clyde Haberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clyde', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed2fa3cd-74a4-5b29-8d50-e91ee30904ad', 'word_count': 974, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed2fa3cd-74a4-5b29-8d50-e91ee30904ad'}, {'abstract': 'Indeed.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/not-a-normal-party/', 'snippet': 'Indeed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My colleague David Brooks seems close to realizing what I realized a decade ago.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Not A Normal Party', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T12:43:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aeebbb40-e00e-52cd-8289-816f82edf19c', 'word_count': 40, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aeebbb40-e00e-52cd-8289-816f82edf19c'}, {'abstract': 'And nobody will admit it.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/liquidity-trapped/', 'snippet': 'And nobody will admit it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Brad DeLong has a nice piece for Bloomberg about the nature of the trap we’re in — and I’m only partly saying that because he gives me credit for warning about this very trap back in the 1990s.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Liquidity Trapped', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T12:58:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf4a0dcb-561b-5428-adfd-44b55a3211ed', 'word_count': 275, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf4a0dcb-561b-5428-adfd-44b55a3211ed'}, {'abstract': 'A Los Angeles television station has partnered with a tech startup to use location data from smartphones to track the effects of a major highway closure.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/phone-data-to-give-a-picture-of-traffic-disaster-in-l-a/', 'snippet': 'A Los Angeles television station has partnered with a tech startup to use location data from smartphones to track the effects of a major highway closure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chaos is expected to descend on Los Angeles on July 16, when a 10-mile stretch of I-405, a major highway running through the center of town that carries an average of 500,000 cars on a summer weekend, shuts down for more than two days.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Phone Data to Give a Picture of Traffic Shutdown in L.A.', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roads and Traffic', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'KABC-TV', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Waze Mobile', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T13:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joshua Brustein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joshua', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brustein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c52bc76c-d692-5309-b377-02aeb20206f5', 'word_count': 484, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c52bc76c-d692-5309-b377-02aeb20206f5'}, {'abstract': 'Turkey’s largest city is developing its tourism sector at lighting speed, opening a slew of flashy restaurants, notable galleries and stylish hotels.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/euro-zone-istanbul-on-the-upswing/', 'snippet': 'Turkey’s largest city is developing its tourism sector at lighting speed, opening a slew of flashy restaurants, notable galleries and stylish hotels.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Turkey inches its way toward the European Union (the E.U. recognized Istanbul as Capital of Culture last year), the country’s largest city is developing its tourism sector at lighting speed, opening a slew of flashy restaurants, notable galleries and stylish hotels. If you’re planning a visit this summer, make note of cultural happenings like the International Jazz Festival (July 1-19), with the headliners Paul Simon and Joss Stone, and the International Opera Festival (July 1-21), featuring open-air performances of Puccini’s “Tosca” and Mozart’s unfinished opus, “Zaide.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Euro Zone | Istanbul on the Upswing', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T13:00:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rocky Casale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rocky', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Casale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/94320baa-03cc-50fe-bd42-c28345a87a1