, 'word_count': 196, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59a29a82-b14d-5797-a002-71c689835ed8'}, {'abstract': 'Rebekah Brooks, the former editor of The News of the World who is now chief executive of the British newspaper division of the News Corporation, wrote on Monday that “it is inconceivable” that she knew that articles on a missing schoolgirl were based on intercepted voice-mail messages.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/former-editor-denies-knowing-that-missing-girls-phone-was-hacked/', 'snippet': 'Rebekah Brooks, the former editor of The News of the World who is now chief executive of the British newspaper division of the News Corporation, wrote on Monday that “it is inconceivable” that she knew that articles on a missing schoolgirl were ba...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last Updated | 5:23 p.m. In response to the allegation that journalists at a British tabloid, The News of the World, hacked into the voice-mail account of a missing schoolgirl in 2002, the paper’s former editor, who is now chief executive of the British newspaper division of Rupert Murdoch’s News Corporation, issued a statement in which she denied any knowledge of the affair.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Former Editor Denies Knowing That Missing Girl’s Phone Was Hacked', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wiretapping and Other Eavesdropping Devices and Methods', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NEWS CORP', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News of the World', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T13:36:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/13bd4899-215e-5753-b382-6e2f814c2150', 'word_count': 1278, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13bd4899-215e-5753-b382-6e2f814c2150'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/morning-take-out-278/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Energy Transfer Raises Southern Union Bid to $5.1 Billion | Energy Transfer Equity on Tuesday raised its bid to $5.1 billion for the natural gas pipeline operator Southern Union, seeking to beat out a rival, the Williams Companies.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Take-Out', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T13:59:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/79e61c42-fd63-56ff-b2fd-86b120397823', 'word_count': 1819, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79e61c42-fd63-56ff-b2fd-86b120397823'}, {'abstract': 'Campaigning in New Hampshire on Tuesday, Mitt Romney once again blamed President Obama for worsening the recession.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/romney-says-obama-made-things-worse/', 'snippet': 'Campaigning in New Hampshire on Tuesday, Mitt Romney once again blamed President Obama for worsening the recession.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WOLFEBORO, N.H. — Sounding very much like a general election candidate, former