b815143492a'}, {'abstract': 'Oil that spewed from an offshore drilling rig in northeastern China for more than two weeks last month spread 320 square miles, government officials acknowledged on Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/06/world/asia/06china.html', 'snippet': 'Oil that spewed from an offshore drilling rig in northeastern China for more than two weeks last month spread 320 square miles, government officials acknowledged on Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — Oil that spewed from an offshore drilling rig in northeastern China for two weeks last month has spread over 320 square miles, government officials acknowledged Tuesday, amid public uproar over why it took so long for fishermen, local residents and environmental groups to be informed of the spill.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/world/asia/06chinamap/06chinamap-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 210, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'China Admits Extent of Spill From Oil Rig', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China Admits Extent of Spill From Oil Rig', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Offshore Drilling and Exploration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ConocoPhillips', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'China National Petroleum', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T15:27:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Jacobs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jacobs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/77eeb0ae-d0c4-523e-8818-6619c2b25fcf', 'word_count': 693, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77eeb0ae-d0c4-523e-8818-6619c2b25fcf'}, {'abstract': 'It shouldn’t have happened, so it didn’t.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/inconceivabilities/', 'snippet': 'It shouldn’t have happened, so it didn’t.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dean Baker is upset at a story that describes Argentina’s economy as “stagnant”. Actually,this sort of thing is quite common — and not just about Argentina. I’ve often found that when things happen that aren’t supposed to happen according to the prevailing economic or political orthodoxy, reporting quite often describes what “should” have happened, not what actually happened.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Inconceivabilities', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T15:28:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df6fa9a4-0e70-5f5d-8080-da8bfcdeff68', 'word_count': 213, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df6fa9a4-0e70-5f5d-8080-da8bfcdeff68'}, {'abstract': 'Another day of runway looks, another Scorecard at your service.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/scorecard-giambattista-valli-wins/', 'snippet': 'Another day of runway looks, another Scorecard at your service.', 'lead_paragraph': 'And Scorecard‘s back from our fashion hiatus! In Paris, Independence Day — err, we mean the first day of the couture shows — was marked by a series of new beginnings. At the storied house of Christian Dior, studio director Bill Gaytten tried his hand with an exuberant display at least in part inspired by Postwar architecture, but it’s safe to say that these prismatic creations failed to launch. Meanwhile, in the context of couture, the Chambre Syndicale’s newest guest member\xa0Giambattista Valli finally lit the critical spark.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Scorecard | Giambattista Valli Wins!', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T15:31:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alison S. Cohn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Cohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee9b5695-99ef-587a-9a9d-c2c1dfe13b8c', 'word_count': 1190, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee9b5695-99ef-587a-9a9d-c2c1dfe13b8c'}, {'abstract': 'Liquidity trap, banana, whatever.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/whats-in-a-name-reposted/', 'snippet': 'Liquidity trap, banana, whatever.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I suspect that it’s a good time to repost something I wrote early into our continuing liquidity trap (the reference to awesome Fed action was about the big lending operations of 2008-2009 — QE1 — not the modest actions of 2010-2011):', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s In A Name? Reposted', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T15:34:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a9f9ae3-b273-5360-938b-cebe37d7d960', 'word_count': 269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a9f9ae3-b273-5360-938b-cebe37d7d960'}, {'abstract': 'If you’re going to be in Paris this summer, make a point of seeing the Hussein Chalayan retrospective at Les Arts Décoratifs, which is part of the Louvre.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/a-hussein-chalayan-fix/', 'snippet': 'If you’re going to be in Paris this summer, make a point of seeing the Hussein Chalayan retrospective at Les Arts Décoratifs, which is part of the Louvre.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you’re going to be in Paris this summer, make a point of seeing the Hussein Chalayan retrospective at Les Arts Décoratifs, which is part of the Louvre. Mr. Chalayan worked on the exhibition with curator Pamela Golbin, and it includes important pieces from Mr. Chalayan’s remarkable career, as well as films and sketches.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Chalayan Fix', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T15:34:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d4528c7-b47e-551d-9de7-9b9b09ea3e82', 'word_count': 113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d4528c7-b47e-551d-9de7-9b9b09ea3e82'}, {'abstract': 'Well known in Paris since his days at Ungaro, Giambattista Valli presented his first haute couture collection the other night in the tiny Galerie de la Madeleine.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/mr-valli-are-you-ready-for-your-close-up/', 'snippet': 'Well known in Paris since his days at Ungaro, Giambattista Valli presented his first haute couture collection the other night in the tiny Galerie de la Madeleine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Well known in Paris since his days at Ungaro, Giambattista Valli presented his first haute couture collection the other night in the tiny Galerie de la Madeleine. His atelier and showroom are just upstairs; his ready-to-wear boutique is in the passage. In a matter of a few years he has staked out this small corner of the Right Bank.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mr. Valli, Are You Ready for Your Close-Up?', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Couture (Fashion)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Valli, Giambattista', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T15:35:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e856455-392c-5724-a332-1bccba7a597c', 'word_count': 151, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e856455-392c-5724-a332-1bccba7a597c'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Rick Perry’s criticisms of George W. Bush expose a long rivalry and the Republican Party’s rightward drift.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/06/us/politics/06perry.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Rick Perry’s criticisms of George W. Bush expose a long rivalry and the Republican Party’s rightward drift.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AUSTIN, Tex. — Gov. Rick Perry, a Republican contemplating a presidential run, shares many attributes with the last man who ran for president from here, his predecessor and onetime patron, George W. Bush. He has the same straight-legged Texas swagger; the down-home, clipped speaking style; the desert-baked conservatism.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/us/jp-PERRY/jp-PERRY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/06/us/jp-PERRY/jp-PERRY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/us/jp-PERRY/jp-PERRY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 765, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/us/jp-PERRY/jp-PERRY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/06/us/jp-PERRY/jp-PERRY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Perry Breaks With a Fellow Texan: Bush', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Perry’s Rift With Bush Could Hold Peril in a Presidential Race', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T15:38:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Rutenberg and Jeff Zeleny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rutenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zeleny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6880ecd-1772-50d9-8bc8-54d3f41e949b', 'word_count': 1171, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6880ecd-1772-50d9-8bc8-54d3f41e949b'}, {'abstract': 'The F. M. Light store survived the Great Depression in the 1930s, and the coming of Wal-Mart in the early ‘90s, and the founder’s family still provides an anchor for the community.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/06/us/06clan.html', 'snippet': 'The F. M. Light store survived the Great Depression in the 1930s, and the coming of Wal-Mart in the early ‘90s, and the founder’s family still provides an anchor for the community.', 'lead_paragraph': 'STEAMBOAT SPRINGS, Colo. — Frank and Carrie Light and their eight children came here around 1900 to what was just a wide spot of a few hundred people. Then the town’s story and the family’s got intertwined. Now it is hard to tell where one begins and the other leaves off.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/us/06clan_span/06clan_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/06/us/06clan_span/06clan_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/us/06clan_span/06clan_span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/us/06clan_span/06clan_span-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/06/us/06clan_span/06clan_span-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Clan and a Colorado Town, Long Thriving as One', 'kicker': 'Steamboat Springs Journal ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Family Still a Vital Part of a Colorado Town’s Fabric', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Steamboat Springs (Colo)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T15:44:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kirk Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kirk', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/098ea4c9-11ce-5d69-bd95-81829f8c3117', 'word_count': 886, 'uri': 'nyt://article/098ea4c9-11ce-5d69-bd95-81829f8c3117'}, {'abstract': 'The move to Federal District Court from United States Bankruptcy Court could result in the dismissal of some lawsuits against prominent banks and limit the amount the Madoff trustee, Irving H. Picard, can recover for investors.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/in-shift-to-new-court-risks-for-madoff-trustees-case/', 'snippet': 'The move to Federal District Court from United States B