kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Europe, a Move to Slash Phone Roaming Charges', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Commission', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cellular Telephones', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T16:26:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': "By Kevin J. O'Brien", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': "O'Brien", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d12847bb-a74f-5e1f-b70d-619f4752e332', 'word_count': 1218, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d12847bb-a74f-5e1f-b70d-619f4752e332'}, {'abstract': 'As the number of mixed-race people grows in the United States, writers and artists are challenging assumptions about identity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/06/arts/mixed-race-writers-and-artists-raise-their-profiles.html', 'snippet': 'As the number of mixed-race people grows in the United States, writers and artists are challenging assumptions about identity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For years Heidi W. Durrow heard the refrain: editors wouldn’t publish her novel because readers couldn’t relate to a protagonist who was part black and part Danish. But when that novel, “The Girl Who Fell From the Sky,” was finally published last year (after about four dozen rejections, said Ms. Durrow, who is, of course, black and Danish), the coming-of-age story landed on best-seller lists.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/arts/Mixed/Mixed-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/arts/Mixed/Mixed-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/06/arts/Mixed/Mixed-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pushing Boundaries, Mixed-Race Artists Gain Notice', 'kicker': 'Race Remixed', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mixed-Race Artists Court Higher-Profile Projects', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Durrow, Heidi W', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Senna, Danzy', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T16:34:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicia R. Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicia', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c915ca19-952c-5f77-a27b-df23b0783395', 'word_count': 1472, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c915ca19-952c-5f77-a27b-df23b0783395'}, {'abstract': 'The production, at the Stratford Shakespeare Festival, begins previews later this month.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/illness-knocks-brian-bedford-out-of-the-misanthrope/', 'snippet': 'The production, at the Stratford Shakespeare Festival, begins previews later this month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Visitors to the Stratford Shakespeare Festival in Canada who were hoping to catch Brian Bedford playing Oronte in “The Misanthrope” this summer will be disappointed. The actor, who has performed at the festival since the mid-1970s, has dropped out because of unspecified medical reasons, according a spokeswoman for the festival. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Illness Knocks Brian Bedford Out of ‘The Misanthrope’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stratford Shakespeare Festival', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tony Awards (Theater Awards)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bedford, Brian', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mcanuff, Des', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T16:39:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2e288e2-ded4-5729-a7cf-e41a8d43f8a2', 'word_count': 162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2e288e2-ded4-5729-a7cf-e41a8d43f8a2'}, {'abstract': 'Scanning the track list at Pitchfork, in anticipation of Patti Smith’s best-of collection, “Outside Society, I was reminded of how much I loved her National Book Award-winning memoir, “Just Kids.”', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/punk-priestess-still-reigns/', 'snippet': 'Scanning the track list at Pitchfork, in anticipation of Patti Smith’s best-of collection, “Outside Society, I was reminded of how much I loved her National Book Award-winning memoir, “Just Kids.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scanning the track list at\xa0Pitchfork, in anticipation of Patti Smith’s best-of collection, “Outside Society,” I was reminded of how much I loved her National Book Award-winning memoir, “Just Kids.” It describes her early years in working-class Philadelphia, life with Robert Mapplethorpe at the Chelsea Hotel, dating Sam Shepard, Max’s Kansas City, becoming a wife and mother in Detroit. It’s not just that she’s incredibly cool, effortlessly glamorous in her own raw-edged way, but that she writes so beautifully and incredibly movingly about her love for Robert, both when it was sexual and after it had, for the most part, ceased to be:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Punk Priestess Still Reigns', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Patti', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T16:39:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sheila Glaser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sheila', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glaser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/942bec2e-eb27-5ff8-a7c4-e136d9ee020e', 'word_count': 184, 'uri': 'nyt://article/942bec2e-eb27-5ff8-a7c4-e136d9ee020e'}, {'abstract': 'The timeless Jack Purcell sneaker gets another update, this time in the hands of the über-cool retailer Aloha Rag.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/step-into-aloha-rag-for-converse/', 'snippet': 'The timeless Jack Purcell sneaker gets another update, this time in the hands of the über-cool retailer Aloha Rag.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The timeless Jack Purcell sneaker gets another update, this time in the hands of the über-cool retailer Aloha Rag. Launching today as part of Aloha Rag’s 20th anniversary, the Aloha Rag for Converse Jack Purcell Zip shoe remains true to Converse’s classic look but is given a bit of edginess. Featuring a calf-leather interior, embroidered skull-and-hearts logo, and zip tongue, the sneaker exudes the owner Tatsugo Yoda’s aesthetic, which combines punk style with nods to luxury. Only 150 pairs will be made available at Aloha Rag stores in New York and Honolulu and on its Web site.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Step Into | Aloha Rag for Converse', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sneakers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Converse Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T16:40:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Tudela', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tudela', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c045c146-11d9-5afe-92e8-80280fa202d8', 'word_count': 108, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c045c146-11d9-5afe-92e8-80280fa202d8'}, {'abstract': 'Andy Pettitte, who was for years a friend and teammate of Roger Clemens, is a key witness in Clemens’s perjury trial, which begins this week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/06/sports/baseball/clemens-goes-on-trial-for-perjury-with-pettitte-as-key-witness.html', 'snippet': 'Andy Pettitte, who was for years a friend and teammate of Roger Clemens, is a key witness in Clemens’s perjury trial, which begins this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One crucial notion setting Roger Clemens’s case apart from other drug scandals involving baseball stars is that his former close friend and loyal teammate Andy Pettitte, a man Clemens considered his little brother, could be the most damaging witness against him.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/sports/06Pettitte1_cnd/06Pettitte1_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/06/sports/06Pettitte1_cnd/06Pettitte1_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/sports/06Pettitte1_cnd/06Pettitte1_cnd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 706, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/sports/06Pettitte1_cnd/06Pettitte1_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/06/sports/06Pettitte1_cnd/06Pettitte1_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Best Friend and Ex-Teammate to Confront Clemens at Trial', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Best Friend and Ex-Teammate To Confront Clemens at Trial', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pettitte, Andy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doping (Sports)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'na