'uri': 'nyt://article/9892e50a-1b8a-5bea-98e5-6cac382bfc96'}, {'abstract': 'Haunted by the memories of a crackdown a generation ago, Hama has emerged as a potent challenge to President Bashar al-Assad.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/06/world/middleeast/06syria.html', 'snippet': 'Haunted by the memories of a crackdown a generation ago, Hama has emerged as a potent challenge to President Bashar al-Assad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — Fired up with zeal, activists say they have set up dozens of checkpoints in the Syrian city of Hama, alerting neighborhood groups with cries of “God is great” to the approach of feared security forces and throwing up barricades of burning tires and trash bins to block their path. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Restive City of Hama Tests Will of Syrian Government', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Restive City of Hama Tests Will of Syrian Government', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T18:41:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Shadid', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shadid', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id':