ction an homage to Japan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Giorgio Armani called his fall haute couture collection an homage to Japan. The designer who helped liberate women from boring executive wear and floppy bow ties confined his homage to traditional Japanese costumes and feminine floral patterns. There was no Goth Lolita moment or anything you might associate with Tokyo street fashion of the last 20 years. He stuck to a silhouette seemingly drawn from the kimono and obi (translated as stiff black patent leather bodices), and one or two models were slowed to a mincing gait. The prints and embroideries were lavish, but as Armani collections go, it was an island unto itself. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Armani Privé: Foreign States', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T19:07:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eebcee19-4c59-5f86-80a2-080281ee1e64', 'word_count': 105, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eebcee19-4c59-5f86-80a2-080281ee1e64'}, {'abstract': 'With kimonos and geishas for inspiration, Giorgio Armani presented a beautiful collection for Privé today, one of his finest since launching the haute couture line 6 years ago.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/just-one-look-giorgio-armani/', 'snippet': 'With kimonos and geishas for inspiration, Giorgio Armani presented a beautiful collection for Privé today, one of his finest since launching the haute couture line 6 years ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With kimonos and geishas for inspiration, Giorgio Armani presented a beautiful collection for Privé today, one of his finest since launching the haute couture line 6 years ago. Black velvet trouser suits lined and outlined in Japanese floral silks were a perfect mash up of his/hers and east/west, and yet linear, untricksy, and exquisite. The evening dresses were columnar, often obi’d, and with a hint of plissé or a jacquard petticoat dusting the floor. Here, a big night stunner with sequined bodice, velvet skirt (cut narrow as trousers) and hints of vivid floral silk.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Giorgio Armani', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T19:10:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sally Singer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sally', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Singer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/308c18b8-012f-5b8a-bda5-e4680266a1e9', 'word_count': 101, 'uri': 'nyt://article/308c18b8-012f-5b8a-bda5-e4680266a1e9'}, {'abstract': 'Sarah Huckabee Sanders, the daughter and top political adviser to Mike Huckabee, the former governor of Arkansas, has joined Tim Pawlenty’s presidential campaign as a senior adviser.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/huckabees-daughter-to-join-pawlenty-campaign/', 'snippet': 'Sarah Huckabee Sanders, the daughter and top political adviser to Mike Huckabee, the former governor of Arkansas, has joined Tim Pawlenty’s presidential campaign as a senior adviser.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sarah Huckabee Sanders, the daughter and top political adviser to Mike Huckabee, the former governor of Arkansas, has joined Tim Pawlenty’s presidential campaign as a senior adviser, the campaign announced Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Huckabee’s Daughter to Join Pawlenty Campaign', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pawlenty, Tim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T19:10:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/47a73e51-453f-53ff-ba1c-53a9c126cd2f', 'word_count': 231, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47a73e51-453f-53ff-ba1c-53a9c126cd2f'}, {'abstract': 'A series of articles alleging that the housekeeper at the Sofitel also worked as a prostitute draw legal action.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/strauss-kahn-accuser-sues-n-y-post-charging-libel/', 'snippet': 'A series of articles alleging that the housekeeper at the Sofitel also worked as a prostitute draw legal action.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The hotel housekeeper in the Dominique Strauss-Kahn case filed a libel suit against The New York Post on Tuesday over a series of articles it published during the Fourth of July weekend claiming that she was a prostitute.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Strauss-Kahn Accuser Files Libel Suit Against N.Y. Post', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Libel and Slander', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strauss-Kahn, Dominique', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Post', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T19:12:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/48cb1e5f-eb73-5c95-b180-d7ea83b8c528', 'word_count': 548, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48cb1e5f-eb73-5c95-b180-d7ea83b8c528'}, {'abstract': 'Intense demand for lawyers with large, established books of business has led corporate law firms to recruit them more aggressively and offer record pay packages.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/more-law-firms-raid-competitors-to-poach-rainmakers/', 'snippet': 'Intense demand for lawyers with large, established books of business has led corporate law firms to recruit them more aggressively and offer record pay packages.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The job of unwinding Bernard L. Madoff’s huge fraud and recovering money for its victims has been lucrative, reaping hundreds of millions of dollars in legal fees. Late last year, a New Jersey law firm tried to poach the legal team handling that assignment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Law Firms Raid Competitors to Poach Rainmakers', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Madoff, Bernard L', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Picard, Irving H', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T19:13:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/02e3bbed-65bd-58d2-9545-d7a8d8ce470c', 'word_count': 1188, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02e3bbed-65bd-58d2-9545-d7a8d8ce470c'}, {'abstract': 'School districts across the country are gutting summer-school programs, cramming classes into four-day weeks or lopping days off the school year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/06/education/06time.html', 'snippet': 'School districts across the country are gutting summer-school programs, cramming classes into four-day weeks or lopping days off the school year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After several years of state and local budget cuts, thousands of school districts across the nation are gutting summer-school programs, cramming classes into four-day weeks or lopping days off the school year, even though virtually everyone involved in education agrees that American students need more instruction time.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/us/TIME/TIME-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/06/us/TIME/TIME-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/us/TIME/TIME-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/us/TIME/TIME-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_nam