 None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f3c3511-69d4-514d-9f51-6df7d01f1be2', 'word_count': 261, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f3c3511-69d4-514d-9f51-6df7d01f1be2'}, {'abstract': 'Although venture capital and private equity are often regarded as the same, they have different operational methods, which became apparent in Silver Lake’s sale of Skype to Microsoft.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/in-silicon-valley-a-culture-clash-sullies-a-romance/', 'snippet': 'Although venture capital and private equity are often regarded as the same, they have different operational methods, which became apparent in Silver Lake’s sale of Skype to Microsoft.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Private equity has broken venture capital’s heart, and V.C. is not taking it well.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Silicon Valley, a Culture Clash Sullies a Romance', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venture Capital', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Silver Lake Partners', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Skype Technologies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Silicon Valley (Calif)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T19:34:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Davidoff Solomon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': 'Davidoff', 'lastname': 'Solomon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa0b3253-3285-51ad-934a-aa0dc468ff4f', 'word_count': 1207, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa0b3253-3285-51ad-934a-aa0dc468ff4f'}, {'abstract': 'What mother…thinks of a hunger strike when gazing into her newborn baby’s eyes and whispering, “I would do anything for you?”', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/the-imprisoned-hikers-moms/', 'snippet': 'What mother…thinks of a hunger strike when gazing into her newborn baby’s eyes and whispering, “I would do anything for you?”', 'lead_paragraph': 'This month marks two years of worry for the parents of Josh Fattal and Shane Bauer, who, along with Shane’s fiancée, Sarah Shourd, were imprisoned by the Iranian government in July 2009, accused of crossing the border illegally. Writing about them won’t end their families’ worry. But it’s all I can do to show another parent that I can’t pretend to imagine their pain. (For more on their story, read Nick Kristof’s blog posts over the years, here, and here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Imprisoned Hikers’ Moms', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T19:38:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Belkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/221b3a82-821a-523e-9721-c9c5ad1039f7', 'word_count': 761, 'uri': 'nyt://article/221b3a82-821a-523e-9721-c9c5ad1039f7'}, {'abstract': 'Pyeongchang, South Korea; Munich; and Annecy, France, are the candidates on which International Olympic Committee delegates will vote Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/06/sports/ioc-to-vote-on-host-for-2018-winter-games.html', 'snippet': 'Pyeongchang, South Korea; Munich; and Annecy, France, are the candidates on which International Olympic Committee delegates will vote Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The host city for the 2018 Games will be chosen Wednesday by the International Olympic Committee among candidates from South Korea, Germany and France.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/sports/06olympic-span/06olympic-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/06/sports/06olympic-span/06olympic-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/sports/06olympic-span/06olympic-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 704, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/sports/06olympic-span/06olympic-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/06/sports/06olympic-span/06olympic-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mix of Old and New in Bids for 2018 Winter Games', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'It’s Old vs. New in Bids for 2018 Games', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Munich (Germany)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2018)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Annecy (France)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pyeongchang (South Korea)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Olympic Committee', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T19:40:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeré Longman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeré', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Longman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/104c6447-99b0-5e0b-a3b4-26f922987b8f', 'word_count': 782, 'uri': 'nyt://article/104c6447-99b0-5e0b-a3b4-26f922987b8f'}, {'abstract': 'From fireworks to fireflies, the Times articles, essays, slide shows and videos in our list explore the pleasures of summer, and encourage a little learning on the side.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/celebrate-summer-ideas-for-teaching-the-season/', 'snippet': 'From fireworks to fireflies, the Times articles, essays, slide shows and videos in our list explore the pleasures of summer, and encourage a little learning on the side.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Learning Network is taking it slow this month, and we hope you are too — though of course we can’t help but encourage a bit of learning as you go.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Celebrate Summer: Ideas for Teaching the Season', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T19:40:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/79a677b0-b259-57b7-90aa-4ec5b5e6701b', 'word_count': 825, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79a677b0-b259-57b7-90aa-4ec5b5e6701b'}, {'abstract': 'The Givenchy couture collection consisted of just 10 outfits, all in white or off-white, with minimal touches of gold, and each far from the everyday, as you expect of couture.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/earth-angels/', 'snippet': 'The Givenchy couture collection consisted of just 10 outfits, all in white or off-white, with minimal touches of gold, and each far from the everyday, as you expect of couture.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Givenchy couture collection on Tuesday consisted of just 10 outfits, all in white or off-white, with minimal touches of gold, and each far from the everyday, as you expect of couture. The mostly long dresses or delicate tops and boleros were made in fragile tulle and lace embroidered with clusters of tiny knots, caviar beads and feathers. Some styles were bareback. Evening bags covered in superlong silk fringe and mounted on hidden stands made at least a few Americans say: “Oh, sweet. It’s Cousin Itt.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Earth Angels', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Couture (Fashion)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Givenchy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T19:44:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a0ff9dfb-f536-5828-ac06-3d5dffd91177', 'word_count': 88, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a0ff9dfb-f536-5828-ac06-3d5dffd91177'}, {'abstract': 'Gary Player will join Arnold Palmer and Jack Nicklaus at the 2012 Masters as an honorary starter.', 'web_url': 'https://onpar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/masters-dream-threesome-player-palmer-and-nicklaus/', 'snippet': 'Gary Player will join Arnold Palmer and Jack Nicklaus at the 2012 Masters as an honorary starter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Big Three will be reunited at the 2012 Masters, Augusta National Golf Club announced Tuesday. Gary Player will make his debut as an honorary starter next year at Augusta, joining Arnold Palmer and Jack Nicklaus on the first tee to fire the opening shots in the popular Thursday ceremony that is the official opening of the tournament.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Masters’ Dream Threesome: Player, Palmer and Nicklaus', 'kicker': 'On Par', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Masters Golf Tournament', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nicklaus, Jack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Palmer, Arnold', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Player, Gary', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T20:02:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Dorman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dorman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/145bcb32-20ae-5418-941a-4259c5f879ce', 'word_count': 129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/145bcb32-20ae-5418-941a-4259c5f879ce'}, {'abstract': 'As retail businesses try to locate near the 1 World Trade Center building, average asking rents in the area have risen by 36 percent since the spring of 2010.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/06/realestate/commercial/1-world-trade-center-progress-spurs-retail-revival.html', 'snippet': 'As retail businesses try to locate near the 1 World Trade Center building, average asking rents in the area have risen by 36 percent since the spring of 2010.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As 1 World Trade Center starts to claim a place on the Lower Manhattan skyline, the area’s retail scene is beginning to revive, with landlords raising rents in anticipation of thousands of new office workers, tourists and residents, commercial real estate experts said.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/realestate/06wtcPicB/06wtcPicB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/realestate/06wtcPicB/06wtcPicB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/06/realestate/06wtcPicB/06wtcPicB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rise of World Trade Center Spurs a Retail Revival', 'kicker': 'Square Feet', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rise of World Trade Center Spurs a Retail Revival', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': '1 World Trade Center (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Renting and Leasing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Trade Center (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Office Buildings and Commercial Properties', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T20:03:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'subsection_name': 'Commercial Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alison Gregor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gregor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a97cfa3-986e-5683-b601-f099135ef919', 'word_count': 1152, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a97cfa3-986e-5683-b601-f099135ef919'}, {'abstract': 'I’m as over Anthony Weiner as any of the rest of you, but as I was catching up on The Nation this weekend, I saw JoAnn Wypijewski’s byline on a story about him and felt compelled to read it.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/one-last-weiner/', 'snippet': 'I’m as over Anthony Weiner as any of the rest of you, but as I was catching up on The Nation this weekend, I saw JoAnn Wypijewski’s byline on a story about him and felt compelled to read it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m as over Anthony Weiner as any of the rest of you, but as I was catching up on The Nation this weekend, I saw JoAnn Wypijewski’s byline on an article about him and felt compelled to read it. JoAnn is one of my favorite journalists. She wrote a nice story for this magazine in 2004 about the disenchantment of black voters with the Democratic Party, but the one that I am most indebted to her for is the riveting account of Nushawn Williams, a young man who infected at least 13 women with H.I.V., which she wrote for Harper’s Magazine in 1998. (Not available free online, sorry. Worth buying a subscription to the magazine, trust me.). This is one of the finest magazine stories I’ve ever read, in part because it so beautifully and sensitively evokes the desperate straits of Jamestown, N.Y., my father’s hometown. Even without that personal connection, you’ll find it a deeply satisfying reading experience.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'One Last Weiner', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wypijewski, JoAnn', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T20:05:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hugo Lindgren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hugo', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lindgren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b5f3539-048e-5099-b216-5a4729967516', 'word_count': 317, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b5f3539-048e-5099-b216-5a4729967516'}, {'abstract': 'A new pro-Romney super PAC, Restore Our Future, announced on Tuesday that it had raised $12 million during the first six months of the year.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/independent-group-bolsters-romneys-fund-raising-totals/', 'snippet': 'A new pro-Romney super PAC, Restore Our Future, announced on Tuesday that it had raised $12 million during the first six months of the year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Mitt Romney, the former Massachusetts governor, releases his campaign fund-raising filings this month, he is expected to report somewhere south of $20 million in contributions for the second quarter of the year — more than any of his rivals for the Republican presidential nomination, but somewhat less than might be expected for the candidate who has built the most robust fund-raising operation in the G.O.P. field.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Independent Group Bolsters Romney’s Fund-Raising Totals', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Priorities USA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T20:15:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Confessore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Confessore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb496f49-98dc-5b69-b760-0189665ab421', 'word_count': 406, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb496f49-98dc-5b69-b760-0189665ab421'}, {'abstract': 'Kenneth L. Lay, the former chief executive of Enron who died of a heart attack five years ago, became the public symbol of executive wrongdoing and financial malfeasance. Why does that matter today?', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/looking-at-ken-lay-and-the-lack-of-financial-crisis-cases/', 'snippet': 'Kenneth L. Lay, the former chief executive of Enron who died of a heart attack five years ago, became the public symbol of executive wrongdoing and financial malfeasance. Why does that matter today?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kenneth L. Lay, the former chief executive of Enron, died of a heart attack five years ago today. The stunning news came a month after a Houston jury convicted him of securities fraud and three months before his scheduled sentencing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Looking at Ken Lay and the Lack of Financial Crisis Cases', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executives and Management', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Antonucci, Charles J Sr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Farkas, Lee B', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lay, Kenneth L', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Enron Corp', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T20:15:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d35b440f-83fc-5044-81db-f477f23e6fcd', 'word_count': 629, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d35b440f-83fc-5044-81db-f477f23e6fcd'}, {'abstract': 'The two-day event will feature “more than 20 bands and multitude of D.J.s,”  according to the Pitchfork Web site.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/pitchfork-plans-a-festival-in-paris/', 'snippet': 'The two-day event will feature “more than 20 bands and multitude of D.J.s,”  according to the Pitchfork Web site.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The folks who run the Pitchfork Music Festival — the influential three-day summer showcase of indie music in Chicago — have announced plans to stage a fall festival in Paris, headlined by the folk-rock group Bon Iver. The European festival is the latest milestone in Pitchfork’s remarkable rise as a force in the world of indie rock. Not only has this summer festival, now in its sixth year, become a must-go event for people interested in indie music, but the Web site of the same name has become one of the most prominent brands in online music journalism, widely seen as having the influence to pluck bands from obscurity and jump-start their careers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pitchfork Plans a Festival in Paris', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vernon, Justin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bon Iver', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pitchfork Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wild Beasts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T20:16:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e21a3fd-78f0-5883-b891-f57fd0c30ad3', 'word_count': 249, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e21a3fd-78f0-5883-b891-f57fd0c30ad3'}, {'abstract': 'When I wrote about shaken baby syndrome last winter for the magazine, a Canadian pathologist named Evan Matshes was working on intriguing new research that hadn’t yet been published.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/new-evidence-on-shaken-baby-syndrome/', 'snippet': 'When I wrote about shaken baby syndrome last winter for the magazine, a Canadian pathologist named Evan Matshes was working on intriguing new research that hadn’t yet been published.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I wrote about shaken baby syndrome last winter for the magazine, a Canadian pathologist named Evan Matshes was working on intriguing new research that hadn’t yet been published. Matshes’s paper is just out, in Academic Forensic Pathology, the journal of the National Association of Medical Examiners. It opens a new avenue of inquiry for this difficult and fraught diagnosis.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Evidence on Shaken Baby Syndrome', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forensic Science', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shaken Baby Syndrome', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T20:25:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily Bazelon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bazelon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/39274826-5bfa-5be2-acdb-dab2e26fc3a0', 'word_count': 865, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39274826-5bfa-5be2-acdb-dab2e26fc3a0'}, {'abstract': 'Unlike a number of New York barbecue joints, which emphasize the woodpile, Neely’s Barbecue Parlor conveys more gracious dining.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/neelys-bringing-barbecue-to-new-york/', 'snippet': 'Unlike a number of New York barbecue joints, which emphasize the woodpile, Neely’s Barbecue Parlor conveys more gracious dining.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pat Neely, along with his brothers, opened his first barbecue restaurant in Memphis in 1988. Their chainlet in Tennessee has expanded since then, involving Pat’s wife, Gina. The couple became Food Network stars three years ago, so now they are poised to make a grand entrance in New York. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Neely’s Barbecue Coming to New York', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Barbecue', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'p