ord_count': 225, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a076dc8d-8017-5c3a-a9c3-6005295a4106'}, {'abstract': 'Chicken simmered gently and well chilled provides a summer snack worthy of finger-licking nibbling or served with sesame oil, scallions, cilantro and jalapeño slices.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/06/dining/chicken-simmered-and-chilled-city-kitchen.html', 'snippet': 'Chicken simmered gently and well chilled provides a summer snack worthy of finger-licking nibbling or served with sesame oil, scallions, cilantro and jalapeño slices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TRUE confession: I love cold chicken. Cold roast chicken, cold fried chicken, a meaty cold chicken carcass for finger-licking nibbling. And during the long days of summer, I crave cold boiled chicken, brightened with hot pepper, sesame oil and scallions.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/dining/KITCH-1/KITCH-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 904, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/dining/KITCH-1/KITCH-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/06/dining/KITCH-1/KITCH-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chicken, Simmered and Chilled', 'kicker': 'City Kitchen', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chicken, Simmered and Chilled', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chickens', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T20:53:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Tanis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tanis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/87919e2e-fa5a-5d3c-9be2-92e6dcdc5ec9', 'word_count': 292, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87919e2e-fa5a-5d3c-9be2-92e6dcdc5ec9'}, {'abstract': 'Chinese boiled chicken gets better in the refrigerator.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/chicken-for-summer-cool-easy-and-exciting/', 'snippet': 'Chinese boiled chicken gets better in the refrigerator.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If the dog days have got you down, cold chicken might be the answer. This Chinese-inspired dish is served straight from the fridge, and only minimal cooking is required. Simmered gently with ginger and star anise, showered with scallions, hot pepper, and sesame —\xa0what’s not to like? What are some of your recipes for cold meals in hot weather?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chicken for Summer: Cool, Easy and Exciting', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T20:56:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Tanis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tanis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fee498f1-87cf-5870-a9a7-dd20fa55c3f9', 'word_count': 115, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fee498f1-87cf-5870-a9a7-dd20fa55c3f9'}, {'abstract': 'The Facing Change collective photographed the Fourth of July this year knowing that its work would be held and preserved for posterity by the Library of Congress.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/a-fourth-for-many-fourths-to-come/', 'snippet': 'The Facing Change collective photographed the Fourth of July this year knowing that its work would be held and preserved for posterity by the Library of Congress.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The subjects on Monday were timeless. There was a backyard barbecue, the National Mall, a neighborhood parade, the Liberty Bell, a swimming pool. And fireworks, of course.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Fourth, for Many Fourths to Come', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Archives and Records', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Independence Day (US) (July 4)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Library of Congress', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T20:58:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Estrin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Estrin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6deba076-9a03-5fba-ab70-bae075e28658', 'word_count': 451, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6deba076-9a03-5fba-ab70-bae075e28658'}, {'abstract': 'Energy Transfer Equity raised its bid for the natural gas pipeline operator to $5.1 billion on Tuesday, seeking to beat out a rival, the Williams Companies.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/energy-transfer-raises-southern-union-bid-to-5-1-billion/', 'snippet': 'Energy Transfer Equity raised its bid for the natural gas pipeline operator to $5.1 billion on Tuesday, seeking to beat out a rival, the Williams Companies.', 'lead_paragraph': '5:23 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Energy Transfer Raises Southern Union Bid to $5.1 Billion', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Natural Gas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pipelines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Energy Transfer Equity LP', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Southern Union Company', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T20:58:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4fd75295-96c8-5cb8-aa19-b5ddffb0d96f', 'word_count': 375, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4fd75295-96c8-5cb8-aa19-b5ddffb0d96f'}, {'abstract': 'In “Tomatoland,” Barry Estabrook delivers a withering criticism of the tactics of the tomato industry in South Florida, where the soil is as devoid of plant nutrients as a pile of moon rocks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/06/books/tomatoland-barry-estabrooks-expose-review.html', 'snippet': 'In “Tomatoland,” Barry Estabrook delivers a withering criticism of the tactics of the tomato industry in South Florida, where the soil is as devoid of plant nutrients as a pile of moon rocks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jonathan Lethem has seen the future of agribusiness, and that future is strange. In his novel “Girl in Landscape” (1998), he imagined humans inhabiting a new planet where meals grow inside “potatoes” that can be planted and harvested. Among the flavors: meat, cake and tea. “Fish,” one character announces, as if he were Ferran Adrià, “is the weirdest one.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/arts/book/book-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 709, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'That Perfect Florida Tomato, Cultivated for Bland Uniformity', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'That Perfect Florida Tomato, Cultivated for Bland Uniformity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Estabrook, Barry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tomatoes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T21:04:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dwight Garner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dwight', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a1da2d2-a3ac-5609-8cf7-e35de6fe5f8b', 'word_count': 1039, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a1da2d2-a3ac-5609-8cf7-e35de6fe5f8b'}, {'abstract': 'Technology firms have gone to market this year by the bushel with little earnings in tow, but Zynga arrives with income aplenty from online games like FarmVille.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/06/business/06views.html', 'snippet': 'Technology firms have gone to market this year by the bushel with little earnings in tow, but Zynga arrives with income aplenty from online games like FarmVille.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Technology firms have gone to market this year by the bushel with little earnings in tow. Zynga arrives with income aplenty from online games like FarmVille. And Zynga’s profitability is even more bountiful than it first appears.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/business/Views/Views-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 973, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Zynga Stands Out Among Tech I.P.O.’s', 'kicker': 'Reuters Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Zynga Stands Out In Tech I.P.O.’s', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NEWS CORP', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Zynga Game Network', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T21:08:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By ROBERT CYRAN and CHRISTOPHER HUGHES', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'CYRAN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'HUGHES', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/50e9732d-472c-5c9f-9a09-6dc2c7769492', 'word_count': 731, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50e9732d-472c-5c9f-9a09-6dc2c7769492'}, {'abstract': 'Michael Tully directs and stars in “Septien,” a Southern gothic tale of a man who returns unannounced to his family’s farm after a long absence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/06/movies/michael-tullys-southern-gothic-septien-review.html', 'snippet': 'Michael Tully directs and stars in “Septien,” a Southern gothic tale of a man who returns unannounced to his family’s farm after a long absence.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Make sure you don’t set anyone’s loins on fire,” a Tennessee plumber (Mark Darby Robinson) instructs his significantly younger and poutier female companion (Rachel Korine) midway through “Septien.” Given the film’s preponderance of flabby men in saggy underwear — not to mention alarming sexual imagery — viewers with weak stomachs can only hope she complies.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/movies/septien-span/septien-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/08/movies/septien-span/septien-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/movies/septien-span/septien-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/movies/septien-span/septien-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/08/movies/septien-span/septien-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Rural Homecoming Stirs Trouble', 'kicker': 'Movie Review | ‘Septien’', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Rural Homecoming Stirs Trouble', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tully, Michael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T21:10:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeannette Catsoulis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeannette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Catsoulis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/1086939e-1ea7-51d8-b010-e0ea416a927d', 'word_count': 505, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1086939e-1ea7-51d8-b010-e0ea416a927d'}, {'abstract': 'Yoani Sánchez, a 35-year-old writer in Havana, has increasingly drawn attention as a chronicler of daily life under Castro.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/06/books/yoani-sanchez-cubas-voice-of-a-blogging-generation.html', 'snippet': 'Yoani Sánchez, a 35-year-old writer in Havana, has increasingly drawn attention as a chronicler of daily life under Castro.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like any other first-time author, Yoani Sánchez was looking forward to receiving copies of her book, “Cuba Libre,” after it was published last year. But when the package sent from Buenos Aires by her publisher arrived in Havana, the Cuban customs service impounded the parcel and, after she complained, sent her a notice explaining its action.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/arts/JUMPSANCHEZ1/JUMPSANCHEZ1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/06/arts/JUMPSANCHEZ1/JUMPSANCHEZ1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/arts/JUMPSANCHEZ1/JUMPSANCHEZ1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 716, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption