man-and-pomellato/', 'snippet': 'Two posh partners collaborate to create a sensational jewelry collection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'These days, high-low collaborations are almost second nature: Versace for H & M, Missoni for Target, Karl Lagerfeld for Macy’s. (Who doesn’t love the chance to purchase some Karl for a fraction of the price?) But two posh partners can produce a pretty sensational must-have, too: See Pomellato’s 12-piece exclusive collection for Bergdorf Goodman.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Team Players | Bergdorf Goodman and Pomellato', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jewels and Jewelry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bergdorf Goodman', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T21:51:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb5b2fff-42b5-51a4-894e-dc40089e2109', 'word_count': 118, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb5b2fff-42b5-51a4-894e-dc40089e2109'}, {'abstract': 'Information provided at the Web sites of Metro-North and the Long Island Rail Road suggest only a grudging tolerance of cyclists.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/bike-friendly-check-the-citys-mass-transit-system/', 'snippet': 'Information provided at the Web sites of Metro-North and the Long Island Rail Road suggest only a grudging tolerance of cyclists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two things about my colleague Christine Haughney’s article on the reluctance of New York-area women to become bicycle commuters were striking. One was the main reason cited: fear. (Excessive sweating followed.) The second was an accompanying  graphic with data from the Census Bureau’s American Community Survey indicating which cities have the most bike commuters and from an Australian study looking at gender differences in bike commuting.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bike-Friendly? Check the City’s Mass Transit System', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bicycles and Bicycling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bike New York', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Caltrain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Long Island Rail Road Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Jersey Transit', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Southeastern Pennsylvania Transportation Authority', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Metropolitan Area Transit Authority', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T22:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicity Barringer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicity', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barringer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/060303bb-d6a8-568e-aa65-6dcf58c73da0', 'word_count': 858, 'uri': 'nyt://article/060303bb-d6a8-568e-aa65-6dcf58c73da0'}, {'abstract': 'A new open-air food court and weekly market, Smorgasburg is a brand extension of the Brooklyn Flea, at East River Waterfront in Williamsburg, Brooklyn.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/07