, Karl Lagerfeld’s collection for Chanel haute couture was a celebration of nightfall and all its aesthetic offshoots: the shimmer of streetlights on cobblestones; the deep blues and purples that bow to black; the silent army of shadows. To make this clear he built a neon-lit model of the Place Vendome in the Grand Palais with Coco herself atop the obelisk. The clothes were sensational and womanly: jutting peplums, ankle grazing dresses and coats, gloves and boots to elongate every silhouette. Here, on Stella Tennant, a draped and tucked dress in black silk taffeta with a spine of crystal buttons.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Chanel', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T22:40:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sally Singer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sally', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Singer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad4f4e82-170e-5cae-a828-46fdc512e574', 'word_count': 109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad4f4e82-170e-5cae-a828-46fdc512e574'}, {'abstract': 'The memo details a new policy that will tie a school’s performance to the school’s ability to roll over money from one year to the next.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/07/06/education/20110706-school-memo.html', 'snippet': 'The memo details a new policy that will tie a school’s performance to the school’s ability to roll over money from one year to the next.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The memo details a new policy that will tie a school’s performance to the school’s ability to roll over money from one year to the next.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York City Schools All