 730, 'width': 577, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/dining/06stuff2/06stuff2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/06/dining/06stuff2/06stuff2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dressing Up Meat in Summer Coats', 'kicker': 'Food Stuff', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dressing Up Meat in Summer Coats', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sauces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Douglas, Tom (Chef)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T23:48:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bbaffef1-a2ab-5f8f-82f7-779fa6f55722', 'word_count': 206, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bbaffef1-a2ab-5f8f-82f7-779fa6f55722'}, {'abstract': 'Williams-Sonoma has introduced a perforated stainless-steel skillet that resembles a wire basket.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/06/dining/a-skillet-is-a-basket-is-a-grill-in-one-food-stuff.html', 'snippet': 'Williams-Sonoma has introduced a perforated stainless-steel skillet that resembles a wire basket.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Williams-Sonoma’s new perforated stainless-steel skillet, which resembles a wire basket, is not just another unnecessary grilling gimmick. You can use it to cook morsels of poultry, seafood, meat and vegetables like a stir-fry, or toss ingredients into it for ratatouille. Its smooth surface releases cooked foods, and it cleans more easily than mesh. A little oil, and you’ll get a bit of flame-up that enhances the pieces of food as they cook. The handle is removable so you can cover the grill while the food cooks or smokes. Other styles include a bigger chef’s pan and a roaster, but the skillet, or fry pan, as it is called, is the most practical.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/dining/06substuff1/06substuff1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 771, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/dining/06substuff1/06substuff1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/06/dining/06substuff1/06substuff1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Skillet Is a Basket Is a Grill', 'kicker': 'Food Stuff', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Skillet Is a Basket Is a Grill', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Williams-Sonoma Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cookware', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T23:50:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea24f01f-8f2c-5632-9ebb-58d903880e9e', 'word_count': 128, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea24f01f-8f2c-5632-9ebb-58d903880e9e'}, {'abstract': 'The Yankees star has soreness in his right triceps, leaving Dave Robertson as the temporary closer.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/rivera-unavailable-to-pitch/', 'snippet': 'The Yankees star has soreness in his right triceps, leaving Dave Robertson as the temporary closer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CLEVELAND — Mariano Rivera completed his normal throwing regimen Tuesday afternoon, but continued soreness in his right triceps sidelined him for a second consecutive game against the Indians. He said that the discomfort, just above his elbow, had subsided since Sunday, but that the head trainer, Gene Monahan, recommended he rest for at least another day.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yankees Say All Is Well as Rivera Sits', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Girardi, Joe', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rivera, Mariano', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T23:54:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/38a1b33d-9ee8-52a5-972d-af9d0dd0f068', 'word_count': 772, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38a1b33d-9ee8-52a5-972d-af9d0dd0f068'}, {'abstract': 'Authorities said the product linked to a deadly E. coli outbreak in Europe was distributed more widely than previously thought.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/06/business/06seeds.html', 'snippet': 'Authorities said the product linked to a deadly E. coli outbreak in Europe was distributed more widely than previously thought.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Authorities are frantically trying to trace all of the tainted fenugreek seeds from a large shipment linked to a deadly E. coli outbreak in Europe, saying the product was distributed more widely than previously thought.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Search Is Under Way for Tainted Sprout Seeds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Search Is Under Way For Tainted Sprout Seeds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sprouts (Seed)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Food Safety Authority', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E Coli (Bacteria)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Contamination and Poisoning', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-05T23:58:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Neuman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Neuman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/523284ad-fb6d-5eda-9a0e-7ef1ee831e30', 'word_count': 420, 'uri': 'nyt://article/523284ad-fb6d-5eda-9a0e-7ef1ee831e30'}, {'abstract': 'Almost four days after an Exxon Mobil pipeline spilled some 42,000 gallons of oil into the Yellowstone River, officials struggled Tuesday to evaluate what the impact to water, birds and fish would be.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/06/science/earth/06brfs-ASSESSINGDAM_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'Almost four days after an Exxon Mobil pipeline spilled some 42,000 gallons of oil into the Yellowstone River, officials struggled Tuesday to evaluate what the impact to water, birds and fish would be.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Almost four days after an Exxon Mobil pipeline broke and spilled some 42,000 gallons of crude oil into the Yellowstone River, government officials and wildlife advocates struggled Tuesday to evaluate what the impact to water, birds and fish would be. Some 350 emergency personnel are working to ease the effects of the spill — absorbing pooled oil and conducting aerial flights to spot oiled birds and other damage. Alan Jeffers, an Exxon spokesman, said that so far, none of the towns that take drinking water from the river have stopped doing so. Amy Cilimburg, an organizer with the conservation group Montana Audubon, confirmed that few oiled birds had been spotted and said that the group was concerned about contaminants’ entering the food chain in the long term. The river rose above flood stage on Tuesday, arousing fears that the oil would be pushed into undamaged areas. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Montana: Assessing Damage From Spill', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | ROCKIES', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Montana: Assessing Damage From Spill', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Exxon Mobil Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-06T00:02:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Leslie Kaufman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Leslie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaufman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt:/