ry’s 18-day revolution. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Acquittals of Ex-Officials Feed Anger Across Egypt', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Acquittals of Ex-Officials Feed Anger Across Egypt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mubarak, Hosni', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-06T00:22:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liam Stack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/404c3690-5c9e-5745-bf9f-c39732f4e1c1', 'word_count': 861, 'uri': 'nyt://article/404c3690-5c9e-5745-bf9f-c39732f4e1c1'}, {'abstract': 'Stephen M. Sweeney, the New Jersey Senate president, called the governor a “bully” and a “punk” in an interview after Mr. Christie made budget cuts that angered Democrats.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/06/nyregion/new-jersey-senate-president-refuses-apology-to-christie.html', 'snippet': 'Stephen M. Sweeney, the New Jersey Senate president, called the governor a “bully” and a “punk” in an interview after Mr. Christie made budget cuts that angered Democrats.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Chris Christie’s office scolded the State Senate president on Tuesday for calling the governor names and saying he wanted to punch him. But the Senate leader, refusing to apologize, said Mr. Christie was in no position to complain about harsh language.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/nyregion/CHRISTIE/CHRISTIE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 926, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/nyregion/CHRISTIE/CHRISTIE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/06/nyregion/CHRISTIE/CHRISTIE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Apologize? To Him? Unrepentant After Some Salty Words for Christie', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Apologize? To Him? Unrepentant After Some Salty Words for Christie', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sweeney, Stephen M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Indecency, Obscenity and Profanity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-06T00:27:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Pérez-Peña', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pérez-Peña', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0d61d1e-cac2-55f6-85fd-ebb18ddc4b58', 'word_count': 509, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0d61d1e-cac2-55f6-85fd-ebb18ddc4b58'}, {'abstract': "The Times's Matthew L. Wald looks at options for safely storing spent