'}, {'abstract': 'Republicans would rather shut down state government than raise taxes on the rich.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/06/opinion/06wed2.html', 'snippet': 'Republicans would rather shut down state government than raise taxes on the rich.', 'lead_paragraph': 'How far will Republican lawmakers go to protect millionaires? Those who think a default on the federal government’s credit seems implausible should take a sobering look at the “closed” signs dotting Minnesota. The Republican Party there readily shut down the state’s government on Friday by refusing to raise taxes on the 7,700 Minnesotans who make more than $1 million a year.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Antitax Extremism in Minnesota', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Antitax Extremism in Minnesota: Republicans would rather shut down state government than raise taxes on the rich', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Minnesota', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dayton, Mark B', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-06T00:59:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/1217e553-5894-5e7e-802a-6d493ca1fc22', 'word_count': 464, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1217e553-5894-5e7e-802a-6d493ca1fc22'}, {'abstract': 'A meeting was characterized by lawyers for Dominique Strauss-Kahn as “constructive.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/06/nyregion/strauss-kahn-lawyers-and-prosecution-to-meet.html', 'snippet': 'A meeting was characterized by lawyers for Dominique Strauss-Kahn as “constructive.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lawyers for Dominique Strauss-Kahn emerged from a meeting on Wednesday with Manhattan prosecutors, characterizing the session as “constructive.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/05/us/6dsk-1-copy/6dsk-1-copy-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/05/us/6dsk-1-copy/6dsk-1-copy-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/05/us/6dsk-1-copy/6dsk-1-copy-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Strauss-Kahn Lawyers and Prosecution Meet to Discuss Dismissal or Plea Deal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Strauss-Kahn Lawyers and Prosecution Meet to Discuss Dismissal or Plea Deal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Post', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vance, Cyrus R Jr', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strauss-Kahn, Dominique', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-06T01:04:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Eligon and William K. Rashbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eligon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': 'K.', 'lastname': 'Rashbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e580988-2af3-5322-8d11-800cbd734c10', 'word_count': 784, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e580988-2af3-5322-8d11-800cbd734c10'}, {'abstract': 'The death of a California bill that would have made it easier for farmworkers to unionize was disappointing. Their union needs to reform itself.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/06/opinion/06wed3.html', 'snippet': 'The death of a California bill that would have made it easier for farmworkers to unionize was disappointing. Their union needs to reform itself.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In California, once a national model of farmworker organizing and progressive labor laws, things have fallen far since the heyday of Cesar Chavez and the United Farm Workers. Of the more than 400,000 workers on 40,000 California farms, the union represents only a tiny share. It listed just 5,219 members in a report to the federal Department of Labor last year. Conditions in the fields and camps are as bad as ever, but the union is adrift and torn by a squalid battle over the movement’s future.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Blow to Farmworkers', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Another Blow to Farmworkers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Farmers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Edmund G Jr', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Migrant and Foreign Workers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-06T01:04:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9fea379-795e-5a35-96a2-ed09c48d6161', 'word_count': 340, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9fea379-795e-5a35-96a2-ed09c48d6161'}, {'abstract': 'A British tabloid is accused of hacking into a murdered 13-year-old girl’s cellphone during an investigation. It is a despicable and outrageous act.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/06/opinion/06wed4.html', 'snippet': 'A British tabloid is accused of hacking into a murdered 13-year-old girl’s cellphone during an investigation. It is a despicable and outrageous act.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Outrage is a word badly weakened by overuse. This is unfortunate because it would be good to have now, at full strength, for the despicable things the British tabloid News of the World is accused of doing to a murdered 13-year-old girl, Milly Dowler, and to her family and friends.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Greater Evil', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Greater Evil', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dowler, Milly', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News of the World', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wiretapping and Other Eavesdropping Devices and Methods', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brooks, Rebekah', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'pers