of steering a nearly bankrupt economy back on track — and, perhaps, preventing another global financial crisis.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/business/Greece/Greece-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/business/Greece/Greece-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/06/business/Greece/Greece-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Greek Finance Minister Moves From Crisis to Crisis', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Finance Minister in Greece Moves From Crisis to Crisis', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Venizelos, Evangelos', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-06T01:25:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Landon Thomas Jr. and Rachel Donadio', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Landon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thomas', 'qualifier': 'Jr.', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Donadio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b43d9658-4831-52d7-af55-5d1265f91be8', 'word_count': 983, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b43d9658-4831-52d7-af55-5d1265f91be8'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Myllyla was a cross-country skier who became a national sports hero in Finland before leaving the sport in disgrace.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/06/sports/mika-myllyla-olympic-skier-in-doping-scandal-dies-at-41.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Myllyla was a cross-country skier who became a national sports hero in Finland before leaving the sport in disgrace.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mika Myllyla, a Finnish Olympic gold medalist and winner of three world championships in cross-country skiing whose career crashed after he was caught up in a doping scandal in 2001, was found dead on Tuesday in his apartment in Kokkola, Finland. He was 41.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/sports/06myllyla-1/06myllyla-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 817, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/sports/06myllyla-1/06myllyla-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/06/sports/06myllyla-1/06myllyla-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mika Myllyla, Olympic Skier in Doping Scandal, Dies at 41', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mika Myllyla, 41, Skier in Doping Scandal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doping (Sports)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Finland', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Myllyla, Mika', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cross-Country Skiing', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-06T01:25:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dennis Hevesi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dennis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hevesi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ea0bc3d-f078-5fd3-9b12-9f22b410299d', 'word_count': 579, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ea0bc3d-f078-5fd3-9b12-9f22b410299d'}, {'abstract': 'What did the Fourth of July mean to Americans, Northern and Southern, black and white, at the start of the Civil War?', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/americas-birthday-under-fire/', 'snippet': 'What did the Fourth of July mean to Americans, Northern and Southern, black and white, at the start of the Civil War?', 'lead_paragraph': 'July 4, 1861 dawned on a divided America, and the holiday itself became a battleground. Across the country, businesses closed, salutes were fired, and people picnicked, but in the South celebrations were unusually restrained. “The Fourth of July passed very quietly here,” reported Sarah Lois Wadley, a Louisiana teenager, “my mind was so much occupied by other things that I had almost forgotten the day.” Wadley approved: “I think that the day should have been observed with unusual strictness, but it is but natural and right that the feeling should have been more of sober thankfulness and religious prayer than of noisy joy.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbStandard.gif', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbStandard.gif', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'America’s Birthday Under Fire', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Independence Day (US) (July 4)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-06T01:30:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Quigley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Quigley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5bfea4ad-9a86-5930-8c79-da8de65f103f', 'word_count': 1003, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5bfea4ad-9a86-5930-8c79-da8de65f103f'}, {'abstract': 'Starting Thursday, the Mets will face seven All-Star pitchers in a row, beginning with Clayton Kershaw of the Dodgers.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/for-mets-a-tough-task-awaits/', 'snippet': 'Starting Thursday, the Mets will face seven All-Star pitchers in a row, beginning with Clayton Kershaw of the Dodgers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES —\xa0 Terry Collins was looking through a collection of statistical analyses on Tuesday, checking over certain matchups that his team would be facing over the next several games, when it hit him.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Mets, a Tough Task Awaits', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Collins, Terry L', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reyes, Jose', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-06T01:31:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1bdcb46f-2b05-538c-bbdc-538ccd6693ac', 'word_count': 759, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1bdcb46f-2b05-538c-bbdc-538ccd6693ac'}, {'abstract': 'The president stepped up pressure on Congressional Republicans, pledging to put popular entitlement programs like Medicare on the table in return for acquiescence to some higher taxes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/06/us/politics/06fiscal.html', 'snippet': 'The president stepped up pressure on Congressional Republicans, pledging to put popular entitlement programs like Medicare on the table in return for acquiescence to some higher taxes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama stepped up pressure on Congressional Republicans on Tuesday to agree to a broad deficit-cutting deal, pledg