ocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gaza Strip', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hamas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-06T01:44:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fares Akram', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fares', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Akram', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea8c16fd-caf7-5037-b512-2f418a03d712', 'word_count': 83, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea8c16fd-caf7-5037-b512-2f418a03d712'}, {'abstract': 'The Afghan Parliament began a heated debate on whether to impeach President Hamid Karzai because of his creation of a special fraud court.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/06/world/asia/06afghanistan.html', 'snippet': 'The Afghan Parliament began a heated debate on whether to impeach President Hamid Karzai because of his creation of a special fraud court.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — Members of the Afghan Parliament came to blows Tuesday as a majority for the first time began to discuss impeaching President Hamid Karzai, signaling the near-total breakdown of relations between the Parliament and the president as the country teeters on the brink of a constitutional crisis. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/world/AFGHANISTAN/AFGHANISTAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/world/AFGHANISTAN/AFGHANISTAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/06/world/AFGHANISTAN/AFGHANISTAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Brawl Erupts During Impeachment Talks in Afghan Parliament', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Brawl Erupts During Impeachment Talks in Afghan Parliament', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karzai, Hamid', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-06T01:44:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alissa J. Rubin and Sangar Rahimi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alissa', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Rubin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Sangar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rahimi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a9ac4c9-2628-5d54-a7a6-428eb95faa40', 'word_count': 1044, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a9ac4c9-2628-5d54-a7a6-428eb95faa40'}, {'abstract': 'Prime Minister Silvio Berlusconi withdrew a clause from the country’s austerity bill that would have allowed one of his family companies to temporarily avoid a heavy fine.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/06/world/europe/06briefs-italy.html', 'snippet': 'Prime Minister Silvio Berlusconi withdrew a clause from the country’s austerity bill that would have allowed one of his family companies to temporarily avoid a heavy fine.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Prime Minister Silvio Berlusconi on Tuesday withdrew a disputed clause of the country’s austerity bill that would have allowed one of his family’s companies to temporarily avoid a heavy fine in a legal dispute. Under the measure, part of the $68 billion bill, companies could ask that especially high fines be suspended as long as appeals were pending. Fininvest, the Berlusconis’ holding company for family assets, was fined $1.09 billion in 2009 for bribery, and a decision by a Milan appeals court is expected this week. Mr. Berlusconi said the measure was “necessary” to protect “companies and citizens.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Italy: Austerity Measure Withdrawn', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | EUROPE', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Italy: Austerity Measure Withdrawn', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fines (Penalties)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berlusconi, Silvio', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-06T01:45:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gaia Pianigiani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gaia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pianigiani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4f81772-7aab-5a32-a776-99e4040b9f2f', 'word_count': 98, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4f81772-7aab-5a32-a776-99e4040b9f2f'}, {'abstract': 'Cy Twombly’s career slyly subverted Abstract Expressionism, toyed briefly with Minimalism, seemed barely to acknowledge Pop art and anticipated some of the concerns of Conceptualism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/07/06/arts/201