d', 'word_count': 630, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff9f193d-4b32-56cb-ab3a-0a7720976e1d'}, {'abstract': 'Peter Collins gets us coming and going.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/nowadays/', 'snippet': 'Peter Collins gets us coming and going.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WEDNESDAY’S PUZZLE — This was not an easy puzzle to construct, I’m telling you that right now.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wednesday: Like Much Social Interaction Nowadays', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-06T02:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0689d73-b127-583d-b77b-cefb88b3ceb1', 'word_count': 293, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0689d73-b127-583d-b77b-cefb88b3ceb1'}, {'abstract': 'A lawyer mailed a criminal complaint to the Paris prosecutor’s office accusing Dominique Strauss-Kahn of attempting to rape the novelist Tristane Banon in 2003.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/06/world/europe/06briefs-Strausskahn.html', 'snippet': 'A lawyer mailed a criminal complaint to the Paris prosecutor’s office accusing Dominique Strauss-Kahn of attempting to rape the novelist Tristane Banon in 2003.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A lawyer said Tuesday that he had mailed a criminal complaint to the Paris prosecutor’s office accusing Dominique Strauss-Kahn of attempting to rape the novelist Tristane Banon in 2003. After Mr. Strauss-Kahn, the former chief of the International Monetary Fund, was arrested in New York in May on a similar charge, Ms. Banon hired the lawyer, David Koubbi. When prosecutors receive the complaint, an investigative judge would be appointed to look into the allegations. Mr. Strauss-Kahn’s lawyers have said that Ms. Banon’s accusations are “imaginary.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France: Strauss-Kahn Formally Accused', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | EUROPE', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France: Strauss-Kahn Formally Accused', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strauss-Kahn, Dominique', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-06T02:02:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Erlanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erlanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/33d167a1-6ca2-5f18-aeed-934549e8898a', 'word_count': 86, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33d167a1-6ca2-5f18-aeed-934549e8898a'}, {'abstract': 'Individual principals will be allowed to roll over money saved from the year before if their schools perform well on progress reports.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/06/nyregion/successful-new-york-city-schools-can-keep-unspent-funds.html', 'snippet': 'Individual principals will be allowed to roll over money saved from the year before if their schools perform well on progress reports.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tying student achievement and school financing in a new way, the city’s schools chancellor has reversed an unpopular move by his predecessor, allowing individual principals to roll over all the money they save from one year to the next — but only if their schools perform well on the city’s controversial progress reports.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Reversal, Schools Doing Well Can Keep Unspent Funds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Reversal, Schools Doing Well Can Keep Unspent Funds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walcott, Dennis M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Principals (School)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Department (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-06T02:04:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fernanda Santos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fernanda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b12f56ef-9207-5f52-9aa8-0bda93a3b5c4', 'word_count': 646, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b12f56ef-9207-5f52-9aa8-0bda93a3b5c4'}, {'abstract': 'On Tuesday, the first day that New York City allowed same-sex couples to initiate the process for marriage, many stumbled over the words “bride” and “groom.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/06/nyregion/seeking-marriage-licenses-gay-couples-hit-roadblock.html', 'snippet': 'On Tuesday, the first day that New York City allowed same-sex couples to initiate the process for marriage, many stumbled over the words “bride” and “groom.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'As he got ready for work on Tuesday, Fredy H. Kaplan, a 5-foot-9, 160-pound gay rights activist from the East Village, turned to his 6-foot-1, 250-pound fiancé and made it official. “You’re going to be the bride,” he said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/nyregion/SAMESEX2/SAMESEX2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/nyregion/SAMESEX2/SAMESEX2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/06/nyregion/SAMESEX2/SAMESEX2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘You’re Making Me the Bride?’ a Hiccup for Gay Unions', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘You’re Making Me the Bride?’ A Hiccup for Gay Unions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-06T02:05:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Javier C. Hernández and Matt Flegenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Javier', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Hernández', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flegenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a63dde19-11a7-53dd-9f9c-fc594ea74931', 'word_count': 884, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a63dde19-11a7-53dd-9f9c-fc594ea74931'}, {'abstract': 'Critics of the Bloomberg administration say the growing caseload and l