 he wanted vengeance before he shot five people in the head in a house in rural Pennsylvania Saturday, but the truth behind his hunger remains unclear.', 'lead_paragraph': 'He emerged from prison more than a year ago, a middle-aged career criminal with a seemingly straightforward story about being done wrong.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/nyregion/ySLAY1/ySLAY1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/nyregion/ySLAY1/ySLAY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/06/nyregion/ySLAY1/ySLAY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Day After a Killer’s Death, Still Sifting for the Truth', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Day After a Killer’s Death, Investigators Still Search for the Truth Behind His Anger', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-06T02:21:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Al Baker and Colin Moynihan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Al', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Colin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moynihan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/515a16ae-de15-5a11-8f01-557cd116de71', 'word_count': 809, 'uri': 'nyt://article/515a16ae-de15-5a11-8f01-557cd116de71'}, {'abstract': 'Derek Jeter’s quest for 3,000 hits will be the subject of a documentary produced by Major League Baseball Productions in collaboration with HBO.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/countdown-for-jeters-movie/', 'snippet': 'Derek Jeter’s quest for 3,000 hits will be the subject of a documentary produced by Major League Baseball Productions in collaboration with HBO.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Derek Jeter’s quest for 3,000 hits will be the subject of a one-hour documentary produced by Major League Baseball Productions in collaboration with HBO. It will be shown a few weeks after he reaches the landmark.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Countdown for Jeter’s … Movie', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jeter, Derek', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-06T02:27:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/294cfd73-6667-57bf-ab0d-2033e54d531c', 'word_count': 153, 'uri': 'nyt://article/294cfd73-6667-57bf-ab0d-2033e54d531c'}, {'abstract': 'The shortstop had two hits, giving him 2,996, and C. C. Sabathia pitched seven shutout innings in becoming the majors’ first 12-game winner.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/06/sports/baseball/jeter-makes-move-on-3000-hits-as-yankees-roll.html', 'snippet': 'The shortstop had two hits, giving him 2,996, and C. C. Sabathia pitched seven shutout innings in becoming the majors’ first 12-game winner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CLEVELAND — With two outs in the second inning Tuesday night, Carlos Carrasco threw Derek Jeter a fastball on a 2-0 count. It was not just any fastball. It was a 90-mile-per-hour fastball that hummed in on the same plane as Jeter’s belt. Were that pitch able to speak, it would have asked him to crush it to Kalamazoo.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/sports/06yanks-1/06yanks-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/06/sports/06yanks-1/06yanks-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/sports/06yanks-1/06yanks-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/sports/06yanks-1/06yanks-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/06/sports/06yanks-1/06yanks-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jeter Moves Closer to 3,000 as Yanks Roll', 'kicker': 'Yankees 9, Indians 2', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jeter Moves Closer to 3,000 As Yanks Roll', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cleveland Indians', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sabathia, C C', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jeter, Derek', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-06T02:40:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4fc5fa2-c639-53db-b12d-939c4f4f86cf', 'word_count': 1070, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4fc5fa2-c639-53db-b12d-939c4f4f86cf'}, {'abstract': 'Working under intense pressure from opponents, Lisa P. Jackson is scheduled to establish a series of environmental regulations that will affect every corner of the economy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/06/science/earth/06epa.html', 'snippet': 'Working under intense pressure from opponents, Lisa P. Jackson is scheduled to establish a series of environmental regulations that will affect every corner of the economy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — In the next weeks and months, Lisa P. Jackson, the Environmental Protection Agency administrator, is scheduled to establish regulations on smog, mercury, carbon dioxide, mining waste and vehicle emissions that will affect every corner of the economy.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/us/EPA-1/EPA-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/06/us/EPA-1/EPA-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/us/EPA-1/EPA-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'sub