f Warren E. Buffett, Bill Gates, Oprah Winfrey, Rupert Murdoch and Mark Zuckerberg.', 'lead_paragraph': '\xa0', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Deal Makers Soak Up Sun Valley', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-06T11:14:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Evelyn M. Rusli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Evelyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f6de398-ef79-5baf-8dbd-04e424d8d441', 'word_count': 673, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f6de398-ef79-5baf-8dbd-04e424d8d441'}, {'abstract': 'European officials threatened credit-rating agencies with possible retaliation after the decision by Moody’s Investors Service to downgrade Portugal’s debt to junk.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/business/global/07euro.html', 'snippet': 'European officials threatened credit-rating agencies with possible retaliation after the decision by Moody’s Investors Service to downgrade Portugal’s debt to junk.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — European officials scrambled on Wednesday to prevent the debt crisis in Greece from destabilizing their currency union, threatening credit-rating agencies with possible retaliation after the decision on Tuesday by Moody’s Investors Service to downgrade Portugal’s debt to junk status. The move raised fears that Spain and Italy might soon find themselves in the line of fire, too. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/07/business/Euro/Euro-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo'