s-as-you-like-it/', 'snippet': 'The comedy, which is to begin performances on Wednesday during the company’s Lincoln Center Festival residency, will not show a dead rabbit being skinned and decapitated, as the British production depicted.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For one unlucky rabbit in each performance of the Royal Shakespeare Company‘s production of “As You Like It,” it was the most unkindest cut of all: an already dead bunny was skinned and decapitated during a scene in that Shakespeare comedy about cross-dressing, mistaken identity and the contrasts between courtly and provincial life. And while all the world’s a stage, the stage will not serve as a butcher’s block when the play is presented in New York: the Royal Shakespeare Company says it has excised the rabbit-skinning scene for its Lincoln Center Festival residency.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Don’t Kill the Rabbit: Scene Cut From Royal Shakespeare Company’s ‘As You Like It’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shakespeare, William', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal Shakespeare Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-06T15:05:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0dc014f-c8af-58cc-981b-093df396638e', 'word_count': 339, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0dc014f-c8af-58cc-981b-093df396638e'}, {'abstract': 'Chart of number of bills printed each year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/07/06/business/some-of-the-denomi