times.com/2011/07/07/business/in-first-week-on-the-job-lagarde-stresses-diversity.html', 'snippet': 'Christine Lagarde, a political conservative, said that people should judge her tenure at the International Monetary Fund by her actions rather than making assumptions based on political labels.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Christine Lagarde said Wednesday that meetings had consumed 18 of her first 24 hours as the new head of the International Monetary Fund, as the former French finance minister seeks to lift her staff’s bruised morale while helping to preserve Europe’s financial stability.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/07/business/Fund/Fund-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 267, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/07/business/Fund/Fund-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 267}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/07/business/Fund/Fund-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 455, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Her First Week at the I.M.F., a New Leader Stresses Diversity and Respect', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Her First Week at the I.M.F., a New Leader Stresses Diversity and Respect', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Monetary Fund', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lagarde, Christine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-06T17:48:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Binyamin Appelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Binyamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Appelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a19754b0-f353-5e4a-8826-346e8d36f61e', 'word_count': 675, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a19754b0-f353-5e4a-8826-346e8d36f61e'}, {'abstract': 'The city is conducting a “weathering study” of Cleopatra’s Needle, a gift from Egypt that has stood in Central Park since 1881 but that Egyptian authorities say is being destroyed by New York’s acid rain.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/06/egypt-or-central-park-where-does-an-ancient-obelisk-belong/', 'snippet': 'The city is conducting a “weathering study” of Cleopatra’s Needle, a gift from Egypt that has stood in Central Park since 1881 but that Egyptian authorities say is being destroyed by New York’s acid rain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Is New York City’s weather destroying a 3,500-year-old Egyptian obelisk?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt or Central Park: Where Does an Ancient Obelisk Belong?', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parks and Other Recreation Areas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hawass, Zahi', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'CENTRAL PARK (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-06T17:54:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Francie Diep and Joseph Castro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Francie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Diep', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organizatio