ght against the Indians, despite strong hints from Manager Joe Girardi that he would receive the day off. Jeter said after Tuesday’s game, when he went 2 for 6 to draw within four hits of the milestone, that he very much wanted to play Wednesday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jeter Will Play, Chase More Hits Against Indians', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jeter, Derek', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-06T18:51:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/35a1f362-7f03-55e4-9cb6-fde43644c0c6', 'word_count': 301, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35a1f362-7f03-55e4-9cb6-fde43644c0c6'}, {'abstract': "Battle of the giants? Google is launching a new social network that aims to be different from Facebook's. Bettina Edelstein speaks with Times technology reporter Claire Cain Miller about what's in store and what's at stake. Security experts recently met at the White House about an ongoing cybersecurity campaign. J.D. Biersdorfer chats with Trend Micro's David Perry about what's happening on that front. The news roundup includes hacks on an Apple server and the FoxNews Twitter feed; the Qosimo 3D laptop from Toshiba; the disappearance of Google's Realtime Search; and crowd sourcing to manage traffic when a 10-mile stretch of highway shuts down for 53 hours in Los Angeles. J.D.'s tip of the week: how to print your address book.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2011/07/06/technology/techtalk.html', 'snippet': "Battle of the giants? Google is launching a new social network that aims to be different from Facebook's. Bettina Edelstein speaks with Times technology reporter Claire Cain Miller about what's in store and what's at stake. Security experts recent...", 'lead_paragraph': "Battle of the giants? Google is launching a new social network that aims to be different from Facebook's. Bettina Edelstein speaks with Times technology reporter Claire Cain Miller about what's in store and what's at stake. Security experts recently met at the White House about an ongoing cybersecurity campaign. J.D. Biersdorfer chats with Trend Micro's David Perry about what's happening on that front. The news roundup includes hacks on an Apple server and the FoxNews Twitter feed; the Qosimo 3D laptop from Toshiba; the disappearance of Google's Realtime Search; and crowd sourcing to manage traffic when a 10-mile stretch of highway shuts down for 53 hours in Los Angeles. J.D.'s tip of the week: how to print your address book.", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': "Claire Cain Miller on Google's social network; cybersecurity awareness; news.", 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-06T18:59:52+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/12905938-878b-5559-983f-30554f54a42b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/12905938-878b-5559-983f-30554f54a42b'}, {'abstract': 'Born in Hungary, Mr. Lang was famous for the transformation of the restaurant in the 1970s into a beloved dining spot.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/nyregion/george-lang-of-cafe-des-artistes-dies-at-86.html', 'snippet': 'Born in Hungary, Mr. Lang was famous for the transformation of the restaurant in the 1970s into a beloved dining spot.', 'lead_paragraph': 'George Lang, a restaurateur and cookbook writer who in the 1970s transformed Café des Artistes into one of New York’s most romantic, beloved dining spots and in the 1990s helped restore the historic Budapest restaurant Gundel to its former glory, died on Tuesday at his home in Manhattan. He was 86.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/07/nyregion/obit-lang/obit-lang-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/07/nyregion/obit-lang/obit-lang-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/07/nyregion/obit-lang/obit-lang-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 686, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/07/nyregion/obit-lang/obit-lang-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/07/nyregion/obit-lang/obit-lang-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'George Lang, Mastermind Behind Café des Artistes, Dies at 86', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'George Lang, Whose Overhaul Made Café des Artistes a Hit, Is Dead at 86', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lang, George', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cafe des Artistes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hotel des Artistes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hungary', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-06T19:02:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Grimes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grimes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d3ab3cb-021a-554f-a470-a80a456c8691', 'word_count': 1235, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d3ab3cb-021a-554f-a470-a80a456c8691'}, {'abstract': 'More than 30 South Koreans kill themselves every day, but Koreans would rather consult a fortuneteller, shaman or pastor than see a shrink.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/world/asia/07iht-psych07.html', 'snippet': 'More than 30 South Koreans kill themselves every day, but Koreans would rather consult a fortuneteller, shaman or pastor than see a shrink.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL — It can sometimes feel as if South Korea, overworked, overstressed and ever anxious, is on the verge of a national nervous breakdown, with a rising divorce rate, students who feel suffocated by academic pressures, a suicide rate among the highest in the world and a macho corporate culture that still encourages blackout drinking sessions after work.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/07/world/07iht-psych_337/07iht-psych_337-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'im