bold pocket square,’’ says the democratizing duke, who was raised in Seville but now lives in Madrid. Here are a few of his standby spots in the capital. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside Track | Rafael Medina’s Madrid', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-06T19:23:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Ferren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ferren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9050f83-08ab-5885-839d-888e27e42a28', 'word_count': 347, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9050f83-08ab-5885-839d-888e27e42a28'}, {'abstract': 'Has Montauk lost its cool or is it more fun? That question hung in the salty air on July 2 at the annual Shark Attack Sounds party.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/07/06/fashion/20110707-scene.html', 'snippet': 'Has Montauk lost its cool or is it more fun? That question hung in the salty air on July 2 at the annual Shark Attack Sounds party.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Has Montauk lost its cool or is it more fun? That question hung in the salty air on July 2 at the annual Shark Attack Sounds party.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/fashion/20110707-scene-slide-B29A/20110707-scene-slide-B29A-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/06/fashion/20110707-scene-slide-B29A/20110707-scene-slide-B29A-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail'