06/george-lang-creator-of-romance-who-lived-through-a-nightmare/', 'snippet': 'The former owner of Café des Artistes died at age 86.', 'lead_paragraph': 'William Grimes recalls the life of George Lang, owner for a quarter century of the former Café des Artistes. Mr. Lang died on Tuesday at the age of 86. He escaped the horrors of his native Hungary in World War II, after losing his parents in Auschwitz. In 1975, he took over the Upper West Side restaurant mainly known for its Howard Chandler Christy murals of naked nymphs. As Mr. Grimes noted in a 2003 review, the restaurant had its ups and downs, but at its best, it could be one of the city’s best-loved and most romantic restaurants. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'George Lang, Creator of Romance Who Lived Through a Nightmare', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-06T19:57:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af3544bd-a3bf-5886-91c2-526762a71b3e', 'word_count': 100, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af3544bd-a3bf-5886-91c2-526762a71b3e'}, {'abstract': 'There have always been compromises with speakers that do away with wires, but a new system solves many of those problems.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/technology/personaltech/aperion-wireless-speakers-review.html', 'snippet': 'There have always been compromises with speakers that do away with wires, but a new system solves many of those problems.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Modern technology is great and all, but it’s still studded with pain points. Just ask anyone who’s ever tried to set up a home network, to send a video by e-mail or to maintain a phone call driving down I-95.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page'