justice for women, the report says that most countries do not explicitly criminalize domestic violence and marital rape, thereby dissuading women from reporting such cases.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Most countries still do not explicitly criminalize rape within marriage, according to a sweeping United Nations report of global women’s rights published Wednesday. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.N. Women’s Agency Publishes Sobering Report on Lack of Gender Equality', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | United Nations', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gaps in Women’s Rights Are Cited', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-06T20:04:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katrin Bennhold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katrin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bennhold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1874b4ff-829b-54b6-915f-9f69c1840dba', 'word_count': 394, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1874b4ff-829b-54b6-915f-9f69c1840dba'}, {'abstract': 'An investigation into the disappearances of newborns from 1950 to 1990 involves allegations of abductions and the existence of criminal networks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/world/europe/07iht-spain07.html', 'snippet': 'An investigation into the disappearances of newborns from 1950 to 1990 involves allegations of abductions and the existence of criminal networks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEVILLE, Spain — Prodded by grieving parents, Spanish judges are investigating hundreds of charges that infants were abducted and sold for adoption 