nt_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Raphael Minder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Raphael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Minder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/12dde9a5-79f7-53c1-9a4e-0fc4a52bd5d2', 'word_count': 1253, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12dde9a5-79f7-53c1-9a4e-0fc4a52bd5d2'}, {'abstract': 'Another day of runway looks, another Scorecard at your service.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/06/scorecard-givenchy-wins-4/', 'snippet': 'Another day of runway looks, another Scorecard at your service.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It appears to Scorecard that a guy named Gil isn’t the only homme nostalgic for 1920s Paris this summer. At midnight — OK, 10 P.M. — Tuesday, Kaiser Karl dazzled at Chanel with a bouclé memory trip down the Rue Cambon. Yet when it comes to reaching new celestial heights, ever-rising star Riccardo Tisci and his petits mains at the Givenchy atelier had the most intricate crystals and dégradé pearls stitched down.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Scorecard | Givenchy Wins!', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-06T20:07:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alison S. Cohn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Cohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/98a6a0c1-b06c-5fd2-98eb-927326c839ba', 'word_count': 1121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98a6a0c1-b06c-5fd2-98eb-927326c839ba'}, {'abstract': 'Taliban fighters attacked several border police check posts, killing 23 police officers in a remote area of northeastern Afghanistan, according to the provincial governor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/world/asia/07afghanistan.html', 'snippet': 'Taliban fighters attacked several border police check posts, killing 23 police officers in a remote area of northeastern Afghanistan, according to the provincial governor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — Taliban fighters attacked and overran several Afghan border police posts on Wednesday, killing nearly two dozen police officers in a remote area of northeastern Afghanistan, according to the provincial governor. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Taliban Fighters Attack Afghan Police Posts', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '23 Are Said to Be Killed In Attack on Afghan Police', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karzai, Hamid', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'North Atlantic Treaty Organization', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-06T20:12:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alissa J. Rubin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alissa', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Rubin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de70ee92-ede0-5e68-ba12-7e782c1f2872', 'word_count': 521, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de70ee92-ede0-5e68-ba12-7e782c1f2872'}, {'abstract': 'Travelers are encouraged to get MMR (measles, mumps and rubella) vaccines before going overseas because of increases in measles outbreaks in Europe, Asia and Africa.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/06/increase-in-measles-cases/', 'snippet': 'Travelers are encouraged to get MMR (measles, mumps and rubella) vaccines before going overseas because of increases in measles outbreaks in Europe, Asia and Africa.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An increase in the number of measles outbreaks in Europe, Asia and Africa in recent months is cause for concern at the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention in the United States. Candice Burns Hoffmann, a press officer for the center, said in a release that the United States was experiencing “the highest number of measles cases since 1996,” in large part because of unvaccinated travelers recently returned from overseas.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Increase in Measles Cases', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Centers for Disease Control and Prevention', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-06T20:12:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Lee Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': 'Lee', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b64656e1-7ebb-5b3e-875a-428336924d6e', 'word_count': 241, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b64656e1-7ebb-5b3e-875a-428336924d6e'}, {'abstract': 'Members of the British Parliament debated serious allegations of wrongdoing by journalists and editors at a British tabloid owned by Rupert Murdoch.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/06/video-of-british-debate-on-hacking-scandal/', 'snippet': 'Members of the British Parliament debated serious allegations of wrongdoing by journalists and editors at a British tabloid owned by Rupert Murdoch.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As my colleagues Sarah Lyall and Alan Cowell report, during a debate in the House of Commons on Wednesday, Prime Minister David Cameron of Britain agreed that there should be a public inquiry into the workings of the British newspapers following reports that journalists for The News of the World hacked into the voice mailboxes of murder and terrorism victims.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video of British Debate on Hacking Scandal', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wiretapping and Other Eavesdropping Devices and Methods', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brooks, Rebekah', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cameron, David', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miliband, Edward S', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NEWS CORP', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News International Ltd', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News of the World', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-06T20:17:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}],