f-the-day-spain-and-elsewhere-3/', 'snippet': 'Photographs from Spain, Greece and Nepal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photographs from Spain, Greece and Nepal.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pictures of the Day: Spain and Elsewhere', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nepal', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-06T20:23:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e729a5f-a7b8-5fb2-a657-f26f6a0d7b99', 'word_count': 6, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e729a5f-a7b8-5fb2-a657-f26f6a0d7b99'}, {'abstract': 'A young couple on a tight budget renovate a two-bedroom apartment with a gallery-like aesthetic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/07/07/greathomesanddestinations/20110706_location.html', 'snippet': 'A young couple on a tight budget renovate a two-bedroom apartment with a gallery-like aesthetic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A young couple on a tight budget renovate a two-bedroom apartment with a gallery-like aesthetic.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Location | Paris', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restoration and Renovation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-06T20:26:56+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Great Homes & Destinations', 'section_name': 'Great Homes & Destinations', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/19c6e7fb-bc5a-5491-923b-4a79cb4393c9', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/19c6e7fb-bc5a-5491-923b-4a79cb4393c9'}, {'abstract': 'Bedtimes defines our pasts and shapes our futures.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/06/please-go-to-sleep/', 'snippet': 'Bedtimes defines our pasts and shapes our futures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bedtime gives us some of our best parenting memories, and some of our worst. There are nights when “The Children’s Hour,” as Longfellow dubbed it, is the sweet, warm essence of all the reasons you had children, but also nights, as Adam Mansbach’s satirical best seller has captured, when you would give anything for them to “Go the ____ to Sleep.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Please, Go to Sleep', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sleep', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-06T20:29:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Belkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c7a80e51-75a3-5156-975d-d1c2ed803900', 'word_count': 1806, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c7a80e51-75a3-5156-975d-d1c2ed803900'}, {'abstract': 'The NBC reality competition draws its third-largest audience.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/06/americas-got-talent-gets-plenty-of-viewers/', 'snippet': 'The NBC reality competition draws its third-largest audience.', 'lead_paragraph': '“America’s Got Talent” attracted its third-largest audience ever on Tuesday as the latest two-hour installment of the NBC reality competition drew 15.5 million viewers and dominated the night’s ratings, according to Nielsen’s estimates. Only the show’s two previous season finales, in 2010 and 2009, garnered more viewers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘America’s Got Talent’ Gets Plenty of Viewers', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Anthony, Casey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC INC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nielsen Media Research', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-06T20:30:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Toff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Toff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1055470a-c929-517f-864a-04b4d9a417ea', 'word_count': 144, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1055470a-c929-517f-864a-04b4d9a417ea'}, {'abstract': 'The iPad 2’s popular Smart Cover protects only the front. If you want to cover the back too, there are many offerings to choose from.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/technology/personaltech/a-closetful-of-options-for-protecting-the-ipad.html', 'snippet': 'The iPad 2’s popular Smart Cover protects only the front. If you want to cover the back too, there are many offerings to choose from.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It dawned on me three months after buying an iPad 2 that keeping the tablet encased in its original clear packing sleeve was a bit like having my living room furniture covered in plastic: practical, yet tacky.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/07/business/07BASIC_SPAN/07BASIC_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 352, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/07/business/07BASIC_SPAN/07BASIC_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 352}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/07/business/07BASIC_SPAN/07BASIC_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/07/business/07BASIC_SPAN/07BASIC_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/07/business/07BASIC_SPAN/07BASIC_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Options Abound to Protect the iPad', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Options Abound To Protect the iPad', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPad', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-06T20:30:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mickey Meece', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mickey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Meece', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a0a2b1a-a39e-57b5-9d2d-f380aea95365', 'word_count': 1193, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a0a2b1a-a39e-57b5-9d2d-f380aea95365'}, {'abstract': 'In Will Lavender’s second novel, “Dominance,” a Vermont college becomes the setting for a copycat murder.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/books/dominance-by-will-lavender-book-review.html', 'snippet': 'In Will Lavender’s second novel, “Dominance,” a Vermont college becomes the setting for a copycat murder.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The setting: a college classroom in Vermont. The year: 1994. The topic: Unraveling a Literary Mystery. The professor: the most brilliant man in captivity, and he actually is in captivity, confined to prison for the 1982 murders of two female students. If Dr. Richard Aldiss reminds you of Dr. Hannibal Lecter, you are as smart as the nine super-special students in this class.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/07/arts/jmp-book/jmp-book-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 668, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/07/arts/jmp-book/jmp-book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/07/arts/jmp-book/jmp-book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Literature Can Turn Most Lethal', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Literature Can Turn Most Lethal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject'