onomy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After steadily climbing for several years, the number of Americans filing for bankruptcy is on the decline, though that is not necessarily an indicator of an improving economy.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fewer Americans File for Bankruptcy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fewer Americans File for Bankruptcy as Debt Woes Ease', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-06T22:23:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Siegel Bernard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': 'Siegel', 'lastname': 'Bernard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4bd8f034-de1d-51d1-999f-01b025a123f5', 'word_count': 581, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4bd8f034-de1d-51d1-999f-01b025a123f5'}, {'abstract': 'In this week’s podcast: Claire Cain Miller on Google’s social network and a White House cybersecurity awareness conference.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/06/tech-talk-podcast-googles-social-network/', 'snippet': 'In this week’s podcast: Claire Cain Miller on Google’s social network and a White House cybersecurity awareness conference.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Battle of the giants? Google is introducing a new social network that aims to be different from Facebook‘s. On this week’s Bits: Tech Talk show, Bettina Edelstein talks to Times technology reporter Claire Cain Miller about Google+, the search engine’s new social network. It’s the fourth go-around for Google in social media