blican presidential campaign, had said in an interview that Michele Bachmann’s candidacy was catching on, in part, because “she’s got a little sex appeal.”', 'lead_paragraph': '9:56 p.m. | Updated  AMES, Iowa – Vin Weber, a top adviser to Tim Pawlenty’s Republican presidential campaign, issued an apology on Wednesday evening after declaring that Michele Bachmann’s candidacy was catching on, in part, because “she’s got a little sex appeal.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pawlenty Aide Apologizes for Citing Bachmann’s ‘Sex Appeal’', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bachmann, Michele M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pawlenty, Tim', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weber, Vin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T00:38:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Zeleny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zeleny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d929c5a-7405-5119-8fed-606ad97785c7', 'word_count': 385, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d929c5a-7405-5119-8fed-606ad97785c7'}, {'abstract': 'Police arrested scores of people standing and clapping on sidewalks, in the latest round of crackdowns aimed at curbing public political expression, human rights groups said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/world/europe/07briefs-FIRSTCLAPSTH_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'Police arrested scores of people standing and clapping on sidewalks, in the latest round of crackdowns aimed at curbing public political expression, human rights groups said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the latest crackdown on a form of protest that has been gathering strength in Belarus, the police arrested scores of people who were standing on sidewalks and clapping Wednesday, human rights groups said. The applauding protests began because authorities in President Aleksandr G. Lukashenko’s government take more severe actions against traditional public political expression, like unfurling banners. The clapping protests are organized anonymously on social networking sites for Wednesday evenings and began last month. Some participants stand silently while others clap. Plainclothes police officers typically swoop in and grab those who applaud, sometimes roughing them up. Vesna, a Belarussian rights group, said the police detained about 150 clappers on Wednesday. After past protests, judges have sentenced clappers to 15 days in jail or a fine. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Belarus: First, Claps; Then, Arrests', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | EUROPE', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Belarus: First, Claps; Then, Arrests', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Belarus', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T00:43:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew E. Kramer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Kramer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/8993213b-c5a1-5c62-9914-f4bdc5f056ff', 'word_count': 128, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8993213b-c5a1-5c62-9914-f4bdc5f056ff'}, {'abstract': 'Craig Biggio was the last to reach 3,000 hits and the ninth to get 