. Conca, a 28-year-old midfielder, signed a 3 ½-year contract after the team agreed to pay the Brazilian champion Fluminense the record fee. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Major Deal for Argentine', 'kicker': 'Sports Briefing | Soccer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Major Deal for Argentine', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T00:57:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bloomberg News', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bloomberg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'News', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d82e2e9f-993b-58d0-950e-00afd249267b', 'word_count': 74, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d82e2e9f-993b-58d0-950e-00afd249267b'}, {'abstract': 'Civil War soldiers took all sorts of animals into battle as mascots.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/06/the-dogs-and-bears-and-camels-of-war/', 'snippet': 'Civil War soldiers took all sorts of animals into battle as mascots.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Union and Confederate soldiers left the comforts of home for the grim realities of war, many brought along family pets or adopted stray or wild animals, which quickly took on semi-official roles. Regiments from the North and the South kept dogs, cats, horses, squirrels and raccoons as mascots. Some chose more unusual animals, including bears, badgers, eagles, wildcats, even a camel.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Dogs (and Bears, and Camels) of War', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'val