': 'By Colin Moynihan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Colin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moynihan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00b4ecb2-873c-51f7-bc0b-f38ebb77b4db', 'word_count': 414, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00b4ecb2-873c-51f7-bc0b-f38ebb77b4db'}, {'abstract': 'INTERNATIONAL', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/pageoneplus/07corrections.html', 'snippet': '', 'lead_paragraph': 'INTERNATIONAL', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T02:06:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b425de4-ede9-5537-97fc-aa3eb47102d9', 'word_count': 269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b425de4-ede9-5537-97fc-aa3eb47102d9'}, {'abstract': 'The law legalizing same-sex weddings goes into effect on a day when municipal offices are usually closed, but city officials said they are willing to accommodate a historic moment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/nyregion/city-setting-sunday-hours-to-grant-gay-unions.html', 'snippet': 'The law legalizing same-sex weddings goes into effect on a day when municipal offices are usually closed, but city officials said they are willing to accommodate a historic moment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York City, whose top elected officials strongly supported the legalization of same-sex marriage, will take the unusual step of opening city offices on a Sunday, July 24, so gay couples can marry on the day the law takes effect.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/07/nyregion/07marriage_inline/07marriage_inline-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/07/nyregion/07marriage_inline/07marriage_inline-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/07/nyregion/07marriage_inline/07marriage_inline-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'City Setting Sunday Hours to Grant Gay Unions', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'City Setting Sunday Hours To Grant Gay Unions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T02:06:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Kaplan and Javier C. Hernández', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Javier', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Hernández', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/58549074-58c7-54cb-87b0-16470bee1a54', 'word_count': 730, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58549074-58c7-54cb-87b0-16470bee1a54'}, {'abstract': 'Zynga, the social gaming company, is taking the unusual step of creating three classes of stock that include one reserved for its founder.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/business/too-many-classes-of-zynga-stock-reuters-breakingviews.html', 'snippet': 'Zynga, the social gaming company, is taking the unusual step of creating three classes of stock that include one reserved for its founder.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s bad enough for shareholders when companies have two classes of shares. Zynga, the social gaming company, will have three, with Mark Pincus, the founder, in a class of his own. This innovation shouldn’t be copied.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/07/business/Views/Views-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 974, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Too Many Classes of Zynga Stock', 'kicker': 'Reuters Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Too Many Classes of Zynga Stock', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Williams Cos Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Compensation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Zynga Game Network', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Energy Transfer Equity LP', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Southern Union Company', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pincus, Mark', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T02:06:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Cyran, Christopher Swann and Lisa Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cyran', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Swann', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/94b621a0-6fbe-5ad6-b701-2c87cf2d81ec', 'word_count': 732, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94b621a0-6fbe-5ad6-b701-2c87cf2d81ec'}, {'abstract': 'Europe’s approach to the Greek debt crisis remains far too blinkered and passive.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/opinion/07thu1.html', 'snippet': 'Europe’s approach to the Greek debt crisis remains far too blinkered and passive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An outright default by Greece on nearly a half-trillion dollars of outstanding debt obligations would be a catastrophe for Greece, for its European creditor banks and for financial institutions everywhere as credit-default swaps on Greek debt worked their way through the derivatives markets. It does not need to happen, but barring an unexpected show of European political and economic leadership, that outcome is becoming increasingly likely. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fumbling Toward Default', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fumbling Toward Default: Europe’s approach to the Greek debt crisis remains far too blinkered and passive', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T02:06:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4ed3f9e-4d30-5acb-b586-40698f4daadd', 'word_count': 509, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4ed3f9e-4d30-5acb-b586-40698f4daadd'}, {'abstract': 'Virginia Cedeno, who became a taxi driver in 1979, rides around in a Crown Victoria with her butterfly-printed cane, a can of Febreze and a coffee mug.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/nyregion/virginia-cedeno-taxi-driver-from-queens.html', 'snippet': 'Virginia Cedeno, who became a taxi driver in 1979, rides around in a Crown Victoria with her butterfly-printed cane, a can of Febreze and a coffee mug.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Virginia Cedeno followed her two brothers’ example when she became a taxi driver in 1979, but she has far outlasted them in the business. Ms. Cedeno, 61, bought her taxi medallion in 1985 and still rides around in a Crown Victoria with her butterfly-printed cane, a can of Febreze, maps to share with less experienced taxi drivers and a coffee mug. She recently drove to Albany to protest proposed taxi legislation. Ms. Cedeno lives in Corona, Queens.  ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/07/nyregion/EXPERIENCE1/EXPERIENCE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/07/nyregion/EXPERIENCE1/EXPERIENCE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit'