mportant budget and policy issue, often splitting 6-3 when they could even agree to a vote.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'State to Appoint New Board of Education in Bridgeport', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'State to Appoint New Board of Education in Bridgeport', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bridgeport (Conn)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T02:08:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Winnie Hu and Robert Davey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Winnie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e6d792b-3901-5df8-8383-c1f4ceb325d1', 'word_count': 851, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e6d792b-3901-5df8-8383-c1f4ceb325d1'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama has made the enlightened decision to begin sending letters of condolence to the families of combat troops who commit suicide.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/opinion/07thu3.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama has made the enlightened decision to begin sending letters of condolence to the families of combat troops who commit suicide.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In an enlightened reversal of the ways of war, President Obama has decided to begin sending letters of condolence to the families of combat troops who commit suicide. Until now, White House policy across several administrations extended the president’s