e of baseball, Derek Jeter and Roger Clemens, are in the spotlight this week for different reasons. Also, what City Room is reading in other papers and blogs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The world of sports has long provided metaphors for life, and for many Americans — certainly this American — no sport is riper for epistemological picking than baseball. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Jeter and Clemens, It’s a Game of Trajectories', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Steroids', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clemens, Roger', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jeter, Derek', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T12:52:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clyde Haberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clyde', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fae5ba83-e467-5861-9c69-af9c748b43d0', 'word_count': 970, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fae5ba83-e467-5861-9c69-af9c748b43d0'}, {'abstract': 'NYSE Euronext shareholders approved the deal with Deutsche Börse. But the German exchange operator must still wait for its investors to tender their shares.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/two-votes-one-hurdle-for-nyse-deutsche-merger/', 'snippet': 'NYSE Euronext shareholders approved the deal with Deutsche Börse. But the German exchange operator must still wait for its investors to tender their shares.', 'lead_paragraph': '8:48 a.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'One Vote Down, One to Go for N.Y.S.E. and Deutsche Borse Merger', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deutsche Borse AG', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Stock Exchange', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NYSE Euronext', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T12:53:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dde60086-e14a-5b9b-a5f6-73b6ffa983a3', 'word_count': 280, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dde60086-e14a-5b9b-a5f6-73b6ffa983a3'}, {'abstract': 'A select few potential Facebook employees are invited to walk with Mark Zuckerberg, Facebook’s founder, through a wooded area of Palo Alto.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/a-walk-in-the-woods-with-mark-zuckerberg/', 'snippet': 'A select few potential Facebook employees are invited to walk with Mark Zuckerberg, Facebook’s founder, through a wooded area of Palo Alto.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You might think a long quiet walk through the woods\xa0with Mark Zuckerberg, the founder of Facebook, is a treat only his closest friends and dearest family get to enjoy. Yet a chummy stroll with one of the richest men in the world is actually reserved for a few select potential Facebook employees.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Walk in the Woods With Mark Zuckerberg', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executives and Management', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiking', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zuckerberg, Mark E', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook.com', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Silicon Valley (Calif)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T12:58:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c55f086-2ea2-5dee-b831-51b11c472a85', 'word_count': 513, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c55f086-2ea2-5dee-b831-51b11c472a85'}, {'abstract': 'When it comes to good bug spray, Sweden knows best.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/vain-glorious-bugs-be-gone/', 'snippet': 'When it comes to good bug spray, Sweden knows best.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After a particularly humid (and therefore buggy) fourth of July weekend, inquiring T staffers wanted to know: is there spray, balm, milk or mist that actually works? Luckily, Andreas Kokkino, one of T’s fashion editors, knew the answer. While in Stockholm, styling for an upcoming feature, he unearthed one of Scandinavia’s best-kept secrets: highly effective insect repellents. Who knew?\xa0At the top of his list is the DEET-free, all-natural MaxMedica MyggA Roll On (around $13, go to familjeapoteket.se). If you prefer a spray, forget the OFF! and opt for MaxMedica MyggA Spray. Another good one: NoSkito Mygglotion, (around $15). It’s easy to slather on and soothes skin with aloe vera.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vain Glorious | Bugs Be Gone', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insects', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T13:00:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allison Malecha', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allison', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Malecha', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36004ee2-7d60-5e52-a285-556d289acaa8', 'word_count': 162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36004ee2-7d60-5e52-a285-556d289acaa8'}, {'abstract': 'G.O.P. leaders and President Obama emerged from talks with a consensus to aim for the biggest possible deal — one resulting in up to $4 trillion in savings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/us/politics/08fiscal.html', 'snippet': 'G.O.P. leaders and President Obama emerged from talks with a consensus to aim for the biggest possible deal — one resulting in up to $4 trillion in savings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama, convening budget talks at the White House on Thursday, said Republicans and Democrats were still “far apart” but expressed confidence they could agree on an ambitious deal to prevent the government from defaulting on its debt.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/us/08fiscalspan/08fiscalspan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/08/us/08fiscalspan/08fiscalspan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/us/08fiscalspan/08fiscalspan-jumbo.jpg', 'hei