a region long known for abandoned coal mines and steep hills scarred by barbed-wire fences, military bunkers and minefields guarding against North Korea.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — When the town of Pyeongchang first pitched its Olympic dream 12 years ago, some International Olympic Committee members confused it with Pyongyang, the North Korean capital. Even within South Korea it was known until recently mainly for having bid unsuccessfully for the 2010 and 2014 Winter Games.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/sports/OLYMPICS1/OLYMPICS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 346, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/08/sports/OLYMPICS1/OLYMPICS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 346}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/sports/OLYMPICS1/OLYMPICS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 714, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/sports/OLYMPICS1/OLYMPICS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/08/sports/OLYMPICS1/OLYMPICS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Twice-Rejected S. Korean Town Lands 2018 Winter Games', 'kicker': 'Pyeongchang 2018', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Perseverance Pays Off', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2018)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pyeongchang (South Korea)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Internat