rt issued on Thursday says Americans have become increasingly obese over the last 20 years. The report, by Trust for America’s Health, a nonpartisan advocacy group, and the Robert Wood Johnson Foundation, tracks the level of obesity in the 50 states since 1990.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'F Is for Americans Getting Fatter', 'kicker': 'Prescriptions', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Obesity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Levi, Jeffrey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Johnson, Robert Wood, Foundation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T14:00:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Reed Abelson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Reed', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abelson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0286680-f622-50a6-bfea-bdf9134b767a', 'word_count': 498, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0286680-f622-50a6-bfea-bdf9134b767a'}, {'abstract': 'As the News Corporation battles a widening phone-hacking scandal, Rupert Murdoch is trying to keep a low profile at the annual Allen & Company conference in Sun Valley.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/the-elusive-rupert-murdoch/', 'snippet': 'As the News Corporation battles a widening phone-hacking scandal, Rupert Murdoch is trying to keep a low profile at the annual Allen & Company conference in Sun Valley.', 'lead_paragraph': '\xa0', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Elusive Rupert Murdoch', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T14:05:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Evelyn M. Rusli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Evelyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a422df4-9a47-5b6e-9983-565aaa27b796', 'word_count': 149, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a422df4-9a47-5b6e-9983-565aaa27b796'}, {'abstract': 'This week’s pairing: the poem “The Water Carriers” by Angelo Giambra and an article from Science Times about a scientist and author who studies bees, “Reports From the Hive, Where the Swarm Concurs.”', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/poetry-pairing-july-7-2011/', 'snippet': 'This week’s pairing: the poem “The Water Carriers” by Angelo Giambra and an article from Science Times about a scientist and author who studies bees, “Reports From the Hive, Where the Swarm Concurs.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In our weekly “Poetry Pairing” series, we collaborate with the Poetry Foundation to feature a work from its American Life in Poetry project alongside content from The Times that somehow echoes, extends or challenges the poem’s themes. Each poem is introduced briefly by Ted Kooser, a former United States poet laureate.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Poetry Pairing | July 7, 2011', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T14:16:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1583fd5-9710-5e9d-ae36-64d41ef16cef', 'word_count': 772, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1583fd5-9710-5e9d-ae36-64d41ef16cef'}, {'abstract': 'The voter-enthusiasm gap that really matters in Washington now wasn’t the one between the two parties — it was the one between conservative Republicans and everyone else, including moderate Republicans.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/why-the-g-o-p-cannot-compromise/', 'snippet': 'The voter-enthusiasm gap that really matters in Washington now wasn’t the one between the two parties — it was the one between conservative Republicans and everyone else, including moderate Republicans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The chart that I’m going to show you is one of the more important ones that we’ve presented at FiveThirtyEight in some time. It helps explain a lot of what’s going on in American politics today, from the negotiations over the federal debt ceiling to the Republican presidential primaries. And it’s pretty simple, really, although it took me some time to track down the data.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why the Republicans Resist Compromise', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T14:17:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5baef1c-3ad6-52de-ac3d-bd4aab55ca9e', 'word_count': 1410, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5baef1c-3ad6-52de-ac3d-bd4aab55ca9e'}, {'abstract': 'As new details emerge about a phone-hacking controversy, regulators are calling for a closer look at the media company’s bid to buy the British Sky Broadcasting Group, the latest challenge for the much-delayed deal.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/news-corp-scandal-could-hurt-bskyb-deal/', 'snippet': 'As new details emerge about a phone-hacking controversy, regulators are calling for a closer look at the media company’s bid to buy the British Sky Broadcasting Group, the latest challenge for the much-delayed deal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Amid the widening phone-hacking scandal, the News Corporation may find its deal-making ambitions diminished.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Corp. Scandal Could Hurt BSkyB Deal', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'British Sky Broadcasting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NEWS CORP', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News of the World', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T14:25:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris V. Nicholson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': 'V.', 'lastname': 'Nicholson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62658a3b-8160-564b-8ff7-f707e0870916', 'word_count': 466, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62658a3b-8160-564b-8ff7-f707e0870916'}, {'abstract': 'Moving spent fuel from pools to dry casks in the absence of a long-term repository has pluses and minuses. On the plus side, the radiation will diminish during dry-cask storage, meaning that the fuel will need less space at its burial site someday.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/haste-vs-procrastination-on-nuclear-waste/', 'snippet': 'Moving spent fuel from pools to dry casks in the absence of a long-term repository has pluses and minuses. On the plus side, the radiation will diminish during dry-cask storage, meaning that the fuel will need less space at its burial site someday...', 'lead_paragraph': 'As I noted in Wednesday’s paper, companies that operate nuclear reactors are increasingly turning to dry casks to store nuclear waste as their pools of spent fuel fill up. Some experts suggest that such casks should be used more widely to reduce the amount of fuel in the pools as a safety measure. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Haste vs. Procrastination on Nuclear Waste', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Energy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Wastes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radiation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Exelon Corp', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Illinois', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nevada', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yucca Mountain (Nev)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T14:27:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5bd83c91-ae74-5e7a-a008-625518eda5fb', 'word_count': 708, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5bd83c91-ae74-5e7a-a008-625518eda5fb'}, {'abstract': 'Rebekah Brooks, the chief executive of News International, Rupert Murdoch’s British newspaper subsidiary, has used a winning combination of charm, effrontery, audacity and tenacity to thrive.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/world/europe/08profile.html', 'snippet': 'Rebekah Brooks, the chief executive of News International, Rupert Murdoch’s British newspaper subsidiary, has used a winning combination of charm, effrontery, audacity and tenacity to thrive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — It was March 2003, and Rebekah Wade, then the editor of The Sun newspaper, was being interrogated by the House of Commons select committee on culture and the media. The topic: dubious tabloid practices.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/world/europe/08profile/08profile-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/08/world/europe/08profile/08profile-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/world/europe/08profile/08profile-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 755, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/world/europe/08profile/08profile-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/08/world/europe/08profile/08profile-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Tenacious Rise to the Top in the Brutal Men’s World of Tabloids', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Tenacious Rise to the Top in the Brutal Men’s World of Tabloids', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News International Ltd', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wiretapping and Other Eavesdropping Devices and Methods', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dowler, Milly', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brooks, Rebekah', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T14:32:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Lyall and Jo Becker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lyall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jo', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Becker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/12467de3-3f25-5e36-987e-76efe75b9501', 'word_count': 1885, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12467de3-3f25-5e36-987e-76efe75b9501'}, {'abstract': 'The stylist and editor in chief of his self-titled magazine discusses his liberal, mostly manicured and sometimes savage remake on the sex rag.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/asked-answered-andrew-richardson/', 'snippet': 'The stylist and editor in chief of his self-titled magazine discusses his liberal, mostly manicured and sometimes savage remake on the sex rag.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The stylist Andrew Richardson is a prime example of what the British really mean when they use the word “smart” — having that rare ability to weather the most indecent (or mundane) of circumstances with a show of dignity and class. As the editor in chief of Richardson magazine, a slow labor counting only five issues in 15 years, Richardson has parlayed his interests in post-punk glamour, Helmut Newton’s heroic erotica and transgressive comic books like Frigidaire into a range of professional experience, including a role in Madonna’s 1992 elegy to moral hang-ups, the “Sex” book, to become an agent provocateur of the most polished kind.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Asked & Answered | Andrew Richardson', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T14:33:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pierre Alexandre de Looz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pierre', 'middlename': 'Alexandre', 'lastname': 'de Looz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/10d06a8f-d06a-55c7-9ec8-7d4d82777ef4', 'word_count': 1760, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10d06a8f-d06a-55c7-9ec8-7d4d82777ef4'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links by the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/what-were-reading-220/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links by the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A collection of links by the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T14:33:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/764420f3-0d8c-540b-93df-d18cc3b5b7bc', 'word_count': 395, 'uri': 'nyt://article/764420f3-0d8c-540b-93df-d18cc3b5b7bc'}, {'abstract': 'Bret Michaels says his accident during the opening number of the 2009 Tony Awards led to a a hemorrhage he had near his brain, which required him to cancel several concerts.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/rock-stars-lawsuit-against-tony-awards-is-moved-to-new-york/', 'snippet': 'Bret Michaels says his accident during the opening number of the 2009 Tony Awards led to a a hemorrhage he had near his brain, which required him to cancel several concerts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bret Michaels will probably have a return engagement with the Tony Awards in New York – not to perform or present any trophies, but to pursue a lawsuit against the organizers of that show and CBS, which broadcast the program and the accident in which, Mr. Michaels said, he was nearly killed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rock Star’s Lawsuit Against Tony Awards Is Moved to New York', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tony Awards (Theater Awards)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Michaels, Bret', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corp', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Radio City Music Hall', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T14:46:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/453fad82-76e5-5f1d-ba0f-449d026d957e', 'word_count': 280, 'uri': 'nyt://article/453fad82-76e5-5f1d-ba0f-449d026d957e'}, {'abstract': 'It was a year into our relationship when my patient finally told me the truth. No wonder he couldn’t keep his medications straight.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/a-problem-in-following-doctors-orders/', 'snippet': 'It was a year into our relationship when my patient finally told me the truth. No wonder he couldn’t keep his medications straight.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mr. M was a typical new patient: 74, with diabetes, hypertension and elevated cholesterol. He had some prostate enlargement and back pain. His bag of pill bottles was depressingly bulky. I spilled the bottles out at our first visit, sorting them by disease.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Problem in Following Doctor’s Orders', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illiteracy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Longevity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T14:47:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Danielle Ofri, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Danielle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ofri', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/48fa4840-efbd-58e9-9cf7-9d34e6676d5d', 'word_count': 886, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48fa4840-efbd-58e9-9cf7-9d34e6676d5d'}, {'abstract': 'TerraCycle is preparing a new program to collect and recycle waste — but will consumers pay for the shipping?', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/what-if-we-just-tell-everyone-to-send-us-their-waste/', 'snippet': 'TerraCycle is preparing a new program to collect and recycle waste — but will consumers pay for the shipping?', 'lead_paragraph': 'I started TerraCycle almost a decade ago with a goal of making a profit by eliminating waste, and today our company offers free collection programs for more than 45 waste streams in the United States, along with similar programs in 15 other countries. The premise is simple: sign up on our Web site, fill a box with a specific type of waste, send it TerraCycle and we’ll donate 2 cents (or the foreign equivalent) for every unit of waste to the charity or school of your choice.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What If We Just Tell Everyone to Send us Their Waste?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Waste Materials and Disposal', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TerraCycle', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T15:00:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Szaky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Szaky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d52312dc-ceeb-5889-9a9d-ac764b186a02', 'word_count': 814, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d52312dc-ceeb-5889-9a9d-ac764b186a02'}, {'abstract': 'But nobody will believe it.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/contraction-still-contractionary/', 'snippet': 'But nobody will believe it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new paper from the IMF (pdf) puts another nail in the coffin of the doctrine of expansionary austerity. It basically shows that results purporting to show economic expansion following spending cuts and/or tax increases were based on a statistical illusion: an expanding economy can often lead to rising revenue and/or falling spending (e.g. because safety-net spending falls or because the government cuts back in an attempt to cool off inflationary pressures). And as a result, what the Alesina-Ardagna results capture is muddle by reverse causation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Contraction, Still Contractionary', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T15:09:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a02b5699-48e1-55ce-85b0-835d02dea454', 'word_count': 264, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a02b5699-48e1-55ce-85b0-835d02dea454'}, {'abstract': 'A new United Nations report strongly criticizes Israel for using live fire against unarmed demonstrators who tried in May to breach its border fence from Lebanon.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/world/middleeast/08mideast.html', 'snippet': 'A new United Nations report strongly criticizes Israel for using live fire against unarmed demonstrators who tried in May to breach its border fence from Lebanon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — A new United Nations report that has been distributed to members of the Security Council strongly criticizes Israel for using live fire against unarmed demonstrators who tried in May to breach its border fence from Lebanon. Israel is planning to respond in detail shortly in a letter to Secretary General Ban Ki-moon, officials here said Thursday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.N. Report Criticizes Israel for Actions at Border', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.N. Report Criticizes Israeli Role in Deaths at Border', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lebanon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Security Council (UN)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boycotts', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T15:11:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Kershner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e077d90e-616d-5954-96b3-1dd7517e20e1', 'word_count': 710, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e077d90e-616d-5954-96b3-1dd7517e20e1'}, {'abstract': 'The leading Internet service providers have agreed to a procedure for notifying customers about repeated instances of digital copyright infringement.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/internet-providers-to-help-thwart-online-piracy/', 'snippet': 'The leading Internet service providers have agreed to a procedure for notifying customers about repeated instances of digital copyright infringement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a deal with the major entertainment media companies that has been years in the making, the leading Internet service providers have agreed to a uniform procedure for notifying customers about repeated instances of digital copyright infringement.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Internet Providers to Help Thwart Online Piracy', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Copyrights and Copyright Violations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T15:12:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a06c8164-5853-54f1-898f-ec5a7b5e17b2', 'word_count': 475, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a06c8164-5853-54f1-898f-ec5a7b5e17b2'}, {'abstract': 'A day ahead of the government’s monthly unemployment report, surveys of jobless benefit claims and new-job creation gave economists reason for optimism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/business/economy/data-point-to-growth-in-jobs-in-june.html', 'snippet': 'A day ahead of the government’s monthly unemployment report, surveys of jobless benefit claims and new-job creation gave economists reason for optimism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New claims for unemployment benefits in the United States declined last week to the lowest level in nearly two months, according to a government survey on Thursday, while a separate report on jobs from the payroll processing company ADP was better than economists had forecast.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Jobs Reports Point To a Higher Gain in June', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Two Jobs Reports Point To a Higher Gain in June', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ADP Employer Services', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T15:17:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2595918e-231b-5ce7-b754-19c228ec2cba', 'word_count': 544, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2595918e-231b-5ce7-b754-19c228ec2cba'}, {'abstract': 'David I. Weprin, a 55-year-old state lawmaker and former city councilman, will face a Republican candidate in a special election in September.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/david-weprin-chosen-by-democrats-to-run-for-weiners-seat/', 'snippet': 'David I. Weprin, a 55-year-old state lawmaker and former city councilman, will face a Republican candidate in a special election in September.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For decades, David I. Weprin has played the role of good Democratic soldier, the scion of a vaunted Queens political family who repeatedly won elections as a city councilman and currently as a state assemblyman.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Democrats Pick David Weprin, an Assemblyman, to Run for Weiner’s Seat', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weiner, Anthony D', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weprin, David I', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'City Council (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T15:17:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7d84d30-f44b-5258-be47-f1a862af04ef', 'word_count': 810, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7d84d30-f44b-5258-be47-f1a862af04ef'}, {'abstract': 'The newest member of the Board of Visitors at West Point will be its first openly gay or lesbian member.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/opening-doors-at-west-point/', 'snippet': 'The newest member of the Board of Visitors at West Point will be its first openly gay or lesbian member.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Brenda S. Fulton graduated in the West Point class of 1980, the first to include women. In a few weeks she will return to the military academy in another historic role: as the first openly gay or lesbian member of its Board of Visitors, which advises the president on all things West Point. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Opening Doors at West Point', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Military Academy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T15:19:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Dao', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dao', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6d9e500-865e-5719-b8a5-399d3d64d7d5', 'word_count': 988, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6d9e500-865e-5719-b8a5-399d3d64d7d5'}, {'abstract': 'Motherlode is apparently a very small world, and a mother explains, after recognizing herself described in the comments.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/the-mother-of-the-noisy-child-responds/', 'snippet': 'Motherlode is apparently a very small world, and a mother explains, after recognizing herself described in the comments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It has always been the goal to create a “small world” feel here on Motherlode. I hadn’t realized how small it had become until one reader recognized herself in another reader’s comments last week. She would like to explain. And ask your advice about her trip home:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Mother of the Noisy Child Responds', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crying', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Noise', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T15:21:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'origi