urt. She was confirmed two months later, becoming the first woman to serve on the nation’s highest court.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'July 7, 1981 | Reagan Nominates O’Connor, First Woman, for Supreme Court', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T18:02:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/91a83af3-08fc-5a9c-a015-bfcdabb6d116', 'word_count': 419, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91a83af3-08fc-5a9c-a015-bfcdabb6d116'}, {'abstract': 'Indian artists’ depictions of the Hindu god Vishnu in his many forms make up the show “Vishnu: Hinduism’s Blue-Skinned Savior,” at the Brooklyn Museum.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/arts/design/vishnu-hinduisms-savior-at-brooklyn-museum-review.html', 'snippet': 'Indian artists’ depictions of the Hindu god Vishnu in his many forms make up the show “Vishnu: Hinduism’s Blue-Skinned Savior,” at the Brooklyn Museum.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hindu sculptures are no ordinary things. They’re cosmic implosions, concentrations of spiritual energy so dense as to turn physics inside out. They funnel light from other universes into our mundane world. And they do so consciously, with intent.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/arts/VISHNU-span/JP-VISHNU-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/08/arts/VISHNU-span/JP-VISHNU-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': No