siness is booming. After working with several local architecture firms, Joshua Howell, Justin Rice and Kagan Taylor decided to strike out on their own. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Seeing Things | Hammer Time', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T18:21:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooke Hodge', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooke', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hodge', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72fb2351-cbd1-59b4-80c8-7a68bfd050e3', 'word_count': 290, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72fb2351-cbd1-59b4-80c8-7a68bfd050e3'}, {'abstract': 'Warren Buffett of Berkshire Hathaway, which gave Goldman Sachs a crucial lifeline during the financial crisis, wants the investment bank’s chief executive to stay.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/buffett-hearts-blankfein/', 'snippet': 'Warren Buffett of Berkshire Hathaway, which gave Goldman Sachs a crucial lifeline during the financial crisis, wants the investment bank’s chief executive to stay.', 'lead_paragraph': '\xa0', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Buffett Hearts Blankfein', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blankfein, Lloyd C', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Buffett, Warren E', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Allen & Company', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Berkshire Hathaway Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date