ent-keeps-viewers-transfixed/', 'snippet': 'Some 12.5 million people watched the NBC show Wednesday night.', 'lead_paragraph': '“America’s Got Talent” had another night on top of the ratings as 12.5 million viewers tuned in to NBC’s reality competition on Wednesday, according to Nielsen’s estimates. The hourlong episode at 9 p.m. far exceeded the ratings for any other program on the night, lifting NBC to No. 1 in prime time, even as the rest of the network’s programs lagged behind in their respective time slots.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘America’s Got Talent’ Keeps Viewers Transfixed', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Anthony, Casey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC INC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nielsen Media Research', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T19:02:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Toff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Toff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4866b39b-5512-5865-8088-21644af32fea', 'word_count': 172, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4866b39b-5512-5865-8088-21644af32fea'}, {'abstract': 'President Ali Abdullah Saleh of Yemen appeared on television Thursday for the first time since he was injured in a bombing of his presidential compound’s mosque a month ago.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/world/middleeast/08saleh.html', 'snippet': 'President Ali Abdullah Saleh of Yemen appeared on television Thursday for the first time since he was injured in a bombing of his presidential compound’s mosque a month ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SANA, Yemen — President Ali Abdullah Saleh of Yemen appeared on television Thursday for the first time since he was injured in a bombing of his presidential compound’s mosque a month ago. The prerecorded broadcast from Saudi Arabia, where he has been recuperating since the attack, showed him speaking with difficulty, with a red Saudi headdress and a darkened face from the severe burns he suffered. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/world/middleeast/08saleh/08saleh-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 655, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/world/middleeast/08saleh/08saleh-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/08/world/middleeast/08saleh/08saleh-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Yemen President Speaks on TV for First Time Since Injury', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Injured President Speaks on TV for First Time Since Attack', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saleh, Ali Abdullah', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T19:04:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_des