paragraph': 'Pauline Gordon wants to know where her savings are.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shift in Treasuries System Vexes Older Investors', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Bonds', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maryland', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T19:12:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c1811c4-3784-5208-929c-65b1b1ac3c7d', 'word_count': 615, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c1811c4-3784-5208-929c-65b1b1ac3c7d'}, {'abstract': 'MasterCard Worldwide is expanding its efforts to bring its long-running “Priceless” advertising campaign to life.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/mastercard-brings-priceless-to-a-pricey-place/', 'snippet': 'MasterCard Worldwide is expanding its efforts to bring its long-running “Priceless” advertising campaign to life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MasterCard Worldwide is expanding its efforts to bring its long-running “Priceless” advertising campaign to life.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'MasterCard Brings ‘Priceless’ to a Pricey Place', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MasterCard Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T19:26:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5d9956d-a59b-51d3-9554-60e014ee220d', 'word_count': 663, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5d9956d-a59b-51d3-9554-60e014ee220d'}, {'abstract': 'Open-window policy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/10/magazine/the-ethicist-hot-and-bothered.html', 'snippet': 'Open-window policy.', 'lead_paragraph': ' I work with a dozen others in a city office building. One colleague says that she has an autoimmune disease. She says that we must keep the windows in our small office closed at all times; if we open them, she becomes ill. With no ventilation, the temperature reaches the high 70s. Our boss has offered her a separate room, but she refuses to move from our shared space. What is the right thing to do? We are all miserable, and productivity is at an all-time low. B.S., NEW YORK', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/02/28/magazine/ethicist-image/ethicist-image-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 391, 'width': 610, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/02/28/magazine/ethicist-image/ethicist-image-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/02/28/magazine/ethicist-image/ethicist-image-