tomobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Stenquist', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stenquist', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/221a19af-c703-58f0-a90a-6b3591477a3d', 'word_count': 513, 'uri': 'nyt://article/221a19af-c703-58f0-a90a-6b3591477a3d'}, {'abstract': 'When the very presence of equipment offends a colleague.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/offended-by-an-office-breast-pump/', 'snippet': 'When the very presence of equipment offends a colleague.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It has been nearly a year since a reader, T., wrote asking for advice on becoming a family of four. Her son arrived in November, and, in spite of T.’s fears (and, perhaps, because of your wise advice) the transition of her daughter has been relatively smooth.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Offended by an Office Breast Pump', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Breastfeeding', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T19:41:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Belkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/962d1556-ff62-5599-96b9-32d745acbc8d', 'word_count': 466, 'uri': 'nyt://article/962d1556-ff62-5599-96b9-32d745acbc8d'}, {'abstract': '“All My Children” and “One Life to Live,” soap operas canceled by ABC three months ago, will be given a second life online by Prospect Park, a two-year-old media and production company.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/canceled-abc-soaps-find-new-home-online/', 'snippet': '“All My Children” and “One Life to Live,” soap operas canceled by ABC three months ago, will be given a second life online by Prospect Park, a two-year-old media and production company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Three months after ABC canceled the soap operas “All My Children” and “One Life to Live,” the network said Thursday that the shows would be given a second life online by Prospect Park, a two-year-old media and production company.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Canceled ABC Soaps Find New Home Online', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'One Life to Live (TV Program)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soap Operas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC INC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T19:45:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cfc60acc-6b3b-534b-9074-b8800b486d49', 'word_count': 480, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cfc60acc-6b3b-534b-9074-b8800b486d49'}, {'abstract': 'In recent years, the financially troubled Greater New York Councils of the Boy Scouts of America had warned it might have to close Pouch Camp, but the Trust for Public Land has come to the rescue.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/staten-islands-imperiled-boy-scout-haven-is-saved/', 'snippet': 'In recent years, the financially troubled Greater New York Councils of the Boy Scouts of America had warned it might have to close Pouch Camp, but the Trust for Public Land has come to the rescue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pouch Camp, the wooded Boy Scout camp on Staten Island that for 60 years has provided the pleasures of overnight camping and summer day camp for thousands of boys and girls, will be saved under an agreement announced this week. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Staten Island’s Imperiled Boy Scout Haven Is Saved', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Camps and Camping', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boy Scouts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Trust for Public Land', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Staten Island (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T19:46:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph Berger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Berger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7f892ae-6e3e-5222-bcd9-d6f50d04a9a2', 'word_count': 340, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7f892ae-6e3e-5222-bcd9-d6f50d04a9a2'}, {'abstract': 'Thousands of New York immigrants threatened with deportation relied on the Rev. Robert Vitaglione, who has been barred from handling cases.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/nyregion/priests-former-caseload-exposes-holes-in-immigration-courts.html', 'snippet': 'Thousands of New York immigrants threatened with deportation relied on the Rev. Robert Vitaglione, who has been barred from handling cases.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For more than three decades, Robert Vitaglione never turned down a client, representing thousands of immigrants in New York’s overburdened federal immigration courts. But he is not a lawyer. He is a Roman Catholic priest without formal legal training or supervision — and it showed.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/nyregion/08FATHERBOB/08FATHERBOB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 367, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/08/nyregion/08FATHERBOB/08FATHERBOB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 367}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/nyregion/08FATHERBOB/08FATHERBOB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/nyregion/08FATHERBOB/08FATHERBOB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/08/nyregion/08FATHERBOB/08FATHERBOB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Removal of Priest’s Cases Exposes Deep Holes in Immigration Courts', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Removal of Priest’s Cases Exposes Deep Holes in Immigration Courts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration Detention', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Priests', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legal Aid for the Poor', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T19:58:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Dolnick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dolnick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/036b7334-1167-58b3-a67e-8b098dc8abff', 'word_count': 1328, 'uri': 'nyt://article/036b7334-1167-58b3-a67e-8b098dc8abff'}, {'abstract': 'Lovers of bold stripes and prints rejoice! A trove of vintage Marikmekko clothes goes on sale next week at 1stdibs.com.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/pattern-boldness-marimekko/', 'snippet': 'Lovers of bold stripes and prints rejoice! A trove of vintage Marikmekko clothes goes on sale next week at 1stdibs.com.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bold stripes and prints may be all the rage right now (think Marni, Jil Sander, Prada), but Marimekko has been doing them for years — 60 to be exact, when the designer Armi Ratia and her husband, Viljo, took over a small Finnish textile company, Printex, and reinvented it with a graphic sensibility and an optimistic, almost utopian, outlook, not just as a global lifestyle brand but as a way of life. Jackie Kennedy wore a red Marimekko dress on the cover of Sports Illustrated in 1960; the Marimekko unisex Even Stripe T-shirt was a fixture on the rock and jazz festival circuit in the ’70s. Today, there is no shortage of new Marimekko material around thanks to collaborations with the likes of Crate and Barrel and Converse; and a free-standing Marimekko shop is scheduled to open in the Flatiron district in the fall. But true believers should get their clicker fingers in shape for July 13, when a trove of vintage Marimekko goes on sale on 1stdibs in conjunction with Katy Kane Vintage and Couture Clothing. The perfect, plain shirtdresses, matching jacket and shorts ensembles in unfussy floral prints and breezy striped shifts all came from a single owner, a Westchester-area homemaker, with very progressive taste. When she found a style she liked, she bought it in multiples. That orange and blue awning stripe shirt a little too bold for your taste? It’s also available in ivory and blue. What is more, many of the pieces were never worn and are still wrapped in tissue paper — and are as fresh and new as the day they were designed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pattern Boldness | Marimekko', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Marimekko', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T20:00:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alix Browne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alix', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Browne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc77152d-259a-56c3-89c1-c5d0f00c5cad', 'word_count': 283, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc77152d-259a-56c3-89c1-c5d0f00c5cad'}, {'abstract': 'The strike has been organized by inmates at Pelican Bay State Prison’s security housing unit. The prisoners are kept in extreme isolation, which they call cruel and unusual.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/us/08hunger.html', 'snippet': 'The strike has been organized by inmates at Pelican Bay State Prison’s security housing unit. The prisoners are kept in extreme isolation, which they call cruel and unusual.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Thousands of inmates at prisons throughout California have been refusing state-issued food in a mass hunger strike to protest conditions at the state’s highest-security prisons, where some inmates are kept in prolonged isolation. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/us/08hunger_span/08hunger_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/08/us/08hunger_span/08hunger_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/us/08hunger_span/08hunger_span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 702, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/us/08hunger_span/08hunger_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/08/us/08hunger_span/08hunger_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hunger Strike by Inmates Is Latest Challenge to California’s Prison System', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'California Inmates Fast to Protest Isolation Cells', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hunger Strikes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T20:02:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Lovett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lovett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/67187189-48bf-5959-914d-c70cf3be3cc5', 'word_count': 827, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67187189-48bf-5959-914d-c70cf3be3cc5'}, {'abstract': '“Warm Up,” an annual summer party, mixes family fun, music and contemporary art.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/07/10/nyregion/20110710JOINTss.html', 'snippet': '“Warm Up,” an annual summer party, mixes family fun, music and contemporary art.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Warm Up,” an annual summer party, mixes family fun, music and contemporary art.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/nyregion/20110710JOINTss-slide-FJGG/20110710JOINTss-slide-FJGG-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/nyregion/20110710JOINTss-slide-FJGG/20110710JOINTss-slide-FJGG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/10/nyregion/20110710JOINTss-slide-FJGG/20110710JOINTss-slide-FJGG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Neighborhood Joint | MoMA PS1', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'PS 1 Contemporary Art Center', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island City (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T20:02:47+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'New York', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/1e327580-d9f0-535c-99dd-218aeb01d740', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/1e327580-d9f0-535c-99dd-218aeb01d740'}, {'abstract': 'New York has been a melting pot of national ballet companies of late.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/07/10/arts/dance/20110710-mariinsky_slide.html', 'snippet': 'New York has been a melting pot of national ballet companies of late.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York has been a melting pot of national ballet companies of late.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/arts/20110710-mariinsky_slide-slide-G603/20110710-mariinsky_slide-slide-G603-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Greetings From Russia; The Feet Will Follow', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kirov Ballet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T20:02:59+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Arts', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/95e593a6-097d-58d9-8209-26ca8f8373a9', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/95e593a6-097d-58d9-8209-26ca8f8373a9'}, {'abstract': 'Words or music? The one that drives the work helps define whether it’s an opera or a musical.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/10/theater/musical-or-opera-the-fine-line-that-divides-them.html', 'snippet': 'Words or music? The one that drives the work helps define whether it’s an opera or a musical.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MORE than ever, composers are busily breaking down walls between stylistic categories. Opera in particular has been a poacher’s paradise. We have had folk opera, jazz opera and rock opera. Bono, who collaborated with the Edge on the music and lyrics of “Spider-Man: Turn Off the Dark,” called the show “Pop-Art opera.” Whatever that means. But of all such efforts, mixing opera with the Broadway musical might seem by far the most natural combination.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/theater/10musical1_span/10musical1_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/10/theater/10musical1_span/10musical1_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/theater/10musical1_span/10musical1_span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/theater/10musical1_span/10musical1_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/10/theater/10musical1_span/10musical1_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Opera? Musical? Please Respect the Difference', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Opera? Musical? Please Respect The Difference', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T20:14:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Tommasini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tommasini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c550cc3-d33c-50be-973d-5c1993c2d22d', 'word_count': 2022, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c550cc3-d33c-50be-973d-5c1993c2d22d'}, {'abstract': 'More of that darn evidence. Don’t tell Obama.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/more-anti-austerianism/', 'snippet': 'More of that darn evidence. Don’t tell Obama.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Via Philip Lane, a paper from the BIS (pdf) analyzing in detail four famous alleged cases of expansionary austerity. The bottom line: none of them show what they were supposed to show. Instead, all they show is that if you have austerity policies at the same time that other big expansionary things are happening, the economy may actually expand.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Anti-Austerianism', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T20:15:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/15220082-db84-5727-b5ed-d665a17a5d9f', 'word_count': 90, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15220082-db84-5727-b5ed-d665a17a5d9f'}, {'abstract': 'A scene from "The Sleeping Beauty," directed by Catherine Breillat.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/movies/100000000898940/exclusive-clip-the-sleeping-beauty.html