 who called homosexuality “completely unnatural.”', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/bad-week-for-gay-rights-on-the-subcontinent/', 'snippet': 'The same week that support for gay rights by America’s ambassador in Islamabad was denounced as “cultural terrorism” against Pakistan, Indians debated a statement by their health minister, who called homosexuality “completely unnatural.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated | Friday | 10:14 a.m. Conservatives in India and Pakistan don’t tend to agree on much, but this week they have found a sliver of common ground: That homosexuality is a treacherous import, brought to the Asian subcontinent by the West. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bad Week for Gay Rights on the Subcontinent', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Azad, Ghulam Nabi', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T22:13:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth A. Harris and Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e75e003c-afda-574c-889f-8a46d1acbb12', 'word_count': 715, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e75e003c-afda-574c-889f-8a46d1acbb12'}, {'abstract': 'N.Y. See: a summer storm greets an actor emerging from an audition. And some other passers-by, too.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/west-49th-street-407-p-m/', 'snippet': 'N.Y. See: a summer storm greets an actor emerging from an audition. And some other passers-by, too.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mallory Maskornick was greeted by a summer storm as she emerged from an audition for “Godspell” at St. Malachy’s church.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'West 49th Street, 4:07 P.M.', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T22:15:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25f09f7b-c5ba-5645-883d-c8f8e913c5d6', 'word_count': 20, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25f09f7b-c5ba-5645-883d-c8f8e913c5d6'}, {'abstract': 'Charlie Gasparino, a senior correspondent for Fox Business Network, exercises in a New York City park almost every day.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/arts/charlie-gasparinos-workout-partner-is-a-new-york-city-park.html', 'snippet': 'Charlie Gasparino, a senior correspondent for Fox Business Network, exercises in a New York City park almost every day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE EAST RIVER PARK in Lower Manhattan was animated on a recent morning: against a backdrop of the city skyline and the boat-dotted water, groups of children played on lush lawns, sunbathers basked in the sun’s glow and joggers ran by on the paved path. And at the playground, Charlie Gasparino was in the middle of a grueling workout. Using the monkey bars, he did more than a dozen sets of pull-ups — some including as many as 30 — and alternated them with fast-paced push-ups. He was soaked in sweat in just 15 minutes and still had another hour to go. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/arts/URBAN-span/URBAN-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/08/arts/URBAN-span/URBAN-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/arts/URBAN-span/URBAN-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 696, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/arts/URBAN-span/URBAN-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/08/arts/URBAN-span/URBAN-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'His Workout Partner? The City', 'kicker': 'Urban Athlete', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'His Workout Partner? The City', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gasparino, Charlie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T22:15:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shivani Vora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shivani', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/103cecef-d394-5023-8dc7-a690641a15b5', 'word_count': 764, 'uri': 'nyt://article/103cecef-d394-5023-8dc7-a690641a15b5'}, {'abstract': 'Images from “Vishnu: Hinduism’s Blue-Skinned Savior,” at the Brooklyn Museum.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/07/07/arts/design/20110708-vishnu.html', 'snippet': 'Images from “Vishnu: Hinduism’s Blue-Skinned Savior,” at the Brooklyn Museum.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Images from “Vishnu: Hinduism’s Blue-Skinned Savior,” at the Brooklyn Museum.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/07/arts/design/20110708-vishnu-slide-86KZ/20110708-vishnu-slide-86KZ-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 588, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/07/arts/design/20110708-vishnu-slide-86KZ/20110708-vishnu-slide-86KZ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/07/arts/design/20110708-vishnu-slide-86KZ/20110708-vishnu-slide-86KZ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Forms of a God', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hinduism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Museum', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T22:16:54+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Arts', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/ac7a57b9-4c37-5b1d-9dd9-e19c4ca2db55', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/ac7a57b9-4c37-5b1d-9dd9-e19c4ca2db55'}, {'abstract': 'Q-Tip will headline the Brooklyn Hip-Hop festival, and the Civil War is remembered at Green-Wood Cemetery.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/arts/brooklyn-hip-hop-festival-with-q-tip.html', 'snippet': 'Q-Tip will headline the Brooklyn Hip-Hop festival, and the Civil War is remembered at Green-Wood Cemetery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Do you remember how to kick it with A Tribe Called Quest? The legendary Tribe took a different approach to hip-hop in the early 1990s, blending Afro-centric rhymes with jazz and promoting social change through its music. This year’s Brooklyn Hip-Hop Festival, which begins on Monday, seeks to do the same with the help of a Tribe member, Q-Tip, who is the headliner at the festival.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/arts/MISER-span/MISER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 342, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/08/arts/MISER-span/MISER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 342}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/arts/MISER-span/MISER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 661, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/arts/MISER-span/MISER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/08/arts/MISER-span/MISER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Weekend Miser', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Weekend Miser', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T22:17:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Lee Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': 'Lee', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8574d63-bbbd-525d-8ae8-8b574b3d8890', 'word_count': 452, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8574d63-bbbd-525d-8ae8-8b574b3d8890'}, {'abstract': 'A selection of classical music and opera listings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/arts/music/classical-music-and-opera-listings.html', 'snippet': 'A selection of classical music and opera listings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Classical', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Classical Music and Opera Listings', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Listings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T22:21:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d3ad75c-1311-5c9c-bf80-3c914f581628', 'word_count': 1574, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d3ad75c-1311-5c9c-bf80-3c914f581628'}, {'abstract': 'Saying yes to adventure, and then thinking better of it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/10/magazine/lives-of-spelunkers-and-he-men.html', 'snippet': 'Saying yes to adventure, and then thinking better of it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s impossible to look cool when you’re part of a tour group. Instead of bravely exploring on your own, you’ve chosen to be led around like a frightened kindergartner. My wife and I were on a tour bus while in Hawaii recently, and our guide made me feel even more uncool because he was very rugged and handsome. After a couple of hours, he announced we were stopping for what he called “snack break,” as if we actually were kindergartners. He then mentioned that down a nearby path there was a cave we could check out. Not being a terrorist mastermind, I’ve never had a huge desire to hang out in a cave. But the opinion of absolute strangers means a lot to me, and I was desperate to differentiate myself from the other travelers in this cool, rugged guide’s eyes. ', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '50', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/magazine/10lives/10lives-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 966, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/magazine/10lives/10lives-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/10/magazine/10lives/10lives-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Too Deep', 'kicker': 'Lives', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Too Deep', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Caves and Caverns', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T22:21:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Ruprecht', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ruprecht', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2afa1329-3c13-5ba5-8ef7-725a22516c10', 'word_count': 788, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2afa1329-3c13-5ba5-8ef7-725a22516c10'}, {'abstract': 'A selection of films and movies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/movies/movies-and-film-series-listing.html', 'snippet': 'A selection of films and movies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Movies', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Movies and Film Series Listing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Listings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T22:24:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/26dbf245-5ba8-563a-839d-2e1609c908b6', 'word_count': 2055, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26dbf245-5ba8-563a-839d-2e1609c908b6'}, {'abstract': 'The interior secretary cuts a deal with the state’s governor requiring Wyoming to maintain just 100 wolves and 10 breeding pairs outside Yellowstone Park.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/wolves-lose-federal-protection-in-wyoming/', 'snippet': 'The interior secretary cuts a deal with the state’s governor requiring Wyoming to maintain just 100 wolves and 10 breeding pairs outside Yellowstone Park.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In another blow to the wolf, the secretary of the interior, Ken Salazar, said Thursday that he had struck a deal with Gov. Matt Mead of Wyoming to take the state’s wolves off the endangered species list and out from under federal protection. Wyoming has long agitated to have the wolves delisted so that hunting could be broadened under state regulations. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wolves Could Lose Federal Protection in Wyoming', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Chan