': {'original': 'Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/6a469683-04cc-5bf6-b739-e4d8cba06d98', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/6a469683-04cc-5bf6-b739-e4d8cba06d98'}, {'abstract': 'With the aid of the European Space Agency’s Herschel Space Observatory, astronomers detected enough cosmic dust, emitted from a supernova first seen almost 25 years ago, to form 200,000 Earths.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/science/12obnova.html', 'snippet': 'With the aid of the European Space Agency’s Herschel Space Observatory, astronomers detected enough cosmic dust, emitted from a supernova first seen almost 25 years ago, to form 200,000 Earths.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Although it is known that a supernova, the violent explosion of a star, is one source of cosmic dust, the origin of the large amounts of dust needed to form planets and stars like the Sun has long been unclear.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/12/science/12obnova/12obnova-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/12/science/12obnova/12obnova-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/12/science/12obnova/12obnova-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 783, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/12/science/12obnova/12obnova-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/12/science/12obnova/12obnova-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cosmic Dust, Detected in Colossal Quantities', 'kicker': 'Observatory', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cosmic Dust, Detected In Colossal Quantities', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stars and Galaxies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Astronomy and Astrophysics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telescopes and Observatories', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T22:55:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sindya N. Bhanoo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sindya', 'middlename': 'N.', 'lastname': 'Bhanoo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/814513e9-b268-5d03-b61a-c84916f942a8', 'word_count': 299, 'uri': 'nyt://article/814513e9-b268-5d03-b61a-c84916f942a8'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Carpenter did groundbreaking work in anthropological filmmaking and ethnomusicology and, with his friend Marshall McLuhan, laid the foundations of modern media studies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/arts/edmund-carpenter-archaelogist-and-anthropologist-dies-at-88.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Carpenter did groundbreaking work in anthropological filmmaking and ethnomusicology and, with his friend Marshall McLuhan, laid the foundations of modern media studies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Edmund Carpenter, an archaeologist and anthropologist who, impatient with traditional boundaries between disciplines, did groundbreaking work in anthropological filmmaking and ethnomusicology and, with his friend Marshall McLuhan, laid the foundations of modern media studies, died on July 1 in Southampton, N.Y. He was 88.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/arts/08carpenter/08carpenter-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 279, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/08/arts/08carpenter/08carpenter-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 279}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/arts/08carpenter/08carpenter-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 477, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/arts/08carpenter/08carpenter-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/08/arts/08carpenter/08carpenter-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Edmund Carpenter, Archaeologist and Anthropologist, Dies at 88', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Edmund Carpenter, Restless Scholar, Dies at 88', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHAEOLOGY AND ANTHROPOLOGY', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carpenter, Edmund', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T23:12:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Grimes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grimes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/046bfbdc-0bcc-5aa0-9f25-8192a3eff51a', 'word_count': 1002, 'uri': 'nyt://article/046bfbdc-0bcc-5aa0-9f25-8192a3eff51a'}, {'abstract': 'Basic economics dictates that fiscal responsibility does not require banning deficits.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/the-trouble-with-balanced-budgets/', 'snippet': 'Basic economics dictates that fiscal responsibility does not require banning deficits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I realize they may just be practicing politics, but Senators Olympia Snowe and Jim DeMint serve up a basic misunderstanding of economics in their commentary on The Wall Street Journal’s op-ed page today. Ms. Snowe, a Republican from Maine, and Mr. DeMint, a Republican from South Carolina, write:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Trouble With Balanced Budgets', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitutional Amendments', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DeMint, Jim', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snowe, Olympia J', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T23:17:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0001198-fb1f-502e-9aa0-45bbea982fef', 'word_count': 545, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0001198-fb1f-502e-9aa0-45bbea982fef'}, {'abstract': 'Paul Giamatti plays King John, who signed the Magna Carta and regretted it, in “Ironclad,” a medieval battle film directed by Jonathan English.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/movies/ironclad-with-paul-giamatti-and-derek-jacobi-review.html', 'snippet': 'Paul Giamatti plays King John, who signed the Magna Carta and regretted it, in “Ironclad,” a medieval battle film directed by Jonathan English.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It can be tough to see the story in “Ironclad” for all the squirting blood and the severed tongues, feet, hands and heads — never mind the mighty distractions provided by some seriously furious eyeball-rolling. Many of the most frenzied ocular calisthenics are provided by Paul Giamatti, who also gives his English accent a vigorous workout to play King John. This was the 13th-century monarch who waged a battle royal against the barons who had forced him to sign the Magna Carta, a foundational document of modern democracy and an absurd excuse for such go-go gore.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/arts/IRONCLAD-span/IRONCLAD-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/08/arts/IRONCLAD-span/IRONCLAD-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/arts/IRONCLAD-span/IRONCLAD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 967, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/arts/IRONCLAD-span/IRONCLAD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/08/arts/IRONCLAD-span/IRONCLAD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Grant a Few Rights, See What Happens?', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Ironclad'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Grant a Few Rights, See What Happens?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giamatti, Paul', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T23:22:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/63c773e7-81be-5287-ba1e-8352e8d45b31', 'word_count': 626, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63c773e7-81be-5287-ba1e-8352e8d45b31'}, {'abstract': 'The Dodgers wanted documents ranging from those showing how baseball has treated other teams to Bud Selig’s approval of TV deals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/sports/baseball/dodgers-denied-access-to-mlb-files-in-bankruptcy-court.html', 'snippet': 'The Dodgers wanted documents ranging from those showing how baseball has treated other teams to Bud Selig’s approval of TV deals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Dodgers’ attempt to show that Major League Baseball is treating them punitively was rejected Thursday by a bankruptcy court judge in Delaware who ruled that the trove of evidence they sought was not relevant to the issue of the team’s interim financing.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dodgers Denied Access to M.L.B. Files', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dodgers Denied Access to M.L.B. Files', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCourt, Frank H Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Dodgers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Selig, Bud', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T23:29:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/02c52e34-7fb2-5492-b3be-d9e2427588b8', 'word_count': 227, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02c52e34-7fb2-5492-b3be-d9e2427588b8'}, {'abstract': 'Bill Keller, who has been The Times’s executive editor for eight years, calls himself a “collapsed Catholic.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/10/books/review/up-front-bill-keller.html', 'snippet': 'Bill Keller, who has been The Times’s executive editor for eight years, calls himself a “collapsed Catholic.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Through the years, The New York Times’s coverage of the Roman Catholic Church and the Vatican has received sharp criticism from practicing Catholics — including the past eight years that Bill Keller has been the paper’s executive editor. Yet Keller, who wrote this week’s cover review of “Absolute Monarchs: A History of the Papacy,” by John Julius Norwich, was raised within the fold.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/books/review/Upfront/Upfront-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 589, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/books/review/Upfront/Upfront-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/10/books/review/Upfront/Upfront-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Up Front: Bill Keller', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Up Front', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keller, Bill', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T23:29:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editors', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editors'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/daa7c5e1-13b4-535c-be3b-15f2f70847fd', 'word_count': 265, 'uri': 'nyt://article/daa7c5e1-13b4-535c-be3b-15f2f70847fd'}, {'abstract': 'John Julius Norwich’s popular history of the papacy finds that the truly great popes were outnumbered by the corrupt, the inept, the venal, the lecherous and the mediocre.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/10/books/review/book-review-absolute-monarchs-a-history-of-the-papacy-by-john-julius-norwich.html', 'snippet': 'John Julius Norwich’s popular history of the papacy finds that the truly great popes were outnumbered by the corrupt, the inept, the venal, the lecherous and the mediocre.', 'lead_paragraph': 'John Julius Norwich makes a point of saying in the introduction to his history of the popes that he is “no scholar” and that he is “an agnostic Protestant.” The first point means that while he will be scrupulous with his copious research, he feels no obligation to unearth new revelations or concoct revisionist theories. The second means that he has “no ax to grind.” In short, his only agenda is to tell us the story.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/books/review/Keller/Keller-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 851, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/books/review/Keller/Keller-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/10/books/review/Keller/Keller-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '2,000 Years of Popes, Sacred and Profane', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sacred and Profane', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Norwich, John Julius', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Popes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Priests', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T23:29:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Keller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c841c0ba-c96a-5480-8d9f-2fc1f0ef893b', 'word_count': 1366, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c841c0ba-c96a-5480-8d9f-2fc1f0ef893b'}, {'abstract': 'A film that looks to ask questions about faith and the existence of God, “The Ledge” features a man threatening to leap off a building.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/movies/the-ledge-with-charlie-hunnam-review.html', 'snippet': 'A film that looks to ask questions about faith and the existence of God, “The Ledge” features a man threatening to leap off a building.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Will he or won’t he? Jump that is. And what on earth could be bugging him? Those questions may or (more likely) may not grip you while watching Matthew Chapman’s contrived psychological thriller, “The Ledge.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/arts/LEDGE-span/LEDGE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/08/arts/LEDGE-span/LEDGE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/arts/LEDGE-span/LEDGE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 539, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/arts/LEDGE-span/LEDGE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/08/arts/LEDGE-span/LEDGE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Looking for Answers Before He Leaps', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'The Ledge'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Looking for Answers Before He Leaps', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hunnam, Charlie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, Patrick', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Howard, Terrence', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T23:33:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/cae33d58-6784-525f-a96b-26504704f14d', 'word_count': 554, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cae33d58-6784-525f-a96b-26504704f14d'}, {'abstract': 'Robert S. Ford, the American ambassador to Syria, made an unannounced visit on Thursday to Hama, a central Syrian city that has become a focal point for the four-month uprising.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/world/middleeast/08syria.html', 'snippet': 'Robert S. Ford, the American ambassador to Syria, made an unannounced visit on Thursday to Hama, a central Syrian city that has become a focal point for the four-month uprising.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — Robert S. Ford, the American ambassador to Syria, made an unannounced visit on Thursday to Hama, a central Syrian city that has become a focal point for the four-month uprising against President Bashar al-Assad. Mr. Ford’s visit came as security forces rounded up what some activists described as hundreds of people in the city and a day ahead of what are expected to be mass protests there. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'American Ambassador to Syria Visits Focal Point in Uprising', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'American Ambassador to Syria Visits Focal Point in Uprising', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ford, Robert S', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T23:37:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nada Bakri', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nada', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakri', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c92ce99-c0a7-575a-bc33-b3ff59a192ac', 'word_count': 595, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c92ce99-c0a7-575a-bc33-b3ff59a192ac'}, {'abstract': '“Sholem Aleichem: Laughing in the Darkness” is a film biography not just of a writer but of a culture.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/movies/sholem-aleichem-laughing-in-the-darkness-review.html', 'snippet': '“Sholem Aleichem: Laughing in the Darkness” is a film biography not just of a writer but of a culture.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Sholem Aleichem: Laughing in the Darkness” is much more than a documentary biography of “the Jewish Mark Twain,” as the creator of Tevye the Dairyman, Menachem-Mendl and other beloved folkloric characters has been called. It is a rich, beautifully organized and illustrated modern history of Eastern European Jewry examined through the life and work of the author, born Sholem Rabinovich in Pereyaslav (near Kiev) in 1859. His literary pseudonym was derived from the Hebrew expression “shalom aleichem,” meaning “peace be with you.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/arts/SUB-SHOLEM/SUB-SHOLEM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 848, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/arts/SUB-SHOLEM/SUB-SHOLEM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/08/arts/SUB-SHOLEM/SUB-SHOLEM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'So, Would It Hurt You to Go See a Documentary About a Yiddish Writer?', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Sholem Aleichem: Laughing in the Darkness'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'So, Would It Hurt You to Go See a Documentary About a Yiddish Writer?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALEICHEM, SHOLEM', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dorman, Joseph', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Yiddish Language', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T23:41:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c4a744cd-0f74-5c69-b54e-2c44ddc9a4e4', 'word_count': 890, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4a744cd-0f74-5c69-b54e-2c44ddc9a4e4'}, {'abstract': 'How one Web site capitalized on the bonds among friends to mobilize people in New York’s gay marriage campaign.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/on-gay-rights-moving-real-life-friends-to-action/', 'snippet': 'How one Web site capitalized on the bonds among friends to mobilize people in New York’s gay marriage campaign.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The successful battle for gay marriage legislation in New York State involved the debut of an intriguing new way to apply social media to social change: Friendfactor.\xa0 While the precise role it played in the law’s passage is unclear, Friendfactor offered \xa0a new model for online organizing that could become very useful in similar rights campaigns.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Gay Rights, Moving Real-Life Friends to Action', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Friendship', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook.com', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tahrir Square (Cairo)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T23:43:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tina Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd8e0e52-ba74-5042-8fda-a9a1410932aa', 'word_count': 1020, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd8e0e52-ba74-5042-8fda-a9a1410932aa'}, {'abstract': 'The potential acquisition of Energy Capital highlights Carlyle’s drive to broaden itself ahead of an initial public offering.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/carlyle-is-said-to-be-in-talks-with-energy-buyout-shop/', 'snippet': 'The potential acquisition of Energy Capital highlights Carlyle’s drive to broaden itself ahead of an initial public offering.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The private equity giant Carlyle Group is in talks to acquire Energy Capital Partners, a buyout shop focused on investments in power plants and gas pipelines, according to two people briefed on the talks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Carlyle Is Said to Be in Talks With Energy Buyout Shop', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carlyle Group', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T23:44:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/02d72ea4-c01f-54f2-94ac-0ef09e489148', 'word_count': 856, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02d72ea4-c01f-54f2-94ac-0ef09e489148'}, {'abstract': 'The automaker is offering a one-year MetLife policy as an incentive to lure buyers into showrooms in Oregon and Washington.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/07/to-combat-lax-sales-g-m-offers-free-insurance-to-buyers-in-pacific-northwest/', 'snippet': 'The automaker is offering a one-year MetLife policy as an incentive to lure buyers into showrooms in Oregon and Washington.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You might remember the car-dealer refrain, “Buy a car, get a check,” or those once-ubiquitous friends and family discounts. In the Pacific Northwest, General Motors is putting another twist on the incentive game, offering a year of free car insurance.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'To Combat Lax Sales, G.M. Offers Free Insurance to Buyers in Pacific Northwest', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Insurance and Liability', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MetLife Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pacific Northwestern States (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Portland (Ore)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Seattle (Wash)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T23:50:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Micheline Maynard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Micheline', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Maynard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/986e4841-9fe4-589d-b90f-5581f56946fb', 'word_count': 605, 'uri': 'nyt://article/986e4841-9fe4-589d-b90f-5581f56946fb'}, {'abstract': 'Katherine Mangu-Ward, left, of Reason and Erica Grieder of The Economist debate the future of space travel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/opinion/100000000899479/the-last-space-shuttle.html', 'snippet': 'Katherine Mangu-Ward, left, of Reason and Erica Grieder of The Economist debate the future of space travel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Katherine Mangu-Ward, left, of Reason and Erica Grieder of The Economist debate the future of space travel.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/07/opinion/video-bhshuttle/video-bhshuttle-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/07/opinion/video-bhshuttle/video-bhshuttle-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/07/opinion/video-bhshuttle/video-bhshuttle-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/07/opinion/video-bhshuttle/video-bhshuttle-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bloggingheads: The Last Space Shuttle', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'SPACE SHUTTLE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privatization', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-07T23:51:37+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Opinion', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'None None', 'person': [{'firstname': 'None', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'None', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/8a16e249-de1e-59cd-b7cb-5c30d527f4a4', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/8a16e249-de1e-59cd-b7cb-5c30d527f4a4'}, {'abstract': 'Pressure to cut the federal budget may outweigh support for the subsidies as consensus builds that the ethanol industry has achieved financial stability.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/business/energy-environment/corn-ethanol-subsidies-may-be-in-jeopardy.html', 'snippet': 'Pressure to cut the federal budget may outweigh support for the subsidies as consensus builds that the ethanol industry has achieved financial stability.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Federal subsidies for corn ethanol have long been considered untouchable in Washington — not least because politicians want the votes of Iowans, who have traditionally held the first nominating caucuses in the contest for the presidency.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/business/ETHANOL/ETHANOL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 325, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/08/business/ETHANOL/ETHANOL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 325}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/business/ETHANOL/ETHANOL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 645, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/business/ETHANOL/ETHANOL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/08/business/ETHANOL/ETHANOL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ethanol Subsidies Besieged', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ethanol Subsidies Besieged', 'n