“last look” at bids submitted by its competitors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JPMorgan Chase reached a $211 million settlement with federal and state authorities on Thursday to resolve allegations that it cheated governments in 31 states by rigging the bidding process for reinvesting the proceeds of dozens of municipal bond transactions. \xa0\xa0', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'JPMorgan Settles Bond Bid-Rigging Case for $211 Million', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'JPMorgan Settles Bond Bid-Rigging Case for $211 Million', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Municipal Bonds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'UBS AG', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JPMorgan Chase & Company', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T01:29:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Dash', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dash', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f6c7eed-e46d-530b-9c49-e1251bcb349e', 'word_count': 652, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f6c7eed-e46d-530b-9c49-e1251bcb349e'}, {'abstract': 'Russia, the world’s fourth-largest gold producer, has been selling in international markets, in part to offset its budget deficit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/business/global/russia-sells-gold-as-world-prices-rise.html', 'snippet': 'Russia, the world’s fourth-largest gold producer, has been selling in international markets, in part to offset its budget deficit.', 'lead_paragraph': ' ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/business/Gold1/Gold1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 696, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/business/Gold1/Gold1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/08/business/Gold1/Gold1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'As More Investors Seek Shelter in Gold, Russia Is Only Too Happy to Sell', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As More Investors Seek Shelter in Gold, Russia Is Only Too Happy to Sell', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gold', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Bank of Russia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T01:37:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew E. Kramer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Kramer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d36bf78-89bb-5b62-89a7-38988591e6d4', 'word_count': 1001, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d36bf78-89bb-5b62-89a7-38988591e6d4'}, {'abstract': 'The White House and Republicans are holding the economy hostage while they remain in a deadlock over how to pay the nation’s bills.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/opinion/08fri1.html', 'snippet': 'The White House and Republicans are holding the economy hostage while they remain in a deadlock over how to pay the nation’s bills.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every fresh report of “progress” on the debt-ceiling talks produces new reasons to feel profoundly uneasy. The talks were misbegotten from the beginning, made necessary only by the irresponsible refusal of Republicans to pay the nation’s bills unless they got everything their way on government spending and taxes. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Negotiating on a Knife’s Edge', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Negotiating on a Knife’s Edge: The danger of expanding the debt-limit talks with the economy held hostage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fourteenth Amendment (US Constitution)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitution (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T01:41:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc428739-40ad-5e86-b6a9-2680abbc9b98', 'word_count': 701, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc428739-40ad-5e86-b6a9-2680abbc9b98'}, {'abstract': 'Adm. Mike Mullen said he believed the Pakistani government was involved in the death of a journalist who had written critical reports.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/world/asia/08mullen.html', 'snippet': 'Adm. Mike Mullen said he believed the Pakistani government was involved in the death of a journalist who had written critical reports.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Adm. Mike Mullen, chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff, said Thursday that he believed that the government of Pakistan had “sanctioned” the killing of a Pakistani journalist who had written scathing reports about the infiltration of Islamic militants into the country’s security services.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Admiral Ties Pakistan to Killing of Journalist', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Admiral Ties Pakistan To Killing Of Journalist', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classified Information and State Secrets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mullen, Michael G', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T01:42:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Bumiller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bumiller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae4fe055-0dca-544c-9962-38485c5c9dfc', 'word_count': 770, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae4fe055-0dca-544c-9962-38485c5c9dfc'}, {'abstract': 'The killing of the journalist Syed Saleem Shahzad has raised many troubling questions about Pakistan’s spy agency. The agency urgently needs reform.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/opinion/08fri2.html', 'snippet': 'The killing of the journalist Syed Saleem Shahzad has raised many troubling questions about Pakistan’s spy agency. The agency urgently needs reform.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After the Pakistani journalist Syed Saleem Shahzad was murdered in May, suspicion fell on Inter-Services Intelligence, the country’s powerful spy agency. Mr. Shahzad reported aggressively on the infiltration of militants into Pakistan’s military and had received repeated threats from ISI. Other journalists said they, too, have been threatened, even tortured, by security forces.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Pakistani Journalist’s Murder', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Pakistani Journalist’s Murder: Implicated in the killing, Pakistan’s spy agency urgently needs reform', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pasha, Ahmed Shuja', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shahzad, Syed Saleem', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Inter-Services Intelligence', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T01:44:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/4438cce0-d711-529b-beb1-d5e03232fa7a', 'word_count': 487, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4438cce0-d711-529b-beb1-d5e03232fa7a'}, {'abstract': 'Way before “Gidget” and the Beach Boys, surfing was a sport in Hawaii. Two new books and a film are reclaiming that story.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/opinion/08fri4.html', 'snippet': 'Way before “Gidget” and the Beach Boys, surfing was a sport in Hawaii. Two new books and a film are reclaiming that story.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Forget, for a moment, what you know about surfing: the professional sport, the multipurpose verb and online metaphor. Put aside the Beach Boys, the baggies, the huarache sandals, too. Surfing’s all that. But those bushy bushy blond hairdos have dark brown roots.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/07/opinion/editorial_surfing/editorial_surfing-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 470, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/07/opinion/editorial_surfing/editorial_surfing-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 470}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/07/opinion/editorial_surfing/editorial_surfing-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 803, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/07/opinion/editorial_surfing/editorial_surfing-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1606, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/07/opinion/editorial_surfing/editorial_surfing-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'lega