to respond to the Obama administration’s decision to participate in the NATO-led air war.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'House Sends Conflicting Signals on Libya', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'House Sends Conflicting Signals on Libya', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cole, Tom', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T03:04:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c284f6c-7136-5e74-8471-3620c198805f', 'word_count': 432, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c284f6c-7136-5e74-8471-3620c198805f'}, {'abstract': 'In “John Carpenter’s The Ward” there is much to remind the viewer of a director’s past heyday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/movies/john-carpenters-the-ward-review.html', 'snippet': 'In “John Carpenter’s The Ward” there is much to remind the viewer of a director’s past heyday.', 'lead_paragraph': '“John Carpenter’s The Ward,” his first feature since the disappointing “Ghosts of Mars” (2001), continues the painful decline of a director who seems more nostalgic for past glories than excited about new ideas. Quaintly old-fashioned in style, plot and special effects, this familiar tale of female derangement and institutional abuse is too tame to scare and too shallow to engage.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/arts/WARD-span/WARD-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 365, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/08/arts/WARD-span/WARD-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 365}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/arts/WARD-span/WARD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 986, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/arts/WARD-span/WARD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/08/arts/WARD-span/WARD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Young, Cute and Menaced, Per Usual', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'John Carpenter’s The Ward'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Young, Cute and Menaced, Per Usual', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carpenter, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gummer, Mamie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Heard, Amber', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harris, Jared', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T03:05:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeannette Catsoulis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeannette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Catsoulis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0695482-9e5f-5bf6-a382-e5f61a9c3fda', 'word_count': 568, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0695482-9e5f-5bf6-a382-e5f61a9c3fda'}, {'abstract': 'Shortages of fuel, personnel and weapons make it unlikely that the rebels will try to take Tripoli, said a colonel who claimed he defected from Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi’s army.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/world/africa/08libya.html', 'snippet': 'Shortages of fuel, personnel and weapons make it unlikely that the rebels will try to take Tripoli, said a colonel who claimed he defected from Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi’s army.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RUJBAN, Libya — For months now, military leaders in the rebel capital, Benghazi, have boldly predicted lightning advances by their fighters and an imminent rout of the forces loyal to Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi in Tripoli that would finally snuff out his brutal four-decade rule. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/world/08libya/08libya-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/08/world/08libya/08libya-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/world/08libya/08libya-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 803, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/world/08libya/08libya-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/08/world/08libya/08libya-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Senior Rebel Is Doubtful Qaddafi Can Be Routed', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Senior Rebel Is Doubtful Qaddafi Can Be Routed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defectors (Political)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qaddafi, Muammar el-', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T03:06:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kareem Fahim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kareem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fahim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97429157-01a2-51c3-9f08-c7d46ee4f927', 'word_count': 963, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97429157-01a2-51c3-9f08-c7d46ee4f927'}, {'abstract': 'With no laws governing the use of physical restraint with unruly students in California schools, questions have arisen as to whether the practice should be overseen more carefully.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/us/08bcrestraint.html', 'snippet': 'With no laws governing the use of physical restraint with unruly students in California schools, questions have arisen as to whether the practice should be overseen more carefully.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Corporal punishment is illegal in California public schools, but physically restraining unruly students is not. As incidents of restraint, seclusion and other emergency interventions have soared in recent years, schools have relied on training programs and physical restraint protocols developed by private companies that in many cases appear to have few qualifications.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/us/08BCRESTRAINT1/08BCRESTRAINT1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 700, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Questions Are Raised on Restraint Training', 'kicker': 'The Bay Citizen', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Questions Are Raised On Restraint Training', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'School Discipline (Students)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T03:09:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Gollan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gollan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3027c85b-3177-5803-907d-de35bf639b89', 'word_count': 1571, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3027c85b-3177-5803-907d-de35bf639b89'}, {'abstract': 'An international commission concluded that both former President Manuel Zelaya and those who overthrew him share blame for the June 2009 coup.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/world/americas/08briefs-BOTHSIDESINC_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'An international commission concluded that both former President Manuel Zelaya and those who overthrew him share blame for the June 2009 coup.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An international commission set up to study the June 2009 Honduran coup concluded that both former President Manuel Zelaya as well as the political leaders and military officers who overthrew him share blame for how the crisis unfolded. The panel’s report, released in Tegucigalpa on Thursday, rejected the assertion by much of the country’s political elite that Mr. Zelaya’s overthrow was legal and said instead it met every definition of a coup. But Eduardo Stein, who led the commission, said it had also found that Mr. Zelaya had violated laws as he pressed ahead with plans to hold a referendum on whether to revise the constitution. Opponents said Mr. Zelaya had hoped to win changes that would allow his re-election. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Honduras: Both Sides in Coup Blamed', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | THE AMERICAS', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Honduras: Both Sides in Coup Blamed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Coups D'Etat and Attempted Coups D'Etat", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Honduras', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zelaya Rosales, Jose Manuel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T03:10:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Malkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Malkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/fadc2896-978e-5802-a4a3-9b91e7c5562b', 'word_count': 120, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fadc2896-978e-5802-a4a3-9b91e7c5562b'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Mackey fought against free-agency restrictions as the president of the league’s players union, in addition to becoming one of the N.F.L.’s greatest tight ends.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/sports/football/john-mackey-dies-at-69-helped-revolutionize-nfl.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Mackey fought against free-agency restrictions as the president of the league’s players union, in addition to becoming one of the N.F.L.’s greatest tight ends.', 'lead_paragraph': 'John Mackey, who bowled over defensive linemen and streaked past pass defenders as one of the N.F.L.’s greatest tight ends, then fought against free-agency restrictions as the president of the league’s players union, died on Wednesday in Baltimore. He was 69.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/sports/obit-mackey-1/obit-mackey-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/08/sports/obit-mackey-1/obit-mackey-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/sports/obit-mackey-1/obit-mackey-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 653, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/sports/obit-mackey-1/obit-mackey-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/08/sports/obit-mackey-1/obit-mackey-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'John Mackey Dies at 69; Helped Revolutionize N.F.L.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'John Mackey Dies at 69; Helped Revolutionize N.F.L.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mackey, John', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T03:11:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Goldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0dcab19-885a-5056-a0ff-560258876b3d', 'word_count': 978, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0dcab19-885a-5056-a0ff-560258876b3d'}, {'abstract': 'Developments, in response to the rise of a new generation of black theatergoers, will include the announcement of a new artistic director and a cultural center in Uptown.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/us/08cnctheater.html', 'snippet': 'Developments, in response to the rise of a new generation of black theatergoers, will include the announcement of a new artistic director and a cultural center in Uptown.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Compared to the rest of Chicago’s theater community, where companies can rise, fall and change directions seemingly from show to show, black theaters have been a bastion of stability — or, according to some critics, stasis. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19B', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/us/08CNCTHEATER/08CNCTHEATER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/08/us