mmarie Huetteman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emmarie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Huetteman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a0ed6004-7ff2-51ad-b80b-8a1017576107', 'word_count': 381, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a0ed6004-7ff2-51ad-b80b-8a1017576107'}, {'abstract': 'Since 2005, though, the Bohemia Jazz Festival has brought renowned musicians to city squares across the Czech Republic for free open-air concerts. This year’s Prague edition runs July 12 and 13.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/jazz-festival-roams-czech-city-squares/', 'snippet': 'Since 2005, though, the Bohemia Jazz Festival has brought renowned musicians to city squares across the Czech Republic for free open-air concerts. This year’s Prague edition runs July 12 and 13.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Prague’s musical heritage is no secret, but often it is restrained to concert halls and the occasional club. Since 2005, though, the Bohemia Jazz Festival has brought renowned musicians to city squares across the Czech Republic for free open-air concerts. The festival, the brainchild of the Czech-American jazz musician Rudy Linka, runs in Prague’s Old Town Square on July 12 and 13. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jazz Festival Roams Czech City Squares', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Festivals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Prague (Czech Republic)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T10:00:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jacy Meyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jacy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Meyer', 'qualifier': 