day Reading: G.M. Offers Free Insurance in Two States', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T14:04:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8fd5f066-f709-5b41-93d3-da2ee528b54a', 'word_count': 150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8fd5f066-f709-5b41-93d3-da2ee528b54a'}, {'abstract': 'Researchers suggest that 12,000 to 24,000 tons of plastic a year is swallowed by fish at intermediate depths of the North Pacific alone.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/fish-ingesting-plastic-waste-study-finds/', 'snippet': 'Researchers suggest that 12,000 to 24,000 tons of plastic a year is swallowed by fish at intermediate depths of the North Pacific alone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than 250 million tons of plastic is produced around the world each year. About seven million tons of it ends up in the world’s oceans, according to some estimates.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fish Ingesting Plastic Waste, Study Finds', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish and Other Marine Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oceans and Seas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Plastics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Waste Materials and Disposal', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 