es's executive editor Bill Keller reviews “Absolute Monarchs: A History of the Papacy,” by John Julius Norwich; Eva Gabrielsson talks about her life with Stieg Larsson, author of the Millenium Trilogy; Julie Bosman has notes from...", 'lead_paragraph': "This week, The Times's executive editor Bill Keller reviews “Absolute Monarchs: A History of the Papacy,” by John Julius Norwich; Eva Gabrielsson talks about her life with Stieg Larsson, author of the Millenium Trilogy; Julie Bosman has notes from the field; and Jennifer Schuessler has best-seller news. Sam Tanenhaus is the host.", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A history of the papacy, life with Stieg Larsson, notes from the field and best-seller news', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T16:00:23+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/4a8e6a75-25de-5efe-9a37-ae6c7eb597f6', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/4a8e6a75-25de-5efe-9a37-ae6c7eb597f6'}, {'abstract': 'A decade’s worth of Harry Potter movies required lots of off-screen wizards. Now the gig of a lifetime has reached its happy ending.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/10/magazine/harry-potters-sorcerers-of-stagecraft.html', 'snippet': 'A decade’s worth of Harry Potter movies required lots of off-screen wizards. Now the gig of a lifetime has reached its happy ending.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Finally, as the posters proclaim, “It All Ends.” Not just the eight-part cinematic saga of Harry Potter (with his Chamber of Secrets, his Goblet of Fire, his Deathly Hallows and so on) but also a decade’s worth of craftsmanship for those toiling off-camera: the ones who clothed the Hogwarters, wrangled the owls, built the snitch, tweaked the goblins and crafted the wands — around 600 wands in all, including backups, duplicates and those made specially for fighting. ', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/magazine/Harry-Potter-slide-4KP4/Harry-Potter-slide-4KP4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/magazine/Harry-Potter-slide-4KP4/Harry-Potter-slide-4KP4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/10/magazine/Harry-Potter-slide-4KP4/Harry-Potter-slide-4KP4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Sorcerers of Stagecraft', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Sorcerers of Stagecraft', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Warner Brothers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T16:02:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Craig Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Craig', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/23ec4e84-094a-5f08-a001-06c6fc68e354', 'word_count': 417, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23ec4e84-094a-5f08-a001-06c6fc68e354'}, {'abstract': 'Readers respond.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/10/magazine/i-illegal-immigrant.html', 'snippet': 'Readers respond.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In his article about his life in America as an undocumented immigrant, Jose Antonio Vargas addressed an issue that should upset us all. I knew Jose when I was his speech coach at Mountain View High School. I didn’t know he was illegal but rather knew him as one of the hardest-working members of the team. I remember working with him to more clearly enunciate in a highly competitive endeavor. He was driven, and he was successful. Yes, he has broken our laws. So have many on Wall Street, who simply paid money, got a slap on the hand and went on to make a lot more money. Jose is a hero \xad— my hero. He worked to be the best he could be, asking nothing of our country beyond the right to stay where his mother sent him as a young boy. He is another example of why we need to pass the Dream Act.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'I, Illegal Immigrant', 'kicker': 'Reply All | Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'I, Illegal Immigrant', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigrants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizenship and Naturalization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T16:08:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/864b6687-373d-5192-a164-7ce71d4405b1', 'word_count': 607, 'uri': 'nyt://article/864b6687-373d-5192-a164-7ce71d4405b1'}, {'abstract': 'A look at how many jobs the economy needs to add before returning to prerecession employment levels.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/comparing-recessions-and-recoveries-job-changes-2/', 'snippet': 'A look at how many jobs the economy needs to add before returning to prerecession employment levels.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Source: Bureau of Labor Statistics. Chart by Amanda Cox. Horizontal axis shows months. Vertical axis shows the ratio of that month’s nonfarm payrolls to the nonfarm payrolls at the start of recession. Note: Because employment is a lagging indicator, the dates for these employment trends are not exactly synchronized with National Bureau of Economic Research’s official business cycle dates.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Comparing Recessions and Recoveries: Job Changes', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T16:10:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7e58b51-18a0-5989-b96b-5055e38ecf40', 'word_count': 343, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7e58b51-18a0-5989-b96b-5055e38ecf40'}, {'abstract': 'Governor Cuomo replaced his current top aide, Steven M. Cohen, with Mr. Schwartz, who had the same crucial job for Governor Paterson.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/cuomo-picks-schwartz-to-be-new-top-aide/', 'snippet': 'Governor Cuomo replaced his current top aide, Steven M. Cohen, with Mr. Schwartz, who had the same crucial job for Governor Paterson.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a shakeup of his senior staff, Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo on Friday appointed Lawrence S. Schwartz, a senior adviser in his administration, to be his top aide. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cuomo Picks Schwartz to Be New Top Aide', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Governors (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cohen, Steven M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schwartz, Lawrence S', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T16:10:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Danny Hakim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Danny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hakim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9d937f0-7105-5e31-af04-f306317edabe', 'word_count': 394, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9d937f0-7105-5e31-af04-f306317edabe'}, {'abstract': 'Readers respond.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/10/magazine/b-day-d-day.html', 'snippet': 'Readers respond.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pardon me if I don’t shed a tear over these multimillionaires’ having to retire early because their idiosyncratic skills — of no value to society as a whole — fade in their 30s. (“For Derek Jeter, on His 37th Birthday,” by Michael Sokolove.) Meanwhile there are millions like me, in their 40s and still paying school debts, with no hope of ever retiring. Poor Derek!', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'B-Day D-Day', 'kicker': 'Reply All | Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'B-Day D-Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jeter, Derek', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T16:12:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0f33e87-f8e7-56c5-ae64-a443f7c89f61', 'word_count': 230, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0f33e87-f8e7-56c5-ae64-a443f7c89f61'}, {'abstract': 'A road trip through British Columbia, Yukon and Alaska.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/07/10/travel/07102011ARCTIC.html', 'snippet': 'A road trip through British Columbia, Yukon and Alaska.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A road trip through British Columbia, Yukon and Alaska.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/07/travel/arctic-promo/arctic-promo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/07/travel/arctic-promo/arctic-promo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/07/travel/arctic-promo/arctic-promo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Journey to the Arctic Circle', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALASKA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Road Trips', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T16:14:49+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow'