agraph': 'BETHLEHEM, West Bank — Israel prevented a gathering of foreigners here on Friday by blocking, deterring or deporting hundreds of air travelers who had been invited by Palestinian activists to fly into Israel’s Ben-Gurion International Airport and then travel to the West Bank for a week of “fellowship and actions.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/09/world/middleeast/09mideast/09mideast-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/09/world/middleeast/09mideast/09mideast-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/09/world/middleeast/09mideast/09mideast-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/09/world/middleeast/09mideast/09mideast-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/09/world/middleeast/09mideast/09mideast-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Israel Blocks Air Travelers to Palestinian Conference', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Israel Blocks Air Travelers to Palestinian Conference', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Council of Churches', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netanyahu, Benjamin', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T17:35:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Kershner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f76223b-ab11-5f19-ad5b-89ea02950baa', 'word_count': 981, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f76223b-ab11-5f19-ad5b-89ea02950baa'}, {'abstract': 'Mathilde Laurent, Cartier’s chic head perfumer, had men on her mind while creating Baiser Volé, the house’s latest women’s scent.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/sexual-preference-men-who-buy-perfume-for-women/', 'snippet': 'Mathilde Laurent, Cartier’s chic head perfumer, had men on her mind while creating Baiser Volé, the house’s latest women’s scent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mathilde Laurent, Cartier’s chic head perfumer, had men on her mind while creating Baiser Volé, the house’s latest women’s scent. “I noticed that when asked about their favorite flower, many men said it was the lily,” she says. “Of course women can choose perfume for themselves, but what’s wrong with putting the man in the equation?” Baiser Volé bucks the trend for “sickly” or “sugary” florals, and it took Laurent two years to capture the fresh yet heady essence of a bouquet of just-cut lilies. The bottle, which was inspired by the company’s famously elegant cigarette lighters, is as come-hither as the pale pink juice it contains, lending a whole new meaning to the term “smoking.” It’s $100 for 1.6 ounces at Nordstrom stores.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vain Glorious | Sexual Preference', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Perfumes and Fragrances', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T17:36:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sandra Ballentine', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ballentine', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/941d332a-cc7b-5dbf-8047-a854fb608a7e', 'word_count': 125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/941d332a-cc7b-5dbf-8047-a854fb608a7e'}, {'abstract': 'The TNT series will revisit the the rivalry between brothers J. R. and Bobby Ewing while chronicling a new feud, between their offspring.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/oil-aboard-tnt-orders-new-dallas-series-for-next-summer/', 'snippet': 'The TNT series will revisit the the rivalry between brothers J. R. and Bobby Ewing while chronicling a new feud, between their offspring.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Don your 10-gallon hat, buy some oil-rich property, cheat your relatives out of their birthrights and do whatever it is J. R. Ewing used to do if you can still remember: “Dallas” is coming back to television. TNT said on Friday that it had officially ordered 10 episodes of a new series based on that 1980s-era prime-time soap opera, updating the internal rivalries of the Ewing family for the 21st century while incorporating several characters from the original show. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Oil Aboard! TNT Orders New ‘Dallas’ Series for Next Summer', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value