, 'snippet': 'The weekly rank of the four titles that have been on the children’s paperback chapter list the most over the past year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The weekly rank of the four titles that have been on the children’s paperback chapter list the most over the past year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Best Sellers Weekly Graphic: What Kids Have Been Reading', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T18:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Books', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/2193efa7-93af-5ff3-84fd-636a77863cde', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/2193efa7-93af-5ff3-84fd-636a77863cde'}, {'abstract': 'Feasting on poets and writers on the subject of food.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/more-cakes-and-ale-literary-food-issues/', 'snippet': 'Feasting on poets and writers on the subject of food.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Lucky Peach is a fast-selling sensation, yes, but the Momofuku-meets-McSweeney’s magazine is not the only literary grub pub hitting newsstands this summer. (There are still newsstands, right?)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Cakes and Ale: Literary Food Issues', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Lapham's Quarterly", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'POETRY MAGAZINE', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T18:01:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_de