ticle/7a3631b8-4b11-54db-a048-1b1aafae8eed'}, {'abstract': 'In practice, we’re doing it.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/austerity-usa/', 'snippet': 'In practice, we’re doing it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m not the only one making this point, but when you hear Republicans saying that what we need to do to create jobs is slash government spending and cut government payrolls, that’s exactly what has been happening for the past year, as the Obama stimulus has faded out. Here’s government employment (that bulge was Census hiring):', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Austerity USA', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T18:05:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/85408f2f-d49f-50d0-aed5-037237eb77fe', 'word_count': 100, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85408f2f-d49f-50d0-aed5-037237eb77fe'}, {'abstract': 'A view of the day in sports, with flowery scenes in France and barreling race cars in Great Britain.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/07/08/sports/20110708-photoreplay.html', 'snippet': 'A view of the day in sports, with flowery scenes in France and barreling race cars in Great Britain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A view of the day in sports, with flowery scenes in France and barreling race cars in Great Britain.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/sports/20110708-photoreplay-slide-19KU/20110708-photoreplay-slide-19KU-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 524, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/sports/20110708-photoreplay-slide-19KU/20110708-photoreplay-slide-19KU-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/08/sports/20110708-photoreplay-slide-19KU/20110708-photoreplay-slide-19KU-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Photo Replay: July 8', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tour de France (Bicycle Race)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Davis Cup', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Scottish Open (Golf)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rowing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T18:13:30+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/63ae1e57-4739-517a-8d4a-ceca0c28c48a', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/63ae1e57-4739-517a-8d4a-ceca0c28c48a'}, {'abstract': 'The multi-hyphenate talks about his second feature television documentary, his solo show of paintings and where he spends his downtime.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/the-lowdown-daniel-peddle/', 'snippet': 'The multi-hyphenate talks about his second feature television documentary, his solo show of paintings and where he spends his downtime.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Daniel Peddle is having a busy summer. Fresh off a plane from Paris, where he was working on casting for men’s fashion shows, he just closed a solo show of paintings at NP Contemporary Art Center in New York. Originally from Winston-Salem, N.C., and now based in the West Village, Peddle came to our fair city in 1992 to study film at N.Y.U. While he was trying to scrape by in the grime that was the early 1990s, his keen eye for beauty led him to the unlikely grind that is street casting. Today, his eponymous company scouts talent for the likes of Phillip Lim, M.A.C. cosmetics, Givenchy and many others. In the meantime, he’s working on his third feature documentary, and his second, “Trail Angels,” about the altruistic souls who tend to the hikers on the six-month journey down the Appalachian Trail, will be make its debut on the Documentary Channel tomorrow night.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Lowdown | Daniel Peddle', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T18:15:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By IO Tillett Wright', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Io', 'middlename': 'Tillett', 'lastname': 'Wright', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cfb50762-ae52-513e-9e19-932f742c0cc9', 'word_count': 310, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cfb50762-ae52-513e-9e19-932f742c0cc9'}, {'abstract': 'An app for anglers shows a map of fishing spots nearby, or on a list, in order of proximity.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/app-smart-extra-gone-fishin/', 'snippet': 'An app for anglers shows a map of fishing spots nearby, or on a list, in order of proximity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week’s App Smart column includes a list of useful boating apps, but it ignores what is, for many boaters, their raison d’etre: fishing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'App Smart Extra: Gone Fishin’', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T18:19:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bob Tedeschi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tedeschi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac230961-acb6-5c45-b009-71ae990eff62', 'word_count': 263, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac230961-acb6-5c45-b009-71ae990eff62'}, {'abstract': 'Newt Gingrich’s loss is Michele Bachmann’s gain as she seeks to expand beyond the grassroots to attract high-dollar contributions.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/bachmann-adds-staff-to-court-major-donors/', 'snippet': 'Newt Gingrich’s loss is Michele Bachmann’s gain as she seeks to expand beyond the grassroots to attract high-dollar contributions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Representative Michele Bachmann, in her bid for the Republican presidential nomination, is beefing up her fund-raising operation as she begins to seek the allegiance of uncommitted major donors around the country.A Bachmann spokesman said on Thursday that two established G.O.P. fund-raisers had joined Mrs. Bachmann’s campaign: Mary Heitman, who previously ran finance operations at the Republican National Committee and Republican Governors Association, and Jody Thomas, a onetime political director and fund-raiser for former Representative J.C. Watts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bachmann Adds Staff to Court Major Donors', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bachmann, Michele M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T18:20:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Confessore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Confessore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2bfbd5f4-fac4-5ec7-8a5f-6f2a2fcc6f21', 'word_count': 211, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2bfbd5f4-fac4-5ec7-8a5f-6f2a2fcc6f21'}, {'abstract': 'State Assemblyman David I. Weprin visited Queens Democratic Party headquarters, where he was nominated to run for Anthony Weiner’s Congressional seat.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/forest-hills-1014-a-m/', 'snippet': 'State Assemblyman David I. Weprin visited Queens Democratic Party headquarters, where he was nominated to run for Anthony Weiner’s Congressional seat.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Forest Hills, 10:14 A.M.', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weprin, David I', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T18:20:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff115ab5-ddaa-5eb1-8286-d60e318ddc2b', 'word_count': 1, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff115ab5-ddaa-5eb1-8286-d60e318ddc2b'}, {'abstract': 'Joyce McKinney, who weathered a sex scandal in Britain in the 1970s, has many problems with Errol Morris’s documentary “Tabloid,” which tells her story.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/10/movies/joyce-mckinney-protests-errol-morriss-tabloid.html', 'snippet': 'Joyce McKinney, who weathered a sex scandal in Britain in the 1970s, has many problems with Errol Morris’s documentary “Tabloid,” which tells her story.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BY her own account Joyce McKinney has attended more prerelease screenings of the documentary “Tabloid” than its director, Errol Morris. She’s turned up in Austin, Tex.; Sarasota, Fla.; Seattle; San Francisco; and at several showings in New York. She’s received rousing ovations and been hassled by ushers. She’s arrived in disguise and, at a recent screening at the Museum of Modern Art, more or less pounced: “I sat till the audience started to leave and waited for the precise moment, and then jumped up and yelled, ‘I’m Joyce McKinney!’\xa0” she said, with considerable glee. “They went crazy.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/movies/10tabloid_span/10tabloid_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/10/movies/10tabloid_span/10tabloid_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/movies/10tabloid_span/10tabloid_span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/movies/10tabloid_span/10tabloid_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/10/movies/10tabloid_span/10tabloid_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Weathering a Scandal and Now a Movie', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Weathering a Scandal and Now a Movie', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morris, Errol', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T18:26:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Anderson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Anderson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c992413-c795-5ff9-93b3-98ddded221a1', 'word_count': 1085, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c992413-c795-5ff9-93b3-98ddded221a1'}, {'abstract': 'Answers to readers’ questions on dealing with a noise-sensitive neighbor, an oversharing sister and cheap guest gifts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/10/fashion/the-negotiation-next-door-social-qs.html', 'snippet': 'Answers to readers’ questions on dealing with a noise-sensitive neighbor, an oversharing sister and cheap guest gifts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My husband likes to trim our many hedges on Sunday afternoons. He uses gas-powered clippers. Our new next-door neighbor asked him to do this on weekdays, during business hours, because the noise bothers him on Sundays. But my husband works then. This neighbor has also called the police five times to complain about the noise. Each time, the police visit and tell us we are doing nothing wrong. Recently, they suggested our filing a harassment lawsuit. What should we do?', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/02/21/fashion/21social-1/21social-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/02/21/fashion/21social-1/21social-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Negotiation Next Door', 'kicker': 'Social Q’s', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Negotiation Next Door', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs, Etiquette and Manners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T18:27:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Philip Galanes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Philip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Galanes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/05876258-0aa3-5a25-b6ff-5051d1e26b25', 'word_count': 777, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05876258-0aa3-5a25-b6ff-5051d1e26b25'}, {'abstract': 'South Sudan has hopes and fears as it declares its independence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/world/africa/100000000900268/the-worlds-newest-nation.html', 'snippet': 'South Sudan has hopes and fears as it declares its independence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'South Sudan has hopes and fears as it declares its independence.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/world/africa/video-southsudan/video-southsudan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'leg