d earth around the stems.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/travel/10Cuba-1_Span/10Cuba-1_Span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/10/travel/10Cuba-1_Span/10Cuba-1_Span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 340}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/travel/10Cuba-1_Span/Cuba-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 691, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/travel/10Cuba-1_Span/10Cuba-1_Span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/10/travel/10Cuba-1_Span/10Cuba-1_Span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Cuba, Yes, but Only With a Purpose', 'kicker': 'Next Stop', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Cuba, Yes, but Only With a Purpose', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel Restrictions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cuba', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T18:55:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Victoria Burnett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Victoria', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burnett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3bcf0de6-f090-5144-aa02-4e7daab679b2', 'word_count': 1335, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3bcf0de6-f090-5144-aa02-4e7daab679b2'}, {'abstract': 'Istanbul’s island of Buyukada is a living diorama of the Ottoman era, a place of grand churches, filigreed mansions, horse-drawn buggies and retro beach clubs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/10/travel/buyukada-near-istanbul-is-an-island-idyll.html', 'snippet': 'Istanbul’s island of Buyukada is a living diorama of the Ottoman era, a place of grand churches, filigreed mansions, horse-drawn buggies and retro beach clubs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LATE on a peaceful night in May, on a quiet island in the Sea of Marmara, I walked alone on a curving street edged by walls dripping with ivy. Behind the walls, palms and red pines loomed above Ottoman mansions that drowsed in the leafy darkness. With no sound but my own footsteps, I continued down a slope that led to my seafront hotel. Then I paused. Ahead of me, in the half-light cast by a streetlamp, I saw a cluster of tall, undulant shapes at the turning. “Women, or horses?” I wondered. Nearing, I nodded: horses. And then I laughed out loud. How on earth, in the 21st century, was it possible for me, or for anyone, to succumb to such poetic confusion? It was possible only on an island like the one where I found myself: the island of Buyukada, an hour’s ferry ride from Istanbul, a place where time stands still.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/travel/10buyukada_span/10buyukada_span-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/10/travel/10buyukada_span/10buyukada_span-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/travel/10buyukada_span/10buyukada_span-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/travel/10buyukada_span/10buyukada_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/10/travel/10buyukada_span/10buyukada_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Turkish Idyll Lost in Time', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Turkish Idyll Lost in Time', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Buyukada (Turkey)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Istanbul (Turkey)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ottoman Empire', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T18:55:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liesl Schillinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liesl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schillinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/489f7876-7af1-5871-b4cd-936e8b85dd0c', 'word_count': 3384, 'uri': 'nyt://article/489f7876-7af1-5871-b4cd-936e8b85dd0c'}, {'abstract': 'The emphasis is on all things local at this restaurant on a restored estate on the island of Mazzorbo, a half-hour’s boat ride from Venice.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/10/travel/restaurant-report-venissa-on-isola-di-mazzorbo-italy.html', 'snippet': 'The emphasis is on all things local at this restaurant on a restored estate on the island of Mazzorbo, a half-hour’s boat ride from Venice.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Half the delight of eating at Gianluca Bisol’s new restaurant, Venissa, is the journey there. It’s a 30-minute boat ride northeast of Venice, and along the way your boat might cut through thin scraps of morning fog still stuck to the water, or chug past a vast brick ruin on an uninhabited vine-choked island.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/travel/10-BITES/10-BITES-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/10/travel/10-BITES/10-BITES-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 340}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/travel/10-BITES/10-BITES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/travel/10-BITES/10-BITES-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/10/travel/10-BITES/10-BITES-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Restaurant Report: Venissa, on Isola di Mazzorbo, Italy', 'kicker': 'Bites ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Isola Di Mazzorbo, Italy: Venissa', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venice (Italy)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T18:55:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rocky Casale', 