e New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Book Review Podcast: A History of the Papacy', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T18:57:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/07970f2d-7530-5571-aac7-ba6acb338c03', 'word_count': 216, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07970f2d-7530-5571-aac7-ba6acb338c03'}, {'abstract': 'The space shuttle Atlantis rocketed off its seaside launching pad, rising atop a tower of smoke and flames as it left Earth on the shuttle program’s final flight.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/07/08/science/20110709-SHUTTLE.html', 'snippet': 'The space shuttle Atlantis rocketed off its seaside launching pad, rising atop a tower of smoke and flames as it left Earth on the shuttle program’s final flight.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The space shuttle Atlantis rocketed off its seaside launching pad, rising atop a tower of smoke and flames as it left Earth on the shuttle program’s final flight.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Final Launching of Atlantis', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Aeronautics and Space Administration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Atlantis (Space Shuttle)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T18:57:23+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/60c93779-e919-5b3c-a62c-3ce803060fab', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/60c93779-e919-5b3c-a62c-3ce803060fab'}, {'abstract': 'John Maus makes weird 1980s-futurist synth-pop and he’s known for even weirder onstage antics, of the growling animal variety. Andrew Kuo charts a recent show Mr. Maus played at the Mercury Lounge on the Lower East Side.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/charting-john-maus-at-mercury-lounge/', 'snippet': 'John Maus makes weird 1980s-futurist synth-pop and he’s known for even weirder onstage antics, of the growling animal variety. Andrew Kuo charts a recent show Mr. Maus played at the Mercury Lounge on the Lower East Side.', 'lead_paragraph': 'John Maus makes weird 1980s-futurist synth-pop and he’s known for even weirder onstage antics, of the growling animal variety. And should we mention he’s also a political philosophy and theory instructor at the University of Hawaii in Manoa? His latest album is “We Must Become the Pitiless Censors of Ourselves” and he recently played the Mercury Lounge on the Lower East Side. The artist Andrew Kuo charts the show. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Charting John Maus at Mercury Lounge', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T19:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Kuo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kuo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc5425a3-ebae-5ed0-aaee-4465cba28ed1', 'word_count': 71, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc5425a3-ebae-5ed0-aaee-4465cba28ed1'}, {'abstract': 'Courthouse Confidential: A state appellate court ruled that the Health and Hospitals Corporation could go forward with planned layoffs, reversing a lower court ruling.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/court-clears-way-for-hospital-corporation-layoffs/', 'snippet': 'Courthouse Confidential: A state appellate court ruled that the Health and Hospitals Corporation could go forward with planned layoffs, reversing a lower court ruling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A state appellate court ruled on Thursday that the city’s Health and Hospitals Corporation could go forward with planned layoffs it had announced last year, reversing a lower court ruling that prevented the staff reductions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Court Clears Way for Hospital Corporation Layoffs', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN LAWYER', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deloitte Consulting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Health and Hospitals Corp', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T19:01:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Eligon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eligon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8568ce96-1b6e-5309-a30a-f65a978d793a', 'word_count': 642, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8568ce96-1b6e-5309-a30a-f65a978d793a'}, {'abstract': 'Despite the importance of the jobs report as a news story, looking at just one report to analyze the presidential race is like trying to determine what’s going on in a baseball game by watching just one at-bat.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/in-coverage-of-jobs-report-misplaced-attention-to-horse-race/', 'snippet': 'Despite the importance of the jobs report as a news story, looking at just one report to analyze the presidential race is like trying to determine what’s going on in a baseball game by watching just one at-bat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The jobs numbers are awful, but they’ve also provided fodder for some poor political punditry.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Coverage of Jobs Report, Misplaced Attention to Horse Race', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T19:04:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c594ca5-ca9d-5404-8b38-4ea529e587c9', 'word_count': 603, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c594ca5-ca9d-5404-8b38-4ea529e587c9'}, {'abstract': 'What happens when you’re forced to really look at a spouse.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/10/fashion/when-troubles-show-on-the-outside-modern-love.html', 'snippet': 'What happens when you’re forced to really look at a spouse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BY the time the scabies entered our house, my husband, Cliff, and I were already occupying two separate orbits, rarely intersecting. A few mont