n Friday, according to a leaked recording.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated | 4:44 p.m. Rebekah Brooks, the embattled former editor of The News of the World who remains chief executive of the British newspaper division of News Corporation despite calls for her resignation over the widening phone-hacking scandal, was criticized as she spoke to the tabloid’s staff on Friday, according to a leaked recording.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Corp. Executive Meets Angry Staff at Shuttered Tabloid', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wiretapping and Other Eavesdropping Devices and Methods', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brooks, Rebekah', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coulson, Andy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, James', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NEWS CORP', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News International Ltd', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News of the World', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T19:29:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5aea4dcb-5732-5fff-b8fd-03da878054ec', 'word_count': 932, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5aea4dcb-5732-5fff-b8fd-03da878054ec'}, {'abstract': 'The premiere of the 13th edition is the top-rated show of the night.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/big-start-for-big-brother/', 'snippet': 'The premiere of the 13th edition is the top-rated show of the night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The debut of the 13th edition of “Big Brother” lifted CBS to No. 1 in the ratings on Thursday as 7.7 million viewers tuned in to the 9 p.m. premiere episode, according to Nielsen’s estimates. The reality show delivered the night’s largest audience, outperforming ABC’s “Wipeout” in the 8 p.m. hour (6.6 million) as well as Fox’s “So You Think You Can Dance” in the same time slot (5.4 million). ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Big Start for ‘Big Brother’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reality Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC INC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nielsen Media Research', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T19:30:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Toff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Toff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/23940c88-9e98-58a4-b02f-7b791eadd46d', 'word_count': 153, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23940c88-9e98-58a4-b02f-7b791eadd46d'}, {'abstract': 'As the party leaders work toward a debt deal, Megan Liberman and Nate Silver discuss how members may respond, and Michael D. Shear reports on a new breed of campaign video tracker.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/us/politics/100000000917710/the-caucus--reception-for-any-debt-deal.html', 'snippet': 'As the party leaders work toward a debt deal, Megan Liberman and Nate Silver discuss how members may respond, and Michael D. Shear reports on a new breed of campaign video tracker.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the party leaders work toward a debt deal, Megan Liberman and Nate Silver discuss how members may respond, and Michael D. Shear reports on a new breed of campaign video tracker.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/us/politics/video-caucus-070811/video-caucus-070811-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/08/us/politics/video-caucus-070811/video-caucus-070811-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/08/us/politics/video-caucus-070811/video-caucus-070811-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/08/us/politics/video-caucus-070811/video-caucus-070811-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Caucus | Resistance to Any Debt Deal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T19:37:57+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'Ben Werschkul', 'person': [{'firstnam