 at David Zwirner Gallery in Chelsea.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If your own cramped, un-air-conditioned apartment isn’t stifling enough for you right about now, pay a visit to “The House Without the Door,” a new group show at David Zwirner Gallery in Chelsea. Some of the homes represented, like Philip-Lorca diCorcia’s charred suburban pile, might very well be broken beyond repair. Gregor Schneider’s “Dead House,” on the other hand, has been so compulsively overconstructed, there is no apparent way out or in. Mona Hatoum’s “Home” is literally a charged place, where ordinary household objects carry the threat of electric shock. And the apartment of Thomas Ruff’s “Interieur 9B,” shown above, looks like its tenant might have been vacated feet first. All of the artists are somehow navigating that fraught psychological turf between house and home, according to Zwirner’s Kristine Bell, who put together the show and who shares her own “inescapable container” with two boys under the age of 6.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Now Showing | Haunted Houses', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Zwirner, David, Gallery', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T20:30:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alix Browne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alix', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Browne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c93571e5-4f3b-542d-b6b6-339bf18c57b8', 'word_count': 168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c93571e5-4f3b-542d-b6b6-339bf18c57b8'}, {'abstract': 'A response to a Mark Bittman column about the virtues of preparing meals at home.', 'web_url': 'https