: 'The group, which advised the Treasury Department during the 2009 auto industry bailout, claimed that improvements to internal combustion engines would allow fleets to meet federal emissions targets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a report sure to rankle proponents and producers of electric vehicles, the Boston Consulting Group concluded that automakers could meet increasingly stringent federal greenhouse emissions requirements for 2020 mainly by making cost-effective improvements to existing internal combustion vehicles.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Consulting Group Says E.V.’s Are Not Needed to Curb Greenhouse Emissions', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fuel Efficiency', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Consulting Group', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Treasury Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T20:57:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Motavalli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Motavalli', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/88d34d19-e973-5e8c-9a68-14b968df8bdb', 'word_count': 369, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88d34d19-e973-5e8c-9a68-14b968df8bdb'}, {'abstract': 'Citing “logistical and timing restrictions,” the Giants will use their facility in East Rutherford instead of their longtime base in Albany.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/09/sports/football/giants-will-stay-home-for-training-camp.html', 'snippet': 'Citing “logistical and timing restrictions,” the Giants will use their facility in East Rutherford instead of their longtime base in Albany.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Giants announced Friday that they would hold training camp at their facility in East Rutherford, N.J., not their longtime summer base in Albany, because of “logistical and timing restrictions” resulting from the N.F.L. lockout.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/09/sports/camp/camp-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 901, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/09/sports/camp/camp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/09/sports/camp/camp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When Time Comes, Giants Will Hold Camp at Home', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Time Comes, Giants Will Hold Camp at Home', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lockouts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T20:58:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Viera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Viera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8895d1c1-6563-5860-8269-9ed1462cc1f8', 'word_count': 283, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8895d1c1-6563-5860-8269-9ed1462cc1f8'}, {'abstract': 'Google made a record 48 deals in 2010. From the hundreds of start-ups in Silicon Valley, how does Google pick its targets and assess their value?', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/dealbook-googles-deal-making-math/', 'snippet': 'Google made a record 48 deals in 2010. From the hundreds of start-ups in Silicon Valley, how does Google pick its targets and assess their value?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a wide-ranging discussion at the Allen & Company conference here with Evelyn M. Rusli, Google’s chairman, Eric E. Schmidt talked to reporters about his company’s takeover ambitions and the threat of regulatory challenges. While increased antitrust scrutiny is a “concern,” Mr. Schmidt, the former chief executive of Google, said it should not significantly impact the company’s purchasing power, since the company is largely focused on bite-size acquisitions that are too small to land on regulators’ radar screens.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'DealBook: Google’s Deal-Making Math', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schmidt, Eric E', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T20:59:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/332497fe-7be5-5ee4-acdd-3e7b864a85d0', 'word_count': 86, 'uri': 'nyt://article/332497fe-7be5-5ee4-acdd-3e7b864a85d0'}, {'abstract': 'The document explores issues like protecting groundwater and mitigating greenhouse gas emissions from drilling.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/drilling-into-new-yorks-fracking-report/', 'snippet': 'The document explores issues like protecting groundwater and mitigating greenhouse gas emissions from drilling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York Department of Environmental Conservation has posted the voluminous draft document laying out how the state plans to regulate the controversial gas drilling method known as fracking.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Drilling Into New York’s Fracking Report', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drilling and Boring', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hydraulic Fracturing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Natural Gas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Department of Environmental Conservation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Marcellus Shale', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T21:01:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mireya Navarro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mireya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Navarro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a89390a-892f-5fdd-a845-8e76f4d2b430', 'word_count': 133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a89390a-892f-5fdd-a845-8e76f4d2b430'}, {'abstract': 'For its 84th anniversary, to be marked on Monday, 7-Eleven is stepping up its presence in social media — the better to help give away an estimated five million Slurpee drinks.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/tweeting-an-anniversary-and-5-million-slurpees/', 'snippet': 'For its 84th anniversary, to be marked on Monday, 7-Eleven is stepping up its presence in social media — the better to help give away an estimated five million Slurpee drinks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Each year, the 7-Eleven chain of convenience stores invites its customers to join in celebrating 7-Eleven Day, which is the anniversary of its founding on July 11, 1927.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tweeting an Anniversary and 5 Million Slurpees', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': '7-Eleven', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T21:05:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c82aa64f-9056-5b9c-9411-f837ffad0a73', 'word_count': 308, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c82aa64f-9056-5b9c-9411-f837ffad0a73'}, {'abstract': 'La La Anthony, the wife of the basketball star Carmelo Anthony, has made a name for herself. Now she’s helping make a name for them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/10/fashion/la-la-anthony-the-first-lady-of-the-nba.html', 'snippet': 'La La Anthony, the wife of the basketball star Carmelo Anthony, has made a name for herself. Now she’s helping make a name for them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AS she was finishing lunch at the R Lounge overlooking Times Square recently, La La Anthony craned her neck and motioned toward the back of the room, over the head of her lunch guest, projectile whispering, “Just give me one second, O.K.!”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/fashion/LALA/LALA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 365, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/10/fashion/LALA/LALA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 365}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/fashion/LALA/LALA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/fashion/LALA/LALA-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/10/fashion/LALA/LALA-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The First Lady of the N.B.A.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The First Lady of the N.B.A.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANTHONY, CARMELO', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Careers and Professions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T21:05:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Douglas Quenqua', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Douglas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Quenqua', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71b44b99-9c2d-5d6b-99e7-95e773322fbb', 'word_count': 1397, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71b44b99-9c2d-5d6b-99e7-95e773322fbb'}, {'abstract': 'Neil Berg, whose “Broadway Showstoppers and the Songs of Neil Berg” is at Feinstein’s at Loews Regency, has never had songs in a Broadway show.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/09/arts/music/neil-berg-at-feinsteins-at-loews-regency-review.html', 'snippet': 'Neil Berg, whose “Broadway Showstoppers and the Songs of Neil Berg” is at Feinstein’s at Loews Regency, has never had songs in a Broadway show.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sincere ambition — a combination of gee-whiz naïveté and drive — might describe the affable stage personality of Neil Berg, a composer, pianist, producer and outspoken baseball enthusiast whose theatrical sampler, “Broadway Showstoppers and the Songs of Neil Berg,” opened a two-week engagement at Feinstein’s at Loews Regency this week. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/09/arts/Sub-Berg/Sub-Berg-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/09/arts/Sub-Berg/Sub-Berg-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/09/arts/Sub-Berg/Sub-Berg-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Playing a Jukebox Full of Show Tunes', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Playing a Jukebox Full of Show Tunes', 'name': None,