50', 'word_count': 1550, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ecddeaa-e86c-5eb9-891f-5535fd127050'}, {'abstract': 'Another day of runway looks, another Scorecard at your service.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/scorecard-azzedine-alaia-wins/', 'snippet': 'Another day of runway looks, another Scorecard at your service.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The rest of the couture shows may have wrapped Wednesday, but Scorecard knows that if the ekphrastic praise for a women’s-wear master forever beloved by one French Culture Minister and one Cher Horowitz showing on schedule (sort-of) for the first time in 8 years is any proof, M. Alaïa wouldn’t have it any other way.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Scorecard | Azzedine Alaïa Wins!', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T22:01:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alison S. Cohn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Cohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0da7ea3a-b163-558d-8a3f-9b7718e23657', 'word_count': 309, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0da7ea3a-b163-558d-8a3f-9b7718e23657'}, {'abstract': 'Judy Gold stars in her own memoir with music, at the DR2 Theater in Manhattan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/09/theater/reviews/the-judy-show-my-life-as-a-sitcom-review.html', 'snippet': 'Judy Gold stars in her own memoir with music, at the DR2 Theater in Manhattan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Near the end of her infectiously nostalgic memoir with music, “The Judy Show: My Life as a Sitcom,” the writer and stand-up comic Judy Gold gives a shout-out to Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo for championing the legislation that allows her to marry her therapist girlfriend in New York State. But the lack of acceptance in Burbank, Calif., still bothers her.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/09/arts/JUDY/JUDY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/09/arts/JUDY/JUDY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/09/arts/JUDY/JUDY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 655, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/09/arts/JUDY/JUDY-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/09/arts/JUDY/JUDY-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'She Wanted a TV Show, but the Stage Will Do, Too', 'kicker': 'Theater Review | ‘The Judy Show: My Life as a Sitcom’', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'She Wanted a TV Show, But the Stage Will Do, Too', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gold, Judy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T22:02:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Rooney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rooney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6f52cfd-cb78-52ac-864b-e0bafa457439', 'word_count': 374, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6f52cfd-cb78-52ac-864b-e0bafa457439'}, {'abstract': 'Slide show: Subjects include a swim down the Hudson River, renovation of the Cortlandt Street subway station and a tour of shadows in Coney Island.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/the-week-in-pictures-for-july-8/', 'snippet': 'Slide show: Subjects include a swim down the Hudson River, renovation of the Cortlandt Street subway station and a tour of shadows in Coney Island.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here is a slide show of photographs from the past week in New York City and the region. Subjects include a swim down the Hudson River, renovation of the Cortlandt Street subway station and a tour of shadows in Coney Island.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Week in Pictures for July 8', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subways', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Swimming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'CONEY ISLAND (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hudson River', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T22:05:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1607bc2-b10b-569a-8330-f211b2935ad5', 'word_count': 89, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1607bc2-b10b-569a-8330-f211b2935ad5'}, {'abstract': 'Movie stars and religious groups teamed up with policy makers to help a forlorn region achieve what few separatist movements do.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/09/world/africa/09sudan.html', 'snippet': 'Movie stars and religious groups teamed up with policy makers to help a forlorn region achieve what few separatist movements do.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JUBA, Sudan — On the desk in his office in Juba, the capital of what will soon be the world’s newest country, R. Barrie Walkley, the American consul general, has a telling picture. It is of him and George Clooney shaking hands in a crowd during the independence referendum here in southern Sudan in January.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/09/world/africa/09sudan1/09sudan1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/09/world/africa/09sudan1/09sudan1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/09/world/africa/09sudan1/09sudan1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/09/world/africa/09sudan1/09sudan1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/09/world/africa/09sudan1/09sudan1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sudan Movement’s Mission Is Secured: Statehood', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Movement’s Mission Is Secured: Statehood', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Sudan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sudan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T22:07:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeffrey Gettleman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeffrey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gettleman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2baedf5-677c-52b5-b90d-74faf90d939a', 'word_count': 1069, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2baedf5-677c-52b5-b90d-74faf90d939a'}, {'abstract': 'Sorting out which versions of Bruckner’s compositions are the definitive ones has been a puzzle for scholars.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/10/arts/music/bruckners-music-which-versions-did-he-intend.html', 'snippet': 'Sorting out which versions of Bruckner’s compositions are the definitive ones has been a puzzle for scholars.', 'lead_paragraph': 'POSTERITY has not always treated Anton Bruckner kindly. The popular image of this composer as an unwitting visionary — “half genius, half klutz,” as the conductor Hans von Bülow once said — developed early on. During Bruckner’s lifetime conservative critics recoiled from his music. Eduard Hanslick called him the “gentlest and most peaceable of men who becomes an anarchist during the act of composition.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/arts/10bruckner1/10bruckner1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 810, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/arts/10bruckner1/10bruckner1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/10/arts/10bruckner1/10bruckner1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Still Searching For Bruckner’s True Intentions', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Still Searching For Bruckner’s True Intentions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cleveland Orchestra', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bruckner, Anton', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T22:08:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Korstvedt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Korstvedt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8608063-04f4-5cea-bd06-961933eaa911', 'word_count': 1817, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8608063-04f4-5cea-bd06-961933eaa911'}, {'abstract': 'On VH1’s “Famous Food,” seven contestants, including Danielle Staub and Heidi Montag, vie for a chance to have an ownership share in a Sunset Strip restaurant.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/09/arts/television/famous-food-on-vh1-review.html', 'snippet': 'On VH1’s “Famous Food,” seven contestants, including Danielle Staub and Heidi Montag, vie for a chance to have an ownership share in a Sunset Strip restaurant.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As goes the economy, so goes the reality-television gravy train. Once it was possible to swan from one show to the next, start a rumble or two, collect a check, then repeat. Shows that collect second-generation D-listers — like “Famous Food,” which begins Sunday on VH1 — serve as after-care facilities for reality veterans, made on the principle that no reality star, once filmed, should go unfilmed.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/09/arts/Famous/Famous-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 348, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/09/arts/Famous/Famous-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 348}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/09/arts/Famous/Famous-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/09/arts/Famous/Famous-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/09/arts/Famous/Famous-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'It’s Hard Out Here for a Reality-Show Celebrity', 'kicker': 'Television Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'It’s Hard Out Here for a Reality-Show Celebrity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'VH1', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T22:09:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/29598a06-9c32-51a6-990d-3ea082f3786d', 'word_count': 720, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29598a06-9c32-51a6-990d-3ea082f3786d'}, {'abstract': 'Hyundai engineered class-leading value and distinctive styling into its latest sedan, but sacrificed down-the-road driving pleasure to its competitors.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/reviewing-the-hyundai-elantra/', 'snippet': 'Hyundai engineered class-leading value and distinctive styling into its latest sedan, but sacrificed down-the-road driving pleasure to its competitors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Sunday’s Automobiles section, Lawrence Ulrich reviews the 2012 Hyundai Elantra. The sedan wears the brand’s so-called fluidic sculpture design theme well, he writes, but a body crease here or a teardrop motif there might represent a touch too much for some shoppers:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reviewing the Hyundai Elantra', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hyundai Motor Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T22:10:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/07df70bb-65c8-5884-9d4d-becc7b367c8c', 'word_count': 198, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07df70bb-65c8-5884-9d4d-becc7b367c8c'}, {'abstract': 'During a break on his journey from the North to the South Pole, Johan Ernst Nilson, a Swedish explorer, mastered transportation in New York City.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/between-the-north-and-south-poles-a-layover-in-new-york/', 'snippet': 'During a break on his journey from the North to the South Pole, Johan Ernst Nilson, a Swedish explorer, mastered transportation in New York City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Few New Yorkers seemed to appreciate this week’s blazing sunshine like Johan Ernst Nilson. A sunburned Swedish explorer, on break from his journey from the North to the South Pole, Mr. Nilson leaned back in his chair in the entrance of the Standard Hotel on Tuesday morning, sipped a soda and relished the warmth. It’s not just been a long winter: it’s been a journey filled with chases by bears and death-defying dips in icy Arctic waters.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Between the North and South Poles, a Layover in New York', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exploration and Explorers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T22:15:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Haughney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haughney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fcee956b-bd77-569b-a3ee-d2bb82d1d012', 'word_count': 326, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fcee956b-bd77-569b-a3ee-d2bb82d1d012'}, {'abstract': 'Marc Andreessen and Warren E. Buffett are two of the largest names in investing, but the two disagree about the value of technology stocks.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/tech-companies-undervalued-or-not/', 'snippet': 'Marc Andreessen and Warren E. Buffett are two of the largest names in investing, but the two disagree about the value of technology stocks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Marc Andreessen, one of Silicon Valley’s biggest venture capitalists, and Warren E. Buffett, of Berkshire Hathaway, have two things in common: They are both worth huge amounts of money, with billions of dollars at their investing disposal, and they both try to invest in companies that are undervalued.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tech Companies: Undervalued or Not?', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Andreessen, Marc L', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Buffett, Warren E', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Berkshire Hathaway Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Electric Company', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Silicon Valley (Calif)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T22:17:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5778c817-74d0-5b62-8953-e1991eca09fe', 'word_count': 280, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5778c817-74d0-5b62-8953-e1991eca09fe'}, {'abstract': 'The Latin Alternative Music Conference, now in its 12th year, is still pushing against language and radio formats.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/09/arts/music/pushing-past-borders-at-latin-alternative-music-conference.html', 'snippet': 'The Latin Alternative Music Conference, now in its 12th year, is still pushing against language and radio formats.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like a lot of the performers at this year’s Latin Alternative Music Conference, Henry D’Arthenay, the guitarist and singer of the Venezuelan band La Vida Bohème, pondered onstage whether to speak to the audience in Spanish or English. On Wednesday night at the Mercury Lounge, he made a quick decision: “Let’s communicate through music,” he said, in both languages. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/09/arts/jp-LAMC/jp-LAMC-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/09/arts/jp-LAMC/jp-LAMC-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/09/arts/jp-LAMC/jp-LAMC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/09/arts/jp-LAMC/jp-LAMC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/09/arts/jp-LAMC/jp-LAMC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Musical Ambition, Defying All Barriers', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Musical Ambition, Defying All Barriers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Latin Alternative Music Conference', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T22:18:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organiza