Golub, a longtime veteran of Lazard, briefly served as the investment bank’s interim chief executive following the death of Bruce Wasserstein.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/lazards-golub-a-vice-chairman-has-retired/', 'snippet': 'Steven J. Golub, a longtime veteran of Lazard, briefly served as the investment bank’s interim chief executive following the death of Bruce Wasserstein.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Steven J. Golub, a longtime veteran of Lazard who briefly served as interim chief executive of the investment bank, has retired, a spokeswoman confirmed on Friday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lazard’s Golub, a Vice Chairman, Retires', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Golub, Steven J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lazard Ltd', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T22:36:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced and Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71fa871e-19c0-574f-918a-0545f31dd691', 'word_count': 223, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71fa871e-19c0-574f-918a-0545f31dd691'}, {'abstract': 'On Friday at 10 p.m. Eastern, Bob Costas and Al Michaels will call the Mets-San Francisco Giants game on the MLB Network.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/08/costas-and-michaels-team-up-to-call-mets-giants/', 'snippet': 'On Friday at 10 p.m. Eastern, Bob Costas and Al Michaels will call the Mets-San Francisco Giants game on the MLB Network.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Friday at 10 p.m. Eastern, Bob Costas and Al Michaels will call the Mets-San Francisco Giants game on the MLB Network. They will announce the first three and the eighth and ninth innings on the network. To accommodate fans in the New York and San Francisco markets, where the MLB broadcast will be blacked out, Costas and Michaels will head to the Mets’ SNY booth for the fourth and fifth innings and SNY’s Gary Cohen and Ron Darling will shift to the MLB booth. When Costas and Michaels work in the Giants’ CSN Bay Area booth for the sixth and seventh innings, the Giants announcers Mike Krukow and Duane Kuiper will replace them on MLB. Although this is billed as the first game Costas and Michaels have called together, they were boothmates in the movie “BASEketball,” a 1998 comedy. It will, indeed, be the first baseball game for Michaels since 1995, when he was at ABC Sports.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Costas and Michaels Team Up to Call Mets-Giants', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Costas, Bob', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Michaels, Al', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco Giants', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-08T22:40:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt