'abstract': 'A suspect in the armed robbery of four musicians in Brooklyn says some spiked marijuana has stolen much of his memory of the night.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/09/nyregion/suspect-in-robbery-of-band-members-claims-stolen-memory.html', 'snippet': 'A suspect in the armed robbery of four musicians in Brooklyn says some spiked marijuana has stolen much of his memory of the night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every now and then on a given afternoon, when the Q100 bus pulls to a stop on 21st Street in Queens, somebody actually gets off. But mostly, people just keep getting on, and on, and on, cramming themselves in the center aisle, all bound for the final destination. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/09/nyregion/CRIMESCENE/CRIMESCENE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/09/nyregion/CRIMESCENE/CRIMESCENE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/09/nyregion/CRIMESCENE/CRIMESCENE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Memory AWOL, Robbery Suspect Still Figures He Didn’t Do It', 'kicker': 'Crime Scene', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Robbery Suspect, Memory AWOL, Still Figures He Didn’t Do It', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bedford-Stuyvesant (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marijuana', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T00:29:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2071aac7-0203-5240-b2ef-f3e94b920ada', 'word_count': 920, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2071aac7-0203-5240-b2ef-f3e94b920ada'}, {'abstract': 'Bob Turner, who made a surprisingly strong showing last year, will take on the Democrat, Assemblyman David I. Weprin, in the special election.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/09/nyregion/bob-turner-is-gop-pick-to-replace-weiner.html', 'snippet': 'Bob Turner, who made a surprisingly strong showing last year, will take on the Democrat, Assemblyman David I. Weprin, in the special election.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Republican Party leaders in Queens and Brooklyn on Friday chose Bob Turner, a retired cable television executive, as their nominee in a Sept. 13 special election to fill the seat of former Representative Anthony D. Weiner.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/09/nyregion/TURNER/TURNER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 242, 'width': 171, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/09/nyregion/TURNER/TURNER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/09/nyregion/TURNER/TURNER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Runner-Up to Weiner in 2010 Is G.O.P. Choice to Run for Seat', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Runner-Up to Weiner in 2010 Is G.O.P. Choice to Run for Seat', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weprin, David I', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weiner, Anthony D', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T00:33:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/45e846b9-7d8b-5c51-8cc8-4cf541d672a1', 'word_count': 398, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45e846b9-7d8b-5c51-8cc8-4cf541d672a1'}, {'abstract': 'The company said it would again seek approval of the diabetes drug Bydureon.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/09/business/amylin-to-resubmit-diabetes-treatment-to-fda.html', 'snippet': 'The company said it would again seek approval of the diabetes drug Bydureon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Amylin Pharmaceuticals, a biopharmaceutical company, said its experimental diabetes treatment Bydureon will be resubmitted for regulatory approval in the United States this quarter. The company, based in San Diego, and its partners, Eli Lilly & Company of Indianapolis and Alkermes of Waltham, Mass., announced late Thursday that a study requested by the Food and Drug Administration did not tie Bydureon to dangerous changes to heart rhythm. The data were released in summary form on June 24. The F.D.A. rejected Bydureon, a longer-acting form of the companies’ Byetta medicine, in October over concerns that high doses might cause heart risks. The companies said Thursday that they planned to refile their application with the new data on heart rhythm in the third quarter, sooner than expected. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Amylin to Resubmit Diabetes Treatment to F.D.A.', 'kicker': 'Business Briefing | HEALTH', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Amylin to Resubmit Diabetes Treatment to F.D.A.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diabetes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMYLIN PHARMACEUTICALS INCORPORATED', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T00:37:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bloomberg News', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bloomberg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'News', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb6849be-2434-5a6e-b643-d382d002accb', 'word_count': 126, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb6849be-2434-5a6e-b643-d382d002accb'}, {'abstract': 'Eric E. Schmidt, the executive chairman of Google, has agreed to testify at a Senate subcommittee hearing on the company’s dominance of the Internet search industry.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/09/technology/googles-chairman-to-testify-before-a-senate-panel.html', 'snippet': 'Eric E. Schmidt, the executive chairman of Google, has agreed to testify at a Senate subcommittee hearing on the company’s dominance of the Internet search industry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Eric E. Schmidt, the executive chairman of Google, has agreed to testify at a Senate subcommittee hearing on the company’s dominance of the Internet search industry, yielding to the panel’s demands. Mr. Schmidt will testify in September, the company said Friday. “We’re happy to accommodate” the subcommittee, said Mistique Cano, a spokeswoman for the company. The move resolves a standoff between the company and the Senate Judiciary antitrust subcommittee, which had threatened to subpoena Mr. Schmidt or Google’s chief executive, Larry Page. The subcommittee plans to examine whether Google is using its position as owner of the world’s most popular search engine to hurt competition in the Internet industry. The Federal Trade Commission, the European Union and the State of Texas are looking into accusations by Internet companies that Google favored its own services in search results and increased ad rates on its rivals. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Google’s Chairman to Testify Before a Senate Panel', 'kicker': 'Business Briefing | TECHNOLOGY', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Google’s Chairman to Testify Before a Senate Panel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antitrust Laws and Competition Issues', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schmidt, Eric E', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T00:38:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bloomberg News', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bloomberg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'News', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab3503b9-7175-52b5-82d5-1f9cdf00c141', 'word_count': 147, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab3503b9-7175-52b5-82d5-1f9cdf00c141'}, {'abstract': 'A nominating committee is expected to consider many options, including adopting a co-chief executive structure, to replace Josef Ackermann when his contract expires in 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/09/business/global/deutsche-bank-said-to-be-ready-to-select-ackermanns-successor.html', 'snippet': 'A nominating committee is expected to consider many options, including adopting a co-chief executive structure, to replace Josef Ackermann when his contract expires in 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The question of who will become chief executive of Deutsche Bank is likely to be resolved this weekend when members of the bank’s board are set to meet and propose a successor to the current chief, Josef Ackermann, according to two people with direct knowledge of the situation.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Deutsche Bank Said to Be Ready to Select New Leader', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Deutsche Bank Said to Be Ready to Select New Leader', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deutsche Bank AG', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ACKERMANN, JOSEF', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executives and Management', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T00:40:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Landon Thomas Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Landon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thomas', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3b5e19c-7793-587b-ac06-cc9b179f0c2a', 'word_count': 771, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3b5e19c-7793-587b-ac06-cc9b179f0c2a'}, {'abstract': 'Bethany Patchin has changed more than a bit since age 18, when she wrote that Christians should not kiss before marriage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/09/us/09beliefs.html', 'snippet': 'Bethany Patchin has changed more than a bit since age 18, when she wrote that Christians should not kiss before marriage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In August 1999, Bethany Patchin, an 18-year-old college sophomore from Wisconsin, wrote in an article for Boundless, an evangelical Web magazine, that Christians should not kiss before marriage. Sam Torode, a 23-year-old Chicagoan, replied in a letter to the editor that Ms. Patchin’s piece could not help but “drive young Christian men mad with desire.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/09/us/BELIEFS/BELIEFS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/09/us/BELIEFS/BELIEFS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/09/us/BELIEFS/BELIEFS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/09/us/BELIEFS/BELIEFS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/09/us/BELIEFS/BELIEFS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Evolving View of Natural Family Planning', 'kicker': 'Beliefs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Evolving View of Natural Family Planning', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None},