2-london-games.html', 'snippet': 'The International Olympic Committee announced that it would ban athletes competing at the London Olympics from possessing needles without clearance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Biathletes and cross-country skiers have been caught with blood-doping paraphernalia at the Olympics. Major League Baseball players have claimed they have received injections — not of steroids, but of vitamins and painkillers. Cycling teams have left behind trash cans littered with syringes.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Tactic in Fight Against Doping: No Syringes Allowed', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Tactic in Fight Against Doping: No Syringes Allowed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doping (Sports)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Olympic Committee', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Steroids', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests (Drug Use)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hypodermic Needles and Syringes', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T00:43:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Juliet Macur', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Juliet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macur', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8437a439-e845-52c9-89a9-d526802b156a', 'word_count': 726, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8437a439-e845-52c9-89