'nyt://article/1cf589b0-f84d-5d34-bad2-6adfd8bc7d2a'}, {'abstract': 'Réunion Surf Bar, the watering hole named for the French island off the coast of Madagascar, serves up tropical cocktails.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/10/nyregion/at-reunion-surf-bar-in-new-york-an-endless-summer.html', 'snippet': 'Réunion Surf Bar, the watering hole named for the French island off the coast of Madagascar, serves up tropical cocktails.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Giving new meaning to the notion of an underground surf scene, Thomas Wilson, a former owner of Mas, and Gene Ashe, a former general manager at 5 Ninth, have brought the feeling of endless summer to the basement of the Film Center Building on 44th Street just east of Ninth Avenue. Open since last summer, Réunion Surf Bar, named for a French-owned island off the coast of Madagascar and decorated with boards Mr. Wilson frequently pulls down to ride out in East Hampton, has become a hub for Broadway actors, employees of Billabong and Quiksilver, creative-industry workers from the area and surfers looking for quirky takes on beach food and tropical cocktails. Last year, Laird Hamilton paid a visit with Julian Schnabel, but on Wednesday the happy hour crowd included two friends from college sharing their impressions of first moving to New York. DIANE CARDWELL ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/nyregion/10TABLE_span/10TABLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/10/nyregion/10TABLE_span/10TABLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/nyregion/10TABLE_span/10TABLE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_nam