feet of supplies for kitchen and table, indoors or outdoors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A good pan is hard to find. But not if you make your way to Harris Restaurant Supply in Port Chester. Although the place has been in business for more than 40 years, the front door is as discreet as a speakeasy’s — even the G.P.S. can’t quite locate it (hint: Harris is just south of Mill Street). Yet inside lies a Disney World of wares for kitchen and table, indoors and out — 8,000 square feet of them. ', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Every Ware Imaginable', 'kicker': 'Cook’s Tour | Port Chester', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Every Ware Imaginable', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cookware', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Westchester County (NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T02:11:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By M.H. REED', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a611a83a-14ee-5432-a5f8-1f493cb64013', 'word_count': 316, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a611a83a-14ee-5432-a5f8-1f493cb64013'}, {'abstract': 'Le Fontane is basically your solid neighborhood Italian restaurant and catering hall, only better, the way these places used to be.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/10/nyregion/at-le-fontane-tastes-of-southern-italy.html', 'snippet': 'Le Fontane is basically your solid neighborhood Italian restaurant and catering hall, only better, the way these places used to be.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE roomy patio of Le Fontane in Katonah is especially appealing on a hot summer’s day, or night. Greenery surrounds the secluded sheltered area, and a few fans keep the air moving. Although this carefully created restaurant with a kitchen inspired by southern Italy is closer to Route 100 than to the Appian Way, the winsome service and warm, garden-sweet air on the patio lend the feel of there, rather than here. Not least, the food can be quite good and the prices reasonable.', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/nyregion/10DINEWE1/10DINEWE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 718, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/nyregion/10DINEWE1/10DINEWE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/10/nyregion/10DINEWE1/10DINEWE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tastes Imported From Southern Italy', 'kicker': 'Westchester Dining | Katonah', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tastes Imported From Southern Italy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Westchester County (NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T02:13:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By M. H. Reed', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e6188fc-347e-55be-9f5e-f600788d8e2f', 'word_count': 768, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e6188fc-347e-55be-9f5e-f600788d8e2f'}, {'abstract': 'Court documents related to the civil case brought by Israel Switt’s heirs. The family wants to retrieve rare coins that the federal government says were stolen.',