, 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a665b1e-10ad-5261-ba62-fcf2cefe30df', 'word_count': 1038, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a665b1e-10ad-5261-ba62-fcf2cefe30df'}, {'abstract': 'Offering at least 30 homemade flavors every day, Salem Valley Farms Ice Cream Company is a local favorite.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/10/nyregion/salem-valley-farms-ice-cream-company-review.html', 'snippet': 'Offering at least 30 homemade flavors every day, Salem Valley Farms Ice Cream Company is a local favorite.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Salem Valley Farms Ice Cream Company is housed in a red, barnlike building that sits amid a patch of grass to the southwest of downtown Salem. It is less than 10 miles from Devil’s Hopyard State Park and Gillette Castle, and on the warmer days of summer every bit as popular a tourist attraction. ', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Caramel Caribou, in a Cone', 'kicker': 'Quick Bite | Salem', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Caramel Caribou, in a Cone', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ICE CREAM', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T02:25:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Brooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/55b6e055-fb12-5a21-ad7a-a354af436e03', 'word_count': 298, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55b6e055-fb12-5a21-ad7a-a354af436e03'}, {'abstract': 'By forgoing fancier food for straightforward brasserie cuisine, Le Laurentis is able to keep prices down and quality up.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/10/nyregion/le-laurentis-brasserie-review.html', 'snippet': 'By forgoing fancier food for straightforward brasserie cuisine, Le Laurentis is able to keep prices down and quality up.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN the shade of a chestnut tree outside Le Laurentis Brasserie in Lakeville, two men wearing aprons over their jeans were playing what I mistakenly referred to as boccie. “It’s pétanque,” one of them said — setting the scene for the solidly Gallic experience to come.', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/nyregion/10DINECT1/10DINECT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 652, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/nyregion/10DINECT1/10DINECT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/10/nyregion/10DINECT1/10DINECT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Brasserie Cuisine True to Its French Roots', 'kicker': 'Connecticut Dining | Lakeville', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Brasserie Cuisine True to Its French Roots', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T02:26:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Brooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe20918b-fce0-5683-a957-0c5d50b626ce', 'word_count': 796, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe20918b-fce0-5683-a957-0c5d50b626ce'}, {'abstract': 'Christopher Michael Cahill, an original member of the pioneering Z-Boys skateboarding team, transformed the sport with punk belligerence and a fluid surfing style.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/09/sports/chris-cahill-54-of-skateboardings-z-boys-dies.html', 'snippet': 'Christopher Michael Cahill, an original member of the pioneering Z-Boys skateboarding team, transformed the sport with punk belligerence and a fluid surfing style.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chris Cahill, an original member of the Zephyr team or Z-Boys, a skateboarding phenomenon that transformed the sport with punk belligerence and a fluid surfing style born in a rundown Southern California neighborhood, was found dead on June 24 at his home in Los Angeles. He was 54.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/sports/obit-cahill/obit-cahill-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 938, 'width': 689, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/sports/obit-cahill/obit-cahill-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/10/sports/obit-cahill/obit-cahill-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chris Cahill, 54, of Skateboarding’s Z-Boys, Dies', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chris Cahill, 54, Tough Z-Boy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Z-Boys', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'SKATEBOARDS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T02:29:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel E. Slotnik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Slotnik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f21508a-46a1-52e4-b5b4-cac533623083', 'word_count': 378, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f21508a-46a1-52e4-b5b4-cac533623083'}, {'abstract': 'At Uber Burger, housed at the Prudential Center, beef and beer may be the main attractions, but the restaurant also serves a sushi-grade ahi tuna burger.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/10/nyregion/at-uber-burger-in-prudential-center-beef-with-pucks-on-side.html', 'snippet': 'At Uber Burger, housed at the Prudential Center, beef and beer may be the main attractions, but the restaurant also serves a sushi-grade ahi tuna burger.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The owners of Uber Burger, a 100-seat, fast-casual restaurant that opened at the Prudential Center complex in December, seem to have a good handle on what people attending an event in the arena might want. One of the seven partners is Mark Gheduzzi, senior vice president for facilities with the New Jersey Devils, and another is Gordon Lavalette, the team’s executive vice president for finance and administration. ', 'print_section': 'NJ', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Burgers, With Pucks on the Side', 'kicker': 'Quick Bite | Newark', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Burgers, With Pucks on the Side', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prudential Center (Newark)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T02:32:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tammy La Gorce', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tammy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'La Gorce', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/447389d0-631a-5c05-9218-d7619386c6be', 'word_count': 306, 'uri': 'nyt://article/447389d0-631a-5c05-9218-d7619386c6be'}, {'abstract': 'At Mo’ Greens Roast House B.B.Q., there are few real greens, but the tastiness of the pulled pork and other meats make up for that.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/10/nyregion/mo-greens-roast-house-bbq-review.html', 'snippet': 'At Mo’ Greens Roast House B.B.Q., there are few real greens, but the tastiness of the pulled pork and other meats make up for that.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT has been years since I savored barbecued pork the way it is served in South Carolina, and even longer since I had a plate of it Memphis-style, but a sign for barbecue still catches my eye. When it is paired with the word greens, evoking dark, silky collards or turnip greens or mustard greens that have been cooked on the back of the stove all day, it’s enough to make me turn the car around.', 'print_section': 'NJ', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/nyregion/10DINENJ1/10DINENJ1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 689, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'