ghts of United States citizens.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Civil rights groups filed a class-action lawsuit on Friday against a new state law that cracks down on illegal immigration, saying it would violate the constitutional rights of United States citizens. The law, which supporters described as the toughest of its kind in the nation, requires public schools to report students’ immigration status, makes it a crime to give a ride to an illegal immigrant and bars all contracts with those immigrants. “This law revisits the state’s painful racial past,” said Mary Bauer, legal director of the Southern Poverty Law Center, one of the groups bringing the suit. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Alabama: Suit Fights Immigration Law', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | SOUTH', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Alabama: Suit Fights Immigration Law', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigrants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALABAMA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T03:46:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad63d191-b85f-566c-867e-1497f661480d', 'word_count': 99, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad63d191-b85f-566c-867e-1497f661480d'}, {'abstract': 'Catherine Greig, the longtime girlfriend of James (Whitey) Bulger, will ask to be released into home confinement at a federal court hearing on Monday, according to papers filed by her lawyer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/09/us/09brfs-Bulger.html', 'snippet': 'Catherine Greig, the longtime girlfriend of James (Whitey) Bulger, will ask to be released into home confinement at a federal court hearing on Monday, according to papers filed by her lawyer.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Catherine Greig, the longtime girlfriend of James (Whitey) Bulger, will ask to be released into home confinement at a federal court hearing on Monday, according to papers filed by her lawyer. Ms. Greig, 60, went on the run with Mr. Bulger in 1995 and was captured with him in California last month. She is charged with harboring a fugitive, a crime that carries a maximum sentence of five years. Her lawyer, Kevin Reddington, wrote in a court filing on Thursday that Ms. Greig was not a criminal but a “traveling companion” to Mr. Bulger, 81, a former Boston crime boss charged in 19 murders. Ms. Greig, he wrote, is “a kind, gentle person with a loving personality.” Ms. Greig and her twin sister would put up their homes as collateral, according to the filing. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Massachusetts: Mob Boss’s Girlfriend Will Ask for Release From Jail', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | NEW ENGLAND', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Massachusetts: Mob Boss’s Girlfriend Will Ask for Release From Jail', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greig, Catherine Elizabeth', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bulger, James J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T03:51:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abby Goodnough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goodnough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material