ee to life in prison for his role during Rwanda’s 1994 genocide.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A Dutch court of appeal has sentenced a Rwandan refugee to life in prison for his role during Rwanda’s 1994 genocide. The refugee, Joseph Mpambara, 43, an ethnic Hutu businessman, led an attack on an Adventist compound in Muganero where Tutsi families had sought shelter, and hundreds were killed during the resulting bloodbath, the court said. He also was involved in holding up an ambulance that was carrying two Tutsi women and their children who were hacked to death with machetes, the three judges found. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rwanda: Sentencing in Genocide', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Africa', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rwanda: Sentencing in Genocide', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tutsi Tribe', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hutu Tribe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rwanda', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T04:26:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marlise Simons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marlise', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Simons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6b59391-2167-5524-b485-ebd25b09c500', 'word_count': 87, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6b59391-2167-5524-b485-ebd25b09c500'}, {'abstract': 'A French court on Friday postponed for the second time a decision about investigating claims that Christine Lagarde abused her power as the French finance minister in 2008.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/09/world/europe/09briefs-Francebrief.html', 'snippet': 'A French court on Friday postponed for the second time a decision about investigating claims that Christine Lagarde abused her power as the French finance minister in 2008.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A French court on Friday postponed for the second time a decision about investigating claims that Christine Lagarde, the new chief of the International Monetary Fund, abused her power as the French finance minister in 2008. A decision is now expected on Aug. 4. At issue is her intervention in a legal battle between the businessman Bernard Tapie and the Crédit Lyonnais bank. As finance minister, Ms. Lagarde cut short legal proceedings and chose independent arbitration instead. Mr. Tapie was awarded about 400 million euros. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France: Inquiry of Official Delayed', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France: Inquiry of Official Delayed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Monetary Fund', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tapie, Bernard', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lagarde, Christine', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T04:29:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Romain Parlier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Romain', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parlier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/59e7dee3-07e0-5deb-842b-19916f35d7c7', 'word_count': 87, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59e7dee3-07e0-5deb-842b-19916f35d7c7'}, {'abstract': 'German opposition parties were unable to muster a majority to oppose the reported multibillion-dollar deal to sell 200 German-made tanks to Saudi Arabia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/09/world/europe/09briefs-Germanbrief.html', 'snippet': 'German opposition parties were unable to muster a majority to oppose the reported multibillion-dollar deal to sell 200 German-made tanks to Saudi Arabia.', 'lead_paragraph': ' German opposition parties were unable to muster a majority to oppose the reported multibillion-dollar deal to sell 200 German-made tanks to Saudi Arabia. The news that Chancellor Angela Merkel and Germany’s security council had signed off on the shipment of state-of-the-art tanks to the Middle East after the Saudis helped suppress the uprising in Bahrain led to an uproar this week and to the failed attempt by left-wing parties to scuttle arms shipments through legislation in the Bundestag. Mrs. Merkel, who also leads the security council, has refused to confirm or deny that a deal is in place, citing legal requirements to keep all the council’s decisions secret. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Germany: Vote on Saudi Tank Deal', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Germany: Vote on Saudi Tank Deal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merkel, Angela', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Saudi Arabia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bahrain', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T04:31:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 's