, 'byline': {'original': 'By Jada F. Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jada', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9615645e-3138-5680-b7ba-380c2e02809e', 'word_count': 405, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9615645e-3138-5680-b7ba-380c2e02809e'}, {'abstract': 'Kerry Collins was a very good quarterback who doesn’t deserve to be forgotten.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/09/kerry-collins-unappreciated-quarterback/', 'snippet': 'Kerry Collins was a very good quarterback who doesn’t deserve to be forgotten.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Because Kerry Collins had an uneven and at times tumultuous career, his retirement announcement on Thursday did not receive much fanfare. (A lockout doesn’t help matters.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kerry Collins, Unappreciated Quarterback', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Collins, Kerry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T10:00:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba92f7dd-1196-5af3-9ad4-ae9225779781', 'word_count': 278, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba92f7dd-1196-5af3-9ad4-ae9225779781'}, {'abstract': 'One thing that most officials seem to agree on amid the conflict over debt is that failing to raise the federal debt ceiling will have undesirable consequences.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/09/what-if-the-debt-ceiling-isnt-raised/', 'snippet': 'One thing that most officials seem to agree on amid the conflict over debt is that failing to raise the federal debt ceiling will have undesirable consequences.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are few signs of progress in the meetings between President Obama and Republican Congressional leaders about the need to raise the federal debt limit.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What if the Debt Ceiling Isn’t Raised?', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T12:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel McDermon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McDermon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/539e8c1c-15c0-5fec-a31a-81f7a7b69717', 'word_count': 587, 'uri': 'nyt://article/539e8c1c-15c0-5fec-a31a-81f7a7b69717'}, {'abstract': 'Black raspberries, sweet and tart, are abundant this time of year, growing wild in parks and backyards.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/09/urban-forager-its-prime-time-for-black-raspberries/', 'snippet': 'Black raspberries, sweet and tart, are abundant this time of year, growing wild in parks and backyards.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sweet, tart and thimble-shaped, black raspberries resemble the red supermarket variety, only they are smaller and give a greater punch to the palate. This time of year, black raspberries are ripe and abundant throughout the city and the metropolitan area, growing wild along the side of the road, on parkland and in neighbors’ backyards.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Urban Forager | It’s Prime Time for Black Raspberries', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blackberries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flowers and Plants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T13:00:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ava Chin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ava', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2af2fca-c377-5773-9e64-69a23bd425a4', 'word_count': 345, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2af2fca-c377-5773-9e64-69a23bd425a4'}, {'abstract': 'Defense Secretary Leon E. Panetta, who arrived in Kabul on Saturday, also said the focus was now on capturing or killing 10 to 20 crucial Qaeda leaders.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/10/world/asia/10military.html', 'snippet': 'Defense Secretary Leon E. Panetta, who arrived in Kabul on Saturday, also said the focus was now on capturing or killing 10 to 20 crucial Qaeda leaders.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — Defense Secretary Leon E. Panetta, who arrived in Kabul on Saturday, said the United States was “within reach of strategically defeating Al Qaeda” and that the American focus had narrowed to capturing or killing 10 to 20 crucial leaders of the terrorist group in Pakistan, Somalia and Yemen. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/world/sub-10military/sub-10military-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/10/world/sub-10military/sub-10military-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/world/sub-10military/sub-10military-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/world/sub-10military/sub-10military-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/10/world/sub-10military/sub-10military-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Panetta Says Defeat of Al Qaeda Is ‘Within Reach’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Pentagon Chief Says Qaeda Defeat in Reach', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Panetta, Leon E', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kabul (Afghanistan)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T13:04:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Bumiller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bumiller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71c7d18e-ad3b-54cc-aa1c-59a4de52c1dd', 'word_count': 916, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71c7d18e-ad3b-54cc-aa1c-59a4de52c1dd'}, {'abstract': 'Joe Nocera has his first cover story for us this week: an exclusive sit-down with Sheila Bair, the outgoing head of the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation. It’s his customary stellar work.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/09/this-sunday-nocera-shoots-scores/', 'snippet': 'Joe Nocera has his first cover story for us this week: an exclusive sit-down with Sheila Bair, the outgoing head of the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation. It’s his customary stellar work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If Joe Nocera had his way — and he usually does — it wouldn’t be me writing this note, it would be him. Last fall, he was a top candidate for the job as editor of this magazine, and miraculously, I ended up with it instead. I didn’t know him well at the time. In fact, the only real conversation I’d had with him before then was when I tried to lure him to come work with me at Bloomberg Businessweek. I liked him instantly, though, and before I even moved in to my new office here, we had lunch, and I asked him to be my part-time consigliere, while he kept writing his Saturday column for the business page.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'This Sunday: Nocera Shoots, Scores', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T13:05:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hugo Lindgren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hugo', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lindgren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/60024ab2-6cad-5631-a3a5-543c49ac80f3', 'word_count'