ccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By JACK BELL', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'BELL', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e43d5cb-040a-5bb0-b33a-0acc026c23e6', 'word_count': 755, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e43d5cb-040a-5bb0-b33a-0acc026c23e6'}, {'abstract': 'Not a structural problem.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/09/the-fatalist-temptation/', 'snippet': 'Not a structural problem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m seeing more and more pieces like this one, in which pundits look at stubbornly high unemployment and declare that it must be structural — something we just have to live with, or at least something that will take long-term policies (translation — someone else’s problem) rather than mere stimulus, to correct.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Fatalist Temptation', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T13:47:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/30f63066-3198-5dd0-ac6b-48f19477f101', 'word_count': 306, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30f63066-3198-5dd0-ac6b-48f19477f101'}, {'abstract': 'Doing the 1937 thing, again.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/09/anti-stimulus-2/', 'snippet': 'Doing the 1937 thing, again.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here’s the CBO estimate of the effect of the Recovery Act on the deficit — not identical to its likely effect on the economy, but a rough guide — in billions of dollars, by fiscal year (fiscal years start in October of the previous calendar year):', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Anti-stimulus', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T14:35:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/362206ff-cb2c-5876-b8dd-5d02a97edac9', 'word_count': 110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/362206ff-cb2c-5876-b8dd-5d02a97edac9'}, {'abstract': 'The Yankees’ Alex Rodriguez has a slight meniscus tear in his right knee and Joe Girardi says he will need surgery, either now or in the off-season.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/09/a-rod-facing-knee-surgery/', 'snippet': 'The Yankees’ Alex Rodriguez has a slight meniscus tear in his right knee and Joe Girardi says he will need surgery, either now or in the off-season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We interrupt the Derek Jeter 3,000 watch for some news with potentially much more importance for the 2011 Yankees: Alex Rodriguez has a meniscus tear in his right knee.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A-Rod Facing Knee Surgery', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodriguez, Alex', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T14:56:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e379d807-b6d4-5c23-985e-4f0db1c2ae83', 'word_count': 215, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e379d807-b6d4-5c23-985e-4f0db1c2ae83'}, {'abstract': 'A court upheld a ruling that fined Prime Minister Silvio Berlusconi’s Fininivest holding company for bribing a judge.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/10/world/europe/10italy.html', 'snippet': 'A court upheld a ruling that fined Prime Minister Silvio Berlusconi’s Fininivest holding company for bribing a judge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — A Milan appeals court on Saturday ordered one of Prime Minister Silvio Berlusconi’s family holding companies to pay $798 million to a rival group as compensation for its corrupt activities in a takeover battle, further weakening the prime minister.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Italy Premier Loses Appeal on a Fine', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Italy Premier Loses Appeal On a Fine', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bribery and Kickbacks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berlusconi, Silvio', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fininvest SpA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T15:37:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gaia Pianigiani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gaia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pianigiani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/300c5a9a-1725-5ee5-9641-adb992fe0667', 'word_count': 324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/300c5a9a-1725-5ee5-9641-adb992fe0667'}, {'abstract': 'After more than five decades of a guerilla struggle and two million lives lost, the Republic of South Sudan, Africa’s 54th state, declared its independence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/10/world/africa/10sudan.html', 'snippet': 'After more than five decades of a guerilla struggle and two million lives lost, the Republic of South Sudan, Africa’s 54th state, declared its independence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JUBA, South Sudan — The celebrations erupted at midnight. Thousands of revelers poured into Juba’s steamy streets in the predawn hours on Saturday, hoisting enormous flags, singing, dancing and leaping on the back of cars.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/world/10sudan-span/10sudan-span-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/10/world/10sudan-span/10sudan-span-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/world/10sudan-span/10sudan-span-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/world/10sudan-span/10sudan-span-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/world/10sudan-span