 country, South Sudan, after a tumultuous independence struggle of more than 50 years that cost more than 3 million lives. South Sudanese deserve the celebration they’re enjoying in Juba and around the country.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Welcome to South Sudan!', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T16:22:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f800f0bc-46cb-50b7-8076-d721f5c22eec', 'word_count': 586, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f800f0bc-46cb-50b7-8076-d721f5c22eec'}, {'abstract': 'Do recent stumbles in the junk bond market signal a buying opportunity, or a category that has peaked?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/10/business/mutfund/junk-bonds-ready-to-rally-or-past-a-peak.html', 'snippet': 'Do recent stumbles in the junk bond market signal a buying opportunity, or a category that has peaked?', 'lead_paragraph': 'AFTER posting impressive double-digit returns for the last two years, high-yield bonds rose at a much slower pace in the first five months of this year and stumbled in June, ending the second quarter with a gain of only 0.65 percent. . ', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/business/10mf-JUNK/10mf-JUNK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 335, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/10/business/10mf-JUNK/10mf-JUNK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600