s', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/029899ae-1a1a-5641-b5b8-100a4a82f897', 'word_count': 883, 'uri': 'nyt://article/029899ae-1a1a-5641-b5b8-100a4a82f897'}, {'abstract': 'The flag that was put on the moon had to be trimmed to make it fit the staff, and the expected selling price of the shreds is $100,000.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/10/science/space/10moon.html', 'snippet': 'The flag that was put on the moon had to be trimmed to make it fit the staff, and the expected selling price of the shreds is $100,000.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was two weeks before the liftoff of the Apollo 11 mission when Thomas Moser’s boss walked into his office at NASA and announced, “We’re putting a flag on the moon.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/us/MOON-2/MOON-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 546, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/us/MOON-2/MOON-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/10/us/MOON-2/MOON-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Shreds of Moon History on the Block', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Shreds of NASA History, Going on the Block', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flags, Emblems and Insignia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Moon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T16:39:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Space & Cosmos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Douglas Quenqua', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Douglas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Quenqua', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5b01f0f-606b-5cff-a294-54fa73977bc4', 'word_count': 525, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5b01f0f-606b-5cff-a294-54fa73977bc4'}, {'abstract': 'The News of the World’s staff assembled on Saturday for the paper’s last working shift before it is shut down by the Murdoch empire.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/10/world/europe/10hacking.html', 'snippet': 'The News of the World’s staff assembled on Saturday for the paper’s last working shift before it is shut down by the Murdoch empire.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — With the tremors of The News of the World scandal still spreading across the landscape of British life, the newspaper’s staff assembled on Saturday for the paper’s last working shift before it is shut down by the Murdoch empire as part of its strategy for limiting the damage to its worldwide brand.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/world/10hack/10hack-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 921, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At a Paper Set to Close, Defiance and Foreboding', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At a Paper Set to Close, Defiance and Foreboding', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name'