liticians who criticized the country’s unforgiving tabloids. At a lunch in Westminster, Ms. Short mentioned in passing that she did not care for the photographs of saucy, topless women that appear every day on Page 3 of the populist tabloid The Sun, owned by Rupert Murdoch’s News Corporation. “I’d like to take the pornography out of our press,” she said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/world/10Britain1/10Britain1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 737, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Years, the Tabloids’ Sting Kept British Politicians in Line', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Years, the Tabloids’ Sting Kept British Politicians in Line', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News of the World', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Daily Mail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NEWS CORP', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sun, The (British Newspaper)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Short, Clare', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kinnock, Neil', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blair, Cherie', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brooks, Rebekah', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T16:39:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Lyall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lyall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4dad52c-f44c-57fa-8212-543521c6ad96', 'word_count': 1382, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4dad52c-f44c-57fa-8212-543521c6ad96'}, {'abstract': 'While N.F.L. lawyers parsed another court ruling, the N.B.A. quietly marked the eighth day of a surprisingly subdued lockout.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/10/sports/basketball/nba-lockout-puts-prospective-players-on-hold.html', 'snippet': 'While N.F.L. lawyers parsed another court ruling, the N.B.A. quietly marked the eighth day of a surprisingly subdued lockout.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The N.F.L.’s labor dispute commenced in March with all of the subtlety of an eight-man blitz. Within hours, the players had dissolved their union and sued the league, and the owners had imposed a lockout.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/sports/dog-nba/dog-nba-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 854, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Lockouts, Each With a Different Playbook', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Two Lockouts, Each With a Different Playbook', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stern, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lockouts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hunter, Billy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T16:44:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Howard Beck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Howard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2fe2a4b9-b37e-5f46-89db-8cc1f2c4ada6', 'word_count': 1075, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2fe2a4b9-b37e-5f46-89db-8cc1f2c4ada6'}, {'abstract': 'Three mutual funds — one focusing on value stocks, one on Asia and one on biotechnology — were among the better performers in a difficult second quarter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/10/business/mutfund/mutual-funds-that-succeeded-in-a-tough-2nd-quarter.html', 'snippet': 'Three mutual funds — one focusing on value stocks, one on Asia and one on biotechnology — were among the better performers in a difficult second quarter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRETFULNESS overtook optimism among stock investors in the second quarter. Many markets started the year strongly. Then, as spring turned to summer, recession worries rumbled back in the United States, debt continued to dog Europe, and inflation fears re-emerged in some emerging economies. The Standard & Poor’s 500-stock index lost 0.4 percent for the quarter, and several key international markets, including China and India, also chalked up losses. ', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url':