10/us/politics/10repubs.html', 'snippet': 'As Republican leaders negotiate over the federal debt limit, the candidates are campaigning against an outcome that involves compromise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DES MOINES — The decision by House Speaker John A. Boehner to scale back budget talks with President Obama unfolded as Republican presidential candidates were campaigning against any outcome that smacks of compromise, underscoring divisions in the party over whether to raise the federal debt limit.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/us/10repubs_span/10repubs_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/10/us/10repubs_span/10repubs_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/us/10repubs_span/10repubs_span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/us/10repubs_span/10repubs_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/10/us/10repubs_span/10repubs_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Presidential Candidates Warn About Debt Deal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Candidates Warn About Debt-Deal Compromise', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pawlenty, Tim', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McConnell, Mitch', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Ron', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bachmann, Michele M', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T19:48:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Zeleny and Carl Hulse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zeleny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hulse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3bc87942-e1e8-5cec-853b-b1649e4218e7', 'word_count': 1098, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3bc87942-e1e8-5cec-853b-b1649e4218e7'}, {'abstract': 'Dispersion plus rigidity.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/09/why-are-wages-still-rising-wonkish/', 'snippet': 'Dispersion plus rigidity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One reason comparisons between current events and the 1970s are so wrong — and fears that stagflation is just around the corner are so wrong (and have been wrong for three years running) — is the absence of any surge in wages:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Are Wages Still Rising? (Wonkish)', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T20:17:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e5f96c0-28cb-50c0-ad4f-f7bf42049931', 'word_count': 335, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e5f96c0-28cb-50c0-ad4f-f7bf42049931'}, {'abstract': 'Irakli Gedenidze, the personal photographer of President Mikhail Saakashvili, was shown on Georgian television confessing to selling information.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/10/world/europe/10georgia.html', 'snippet': 'Irakli Gedenidze, the personal photographer of President Mikhail Saakashvili, was shown on Georgian television confessing to selling information.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — The personal photographer of President Mikheil Saakashvili of Georgia was shown Saturday on Georgian television confessing to selling information to a man he suspected of being an agent for Russia.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Aide to Leader of Georgia Tied to Spying', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Aide to Leader Of Georgia Tied to Spying', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia (Georgian Republic)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classified Information and State Secrets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saakashvili, Mikheil', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T20:21:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ellen Barry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ellen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'An Appraisal', '_id': 'nyt://article/620b19c3-0357-5f85-b1f1-5a3d9d3599c4', 'word_count': 309, 'uri': 'nyt://article/620b19c3-0357-5f85-b1f1-5a3d9d3599c4'}, {'abstract': 'Challenging the competency of juvenile defendants to stand trial has become an increasingly popular move among defense lawyers, but the strategy has created new problems.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/10/us/10bcjuvenile.html', 'snippet': 'Challenging the competency of juvenile defendants to stand trial has become an increasingly popular move among defense lawyers, but the strategy has created new problems.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In April 2010, three boys, ages 12, 12 and 13, were accused of raping a 12-year-old female classmate in the gymnasium of their San Francisco middle school. Last month, the allegations against two of the boys were found to be true by a juvenile court judge, and they now await sentencing. The third boy is free and could have had his case dismissed — despite a detailed confession to the police — because a psychologist chosen by his lawyer said he was not competent to face a judge.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/us/10BCJUVENILE/10BCJUVENILE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 651, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/us/10BCJUVENILE/10BCJUVENILE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/10/us/10BCJUVENILE/10BCJUVENILE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Legal Tactic Raises Issues for Juveniles', 'kicker': 'The Bay Citizen', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Legal Tactic Raises Issues For Juveniles', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Juvenile Delinquency', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Judges', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T20:22:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Trey Bundy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Trey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bundy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f365737a-84f5-53e5-9a06-095285402dab', 'word_count': 1252, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f365737a-84f5-53e5-9a06-095285402dab'}, {'abstract': 'Derek Jeter went 5 for 5, including his 3,000th hit, and drove in the winning run before family, friends and adoring fans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/10/sports/baseball/after-making-history-jeter-makes-the-yankees-winners.html', 'snippet': 'Derek Jeter went 5 for 5, including his 3,000th hit, and drove in the winning run before family, friends and adoring fans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With one out in the third inning Saturday, space was at a premium on the rail of the Yankees’ dugout. Players and staff members crowded shoulder to shoulder, jostling for what they hoped would be the best view of history. Manager Joe Girardi was at one end, arms draped over the railing in his familiar pose; second baseman Robinson Cano was at the other end, a towel across his shoulder and one leg raised on the steps. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/sports/10jeter9/10jeter9-articleLarge.jp