//www.nytimes.com/2011/07/10/opinion/sunday/10kristof.html', 'snippet': 'Who said important books couldn’t be fun? Here’s the best beach reading ever.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SUMMER reading often consists of mindless page-turners, equally riveting and vacuous. So as a public service I’m delighted to offer a list of mindful page-turners — so full of chase scenes, romance and cliffhangers that you don’t mind the redeeming social value.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/nicholas-kristof/nicholas-kristof-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/nicholas-kristof/nicholas-kristof-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/nicholas-kristof/nicholas-kristof-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/nicholas-kristof/nicholas-kristof-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/nicholas-kristof/nicholas-kristof-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/nicholas-kristof/nicholas-kristof-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/nicholas-kristof/nicholas-kristof-thumbLarge-v2.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Action! Romance! Social Justice!', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Action! Romance! Social Justice!', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T21:11:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/6cbdd1b2-4169-570f-ae02-4d7671b8cbb2', 'word_count': 862, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6cbdd1b2-4169-570f-ae02-4d7671b8cbb2'}, {'abstract': 'A state of imposed ignorance was as native to pop culture nerds of the 20th century as it is foreign to those of the on-demand 21st.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/10/opinion/sunday/10coates.html', 'snippet': 'A state of imposed ignorance was as native to pop culture nerds of the 20th century as it is foreign to those of the on-demand 21st.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I saw Gil Scott-Heron perform, for the first time, in the fall of 1994. Like any scion of radical parentage, I was well acquainted with Heron’s sprawling catalogue. Still, even for me, a young man who reveled in the track listings of limited releases, the rangy Heron had packed a few surprises. In the midst of old favorites, he uncorked a haunting and somber ode to the civil rights activist Fannie Lou Hamer. If he gave the title I missed it, which is possible given that I was mesmerized by the song’s elegiac simplicity. I tried to commit every note to memory, but ultimately, I was left with shards of lyrics, pieces of melody and a deep intense longing for a song I couldn’t name.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/sunday-review/0710Coates/0710Coates-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 665, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/sunday-review/0710Coates/0710Coates-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/10/sunday-review/0710Coates/0710Coates-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Instant Music Gratification', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Instant Music Gratification', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rap and Hip-Hop', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scott-Heron, Gil', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T21:12:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ta-Nehisi Coates', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ta-nehisi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Coates', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/34d7670a-fabf-5e6c-acfd-55faf222a4aa', 'word_count': 773, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34d7670a-fabf-5e6c-acfd-55faf222a4aa'}, {'abstract': 'June’s bleak job numbers should change the conversation in the debt-limit talks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/10/opinion/sunday/10sun1.html', 'snippet': 'June’s bleak job numbers should change the conversation in the debt-limit talks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was not surprising to hear the Republican presidential candidates repeat their tiresome claim that excessive government spending and borrowing were behind Friday’s terrible unemployment report. It was depressing to hear President Obama sound as if he agreed with them.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Worst Time to Slow the Economy', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Worst Time to Slow the Economy: June’s bleak job numbers should change the conversation in the debt-limit talks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Labor Department (US)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T21:13:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e266fdc-0428-585f-8a92-17009749ec8a', 'word_count': 538, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e266fdc-0428-585f-8a92-17009749ec8a'}, {'abstract': 'At least one of the newly elected freshman Republican congressmen from Illinois won’t be around in January 2013, thanks to the redistricting maps drawn up by Democrats in the state legislature.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/10/us/10cncwarren.html', 'snippet': 'At least one of the newly elected freshman Republican congressmen from Illinois won’t be around in January 2013, thanks to the redistricting maps drawn up by Democrats in the state legislature.', 'lead_paragraph': 'James Warren writes a column for the Chicago News Cooperative.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Redistricting Squeezes G.O.P. Class of 2010', 'kicker': 'Chicago News Cooperative', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Redistricting Squeezes G.O.P. Class of 2010', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Redistricting and Reapportionment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T21:17:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Warren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Warren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9199cf47-0195-5ed6-9ff6-baaaea4461ba', 'word_count': 760, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9199cf47-0195-5ed6-9ff6-baaaea4461ba'}, {'abstract': 'NASA’s James Webb Space Telescope hits a budgetary wall, but it would be premature to terminate the program.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/10/opinion/sunday/10sun2.html', 'snippet': 'NASA’s James Webb Space Telescope hits a budgetary wall, but it would be premature to terminate the program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the space shuttle carries out its final mission to the space station orbiting 220 miles above the globe, NASA’s plan to conduct far more important research from a telescope that would be perched almost a million miles from Earth is in trouble. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Way Above the Shuttle Flight', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Way Above the Shuttle Flight: NASA’s next great space telescope hits a budgetary wall', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'James Webb Space Telescope', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Aeronautics and Space Administration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T21:20:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1c7f68c-43a3-5ed2-a933-0bdd145a4014', 'word_count': 414, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1c7f68c-43a3-5ed2-a933-0bdd145a4014'}, {'abstract': 'An exhibition of art created by laid-off Chicago art teachers has opened at the Flat Iron Building in Wicker Park.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/10/us/10cncteachers.html', 'snippet': 'An exhibition of art created by laid-off Chicago art teachers has opened at the Flat Iron Building in Wicker Park.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Katrina Barge, an artist who was among the 1,000 public schoolteachers laid off last summer, sat up a bit straighter as she described a recent painting. “It’s called ‘Though I’m Broken and Bruised, There’s Hope in This Pain,’\xa0” she said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/us/10CNCTEACHERS/10CNCTEACHERS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 734, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/us/10CNCTEACHERS/10CNCTEACHERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/10/us/10CNCTEACHERS/10CNCTEACHERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Laid-Off Art Teachers Turn to Their Craft to Express Themselves', 'kicker': 'Chicago News Cooperative', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Laid-Off Art Teachers Turn to Their Craft to Express Themselves', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T21:22:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jessica Reaves', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jessica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reaves', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d072bee1-8e7f-584d-bc5a-4e59e63b0db5', 'word_count': 521, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d072bee1-8e7f-584d-bc5a-4e59e63b0db5'}, {'abstract': 'The Israeli writer and filmmaker Etgar Keret talks about what’s interesting.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/10/opinion/sunday/10download.html', 'snippet': 'The Israeli writer and filmmaker Etgar Keret talks about what’s interesting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What’s interesting? The Sunday Review asked Etgar Keret, an Israeli short story writer and filmmaker who lectures at Ben-Gurion University of the Negev in Beersheba and at Tel Aviv University. Last year he received the Chevalier Medallion of France’s Ordre des Arts et des Lettres.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/sunday-review/0710Download/0710Download-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 769, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/sunday-review/0710Download/0710Download-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/10/sunday-review/0710Download/0710Download-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Etgar Keret', 'kicker': 'Download', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Etgar Keret', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keret, Etgar', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tel Aviv University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T21:25:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a140f5d-9967-5428-81cc-e0f13794262c', 'word_count': 417, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a140f5d-9967-5428-81cc-e0f13794262c'}, {'abstract': 'The state has reformed its juvenile system in impressive ways, including moving away from the prison model.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/10/opinion/sunday/10sun3.html', 'snippet': 'The state has reformed its juvenile system in impressive ways, including moving away from the prison model.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just four years ago, the Texas juvenile justice system was awash in allegations of brutality, neglect and sexual abuse by staff members. Thanks to leadership by Gov. Rick Perry and thoughtful, decisive action by the Legislature, a state juvenile justice system that was in chaos a few years ago is making impressive strides. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Texas’s Progress on Juvenile Justice', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Texas’s Progress on Juvenile Justice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Juvenile Delinquency', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T21:25:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/589a61a6-9c52-55e5-84e1-8b9284f49921', 'word_count': 329, 'uri': 'nyt://article/589a61a6-9c52-55e5-84e1-8b9284f49921'}, {'abstract': 'Readers offer their own suggestions for best beach reading.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/09/even-better-beach-reading/', 'snippet': 'Readers offer their own suggestions for best beach reading.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My Sunday column offers my own list of the Best Beach Reading Ever — essentially a list of my favorite works of fiction, in the sense of great page-turners that also brim with literary value or illuminate social justice themes. I listed my top 10, and I invite you to tell me where I erred — and which of your favorites I left off. This is your chance to recommend to other readers what novel to take on a summer vacation. Go for it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Even Better Beach Reading!', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T21:26:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c34bba28-d413-5efe-856e-9076cdba3fde', 'word_count': 85, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c34bba28-d413-5efe-856e-9076cdba3fde'}, {'abstract': 'Test your knowledge of recent events.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/10/opinion/sunday/10wait.html', 'snippet': 'Test your knowledge of recent events.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NPR’s “Wait Wait ... Don’t Tell Me!” is heard weekends on public radio stations across the country. (npr.org/programs/wait-wait-dont-tell-me/)', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/sunday-review/26QUIZ/26QUIZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 348, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'i