id something I have never done before as a journalist. I meddled with the story I was reporting. I entered it as a character who could affect its plot.” ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/sunday-review/INTERVIEW/INTERVIEW-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 474, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/sunday-review/INTERVIEW/INTERVIEW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/10/sunday-review/INTERVIEW/INTERVIEW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Art of the Interview', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Art of the Interview', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Malcolm, Janet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Paris Review', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roiphe, Katie', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Yorker', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T21:41:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Atlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Atlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/746bbee7-15e1-5b24-85c3-41cdd6096772', 'word_count': 1230, 'uri': 'nyt://article/746bbee7-15e1-5b24-85c3-41cdd6096772'}, {'abstract': 'Does Birmingham owe a debt to Chris McNair, whose 11-year-old daughter, Denise, died in a 1963 Ku Klux Klan bombing?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/10/opinion/sunday/10birmingham.html', 'snippet': 'Does Birmingham owe a debt to Chris McNair, whose 11-year-old daughter, Denise, died in a 1963 Ku Klux Klan bombing?', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHRIS McNAIR, symbol of the civil rights struggle in Birmingham, Ala., reported to federal prison last month, bereft of the media respect that has been his companion for most of his 85 years. In 1963, Mr. McNair’s 11-year-old daughter, Denise, died along with three other black Sunday school girls in the Ku Klux Klan bombing of the 16th Street Baptist Church. Mr. McNair, then a school-teacher turned photographer, transcended his anguish to become an agent of community healing, a popular politician whom white people appreciated for his policy of not bringing up his child’s martyrdom.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/sunday-review/0710Birgminham1/0710Birgminham1-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 411, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/10/sunday-review/0710Birgminham1/0710Birgminham1-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 411}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/sunday-review/0710Birgminham1/0710Birgminham1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 691, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/10/sunday-review/0710Birgminham1/0710Birgminham1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/10/sunday-review/0710Birgminham1/0710Birgminham1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Redemption in Birmingham', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Redemption in Birmingham', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Amnesties, Commutations and Pardons', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Birmingham (Ala)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T21:42:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Diane McWhorter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Diane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McWhorter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9c942be-5c2d-52c5-a471-740c8c20970b', 'word_count': 1602, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9c942be-5c2d-52c5-a471-740c8c20970b'}, {'abstract': 'Modern lust focuses less on carnal pleasure than on control.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/10/opinion/sunday/10sex.html', 'snippet': 'Modern lust focuses less on carnal pleasure than on control.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHAT could be more eternal than sexuality? The fog of longing, the obsession with the loved one’s voice, smell, touch. Sex is discombobulating and distracting, it makes you immune to money, politics and family. And sometimes I think the younger generation wants 