 from Venezuela who switch-hits, wears No. 13 and first belonged to the Mariners. This was true in the 1990s, when Omar Vizquel roamed the infield. It is true again, with Asdrubal Cabrera.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/09/in-vizquels-mold-but-all-his-own/', 'snippet': 'Cleveland’s shortstop is a dazzling defensive player from Venezuela who switch-hits, wears No. 13 and first belonged to the Mariners. This was true in the 1990s, when Omar Vizquel roamed the infield. It is true again, with Asdrubal Cabrera.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CLEVELAND — The shortstop for the Cleveland Indians is a dazzling defensive player from Venezuela who switch-hits, wears No. 13 and first belonged to the Seattle Mariners. This was true in the 1990s, when Omar Vizquel helped the Indians to two American League pennants. It is true again today, with Asdrubal Cabrera.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Vizquel’s Mold, but All His Own', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vizquel, Omar', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cleveland Indians', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T22:16:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9524f58e-eade-553a-96c0-dc2ede637924', 'word_count': 695, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9524f58e-eade-553a-96c0-dc2ede637924'}, {'abstract': 'A failed holdup quickly turns into something far more serious.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/09/queens-grocery-owner-slain-in-robbery/', 'snippet': 'A failed holdup quickly turns into something far more serious.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was around closing time when a masked man with a gun walked into a Queens grocery on Friday night and, as a robbery attempt failed, fatally shot a 65-year-old clerk as he ran for the front door, the authorities said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Queens Grocery Worker Slain in Robbery', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-09T22:22:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Al Baker and Tim Stelloh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Al', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelloh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e88f4876-6a77-5fd7-b79f-af713898e92d', 'word_count': 651, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e88f4876-6a77-5fd7-b79f-af713898e92d'}, {'abstract': 'The cancellation of hundreds of millions in aid is meant to chasten Pakistan for expelling American trainers and press its army to fight militants more effectively.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/10/world/asia/10intel.html', 'snippet': 'The cancellation of hundreds of millions in aid is meant to chasten Pakistan for expelling American trainers and press its army to fight militants more effectively.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Obama administration is suspending and, in some cases, canceling hundreds of millions of dol