enturous guests can now spend the night in their very own boat and sleep under the stars in Far Rockaway.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As part of an art installation, adventurous guests can now spend the night in their very own boat and sleep under the stars in Far Rockaway.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/11/multimedia/video-boatel/video-boatel-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/11/multimedia/video-boatel/video-boatel-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/11/multimedia/video-boatel/video-boatel-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/11/multimedia/video-boatel/video-boatel-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'If You Build It', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boats and Boating', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-10T22:20:59+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'Melena Ryzik|Channon Hodge', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': 'Ryzik', 'lastname': 'Channon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/1b6b9e8a-da98-50ac-92db-df9f246bfe88', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/1b6b9e8a-da98-50ac-92db-df9f246bfe88'}, {'abstract': 'The following tax-exempt fixed-income issues are scheduled for pricing this week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/11/business/treasury-auctions-set-for-this-week.html', 'snippet': 'The following tax-exempt fixed-income issues are scheduled for pricing this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Treasury’s schedule of financing this week includes Monday’s regular weekly auction of new three- and six-month bills and an auction of four-week bills on Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Treasury Auctions Set for This Week', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Treasury Auctions Set for This Week', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-10T22:23:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb76d238-ecaf-5d12-9dac-c82808ab0745', 'word_count': 375, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb76d238-ecaf-5d12-9dac-c82808ab0745'}, {'abstract': 'Elected officials defended the woman who has accused Dominique Strauss-Kahn of sexual assault, and asked that the case be brought to trial.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/10/in-harlem-a-rally-to-an-accusers-defense/', 'snippet': 'Elected officials defended the woman who has accused Dominique Strauss-Kahn of sexual assault, and asked that the case be brought to trial.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the sexual assault case against Dominique Strauss-Kahn teetered on the brink of collapse, several supporters of his accuser gathered in Harlem on Sunday to urge the Manhattan district attorney, Cyrus R. Vance Jr., to pursue the case “vigorously.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Harlem, a Rally to an Accuser’s Defense', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-10T22:27:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noah Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/96dc7991-bacc-5f5b-9445-8046d86410e5', 'word_count': 464, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96dc7991-bacc-5f5b-9445-8046d86410e5'}, {'abstract': 'The Hallmark Hall of Fame movie franchise has a new home on network television: ABC.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/11/arts/television/abc-sends-greetings-to-hallmark-movies.html', 'snippet': 'The Hallmark Hall of Fame movie franchise has a new home on network television: ABC.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Hallmark Hall of Fame movie franchise has a new home on network television: ABC. A multiyear agreement, announced last week by Hallmark, came two months after CBS decided not to renew its deal to show the feel-good movies at greeting-card-buying times of the year. In a twist the Hallmark Channel will show the movies a week after they have their premieres on ABC. “Our agreement to follow ABC premieres with encores on Hallmark Channel is an exciting, unprecedented use of broadcast and cable,” Brad Moore, the president of the Hallmark Hall of Fame, said in a statement. The first movie on ABC, “Mitch Albom’s Have a Little Faith,” will be shown in December.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'ABC Sends Greetings to Hallmark Movies', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'ABC Sends Greetings To Hallmark Movies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hallmark Channel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC INC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-10T22:43:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c366f58-624b-5860-b2be-77b0c8f0dda9', 'word_count': 116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c366f58-624b-5860-b2be-77b0c8f0dda9'}, {'abstract': 'The 23rd James Bond film has begun casting in earnest, with Javier Bardem and Ralph Fiennes both confirmed to appear, according to The Daily Mail.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/11/movies/stars-announced-for-next-bond-film.html', 'snippet': 'The 23rd James Bond film has begun casting in earnest, with Javier Bardem and Ralph Fiennes both confirmed to appear, according to The Daily Mail.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After being held back for years by financial troubles at MGM Studios, the 23rd James Bond film has begun casting in earnest, with Javier Bardem and Ralph Fiennes, both confirmed to appear, according to The Daily Mail. Mr. Bardem, who won an Academy Award in 2008 for his villainous turn in “No Country for Old Men,” has been previously quoted by The Los Angeles Times as saying that he was in talks to play the nemesis of Daniel Craig’s 007. Mr. Fiennes’s role was not specified. Directed by Sam Mendes and partly financed by Sony, the film is slated for release on Nov. 9, 2012, and is to begin shooting this year.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stars Announced for Next Bond Film', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stars Announced For Next Bond Film', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fiennes, Ralph', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bardem, Javier', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bond, James (Fictional Character)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-10T22:44:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8f95c1e-7aa2-54c7-800f-ca11a9694fc1', 'word_count': 116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8f95c1e-7aa2-54c7-800f-ca11a9694fc1'}, {'abstract': 'A concert performance in Dallas by the singer Rihanna ended abruptly on Friday night after a small fire broke out above the stage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/11/arts/music/fire-stops-rihanna.html', 'snippet': 'A concert performance in Dallas by the singer Rihanna ended abruptly on Friday night after a small fire broke out above the stage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A concert performance in Dallas by the singer Rihanna ended abruptly on Friday night after a small fire broke out above the stage. The fire occurred during the hit song “California King Bed,” forcing concertgoers to evacuate the American Airlines Center as sparks rained down on the stage from the rafters, according to the Web site Celebuzz! Although no official makeup date has been announced, Rihanna expressed her frustration on her Twitter account with a promise that she would return. No injuries were reported.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fire Stops Rihanna', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fire Stops Rihanna', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rihanna', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-10T22:54:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed137488-1593-5235-bb14-6e53f9207442', 'word_count': 85, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed137488-1593-5235-bb14-6e53f9207442'}, {'abstract': 'A brazen faux celebrity was known for stunts in a less security-conscious time.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/11/us/11bremen.html', 'snippet': 'A brazen faux celebrity was known for stunts in a less security-conscious time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Barry Bremen, a novelty-goods salesman who achieved a kind of flash celebrity in the 1980s as a ubiquitous impostor who slipped past security to shag fly balls in the major leagues, shoot baskets in the N.B.A. and accept somebody else’s Emmy Award on national television, died on June 30 in Phoenix. He was 64.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/11/us/11bremen_1/11bremen_1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/11/us/11bremen_1/11bremen_1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/11/us/