om seawater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Princeton, N.J.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/11/opinion/11oped-art/11oped-art-articleLarge-v6.jpg', 'height': 432, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/11/opinion/11oped-art/11oped-art-articleLarge-v6.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 432}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/11/opinion/11oped-art/11oped-art-jumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 937, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/11/opinion/11oped-art/11oped-art-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/11/opinion/11oped-art/11oped-art-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Seawater Can Power the World', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How Seawater Can Power the World', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fusion (Nuclear Reaction)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Laboratories and Scientific Equipment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-11T01:07:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stewart C. Prager', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stewart', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Prager', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/c80789de-b8a5-513a-a898-1e1837e410d5', 'word_count': 764, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c80789de-b8a5-513a-a898-1e1837e410d5'}, {'abstract': 'The impact of Carlos Beltran’s speech cannot be measured, but some of the things he saw that compelled him to feel positively can be examined.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/11/sports/baseball/mets-first-half-review-beltrans-reaction-to-an-owners-public-criticisms.html', 'snippet': 'The impact of Carlos Beltran’s speech cannot be measured, but some of the things he saw that compelled him to feel positively can be examined.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — In the wake of public criticisms from Fred Wilpon, the Mets’ principal owner, in a May edition of The New Yorker, the team held a meeting in the cramped visitors’ clubhouse at Wrigley Field. Carlos Beltran, one of the players singled out by Wilpon, spoke to his teammates and the coaching staff.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/11/sports/subYHALFMETS2/subYHALFMETS2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 945, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/11/sports/subYHALFMETS2/subYHALFMETS2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/11/sports/subYHALFMETS2/subYHALFMETS2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Despite Criticism by an Owner, Positive Feelings', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Despite Criticism By an Owner, Positive Feelings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reyes, Jose', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilpon, Fred', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beltran, Carlos', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-11T01:12:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f19b305-7e59-56d3-976d-3e02346b6ec2', 'word_count': 1107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f19b305-7e59-56d3-976d-3e02346b6ec2'}, {'abstract': 'For Rupert Murdoch, newspapers have been useful in wielding influence and are the very thing that brought his company into the cross hairs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/11/business/media/a-tabloid-shame-exposed-by-honest-rivals.html', 'snippet': 'For Rupert Murdoch, newspapers have been useful in wielding influence and are the very thing that brought his company into the cross hairs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The phone-hacking scandal that is mushrooming in Britain, with arrests, skullduggery and influence peddling, would be a delicious story for The News of the World if it were not about the newspaper itself. Instead, the hunter became the hunted, and last Thursday Rupert Murdoch’s News Corporation summarily slid the 168-year-old News of the World under a double-decker bus. Its final issue was Sunday. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': No