 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8afa3c3-7a24-5555-b36d-c9c067a1c938', 'word_count': 406, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8afa3c3-7a24-5555-b36d-c9c067a1c938'}, {'abstract': 'The rush speaks to improvements in a transit system once seen as a national symbol of urban blight, but it also points to the shifting cultural and economic picture of New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/11/nyregion/with-weekends-not-sleepy-anymore-subway-faces-a-test.html', 'snippet': 'The rush speaks to improvements in a transit system once seen as a national symbol of urban blight, but it also points to the shifting cultural and economic picture of New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York City slows down on the weekends, and its subway is no exception: long waits, jumbled routes, trains that skip stops and sometimes never appear. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/11/nyregion/subway1/subway1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/11/nyregion/subway1/subway1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/11/nyregion/subway1/subway1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 701, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/11/nyregion/subway1/subway1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/11/nyregion/subway1/subway1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Subway Crush No Longer Gets Weekends Off', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Subway Crush No Longer Gets Weekends Off', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Transportation Authority', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subways', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-11T01:42:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael M. Grynbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0143d97-3254-5e35-af3a-4c7b48df4b3a', 'word_count': 1088, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0143d97-3254-5e35-af3a-4c7b48df4b3a'}, {'abstract': 'City Room wants our readers to chime in with their own memories. Is there such a thing as nostalgia for that dark time of the underground?', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/10/remembrances-of-empty-subways-of-weekends-past/', 'snippet': 'City Room wants our readers to chime in with their own memories. Is there such a thing as nostalgia for that dark time of the underground?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ah, weekends on the New York City subway — that bucolic, tranquil period when the commuting masses empty out of the metropolis and blissfully human-free subway cars yield a comfortable seat to even the most jaded straphangers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Remembrances of Empty Subways of Weekends Past', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subways', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transit Systems', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Transportation Authority', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-11T01:50:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael M. Grynbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7c5beea-b412-5d54-8295-4cba0b03c7cd', 'word_count': 360, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7c5beea-b412-5d54-8295-4cba0b03c7cd'}, {'abstract': 'A strategy for making Israel’s 1967 borders defensible.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/11/opinion/11Sneh.html', 'snippet': 'A strategy for making Israel’s 1967 borders defensible.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Herzliya, Israel', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bad Borders, Good Neighbors', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bad Borders, Good Neighbors', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netanyahu, Benjamin', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-11T01:52:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ephraim Sneh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ephraim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sneh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/d913cf45-9983-509f-b085-f85dfb6d2fc3', 'word_count': 834, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d913cf45-9983-509f-b085-f85dfb6d2fc3'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Cabral was a protesting voice of conscience against social injustice and dictatorship in Latin America.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/11/arts/music/facundo-cabral-argentine-singer-songwriter-dies-at-74.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Cabral was a protesting voice of conscience against social injustice and dictatorship in Latin America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Facundo Cabral, an Argentine singer-songwriter who was one of the most eloquent voices of protest against military dictatorships in Latin America from the 1970s onward, died on Saturday, shot to death while on tour in Guatemala. He was 74 and lived in Buenos Aires.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/11/arts/cabral-obit/cabral-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 985, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/11/arts/cabral-obit/cabral-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/11/arts/cabral-obit/cabral-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Facundo Cabral, Singer of Conscience, Dies at 74', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Facundo Cabral, 74, Singer of Conscience', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Latin America', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-11T01:59:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Rohter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/c459ab53-af9d-5cf3-bfa5-1afd333916cd', 'word_count': 782, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c459ab53-af9d-5cf3-bfa5-1afd333916cd'}, {'abstract': 'Tough new limits on power plant emissions will improve lives and save money.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/11/opinion/11mon1.html', 'snippet': 'Tough new limits on power plant emissions will improve lives and save money.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Environmental Protection Agency on Thursday issued a welcome and overdue rule compelling power plants in 27 states and the District of Columbia to reduce smokestack emissions that pollute the air and poison forests, lakes and streams across the eastern United States. The regulation reflects the E.P.A.’s determination to carry out its mandates under the Clean Air Act despite fierce Congressional opposition, and bodes well for progress on a host of other regulatory challenges the agency faces. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Aggressive Ruling on Clean Air', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Aggressive Ruling on Clean Air: Tough new limits on power plant emissions will improve lives and save money', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Clean Air Act', 'rank'