'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cho, Seung-Hui', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-11T03:04:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/3986ca2f-3764-5888-8937-ef2751b7c159', 'word_count': 515, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3986ca2f-3764-5888-8937-ef2751b7c159'}, {'abstract': 'If the State Senate doesn’t stop blocking the exchanges, New York may lose out on millions of dollars in federal support.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/11/opinion/11mon3.html', 'snippet': 'If the State Senate doesn’t stop blocking the exchanges, New York may lose out on millions of dollars in federal support.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the frenzied final days of New York’s legislative session, an important health care measure fell by the wayside. The Republican-led State Senate failed to pass a bill to establish a health insurance exchange where individuals and small businesses would be able to buy coverage starting in 2014. An identical bill had already passed the Democratic-led Assembly.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dropping the Ball on Health Exchanges', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dropping the Ball on Health Exchanges', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-11T03:07:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/c879de79-65c9-573b-869c-928faf751d70', 'word_count': 322, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c879de79-65c9-573b-869c-928faf751d70'}, {'abstract': 'Three thousand hits is a wonderful milestone, but numbers alone cannot adequately measure the achievement of the Yankees’ Derek Jeter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/11/opinion/11mon4.html', 'snippet': 'Three thousand hits is a wonderful milestone, but numbers alone cannot adequately measure the achievement of the Yankees’ Derek Jeter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here’s the thing about Derek Jeter: He’s great and we love him, with an admiration that has little to do with statistical milestones and big round numbers. He got his 3,000th hit on Saturday, as a million flashbulbs popped and documentary cameras rolled and cheers and emotion washed over Yankee Stadium. It was an extraordinary moment, mixed with relief. His chase for an abstraction was finally over, and he could go back to the day-in, day-out job of being Derek Jeter, Yankee shortstop. That’s the great long trip he’s still on, and we’re just glad to be along, never mind what the hit odometer says.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jeter’s Moment', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jeter’s Moment', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jeter, Derek', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Records and Achievements', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-11T03:09:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'sect