mes', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Winning New York-Balanced Meal', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-11T15:54:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Kolomatsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kolomatsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/23628890-2381-529d-aa50-dc8223a56ec9', 'word_count': 233, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23628890-2381-529d-aa50-dc8223a56ec9'}, {'abstract': 'The Lonza Group, a Swiss supplier of pharmaceutical ingredients, has agreed to buy Arch Chemicals, a maker of antimicrobial products based in Connecticut.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/07/11/lonza-to-buy-arch-chemicals-for-1-2-billion/', 'snippet': 'The Lonza Group, a Swiss supplier of pharmaceutical ingredients, has agreed to buy Arch Chemicals, a maker of antimicrobial products based in Connecticut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Lonza Group, a Swiss supplier of pharmaceutical ingredients seeking to diversify its product lineup, said on Monday that it had agreed to buy Arch Chemicals for $1.2 billion in cash.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lonza to Buy Arch Chemicals for $1.2 Billion', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Microbiology', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARCH CHEMICALS INC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-11T15:55:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris V. Nicholson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': 'V.', 'lastname': 'Nicholson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/74136be2-109e-52fb-91c9-4f3d1cee4fcc', 'word_count': 298, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74136be2-109e-52fb-91c9-4f3d1cee4fcc'}, {'abstract': 'As a result of myriad obstacles, just 10 percent of adults over age 60 were vaccinated against shingles in 2009 in the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/health/12shingles.html', 'snippet': 'As a result of myriad obstacles, just 10 percent of adults over age 60 were vaccinated against shingles in 2009 in the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Five years have passed since the Food and Drug Administration approved a vaccine against shingles. By now, experts had expected a substantial proportion of people older than 60, the most vulnerable population, to be protected from outbreaks of this nasty viral disease and the persistent, debilitating pain it can leave behind.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Drive to Stem Shingles Meets Few Expectations', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Drive to Stem Shingles Meets Few Expectations', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shingles (Disease)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shortages', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-11T15:56:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paula Span', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paula', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Span', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f31f7c74-30f3-5727-9ba7-8d53473967cf', 'word_count': 1147, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f31f7c74-30f3-5727-9ba7-8d53473967cf'}, {'abstract': 'A “dream come true” for Liza Minnelli, who was awarded the rank of “officier” in the Legion of Honor by France’s culture minister, Frédéric Mitterrand.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/11/star-icon-and-now-an-officer-in-the-legion-of-honor/', 'snippet': 'A “dream come true” for Liza Minnelli, who was awarded the rank of “officier” in the Legion of Honor by France’s culture minister, Frédéric Mitterrand.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS – Liza Minnelli has three Tonys, two Golden Globes, an Oscar, an Emmy and a Grammy legend award. Now the 65-year-old singer and actress also has the rank of “officier” in the Legion of Honor, the award for service to the French state created by Napoleon in 1802. In the grand salon of his ministry on Monday, Culture Minister Frédéric Mitterrand pinned an enameled vermeil medal affixed to a red grosgrain ribbon onto Ms. Minnelli’s black silk brocade jacket. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Star Is Now an ‘Officier’ in the Legion of Honor', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Caine, Michael', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eastwood, Clint', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Minnelli, Liza', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Minnelli, Vincente', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mitterrand, Frederic', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Napoleon I', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Redford, Robert', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sartre, Jean-Paul', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spielberg, Steven', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-11T15:57:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elaine Sciolino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elaine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sciolino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6bda8ef7-c1a6-5363-893c-bc395a9082c5', 'word_count': 759, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6bda8ef7-c1a6-5363-893c-bc395a9082c5'}, {'abstract': 'Nice work if you can get it.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/11/turning-fresh-water-into-very-expensive-wine/', 'snippet': 'Nice work if you can get it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Paul Ryan’s drinking companions identified. A bit about one of the two amigos in my Keynes lecture.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Turning (Fresh) Water Into (Very Expensive) Wine', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-11T16:04:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ceaecf1-3967-573e-b217-ef37ce210677', 'word_count': 17, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ceaecf1-3967-573e-b217-ef37ce210677'}, {'abstract': 'The large and deadly accidental blast leveled a munitions storage facility on Monday, killing at least 12 people and wounding dozens more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/world/europe/12cyprus.html', 'snippet': 'The large and deadly accidental blast leveled a munitions storage facility on Monday, killing at least 12 people and wounding dozens more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATHENS — The leader of the Cyprus Navy died in a large blast that leveled a munitions storage facility and prompted two of the country’s highest military leaders to resign from their posts, the defense ministry said. At least 11 others — including the commander of the naval base — also died, and dozens more were wounded.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cyprus Navy Chief Dies in Blast at Arms Depot', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cyprus: Blast at Base Kills Navy Chief', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cyprus', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-11T16:20:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Niki Kitsantonis and J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Niki', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kitsantonis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aaf3b8aa-984d-54ce-9b6b-f68402c886e7', 'word_count': 329, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aaf3b8aa-984d-54ce-9b6b-f68402c886e7'}, {'abstract': 'Don’t discredit the barbecued poultry just yet-  there are ways to keep chicken from going dry.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/11/now-grilling-juicy-summer-chicken/', 'snippet': 'Don’t discredit the barbecued poultry just yet-  there are ways to keep chicken from going dry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I suspect I’m not the only griller around whose friends are grateful he studied\xa0Sam Sifton’s walk-through for Texas-style beef ribs, but on the days when I didn’t have 8 hours to slow cook 12 pounds of meat, I would default to German hamburgers and Italian sausages. This opened the floodgates. Without my noticing, I went from cooking barbecue bimonthly (that’s every other month) to semimonthly (almost every other week).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Now Grilling | Juicy Summer Chicken', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-11T16:27:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Nichols', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nichols', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/30463936-4660-57e7-9499-1537f60e3881', 'word_count': 968, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30463936-4660-57e7-9499-1537f60e3881'}, {'abstract': 'As a phone-hacking scandal threatens to derail News Corporation’s bid to buy BSkyB, Jeremy Hunt said that the Competition Commission would take up the review process, which could delay approval for months.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/07/11/british-official-refers-bskyb-deal-to-another-regulator/', 'snippet': 'As a phone-hacking scandal threatens to derail News Corporation’s bid to buy BSkyB, Jeremy Hunt said that the Competition Commission would take up the review process, which could delay approval for months.', 'lead_paragraph': ' As a phone-hacking scandal threatens to derail News Corporation’s bid to buy BSkyB, a British official has referred the merger to the Competition Commission for approval, which could delay approval for months.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'British Official Refers BSkyB Deal to Another Regulator', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'British Sky Broadcasting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NEWS CORP', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-11T16:27:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4031a59e-0822-589d-be2e-12dd36132c89', 'word_count': 187, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4031a59e-0822-589d-be2e-12dd36132c89'}, {'abstract': 'Did a fan make a mistake in giving Derek Jeter the baseball that the Yankee shortstop struck for his 3,000th career hit?', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/11/rethinking-a-gift-to-jeter/', 'snippet': 'Did a fan make a mistake in giving Derek Jeter the baseball that the Yankee shortstop struck for his 3,000th career hit?', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was gracious, magnanimous, a class act.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rethinking a Gift to Jeter', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Records and Achievements', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jeter, Derek', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-11T16:28:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5df6d42-ca6b-517a-af49-bf8d20c894f4', 'word_count': 189, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5df6d42-ca6b-517a-af49-bf8d20c894f4'}, {'abstract': 'From a distance, watching the beautiful game in its truest form at the Women’s World Cup.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/11/womens-world-cup-a-great-cultural-display-of-futbol/', 'snippet': 'From a distance, watching the beautiful game in its truest form at the Women’s World Cup.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This past weekend, I witnessed the beautiful game in its truest form.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Women’s World Cup: A Great Cultural Display of Fútbol', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's World Cup (Soccer)", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Solo, Hope', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wambach, Abby', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "United States Women's National Soccer Team", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-11T16:42:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Yael Averbuch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Yael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Averbuch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/adb8953d-2065-551a-9c77-12f6c2bd6ecd', 'word_count': 607, 'uri': 'nyt://article/adb8953d-2065-551a-9c77-12f6c2bd6ecd'}, {'abstract': 'Jobless workers may not be living comfortably, but they are at least able to get by. That means they have less need to resort to more radical political activities — for now.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/11/are-jobless-benefits-keeping-the-unemployed-complacent-and-invisible/', 'snippet': 'Jobless workers may not be living comfortably, but they are at least able to get by. That means they have less need to resort to more radical political activities — for now.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In an article on Sunday, I wrote about why our unemployment crisis has been largely ignored by Washington. Among the major factors I cited were that unemployed workers are less likely to vote than their employed counterparts. Additionally, the jobless are not as politically organized as they once were because they are more geographically dispersed and because the institutions that organized them have become weaker.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Are Jobless Benefits Keeping the Unemployed Complacent (and Invisible)?', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment Insurance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-11T16:47:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/79400c2c-7833-5fe5-bf0b-03ee69e6b4f2', 'word_count': 420, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79400c2c-7833-5fe5-bf0b-03ee69e6b4f2'}, {'abstract': 'Virgin Mobile Freefest tickets will be given out on Facebook on Friday, and 40,000 people are expected to attend the free concert in Maryland in September.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/11/free-tickets-for-virgin-mobile-music-festival/', 'snippet': 'Virgin Mobile Freefest tickets will be given out on Facebook on Friday, and 40,000 people are expected to attend the free concert in Maryland in September.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TV on the Radio, The Black Keys and Cee Lo Green will be among the bands appearing at this year’s Virgin Mobile Freefest, a free music festival to be held on Sept. 10 in Columbia, Md., the festival’s organizers announced on Monday. This is the third year that this mobile telephone company started by Richard Branson, along with Kyocera Wireless, has footed the bill for the festival, which is expected to draw about 40,000 people. The tickets are to be given away through Virgin Mobile Live’s Facebook page starting at 10 a.m. Friday. For the past annual festivals, the tickets disappeared in a matter of minutes.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Free Tickets for Virgin Mobile Music Festival', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lineup Announced For Free Music Festival', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Big Sean (1988- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Branson, Richard', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Green, Cee Lo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Patti', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Black Keys', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook.com', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Grace Potter and the Nocturnals', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kyocera Corporation', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Okkervil River', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TV on the Radio', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Virgin Mobile', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-11T16:47:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5fe5090-96d6-5d70-8382-554f781502b8', 'word_count': 270, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5fe5090-96d6-5d70-8382-554f781502b8'}, {'abstract': 'Sheila C. Bair, who ended a tumultuous five-year term as chairwoman of the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation this month, has landed a book deal to give her inside account of the financial crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/11/sheila-bair-to-write-book-on-financial-crisis/', 'snippet': 'Sheila C. Bair, who ended a tumultuous five-year term as chairwoman of the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation this month, has landed a book deal to give her inside account of the financial crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sheila C. Bair has landed a book deal to give her inside account of the financial crisis, just as her tumultuous five-year term as chairwoman of the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation has ended.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sheila Bair to Write Book on Financial Crisis', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bair, Sheila C', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Deposit Insurance Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-11T16:55:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c451ea4-b232-5c74-a613-6a1f63c95caa', 'word_count': 406, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c451ea4-b232-5c74-a613-6a1f63c95caa'}, {'abstract': 'Republicans want to reverse a measure that required incandescent bulbs to be more efficient. Foes of their effort point out that consumers will save money over all if the rule stays in place.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/11/house-to-vote-on-light-bulb-repeal/', 'snippet': 'Republicans want to reverse a measure that required incandescent bulbs to be more efficient. Foes of their effort point out that consumers will save money over all if the rule stays in place.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The House is expected to vote as early as Monday night on a measure to repeal efficiency standards for light bulbs that are scheduled to take effect at the beginning of next year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Repeal Vote Set on Light Bulb Standards', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Compact Fluorescent Light Bulbs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservation of Resources', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Light Bulbs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Energy Efficiency', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Light-Emitting Diodes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barton, Joe L', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beck, Glenn', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chu, Steven', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Limbaugh, Rush', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Upton, Fred', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-11T17:01:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By John M. Broder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/691dca8a-c206-5e94-ab68-ab20995cf198', 'word_count': 663, 'uri': 'nyt://article/691dca8a-c206-5e94-ab68-ab20995cf198'}, {'abstract': 'A report found that in 92 percent of the cases in which an Alabama judge overrode a juries’ recommendation, the judge imposed the death sentence over life in prison.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/us/12bar.html', 'snippet': 'A report found that in 92 percent of the cases in which an Alabama judge overrode a juries’ recommendation, the judge imposed the death sentence over life in prison.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Alabama allows judges to reject sentencing decisions from capital juries, which sounds like a sensible idea. You might want a mature and dispassionate jurist standing between a wounded community’s impulse toward vengeance and a defendant at risk of execution.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Overriding the Jury in Capital Cases', 'kicker': 'Sidebar', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Overriding the Jury In Capital Cases', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Judges', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALABAMA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jury System', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-11T17:03:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Liptak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liptak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2bb6bcb8-b235-5c2e-9088-acf99b1911c2', 'word_count': 836, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2bb6bcb8-b235-5c2e-9088-acf99b1911c2'}, {'abstract': 'Our first winner of this month’s weekly Summer Reading Contest, and some reflections on the other wonderful submissions we received.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/11/student-reading-contest-winner-on-dominique-strauss-kahn/', 'snippet': 'Our first winner of this month’s weekly Summer Reading Contest, and some reflections on the other wonderful submissions we received.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We promise we didn’t plant, pay for or otherwise cajole BrandonK-BSGE2016 to post the comment above to the first week of our summer reading contest. If we had written our fantasy response, however, I’m not sure we could have done better.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Student Reading Contest Winner | On Dominique Strauss-Kahn', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-11T17:06:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/40d62e74-30f4-599b-b922-584429b1692a', 'word_count': 791, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40d62e74-30f4-599b-b922-584429b1692a'}, {'abstract': 'Elizabeth Bishop versus A.E. Hotchner, Dana Goodyear, John Doerr and Dorothy Parker.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/11/sentence-of-the-week-telegram-edition/', 'snippet': 'Elizabeth Bishop versus A.E. Hotchner, Dana Goodyear, John Doerr and Dorothy Parker.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here are this week’s candidates:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sentence of the Week, Telegram Edition', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parker, Dorothy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-11T17:23:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Anderson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Anderson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bfe83704-209d-5ae6-871c-6fad079286c9', 'word_count': 457, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bfe83704-209d-5ae6-871c-6fad079286c9'}, {'abstract': 'A study says that until the whaling industry depleted their ranks, California gray whales thrived for millions of years during ice ages that cut off their migration routes and compromised their diets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/science/12obwhale.html', 'snippet': 'A study says that until the whaling industry depleted their ranks, California gray whales thrived for millions of years during ice ages that cut off their migration routes and compromised their diets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like those of its cousins the humpback and the blue, the population of the California gray whale was severely depleted by the whaling industry. But researchers are reporting that until humans came along, the California gray was remarkably resilient.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/12/science/12obwhale/OBOX-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 454, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/12/science/12obwhale/OBOX-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 454}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/12/science/12obwhale/OBOX-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 766, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/12/science/12obwhale/OBOX-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/12/science/12obwhale/OBOX-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'To Survive Ice Ages, Gray Whales Adapted', 'kicker': 'Observatory', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Survive Ice Ages, Gray Whales Adapted', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Whales and Whaling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-11T17:26:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sindya N. Bhanoo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sindya', 'middlename': 'N.', 'lastname': 'Bhanoo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a77d38aa-c17a-5579-bf44-51f8aba3a0b5', 'word_count': 279, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a77d38aa-c17a-5579-bf44-51f8aba3a0b5'}, {'abstract': 'A spot filmed on the High Line in Manhattan focuses on Fidelity Investments’ green line brand symbol.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/11/business/media/q-and-a-with-stuart-elliott.html', 'snippet': 'A spot filmed on the High Line in Manhattan focuses on Fidelity Investments’ green line brand symbol.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q: (Reader)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/05/27/business/media/stuart-elliott-headshot/stuart-elliott-headshot-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 234, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/05/27/business/media/stuart-elliott-headshot/stuart-elliott-headshot-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 234, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/05/27/business/media/stuart-elliott-headshot/stuart-elliott-headshot-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/05/27/business/media/stuart-elliott-headshot/stuart-elliott-head