t': 'Attaching a tennis ball to the back of one’s pajamas may thwart back sleeping, but it does not appear to significantly reduce snoring.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE FACTS', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Really? The Claim: A Tennis Ball on the Back of Pajamas Can Cut Snoring', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sleep', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snoring', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-11T17:51:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': "By Anahad O'Connor", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anahad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Connor", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce0929d4-dead-5512-81a7-79b3ab1172a8', 'word_count': 305, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce0929d4-dead-5512-81a7-79b3ab1172a8'}, {'abstract': 'The play is scheduled to open in September at the Lucille Lortel Theater.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/11/jonathan-groff-and-rutina-wesley-named-to-cast-for-the-submission/', 'snippet': 'The play is scheduled to open in September at the Lucille Lortel Theater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The actors Jonathan Groff and Rutina Wesley have played characters in emotionally charged tight spots before, he in Broadway’s “Spring Awakening” (and in diva showdowns on Fox’s “Glee”) and she on HBO’s “True Blood” as Sookie’s troubled friend Tara. This fall the two will find themselves together in a pickle of their own making in the new Off Broadway play “The Submission,” which MCC Theater is producing at the Lucille Lortel Theater.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jonathan Groff and Rutina Wesley Named to Cast of ‘The Submission’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Groff and Wesley In u2018Submissionu2019 Cast', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beale, Simon Russell', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bobbie, Walter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Groff, Jonathan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rogers, Will (1982- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Talbott, Jeff', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thomas, Eddie Kaye', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lortel, Lucille, Theater', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MCC Theater', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Public Theater', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Showtime', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-11T17:55:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f631d81-cdbe-5c8d-91bc-002c490d195a', 'word_count': 270, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f631d81-cdbe-5c8d-91bc-002c490d195a'}, {'abstract': 'Here are two companies that believe the effort they expend on Facebook and YouTube is paying off.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/11/small-businesses-that-understand-social-media/', 'snippet': 'Here are two companies that believe the effort they expend on Facebook and YouTube is paying off.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few weeks ago, I wrote a post questioning whether all small businesses should invest time and money in social media. The post was a reminder that business owners need to consider the costs and potential returns of social media before taking the leap.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Small Businesses That Understand Social Media', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook.com', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rolex SA', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'YouTube.com', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-11T18:00:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By MP Mueller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mp', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mueller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/130e91e1-23bf-50bc-9669-b8fd41202cbc', 'word_count': 896, 'uri': 'nyt://article/130e91e1-23bf-50bc-9669-b8fd41202cbc'}, {'abstract': 'Giorgio Armani’s love for blue translates into a “rare and unique” perfume.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/11/vain-glorious-blue-crush/', 'snippet': 'Giorgio Armani’s love for blue translates into a “rare and unique” perfume.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yves Klein. Stéphane Mallarmé. Joni Mitchell. The color blue has served as inspiration for artists, poets and musicians, so why not Giorgio Armani? The designer showed an entirely blue collection this past spring, and this week he takes it to the perfume counter with the release of La Femme Bleue. “I wanted to create a fragrance that absolutely evoked the idea of the color blue,” Armani said. “I was inspired by my collection, which was itself inspired by the desert of the Tuareg nomads. I wished to create a rare and unique perfume that would stimulate certain olfactory senses and refer back to my fashion collection.” If notes like black iris and dark chocolate don’t say “rare and unique,” the fact that only 1,000 numbered bottles of La Femme Bleue were produced should do the trick. Not to mention the $600 price tag. At Giorgio Armani boutiques and Bergdorf Goodman.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vain Glorious | Blue Crush', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-11T18:00:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holly Siegel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holly', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Siegel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b017d69a-362a-5006-80ba-91535bd8cece', 'word_count': 150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b017d69a-362a-5006-80ba-91535bd8cece'}, {'abstract': 'As research budgets tighten, a new crop of Web-savvy scientists is hoping the wisdom and generosity of crowds will come to the rescue.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/science/12crowd.html', 'snippet': 'As research budgets tighten, a new crop of Web-savvy scientists is hoping the wisdom and generosity of crowds will come to the rescue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In January, a time when many scientists concentrate on grant proposals, Jennifer D. Calkins and Jennifer M. Gee, both biologists, were busy designing quail T-shirts and trading cards. The T-shirts went for $12 each and the trading cards for $15 in a fund-raising effort resembling an online bake sale. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/12/science/12crow/12crow-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/12/science/12crow/12crow-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/12/science/12crow/CROW-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/12/science/12crow/12crow-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/12/science/12crow/12crow-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Scientists Turn to Crowds on the Web to Finance Their Projects', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Scientists Turn to Crowds on the Web to Finance Their Projects', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Evergreen State College', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kickstarter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-