Safety', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Youth', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drownings', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-11T18:19:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane E. Brody', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Brody', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b26c541c-930d-52e4-a476-ed1e0245abf1', 'word_count': 650, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b26c541c-930d-52e4-a476-ed1e0245abf1'}, {'abstract': 'Unseen pollutants can cause ailments of the ears, eyes, skin, nervous system, gastrointestinal and respiratory tracts, and any cut or scratch you may have.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/health/12brody.html', 'snippet': 'Unseen pollutants can cause ailments of the ears, eyes, skin, nervous system, gastrointestinal and respiratory tracts, and any cut or scratch you may have.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I learned to swim at age 3 at Brighton Beach, where each morning, June to October, my father swam freestyle back and forth between the rock jetties. Summering near water was a family essential as I was growing up, a pleasure I carried into adulthood. For more than 30 summers, I swam daily from Minnesota to Wisconsin and back against the current of the scenic St. Croix River. In my 40s, I joined the local YMCA so I could swim year-round.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/12/science/12brod/BROD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 625, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name'