ff-87b6-c7f13ae8a61f'}, {'abstract': 'ABC News scored a ratings coup on Sunday, with Diane Sawyer’s interview of kidnapping victim Jaycee Dugard.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/11/nearly-15-million-tune-in-for-jaycee-dugard-interview/', 'snippet': 'ABC News scored a ratings coup on Sunday, with Diane Sawyer’s interview of kidnapping victim Jaycee Dugard.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ABC News scored a ratings coup Sunday night thanks to Diane Sawyer’s interview of the kidnapping victim Jaycee Lee Dugard. The two-hour special on ABC attracted almost 15 million viewers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nearly 15 Million Tune in for Jaycee Dugard Interview', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dugard, Jaycee Lee', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sawyer, Diane', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC News', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-11T19:26:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/762409a5-fbb5-5b8a-8e4b-d3c5af28812f', 'word_count': 131, 'uri': 'nyt://article/762409a5-fbb5-5b8a-8e4b-d3c5af28812f'}, {'abstract': 'The new Richard Chai for Acura glove was inspired by “Thor,” the film about Marvel’s Norse hero.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/11/glove-department-superhero-style/', 'snippet': 'The new Richard Chai for Acura glove was inspired by “Thor,” the film about Marvel’s Norse hero.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the old days, superhero tie-ins were simple affairs — a sticker at the end of a loaf of Wonder Bread, say, or a toy in a Happy Meal. These days, as superheroes have become huge box-office draws, the tie-ins are more high-end. Take, for example, the Richard Chai x Acura glove. It was inspired by “Thor,” the film about Marvel’s Norse hero, and S.H.I.E.L.D., the intelligence and security organization that has been lurking around Marvel’s other superhero films and whose agents drive Acuras. Ah, corporate synergy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Glove Department | Superhero Style', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-11T19:32:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Gustines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gustines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/38863a44-6c5a-5d5c-b83a-a231e69362bf', 'word_count': 216, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38863a44-6c5a-5d5c-b83a-a231e69362bf'}, {'abstract': 'Seven steps to take when disputing a denied health insurance claim, from a man who fights insurance companies for a living.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/11/7-steps-in-appealing-a-health-insurance-denial/', 'snippet': 'Seven steps to take when disputing a denied health insurance claim, from a man who fights insurance companies for a living.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s unsettling to receive a letter from your insurance company telling you that your request for medical care, or for payment of care you’ve already received, has been denied. But there are some steps you can take to help boost the odds of filing a successful appeal.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '7 Steps in Appealing a Health Insurance Denial', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insurance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-11T19:41:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1920a9a0-4982-5a57-9709-fd2a5ac30ebf', 'word_count': 775, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1920a9a0-4982-5a57-9709-fd2a5ac30ebf'}, {'abstract': 'A cheap deworming pill used in Africa for 25 years against river blindness was recently shown to kill mosquitoes when they bite people who have recently swallowed the drug.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/health/12mosquito.html', 'snippet': 'A cheap deworming pill used in Africa for 25 years against river blindness was recently shown to kill mosquitoes when they bite people who have recently swallowed the drug.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scientists have proposed an intriguing new way to fight malaria: turning people into human time bombs for mosquitoes.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/12/science/12mosq/12mosq-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 629, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/12/science/12mosq/12mosq-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/12/science/12mosq/12mosq-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Human Swallows Pill. Mosquito Bites Human. Mosquito Dies.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Human Swallows Pill. Mosquito Bites Human. Mosquito Dies.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Worms', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Malaria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mosquitoes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-11T19:58:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Donald G. McNeil Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Donald', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'McNeil', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2aebd7f-6090-5b36-a769-a3bace12df28', 'word_count': 514, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2aebd7f-6090-5b36-a769-a3bace12df28'}, {'abstract': 'The overall evidence on whether players do better when they are playing for a contract is mixed.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/11/keeping-score-good-luck-and-better-timing-increase-reyess-leverage/', 'snippet': 'The overall evidence on whether players do better when they are playing for a contract is mixed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before Jose Reyes was placed on the disabled list with a hamstring injury this month, he was having by far the best season of his career — and the best season of any player in the National League as well.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'head