ic health officials announced last week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/health/research/12childbirth.html', 'snippet': 'Women who have just given birth should wait at least three weeks before they start using birth control pills because of the risk of deep-vein thrombosis, public health officials announced last week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Women who have just given birth should wait at least three weeks before they start using birth control pills because of the risk of serious, potentially fatal blood clots, public health officials announced last week. Women who deliver by Caesarean section or have other risk factors for blood clots — like obesity or a history of previous blood clots — should wait at least six weeks before using these medications, they said.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Childbirth: Wait to Restart the Pill, C.D.C. Says', 'kicker': 'Vital Signs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Childbirth: Wait to Restart the Pill, C.D.C. Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Estrogen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-11T20:47:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Research', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roni Caryn Rabin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roni', 'middlename': 'Caryn', 'lastname': 'Rabin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c157e65-3f86-5850-9ce5-0b4502a0dc2c', 'word_count': 212, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c157e65-3f86-5850-9ce5-0b4502a0dc2c'}, {'abstract': 'An engineer projects that the pipeline would experience 91 spills prod