eater', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/f273fdda-660f-55f7-af81-4fcec447497f', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/f273fdda-660f-55f7-af81-4fcec447497f'}, {'abstract': 'Is the 3,000-hit plateau as special today as it once was?', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/11/is-3250-the-new-3000/', 'snippet': 'Is the 3,000-hit plateau as special today as it once was?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Derek Jeter did not need to reach 3,000 hits to be considered among the game’s greats, and perhaps the milestone — like 500 home runs — should no longer carry that implication. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is 3,250 the New 3,000?', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jeter, Derek', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-11T21:44:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By JORGE CASTILLO', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jorge', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'CASTILLO', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/be340baa-125b-583f-9c47-ebd5d7d3a544', 'word_count': 264, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be340baa-125b-583f-9c47-ebd5d7d3a544'}, {'abstract': 'Publishers Clearing House, which is offering “$5,000 every week for life” in its current sweepstakes, will take over the AOL home page on Tuesday with an ad that mimics the company’s Prize Patrol van pulling up to a home.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/11/prize-patrol-heads-over-to-aol/', 'snippet': 'Publishers Clearing House, which is offering “$5,000 every week for life” in its current sweepstakes, will take over the AOL home page on Tuesday with an ad that mimics the company’s Prize Patrol van pulling up to a home.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For years, Publishers Clearing House has supported the television campaigns for its sweepstakes with a robust advertising presence online. For its current sweepstakes, offering “$5,000 every week for life,” the online component is being stepped up with a promotion on Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Prize Patrol Heads Over to AOL', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Online Advertising', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AOL', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Publishers Clearing House', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-11T21:47:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/480aa6ad-c8fe-5fd9-924e-eff61abf6783', 'word_count': 485, 'uri': 'nyt://article/480aa6ad-c8fe-5fd9-924e-eff61abf6783'}, {'abstract': 'A group of hackers intensified its assault on government-related targets, claiming to have infiltrated the network of Booz Allen Hamilton, a top technology contractor.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/11/hackers-say-they-hit-another-military-contractor/', 'snippet': 'A group of hackers intensified its assault on government-related targets, claiming to have infiltrated the network of Booz Allen Hamilton, a top technology contractor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A group of hackers intensified its assault on government-related targets Monday, claiming to have infiltrated the computer network of Booz Allen Hamilton, a top technology contractor to the United States military and many federal government agencies, and boldly threatening more attacks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hackers Say They Hit Another Military Contractor', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hackers (Computers)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Booz Allen Hamilton', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-11T21:47:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Riva Richmond', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Riva', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Richmond', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f75d2004-7d61-5d17-989a-7dd76136d4c9', 'word_count': 361, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f75d2004-7d61-5d17-989a-7dd76136d4c9'}, {'abstract': 'City Opera’s terms call for an end to guaranteed numbers of workweeks and members. The proposal also eliminates vacation pay, tenure, leaves and the current health insurance plans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/arts/music/city-opera-unions-denounce-contract-offer.html', 'snippet': 'City Opera’s terms call for an end to guaranteed numbers of workweeks and members. The proposal also eliminates vacation pay, tenure, leaves and the current health insurance plans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A day before New York City Opera was to announce its first post-Lincoln Center season, the company’s unions charged on Monday that the company had made proposals for a new contract that would gut the chorus and the orchestra, and turn the “people’s opera” into a freelance outfit.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/12/arts/opera/opera-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 528, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/12/arts/opera/opera-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/12/arts/opera/opera-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Unions Say City Opera Offer Would Gut Chorus and Orchestra', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Unions Say City Opera Offer Would Gut Chorus and Orchestra', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN GUILD OF MUSICAL ARTISTS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Steel, George', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Opera', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Koch, David H, Theater', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-11T21:50:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/158ab125-232a-5cf5-a112-2db5b6270116', 'word_count': 719, 'uri': 'nyt://article/158ab125-232a-5cf5-a112-2db5b6270116'}, {'abstract': 'The New Juilliard Ensemble, directed by Joel Sachs, performed in the Summergarden series at the Museum of Modern Art.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/arts/music/new-juilliard-ensemble-in-summergarden-review.html', 'snippet': 'The New Juilliard Ensemble, directed by Joel Sachs, performed in the Summergarden series at the Museum of Modern Art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Museum of Modern Art opened its free Summergarden series in the Abby Aldrich Rockefeller Sculpture Garden on Sunday evening, and the atmosphere was very much what it was when the series left off last year. Joel Sachs and the superb young musicians of the New Juilliard Ensemble were on the stage, fresh new works were on the music stands, the birds were making a ruckus in the sculpture garden’s trees (at least during the first half) and the garden was packed with listeners sipping drinks and taking in the performance. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/12/arts/ENSEMBLE/ENSEMBLE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 820, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Surprises in a Setting That Could Wither', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Surprises in a Setting That Could Wither', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Juilliard Ensemble', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sachs, Joel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-11T21:52:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'origi