iliar faces: Fellow parents at the school, who want to ensure she is made to pay the money back.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Providence Hogan, the former PTA treasurer charged with embezzling tens of thousands of dollars from the PTA coffers, appeared in Brooklyn Supreme Court on Monday, she was joined by some familiar faces: More than a dozen parents from the school, Public School 29 in Cobble Hill, sat in the courtroom, in a show of solidarity with prosecutors. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ex-PTA Treasurer Ordered to Pay Back About $82,000', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Youth', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embezzlement', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parent-Teacher Associations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Plea Bargaining', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Flamhaft, Stephen', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hogan, Providence', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Parent Teacher Assn', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Public School 29', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cobble Hill (NYC)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-11T23:08:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Robbins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robbins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf608753-4a8d-5444-80ee-2cc9cdb764f8', 'word_count': 624, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf608753-4a8d-5444-80ee-2cc9cdb764f8'}, {'abstract': 'We don’t want inflows!', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/11/obama-and-the-capital-flow-fallacy/', 'snippet': 'We don’t want inflows!', 'lead_paragraph': 'Obama’s press conference wasn’t as bad as it could have been; he actually more or less said that stimulus should be sustained, except it isn’t politically possible. But he also invoked the confidence fairy – and introduced another fallacy, showing that he and his advisers still don’t get the essence of macroeconomics in a liquidity trap:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama and the Capital Flow Fallacy', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-11T23:12:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97540fa5-e57e-5736-a40c-d13982c63e32', 'word_count': 253, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97540fa5-e57e-5736-a40c-d13982c63e32'}, {'abstract': 'Tom Perkins, the renowned American venture capitalist, is a prime candidate to lead the charge for a badly needed overhaul of governance at the News Corporation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/business/media/perkins-is-best-hope-for-news-corp.html', 'snippet': 'Tom Perkins, the renowned American venture capitalist, is a prime candidate to lead the charge for a badly needed overhaul of governance at the News Corporation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The best hope for shareholders of the News Corporation may be Tom Perkins, the renowned American venture capitalist. He is the closest thing to a truly independent director on the roster of Rupert Murdoch cronies. Mr. Perkins also has some relevant experience: he quit the board of Hewlett-Packard five years ago over a phone-hacking scandal. That makes him a prime candidate to lead the charge for a badly needed overhaul of governance at the News Corporation.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Perkins Is Best Hope for News Corp.', 'kicker': 'Reuters Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Best Hope For News Corp.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wiretapping and Other Eavesdropping Devices and Methods', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Morgan Stanley', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-11T23:14:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By JEFFREY GOLDFARB and ANTONY CURRIE', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeffrey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'GOLDFARB', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Antony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'CURRIE', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ccdc74b-b710-5f8d-8a1a-f489a1928f68', 'word_count': 749, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ccdc74b-b710-5f8d-8a1a-f489a1928f68'}, {'abstract': 'Nothing more to be said.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/11/hes-just-not-that-into-you/', 'snippet': '