.html', 'snippet': 'The Central Intelligence Agency ran a phony program in Pakistan to obtain DNA from the Bin Laden family.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — In the months before Osama bin Laden was killed, the Central Intelligence Agency ran a phony vaccination program in Abbottabad, Pakistan, as a ruse to obtain DNA evidence from members of Bin Laden’s family thought to be holed up in an expansive compound there, according to an American official.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vaccination Ruse Used in Pursuit of Bin Laden', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Vaccination Ruse Used In Pursuit of Bin Laden', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Intelligence Services', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Intelligence Agency', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DNA (Deoxyribonucleic Acid)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Abbottabad (Pakistan)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T01:40:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Mazzetti', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mazzetti', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/86ee6ab5-0b7e-54e8-9eab-51637dbcbba8', 'word_count': 597, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86ee6ab5-0b7e-54e8-9eab-51637dbcbba8'