ill, the practice played a key role in United States’ quarterfinal victory over Brazil.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/sports/soccer/at-the-womens-world-cup-drama-without-all-the-dramatics.html', 'snippet': 'Research has determined that women were much less likely than men to fake injuries on the soccer field. Still, the practice played a key role in United States’ quarterfinal victory over Brazil.', 'lead_paragraph': 'COLOGNE, Germany — There often seems to be more diving in soccer than in the Summer Olympics. Phantom contact, or the slightest collision, can lead to theatrical belly flops and exaggerated somersaults by players deceptively trying to draw fouls on their opponents, kill time or catch a breather when tired. A player writhes on the ground, seemingly unable to continue, and is whisked away on a stretcher, only to return moments later, miraculously healed.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/12/sports/12dive_337/12dive_337-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/12/sports/12dive_337/12dive_337-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Routine Ruse in Men’s Soccer Tumbles Into Women’s World Cup', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Routine Ruse in Men’s Soccer Tumbles Into Women’s World Cup', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's World Cup (Soccer)", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Officiating (Sports)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cheating', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 