/12/opinion/12tue2.html', 'snippet': 'No matter what Hezbollah says, the men accused of Rafik Hariri’s murder must be arrested.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An international tribunal has called on Lebanon’s government to arrest four suspects indicted in the 2005 car-bomb killing of former Prime Minister Rafik Hariri and 21 others. All four of the accused are members of Hezbollah, the militant Shiite movement whose cynical mix of politics and armed intimidation helped bring Prime Minister Najib Mikati to power.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Long Pursuit of Justice in Lebanon', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Long Pursuit of Justice in Lebanon: No matter what Hezbollah says, the men accused of Rafik Hariri’s murder must be arrested', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mikati, Najib', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lebanon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hezbollah', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hariri, Rafik', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assassinations and Attempted Assassinations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T01:48:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ddb78aff-79b8-57df-b7e1-b75ea734474e', 'word_count': 354, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ddb78aff-79b8-57df-b7e1-b75ea734474e'}, {'abstract': 'Sometimes, the stories that immigrants offer to support pleas to remain in the United States are more fiction than fact.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/nyregion/immigrants-may-be-fed-false-stories-to-bolster-asylum-pleas.html', 'snippet': 'Sometimes, the stories that immigrants offer to support pleas to remain in the United States are more fiction than fact.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The man caught on the wiretap urged his immigrant client to fabricate a tragic past if he wanted asylum in the United States. To say that he was a victim of political repression in Albania. Or police brutality. Or even a blood feud.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/12/nyregion/jp-asylum2/jp-asylum2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/12/nyregion/jp-asylum2/jp-asylum2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/12/nyregion/jp-asylum2/jp-asylum2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/12/nyregion/jp-asylum2/jp-asylum2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/12/nyregion/jp-asylum2/jp-asylum2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Immigrants May Be Fed False Stories to Bolster Asylum Pleas', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Asylum Ploys Play Off News To Open Door', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Asylum, Right of', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T01:49:27+0000', 'documen