, 'word_count': 276, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0dcc85bf-ed2e-5468-8333-0d1c2c6d1f06'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Denoff won four Emmys, including two for “The Dick Van Dyke Show.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/arts/television/sam-denoff-tv-writer-is-dead-at-83.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Denoff won four Emmys, including two for “The Dick Van Dyke Show.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sam Denoff, an Emmy-winning writer for “The Dick Van Dyke Show” who helped bring to the screen some of its most memorable episodes, including “That’s My Boy???,” “Bupkis” and “Coast-to-Coast Big Mouth,” died on Friday at his home in Los Angeles. He was 83.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/12/arts/DENOFF-obit/DENOFF-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 899, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/12/arts/DENOFF-obit/DENOFF-obit-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/12/arts/DENOFF-obit/DENOFF-obit-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sam Denoff, TV Writer, Is Dead at 83', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sam Denoff, TV Writer, Is Dead at 83', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T01:57:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margalit Fox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margalit', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fox', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b3ab9e5-5ee2-5223-ad53-24a26360e843', 'word_count': 592, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b3ab9e5-5ee2-5223-ad53-24a26360e843'}, {'abstract': 'Bill Thompson’s return puzzle has some missing words.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/11/cupule/', 'snippet': 'Bill Thompson’s return puzzle has some missing words.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TUESDAY’S PUZZLE — The last time we saw Bill Thompson, he wowed us with a debut pangrammatic puzzle (Across Lite, Solution, blog) and he’s back today with a missing word theme that you might guess before you get to the payoff at 68 Across, but if you don’t, worry not. All will become clearer in the light of DAY.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tuesday: Nut With a Cupule', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T02:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8069764-b530-5e17-8cf7-d76373cb9710', 'word_count': 348, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8069764-b530-5e17-8cf7-d76373cb9710'}, {'abstract': '“Silence! The Musical” is an exuberantly gross spoof of “The Silence of the Lambs.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/theater/reviews/silence-the-musical-at-theater-80-review.html', 'snippet': '“Silence! The Musical” is an exuberantly gross spoof of “The Silence of the Lambs.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The prospect of being serenaded by Hannibal Lecter is certainly more appealing than sitting down to dinner with him, at least to the noncannibals among us. Now, thanks to the composer-lyricists Jon and Al Kaplan, we can bask in the song stylings of one of the movies’ most famous mass murderers, in “Silence! The Musical,” an exuberantly gross spoof at Theater 80 in the East Village.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/12/arts/SILENCE/SILENCE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 792, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Knives, and Forks, Are Out', 'kicker': "Theater Review | 'Silence! The Musical'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Knives, and Forks, Are Out', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gattelli, Christopher', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barrett, Brent', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bell, Hunter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T02:02:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Isherwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isherwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b78f6354-0b4c-59fb-a422-daf69b1313df', 'word_count': 1025, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b78f6354-0b4c-59fb-a422-daf69b1313df'}, {'abstract': 'Any banker, Democratic Keynesian or staunch Republican who thinks he’s found the tool to master today’s economy might instead consider a range of competing options.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/opinion/12brooks.html', 'snippet': 'Any banker, Democratic Keynesian or staunch Republican who thinks he’s found the tool to master today’s economy might instead consider a range of competing options.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The world economy is a complex, unknowable organism. Most of us try to diversify our investments and balance risk and security to protect against the unexpected.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-thumbLarge-v2.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', '