ial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fairer Treatment for Katrina’s Victims', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'HURRICANE KATRINA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Louisiana', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Housing and Urban Development Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minorities', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Area Planning and Renewal', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T02:37:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8491193-0633-5541-9767-8c733dfe2c7e', 'word_count': 326, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8491193-0633-5541-9767-8c733dfe2c7e'}, {'abstract': 'A corner of southwest Georgia is scorched by heat and drought.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/07/11/us/DROUGHT.html', 'snippet': 'A corner of southwest Georgia is scorched by heat and drought.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A corner of southwest Georgia is scorched by heat and drought.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/11/us/DROUGHT-slide-TIM4/DROUGHT-slide-TIM4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/11/us/DROUGHT-slide-TIM4/DROUGHT-slide-TIM4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/11/us/DROUGHT-slide-TIM4/DROUGHT-slide-TIM4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Waiting for Rain', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drought', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AGRICULTURE', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T02:38:40+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/7877182b-5ce1-5259-8ac7-d5dcf47fd8c9', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/7877182b-5ce1-5259-8ac7-d5dcf47fd8c9'}, {'abstract': 'Deputies from the main opposition party agreed to be sworn in,following an agreement with the ruling party to try and bring imprisoned politicians who had been elected back to Parliament.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/world/europe/12briefs-DEALBREAKSDE_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'Deputies from the main opposition party agreed to be sworn in,following an agreement with the ruling party to try and bring imprisoned politicians who had been elected back to Parliament.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Turkey’s main opposition party ended a two-week parliamentary deadlock on Monday, when the deputies agreed to be sworn in after reaching a deal with the ruling party to show common effort in bringing imprisoned politicians who had been elected back to Parliament. The 134 delegates from the Republican People’s Party, or CHP, were joined by 36 pro-Kurdish politicians in boycotting the parliamentary opening on June 28, in protest of local court rulings that barred nine elected candidates, currently in jail on terrorism-related charges, from joining the assembly. The Parliament still convened but establishment of legal commissions for executive activities was delayed in absence of opposition deputies, who lacked parliamentary approval without the oath. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Turkey: Deal Breaks Deadlock', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | EUROPE', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Turkey: Deal Breaks Deadlock', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T02:50:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sebnem Arsu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sebnem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Arsu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/5edb9b62-23c4-5e18-968c-d361faf8d2c5', 'word_count': 114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5edb9b62-23c4-5e18-968c-d361faf8d2c5'}, {'abstract': 'The Obama administration unveiled standards for insurance exchanges that will give individuals, families and small businesses “purchasing power” in their health care coverage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/us/politics/12health.html', 'snippet': 'The Obama administration unveiled standards for insurance exchanges that will give individuals, families and small businesses “purchasing power” in their health care coverage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — In a big step to carry out the new health care law, the Obama administration unveiled standards on Monday for insurance marketplaces that will allow individuals, families and small businesses in every state to shop for insurance, compare prices and benefits and buy coverage.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Administration Rolls Out Standards for Health Insurance Marketplaces', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama Administration Rolls Out Standards for Health Insurance Marketplaces', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T03:02:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Pear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pear', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/28860a73-eb03-5d35-9c2f-46191162baa2', 'word_count': 733, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28860a73-eb03-5d35-9c2f-46191162baa2'}, {'abstract': 'Was your favorite U.S. Soccer moment produced by Landon Donovan, or Abby Wambach, or someone else?', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/11/seeking-your-favorite-u-s-soccer-moment/', 'snippet': 'Was your favorite U.S. Soccer moment produced by Landon Donovan, or Abby Wambach, or someone else?', 'lead_paragraph': 'George Vecsey writes for Tuesday’s Times that, for him, Abby Wambach’s injury-time goal against Brazil on Sunday immediately brought to mind Landon Donovan’s injury-time winner against Algeria at last summer’s World Cup. Maybe it did the same for you.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Seeking Your Favorite U.S. Soccer Moment', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headli