ening of monetary and fiscal policy in the belief that the Great Depression had run its course provides a cautionary tale, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bruce Bartlett held senior policy roles in the Reagan and George H.W. Bush administrations and served on the staffs of Representatives Jack Kemp and Ron Paul.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Are We About to Repeat the Mistakes of 1937?', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Great Depression (1930's)", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morgenthau, Henry IV', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roosevelt, Franklin Delano', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T10:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Bartlett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bartlett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/50277a0e-e43a-53b3-828e-7d8b92c28556', 'word_count': 842, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50277a0e-e43a-53b3-828e-7d8b92c28556'}, {'abstract': 'The outsize influence of Rome on 16th-century art is spotlighted at the “Rome: Nature and the Ideal: Landscapes 1600-1650” exhibition, running through Sept. 25 at the Prado in Madrid.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/at-prado-in-madrid-romes-artistic-influence/', 'snippet': 'The outsize influence of Rome on 16th-century art is spotlighted at the “Rome: Nature and the Ideal: Landscapes 1600-1650” exhibition, running through Sept. 25 at the Prado in Madrid.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Western landscape painting only began to flourish in the 16th century, as artists from all over Europe made their way to Rome; the city became a sort of research laboratory for the exchange of ideas between artists of different nationalities. Foreign painters encountered works by Caravaggio and Raphael, themselves inspired by archaeological sites and the naturalistic and poetic paintings of Giorgione and Titian. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Prado in Madrid, Rome’s Artistic Influence', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Prado Museum', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Madrid (Spain)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rome (Italy)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T10:00:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Valerie Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Valerie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0f7d3ad-041a-502c-806d-eb5c43aa75db', 'word_count': 203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0f7d3ad-041a-502c-806d-eb5c43aa75db'}, {'abstract': 'Two recent graduates from the Royal College of Art see their Box car filling car-sharing fleets in Europe and abroad.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/packed-in-a-box-another-transportation-idea-for-cities/', 'snippet': 'Two recent graduates from the Royal College of Art see their Box car filling car-sharing fleets in Europe and abroad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — As car-sharing services continue to evolve, so should the vehicles used in those programs, say James Brooks and Richard Bone, recent graduates of the Vehicle Design program at the Royal College of Art. The former classmates recently opened their own firm, Brooks & Bone, and designed a vehicle specifically for urban car-sharing services that resembles the prototypical box on wheels. And that, precisely, is the point.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Packed in a Box, Another Transportation Idea for Cities', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Car-Pooling and Ride-Sharing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Urban Areas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal College of Art (London)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T10:00:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Witkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Witkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f08af0c9-efc3-5b56-82cd-aa6deb91116c', 'word_count': 532, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f08af0c9-efc3-5b56-82cd-aa6deb91116c'}, {'abstract': 'A look by position at baseball’s top fantasy league performers in the first half.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/fantasy-focus-first-half-all-stars/', 'snippet': 'A look by position at baseball’s top fantasy league performers in the first half.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here are the players at each position who have earned the most profit relative to their draft-day costs. All a