cking Scandal', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wiretapping and Other Eavesdropping Devices and Methods', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NEWS CORP', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News of the World', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T12:06:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/317a8ce6-4b3e-54eb-9894-d5ed098c02d4', 'word_count': 5397, 'uri': 'nyt://article/317a8ce6-4b3e-54eb-9894-d5ed098c02d4'}, {'abstract': 'Two years after hydraulic fracturing fluids were legally spread on a section of the Fernow Experimental Forest in West Virginia, more than half of the trees in the affected area were dead.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/fracking-water-killed-trees-study-finds/', 'snippet': 'Two years after hydraulic fracturing fluids were legally spread on a section of the Fernow Experimental Forest in West Virginia, more than half of the trees in the affected area were dead.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A study that argues for more research into the safe disposal of chemical-laced wastewater resulting from natural gas drilling found that a patch of national forest in West Virginia suffered quick and serious loss of vegetation after it was sprayed with hydraulic fracturing fluids.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fracking Water Killed Trees, Study Finds', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forests and Forestry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hydraulic Fracturing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Natural Gas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Journal of Environmental Quality', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Monongahela River', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Virginia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T12:23:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mireya Navarro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mireya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Navarro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/672d62cc-9c04-5881-bc78-54cbe3e7e3f7', 'word_count': 376, 'uri': 'nyt://article/672d62cc-9c04-5881-bc78-54cbe3e7e3f7'}, {'abstract': 'It’s possible for voters to rebuke Mr. Obama and trust his opposition even less. And in fact, polling shows that is exactly what is going on.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/why-obama-will-win-on-debt-ceiling-fight/', 'snippet': 'It’s possible for voters to rebuke Mr. Obama and trust his opposition even less. And in fact, polling shows that is exactly what is going on.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last year, President Obama and House Republicans managed to reach a last-minute accord on preserving the Bush tax cuts, and then in April they just barely averted a government shutdown. But now, in this debate over the debt ceiling, each side seems ready to make a stand at last and find out whom the voters really trust when it comes to righting the nation’s finances. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Debt Ceiling Fight, Obama Has the Edge', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T12:26:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Bai', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bai', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00adac8e-8928-5c52-a8a5-9d05620bec10', 'word_count': 821, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00adac8e-8928-5c52-a8a5-9d05620bec10'}, {'abstract': 'No, but I believe in antibiotics.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/do-you-believe-in-magic/', 'snippet': 'No, but I believe in antibiotics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OK, David Brooks has what amounts to a reply. I don’t want to get into a tit for tat. But I do want to take on the claim that believing that simple actions can bring big improvements in the economy amounts to belief in magic.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Do You Believe in Magic?', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T12:28:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1bf7eb86-c7e0-5576-8eac-a15c4ad19f11', 'word_count': 324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1bf7eb86-c7e0-5576-8eac-a15c4ad19f11'}, {'abstract': 'The founders of Opening Ceremony have been chosen to be the creative directors of Kenzo.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/kenzo-picks-new-york-retailers-to-lead/', 'snippet': 'The founders of Opening Ceremony have been chosen to be the creative directors of Kenzo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LVMH Moet Hennessy Louis Vuitton announced Tuesday that Humberto Leon and Carol Lim, founders of Opening Ceremony, will be creative directors of Kenzo. Their first collection for the Paris-based brand will be shown this fall.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kenzo Picks New York Retailers to Lead', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leon, Humberto', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lim, Carol', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'LVMH Moet Hennessy Louis Vuitton SA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T12:46:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d25baca-9505-505d-b1d1-a6482872a705', 'word_count': 219, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d25baca-9505-505d-b1d1-a6482872a705'}, {'abstract': 'The government sets standards for new health insurance exchanges, motorists are enraged by camera-issued tickets, repeal vote set for light bulb efficiency and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/tuesday-reading-rules-set-for-new-health-insurance-exchanges/', 'snippet': 'The government sets standards for new health insurance exchanges, motorists are enraged by camera-issued tickets, repeal vote set for light bulb efficiency and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and online in our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tuesday Reading: Rules Set for New Health Insurance Exchanges', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T12:51:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff6fcea7-61c7-5b36-a174-9d57b3258b41', 'word_count': 133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff6fcea7-61c7-5b36-a174-9d57b3258b41'}, {'abstract': 'The tiny, affluent sandbar on the northern tip of Cape Cod remains a low-key, largely gay resort town for the summer — except during theme weeks, when the population swells to more than 100,000, many of them bopping to a heavy disco beat.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/out-and-about-provincetown-on-parade/', 'snippet': 'The tiny, affluent sandbar on the northern tip of Cape Cod remains a low-key, largely gay resort town for the summer — except during theme weeks, when the population swells to more than 100,000, many of them bopping to a heavy disco beat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Summer sojourners to Provincetown, Mass., typically have an object in sight: a breezy beach, a lobster roll, a parade of thousands. The tiny, affluent sandbar on the northern tip of Cape Cod remains a low-key, largely gay resort town for the summer — except during theme weeks, when the population swells to more than 100,000, many of them bopping to a heavy disco beat. Every tribe has its week in P-town: there’s Bear Week (happening now), Family Pride Week (July 30-Aug. 6) and by late August it’s time for Carnival (Aug. 14-19). That means rollicking street parties, colorful floats and an infinite supply of garish costumes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Out and About | Provincetown on Parade', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T13:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rocky Casale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rocky', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Casale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a67804fc-d27a-5553-9d57-c5be3f50fea9', 'word_count': 334, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a67804fc-d27a-5553-9d57-c5be3f50fea9'}, {'abstract': 'Understanding the anti-deficit lobby.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/insincerely-yours-2/', 'snippet': 'Understanding the anti-deficit lobby.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jonathan Chait is puzzled by the behavior of the anti-deficit lobby, which persists in blaming Democrats for the failure of Republicans to act responsibly:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Insincerely Yours', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T13:08:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/782fc91e-5d44-5b4e-b1d4-bf32629d5d6b', 'word_count': 362, 'uri': 'nyt://article/782fc91e-5d44-5b4e-b1d4-bf32629d5d6b'}, {'abstract': 'The Commerce Department said the deficit increased 15.1 percent to $50.2 billion, the largest imbalance since October 2008, mostly on oil imports.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/business/economy/us-trade-deficit-jumped-in-may.html', 'snippet': 'The Commerce Department said the deficit increased 15.1 percent to $50.2 billion, the largest imbalance since October 2008, mostly on oil imports.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A rise in imports of petroleum products helped widen the United States trade deficit in May to more than $50 billion, marking its largest gap since late 2008, according to government statistics released on Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Trade Deficit Jumped in May', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Trade Deficit Jumped in May', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T13:10:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b45b249e-00cb-5897-a3a5-a064067b989c', 'word_count': 509, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b45b249e-00cb-5897-a3a5-a064067b989c'}, {'abstract': 'The Murdoch story keeps getting worse.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/thugs-of-the-world/', 'snippet': 'The Murdoch story keeps getting worse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I obviously never had a very good opinion of Rupert Murdoch’s role in US and UK affairs. But I never expected to see the kinds of things now coming to light as the phone-hacking scandal metastasizes — hacking Gordon Brown and the Queen, bribing the police, hiring investigators to dig up dirt on the people investigating the hacking, and on and on.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thugs of the World', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T13:24:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/264d3132-71fe-5876-ad7c-d8432e4b419a', 'word_count': 84, 'uri': 'nyt://article/264d3132-71fe-5876-ad7c-d8432e4b419a'}, {'abstract': 'General Motors and the United Automobile Workers are cooperating to build the Sonic subcompact at a smaller plant using new methods while paying lower wages to most workers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/business/with-chevrolet-sonic-gm-and-uaw-reinvent-automaking.html', 'snippet': 'General Motors and the United Automobile Workers are cooperating to build the Sonic subcompact at a smaller plant using new methods while paying lower wages to most workers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ORION TOWNSHIP, Mich. — The only subcompact car being built on American soil will soon roll out of an assembly plant here in suburban Detroit that is as unusual as the car itself.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/13/business/13sonic-span/13sonic-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/13/business/13sonic-span/13sonic-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/13/business/13sonic-span/13sonic-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/13/business/13sonic-span/13sonic-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/13/business/13sonic-span/13sonic-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'With Sonic, G.M. Stands Automaking on Its Head', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Make Tiny American Car, G.M. Also Shrinks Plant and Wages', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Automobile Workers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chevrolet Division of General Motors Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Cars (Compact, Subcompact and