they employ less workers, American factories have been resilient in some regards, a study by the Minneapolis Fed shows.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/the-factory-age-isnt-over/', 'snippet': 'Even if they employ less workers, American factories have been resilient in some regards, a study by the Minneapolis Fed shows.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The number of factories in the United States employing more than 1,000 workers fell by one-third from 1997 to 2007, leaving 1,014 such factories. This probably will not surprise you. The shattered windows of empty factories have become a familiar sight.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Factory Age Isn’t Over', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve Bank of Minneapolis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T19:01:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Binyamin Appelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Binyamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Appelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d567e4d0-17f9-5919-8964-66c69b64f3a0', 'word_count': 249, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d567e4d0-17f9-5919-8964-66c69b64f3a0'}, {'abstract': 'As Moody’s cut Ireland’s credit rating to junk status, European Union ministers voiced support for weak banks but left unresolved deep disputes that have held up a second rescue package for Greece.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/business/global/eu-leaders-to-hold-emergency-meeting-over-greece.h