d Nada Zakula, a spokeswoman for the company. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Show Is Stopped but Then Goes On After Injury to Royal Shakespeare Company’s Romeo', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Romeo and Juliet (Play)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lincoln Center Festival', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Park Avenue Armory (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal Shakespeare Co', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T20:12:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a51f238c-221b-598b-9082-dbd2987dcaa0', 'word_count': 136, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a51f238c-221b-598b-9082-dbd2987dcaa0'}, {'abstract': 'Saying that a bipartisan budget deal was probably out of reach, the Republican leader offered a plan to allow the president to increase the federal debt limit without Congressional approval for offsetting spending cuts.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/mcconnell-proposal-gives-obama-power-to-increase-debt-limit/', 'snippet': 'Saying that a bipartisan budget deal was probably out of reach, the Republican leader offered a plan to allow the president to increase the federal debt limit without Congressional approval for offsetting spending cuts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Senate Republican leader, Mitch McConnell of Kentucky, said Tuesday that a bipartisan budget deal with President Obama was probably out of reach, and he proposed a plan under which the president could increase the federal debt limit without Congressional approval for offsetting spending cuts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'McConnell Proposal Gives Obama Power to Increase Debt Limit', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McConnell, Mitch', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T20:13:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jackie Calmes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jackie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Calmes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/574cd51f-e4ba-5e07-978e-cbcad67584b4', 'word_count': 712, 'uri': 'nyt://article/574cd51f-e4ba-5e07-978e-cbcad67584b4'}, {'abstract': 'Photographs from Russia, West Bank, Kenya and Afghanistan.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/pictures-of-the-day-russia-and-elsewhere-2/', 'snippet': 'Photographs from Russia, West Bank, Kenya and Afghanistan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photographs from Russia, West Bank, Kenya and Afghanistan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pictures of the Day: Russia and Elsewhere', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kenya', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T20:20:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed06ba6b-7bcf-54c7-ad6d-084e2114cf47', 'word_count': 8, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed06ba6b-7bcf-54c7-ad6d-084e2114cf47'}, {'abstract': 'A developer in Long Island City provides a lot for vendors to gather.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/new-yorks-first-private-food-truck-court-comes-to-queens/', 'snippet': 'A developer in Long Island City provides a lot for vendors to gather.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The city’s moveable food-truck feast is about to become more stationary, with the establishment in Long Island City, Queens, of what may be its first food truck court on private land. It’s expected to open in two weeks at 43-29 Crescent Street, not far from Jackson Avenue.Rockrose Development Corporation, the lot’s owner, has come to an agreement with the New York City Food Truck Association, which has recruited a group of trucks interested in participating, said David Weber, president of the trade group. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York’s First Private Food Truck Court Comes to Queens', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T20:26:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Glenn Collins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Glenn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/32c1abbf-e95a-5b4c-9e50-ed7b06bb2d69', 'word_count': 499, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32c1abbf-e95a-5b4c-9e50-ed7b06bb2d69'}, {'abstract': 'A thrilling victory over Brazil may help the 2011 United States women’s team come out of the shadow of the pioneering 1999 team.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/u-s-women-working-on-legacy-apart-from-99-team/', 'snippet': 'A thrilling victory over Brazil may help the 2011 United States women’s team come out of the shadow of the pioneering 1999 team.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MÖNCHENGLADBACH, Germany — Sunday’s wild victory over Brazil allowed the United States to begin coming out of the considerable shadow of the 1999 team that won the Women’s World Cup with pioneering players like Mia Hamm, Brandi Chastain, Julie Foudy, Kristine Lilly and Briana Scurry.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Women Working on Legacy Apart From 1999 Team', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's World Cup (Soccer)", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lloyd, Carli', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Solo, Hope', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T20:29:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeré Longman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeré', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Longman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/425d87af-ad0a-532f-93b7-db102006ea51', 'word_count': 294, 'uri': 'nyt://article/425d87af-ad0a-532f-93b7-db102006ea51'}, {'abstract': 'A $16 million musical production of “Rebecca,” based on the classic 1938 novel by Daphne du Maurier, has been scaled down.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/rebecca-to-sing-manderley-to-burn-on-broadway/', 'snippet': 'A $16 million musical production of “Rebecca,” based on the classic 1938 novel by Daphne du Maurier, has been scaled down.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A $16 million musical production of “Rebecca,” based on the classic 1938 novel by Daphne du Maurier, has been scaled down to a budget of about $12 million — largely thanks to the loss of a collapsing staircase special effect — and is now on track for Broadway, the producers announced on Tuesday. Preview performances at a Shubert theater still to be named are scheduled to begin March 27, 2012, with an opening night set for April 22.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Rebecca’ to Sing, Manderley to Burn on Broadway', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T20:30:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c580f5a-c176-5fdc-a5dc-305c6d019a41', 'word_count': 552, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c580f5a-c176-5fdc-a5dc-305c6d019a41'}, {'abstract': 'In June 2010, faculty, staff and administrators at Dartmouth had their desk trash cans replaced with six-inch-tall cartons. A year later, the college has sent 200 less tons of trash to the landfill, and recycling is up by one third.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/with-tiny-cans-a-new-trash-equation/', 'snippet': 'In June 2010, faculty, staff and administrators at Dartmouth had their desk trash cans replaced with six-inch-tall cartons. A year later, the college has sent 200 less tons of trash to the landfill, and recycling is up by one third.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Reaching for a petite dessert dish instead of the mixing bowl may help you curb your ice cream consumption. Grabbing a basket rather than a shopping cart helps control how many “necessities” you pick up at the store.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Tiny Cans, a New Trash Equation', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Containers and Packaging', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recycling of Waste Materials', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping Bags', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Waste Materials and Disposal', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T20:38:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanna M. Foster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b930514f-b349-528d-92a5-1c2f24dadd91', 'word_count': 345, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b930514f-b349-528d-92a5-1c2f24dadd91'}, {'abstract': 'It will have a somewhat different menu than the original in Brooklyn.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/fatty-cue-is-coming-to-the-village/', 'snippet': 'It will have a somewhat different menu than the original in Brooklyn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To replace their former restaurant Cabrito, Zakary Pelaccio and Rick Camac plan a Manhattan version of Fatty ‘Cue, their Asian-style barbecue place in Williamsburg, Brooklyn. They don’t have the details yet, but they say it will have a somewhat different menu and design and no smokehouse, which the one in Brooklyn has. They hope to open around Labor Day. Follow @ZakaryPelaccio on Twitter for updates. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fatty  ‘Cue Is Coming to the Village', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T20:40:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2fdd1660-e18b-583e-aeb9-5c33ab843cff', 'word_count': 76, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2fdd1660-e18b-583e-aeb9-5c33ab843cff'}, {'abstract': 'Zachary Golper and Kate Wheatcroft have opened a bakery called Bien Cuit, in Boerum Hill, Brooklyn.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/baking-bread-and-more-in-brooklyn/', 'snippet': 'Zachary Golper and Kate Wheatcroft have opened a bakery called Bien Cuit, in Boerum Hill, Brooklyn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Zachary Golper, who baked bread and pastries for Le Bec-Fin in Philadelphia, and Kate Wheatcroft, his wife, have had New York in their sights for some time. The result is the bakery Bien Cuit, in Boerum Hill, Brooklyn.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Baking Bread (and More) in Brooklyn', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bakeries and Baked Products', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T20:43:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7511599a-7e5a-57d8-b6e2-a07b6c49b09c', 'word_count': 218, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7511599a-7e5a-57d8-b6e2-a07b6c49b09c'}, {'abstract': '“Mrs Parry is a woman battered by events that were outside her control.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/books/excerpt-chavs-by-owen-jones.html', 'snippet': '“Mrs Parry is a woman battered by events that were outside her control.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chapter 7: Broken Britain', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Chavs’', 'kicker': 'Excerpt', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T20:44:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Owen Jones', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Owen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jones', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'First Chapter', '_id': 'nyt://article/bead55d3-7d87-5a2b-b00d-ec0945546437', 'word_count': 12985, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bead55d3-7d87-5a2b-b00d-ec0945546437'}, {'abstract': 'Writing with wit and outrage, Owen Jones offers a portrait and a defense of the British working class.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/books/chavs-the-demonization-of-the-working-class-review.html', 'snippet': 'Writing with wit and outrage, Owen Jones offers a portrait and a defense of the British working class.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Owen Jones’s first book, “Chavs: The Demonization of the Working Class,” begins more like a Noël Coward play or a late-model Ian McEwan novel than like a rumbling social polemic. That is, it opens with a misfired witticism uttered at an elite East London dinner party. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/13/arts/book/book-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 791, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/13/arts/book/book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/13/arts/book/book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Get Your Bling and Adidas Tracksuit, Wayne, a British Class War Is Raging', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Get Your Bling and Adidas Tracksuit, Wayne, a British Class War Is Raging', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T20:45:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dwight Garner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dwight', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f405f46a-a581-5ef5-b39b-111ed5ca1f13', 'word_count': 1058, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f405f46a-a581-5ef5-b39b-111ed5ca1f13'}, {'abstract': "Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg addresses the negotiations W