or in Outer Space', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tumbles and Twitches in an Alien World Undersea or in Outer Space', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pilobolus Dance Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Joyce Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T20:59:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claudia La Rocco', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claudia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'La Rocco', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9572088-5196-52b0-ba38-0cff1bb0a700', 'word_count': 461, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9572088-5196-52b0-ba38-0cff1bb0a700'}, {'abstract': 'For all the virtues that today’s social networks offer us, the inability to categorize friends online has become increasingly frustrating. Google+ hopes to offer a solution to this problem.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/organizing-my-online-friends/', 'snippet': 'For all the virtues that today’s social networks offer us, the inability to categorize friends online has become increasingly frustrating. Google+ hopes to offer a solution to this problem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I don’t consider my neighbor my “friend.” My boss isn’t necessarily my “friend” either (although I do like my boss!). I also wouldn’t categorize a person I met 20 years ago in high school as my “friend.” Yet on social Web sites like Facebook these people are all lumped into one giant social bucket called “friends.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Organizing My Online Friends', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'na