o get a meal at a men-only homeless shelter in Boston nearly 40 years ago — so much so that she went ahead and founded the nation’s first homeless shelter for women. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/13/sports/13tiernan/13tiernan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 829, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/13/sports/13tiernan/13tiernan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/13/sports/13tiernan/13tiernan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Kip Tiernan, Founder of First Shelter for Homeless Women, Dies at 85', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Kip Tiernan, 85; Founded Shelter for Women', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homeless Persons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T21:15:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dennis Hevesi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dennis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hevesi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/40d28bd9-774f-5529-8846-b218ce26c438', 'word_count': 717, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40d28bd9-774f-5529-8846-b218ce26c438'}, {'abstract': "Hamid Karzai's half brother is killed; calls grow for News Corporation to drop the BSkyB bid; and the phone-hacking scandal puts David Cameron in an awkward position.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/multimedia/100000000942217/timescast--july-12-2011.html', 'snippet': "Hamid Karzai's half brother is killed; calls grow for News Corporation to drop the BSkyB bid; and the phone-hacking scandal puts David Cameron in an awkward position.", 'lead_paragraph': "Hamid Karzai's half brother is killed; calls grow for News Corporation to drop the BSkyB bid; and the phone-hacking scandal puts David Cameron in an awkward position.", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/12/multimedia/video-tc-110712/video-tc-110712-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/12/multimedia/video-tc-110712/video-tc-110712-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/12/multimedia/video-tc-110712/video-tc-110712-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/12/multimedia/video-tc-110712/video-tc-110712-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'TimesCast | July 12, 2011', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News of the World', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T21:15:25+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'ContinuousNews', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'Zena Barakat|Ben Solomon|Emily B. Hager|Channon Hodge', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zena', 'middlename': 'Barakat', 'lastname': 'Ben', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/48a05b5e-cb88-56bc-b69c-6e2484ace54b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/48a05b5e-cb88-56bc-b69c-6e2484ace54b'}, {'abstract': 'Guest blogger Lisa Shannon writes about Sister Somalia, a new organization devoted to helping victims of gender-based violence in Somalia.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/in-mogadishu-a-lifeline-for-somali-rape-victims/', 'snippet': 'Guest blogger Lisa Shannon writes about Sister Somalia, a new organization devoted to helping victims of gender-based violence in Somalia.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Why did you come here when no one else does?” The African Union communications director asked us over dinner at its compound in Mogadishu. Good question. We were warned against it, especially by war-zone regulars. It’s been called the most dangerous city—or place—on earth. In fact, we had to delay our trip for two weeks due to multiple suicide bombings and riots inside the area controlled by Mogadishu’s transitional government (TFG). So, why go? I gave the short answer, “We’re supporting a local social entrepreneur in launching a sexual violence hotline.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Mogadishu: A Lifeline For Somali Rape Victims', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mogadishu (Somalia)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Somalia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T21:16:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Shannon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shannon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8dc56383-1859-5b1c-bfcc-5dc1d4907054', 'word_count': 1288, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8dc56383-1859-5b1c-bfcc-5dc1d4907054'}, {'abstract': 'The Texas city’s signature drink: a large margarita served in a martini glass, with olives, called the Mexican Martini.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/dining/austins-very-own-martini.html', 'snippet': 'The Texas city’s signature drink: a large margarita served in a martini glass, with olives, called the Mexican Martini.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AUSTIN, Tex.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/13/dining/13SUBMartini_span/13SUBMartini_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/13/dining/13SUBMartini_span/13SUBMartini_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/13/dining/13SUBMartini_span/SUB-Martini-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/13/dining/13SUBMartini_span/13SUBMartini_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/13/dining/13SUBMartini_span/13SUBMartini_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Austin’s Very Own Martini', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Austin’s Very Own Martini', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cocktails', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Austin (Tex)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bars', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T21:17:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By JORDAN MACKAY', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jordan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MACKAY', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5bc63d8f-8040-55ee-82a0-04c672b4eb99', 'word_count': 977, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5bc63d8f-8040-55ee-82a0-04c672b4eb99'}, {'abstract': 'Additional letters to the public editor on his three most recent columns.', 'web_url': 'https://publiceditor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/additional-letters-searching-for-perspective/', 'snippet': 'Additional letters to the public editor on his three most recent columns.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Following up on the reader letters that appeared in my print column for this week, here are some additional letters via e-mail to my last three columns, Surrounded by Opinion, the Times Raises Its Voices, On NYTimes.com, Now You See It, Now You Don’t and Where Words Can Never Do Justice.Thank you, stateless soul, for your informative discussion of feedback on the new Sunday Review in the Times July 3. I cannot convey how much I dislike the new format. I, like the feedback you mentioned, sorely miss the political cartoons and the late-night television gag lines. The weekly news is dire enough without taking away our opportunity to laugh while we are informed. The political cartoons were always the first thing I turned to on a Sunday morning. Wouldn’t Art Buchwald turn over in his grave to see you eliminate his life’s work?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Additional Letters: Searching for Perspective', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T21:18:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Arthur S. Brisbane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Arthur', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Brisbane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/803cefce-f2a8-5945-acb1-4c61e906688d', 'word_count': 2324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/803cefce-f2a8-5945-acb1-4c61e906688d'}, {'abstract': 'Rupert Goold’s “Romeo and Juliet,” the second production in the Royal Shakespeare Company’s repertory season at the Park Avenue Armory, utterly fails to stir the heart.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/theater/reviews/royal-shakespeare-companys-romeo-and-juliet-review.html', 'snippet': 'Rupert Goold’s “Romeo and Juliet,” the second production in the Royal Shakespeare Company’s repertory season at the Park Avenue Armory, utterly fails to stir the heart.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fire breathes from just about every scene in Rupert Goold’s hot-tempered, hard-charging staging of “Romeo and Juliet,” the second production in the Royal Shakespeare Company’s repertory season at the Park Avenue Armory. The warring Capulets and Montagues show occasional signs of pathological pyromania, and the buildings of Verona appear to be wallpapered in mesmerizing images of flames.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/13/arts/romeo/romeo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 355, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/13/arts/romeo/romeo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 355}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/13/arts/romeo/romeo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 728, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/13/arts/romeo/romeo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/13/arts/romeo/romeo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Love’s Flames Amid a City in Flames', 'kicker': "Theater Review | 'Romeo and Juliet' ", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Love’s Flames Amid a City In Flames', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shakespeare, William', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Park Avenue Armory (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goold, Rupert', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lincoln Center Festival', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal Shakespeare Co', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T21:22:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Isherwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isherwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9df4ac02-b708-5042-9132-af5bae1e62e7', 'word_count': 1366, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9df4ac02-b708-5042-9132-af5bae1e62e7'}, {'abstract': 'New York Live Arts, the new artistic initiative, is offering something new for artists and audiences this fall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/arts/new-york-live-arts-announces-fall-season.html', 'snippet': 'New York Live Arts, the new artistic initiative, is offering something new for artists and audiences this fall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York Live Arts, the new artistic initiative created this year by the Bill T. Jones/Arnie Zane Dance Company and Dance Theater Workshop, is offering something new for artists and audiences this fall. For theatergoers, the group plans to present works from more than 40 artists, including a Replay Series that looks back at artists’ most significant and popular works. The performers include Big Dance Theater, John Jasperse, John Kelly, Yvonne Meier, Richard Move and Reggie Wilson. For artists, New York Live Arts has begun a two-year residency that offers a rarity in the art world: salary, health benefits and a commission for a work. The first artist to benefit is Yasuko Yokoshi, a Hiroshima-born choreographer who came to the United States in 1981.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Live Arts Announces Fall Season', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New York Live Arts Announces Fall Season', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T21:23:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e3396ed-bc8e-5368-b79d-3adda108c27a', 'word_count': 126, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e3396ed-bc8e-5368-b79d-3adda108c27a'}, {'abstract': 'We live in “a society of people who subsist on mutual aid and redistributive policies who’ve been conned (and conned themselves) into thinking that they are rugged individualists and that everyone\xa0else is a parasite.”', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/everyone-elses-problem/', 'snippet': 'We live in “a society of people who subsist on mutual aid and redistributive policies who’ve been conned (and conned themselves) into thinking that they are rugged individualists and that everyone\xa0else is a parasite.”', 'lead_paragraph': '“Half of U.S. social program recipients believe they ‘have not used a government social program,’ ” according to a paper by Suzanne Mettler, a professor at Cornell, posted on Boing Boing. And, yes, that includes everyone who has ever taken a mortgage deduction, taken out a student loan or collected Social Security upon retirement. If you’re wondering why it’s so difficult to come to an agreement on the debt ceiling and taxes, it may be because, as Cory Doctorow writes, we live in “a society of people who subsist on mutual aid and redistributive policies who’ve been conned (and conned themselves) into thinking that they are rugged individualists and that everyone\xa0else is a parasite.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Everyone Else’s Problem', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T21:23:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sheila Glaser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sheila', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glaser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7bcfff08-22e6-53eb-b11f-b4b4e44b3ff6', 'word_count': 114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7bcfff08-22e6-53eb-b11f-b4b4e44b3ff6'}, {'abstract': 'The final season of “Rescue Me,” the FX series about firefighters, makes for a passionate tribute to the suffering and heroism of 9/11.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/arts/television/rescue-me-denis-learys-911-tribute-on-fx.html', 'snippet': 'The final season of “Rescue Me,” the FX series about firefighters, makes for a passionate tribute to the suffering and heroism of 9/11.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 10th anniversary of 9/11 is near, summoning not only horrible memories of that cataclysm but also the anxiety of measuring up. Ten years on, there still aren’t enough words, gestures, ceremonies or moments of silence to match the wound. Not paying attention is unthinkable, but it’s even harder to think of an adequate tribute.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/13/arts/rescue/rescue-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/13/arts/rescue/rescue-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/13/arts/rescue/rescue-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 425, 'width': 510, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/13/arts/rescue/rescue-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/13/arts/rescue/rescue-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Still Fighting Fire With Fire to Honor the Fallen of 9/11', 'kicker': 'The TV Watch', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Still Fighting Fire With Fire To Honor the Fallen of 9/11', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leary, Denis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'FX', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T21:24:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alessandra Stanley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alessandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stanley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f1035c3-70d5-53dd-acde-a49154b180e7', 'word_count': 945, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f1035c3-70d5-53dd-acde-a49154b180e7'}, {'abstract': 'Diageo, the British maker of Smirnoff vodka, is going after local spirits makers in expanding economies like China to make up for declining sales elsewhere.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/business/global/british-distiller-diageo-shifts-focus-to-growing-markets.html', 'snippet': 'Diageo, the British maker of Smirnoff vodka, is going after local spirits makers in expanding economies like China to make up for declining sales elsewhere.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Baijiu, a popular Chinese spirit known for its harsh and fiery kick, might not be everyone’s preferred drink, but the management at Diageo liked it so much that it pursued a takeover of a baijiu maker in China for two years.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/13/business/DIAGIO/DIAGIO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 335, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/13/business/DIAGIO/DIAGIO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 335}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/13/business/DIAGIO/DIAGIO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'British Distiller Diageo Shifts Its Focus in Acquisitions to Fast-Growing Markets', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'British Distiller Diageo Shifts Its Focus in Acquisitions to Fast-Growing Markets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Diageo PLC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALCOHOLIC BEVERAGES', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sales', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T21:26:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Werdigier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werdigier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c3a17bb-0603-5b1f-b26a-7096389116d5', 'word_count': 1063, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c3a17bb-0603-5b1f-b26a-7096389116d5'}, {'abstract': 'Alexei Ratmansky’s version of “Anna Karenina” is being performed this week by the Mariinsky Ballet at the Metropolitan Opera House as part of the Lincoln Center Festival.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/arts/dance/ratmanskys-anna-karenina-with-mariinsky-ballet-review.html', 'snippet': 'Alexei Ratmansky’s version of “Anna Karenina” is being performed this week by the Mariinsky Ballet at the Metropolitan Opera House as part of the Lincoln Center Festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As bad ballets go, Alexei Ratmansky’s two-act “Anna Karenina” is one of the best. It tells its potted version of Tolstoy’s novel with a fair bit of narrative clarity; it manages many complex changes of scene deftly; its décor and costumes (by Mikael Melbye) are generally elegant; its extensive use of video projections (by Wendall Harrington) is unusual and effective; and most of its leading characters are immediately identifiable and distinct. But these virtues don’t suffice. The ballet is a complete waste of everybody’s time.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/13/arts/MARIINSKY/MARIINSKY-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 756, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/13/arts/MARIINSKY/MARIINSKY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/13/arts/MARIINSKY/MARIINSKY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Illicit Love and All Its Consequences', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Illicit Love and All Its Consequences', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mariinsky Ballet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gergiev, Valery', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ratmansky, Alexei', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lincoln Center Festival', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T21:31:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/463d0997-c59b-56f6-aa19-89e8b7329810', 'word_count': 1042, 'uri': 'nyt://article/463d0997-c59b-56f6-aa19-89e8b7329810'}, {'abstract': 'ABC News, thanks to a preview of its extensive interview with kidnapping victim Jaycee Lee Dugard, managed to edge ahead of NBC’s “Nightly News” in the evening news competition last Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/with-dugard-abc-news-notches-a-rare-win/', 'snippet': 'ABC News, thanks to a preview of its extensive interview with kidnapping victim Jaycee Lee Dugard, managed to edge ahead of NBC’s “Nightly News” in the evening news competition last Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ABC News got one more boost from its exclusive interview with the kidnapping victim Jaycee Lee Dugard: it beat NBC in the evening news competition last Thursday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Dugard, ABC News Notches a Rare Win', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dugard, Jaycee Lee', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC News', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T21:32:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62354f65-58be-5916-8bcb-af7b5b47e4fe', 'word_count': 216, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62354f65-58be-5916-8bcb-af7b5b47e4fe'}, {'abstract': 'Avoid a default, a group of executives and investors said, or risk disarray in the markets and disruption to the economic recovery.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/wall-street-warns-lawmakers-on-debt/', 'snippet': 'Avoid a default, a group of executives and investors said, or risk disarray in the markets and disruption to the economic recovery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The White House and Congress received dual warnings from Wall Street on Tuesday about the consequences of failing to raise the federal debt ceiling in a timely manner.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wall Street Warns Lawmakers on Debt', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Business Roundtable', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities Industry and Financial Markets Assn', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T21:35:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Southall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Southall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/83985a37-9b94-5c28-9f89-a000a746d3b9', 'word_count': 348, 'uri': 'nyt://article/83985a37-9b94-5c28-9f89-a000a746d3b9'}, {'abstract': 'VMware announced product moves that suggest its is to become the Microsoft of cloud computing.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/vmware-shows-its-cloud-strategy/', 'snippet': 'VMware announced product moves that suggest its is to become the Microsoft of cloud computing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VMware made a handful of product announcements on Tuesday that add up to the company’s bid to become the Microsoft of cloud computing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'VMware Shows Its Cloud Strategy', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cloud Computing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Productivity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Software', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maritz, Paul', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'VMware Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T21:37:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Lohr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lohr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/63966226-f0d6-5751-9b42-eb815ec7f2a2', 'word_count': 358, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63966226-f0d6-5751-9b42-eb815ec7f2a2'}, {'abstract': 'The mayor urged national leaders to first focus on the debt ceiling, accusing them of playing “chicken” with the American economy.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/bloomberg-urges-washington-to-raise-debt-limit/', 'snippet': 'The mayor urged national leaders to first focus on the debt ceiling, accusing them of playing “chicken” with the American economy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg, warning of potentially “catastrophic” effects to the financial system, urged Republicans and Democrats on Tuesday to stop bickering over taxes and spending cuts and move swiftly toward an agreement to raise the country’s debt limit. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bloomberg Urges Washington to Raise Debt Limit', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-12T21:38:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Javier C. Hernández', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Javier', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Hernández', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b352bd9c-73f9-51d3-9da4-0953e9e1e959', 'word_count': 245, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b352bd9c-73f9-51d3-9da4-0953e9e1e959'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Blossom played a great many curmudgeons but may be best recalled for his turn as the surprisingly sweet Old Man Marley in “Home Alone.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/arts/roberts-blossom-quirky-character-actor-dies-at-87.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Blossom played a great many curmudgeons but may be best recalled for his turn as the surprisingly sweet Old Man Marley in “Home Alone.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Roberts Blossom, a durable character actor who was known for playing cantankerous old coots, both comic and sinister, but who may be best remembered as the kindly next-door neighbor in the comedy “Home Alone,” died on Friday in Santa Monica, Calif. He was 87.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25',