er have their place in social change, but real revolutions take place in the street.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/12/friends-in-revolution/', 'snippet': 'Facebook and Twitter have their place in social change, but real revolutions take place in the street.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Friday, I wrote about Friendfactor, an organizing tool used in the successful battle for gay marriage in New York State.\xa0 Friendfactor combines social media and real-world friendship to motivate people to get active.\xa0 Instead of getting an e-mail from a group asking you to support a political goal, you get one from a close friend or family member asking you to “help me get my full rights.”\xa0\xa0\xa0 Friendfactor is particularly interesting because it seems to offer a solution to one of the biggest obstacles in using social media for political change:\xa0 people need close personal connections in order to get them to take action — especially if that action is risky and difficult.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Friends in Revolution', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'April 6 Youth Movement', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook.com', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Otpor', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tahrir Square (Cairo)', 'ran