986a391', 'word_count': 622, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04f162dd-1485-571e-a187-21f3f986a391'}, {'abstract': 'Mercado del Barrio is a 311,000-square-foot retail and housing complex that points to greater interest by commercial developers in the Latino market.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/realestate/commercial/in-san-diegos-barrio-logan-mercado-del-barrio-nears-completion.html', 'snippet': 'Mercado del Barrio is a 311,000-square-foot retail and housing complex that points to greater interest by commercial developers in the Latino market.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN DIEGO — A 20-year effort by city officials to bring a supermarket and other essential services to Barrio Logan, a working-class neighborhood south of downtown, has entered its final phase with the construction of a $58 million retail and housing development aimed at Hispanic shoppers. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/13/business/BARRIO/BARRIO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A San Diego Barrio’s $58 Million Moment Arrives', 'kicker': 'Square Feet', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A San Diego Barrio’s $58 Million Moment Arrives', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Diego (Calif)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Area Planning and Renewal', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T01:42:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'subsection_name': 'Commercial Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Morris Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Morris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7da1b35a-a64b-523b-9367-c879a0b0199e', 'word_count': 849, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7da1b35a-a64b-523b-9367-c879a0b0199e'}, {'abstract': 'Arts businesses in the Manhattan neighborhood are surviving residential development because they had the foresight to purchase their gallery and studio spaces.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/realestate/commercial/manhattan-artists-preserve-chelsea-by-buying-not-renting.html', 'snippet': 'Arts businesses in the Manhattan neighborhood are surviving residential development because they had the foresight to purchase their gallery and studio spaces.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is an all-too-familiar pattern in many communities: artists discover an inexpensive, underdeveloped neighborhood and move in, only to be ousted from the area by soaring retail rents once it catches on in popularity.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/13/business/Galleries1/Galleries1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 699, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/13/business/Galleries1/Galleries1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/13/business/Galleries1/Galleries1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Art Groups Preserve Chelsea by Buying, Not Renting', 'kicker': 'Square Feet', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Art Groups Preserve Chelsea by Buying, Not Renting', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chelsea (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Office Buildings and Commercial Properties', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'High Line (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T01:43:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'subsection_name': 'Commercial Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alison Gregor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gregor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe95ab5a-2d6d-54d5-bc77-1277a7176599', 'word_count': 1318, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe95ab5a-2d6d-54d5-bc77-1277a7176599'}, {'abstract': 'This is not your parents’ job market. Workers need to be able to invent, adapt and reinvent their jobs every day.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/opinion/13friedman.html', 'snippet': 'This is not your parents’ job market. Workers need to be able to invent, adapt and reinvent their jobs every day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The rise in the unemployment rate last month to 9.2 percent has Democrats and Republicans reliably falling back on their respective cure-alls. It is evidence for liberals that we need more stimulus and for conservatives that we need more tax cuts to increase demand. I am sure there is truth in both, but I do not believe they are the whole story. I think something else, something new — something that will require our kids not so much to find their next job as to invent their next job — is also influencing today’s job market more than people realize.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Start-Up of You', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Start-Up Of You', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons',