g. It operates along the lines of a beauty contest or spelling bee, with regional winners advancing to the grand finals, hosted last year by Jay Leno in Palm Springs, Calif.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Time Clock Is Expensive, Not Exclusive', 'kicker': 'About New York', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Inflated Bills? Kickbacks? Just the Start', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bribery and Kickbacks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Allen, Reddy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Allen, Padma', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T01:54:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Dwyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dwyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cdc5fd10-3b02-55d2-a9fb-ef3244fb178b', 'word_count': 769, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cdc5fd10-3b02-55d2-a9fb-ef3244fb178b'}, {'abstract': 'While we have channeled capital into wars and debt, our competitors have worked with infrastructure banks to lay a sound foundation for growth.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/opinion/13likosky.html', 'snippet': 'While we have channeled capital into wars and debt, our competitors have worked with infrastructure banks to lay a sound foundation for growth.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOR decades, we have neglected the foundation of our economy while other countries have invested in state-of-the-art water, energy and transportation infrastructure. Our manufacturing base has migrated abroad; our innovation edge may soon follow. If we don’t find a way to build a sound foundation for growth, the American dream will survive only in our heads and history books.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/13/opinion/13ikosky-oped/13ikosky-oped-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/13/opinion/13ikosky-oped/13ikosky-oped-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/13/opinion/13ikosky-oped/13ikosky-oped-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Banking on the Future', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Banking on the Future', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infrastructure (Public Works)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kerry, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hutchison, Kay Bailey', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T01:55:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael B. Likosky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None,