s Lite, has released Across Lite v2.1 specifically for Mac users who run SnowLeopard (OS X 10.6) or the new Lion (OS X 10.7). On Thursday, July 14, you will be able to download the update here, and there will be a permanent link to this page in the right-hand column under “Solving Software and Apps”, as well as a link on the Premium Puzzle page in the near future.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wednesday: Patron Saint of Sailors', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T02:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/caaabd0c-d5e9-50a0-af04-c2424fed21b2', 'word_count': 343, 'uri': 'nyt://article/caaabd0c-d5e9-50a0-af04-c2424fed21b2'}, {'abstract': 'The White House is seeking to redefine what is owed on goods sold, while lobbyists from companies of all sizes are swarming around Congress to kill the proposal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/us/politics/13tax.html', 'snippet': 'The White House is seeking to redefine what is owed on goods sold, while lobbyists from companies of all sizes are swarming around Congress to kill the proposal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — One of the biggest revenue-raisers proposed by President Obama in negotiations with Congress is what he describes as an arcane change in the tax treatment of business inventories — things like steel, groceries and oil.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/13/us/TAX