cle/94b75651-4bd6-5553-8554-2cdaffe2dad0'}, {'abstract': 'For Arizona, a state hard hit by the recession, a bustling downtown Phoenix before the sold-out All-Star Game was a welcome sight.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/sports/baseball/all-star-game-plenty-of-pregame-action-but-no-immigration-law-protests.html', 'snippet': 'For Arizona, a state hard hit by the recession, a bustling downtown Phoenix before the sold-out All-Star Game was a welcome sight.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHOENIX — The All-Star Game parade was snaking along Jefferson Street on Tuesday afternoon when a rancorous voice rang out from the crowd. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/13/sports/subALLSTAR2/subALLSTAR2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 867, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Plenty of Action Before the Game, but No Immigration Law Protests', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Plenty of Action Before the Game, Not Much of It on Immigration Law', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Arizona Immigration Law (SB 1070)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALL STAR GAMES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigrants', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Phoenix (Ariz)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T02:25:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5383782-00b8-5561-b821-b0374a551af5', 'word_count': 835, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5383782-00b8-5561-b821-b0374a551af5'}, {'abstract': 'The historian, Barry H. Landau and his colleague, Jason Savedoff are accused of stealing documents from the Maryland Historical Society, including some signed by Abraham Lincoln.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/us/13historian.html', 'snippet': 'The historian, Barry H. Landau and his colleague, Jason Savedoff are accused of stealing documents from the Maryland Historical Society, including some signed by Abraham Lincoln.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — A presidential historian and author, Barry H. Landau, was arrested with a colleague on Saturday in Baltimore on charges of stealing historical documents from the Maryland Historical Society, including ones signed by Abraham Lincoln. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Presidential Historian and Colleague Arrested in Theft of Documents in Maryland', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Presidential Historian and Colleague Arrested in Theft of Documents in Maryland', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Landau, Barry H', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lincoln, Abraham', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T02:26:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sabrina Tavernise', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sabrina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tavernise', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b3e7a7d-d83b-558b-b031-b036aac4229f', 'word_count': 412, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b3e7a7d-d83b-558b-b031-b036aac4229f'}, {'abstract': 'Representative Lamar Smith wants to block the president’s ability to use discretion in deportation cases. But he would not suspend the powers for every president, just this one.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/opinion/13wed3.html', 'snippet': 'Representative Lamar Smith wants to block the president’s ability to use discretion in deportation cases. But he would not suspend the powers for every president, just this one.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama’s top immigration enforcer, John Morton, recently instructed his officials to take mitigating factors into account, like an immigrant’s family ties in the United States and education status, when deciding which deportation cases to pursue. It was not a major breakthrough, but it was sensible and humane, which is why it drew the ire of Representative Lamar Smith, who thinks Mr. Obama is too soft on illegal immigrants. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Forgetful Mr. Smith', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Forgetful Mr. Smith', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Lamar S', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deportation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T02:26:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/c08a761c-8850-5ddd-87db-dfc35be337e3', 'word_count': 320, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c08a761c-8850-5ddd-87db-dfc35be337e3'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Roszak popularized the term “counterculture” in referring to a generation that rebelled against war and sought new ways of thinking.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/books/theodore-roszak-60s-scholar-dies-at-77.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Roszak popularized the term “counterculture” in referring to a generation that rebelled against war and sought new ways of thinking.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Theodore Roszak, who three weeks after the Woodstock Festival in 1969 not only published a pivotal book about a young generation’s drug-fueled revolt against authority but also gave it a name — “counterculture” — died on July 5 at his home in Berkeley, Calif. He was 77. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/13/us/ROSZAK-obit/ROSZAK-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 709, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/13/us/ROSZAK-obit/ROSZAK-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/13/us/ROSZAK-obit/ROSZAK-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Theodore Roszak, ’60s Expert, Dies at 77', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Theodore Roszak, ’60s Scholar, Dies at 77', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 