ace the accusations, made by two women in Stockholm last year. Ben Emmerson, one of Mr. Assange’s lawyers, said that his client’s behavior in Sweden might have been “disreputable, discourteous, disturbing,” but that it did not constitute a crime under British law, rendering any Swedish arrest warrant invalid. The hearing will continue Wednesday. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/13/world/BRIEFS/BRIEFS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/13/world/BRIEFS/BRIEFS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Britain: Assange Extradition Fight', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | EUROPE', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Britain: Assange Extradition Fight', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sweden', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assange, Julian P', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Extradition', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T04:32:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ravi Somaiya', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ravi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Somaiya', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff43dfca-693d-5669-8350-99d7837ec97e', 'word_count': 112, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff43dfca-693d-5669-8350-99d7837ec97e'}, {'abstract': 'The Mets sent the closer and a substantial amount