s many Japanese switched off their air-conditioners in response to government appeals to curb electricity use. Twenty-six peopled died of heatstroke from June 1 to July 10, the government said, and almost 13,000 were taken to hospitals for treatment. Japan has shut down 35 of its 54 nuclear reactors since the March earthquake and tsunami, reducing national power capacity by 11 percent. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Japan: Jump in Heatstroke Deaths', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | ASIA', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Japan: Jump in Heatstroke Deaths', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Japan Earthquake and Tsunami (2011)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Energy Efficiency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Heatstroke', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T05:17:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bloomberg News', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bloomberg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'News', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/189d2fb4-c5b4-596a-b893-97d6931c26b3', 'word_count': 69, 'uri': 'nyt://article/189d2fb4-c5b4-596a-b893-97d6931c26b3'}, {'abstract': 'While Japan has a long history in women’s soccer, a lack of resources for the women’s game has meant that it has not enjoyed success like this summer’s until recently.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/japans-women-have-come-farther-than-most/', 'snippet': 'While Japan has a long history in women’s soccer, a lack of resources for the women’s game has meant that it has not enjoyed success like this summer’s until recently.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nadeshiko Japan! A word unknown to the soccer world outside of Japan, Nadeshiko is the name used for the Japanese women’s national team. It means beautiful flower.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Japan’s Women Have Come Farther Than Most', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T05:32:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Byer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Byer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f3e8a121-f8a5-58d3-93c6-b144d3b9d297', 'word_count': 614, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f3e8a121-f8a5-58d3-93c6-b144d3b9d297'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on July 13, 2011.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/pageoneplus/corrections-july-13.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on July 13, 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NATIONAL', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: July 13', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T05:37:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/224255ad-2034-5ab1-a5ba-d0d79a2c7690', 'word_count': 717, 'uri': 'nyt://article/224255ad-2034-5ab1-a5ba-d0d79a2c7690'}, {'