 Downing Street.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/world/europe/14hacking.html', 'snippet': 'The significance many British see in the hacking scandal found expression in the sight of an ordinary family standing at the door of 10 Downing Street.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — On the day when Rupert Murdoch retreated from the biggest media takeover bid in Britain’s history, the wider significance that many here see for the way that power in the country is wielded found its most poignant expression in the sight of an ordinary family standing silently, subdued but assuaged at last, at the door of 10 Downing Street.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/14/world/14hacking/14hacking-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/14/world/14hacking/14hacking-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/14/world/14hacking/14hacking-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 546, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Victim’s Family Appears Amid Rage at Tabloids', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Victim’s Family Appears Amid Rage at Tabloids', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dowler, Milly', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News of the World', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cameron, David', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NEWS CORP', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'British Sky Broadcasting Group Plc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News International Ltd', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, James R', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brooks, Rebekah', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Gordon', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T11:52:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By John F. Burns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Burns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/19ab6795-67e3-5911-90e0-71ee9214b616', 'word_count': 1082, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19ab6795-67e3-5911-90e0-71ee9214b616'}, {'abstract': 'The fact that the parties can’t agree on what happens if they don’t raise the debt ceiling is significant.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/parties-cant-agree-on-the-consequences-of-default/', 'snippet': 'The fact that the parties can’t agree on what happens if they don’t raise the debt ceiling is significant.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The fact that politicians in Washington can’t agree on how to raise the debt ceiling is hardly surprising. The fact that they can’t agree on what happens if they don’t may be more significant.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Parties Can’t Agree on the Consequences of Default', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bachmann, Michele M', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McConnell, Mitch', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pawlenty, Tim', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T12:00:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5488fd4-b6f9-5878-9bd8-f9227aa89fb1', 'word_count': 811, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5488fd4-b6f9-5878-9bd8-f9227aa89fb1'}, {'abstract': 'The city’s once-hip central Mitte neighborhood has officially jumped the shark. The new neighborhood to visit, with the arrival of Andreas Murkudis’s sprawling concept shop, may well be Potsdamer Strasse.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/big-in-berlin/', 'snippet': 'The city’s once-hip central Mitte neighborhood has officially jumped the shark. The new neighborhood to visit, with the arrival of Andreas Murkudis’s sprawling concept shop, may well be Potsdamer Strasse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s not as though anyone in Berlin really needed proof, last week, that the city’s once-hip central Mitte neighborhood had officially jumped the shark — two years’ worth of boutique hotel and Mavi-store openings, plus skyrocketing rents and a mass exodus of the gallery scene, had all been fairly obvious clues. But as the local fashion crowd milled around on Wednesday night outside the opening of Andreas Murkudis’s sprawling concept shop, newly and thrillingly relocated to a remote stretch of Potsdamer Strasse once ruled by drug dealers and prostitutes, there seemed to be only one sentiment on everybody’s lips: Goodbye, and good riddance. Murkudis may have helped pioneer the Mitte retail scene when he began selling Margiela and Yohji from three minimalist storefronts inside a courtyard off Münzstrasse in the early 2000s, but with a few notable exceptions — the recently opened Gestalten bookshop, the Kunstwerke contemporary art museum — it’s no longer the place that in-the-know young people go to hang out and discover things. It’s the place they go when they need something from American Apparel.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Big in Berlin', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T12:00:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Monica Khemsurov', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Monica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Khemsurov', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/38f80d81-5a45-5a7a-b8ed-ec805d77a0b9', 'word_count': 393, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38f80d81-5a45-5a7a-b8ed-ec805d77a0b9'}, {'abstract': 'In a vast match-fixing case, prosecutors in Changwon have indicted 55 soccer players, almost one out of every 10 professional players in the country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/sports/soccer/south-korea-confronts-dirty-secret-of-its-sports.html', 'snippet': 'In a vast match-fixing case, prosecutors in Changwon have indicted 55 soccer players, almost one out of every 10 professional players in the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL — On the day South Koreans rejoiced over the selection of Pyeongchang as the host city of the 2018 Winter Olympics, prosecutors continued to peel back layers of a long-hushed dirty secret of the nation’s sports landscape.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In South Korean Sports, a Culture of Corruption', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In South Korean Sports, A Culture of Corruption', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bribery and Kickbacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cheating', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2018)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gambling', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption in Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Athletics and Sports', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T12:01:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Choe Sang-Hun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Choe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sang-Hun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3dd0aa92-ddec-58c9-a676-03003d51cb75', 'word_count': 544, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3dd0aa92-ddec-58c9-a676-03003d51cb75'}, {'abstract': 'Prime Minister Naoto Kan said Wednesday that Japan should reduce and eventually eliminate its dependence on nuclear energy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/world/asia/14japan.html', 'snippet': 'Prime Minister Naoto Kan said Wednesday that Japan should reduce and eventually eliminate its dependence on nuclear energy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — Prime Minister Naoto Kan said Wednesday that Japan should reduce and eventually eliminate its dependence on nuclear energy in what would be a radical shift in the country’s energy policy, saying that the Fukushima accident had demonstrated the dangers of the technology.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Japan Premier Wants Shift Away From Nuclear Power', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Japan Premier Wants Shift Away From Nuclear Power', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kan, Naoto', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Energy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fukushima Daiichi Nuclear Power Plant (Japan)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T12:02:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hiroko Tabuchi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hiroko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tabuchi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7fd5c192-0153-5c8d-8a53-6ed47bdee1f6', 'word_count': 573, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7fd5c192-0153-5c8d-8a53-6ed47bdee1f6'}, {'abstract': 'But shrill!', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/the-few-the-proud-the-non-hysteric/', 'snippet': 'But shrill!', 'lead_paragraph': 'Martin Wolf:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Few, The Proud, The Non-Hysteric', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T12:33:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6305ee8b-c939-5921-becf-b1905a3260e8', 'word_count': 116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6305ee8b-c939-5921-becf-b1905a3260e8'}, {'abstract': 'The Dodd-Frank financial regulatory overhaul will turn a year old next week. In honor of its birthday, bankers, regulators and journalists are gathering in New York to discuss some of the law’s thorniest provisions.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/live-blog-lobbyists-meeting-on-financial-overhaul/', 'snippet': 'The Dodd-Frank financial regulatory overhaul will turn a year old next week. In honor of its birthday, bankers, regulators and journalists are gathering in New York to discuss some of the law’s thorniest provisions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Dodd-Frank financial regulatory overhaul will turn a year old next week. In honor of its birthday, bankers, regulators and journalists are gathering in New York on Wednesday to discuss some of the law’s thorniest provisions — derivatives, the new consumer protection agency and, of course, its efforts to end “too big to fail.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Live Blog: Lobbyists Meeting on Financial Overhaul', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline