metics/', 'snippet': 'The company’s C.E.O. shares some of her favorite eco-friendly products.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tina Turnbow is a professional makeup artist, who is known for lending her celebrity clients editorial polish. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Face Time | Maureen Kelly, Tarte Cosmetics', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T13:00:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tina Turnbow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Turnbow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d196407-1b1d-5953-95d8-f5c1a3a49912', 'word_count': 739, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d196407-1b1d-5953-95d8-f5c1a3a49912'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Wiig, the star and co-writer of the hit summer comedy “Bridesmaids,” will play the lead in “Imogene,” a dark comedy about a New York playwright.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/not-always-a-bridesmaid-kristen-wiig-plans-a-follow-up-film/', 'snippet': 'Ms. Wiig, the star and co-writer of the hit summer comedy “Bridesmaids,” will play the lead in “Imogene,” a dark comedy about a New York playwright.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When your screenwriting debut is viewed as a a bellwether for the viability of female-oriented comedies and becomes one of the biggest successes of the season, it’s safe to say the film industry won’t let you stay idle for very long. So it goes for Kristen Wiig, the star and co-writer of “Bridesmaids,” the $150 million hit, who could be spending her summer unwinding to the music of Wilson Phillips and chowing down on cheap Brazilian food but is instead moving on to her next project.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Not Always a ‘Bridesmaid,’ Kristen Wiig Plans a Follow-Up Film', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pulcini, Robert', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Springer Berman, Shari', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wiig, Kristen', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T13:05:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e62d264-89e9-51e7-9dc3-07cc8a0884dc', 'word_count': 194, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e62d264-89e9-51e7-9dc3-07cc8a0884dc'}, {'abstract': 'Spending time with Leonardo’s “Last Supper” in Milan can be a peculiar experience, one eliciting nostalgia and guilt.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/arts/design/postcard-from-milan-15-long-minutes-with-last-supper.html', 'snippet': 'Spending time with Leonardo’s “Last Supper” in Milan can be a peculiar experience, one eliciting nostalgia and guilt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MILAN — The setting can seem a lot like quarantine. The entrance, through several holding pens and sets of automatic doors, leads to an enormous, vaulted, semiprivate room, the patient stretched out to the right. A bedside crowd coos appropriately.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/13/arts/postcardcap/postcardcap-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'ran