corporate Moorish elements in their places of worship as a way of distinguishing them from Christian churches.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Damaged Synagogue Is an Architectural Milestone Too', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Synagogues', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Congregation Kehilath Jeshurun (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T15:51:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Dunlap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Dunlap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d52224d-16b1-5589-8dc4-4996c57256d9', 'word_count': 342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d52224d-16b1-5589-8dc4-4996c57256d9'}, {'abstract': 'With the rise in popularity of the Toyota Prius and other greener cars, the complexion of the government motor pool is changing.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/whither-the-government-sedan/', 'snippet': 'With the rise in popularity of the Toyota Prius and other greener cars, the complexion of the government motor pool is changing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With about 600,000 federal cars and trucks under his watch, President Obama wants the government fleet to “lead by example” by adopting hybrid, electric or other advanced powertrain technologies in coming years. On Tuesday, Mayor Bloomberg unveiled an N.Y.P.D. cruiser based on the Chevrolet Volt, part of a 70-unit order of plug-in hybrids and electric vehicles for New York.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Whither the Government Sedan?', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T15:52:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phil Patton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Patton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/708da81f-340b-50dd-912a-c243a3d74e88', 'word_count': 559, 'uri': 'nyt://article/708da81f-340b-50dd-912a-c243a3d74e88'}, {'abstract': 'A graphic novel about video games, growing up Asian-American and the challenges of meeting parental expectations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/books/review/young-adult-level-up-by-gene-luen-yang.html', 'snippet': 'A graphic novel about video games, growing up Asian-American and the challenges of meeting parental expectations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are the cartoonish headline tales of Tiger Moms and their obedient, violin-playing daughters and dutiful, Intel STS-prize-winning sons. And then there are the often more complicated lives of real Asian-American sons and daughters, recently explored by Wesley Yang in his much commented-on article “Paper Tigers” in New York magazine.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/13/books/review/13childrens-inline/13childrens-inline-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 824, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': '