t entry in theJ. K. Rowling series or to see the most recent installment in the multibillion-dollar movie franchise, the final chapter of which opens Friday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Harry Potter Sang Bass, Hermione Sang Tenor', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rowling, J K', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T16:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kim Nowacki', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nowacki', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/85560725-9c52-53d6-99ed-f0cfe36c23c1', 'word_count': 726, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85560725-9c52-53d6-99ed-f0cfe36c23c1'}, {'abstract': 'Ai Weiwei said Wednesday that he had agreed to become a visiting lecturer at Berlin University of the Arts in 2012, but that he did not know whether China’s government would allow it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/world/asia/14artist.html', 'snippet': 'Ai Weiwei said Wednesday that he had agreed to become a visiting lecturer at Berlin University of the Arts in 2012, but that he did not know whether China’s government would allow it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — Ai Weiwei, the Chinese artist and recently imprisoned dissident, said Wednesday that he had agreed to become a visiting lecturer at the Berlin University of the Arts in 2012, but that he did not know whether China’s government would allow him to leave the country to work there.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Freed Chinese Artist Accepts Job in Berlin', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Freed Chinese Artist Accepts Job in Berlin', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ai Weiwei', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Berlin (Germany)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T16:08:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Wines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/362f6910-9e33-5748-b2fd-269f1e108813', 'word_count': 468, 'uri': 'nyt://article/362f6910-9e33-5748-b2fd-269f1e108813'}, {'abstract': 'Derek Jeter’s milestone hit has led to sales of memorabilia and clothing to rival those from a World Series championship.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/sports/baseball/jeters-3000th-hit-produces-run-on-merchandise.html', 'snippet': 'Derek Jeter’s milestone hit has led to sales of memorabilia and clothing to rival those from a World Series championship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since Saturday, $2.5 million to $3 million of products related to Derek Jeter’s 3,000th hit have been sold by Steiner Sports, which has partnerships with Jeter and the Yankees.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/14/sports/14sales1/14sales1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/14/sports/14sa