l-star-game-milwaukees-big-night-leading-off.html', 'snippet': 'After Prince Fielder of the Brewers was named most valuable player of the All-Star Game, the team announced its trade for Francisco Rodriguez.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The All-Star Game happened a long way from Wisconsin, but for a game held in Phoenix, Milwaukee had a pretty good night. Prince Fielder put on a show, turned fans who spent most of the festivities booing him into his personal fan club, and then everyone found out that the Brewers had traded for Mets closer Francisco Rodriguez.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'All Milwaukee', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'All Milwaukee', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Upton, Justin (1987- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rambis, Kurt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, Brian', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goodell, Roger', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McIlroy, Rory', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALDERSON, SANDY', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beltran, Carlos', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bochy, Bruce', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harrison, James (1978- )', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T16:12:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/960b40b1-a807-555e-bc1f-320f376853a9', 'word_count': 708, 'uri': 'nyt://article/960b40b1-a807-555e-bc1f-320f376853a9'}, {'abstract': 'A suicide bomber killed five French troops guarding a meeting between NATO officers and Afghan tribal elders on Wednesday morning northeast of the capital.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/world/asia/14afghanistan.html', 'snippet': 'A suicide bomber killed five French troops guarding a meeting between NATO officers and Afghan tribal elders on Wednesday morning northeast of the capital.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — A suicide bomber killed five French soldiers guarding a meeting between NATO officers and Afghan tribal elders on Wednesday morning northeast of the capital, one of the bloodiest days for French troops in Afghanistan. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Suicide Bomber Kills 5 French Soldiers in Afghanistan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Suicide Bomber Kills 5 French Soldiers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'North Atlantic Treaty Organization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karzai, Hamid', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sarkozy, Nicolas', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T16:14:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93f04758-60ff-5cbf-b22d-f5cfce4f408e', 'word_count': 418, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93f04758-60ff-5cbf-b22d-f5cfce4f408e'}, {'abstract': 'A doctor urges health care providers to think harder about whether a medical procedure will improve an elderly patient’s comfort and function.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/two-words-to-live-by/', 'snippet': 'A doctor urges health care providers to think harder about whether a medical procedure will improve an elderly patient’s comfort and function.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not long ago I suggested that frail, elderly patients write “Do Less” across their foreheads with a Sharpie, but I’m rethinking that. Two other words might serve better: “comfort” and “function.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Words to Live By', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sloan, John', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T16:14:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paula Span', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paula', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Span', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/74fabf7f-3838-5a3f-a95c-c53996378c5b', 'word_count': 883, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74fabf7f-3838-5a3f-a95c-c53996378c5b'}, {'abstract': 'The British actor Julian Ovenden plays Death in the Roundabout Theater Company’s production of the supernatural romance “Death Takes a Holiday.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/17/theater/julian-ovenden-in-roundabouts-death-takes-a-holiday.html', 'snippet': 'The British actor Julian Ovenden plays Death in the Roundabout Theater Company’s production of the supernatural romance “Death Takes a Holiday.”', 'lead_paragraph': '“I\u2002WAS looking for Cary Grant with high notes,” the director Doug Hughes said, describing the job requirements for the role of the not-so-Grim Reaper in his Roundabout Theater Company production of “Death Takes a Holiday.” “A gift for light comedy, a gift for sincerity — gifts that don’t often coexist — and a great singer. It’s a combination of elements you might have in a studio star of the ’30s, ’40s or ’50s.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/arts/OVENDEN--1SUB/OVENDEN--1SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 377, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/17/arts/OVENDEN--1SUB/OVENDEN--1SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 377}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/arts/OVENDEN--1SUB/OVENDEN--1SUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/arts/OVENDEN--1SUB/OVENDEN--1SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/17/arts/OVENDEN--1SUB/OVENDEN--1SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Death Becomes a Soaring Tenor', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Death Becomes a Soaring Tenor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roundabout Theater Co', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T16:25:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Rooney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rooney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99a910e3-a218-5311-9e5a-ea33b5e8d123', 'word_count': 1324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99a910e3-a218-5311-9e5a-ea33b5e8d123'}, {'abstract': 'Beyoncé holds the top spot on the Billboard album chart this week, despite a 63 percent drop in sales from last week.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/beyonce-holds-on-to-no-1-with-4/', 'snippet': 'Beyoncé holds the top spot on the Billboard album chart this week, despite a 63 percent drop in sales from last week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Beyoncé holds the top spot on the Billboard album chart this week, with her “4” (Columbia) selling 115,000 copies in its second week out, according to Nielsen SoundScan. That is a 63 percent drop from last week, but still a healthy lead over Adele’s “21” (XL/Columbia), which remains at No. 2 with 79,000 sales.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Beyoncé Holds On to No. 1 With ‘4’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Knowles, Beyonce', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T16:30:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e864fe8-b55e-54d5-928d-7d00cace4e46', 'word_count': 171, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e864fe8-b55e-54d5-928d-7d00cace4e46'}, {'abstract': 'The model Hilary Rhoda provides a crisp take on summer casual.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/look-of-the-moment-hilary-rhoda/', 'snippet': 'The model Hilary Rhoda provides a crisp take on summer casual.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Look: Tightly edited — a cropped pantsuit paired with minimally embellished sandals is a crisp take on summer casual.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Look of the Moment | Hilary Rhoda', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T16:30:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd97c74f-9b3b-5dab-9eb8-f4359b7702aa', 'word_count': 52, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd97c74f-9b3b-5dab-9eb8-f4359b7702aa'}, {'abstract': 'Kristin Scott Thomas stars in Ian Rickson’s terrific new production of Harold Pinter’s “Betrayal.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/london-theater-journal-surprised-by-betrayal/', 'snippet': 'Kristin Scott Thomas stars in Ian Rickson’s terrific new production of Harold Pinter’s “Betrayal.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — This woman doesn’t know what to do with her face. That’s the impression given by Kristin Scott Thomas in the first scene of Ian Rickson’s terrific new production of Harold Pinter’s “Betrayal,” which I saw Tuesday night at the Comedy Theater. Ms. Scott Thomas’s impeccably chiseled features — a glamorous alabaster mask in films like “The English Patient” — appear almost to be melting here, involuntarily rearranging themselves as she tries to settle on a single, composed expression.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'London Theater Journal: Surprised by ‘Betrayal’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Betrayal (Play)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ibsen, Henrik', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pinter, Harold', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T16:31:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/583ac80d-787c-5b9a-a0be-cc84f212b0aa', 'word_count': 1101, 'uri': 'nyt://article/583ac80d-787c-5b9a-a0be-cc84f212b0aa'}, {'abstract': 'Chrysler’s truck division told N.H.T.S.A. that a broken tie rod could lead to a “loss in directional stability” on the affected pickups.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/nearly-250000-ram-pickups-recalled-for-steering-flaw/', 'snippet': 'Chrysler’s truck division told N.H.T.S.A. that a broken tie rod could lead to a “loss in directional stability” on the affected pickups.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chrysler is recalling almost 243,000 of its Ram pickup trucks because there could be a “loss of directional stability,” the automaker told the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nearly 250,000 Ram Pickups Recalled for Steering Flaw', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chrysler LLC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Highway Traffic Safety Administration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T16:31:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4364c071-e387-525e-877f-6ce0f9e1ea8a', 'word_count': 227, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4364c071-e387-525e-877f-6ce0f9e1ea8a'}, {'abstract': 'Though News Corporation has withdrawn its bid for BSkyB, the phone hacking scandal may prompt the media giant to take further action, like spinning off its troubled British newspaper unit.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/after-bskyb-deals-collapse-whats-next-for-news-corp/', 'snippet': 'Though News Corporation has withdrawn its bid for BSkyB, the phone hacking scandal may prompt the media giant to take further action, like spinning off its troubled British newspaper unit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The News Corporation‘s investors appear to be breathing a sigh of relief now that the media conglomerate has withdrawn its troubled $12 billion bid for British Sky Broadcasting. Shares in the company were up more than 6 percent as of early Wednesday afternoon, to $16.31.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After BSkyB Deal’s Collapse, What’s Next for News Corp.?', 'k