_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1201371-b676-52ba-8e24-64ccffa83303', 'word_count': 2196, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1201371-b676-52ba-8e24-64ccffa83303'}, {'abstract': 'The burgeoning Manchester International Festival offers a stellar lineup of music, theater and visual arts events to match the city’s reputation as both a creative incubator and provocateur.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/live-from-manchester/', 'snippet': 'The burgeoning Manchester International Festival offers a stellar lineup of music, theater and visual arts events to match the city’s reputation as both a creative incubator and provocateur.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Back in 2009, Hans-Ulrich Obrist, the co-director of London’s Serpentine Gallery, described the burgeoning Manchester International Festival (MIF) as a tribute to the British architect Cedric Price, who, in the 1960s had an idea to build a flexible, interdisciplinary arts space in East London. Price’s “Fun Palace,” as he called it, was never realized, but its spirit thrives in this biannual 18-day festival, now in its third incarnation. This year, Alex Poots, the festival’s director, has come up with another stellar lineup of music, theater and visual arts events to match the city’s reputation as both a creative incubator and provocateur.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Live From Manchester', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T17:12:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marina Cashdan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cashdan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/54e0e850-939b-5bbc-a6da-60e12d38d49d', 'word_count': 702, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54e0e850-939b-5bbc-a6da-60e12d38d49d'}, {'abstract': 'The Red Bulls on Wednesday signed the veteran German goalkeeper Frank Rost as the team’s third designated player.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/red-bulls-sign-rost-veteran-german-goalkeeper/', 'snippet': 'The Red Bulls on Wednesday signed the veteran German goalkeeper Frank Rost as the team’s third designated player.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Going against the conventional wisdom in Major League Soccer that asserts paying big money for a goalkeeper rarely makes sense, the Red Bulls on Wednesday used their third slot for a designated player to sign Frank Rost, 38, whose contract with Hamburg of the German Bundesliga had expired.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Red Bulls Sign Rost, Veteran German Goalkeeper', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Soler, Erik', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'German Bundesliga', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Soccer', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Red Bulls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T17:14:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Bell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0971e4bd-f263-5547-83d7-83782abb7d51', 'word_count': 466, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0971e4bd-f263-5547-83d7-83782abb7d51'}, {'abstract': 'Aimed at changing how Wall Street does business, the Dodd-Frank Act is also peppered with little-known items on issues like so-called conflict minerals and mining safety — the pet concerns of lawmakers.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/unearthing-exotic-provisions-buried-in-dodd-frank/', 'snippet': 'Aimed at changing how Wall Street does business, the Dodd-Frank Act is also peppered with little-known items on issues like so-called conflict minerals and mining safety — the pet concerns of lawmakers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At a meeting in February to discuss the recent overhaul of financial regulations, lobbyists and policy makers never once mentioned Wall Street. They did not talk about derivatives, mortgage-backed securities or any of the exotic products at the center of the crisis.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Unearthing Exotic Provisions Buried in Dodd-Frank', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T17:16:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f1c537e-a160-5e17-996e-8500dd71de20', 'word_count': 946, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f1c537e-a160-5e17-996e-8500dd71de20'}, {'abstract': 'Punting the deficit debate to the next administration.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/wait-til-2013/', 'snippet': 'Punting the deficit debate to the next administration.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rich Lowry on the debt ceiling negotiations and the next election:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wait ‘Til 2013', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T17:17:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e59c97e7-eb9f-5786-a364-6abeff33a719', 'word_count': 340, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e59c97e7-eb9f-5786-a364-6abeff33a719'}, {'abstract': 'Cal Ripken says Derek Jeter should contain his emotions and keep an open mind as he goes forward from 3,000 hits.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/sports/baseball/cal-ripkens-advice-for-derek-jeter.html', 'snippet': 'Cal Ripken says Derek Jeter should contain his emotions and keep an open mind as he goes forward from 3,000 hits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'History sublimely addressed, a threshold spectacularly crossed, Derek Jeter now resumes the indeterminate life of an aging shortstop. Yes, 3,000 hits are indelibly carved as a franchise first, but the resulting glow is bound to fade like perspiration stains on his pinstriped jersey.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/14/sports/14araton1/14araton1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 767, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/14/sp