ven', 'middlename': 'Davidoff', 'lastname': 'Solomon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d99bef5a-5647-556c-a535-7831eb1827a7', 'word_count': 1041, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d99bef5a-5647-556c-a535-7831eb1827a7'}, {'abstract': 'Americans will leave soon, but the fighting in Iraq is likely to continue.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/anxiety-hovers-over-iraqi-commandos/', 'snippet': 'Americans will leave soon, but the fighting in Iraq is likely to continue.', 'lead_paragraph': ' BAGHDAD — A photographer and I recently embedded with an Army Special Forces unit that operates from a corner of Camp Victory, the United States military’s vast complex near the airport. Such embeds are extremely rare and this one took many months to secure — while the regular Army welcomes reporters with nearly unimpeded access, the Special Forces are leery of journalists. This was underscored by the long list of ground rules they require reporters to adhere to in order to protect operational secrecy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Anxiety Hovers Over Iraqi Commandos', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sadr, Moktada Al-', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA IN MESOPOTAMIA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Iraqi Army', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mahdi Army', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Baghdad (Iraq)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T19:05:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_nam