ted by the Minnesota government shutdown skip a loan payment.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/when-its-o-k-to-skip-a-loan-payment/', 'snippet': 'U.S. Bank is letting customers affected by the Minnesota government shutdown skip a loan payment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s generally a bad idea to skip mortgage and other loan payments. Late payments damage your credit score and add late fees to your monthly total.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When It’s O.K. to Skip a Loan Payment', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Employees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'US Bancorp', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Minnesota', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T19:27:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e578709-813c-5932-8948-aa85487eac11', 'word_count': 203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e578709-813c-5932-8948-aa85487eac11'}, {'abstract': 'Should have sex with the girl you have been dating for a year mean you are labeled as a sex offender for the rest of your life?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/when-a-sex-offender-isnt/', 'snippet': 'Should have sex with the girl you have been dating for a year mean you are labeled as a sex offender for the rest of your life?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Boy meets girl. Boy and girl fall in love. After dating for a year, they have sex, and the girl’s mother thinks they are moving too quickly. The girl’s mother calls the police, hoping they will scare boy and girl a little. Instead, he is arrested and put on the Texas sex-offender list, since he is 19 and she is 16, which is a year shy of the state’s age of consent. Boy avoids jail, is put on probation, and is forced to move out of his home because the law says he can’t live in the same house as his 12-year-old sister. Eventually, boy and girl marry, have four daughters and, 15 years later, he is still a registered sex offender who is not allowed to coach his children’s soccer teams, get a job at a major corporation or leave the state without registering with law enforcement.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When a Sex Offender Isn’t', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dating and Courtship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T19:31:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Belkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf030a8b-cc78-5f40-b61b-0ff1ba754c36', 'word_count': 533, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf030a8b-cc78-5f40-b61b-0ff1ba754c36'}, {'abstract': 'Limited editions, sales, trunk shows and a fragrance debut.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/fashion/new-york-shopping-events