article/568a6ed5-6423-545c-909b-15e3c4e26ba6'}, {'abstract': 'In Central Park Tuesday night, curious guests and passers-by were able to examine some of the city’s fleet of green vehicles. The total has just increased to 430.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/on-electric-cars-city-hopes-to-lead-by-examples/', 'snippet': 'In Central Park Tuesday night, curious guests and passers-by were able to examine some of the city’s fleet of green vehicles. The total has just increased to 430.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It may have been the only auto showroom in city history to feature shirtless roller skaters, tip-seeking jugglers and an on-site churro vendor.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Electric Cars, City Hopes to Lead by Examples', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Vehicles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T20:00:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Flegenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flegenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68288369-508a-5123-9634-fb01fc6c57a7', 'word_count': 699, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68288369-508a-5123-9634-fb01fc6c57a7'}, {'abstract': 'ArtsBeat will cover the announcement of the nominees for the 63rd Primetime Emmy Awards on Thursday morning.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/counting-down-to-the-primetime-emmy-nominations/', 'snippet': 'ArtsBeat will cover the announcement of the nominees for the 63rd Primetime Emmy Awards on Thursday morning.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You’ve watched the shows, admired the actors, writers and producers, posted your reactions on Twitter and Facebook, read the recaps and commented on the criticism. But none of it matters until the television industry decides the best work of the 2010-2011 season, the only way it knows how: by handing out awards.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Counting Down to the Primetime Emmy Nominations', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emmy Awards', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T20:03:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f97d3e9-8171-569c-b5d0-f909c39c84a4', 'word_count': 221, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f97d3e9-8171-569c-b5d0-f909c39c84a4'}, {'abstract': 'Despite their strong support for the mortgage interest deduction, middle-class Americans are not the primary beneficiaries — the wealthy are.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/despite-benefit-disparities-middle-class-supports-mortgage-deduction/', 'snippet': 'Despite their strong support for the mortgage interest deduction, middle-class Americans are not the primary beneficiaries — the wealthy are.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A couple of weeks ago, David Streitfeld and Megan Thee-Brenan of The New York Times reported on the results of a Times/CBS News poll on homeownership in the United States. The poll found continued support for government subsidies for homeownership, including the mortgage interest deduction. Noting broad, bipartisan support for the deduction, Mr. Streitfeld and Ms. Thee-Brenan acknowledged that “… almost no one favors discontinuing the mortgage tax deduction, a prized middle-class benefit that has been featured on some budget-cutting proposals.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Despite Benefit Disparities, Middle Class Supports Mortgage Deduction', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T20:04:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian J. McCabe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'McCabe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/56d27fbf-7eff-5763-906d-b7cee04d524c', 'word_count': 863, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56d27fbf-7eff-5763-906d-b7cee04d524c'}, {'abstract': 'Trials conducted in Africa were the first to show protection in heterosexuals whose partners had H.I.V.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/health/research/14aids.html', 'snippet': 'Trials conducted in Africa were the first to show protection in heterosexuals whose partners had H.I.V.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two new studies released on Wednesday add to the growing body of evidence that taking a daily pill containing one or two AIDS drugs can keep an uninfected person from catching the fatal human immunodeficiency virus.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/14/us/AIDS/AIDS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 853, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/14/us/AIDS/AIDS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/14/us/AIDS/AIDS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Studies Show Pills Can Prevent H.I.V. Infection', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Two Studies Show Pills Can Prevent H.I.V. Infection', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Acquired Immune Deficiency Syndrome', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Condoms', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T20:06:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Research', 'byline': {'original': 'By Donald G. McNeil Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Donald', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'McNeil', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5565a7c9-dc8a-5078-9ccb-e7f96d70006d', 'word_count': 611, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5565a7c9-dc8a-5078-9ccb-e7f96d70006d'}, {'abstract': 'While Tim Pawlenty balanced the state budget without new taxes, critics say he relied on one-time accounting maneuvers that contributed to the current government shutdown.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/us/politics/14pawlenty.html', 'snippet': 'While Tim Pawlenty balanced the state budget without new taxes, critics say he relied on one-time accounting maneuvers that contributed to the current government shutdown.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the presidential campaign trail, Tim Pawlenty, who in January completed two terms as governor of Minnesota, runs largely as an implacable foe of government spending, saying he drew “a line in the sand” in his home state and stood tough against Democrats during a government shutdown in 2005.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/14/us/14pawlenty_span/14pawlenty_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/14/us/14pawlenty_span/14pawlenty_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/14/us/14pawlenty_span/14pawlenty_span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 690, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/14/us/14pawlenty_span/14pawlenty_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/14/us/14pawlenty_span/14pawlenty_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Amid Minnesota Crisis, Pawlenty Faces Scrutiny', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Amid Minnesota Crisis, Pawlenty Faces Scrutiny', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pawlenty, Tim', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Minnesota', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T20:07:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Nation