ed him at gunpoint. Through the Daily Express, McKinney claimed that Anderson consented to a three-day tryst at a cottage in Devon and was later brainwashed by the Mormon Church. With headlines like “Manacled Mormon,” the Daily Mirror told a different story, one that painted McKinney as an S&M-practicing predator who chained Anderson to a bed and forced him to have sex with her with the hope of getting pregnant. McKinney fled the country in an outlandish disguise and, three decades later, made the news again, this time for persuading a South Korean doctor to clone her beloved pit bull, Booger. The Moment sat down with Morris in SoHo to discuss his mad meditation on obsession, hysteria and the tabloid rag.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Asked & Answered | Errol Morris', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T20:35:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abby Aguirre', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Aguirre', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62bdd30d-440c-5e36-accf-844ef8c02972', 'word_count': 1694, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62bdd30d-440c-5e36-accf-844ef8c02972'}, {'abstract': 'Photographs from India, Afghanistan and Spain.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/pictures-of-the-day-afghanistan-and-elsewhere-14/', 'snippet': 'Photographs from India, Afghanistan and Spain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photographs from India, Afghanistan and Spain.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pictures of the Day: Afghanistan and Elsewhere', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': 