artist who wrote the Facebook story “The Accidental Billionaires,” concerns the theft of priceless Moon rock samples.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here is the no-frills version of the Thad Roberts story: Mr. Roberts aspired to a career with NASA and became an intern at the Johnson Space Center. In 2002 he stole a 661-pound safe that contained priceless Moon rock samples. He was caught by an F.B.I. sting as he tried to sell this loot to mineral collectors. He was sentenced to eight years and four months in prison. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/14/arts/JPBOOK/JPBOOK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/14/arts/JPBOOK/JPBOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/14/arts/JPBOOK/JPBOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Supposition as Research: A Sort-of-True Story About NASA and a Thief', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Supposition as Research: A Sort-of-True Story About NASA and a Thief', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mezrich, Ben', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Moon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T21:02:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Janet Maslin', '