53-829f-537e3b34260d', 'word_count': 804, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44d0c176-e373-5253-829f-537e3b34260d'}, {'abstract': 'The magazine is expected to begin publishing a quarterly edition in late September.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/creem-set-to-return-to-the-newstand/', 'snippet': 'The magazine is expected to begin publishing a quarterly edition in late September.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It has been more than two decades since rock fans could pick up a copy of Creem magazine at a newsstand and submerse themselves in the fabled publication where critics like Lester Bangs and Dave Marsh helped define a generation of popular musicians. But there are plans afoot to resurrect the printed magazine this fall, The Associated Press reported this week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Creem Set to Return to the Newstand', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crowe, Cameron', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roxy Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T21:08:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa1f91dc-a5e0-55f5-aab0-051f00538e07', 'word_count': 538, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa1f91dc-a5e0-55f5-aab0-051f00538e07'}, {'abstract': 'The United States’ victory in the Women’s World Cup semifinals would not have been so thrilling without France’s aggressiveness and 25-11 lead in shots on goal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/sports/soccer/womens-world-cup-french-elegance-helps-make-another-american-beauty.html', 'snippet': 'The United States’ victory in the Women’s World Cup semifinals would not have been so thrilling without France’s aggressiveness and 25-11 lead in shots on goal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The proper thing to do — even before praising American resilience and Pia Sundhage’s coaching — is to respect France.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/14/sports/14vecsey-2/14vecsey-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 671, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/14/sports/14vecsey-2/14vecsey-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/14/sports/14vecsey-2/14vecsey-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'France Loses to the U.S., With Typical Elegance', 'kicker': 'Sports of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France Loses to the U.S., With Typical Elegance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's World Cup (Soccer)", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wambach, Abby', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T21:09:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Vecsey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vecsey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/252429f9-2a16-57