thin a popular and important national park in Madagascar, a critical habitat for a number of rare endemic fishes has been devastated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'John S. Sparks, curator of ichthyology at the American Museum of Natural History, writes about his expedition to Madagascar, where he studied native freshwater fish.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Returning Upriver With Very Few Fish', 'kicker': 'Scientist at Work', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish and Other Marine Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lakes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rivers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN MUSEUM OF NATURAL HISTORY', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Madagascar', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T21:18:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By John S. Sparks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Sparks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5fb117c3-8bc0-5fe4-9866-60f4c1d0b214', 'word_count': 1411, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5fb117c3-8bc0-5fe4-9866-60f4c1d0b214'}, {'abstract': 'The opening-night party for the Bread & Butter urban and street fashion trade fair looked like something out of Burning Man.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/07/13/fashion/20110714-breadandbutter.html', 'snippet': 'The opening-night party for the Bread & Butter urban and street fashion trade fair looked like something out of Burning Man.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The opening-night party for the Bread & Butter urban and street fashion trade fair looked like something out of Burning Man.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/13/fashion/20110714-breadandbutter-slide-IG5D/20110714-breadandbutter-slide-IG5D-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/13/fashion/20110714-breadandbutter-slide-IG5D/20110714-breadandbutter-slide-IG5D-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/13/fashion/20110714-breadandbutter-slide-IG5D/20110714-breadandbutter-slide-IG5D-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Kickoff', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Berlin (Germany)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trade Shows and Fairs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T21:22:48+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Fashion & Style', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/018a6fb1-2f1c-522e-aa40-f1672baceacf', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/018a6fb1-2f1c-522e-aa40-f1672baceacf'}, {'abstract': 'The latest of the “Giselle” movies, this time in 3-D, stars Natalia Osipova and Leonid Sarafanov at the Mariinsky Theater in St. Petersburg.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/arts/dance/natalia-osipova-at-the-mariinsky-theater-in-giselle-in-3d.html', 'snippet': 'The latest of the “Giselle” movies, this time in 3-D, stars Natalia Osipova and Leonid Sarafanov at the Mariinsky Theater in St. Petersburg.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Films of the two-act Romantic ballet “Giselle” go back almost 80 years. The clips of black-and-white silent film of Olga Spessivtseva (1932) and Margot Fonteyn (1937) used to be rare as gold dust; now you can see them on YouTube. The ancient film technology, however, makes anyone watching today frustrated by its obvious inadequacies. So it’s dismaying that the new “Giselle in 3D,” featuring one of the finest casts achievable today, makes even more basic cinematic errors. The performance, recorded at the Mariinsky Theater in St. Petersburg, features Natalia Osipova, from the Bolshoi Ballet in Moscow, as Giselle amid an otherwise all-Mariinsky cast. The filming is by the British company Can Communicate, a title that turns out to be somewhat optimistic.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/14/arts/GISELLE/GISELLE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/14/arts/GISELLE/GISELLE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/14/arts/GISELLE/GISELLE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Flying Giselle, Coming Right at You', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Flying Giselle, Coming Right at You', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN BALLET THEATER', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal Ballet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mariinsky Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Osipova, Natalia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vishneva, Diana', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T21:23:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d56c9e7d-8280-5792-886d-d471ec2cfa56', 'word_count': 916, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d56c9e7d-8280-5792-886d-d471ec2cfa56'}, {'abstract': 'The former governor of Minnesota on Wednesday offered a textbook, three-step process that he hopes will lessen the impact of his decision not to sign on to the Family Leader Marriage Pledge.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/pawlenty-playbook-for-declining-marriage-pledge/', 'snippet': 'The former governor of Minnesota on Wednesday offered a textbook, three-step process that he hopes will lessen the impact of his decision not to sign on to the Family Leader Marriage Pledge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here’s a political puzzle: How do you decline to sign a pledge defending marriage if you are a Republican presidential candidate? Now, consider you need to win Iowa, where conservative voters have proven their affinity for candidates who are demonstrative about their faith. And those voters already have made it know that they feel that the candidates are focusing almost exclusively on the economy at the expense of social issues.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pawlenty’s Playbook for Skipping Marriage Pledge', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pawlenty, Tim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T21:35:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/539371ed-075d-518d-9e86-900eacffe4c8', 'word_count': 766, 'uri': 'nyt://article/539371ed-075d-518d-9e86-900eacffe4c8'}, {'abstract': 'This week, Fearne Cotton, Charlotte Poutrel and Karolina Kurkova wear clothes that get attention for their vivid color.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/summer-styles-sirens/', 'snippet': 'This week, Fearne Cotton, Charlotte Poutrel and Karolina Kurkova wear clothes that get attention for their vivid color.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The hazy and humid days of summer are upon us, and it seems many are coming down with a case of scarlet fever. Rather than run around in barely there ensembles, women are wearing clothes that get attention for their vivid color. The English television presenter Fearne Cotton keeps things casual in cheery off-shades, while the actress Charlotte Poutrel goes glamorous and the model Karolina Kurkova dazzles in floor-length silk. The heat is on.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Summer Styles | Sirens', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T21:38:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/371642c7-5dbe-5b3b-9c6c-4053b96ebd57', 'word_count': 78, 'uri': 'nyt://article/371642c7-5dbe-5b3b-9c6c-4053b96ebd57'}, {'abstract': 'Yob, a doom-metal band from Eugene, Ore., plumbed the depths of patterned, simple chord structures at Le Poisson Rouge on Tuesday night.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/arts/music/yob-at-le-poisson-rouge-review.html', 'snippet': 'Yob, a doom-metal band from Eugene, Ore., plumbed the depths of patterned, simple chord structures at Le Poisson Rouge on Tuesday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was Mike Scheidt, the guitarist and singer from the doom-metal trio Yob, at Le Poisson Rouge on Tuesday night. He was playing a pattern, long-form and superficially simple. Doom tends to stay slow and precise; he cycled a few chords, or sometimes only one, over and over.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/14/arts/YOB/YOB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 348, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/14/arts/YOB/YOB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 348}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/14/arts/YOB/YOB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/14/arts/YOB/YOB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/