}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Arias With a Twist (Play)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Arias, Joey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Twist, Basil', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABRONS ARTS CENTER', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T21:48:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f988368b-5b92-5b4f-aa65-6222577efc1f', 'word_count': 110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f988368b-5b92-5b4f-aa65-6222577efc1f'}, {'abstract': 'NBC announced Wednesday that Jennifer Salke will join the network as president of entertainment.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/nbc-names-jennifer-salke-its-entertainment-president/', 'snippet': 'NBC announced Wednesday that Jennifer Salke will join the network as president of entertainment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NBC filled a long dormant top spot in its entertainment division Wednesday when it announced that Jennifer Salke would join the network as president of entertainment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'NBC Names Jennifer Salke Its Entertainment President', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T21:49:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8341b0d1-9464-57b4-8904-7172f17feec2', 'word_count': 127, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8341b0d1-9464-57b4-8904-7172f17feec2'}, {'abstract': 'Inspired by the Mexican Martini of Austin, Tex., readers respond on Facebook.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/readers-favorite-local-drinks/', 'snippet': 'Inspired by the Mexican Martini of Austin, Tex., readers respond on Facebook.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Times asked readers on Facebook to share their favorite local drinks, like the Mexican Martini of Austin, Tex. Beers, cocktails and spirits are all eligible. Below are a few highlights; add yours to the mix in the comments section below.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Readers’ Favorite Local Drinks', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T21:50:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/efbae77b-a7ae-5f75-a12a-5055f43183e1', 'word_count': 226, 'uri': 'nyt://article/efbae77b-a7ae-5f75-a12a-5055f43183e1'}, {'abstract': 'Readers weigh in on the cookers.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/do-you-use-a-big-green-egg/', 'snippet': 'Readers weigh in on the cookers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I lived in Atlanta in the late 1980s, I learned to cook Thanksgiving turkeys, Fourth of July pork shoulders, and Sunday night burgers on the Big Green Egg. When I moved to Oxford, Miss. in 1995, I had to leave my Egg behind. It wouldn’t fit in the moving truck.When my mother in law, Marley Hobbs, age 88, moved two doors down a couple years ago, she saved enough room in her moving truck for her Egg. Of late, I’ve been borrowing hers more frequently, while pondering the purchase of a Primo, one of those glossy black oblong models. Sure, they’re expensive. But, after reporting my story on them, I want one more than ever. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Do You Use a Big Green Egg?', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T21:54:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By John T. Edge', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'T.', 'lastname': 'Edge', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d75b6e2a-f307-5242-a9be-d0622326c63b', 'word_count': 155, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d75b6e2a-f307-5242-a9be-d0622326c63b'}, {'abstract': 'The agreement comes more than a year after an adopted-child abandonment scandal led Russian officials to threaten a ban on adoptions of Russian children by Americans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/world/europe/14moscow.html', 'snippet': 'The agreement comes more than a year after an adopted-child abandonment scandal led Russian officials to threaten a ban on adoptions of Russian children by Americans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — More than a year after an adopted-child abandonment scandal led Russian officials to threaten a ban on adoptions of Russian children by Americans, the United States and Russia have reached an agreement that will allow such adoptions to proceed under heightened scrutiny. ', 'print_section':