 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Track Your Stolen Hardware With These Apps', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vigilantes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T22:31:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Biggs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Biggs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f0a0c35-ec46-53d8-97bf-c6cd917c3987', 'word_count': 285, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f0a0c35-ec46-53d8-97bf-c6cd917c3987'}, {'abstract': 'Polls suggest the Democrats are on the right side of public opinion in the fiscal debate.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/house-republicans-no-tax-stance-far-outside-political-mainstream/', 'snippet': 'Polls suggest the Democrats are on the right side of public opinion in the fiscal debate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The back-and-forth of the debt limit negotiations can be perplexing. But the facts driving the debate are quite straightforward. Any deal, or any workaround to a deal, will need to be approved by a majority of the House of Representatives. The Republicans in the House of Representatives are extremely conservative on fiscal matters and are significantly out of step with the public as a whole. Given that Democrats continue to control the Senate and the White House, and that their votes may be necessary in the House as well, this makes compromise nearly impossible.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'G.O.P.’s No-Tax Stance Is Outside Political Mainstream', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McConnell, Mitch', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Norquist, Grover G', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICANS FOR TAX REFORM', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T22:32:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/60a40389-497c-5a88-873d-b8d32ffa193f', 'word_count': 800, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60a40389-497c-5a88-873d-b8d32ffa193f'}, {'abstract': 'A leading analyst of global risk says economic overshoot has pushed environmental overshoot off his list of concerns.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/on-debt-death-taxes-and-temperatures/', 'snippet': 'A leading analyst of global risk says economic overshoot has pushed environmental overshoot off his list of concerns.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few days ago, I had a short e-mail exchange with Vaclav Smil, a master analyst of risks and resources, on strokes and aging, climate policy, the global debt crisis and a few other light subjects. I’ve excerpted our chat below in the form of a dialogue.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Debt, Death, Taxes and Temperatures', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emergency Medical Treatment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stroke', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mullen, Michael G', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Joint Chiefs of Staff', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T22:33:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7cf92b25-ec39-5271-9798-8ccec7f119e2', 'word_count': 1180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7cf92b25-ec39-5271-9798-8ccec7f119e2'}, {'abstract': 'Danielle Chiesi, convicted in the Galleon Group insider trading case, is resolving a suit filed by the Securities and Exchange Commission.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/business/danielle-chiesi-to-settle-with-sec-for-540000.html', 'snippet': 'Danielle Chiesi, convicted in the Galleon Group insider trading case, is resolving a suit filed by the Securities and Exchange Commission.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Danielle Chiesi, convicted of insider trading as part of the case against the Galleon Group hedge fund, agreed to pay $540,000 to settle related allegations by the Securities and Exchange Commission.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Galleon Case Figure Settles With S.E.C.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Galleon Case Figure Settles With S.E.C.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chiesi, Danielle', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Securities and Commodities Violations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Galleon Group', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T22:34:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bloomberg News', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bloomberg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'News', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd768500-8f03-55e6-b93c-d7e94efb156b', 'word_count': 212, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd768500-8f03-55e6-b93c-d7e94efb156b'}, {'abstract': 'Though they come at a price, voice-guided navigation apps also have a wealth of features and ease of use.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/technology/personaltech/with-mobile-navigation-comes-easy-directions-app-smart.html', 'snippet': 'Though they come at a price, voice-guided navigation apps also have a wealth of features and ease of use.', 'lead_paragraph': 'App shopping is a fairly painless diversion, thanks to all the $1 programs on the market. But in one important category, voice-guided navigation for drivers, the stakes are higher. You can spend $70 on one, or you can take your chances with something cheap or free.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'cap