ltaneously, Doug Mills, a staff photographer in the Washington bureau of The New York Times, has tried a creative trick or two. He once strapped the video camera around his neck, using his stomach to hold it in place. The results, he said, were “freewheeling and dangling and very difficult to work with.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shooting Twice, at Once', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cameras', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clemens, Roger', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T22:41:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kerri MacDonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kerri', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacDonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7d8d333-8501-5426-8f68-76950585faba', 'word_count': 279, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7d8d333-8501-5426-8f68-76950585faba'}, {'abstract': 'Peter King is the first Republican to call for an inquiry into the company’s practices, including anonymous allegations that journalists tried to get phone information on 9/11 victims.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/criticism-of-news-corp-spreads-in-the-u-s/', 'snippet': 'Peter King is the first Republican to call for an inquiry into the company’s practices, including anonymous allegations that journalists tried to get phone information on 9/11 victims.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Public criticism of the News Corporation’s conduct in the British hacking scandal has crossed the ocean to the United States — and crosse