7d5'}, {'abstract': 'The Orchard low table from Fern has a tabletop made of salvaged claro walnut from Northern California.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/garden/a-table-of-patchwork-walnut.html', 'snippet': 'The Orchard low table from Fern has a tabletop made of salvaged claro walnut from Northern California.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jason Roskey, a furniture designer who runs the Brooklyn company Fern with his wife, Maggie Goudsmit, started out as a visual artist making mixed-media pieces and collages. And the Orchard low table, his latest creation, seems to reflect that: the tabletop has what he calls a “patchwork construction” of salvaged claro walnut from orchards in Northern California.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/14/garden/14furniture-span/14furniture-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 327, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/14/garden/14furniture-span/14furniture-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 327}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/14/garden/14furniture-span/14furniture-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/14/garden/14furniture-span/14furniture-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/14/garden/14furniture-span/14furniture-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Table of Patchwork Walnut', 'kicker': 'Currents | Furniture', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Table of Patchwork Walnut', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tables', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T23:02:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rima Suqi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rima', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Suqi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7fd44df0-17f2-5270-b374-8980166f6c08', 'word_count': 127, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7fd44df0-17f2-5270-b374-8980166f6c08'}, {'abstract': 'Meticulously and gorgeously wrought, Clark Sanders’s stone house and straw-bale structures in the Catskills are his calling cards.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/07/14/garden/20110714-STRAWBALE.html', 'snippet': 'Meticulously and gorgeously wrought, Clark Sanders’s stone house and straw-bale structures in the Catskills are his calling cards.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Meticulously and gorgeously wrought, Clark Sanders’s stone house and straw-bale structures in the Catskills are his calling cards.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/14/garden/20110714-STRAWBALE-slide-XD3W/20110714-STRAWBALE-slide-XD3W-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 748, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/14/garden/20110714-STRAWBALE-slide-XD3W/20110714-STRAWBALE-slide-XD3W-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/14/garden/20110714-STRAWBALE-slide-XD3W/20110714-STRAWBALE-slide-XD3W-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Houses Made of Sticks and Stones', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Catskills (NYS Area)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T23:02:48+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Home & Garden', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/c23a2902-ee5a-5eb3-9010-0035c203c0a1', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/c23a2902-ee5a-5eb3-9010-0035c203c0a1'}, {'abstract': 'The second edition of “A History of Design from the Victorian Era to the Present” is being published this week, more than four decades after the first edition.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/garden/a-history-of-design-gets-an-update.html', 'snippet': 'The second edition of “A History of Design from the Victorian Era to the Present” is being published this week, more than four decades after the first edition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The second edition of “A History of Design from the Victorian Era to the Present” (W. W. Norton; $50) is being published this week, more than four decades after the first edition. The new book, by Ann Ferebee and Jeff Byles, is “a capsule history of design in a nutshell, with all the major players and the major pieces,” said Nancy Green, the editor of both editions (the first was published by Van Nostrand Reinhold, in 1970).', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/14/garden/13books/13books-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 904, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'th