ics business.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/jawbone-will-sell-a-health-tracking-bracelet/', 'snippet': 'Jawbone, a company known for its fashionable audio products, is getting into the wearable electronics business.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jawbone, a company best known for its line of sleek, futuristic-looking Bluetooth headsets and music accessories, is taking a big leap away from the audio industry. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jawbone Will Sell a Health-Tracking Bracelet', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T23:12:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenna Wortham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wortham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1db21840-a75d-5129-8a62-00ec80d22a2e', 'word_count': 289, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1db21840-a75d-5129-8a62-00ec80d22a2e'}, {'abstract': 'In this week’s podcast: Ben Sisario on a new piracy crackdown and David Perry on the shadowy groups behind some of the recent major hacking exploits.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/tech-talk-podcast-piracy-and-hacking/', 'snippet': 'In this week’s podcast: Ben Sisario on a new piracy crackdown and David Perry on the shadowy groups behind some of the recent major hacking exploits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Internet service providers and the music and movie industries are joining forces to fight copyright infringement. On this week’s Bits: Tech Talk show, Bettina Edelstein talks to Ben Sisario, a Times media reporter, about a new joint effort to crack down on downloads of pirated content with repeated warnings for offenders and eventually, tougher measures, like slowed-down connections and blocked browsing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tech Talk Podcast: Piracy and Hacking', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Copyrights and Copyright Violations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hackers (Computers)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T23:15:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/185e158e-931b-58ac-9107-4cf117dad4bd', 'word_count': 226, 'uri': 'nyt://article/185e158e-931b-58ac-9107-4cf117dad4bd'}, {'abstract': 'Google has announced the winners of its first science fair, and they are all young women who did projects in the medical field.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/13/girl-power-wins-at-googles-first-science-fair/', 'snippet': 'Google has announced the winners of its first science fair, and they are all young women who did projects in the medical field.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If Google‘s first science fair is any indication, the top scientists of the future will be women. Google has announced the fair’s winners, and they are all young women.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Girl Power Wins at Google’s First Science Fair', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Contests and Prizes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion'