solated and overwhelmed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/world/asia/14kabul.html', 'snippet': 'The political, economic, military and diplomatic troubles facing President Hamid Karzai are making him appear increasingly isolated and overwhelmed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — At midday, the glare and dust obscures Afghanistan’s horizon in what seems a metaphor for the position of the Afghan president as political and economic crises mount on every front: it is increasingly hard to see how he will find his way. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/14/world/14kabul/14kabul-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/14/world/14kabul/14kabul-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/14/world/14kabul/14kabul-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 772, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/14/world/14kabul/14kabul-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/14/world/14kabul/14kabul-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Clouds Around Karzai Darken the Road Ahead', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Clouds Around Karzai Darken the Road Ahead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karzai, Hamid', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-13T23:49:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alissa J. Rubin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alissa', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Rubin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/7461d9f7-8278-5a83-acf5-df5566ba8c17', 'word_count': 1165, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7461d9f7-8278-5a83-acf5-df5566ba8c17'}, {'abstract': 'Because the company is run at Mr. Murdoch’s whim, its shares trade more cheaply than rivals’, and the phone-hacking scandal has widened that gap.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/business/murdoch-discount-in-news-corp-stock.html', 'snippet': 'Because the company is run at Mr. Murdoch’s whim, its shares trade more cheaply than rivals’, and the phone-hacking scandal has widened that gap.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rupert Murdoch’s political influence may be surpassed by his impact on the value of the News Corporation. The stock routinely trades more cheaply than media rivals’, largely because the company, which is listed in the United States, is run at Mr. Murdoch’s whim. As a result of the British phone-hacking scandal, the Murdoch discount has widened to 30 percent.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Murdoch Discount in News Corp. Stock', 'kicker': 'Reuters Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For News Corp., Murdoch Discount', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 