of mortality and bittersweet smiles in “Harry Potter and the Deathly Hallows: Part 2,” the grave, deeply satisfying final movie in the series. A pop cultural happening extraordinaire, the Potter movies took uncertain flight in 2001 with Harry, then an orphan of 11, home alone with his grotesquely unloving relatives. Times were grim, at least off screen — the first opened in November of that year — but Chris Columbus’s directorial touch was insistently light as Harry was initiated into a world alive with odd doings, strange creatures and the evil that would almost consume it.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/movies/15harry3_span/15harry3_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/15/movies/15harry3_span/15harry3_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/movies/15harry3_span/15harry3_span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/movies/15harry3_span/15harry3_span-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/15/movies/15harry3_span/15harry3_span-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Class Dismissed', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Harry Potter and the Deathly Hallows: Part 2'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Class Dismissed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yates, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rowling, J K', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Watson, Emma', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grint, Rupert', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Radcliffe, Daniel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T00:58:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9bccc5ff-2693-5096-9279-3bb09975fb65', 'word_count': 1727, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9bccc5ff-2693-5096-9279-3bb09975fb65'}, {'abstract': 'The dismembered body of Leiby Kletzky, 8, was discovered, and a 35-year-old man who lives in the neighborhood was charged in the killing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/nyregion/arrest-made-in-brooklyn-killing-of-leiby-kletzky.html', 'snippet': 'The dismembered body of Leiby Kletzky, 8, was discovered, and a 35-year-old man who lives in the neighborhood was charged in the killing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was only seven blocks. The boy had begged and his parents had said yes, he could walk part of the way home from day camp by himself. Together they had memorized the route. They had practiced a dry run together. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/14/nyregion/Boy-1310594858731/Boy-1310594858731-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 365, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/14/nyregion/Boy-1310594858731/Boy-1310594858731-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargehe