agraph': 'A horrified city can only imagine the darkness that must now envelop the family of Leiby Kletzky, the 8-year-old boy from Borough Park, Brooklyn, whose dismembered remains were found on Wednesday, two days after he had disappeared. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Horror Recalls Another', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Youth', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Patz, Etan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ramos, Jose A', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vance, Cyrus R Jr', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'SoHo (NYC)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T10:58:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clyde Haberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clyde', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/12a2fff8-7885-58bf-9720-dae5b44490ba', 'word_count': 976, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12a2fff8-7885-58bf-9720-dae5b44490ba'}, {'abstract': 'Roost specializes in helping business owners who are clueless about social media or severely time-challenged or both.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/a-tool-to-help-business-owners-struggling-with-social-media/', 'snippet': 'Roost specializes in helping business owners who are clueless about social media or severely time-challenged or both.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carolyn Betts is more knowledgeable about social networking than the average small-business owner. Back in 2004, when she had just started working for an executive recruiting firm, she saw how her sister in college was spending a lot of time on this student-focused site called Facebook and immediately started using it to reach out to sharp graduates to fill junior-level positions. She soon became a relatively early user of LinkedIn and Twitter, using them to expand her online presence. So when Ms. Betts started her own recruiting company in San Francisco in 2009 to find sales executives for start-ups, no one had to tell her to make social networks part of her operation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Tool to Help Business Owners Struggling With Social Media', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T11:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By David H. Freedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'H.', 'lastname': 'Freedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a79efa36-f6bf-5752-abce-c57bf77cab69', 'word_count': 991, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a79efa36-f6bf-5752-abce-c57bf77cab69'}, {'abstract': 'Robust gains in almost all of JPMorgan Chase’s main businesses offered hope that the banking industry’s prospects were not as bad as feared.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbo