eeking to spin off its refinery business and focus on exploration.', 'lead_paragraph': '9:31 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'ConocoPhillips to Split Into Two Businesses', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ConocoPhillips', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T11:28:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c9561b7-ae72-554b-a427-1cdcb5052027', 'word_count': 494, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c9561b7-ae72-554b-a427-1cdcb5052027'}, {'abstract': 'Being academic.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/nbering/', 'snippet': 'Being academic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I should have given notice that yesterday was NBER day; Gauti Eggertsson and I presented our debt-deleveraging paper to the NBER Summer Institute. Really good discussion. Also, “to haircut” is now a verb, as in, “The ECB shouldn’t cut anyone off, it should just haircut the riskier debt.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'NBERing', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T11:45:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b576366-5460-50e9-9276-12da313238ad', 'word_count': 48, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b576366-5460-50e9-9276-12da313238ad'}, {'abstract': 'Extraordinary concessions, rejected.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/obama-moderate-republican/', 'snippet': 'Extraordinary concessions, rejected.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OK, not exactly. But Nate Silver’s analysis of the budget proposals is a must-read. Nate looks at polling, and extracts the following implied preferences for the mix between tax increases and spending cuts in a debt deal:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama, Moderate Republican', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T11:55:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef9a10ca-d184-57f1-a1bc-c1af9272dbcc', 'word_count': 108, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef9a10ca-d184-57f1-a1bc-c1af9272dbcc'}, {'abstract': 'Photofly, a service from Autodesk that builds 3-D models from photographs, has spawned a mini-genre of YouTube videos showing what can be done with the service.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/photofly-brings-3-d-models-to-the-masses/', 'snippet': 'Photofly, a service from Autodesk that builds 3-D models from photographs, has spawned a mini-genre of YouTube videos showing what can be done with the service.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since Photofly, a service\xa0that turns uploaded photos into three-dimensional models,\xa0was introduced in May, it has received an average of 80 uploads an hour, for a total of 70,000 images, according to Autodesk, the service’s creator.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Photofly Brings 3-D Models to the Masses', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Software', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Three-Dimensional Devices and Effects', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AutoDesk Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T12:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer 8. Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2bc97e5e-0fe8-5d86-817a-35334f3f3755', 'word_count': 468, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2bc97e5e-0fe8-5d86-817a-35334f3f3755'}, {'abstract': 'In our exclusive video, the model discusses her eponymous new cashmere line in her Notting Hill living room.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/claudia-schiffer-sweater-girl/', 'snippet': 'In our exclusive video, the model discusses her eponymous new cashmere line in her Notting Hill living room.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I wanted to make easy pieces that are practical yet chic,” says the model Claudia Schiffer, as she showed off examples from an eponymous new cashmere line in her airy, art-filled Notting Hill, London living room. “You know simple but well-cut dresses and tops that you can throw on with leggings and boots for the school run, and pair with a great pair of earrings or a cool cuff for dinner.’’ Comprised of chunky-knit jackets, dresses and buttery boyfriend sweaters, the collection (created in collaboration with the German knitwear label Iris von Arnim) ranges from about $400 to $1,600, and debuts later this month at net-a-porter.com. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Claudia Schiffer | Sweater Girl', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schiffer, Claudia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T12:00:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sandra Ballentine', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ballentine', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7db04fa5-051a-5ffb-8bfa-111bb0fad423', 'word_count': 109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7db04fa5-051a-5ffb-8bfa-111bb0fad423'}, {'abstract': "Behind-the-scenes from Miranda July's cover shoot with Sam Taylor-Wood. Video courtesy of Jennifer Johnson.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/magazine/100000000943963/miranda-july-lets-loose.html', 'snippet': "Behind-the-scenes from Miranda July's cover shoot with Sam Taylor-Wood. Video courtesy of Jennifer Johnson.", 'lead_paragraph': "Behind-the-scenes from Miranda July's cover shoot with Sam Taylor-Wood. Video courtesy of Jennifer Johnson.", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/13/magazine/video-mag-mirandajuly/video-mag-mirandajuly-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/13/magazine/video-mag-mirandajuly/video-mag-mirandajuly-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}},