1c2'}, {'abstract': 'A 13-room converted Georgian town house offers a minibar that takes the “bar” part seriously.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/a-hotel-mini-bar/', 'snippet': 'A 13-room converted Georgian town house offers a minibar that takes the “bar” part seriously.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s no secret that minibars have been evolving of late. Once receptacles of mass-market mixers and anemic airplane bottles of spirits, the in-room refrigerators at many hotels now offer an altogether more thoughtful selection, often with idiosyncratic touches like guitar strings and artisanal chocolates. But rare is the minibar that takes the “bar” part seriously. Enter Zetter Townhouse, in London’s Clerkenwell District.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Hotel Minibar', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T13:00:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Rowan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rowan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ccb44475-43bb-52fa-84a9-54ba9d0bf785', 'word_count': 251, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ccb44475-43bb-52fa-84a9-54ba9d0bf785'}, {'abstract': 'The Williams Companies has made a sweetened $5.5 billion offer for the Southern Union Company, topping a revised $5.1 billion bid from Energy Transfer Equity and extending a bidding war for the pipeline operator.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/williams-raises-southern-union-bid-to-5-5-billion/', 'snippet': 'The Williams Companies has made a sweetened $5.5 billion offer for the Southern Union Company, topping a revised $5.1 billion bid from Energy Transfer Equity and extending a bidding war for the pipeline operator.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Williams Companies on Thursday raised its offer for the Southern Union Company to $5.5 billion, extending a bidding war for the pipeline operator by topping a revised $5.1 billion bid from Energy Transfer Equity.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Williams Raises Its Bid for Southern Union to $5.5 Billion', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Energy Transfer Equity LP', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Southern Union Company', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Williams Cos Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T13:00:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/065fe689-27a3-5225-ac0f-0f0bc2f3dbea', 'word_count': 345, 'uri': 'nyt://article/065fe689-27a3-5225-ac0f-0f0bc2f3dbea'}, {'abstract': 'The 20-year-old amateur Tom Lewis was tied with the veteran Thomas Bjorn at 65 after the first round of the British Open.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/sports/golf/2011-british-open-star-crossed-bjorn-takes-early-lead.html', 'snippet': 'The 20-year-old amateur Tom Lewis was tied with the veteran Thomas Bjorn at 65 after the first round of the British Open.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SANDWICH, England — The arc of European Tour dominance in major championship golf, which began at the 2010 United States Open with the surprise victory by Northern Ireland’s Graeme McDowell, did not merely continue Thursday in the first round of the British Open at Royal St. George’s. It also got younger.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/sports/OPEN1/OPEN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 363, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/15/sports/OPEN1/OPEN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 363}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/sports/OPEN1/OPEN1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 621, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/sports/OPEN1/OPEN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/15/sports/OPEN1/OPEN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'English Amateur Secures Share of Lead With a 65', 'kicker': 'British Open | Royal St. Georges', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'English Amateur Secures Share of Lead With a 65', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'England', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'British Open (Golf)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bjorn, Thomas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jimenez, Miguel Angel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McIlroy, Rory', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lewis, Tom', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T13:06:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'ori