 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6219ad1a-a680-57c9-96a4-09eb730c607f', 'word_count': 188, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6219ad1a-a680-57c9-96a4-09eb730c607f'}, {'abstract': 'A silversmith who worked for Tiffany’s makes exquisite use of his skills with a new jewelry line called American Estate.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/natural-splendor/', 'snippet': 'A silversmith who worked for Tiffany’s makes exquisite use of his skills with a new jewelry line called American Estate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Known for transforming ordinary tabletops into shinier talking points with his bas-relief-esque goblets, pitchers and trays, Michael Galmer of Galmer Silversmiths in Long Island City, Queens, has always believed that silver can be as polished a metal as any. “It’s very dynamic,” says Galmer, who has three decades of experience and a number of special projects for Tiffany & Company under his belt. “I was always in love with it.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Natural Splendor', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tiffany & Company', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T14:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65480277-a05a-53b3-843f-4d984d7885d8', 'word_count': 213, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65480277-a05a-53b3-843f-4d984d7885d8'}, {'abstract': 'A new report on college grade inflation finds that about 43 percent of all letter grades given are A’s, an increase of 28 percentage points since 1960 and 12 percentage points since 1988.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/the-history-of-college-grade-inflation/', 'snippet': 'A new report on college grade inflation finds that about 43 percent of all letter grades given are A’s, an increase of 28 percentage points since 1960 and 12 percentage points since 1988.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We’ve written before about some of the work of Stuart Rojstaczer and Christopher Healy, grade inflation chroniclers extraordinaire. They have put together a new, comprehensive study of college grading over the decades, and let me tell you, it is a doozy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A History of College Grade Inflation', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grading of Students', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T14:00:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ac2d8e0-562c-5571-a720-750a8647e6ba', 'word_count': 568, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ac2d8e0-562c-5571-a720-750a8647e6ba'}, {'abstract': 'Politicians are using redistricting battles to advance their own agendas — ones that often have nothing to do with Latino representation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/us/15redistrict.html', 'snippet': 'Politicians are using redistricting battles to advance their own agendas — ones that often have nothing to do with Latino representation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAS VEGAS — The population of Latinos has exploded here, and they want their voices heard not just in the halls of schools like Clark High or on the growing number of Spanish-language radio stations, but also in Congress.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/01/us/1redistrict_span/1redistrict_span-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 353, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/08/01/us/1redistrict_span/1redistrict_span-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 353}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/01/us/1redistrict_span/1redistrict_span-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/01/us/1redistrict_span/1redistrict_span-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/08/01/us/1redistrict_span/1redistrict_span-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Faces, New Maps, New Battles', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Faces, New Maps, New Battles', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Redistricting and Reapportionment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Census', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name'