es Sarah Lyall and Alan Cowell report, Rupert Murdoch and his son James both reluctantly agreed to testify next week before a British parliamentary committee investigating phone hacking at newspapers owned by their News Corporation, after this post was originally published. The decision came after the two men initially refused an invitation to attend an oversight committee hearing, and Parliament then took the extraordinary step of issuing a summons to order them to appear.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Confusion Over Parliament’s Power to Compel Murdochs to Testify', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wiretapping and Other Eavesdropping Devices and Methods', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brooks, Rebekah', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, James R', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NEWS CORP', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T15:01:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68c762f4-634c-5a82-9df3-db6a0b5bb2a0', 'word_count': 1625, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68c762f4-634c-5a82-9df3-db6a0b5bb2a0'}, {'abstract': 'It feels like the nominators are congratulating themselves for their good taste in liking the show. The most deserving of the four, Ty Burrell, is probably the least likely to win.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/psychodrama-in-the-comedy-category/', 'snippet': 'It feels like the nominators are congratulating themselves for their good taste in liking the show. The most deserving of the four, Ty Burrell, is probably the least likely to win.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the strange bedfellows department: Louis C.K. and Matt LeBlanc, fellow nominees for lead actor in a comedy. I don’t begrudge Mr. LeBlanc — “Episodes” wasn’t nearly as funny or interesting as it should have been, but he was the best thing about it, and he showed some real wit in his approach to playing himself, or someone sort of like him.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Psychodrama in the Comedy Category', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emmy Awards', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lynch, Jane', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Offerman, Nick', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stonestreet, Eric', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'White, Betty', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T15:01:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Hale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff0058e8-5ff9-5778-95c7-e044efe1fbcc', 'word_count': 332, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff0058e8-5ff9-5778-95c7-e044efe1fbcc'}, {'abstract': 'Steve Bartlett, the head of the Financial Services Roundtable, has played a pivotal role in lobbyists’ efforts to delay or water down financial regulatory changes.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/07