tum behind Steve Buscemi, who worked very hard to give some life to the lead character among the cardboard cast of “Boardwalk Empire.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Closer Look at the Acting Categories', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emmy Awards', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T15:40:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Hale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f021e0af-b1c9-5ace-bf73-a82fa36475c3', 'word_count': 266, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f021e0af-b1c9-5ace-bf73-a82fa36475c3'}, {'abstract': 'Nostylgia sells stylish clothes, coffee, tea and the pleasures of a gentler era amid an atmosphere of anything-goes eclecticism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/17/nyregion/at-nostylgia-in-inwood-a-spot-to-shop-sip-tea-or-hang-out.html', 'snippet': 'Nostylgia sells stylish clothes, coffee, tea and the pleasures of a gentler era amid an atmosphere of anything-goes eclecticism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ON summer evenings, a tree-lined strip of Dyckman Street — a main thoroughfare in Inwood, near Manhattan’s northern prow — becomes a giant block party. Crowds from several splashy bars spill out onto the sidewalk, clutching beers and cigarettes as they chatter loudly and peck away on their smartphones.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/nyregion/17JOINT1/17JOINT1-articleLarge.jpg',