y-of-the-bike/', 'snippet': 'About to begin a cross-country cycling trip, Bruce Weber describes his new baby: a red, custom-built, lightweight bike.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A bicyclist not in possession of his bicycle is at sixes and sevens. Mine, after only about 65 miles of test driving here in New York City, is now winging its way, via FedEx, to Portland, Ore., where I’ll pick it up on Monday for the trip home. (Cost of shipping: $180.) In the meantime, like any bereft parent missing a child, I can tell you about it. (You can read about my previous cross-country bike ride, and why I am going to cycle across the country again, in my recent story in the Travel section.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Life Is a Wheel: The Story of the Bike', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bicycles and Bicycling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oregon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T15:41:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Weber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e42284d3-c2c1-5947-be45-e77ecc754318', 'word_count': 766, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e42284d3-c2c1-5947-be45-e77ecc754318'}, {'abstract': 'The brand’s high-performance midsize coupe and convertible are losing their V-8 in favor of a supercharged V-6.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/audi-a5-sheds-two-cylinders-in-midcycle-refresh/', 'snippet': 'The brand’s high-perform