oon.html', 'snippet': 'Alpha males may hold power and attract females, but a study of baboon troops in Kenya shows they also have very high levels of stress.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At last, good news for the beta male.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/us/15baboon_337/15baboon_337-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/us/15baboon_337/15baboon_337-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/15/us/15baboon_337/15baboon_337-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Baboon Study Shows Benefits for Nice Guys, Who Finish 2nd', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Baboon Study Shows Benefits For Nice Guys, Who Finish 2nd', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monkeys and Apes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biology and Biochemistry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T18:01:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Gorman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gorman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/032dec1c-0367-545f-99bf-9f0cb01375b1', 'word_count': 843, 'uri': 'nyt://article/032dec1c-0367-545f-99bf-9f0cb01375b1'}, {'abstract': 'Harvard researchers devised a method for making hundreds of changes in the bacterium’s genome simultaneously, paving the way to replace the deleted genetic function with another.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/health/15genome.html', 'snippet': 'Harvard researchers devised a method for making hundreds of changes in the bacterium’s genome simultaneously, paving the way to replace the deleted genetic function with another.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Synthetic biology, the quest to hijack living systems and convert them to human-directed goals, is on the march. Last year biologists synthesized the entire genome of a small bacterium and showed how it could successfully infect a second bacterium. Now, in what may be a more significant advance, biologists have shown they can radically change a genome, not just copy it.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Genetic Code of E. Coli Is Hijacked by Biologists', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Genetic Code of E. Coli Is Hijacked by Biologists', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetics and Heredity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DNA (Deoxyribonucleic Acid)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bacteria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Synthetic Biology', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Microbiology', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T18:01:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Wade', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wade', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7594b4f-49f4-59be-b9ea-99dbc2c2d3a7', 'word_count': 1074, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7594b4f-49f4-59be-b9ea-99dbc2c2d3a7'}, {'abstract': 'On a rainy day with a group of Chechen refugees in Georgia, Daro Sulakauri sensed a moment coming. So she got close.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/too-close-for-comfort/', 'snippet': 'On a rainy day with a group of Chechen refugees in Georgia, Daro Sulakauri sensed a moment coming. So she got close.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Daro Sulakauri , 26, is a freelance photographer in Tbilisi, Georgia. She graduated from the International Center of Photography in 2006. She was chosen by Photo District News as one 30 new and emerging photographers to watch in 2011. Her conversation with Kerri MacDonald for the Turning Point series has been edited and condensed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Too Close for Comfort', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Capa, Robert', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Magnum Photos', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia (Georgian Republic)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T18:08:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kerri MacDonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kerri', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacDonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62703bcc-66a6-54d6-a5be-ff72a5ec455d', 'word_count': 433, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62703bcc-66a6-54d6-a5be-ff72a5ec455d'}, {'abstract': 'Another reason to visit the beautiful Balearic island of Mallorca: the opening of a new restaurant by the Englishman Marc Fosh.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/eurofile-where-europe-eats-on-vacation/', 'snippet': 'Another reason to visit the beautiful Balearic island of Mallorca: the opening of a new restaurant by the Englishman Marc Fosh.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The beautiful Balearic island of Mallorca is Europe’s Florida, a one-size-fits-all holiday destination par excellence. Scan the arrival boards at Palma’s Son Sant Joan airport, one of the busiest in Europe, and almost no major European city goes missing, which means Mallorca is the perfect place to see what Europeans like to eat on vacation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Eurofile | Misa Braseria', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T18:08:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexander Lobrano', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexander', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lobrano', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f0be31e-77d4-550a-97dd-45c726e60ce5', 'word_count': 901, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f0be31e-77d4-550a-97dd-45c726e60ce5'}, {'abstract': 'The Times\'s fitness guinea pig, Karen Barrow, tries a Figure 4 barre workout. For more Gym Class videos, go to <a href="http://well.blogs.nytimes.com/tag/gym-class/">nytimes.com/well</a>.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/science/100000000897855/gym-class-the-barre-workout.html', 'snippet': 'The Times\'s fitness guinea pig, Karen Barrow, tries a Figure 4 barre workout. For more Gym Class videos, go to <a href="http://well.blogs.nytimes.com/tag/gym-class/">nytimes.com/well</a>.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Times\'s fitness guinea pig, Karen Barrow, tries a Figure 4 barre workout. For more Gym Class videos, go to <a href="http://well.blogs.nytimes.com/tag/gym-class/">nytimes.com/well</a>.', 'sourc