ty things Wednesday night. Jet lag, which had been crouching in corners since I arrived last weekend, finally decided to leap out and smack me around. And that double martini at lunch probably hadn’t been a good idea. By 7:30 all I really wanted was to stay at home, horizontal, and watch something silly, trashy, a tad shameful – maybe a vintage 1980s Britcom on one of those recycling channels where they advertise miracle diet pills.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'London Theater Journal: A ‘Much Ado’ With Dr. Who', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shakespeare, William', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T18:28:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e2f19c5-55b5-56e3-b18d-cf9d2bb440ea', 'word_count': 746, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e2f19c5-55b5-56e3-b18d-cf9d2bb440ea'}, {'abstract': 'N.Y. See: After a windswept storm pummeled the city, a magnificent rainbow appeared.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/whitestone-bridge-bronx-741-p-m-wednesday/', 'snippet': 'N.Y. See: After a windswept storm pummeled the city, a magnificent rainbow appeared.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Whitestone Bridge, Bronx, 7:41 P.M. Wednesday', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subjec