4T18:43:43+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Blogs', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/d0117e15-ccfd-5854-a95e-eafbed2313a7', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/d0117e15-ccfd-5854-a95e-eafbed2313a7'}, {'abstract': 'A German billionaire has paid more than 50 million euros ($70 million) to buy an oil painting of the Madonna by Hans Holbein the Younger, Bloomberg News reported.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/holbein-sells-for-more-than-70-million-says-dealer/', 'snippet': 'A German billionaire has paid more than 50 million euros ($70 million) to buy an oil painting of the Madonna by Hans Holbein the Younger, Bloomberg News reported.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A German billionaire has paid more than 50 million euros ($70 million) to buy an oil painting of the Madonna by Hans Holbein the Younger, Bloomberg News reported. Reinhold Wuerth, a manufacturer of screws and other industrial hardware, bought the painting from the heirs of the princes and landgraves of the state of Hesse, according to an e-mailed statement sent Thursday by Britta Fischer Public Relations on behalf of the Wuerth Collection, Bloomberg reported. The Staedel Museum, where the painting has been displayed since 2003 on long-term loan, said in a statement that it had tried to buy the work itself, but that its offer of 40 million euros ($57 million) was rejected. Christoph Graf Douglas, the art dealer who handled the sale, would not give the final purchase price but said it was more than 50 million euros. The painting, “The Madonna With the Family of Mayor Meyer,” from 1525-28, depicts the mayor of Basel’s family–to whom it belonged for nearly 100 years–at the feet of the Madonna. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Holbein Sells for More Than $70 Million, Says Dealer', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holbein, Hans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T19:00:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicia R. Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicia', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/690768c5-4295-5acd-b5d7-2bdd55009464', 'word_count': 172, 'uri': 'nyt://article/690768c5-4295-5acd-b5d7-2bdd55009464'}, {'abstract': 'Photos of “Cats,” “The Phantom of the Opera” and other shows.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/07/17/theater/20110717-webber.html', 'snippet': 'Photos of “Cats,” “The Phantom of the Opera” and other shows.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photos of “Cats,” “The Phantom of the Opera” and other shows.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/theater/20110717-webber-slide-PILR/20110717-webber-slide-PILR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/theater/20110717-webber-slide-PILR/20110717-webber-slide-PILR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/17/theater/20110717-webber-slide-PILR/20110717-webber-slide-PILR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Musicals of Andrew Lloyd Webber', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lloyd Webber, Andrew', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T19:03:35+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Theater', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/a3d210f0-1971-57a1-ac72-459e8cec96bb', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/a3d210f0-1971-57a1-ac72-459e8cec96bb'}, {'abstract': 'Alberto Contador, the defending champion of the Tour de France, was visibly struggling in the last of three stiff climbs in the 12th stage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/sports/cycling/15iht-bike15.html', 'snippet': 'Alberto Contador, the defending champion of the Tour de France, was visibly struggling in the last of three stiff climbs in the 12th stage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LUZ-ARDIDEN, France — Alberto Contador, the defending champion of the Tour de France, lost precious time to his main rivals Thursday in a grueling stage in which he had been expected to begin a long-awaited push. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/sports/tour/tour-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 352, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/15/sports/tour/tour-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 352}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/sports/tour/tour-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/sports/tour/tour-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/15/sports/tour/tour-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Contador Fades at End of Grueling Stage and Loses Time to Top Rivals', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Contador Fades at the End of a Grueling Stage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Contador, Alberto', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tour de France (Bicycle Race)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bicycles and Bicycling', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanchez, Samuel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Voeckler, Thomas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T19:09:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Cycling', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Pfanner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pfanner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/961fc109-65ff-58c9-8036-4625ce488902', 'word_count': 643, 'uri': 'nyt://article/961fc109-65ff-58c9-8036-4625ce488902'}, {'abstract': 'Andrew Lloyd Webber has long been a hands-on theater creator and producer, but lately, after a battle with cancer, he has been more content to let others interpret his work.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/17/theater/andrew-lloyd-webber-and-wizard-of-oz.html', 'snippet': 'Andrew Lloyd Webber has long been a hands-on theater creator and producer, but lately, after a battle with cancer, he has been more content to let others interpret his work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON -- Andrew Lloyd Webber has earned seven Tony Awards, a knighthood and hundreds of millions of dollars for writing some of the most popular musicals of all time, from his 1968 breakthrough, “Joseph and the Amazing Technicolor Dreamcoat,” to “The Phantom of the Opera,” the longest-running show ever on Broadway. Nearly as legendary is his ego, a self-confidence worthy of an impresario whose success has long emboldened him to think on grand scales.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/arts/WEBER-2/WEBER-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 610, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/arts/WEBER-2/WEBER-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/17/arts/WEBER-2/WEBER-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lloyd Webber’s Latest Creation: Breathing Space', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lloyd Webber’s Latest Creation: Breathing Space', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lloyd Webber, Andrew', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T19:10:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/149ecc90-eb2c-5580-a0c7-cd9a29b70cce', 'word_count': 1689, 'uri': 'nyt://article/149ecc90-eb2c-5580-a0c7-cd9a29b70cce'}, {'abstract': 'The comedian and star of the FX series “Louie” says the distinction “feels like, hopefully, you’ve got a ladder underneath you, rather than a frayed rope and a chasm.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/louis-c-k-learns-to-appreciate-an-emmy-nomination/', 'snippet': 'The comedian and star of the FX series “Louie” says the distinction “feels like, hopefully, you’ve got a ladder underneath you, rather than a frayed rope and a chasm.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'We anticipated that Louis C. K. might react to the news that he’d been nominated for an Emmy (as lead actor in his FX comedy series, “Louie”) the same way that a timid audience member might react to his so-honest-till-you-can’t-take-it-anymore standup performances: by covering his eyes and hanging his head in shame.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Louis C. K. Learns to Appreciate an Emmy Nomination', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emmy Awards', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'C K, Louis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T19:20:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9f09aa9-3c7d-5b68-8a18-e7e7b8ba4843', 'word_count': 442, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9f09aa9-3c7d-5b68-8a18-e7e7b8ba4843'}, {'abstract': 'The Italian Senate rushed through approval of a deficit-cutting austerity package on Thursday in an effort to fend off a sovereign debt crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/world/europe/15italy.html', 'snippet': 'The Italian Senate rushed through approval of a deficit-cutting austerity package on Thursday in an effort to fend off a sovereign debt crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — Even as the Italian Senate rushed through approval of a deficit-cutting austerity package on Thursday to fend off a sovereign debt crisis, doubts were growing about the staying power of the government of Prime Minister Silvio Berlusconi. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Italy to Adopt Austerity Plan to Fend Off a Debt Crisis', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Italy to Adopt Austerity Plan To Fend Off A Debt Crisis', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berlusconi, Silvio', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "D'Alema, Massimo", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bersani, Pierluigi', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T19:23:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Donadio', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Donadio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebaa3779-8eac-52ee-9b8a-616991aebb03', 'word_count': 726, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebaa3779-8eac-52ee-9b8a-616991aebb03'}, {'abstract': 'Sarah Palin’s political action committee raised $1.65 million in the first six months of 2011 and spent about the same amount.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/palin-p-a-c-releases-fund-raising-numbers/', 'snippet': 'Sarah Palin’s political action committee raised $1.65 million in the first six months of 2011 and spent about the same amount.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sarah Palin‘s political action committee raised $1.65 million in the first six months of 2011 and spent about the same amount, the PAC reported on Thursday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Palin PAC Raised $1.7 Million in First Half of ’11', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Palin, Sarah', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALASKA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T19:28:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b231f36-4809-529d-aed5-2d4977c1a4cc', 'word_count': 215, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b231f36-4809-529d-aed5-2d4977c1a4cc'}, {'abstract': 'Some resort towns get trendier over the years, but Bar Harbor — a delightful base from which to bike, hike and sail around Maine’s Mount Desert Island — feels deliciously frozen in time.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/17/travel/36-hours-in-bar-harbor.html', 'snippet': 'Some resort towns get trendier over the years, but Bar Harbor — a delightful base from which to bike, hike and sail around Maine’s Mount Desert Island — feels deliciously frozen in time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THERE are summer resorts that get busier and more chic over the years. And then there are the ones, like Bar Harbor, Me., that feel deliciously frozen in time. Don’t look for Starbucks, McDonald’s or Ralph Lauren here. Fashion shoppers stop at places with names like Cool as a Moose. Carmen Verandah and the Thirsty Whale are among the evening hot spots. Bar Harbor is the largest town on Mount Desert Island, and nearby Acadia National Park encompasses some 50 square miles. The rest of Mount Desert belongs to residents and a tony array of summer tenants: Brooke Astor summered here, as did myriad Rockefellers and, once upon a time, the town of Northeast Harbor had so many Philadelphia families that it was dubbed “Philadelphia on the rocks.” They all came lured by the striking setting of mountains, woodlands, lakes and ocean waves crashing against granite cliffs. Then and now, Mount Desert has served as a glorious nature camp for biking, hiking and boating. At day’s end, a visitor can cozy up with a blueberry beer and lobster. Evening strollers can watch sailboats drop anchor and the mist slip down over the hundreds of islands that dot the water.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/travel/17hours_span/17hours_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 225, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/17/travel/17hours_span/17hours_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 225}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/travel/17hours_span/17hours_span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 225, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/travel/17hours_span/17hours_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/17/travel/17hours_span/17hours_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '36 Hours in Bar Harbor, Me.', 'kicker': '36 Hours', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bar Harbor, Me.', '