: 486, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8bd12aa-9f1f-576e-9604-f35e8748a8a9'}, {'abstract': 'Trailer for "The Future" starring Miranda July.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/magazine/100000000946001/the-future.html', 'snippet': 'Trailer for "The Future" starring Miranda July.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Trailer for "The Future" starring Miranda July.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/14/magazine/video-17july-trailer/video-17july-trailer-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/14/magazine/video-17july-trailer/video-17july-trailer-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/14/magazine/video-17july-trailer/video-17july-trailer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/14/magazine/video-17july-trailer/video-17july-trailer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Trailer for "The Future"', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T19:38:07+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'Roadside Attractions', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roadside', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Attractions', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/5bd96938-79ad-5ac9-8ca4-eef41c711192', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/5bd96938-79ad-5ac9-8ca4-eef41c711192'}, {'abstract': 'Turns out shorter announcements at 59th Street-Columbus Circle subway station are not the doing of some M.T.A. lawyer, but an effort to stop announcements from overlapping at the busy station.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/a-pile-up-of-public-service-messages-in-the-subway/', 'snippet': 'Turns out shorter announcements at 59th Street-Columbus Circle subway station are not the doing of some M.T.A. lawyer, but an effort to stop announcements from overlapping at the busy station.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It wasn’t my imagination after all. Train announcements at 59th Street-Columbus Circle were so plentiful, audible and detailed — be careful what you wish for, as we are ever reminded —that it seemed at times as if they never ended. No more rumble of a subway train; a trip underground had become a nonstop serenade by the voice of Carolyn Hopkins: “Ladies and gentlemen, the next Brooklyn-bound local train is now arriving. Please stand away from the platform edge, especially when trains are entering and leaving the station.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Pile-Up of Public Service Messages in the Subway', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subways', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Transit Authority', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T19:39:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Dunlap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Dunlap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/672501cf-2355-5f44-a800-5b8c55dd80ff', 'word_count': 320, 'uri': 'nyt://article/672501cf-2355-5f44-a800-5b8c55dd80ff'}, {'abstract': 'Borough President Rubén Díaz Jr. is asking the federal government to stop the mayor’s plan for converting a former military base into a shelter to be run by Doe Foundation.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/city-hall-accused-of-steamrolling-opposition-to-bronx-shelter/', 'snippet': 'Borough President Rubén Díaz Jr. is asking the federal government to stop the mayor’s plan for converting a former military base into a shelter to be run by Doe Foundation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 5:49 p.m. | The Bronx borough president, Rubén Díaz Jr., accused the Bloomberg administration of lying to him and misleading the federal government in order to place a homeless shelter in a former military base in the Wakefield section.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'City Hall Accused of Steamrolling Opposition to Bronx Shelter', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Military Bases and Installations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Diaz, Ruben Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'WAKEFIELD (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T19:46:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Boryga', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Boryga', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f74be7a-e808-5e0e-afe1-79d09f7bef4b', 'word_count': 623, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f74be7a-e808-5e0e-afe1-79d09f7bef4b'}, {'abstract': 'The networks finish in a virtual tie for first place in the ratings.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/photo-finish-for-nbc-and-cbs/', 'snippet': 'The networks finish in a virtual tie for first place in the ratings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A game show, a talent show and a dating show lifted NBC into a virtual tie for first place with CBS in the ratings on Wednesday night as NBC drew about as many viewers on average as CBS’s lineup of “Big Brother” and crime show reruns. According to Nielsen’s estimates, NBC’s reality competition “America’s Got Talent” earned the night’s largest audience with 11 million viewers at 9 p.m., but the network lagged behind CBS the rest of the night as “Minute to Win It” garnered just 4.8 million at 8 and “Love in the Wild” drew 5.1 million at 10.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Photo Finish for NBC and CBS', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC INC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nielsen Media Research', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T19:50:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Toff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Toff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b1262ff-7142-5450-ad89-5962bbe4382a', 'word_count': 167, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b1262ff-7142-5450-ad89-5962bbe4382a'}, {'abstract': 'Some ventures cook coal into a gas and then sequester it; one may sell its carbon dioxide to oil drillers who use it to force petroleum to the surface.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/scattered-attempts-at-carbon-capture/', 'snippet': 'Some ventures cook coal into a gas and then sequester it; one may sell its carbon dioxide to oil drillers who use it to force petroleum to the surface.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As my colleague John Broder and I reported in Thursday’s paper, American Electric Power is dropping its plan to build a commercial-scale version of a carbon dioxide scrubber at Mountaineer, its coal-fired power plant in New Haven, W.Va. The company decided that since public service commissions in West Virginia and Virginia had refused to give it full reimbursement for a pilot version that it ran for two years, it could not expect to recover its investment for the full-scale version — even if the Energy Department was going to pony up $334 million, or half the cost.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Scattered Attempts at Carbon Capture', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carbon Dioxide', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coal', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ALSTOM', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Electric Power Co Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARCHER-DANIELS-MIDLAND CO', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Energy Department', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Southern Company', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Illinois', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Louisiana', 'ran