-options-to-keep-angelenos-moving/', 'snippet': 'Various services are stepping into the void left by the freeway’s closing to move Los Angeles County residents along.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This weekend, Los Angeles residents face a 53-hour closing of the 405 freeway, the primary north-south highway through the city’s West Side, as road crews take a sledgehammer to the Mulholland Drive bridge. The planned work threatens to clog surface streets near the Interstate, leading many Angelenos to call the impending amalgam of bottlenecks, honked horns and frayed nerves Carmageddon.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The 405 Closing: a Myriad of Options to Keep Angelenos Moving', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roads and Traffic', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JetBlue Airways', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Police Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T19:57:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Schultz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schultz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/11d4eaac-7922-5454-b8e8-d978bf500169', 'word_count': 320, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11d4eaac-7922-5454-b8e8-d978bf500169'}, {'abstract': "Anthony Tommasini discusses the New York City Opera's departure from Lincoln Center and Harry Potter hysteria has its own rock 'n' roll genre.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/arts/100000000945883/artsbeat-july-14-2011.html', 'snippet': "Anthony Tommasini discusses the New York City Opera's departure from Lincoln Center and Harry Potter hysteria has its own rock 'n' roll genre.", 'lead_paragraph': "Anthony Tommasini discusses the New York City Opera's departure from Lincoln Center and Harry Potter hysteria has its own rock 'n' roll genre.", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/14/arts/video-ab-07142011/video-ab-07142011-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/14/arts/video-ab-07142011/video-ab-07142011-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/14/arts/video-ab-07142011/video-ab-07142011-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/14/arts/video-ab-07142011/video-ab-07142011-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Artsbeat-July 14, 2011', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T19:58:52+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'Gabe Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gabe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/619cbca9-bcca-5aa5-a830-1fe54c564391', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/619cbca9-bcca-5aa5-a830-1fe54c564391'}, {'abstract': 'Asked by the Times to attend one of the first United States performances of Alexei Ratmansky’s “Anna Karenina,” by Russia’s Mariinsky Ballet \xad I agreed, with nagging reservations.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/a-book-critic-at-the-ballet/', 'snippet': 'Asked by the Times to attend one of the first United States performances of Alexei Ratmansky’s “Anna Karenina,” by Russia’s Mariinsky Ballet \xad I agreed, with nagging reservations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few years ago, The Guardian had the witty idea to ask its sports writers and cultural critics to swap jobs for a day. The results were delightful. An observation from the newspaper’s rugby columnist, Thomas Castalgnede, sent to review a production of “Tosca” at the Royal Opera House, has stuck with me. “What I saw in ‘Tosca’ was exactly what drew me to sport,” he wrote. “I just love to watch people give it everything — in any walk of life.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Book Critic at the Ballet', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ratmansky, Alexei', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mariinsky Ballet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T20:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dwight Garner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dwight', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/351d0fab-6aaf-5882-9810-777120b98143', 'word_count': 534, 'uri': 'nyt://article/351d0fab-6aaf-5882-9810-777120b98143'}, {'abstract': 'A look at competing versions of what happened between Preside