-with-helen-mirren.html', 'snippet': 'With an American version of “Prime Suspect” beginning on NBC in the fall, Alessandra Stanley says now is the time to revisit the British TV series of the same title, starring Helen Mirren.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The pursuit of happiness is relentless on American television. Even the most willful, irascible loners find true love in the end. Brenda, the bossy and single-minded homicide detective played by Kyra Sedgwick on “The Closer,” got married. Mary, the misanthropic United States Marshal played by Mary McCormack on “In Plain Sight,” is expecting a baby. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/STANLEY/STANLEY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 367, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/STANLEY/STANLEY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 367}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/STANLEY/STANLEY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 759, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/STANLEY/STANLEY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/STANLEY/STANLEY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Prime Suspect’: Returning to the Source', 'kicker': 'The Hot List | Television', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Prime Suspect’: Returning to the Source', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Public Broadcasting Service', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'British Broadcasting Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bello, Maria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mirren, Helen', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T22:05:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alessandra Stanley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alessandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stanley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/01ea05da-f9b8-55ae-bf39-d69a57628fc2', 'word_count': 363, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01ea05da-f9b8-55ae-bf39-d69a57628fc2'}, {'abstract': 'Charles Isherwood on the artistry and unfettered imagination of “Alexander McQueen: Savage Beauty,” at the Metropolitan Museum.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/theater/theatrical-beauty-in-alexander-mcqueen-savage-beauty.html', 'snippet': 'Charles Isherwood on the artistry and unfettered imagination of “Alexander McQueen: Savage Beauty,” at the Metropolitan Museum.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Although summer is considered the off season for New York theater, there’s always plenty to see from Memorial Day to Labor Day. “Hair” is back, swinging its free-loving tresses on Broadway, where Maria Callas is also giving life lessons courtesy of Terrence McNally and Tyne Daly in “Master Class.” Visiting Britons from the Royal Shakespeare Company are mounting five full-scale productions at the Park Avenue Armory. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/ISHERWOOD/ISHERWOOD-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/ISHERWOOD/ISHERWOOD-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/ISHERWOOD/ISHERWOOD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 725, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/ISHERWOOD/ISHERWOOD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/ISHERWOOD/ISHERWOOD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Intense Drama, Via the Catwalk', 'kicker': 'The Hot List | Theater', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Intense Drama, Via the Catwalk', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Museum of Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T22:10:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Isherwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isherwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5a45fc4-e5d7-5de4-a514-fd4b4c892564', 'word_count': 333, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5a45fc4-e5d7-5de4-a514-fd4b4c892564'}, {'abstract': 'Allan Kozinn on the stimulating Festival of Contemporary Music, with performances by guests artists from the new-music world and students and faculty members of the Tanglewood Music Center.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/arts/music/festival-of-contemporary-music-at-tanglewood.html', 'snippet': 'Allan Kozinn on the stimulating Festival of Contemporary Music, with performances by guests artists from the new-music world and students and faculty members of the Tanglewood Music Center.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I try never to let a summer go by without spending some quality time at Tanglewood. But as much as I enjoy the atmosphere (and most times, the performances) at the Boston Symphony’s weekend concerts at the Koussevitzky Music Shed, for me the most stimulating programming is the annual Festival of Contemporary Music, now held at Seiji Ozawa Hall. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/15kozinn/15kozinn-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/15kozinn/15kozinn-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/15kozinn/15kozinn-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 702, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/15kozinn/15kozinn-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/15kozinn/15kozinn-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Festival With a Lot of Wiggle Room', 'kicker': 'The Hot List | Music', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Festival With a Lot of Wiggle Room', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tanglewood Music Festival (Lenox, Mass)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Symphony Orchestra', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T22:12:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/13d47a07-85d0-5ed4-bde2-e70b0ddd5161', 'word_count': 282, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13d47a07-85d0-5ed4-bde2-e70b0ddd5161'}, {'abstract': 'Trying to dissect claims that either party to the debt ceilings negotiations could benefit from a default.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/nobody-wins-the-debt-default-blame-game/', 'snippet': 'Trying to dissect claims that either party to the debt ceilings negotiations could benefit from a default.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The chances of a default on the United States debt are still fairly small. The prices for credit default swaps, financial instruments that pay investors in the event that a default happens, imply just a 0.05 percent chance, or 1-in-2,000, of a default occurring within the next year, according to The Wall Street Journal.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nobody Wins the Debt Default Blame Game', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T22:13:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f4247ce-26df-5f5f-9f49-a6fb74508952', 'word_count': 1155, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f4247ce-26df-5f5f-9f49-a6fb74508952'}, {'abstract': 'Jon Caramanica writes that while listening to music in his care on his commute, the destination doesn’t matter as much as the song.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/arts/music/jon-caramanicas-driving-music.html', 'snippet': 'Jon Caramanica writes that while listening to music in his care on his commute, the destination doesn’t matter as much as the song.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Get me to my car, stat. Windows down. Sun roof back. Radio blaring, damaging the already tender speakers. It’s where music sounds best, where a new song jumping out of the radio can be enough to put nearby drivers at risk. Two a.m., F.D.R. Drive, “Make It Rain” bouncing off the car frame — that’s when things make sense. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/CARAMANICA/CARAMANICA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/CARAMANICA/CARAMANICA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/CARAMANICA/CARAMANICA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 670, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/CARAMANICA/CARAMANICA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/CARAMANICA/CARAMANICA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Riding in Cars With Music', 'kicker': 'The Hot List | Music', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Riding in Cars With Music', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radio', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'SHEEPSHEAD BAY (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T22:15:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bebc7301-124b-5bd1-b655-bbcc97d5879a', 'word_count': 322, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bebc7301-124b-5bd1-b655-bbcc97d5879a'}, {'abstract': 'The league laid off 11 percent of its work force in a move that it says was not directly related to the lockout.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/sports/basketball/nba-lays-off-11-percent-of-staff.html', 'snippet': 'The league laid off 11 percent of its work force in a move that it says was not directly related to the lockout.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than 100 N.B.A. employees were laid off this week, heightening the sense of economic distress as the league’s owners and players haggle over a new labor agreement.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'N.B.A. Lays Off 11 Percent of Workers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'N.B.A.’s Twin Realities: Lockout and Layoffs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stern, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lockouts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T22:16:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Howard Beck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Howard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/384ad72f-be55-5e75-b2f6-d98bb1e2dd1a', 'word_count': 613, 'uri': 'nyt://article/384ad72f-be55-5e75-b2f6-d98bb1e2dd1a'}, {'abstract': 'Summer may (finally) provide a few hours for an old inspiration: the nonlinear, anti-rational “Zazie Dans le Métro,” Louis Malle’s film from 1960.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/movies/a-o-scott-on-the-1960-film-zazie-dans-le-metro.html', 'snippet': 'Summer may (finally) provide a few hours for an old inspiration: the nonlinear, anti-rational “Zazie Dans le Métro,” Louis Malle’s film from 1960.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the perks of my job is that I get a lot of free DVDs in the mail, and one of the frustrations is that there is never enough time to watch them. This summer, though, I am determined to find a few hours for “Zazie Dans le Métro.” This 1960 Louis Malle film, released by the Criterion Collection in June, is one of the movies that made me who I am today.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/SCOTT/SCOTT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/SCOTT/SCOTT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/SCOTT/SCOTT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 834, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/SCOTT/SCOTT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/SCOTT/SCOTT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Few Hours for the Best of Youth', 'kicker': 'The Hot List | Film', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Few Hours for the Best of Youth', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Malle, Louis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Criterion Collection', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T22:17:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/61ea1308-82ef-5ec5-a0bc-e08c1cf3ddef', 'word_count': 372, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61ea1308-82ef-5ec5-a0bc-e08c1cf3ddef'}, {'abstract': 'Dwight Garner revisits “Hooked,” the ninth collection of Pauline Kael’s film reviews from The New Yorker.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/books/pauline-kaels-hooked-a-worthy-beach-read.html', 'snippet': 'Dwight Garner revisits “Hooked,” the ninth collection of Pauline Kael’s film reviews from The New Yorker.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pauline Kael died 10 years ago this summer, only a few days before 9/11; most remembrances of her were lost in the haze and fury. I’ve been thinking about Kael a lot recently, missing her bawdy and crackling voice, wondering what she’d say if she were alive to weigh in on, say, “Black Swan” or “The Social Network.” (I suspect she’d have smacked both around, while finding things to enjoy about David Fincher and Aaron Sorkin’s work in the Facebook movie.) ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/15garner/15garner-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 755, 'width': 567, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/15garner/15garner-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/15garner/15garner-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Great Guide (Apologies to Its Author)', 'kicker': 'The Hot List | Books', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Great Guide (Apologies to Its Author)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T22:19:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dwight Garner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dwight', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/39526f23-3a5e-56d4-9333-0b495a7bd29c', 'word_count': 391, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39526f23-3a5e-56d4-9333-0b495a7bd29c'}, {'abstract': 'John Kerry knows as well as anyone that diplomacy fails most of the time. But someone has to go to Islamabad.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/17/magazine/john-kerry-our-man-in-kabul.html', 'snippet': 'John Kerry knows as well as anyone that diplomacy fails most of the time. But someone has to go to Islamabad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'John Kerry surprised a lot of people when he endorsed Barack Obama for president in early 2008. Kerry was a longtime friend of Obama’s chief rival, Hillary Clinton. He had served in the Senate for a quarter-century and had built a reputation as a cautious, incremental figure — like Clinton herself. But for Kerry the time had come for a decisive break with the past. “I felt very strongly we needed a new narrative for the country,” he told me during a long conversation last fall.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/magazine/17kerry3_span/17kerry3_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/17/magazine/17kerry3_span/17kerry3_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/magazine/17kerry3_span/17kerry3_span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/magazine/17kerry3_span/17kerry3_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/17/magazine/17kerry3_span/17kerry3_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The All-American', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The All-American', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kerry, John', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T22:20:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Traub', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Traub', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/12a90823-ba0b-5305-8e07-cd1519b1f239', 'word_count': 4892, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12a90823-ba0b-5305-8e07-cd1519b1f239'}, {'abstract': 'Thomas Demand has organized a show for Matthew Marks Gallery; a Klimt landscape goes up for auction at Sotheby’s; and works by Alison Saar will be coming to Madison Square Park.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/arts/design/thomas-demand-organizes-a-show-for-matthew-marks-gallery.html', 'snippet': 'Thomas Demand has organized a show for Matthew Marks Gallery; a Klimt landscape goes up for auction at Sotheby’s; and works by Alison Saar will be coming to Madison Square Park.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It has become something of an annual tradition at the Matthew Marks Gallery to invite one of its artists to organize a summer exhibition, and this year it is Thomas Demand. He has taken over the gallery’s West 22nd Street space in Chelsea, reconfiguring it with an installation of labyrinthine walls based on a drawing by the artist Martin Boyce and presenting a show opening Tuesday called “La Carte d’Après Nature.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/VOGEL/VOGEL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 823, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/VOGEL/VOGEL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/VOGEL/VOGEL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Artist Shows His Train of Thought', 'kicker': 'Inside Art', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Artist Shows His Train of Thought', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klimt, Gustav', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Demand, Thomas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saar, Alison', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T22:21:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Vogel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vogel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/facf6edf-3f60-542f-8fd7-334b42131656', 'word_count': 946, 'uri': 'nyt://article/facf6edf-3f60-542f-8fd7-334b42131656'}, {'abstract': 'Manohla Dargis plans to take in the celebration of the centenary of the architect John Lautner, some of whose homes became movie sets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/movies/john-lautner-centenary-celebration.html', 'snippet': 'Manohla Dargis plans to take in the celebration of the centenary of the architect John Lautner, some of whose homes became movie sets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When he arrived in Los Angeles, the architect John Lautner said that he was so shocked that he was physically ill for a year. “It was so ugly,” he said of the city where, for the next 50 years or so, he nonetheless built some of the most celebrated buildings of the 20th century. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/15subdargis/15subdargis-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 765, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/15subdargis/15subdargis-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/15subdargis/15subdargis-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A House Tour for Cinephiles', 'kicker': 'The Hot List | Film', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A House Tour For Cinephiles', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lautner, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T22:21:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70aaccd9-4aba-5b8f-8f06-ce924295ba61', 'word_count': 346, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70aaccd9-4aba-5b8f-8f06-ce924295ba61'}, {'abstract': 'Federal authorities said they had broken up an international ring that had been smuggling Egyptian antiquities into the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/arts/design/federal-authorities-charge-4-people-in-antiquities-smuggling.html', 'snippet': 'Federal authorities said they had broken up an international ring that had been smuggling Egyptian antiquities into the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Federal authorities announced on Wednesday that they had broken up an international ring that had been smuggling Egyptian antiquities into the United States. The Immigration and Customs Enforcement’s Homeland Security Investigations department said it was the first time that a cultural property smuggling network had been dismantled in the United States.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/SMUGGLE/SMUGGLE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 756, 'width': 911, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '4 Charged in Smuggling Egyptian Antiquities', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '4 Charged in Smuggling Egyptian Antiquities', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smuggling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Egyptian Civilization', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hawass, Zahi', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T22:22:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/56eee16c-f5c8-5db3-8826-37c72bb83ac4', 'word_count': 406, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56eee16c-f5c8-5db3-8826-37c72bb83ac4'}, {'abstract': 'Ben Brantley anticipates the great stage actor Simon Russell Beale’s tackling a smaller-than-life character in the Atlantic Theater Company production of “Bluebird.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/theater/simon-russell-beale-tackles-a-smaller-than-life-character-in-bluebird.html', 'snippet': 'Ben Brantley anticipates the great stage actor Simon Russell Beale’s tackling a smaller-than-life character in the Atlantic Theater Company production of “Bluebird.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Having seen Simon Russell Beale memorably embody the most noble of princes (in the title role of “Hamlet”), the baddest of all lieutenants (as Iago in “Othello”) and the most fatuous of fops (in Dion Boucicault’s “London Assurance”), I am looking forward to his portrayal of someone to whom superlatives do not apply. That’s Jimmy MacNeill, the willfully anonymous London taxi driver of “Bluebird,” a 1998 play by Simon Stephens receiving its American premiere this August in an Atlantic Theater Company production. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/BRANTLEY-1-1310506448167/BRANTLEY-1-1310506448167-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 671, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/BRANTLEY-1-1310506448167/BRANTLEY-1-1310506448167-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/BRANTLEY-1-1310506448167/BRANTLEY-1-1310506448167-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Taxi Fare for the Uncommon Man', 'kicker': 'The Hot List | Theater', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Taxi Fare for the Uncommon Man', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Theater Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beale, Simon Russell', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T22:23:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8010f7fe-6745-57b2-8822-1fbebae352f7', 'word_count': 299, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8010f7fe-6745-57b2-8822-1fbebae352f7'}, {'abstract': 'Gary Lynch, who started this week as global head of legal, compliance and regulatory relations, received just over 415,000 restricted stock units of Bank of America.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/bank-of-americas-4-million-welcome-for-lynch/', 'snippet': 'Gary Lynch, who started this week as global head of legal, compliance and regulatory relations, received just over 415,000 restricted stock units of Bank of America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gary Lynch, the former chief legal officer at Morgan Stanley who decamped to Bank of America this year, received a stock award worth approximately $4 million from his new employer, a regulatory filing showed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '$4 Million Welcome for Lynch at Bank of America', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bonuses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lynch, Gary', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bank of America Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T22:24:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin Roose', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roose', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/58121c6d-d94f-566c-b2ab-2046fb5082ad', 'word_count': 325, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58121c6d-d94f-566c-b2ab-2046fb5082ad'}, {'abstract': 'The work of two artists, Birgir Andresson And Poul Gernes, is joined, posthumously, in an exhibition.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/arts/design/birgir-andresson-and-poul-gernes-bolt-out-of-the-blue.html', 'snippet': 'The work of two artists, Birgir Andresson And Poul Gernes, is joined, posthumously, in an exhibition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sean Kelly Gallery', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'BIRGIR ANDRESSON AND POUL GERNES: ‘Bolt Out of the Blue’', 'kicker': 'Art in Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Birgir Anderson And Poul Gernes: ‘Bolt Out of the Blue’', 'name': None, 'seo': None