city nightspot: Lower Manhattan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/arts/design/night-vision-photography-after-dark-at-the-met.html', 'snippet': 'Holland Cotter visits the Met’s “Night Vision: Photography After Dark,” which conjures memories of a treasured city nightspot: Lower Manhattan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Middle of the night is my time, always has been, especially in New York in the summer. The city looks better, sounds better, feels softer, or at least a little less specific. I think and remember better late, or imagine I do. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/COTTER/COTTER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1006, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/COTTER/COTTER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/COTTER/COTTER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Past Meets Present in Walk After Dark', 'kicker': 'The Hot List | Art', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Past Meets Present In Walk After Dark', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crane, Hart', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Poe, Edgar Allan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Whitman, Walt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Agnes', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Melville, Herman', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T23:01:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holland Cotter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holland', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cotter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ba2ffaf-3295-5e67-adf2-2d1441cf6bcf', 'word_count': 363, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ba2ffaf-3295-5e67-adf2-2d1441cf6bcf'}, {'abstract': 'The chairman of the Federal Reserve, Ben S. Bernanke, appeared to retreat from statements that the central bank was prepared to expand its economic aid program.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/business/bernanke-moderates-his-remarks-on-new-stimulus.html', 'snippet': 'The chairman of the Federal Reserve, Ben S. Bernanke, appeared to retreat from statements that the central bank was prepared to expand its economic aid program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A day after he helped lift markets with his testimony, Ben S. Bernanke, the chairman of the Federal Reserve, tempered his words. And in reaction, the markets, too, pulled back.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fed Chief Hedges Remarks on Possible New Stimulus', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fed Chief Hedges Remarks On Possible New Stimulus', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bernanke, Ben S', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quantitative Easing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T23:02:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bloomberg News', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bloomberg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'News', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/230a17a2-eebe-59b0-a9b9-0fb61d581d54', 'word_count': 654, 'uri': 'nyt://article/230a17a2-eebe-59b0-a9b9-0fb61d581d54'}, {'abstract': 'A look at the work of the Minimalist artist Carl Andre.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/07/17/arts/design/20110717_andre_ss.html', 'snippet': 'A look at the work of the Minimalist artist Carl Andre.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A look at the work of the Minimalist artist Carl Andre.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/arts/07172011_andre_ss-slide-D7PY/07172011_andre_ss-slide-D7PY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Materials and Their Space', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sculpture', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Andre, Carl', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T23:03:38+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Arts', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/fb491068-f726-540f-b006-71ac4b0c7a46', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/fb491068-f726-540f-b006-71ac4b0c7a46'}, {'abstract': 'Laura Kipnis’s writing combines sharp analysis with blistering wit to challenge prevailing notions about love and sex, power and desire, hubris and retribution in American life.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/17/books/review/up-front-laura-kipnis.html', 'snippet': 'Laura Kipnis’s writing combines sharp analysis with blistering wit to challenge prevailing notions about love and sex, power and desire, hubris and retribution in American life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In books like “Against Love: A Polemic” and “How to Become a Scandal,” Laura Kipnis has combined sharp analysis with blistering wit to challenge prevailing notions about love and sex, power and desire, hubris and retribution in American life. On our cover this week, she reviews “The Art of Cruelty,” by Maggie Nelson, a wide-ranging inquiry into the aesthetic and ethical questions raised by images of brutality in our culture.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/books/review/Upfront/Upfront-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1020, 'width': 650, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/books/review/Upfront/Upfront-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/17/books/review/Upfront/Upfront-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Up Front: Laura Kipnis', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Up Front', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kipnis, Laura', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T23:04:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editors', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editors'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6726f373-5e26-59ed-aeea-a1f9a7a80107', 'word_count': 258, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6726f373-5e26-59ed-aeea-a1f9a7a80107'}, {'abstract': 'Franz Welser-Möst, a Bruckner champion, conducted the Cleveland Orchestra in a series titled Bruckner: (R)evolution at Avery Fisher Hall on Wednesday night.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/arts/music/cleveland-orchestra-at-the-lincoln-center-festival.html', 'snippet': 'Franz Welser-Möst, a Bruckner champion, conducted the Cleveland Orchestra in a series titled Bruckner: (R)evolution at Avery Fisher Hall on Wednesday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Anton Bruckner had a steadfast circle of supporters, including some significant conductors and composers. But, as his obituaries in 1896 made clear, he was more widely seen as a strangely solitary Austrian church musician with oversized ambitions whose sprawling symphonies were earnest yet awkward and self-indulgent works. Bruckner faced setbacks and adversity, and feared that his music would never be appreciated.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/CLEVE/CLEVE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/CLEVE/CLEVE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/CLEVE/CLEVE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 888, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/CLEVE/CLEVE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/CLEVE/CLEVE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbna