heir summer bucket list.  What one thing – read that book, see that movie, watch that show – must you do this summer?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just one thing, you tell yourself, as the summer slips by like so many summers before it. If you manage to do nothing else for your own pleasure in this season of unclaimed hours, you will read that book, see that movie, watch that show, gaze at that painting, listen to that guitarist. Even people who do these things for a living – the New York Times arts critics – can’t always organize their cultural calendars to include what they most want to do. We asked them to share the single item in, or closely related to, their critical discipline at the very top of their summer bucket list. Here are their selections. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Hot List: A Single Pleasure Ere Summer Fades', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T23:11:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/35b0b3f5-11d7-5b3d-9edb-cc4c712ab3ab', 'word_count': 285, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35b0b3f5-11d7-5b3d-9edb-cc4c712ab3ab'}, {'abstract': 'Touring without a new album, A Perfect Circle mostly performed songs from its first release on Wednesday at Hammerstein Ballroom.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/16/arts/music/a-perfect-circle-at-hammerstein-ballroom.html', 'snippet': 'Touring without a new album, A Perfect Circle mostly performed songs from its first release on Wednesday at Hammerstein Ballroom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Maynard James Keenan works in mysterious ways. He juggles three bands: Tool, Puscifer and A Perfect Circle, the one he brought to Hammerstein Ballroom on Wednesday night. He’s a frontman who stays out of the spotlight: on a platform separate from the rest of the band, set back on the stage, lighted so that he is just a silhouette. And he tours at whim. A Perfect Circle’s most recent album, “eMOTIVe” (Virgin), was released in 2004. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/16/arts/Perfect/Perfect-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 349, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/16/arts/Perfect/Perfect-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 349}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/16/arts/Perfect/Perfect-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 757, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/16/arts/Perfect/Perfect-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/16/arts/Perfect/Perfect-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Desolate Croon That Seethes and Hints at a Band’s Next Phase', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Desolate Croon That Seethes and Hints at a Band’s Next Phase', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keenan, Maynard James', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T23:11:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'repo