, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-14T23:51:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeannette Catsoulis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeannette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Catsoulis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/17d08bfc-5783-5799-9e24-b5e4064eeb36', 'word_count': 328, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17d08bfc-5783-5799-9e24-b5e4064eeb36'}, {'abstract': 'Share your photos from this weekend’s Harry Potter screenings.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/seeking-your-harry-potter-photos/', 'snippet': 'Share your photos from this weekend’s Harry Potter screenings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Can you show us your best Hermione? Your finest Dumbledore? Your slickest Snape? The final film in the Harry Potter series opens at midnight tonight and for fans, plenty of magic is likely to happen both onscreen and off. Are you planning to see the film and will you be dressing up? We’re taking photo submissions of all the wizardly costumes you come across. Submit them to http://submit.nytimes.com/harry-potter.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Seeking Your Harry Potter Photos', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-15T00:00:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f9ca834-ac0c-5aa9-97f2-1263203b8537', 'word_count': 98, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f9ca834-ac0c-5aa9-97f2-1263203b8537'}, {'abstract': 'A Pakistani court granted bail on Thursday to the person suspected of being the mastermind of a deadly 2009 attack on the Sri Lankan cricket team.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/world/asia/15briefs-BAILFORTERRO_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'A Pakistani court granted bail on Thursday to the person suspected of being the mastermind of a deadly 2009 attack on the Sri Lankan cricket team.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Pakistani court granted bail on Thursday to the person suspected of being the mastermind of a deadly 2009 attack on the Sri Lankan cricket team. The suspect, Malik Ishaq, left, had been kept in jail since 1997 on a series of terrorism charges, and he was showered with rose petals by hundreds of waiting supporters as he left prison. “We will peacefully continue our mission,” Mr. Ishaq told reporters, saying his hard-line Sunni group, Lashkar-e-Jhangvi, would continue to pursue its anti-Shiite struggle through legislative means. The group is suspected to have been a central player in several terror attacks in the Punjab Province of Pakistan, and had been linked to the March 2009 attack, which killed six police guards and two bystanders in the eastern city of Lahore and halted international cricket competitions in Pakistan. The date for the trial has not been set. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/world/asia/15briefs-ishaq/15briefs-ishaq-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/15/world/asia/15briefs-ishaq/15briefs-ishaq-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pakistan: Bail for Terror Suspect', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | ASIA', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pakistan: Bail for Terror Suspect', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sri Lanka', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lashkar-e-Jhangvi', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-15T00:01:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Waqar Gillani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Waqar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gillani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/1aa54de9-dbdd-5ae2-9983-dce819fae0f8', 'word_count': 147, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1aa54de9-dbdd-5ae2-9983-dce819fae0f8'}, {'abstract': '“Girlfriend” is about a young man with Down syndrome who lives in a small Massachusetts town, and the role is played by the man who inspired the story.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/movies/girlfriend-about-young-man-with-down-syndrome-review.html', 'snippet': '“Girlfriend” is about a young man with Down syndrome who lives in a small Massachusetts town, and the role is played by the man who inspired the story.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Justin Lerner’s debut feature, “Girlfriend,” is set and shot in his Massachusetts hometown, and the story is built around a man in his 20s named Evan, a character inspired by, and played by, a local actor with Down syndrome, Evan Sneider. As you might expect, the film is eminently respectful in its handling of this kindhearted, sexually curious protagonist, at times irritatingly so, as when the camera goes coy and turns away to focus on autumn leaves during one particularly physical encounter.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/arts/ROUNDUP-1/ROUNDUP-1-article