g quality natural gas assets for a good price, since the independent energy company needed more capital.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BHP Billiton‘s $12.1 billion purchase of Petrohawk Energy places a hefty premium on the independent energy company. But in the deal, BHP believes it is getting a bargain.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Petrohawk’s Sale to BHP, a Quest for Capital', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shale', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BHP Billiton PLC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'PETROHAWK ENERGY CORP', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-15T01:08:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8a6b3d0-4204-53e7-a808-bbc256499cd1', 'word_count': 276, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8a6b3d0-4204-53e7-a808-bbc256499cd1'}, {'abstract': 'The Soso Rengo team, a combination of players from three high schools just miles from the crippled nuclear reactors in Fukushima, lost in the opening round of a regional knock-out contest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/sports/baseball/soso-rengo-eliminated.html', 'snippet': 'The Soso Rengo team, a combination of players from three high schools just miles from the crippled nuclear reactors in Fukushima, lost in the opening round of a regional knock-out contest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Soso Rengo team, a combination of players from three high schools just miles from the crippled nuclear reactors in Fukushima, lost, 8-1, in the opening round of a regional knock-out contest in Fukushima. The team of players sent into exile by the tsunami and nuclear crisis that started in March had hoped to qualify for a trip to the national summer championship tournament in August.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Soso Rengo Eliminated', 'kicker': 'Sports Briefing | Baseball', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Soso Rengo Eliminated', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Japan Earthquake and Tsunami (2011)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fukushima Daiichi Nuclear Power Plant (Japan)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-15T01:09:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kantaro Suzuki', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kantaro', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Suzuki', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/deb7363f-3f0d-5db9-85ab-9878b2aa0939', 'word_count': 66, 'uri': 'nyt://article/deb7363f-3f0d-5db9-85ab-9878b2aa0939'}, {'abstract': 'According to the man suspected of killing him, Leiby Kletzky spent Tuesday watching TV: something almost never done in the Hasidic community of Borough Park.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/nyregion/sheltered-hasidic-community-stunned-by-kletzky-killing.html', 'snippet': 'According to the man suspected of killing him, Leiby Kletzky spent Tuesday watching TV: something almost never done in the Hasidic community of Borough Park.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Down the block from the home of Levi Aron, the hardware-store clerk accused this week of slaughtering a child in Brooklyn, a neighbor, Miriam Levy, spoke about peculiar qualities that she had discovered only after Mr. Aron’s arrest.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A World Sheltered From TV, if Not Violence', 'kicker': 'About New York', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A World Sheltered From TV, If Not Violence', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kletzky, Leiby', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Aron, Levi', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hasidism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'BOROUGH PARK (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-15T01:09:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Dwyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dwyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6dbad66d-f771-5762-92ca-1d8cd35d8638', 'word_count': 690, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6dbad66d-f771-5762-92ca-1d8cd35d8638'}, {'abstract': 'Rapprochement between the world’s leading military power and the fastest-rising one is proving to be a difficult task.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/world/asia/15beijing.html', 'snippet': 'Rapprochement between the world’s leading military power and the fastest-rising one is proving to be a difficult task.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — During three days in China this week, the top American military officer, Adm. Mike Mullen, exchanged warm pledges with his Chinese counterpart to improve the reliably fractious relationship between the two forces. He watched Chinese Su-27 fighters barrel roll over an air base, saw a Chinese counterterrorism exercise in a stifling bunker beneath an army post and squeezed into a Chinese submarine at a naval base.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/world/asia/alt2-15beijing/alt2-15beijing-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 787, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/world/asia/alt2-15beijing/alt2-15beijing-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/15/world/asia/alt2-15beijing/alt2-15beijing-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. and China Try to Agree on Military Strategy', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wary Rivals, U.S. and China Try to Reach Truce on Military Strategy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mullen, Michael G', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Military Bases and Installations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-15T01:10:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Wines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/e948c8d0-225f-57e7-aaee-2e840221bede', 'word_count': 1177, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e948c8d0-225f-57e7-aaee-2e840221bede'}, {'abstract': 'Congress and the White House can no longer ignore the imminent threat to the economy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/opinion/15fri1.html', 'snippet': 'Congress and the White House can no longer ignore the imminent threat to the economy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As negotiators in the debt-ceiling talks sputtered and raged, the chill reality of an imminent government default crept up Wednesday and made a mockery of their gamesmanship. Two major rating agencies warned that a once-unthinkable downgrade of the nation’s credit rating would be at hand if this crisis was not immediately defused.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Debt Alarm Is Heard', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Debt Alarm Is Heard: Congress and the White House can no longer ignore the imminent threat to the economy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McConnell, Mitch', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Standard & Poor's Corp", 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Moody's Corporation", 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-15T01:11:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ed32705-5570-5dab-bb41-96e286b70a7c', 'word_count': 583, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ed32705-5570-5dab-bb41-96e286b70a7c'}, {'abstract': "July 14, 2011 - A new study shows that although alpha males may get all the attention, it could be better being a beta. At least if you're a baboon.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/science/100000000946692/timescast--better-being-a-beta.html', 'snippet': "July 14, 2011 - A new study shows that although alpha males may get all the attention, it could be better being a beta. At least if you're a baboon.", 'lead_paragraph': "July 14, 2011 - A new study shows that although alpha males may get all the attention, it could be better being a beta. At least if you're a baboon.", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/14/science/video-tc-110714-baboon/video-tc-110714-baboon-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/14/science/video-tc-110714-baboon/video-tc-110714-baboon-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/14/science/video-tc-110714-baboon/video-tc-110714-baboon-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 126, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/14/science/video-tc-110714-baboon/video-tc-110714-baboon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/14/science/video-tc-110714-baboon/video-tc-110714-baboon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'TimesCast | Better Being a Beta', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monkeys and Apes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-15T01:11:10+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'Emily B. Hager', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/4eaacf50-cb15-519e-baa1-f2157c2c021a', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/4eaacf50-cb15-519e-baa1-f2157c2c021a'}, {'abstract': 'An initiative that brings struggling families together to help each other out of poverty is providing a new model for social welfare.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/14/out-of-poverty-family-style/', 'snippet': 'An initiative that brings struggling families together to help each other out of poverty is providing a new model for social welfare.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Shortly after Candace Keshwar immigrated from Trinidad to Boston in 2002, her life took a difficult turn. Her dream had been to go to college and have a career where she could help others. But her first daughter was born with cerebral palsy and Keshwar spent the next seven years caring for her at home. She grew isolated. Her husband worked in construction, but jobs were sporadic, and the family relied on government assistance. “It was a real dark space for me,” Keshwar said. “I kept thinking, ‘This cannot be my life. I know I have the potential to do so much more.’”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Out of Poverty, Family-Style', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-15T01:15:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Bornstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bornstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/58384c8b-dce4-5537-9492-2d01c1b5d95d', 'word_count': 1924, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58384c8b-dce4-5537-9492-2d01c1b5d95d'}, {'abstract': 'The catalyst for a crackdown on food trucks in Manhattan was the recent explosion of high-end vendors in Midtown.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/opinion/15zachbrooks.html', 'snippet': 'The catalyst for a crackdown on food trucks in Manhattan was the recent explosion of high-end vendors in Midtown.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE past few years have been a golden age for street food in New York City. You could get just about anything from a food truck in Midtown Manhattan — from waffles and schnitzel to halal chicken and lamb over rice — despite the fact that street vending is for all intents and purposes illegal there.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/opinion/15brooks-opedart/15brooks-opedart-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/opinion/15brooks-opedart/15brooks-opedart-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop