'nyt://article/b873964e-184b-5a8e-87b4-deab5cbbdef4'}, {'abstract': 'Seeking to put Clorox on the auction block, Carl C. Icahn said the company could get “numerous superior bids” exceeding his offer if it sought other suitors.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/icahn-bids-for-clorox/', 'snippet': 'Seeking to put Clorox on the auction block, Carl C. Icahn said the company could get “numerous superior bids” exceeding his offer if it sought other suitors.', 'lead_paragraph': '8:03 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Icahn Bids for Clorox, but Urges It to Seek Higher Offers', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Icahn, Carl C', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Clorox Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-15T11:31:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris V. Nicholson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': 'V.', 'lastname': 'Nicholson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a28041e9-fe63-53e1-8a71-78e541a160e8', 'word_count': 606, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a28041e9-fe63-53e1-8a71-78e541a160e8'}, {'abstract': 'A musician and sometime D.J. from Germany talks about his latest project: a niche magazine called The Travel Almanac.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/the-insider-paul-kominek/', 'snippet': 'A musician and sometime D.J. from Germany talks about his latest project: a niche magazine called The Travel Almanac.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Travel Almanac, the newest of a growing crop of compact niche magazines (see: Apartamento, Boat and Afterzine), looks at the art of travel through the perspectives of artists, musicians, writers and filmmakers who are well, well-traveled. The journal was founded two years ago by Paul Kominek, a musician and sometime D.J. from Germany, with the help of his friend John Roberts, an American musician who, like Kominek, lives in Berlin. “By using the topic of traveling as an overarching theme, it gave us an amazing excuse to ask high-profile artists or cultural icons questions that avoid the obligatory ‘What do you do?’ and ‘How did you get started?’ and instead ask about different aspects of their lives that we personally find more interesting,” says Kominek. The first volume, on Japan, debuted this spring. The cover is printed on textured German cardstock, the interior pages on creamy Swedish drawing paper. It features tips from the likes of David Lynch, James Murphy and Javier Peres, as well as some handsome photographs of traditional Japanese inns, called “ryokans.” T turned the tables on Kominek and asked for his own travel preferences, and his Berlin mainstays.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Insider | Paul Kominek', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-15T12:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Yuri Chong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Yuri', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8812850-5d92-51c0-86a9-cbad21794088', 'word_count': 1238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8812850-5d92-51c0-86a9-cbad21794088'}, {'abstract': 'The AMC series “Breaking Bad” returns for its fourth season on Sunday, but don’t expect the show’s main character, Walter White, to transform back 