t': 'Deleveraging, the evidence.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/it-was-debt-what-did-it/', 'snippet': 'Deleveraging, the evidence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Never mind William Galston’s strange belief that debt-deleveraging is a new theory, unknown to Keynesian economics; Mian and Sufi are in fact doing terrific work. They have been testing the effects of household leverage by looking at cross-sectional evidence, in particular county-level US data. Here’s the chart I found most compelling:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'It Was Debt What Did It', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-15T13:16:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70ec8f0d-f69f-50de-b4fe-694e43e0e354', 'word_count': 211, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70ec8f0d-f69f-50de-b4fe-694e43e0e354'}, {'abstract': 'The British Open crowds enthusiastically greeted Darren Clarke to the top of the leader board in the second round, where he was joined by Lucas Glover.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/16/sports/golf/2011-british-open-placid-weather-helps-second-round-leaders.html', 'snippet': 'The British Open crowds enthusiastically greeted Darren Clarke to the top of the leader board in the second round, where he was joined by Lucas Glover.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SANDWICH, England — The only thing that can be said with any certitude at the halfway mark of the 140th British Open is that neither the No. 1-ranked golfer in the world, Luke Donald, nor the No. 2-ranked golfer in the world, Lee Westwood, will be factors this weekend at Royal St. George’s. The two, each from England, were done in by a seaside links course that will only get tougher.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/16/sports/OPEN1/OPEN1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 946, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/16/sports/OPEN1/OPEN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/16/sports/OPEN1/OPEN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Weather Clears, but Field Bunches Together', 'kicker': 'British Open | Royal St. Georges', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Weather Clears, but Field Bunches Together', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'British Open (Golf)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Glover, Lucas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clarke, Darren', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-15T13:17:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Dorman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dorman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/74114bd0-7696-51d0-af01-bb2fd460f8cc', 'word_count': 1005, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74114bd0-7696-51d0-af01-bb2fd460f8cc'}, {'abstract': 'BP outlined to regulators how it would change some of its oil drilling standards in the Gulf of Mexico to prevent another disaster.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/16/business/global/bp-announces-tighter-standards-for-deepwater-drilling.html', 'snippet': 'BP outlined to regulators how it would change some of its oil drilling standards in the Gulf of Mexico to prevent another disaster.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — BP said on Friday that it was changing its deepwater drilling standards in the Gulf of Mexico as it seeks to repair its reputation and resume offshore operations after the disastrous oil spill last year.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'BP to Tighten Deep-Sea Drilling Practices as It Tries to Rebound', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'BP to Tighten Deep-Sea Drilling Practices as It Tries to Rebound', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BP Plc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-15T13:31:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Werdigier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werdigier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c010b28-a7c0-58b0-8f66-c61dee2dfffd', 'word_count': 409, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c010b28-a7c0-58b0-8f66-c61dee2dfffd'}, {'abstract': 'Fannie Freddie fraud.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/evil-stupid/', 'snippet': 'Fannie Freddie fraud.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Atrios likes to say that the eternal question, as you look at absurd policy debates, is whether these people are evil or stupid.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Evil > Stupid', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-15T13:31:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/abd7c648-2c0f-5df9-b146-29b03cc7386a', 'word_count': 319, 'uri': 'nyt://article/abd7c648-2c0f-5df9-b146-29b03cc7386a'}, {'abstract': 'BP says the formula used to determine compensation for businesses hurt in last year’s spill is too generous.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/16/us/16gulf.html', 'snippet': 'BP says the formula used to determine compensation for businesses hurt in last year’s spill is too generous.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GULF SHORES, Ala. — It seems like old times here on the Gulf Coast. The Flora-Bama Lounge is hopping, there’s a two-hour wait for a table at the Original Oyster House, and the first complaints you hear among the charter boat operators are about the latest fishing limits — not oil slicks.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/16/us/16gulf/16gulf-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/16/us/16gulf/16gulf-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 340}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/16/us/16gulf/16gulf-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/16/us/16gulf/16gulf-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/16/us/16gulf/16gulf-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'No Vacancies, but Some Reservations', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Vacancies, but Some Reservations', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gulf of Mexico', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gulf Coast Claims Facility', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BP Plc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALABAMA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feinberg, Kenneth R', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-15T13:38:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Campbell Robertson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Campbell', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robertson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2313a71-65e4-5903-ac4d-38e6c36e79b4', 'word_count': 1141, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2313a71-65e4-5903-ac4d-38e6c36e79b4'}, {'abstract': 'Activists said that 19 people were killed in attacks on protesters across the country on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/16/world/middleeast/16syria.html', 'snippet': 'Activists said that 19 people were killed in attacks on protesters across the country on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — Even as the now-familiar ritual of Friday protests raged across Syria, activists, diplomats and some government officials suggest that a staggering economy, a better-organized though still divided opposition, and a fumbling government response are recasting Syria, even if President Bashar al-Assad manages to survive in office. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Security Forces Open Fire on Syrian Protesters', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stalemate In Syria Chips Away At Assad', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-15T13:44:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Shadid', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shadid', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a29388e5-f1df-55b7-855e-4ce54196fc53', 'word_count': 1098, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a29388e5-f1df-55b7-855e-4ce54196fc53'}, {'abstract': 'David Michalek and Dr. Paul Ekman discuss the video “Portraits in Dramatic Time” at Lincoln Center.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/arts/david-michalek-and-dr-paul-ekman-converse-at-lincoln-center.html', 'snippet': 'David Michalek and Dr. Paul Ekman discuss the video “Portraits in Dramatic Time” at Lincoln Center.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dr. Paul Ekman, a psychologist and specialist in the study of emotions and deceit, sits with the artist David Michalek to talk about Mr. Michalek’s new video installation, “Portraits in Dramatic Time,” on view at Lincoln Center. Mr. Michalek’s “Portraits” are short films of actors and artists performing scenes. But the film is wound down to what its creator calls “hyperslow motion,” showing the nuance of each gesture and facial expression, frame by frame, on an 85-by-45-foot screen on the wall of the David H. Koch Theater in the plaza. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Weekend Miser', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Weekend Miser', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Public Library for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-15T13:50:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Lee Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': 'Lee', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a162233-a4b6-5dbb-a828-0ad4e9ed5e03', 'word_count': 491, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a162233-a4b6-5dbb-a828-0ad4e9ed5e03'}, {'abstract': 'Federal regulators are considering backing off a plan to curb Wall Street’s control over the derivatives market, another potential win for the big banks.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/regulators-weigh-softer-derivatives-rules/', 'snippet': 'Federal regulators are considering backing off a plan to curb Wall Street’s control over the derivatives market, another potential win for the big banks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Federal regulators are considering backing off a plan to curb Wall Street’s control over the derivatives market, another potential win for the big banks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Regulators Are Said to Weigh Softer Derivatives Rules', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Derivatives (Financial Instruments)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lobbying and Lobbyists', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Commodity Futures Trading Commission', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-15T13:59:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e83e01b-106a-5b89-9c40-6dbd8a5520a4', 'word_count': 343, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e83e01b-106a-5b89-9c40-6dbd8a5520a4'}, {'abstract': 'A piece of runway jewelry by Jason Wu is now available for sale.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/night-owls-alexis-bittar-for-jason-wu/', 'snippet': 'A piece of runway jewelry by Jason Wu is now available for sale.', 'lead_paragraph': 'All too often, the jewelry that we see at fashion shows makes it only to the end of the runway and back. Thankfully, the owl pin designed by Alexis Bittar for Jason Wu — the one that adorned Wu’s fall peacoats and blazers — is very much real and ours for the buying, arriving in stores on Friday. Fans will recognize the owl, a k a Miss Wu, the designer’s muse and logo (“perhaps because of too many late nights sketching,” Wu says), and also appreciate Bittar’s gutsy take on it. Inspired by the photographer Robert Polidori’s book on the restoration of Versailles, “Parcours Museologique Reviste” (Steidl), the two fell hard for the contrast between grand décor and raw metals. “I love the juxtaposition,” says Wu, who calls his fall collection Baroque Sportswear. “The piece combines opulence with early ’90s grunge,” Bittar says. “And a sense of raw romanticism,” Wu adds. “A perfect complement to the clothes.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Night Owls | Alexis Bittar for Jason Wu', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-15T14:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Waldman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9e78f30-b72c-5b32-9937-03a7fe57ea63', 'word_count': 165, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9e78f30-b72c-5b32-9937-03a7fe57ea63'}, {'abstract': 'In a news conference Friday, President Obama held out hope that a broad deal could be reached to raise the debt ceiling as lawmakers raced to avoid the nation’s first financial default.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/obama-returns-to-the-podium-to-discuss-debt-talks/', 'snippet': 'In a news conference Friday, President Obama held out hope that a broad deal could be reached to raise the debt ceiling as lawmakers raced to avoid the nation’s first financial default.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama on Friday reiterated his desire to reach a grand bargain that would deal with the nation’s long-term debt problems even as leaders in Washington take action to avoid a financial default by the government.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Reiterates Desire for Comprehensive Budget Package', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-15T14:00:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eeedbe4d-7c46-55ca-8b07-6a3bb374a314', 'word_count': 761, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eeedbe4d-7c46-55ca-8b07-6a3bb374a314'}, {'abstract': 'The move gives the rebels access to $30 billion in frozen Libyan assets in the United States and increases pressure on Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi to resign.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/16/world/africa/16libya.html', 'snippet': 'The move gives the rebels access to $30 billion in frozen Libyan assets in the United States and increases pressure on Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi to resign.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISTANBUL — The United States formally recognized the rebel leadership in Libya as the country’s legitimate government on Friday, allowing the rebel government access to $30 billion in Libyan assets held in the United States. It is not yet clear how and when the money would be released. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/16/world/16libya/16libya-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/16/world/16libya/16libya-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/16/world/16libya/16libya-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight'