at the side of the literary road. Where are these Freudian howlers of the night? Theirs has been rather a raw deal. ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/books/review/Cronin/Cronin-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 961, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/books/review/Cronin/Cronin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/17/books/review/Cronin/Cronin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Melancholy Werewolf’s Existential Howl', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Existential Howl', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duncan, Glen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-15T15:41:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Justin Cronin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cronin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/acea03ec-b971-53e9-ab0f-14f0dad76448', 'word_count': 1235, 'uri': 'nyt://article/acea03ec-b971-53e9-ab0f-14f0dad76448'}, {'abstract': 'Dennis Albaugh oftens opens his garage as a fund-raiser for groups. He once raised $60,000 for the local high school.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/17/automobiles/opening-the-doors-to-serve-a-good-cause.html', 'snippet': 'Dennis Albaugh oftens 