/www.nytimes.com/2011/07/16/theater/doctor-who-reigns-in-manchester-theater-festival.html', 'snippet': 'Turning children into hands-on heroes of “The Crash of the Elysium” and giving some of them their first taste of theater are among the goals of the Punchdrunk theater troupe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SALFORD, England — The 15 schoolchildren knew they weren’t in danger, but theater still worked its magic as they spied the six-foot-tall stone monster behind them in the corridor of a spaceship. When the dusky lighting went black, and a pulsing strobe light began to illuminate the monster closing in, they let out a collective shriek and fled through a portal that, mysteriously, opened onto a tented fairground where a sign announced the date: “6 July 1888.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/16/arts/16who/16who-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/16/arts/16who/16who-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 345}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/16/arts/16who/16who-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/16/arts/16who/16who-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/16/arts/16who/16who-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Time-Travel Adventure to Save the Life of Doctor Who', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Time-Travel Adventure to Save the Life of Doctor Who', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Punchdrunk Theatricals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Youth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-15T16:19:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/235cbb9c-7703-5d67-b952-04b2aca4dd8d', 'word_count': 1138, 'uri': 'nyt://article/235cbb9c-7703-5d67-b952-04b2aca4dd8d'}, {'abstract': 'James B. Stewart warns of the risks of a perjury epidemic that has “infected nearly every aspect of society.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/17/books/review/book-review-tangled-webs-by-james-b-stewart.html', 'snippet': 'James B. Stewart warns of the risks of a perjury epidemic that has “infected nearly every aspect of society.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'James B. Stewart dedicates his new book “to all who seek the truth.” But in his view, the ranks of committed truth-seekers are shrinking before our eyes. “Mounting evidence suggests that the broad public commitment to telling the truth under oath has been breaking down, eroding over recent decades, a trend that has been accelerating in recent years,” he declares. “Perjury has infected nearly every aspect of society.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/books/review/bkr-Rosen-t_CA0/bkr-Rosen-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/17/books/review/bkr-Rosen-t_CA0/bkr-Rosen-t_CA