d deal-making record.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carl C. Icahn may have bid $10.2 billion for Clorox. But as his letter to the consumer products company makes clear, he is not necessarily interested in owning the detergents maker.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Icahn, a Deal Maker With a Spotty Record', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Icahn, Carl C', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Clorox Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-15T17:47:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/733d717d-1eee-569e-9e4d-afdf47dcf6c6', 'word_count': 544, 'uri': 'nyt://article/733d717d-1eee-569e-9e4d-afdf47dcf6c6'}, {'abstract': 'Google is getting into the business of writing e-books with a marketing book titled “Winning the Zero Moment of Truth.”', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/google-offers-marketing-ideas-by-the-book/', 'snippet': 'Google is getting into the business of writing e-books with a marketing book titled “Winning the Zero Moment of Truth.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Google seems to be able to do just about anything, at least if the robust earnings report the company issued on Thursday is any indication. So perhaps it is not surprising that Google is also getting into the business of writing e-books.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Google Offers Marketing Ideas, by the Book', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 's