morabilia/', 'snippet': 'Paul Sullivan writes about the relative value of baseball memorabilia in his Wealth Matters column.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Paul Sullivan, in his Wealth Matters column this week, writes about the market for baseball memorabilia. In the wake of Derek Jeter’s 3,000th hit, he was trying to understand the market for signed baseballs and bats, jerseys and photos. What sorts of items appreciate? And, he asked, how do you know if what you have is valuable?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Valuing Baseball Memorabilia', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Memorabilia and Souvenirs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-15T18:08:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bucks Editors', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bucks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Editors', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ebc38d0-f655-53d8-8b89-d5a9c5940342', 'word_count': 141, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ebc38d0-f655-53d8-8b89-d5a9c5940342'}, {'abstract': 'Elizabeth Warren, charged with setting up the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau, recently sat down with DealBook to discuss the attacks on the bureau, the delay in naming its director and her dog Otis.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/dealbook-portraits-elizabeth-warren/', 'snippet': 'Elizabeth Warren, charged with setting up the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau, recently sat down with DealBook to discuss the attacks on the bureau, the delay in naming its director and her dog Otis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Elizabeth Warren has spent nearly a year setting up the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau. The all-consuming project has led her to meet with dozens of politicians and bankers from every state. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'DealBook Portraits: Elizabeth Warren', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Warren, Elizabeth', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Financial Protection Bureau', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-15T18:10:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess and Mac William Bishop', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Mac', 'middlename': 'William', 'lastname': 'Bishop', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc1a90e4-cb08-5ab9-8a56-956d702e2fb4', 'word_count': 316, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc1a90e4-cb08-5ab9-8a56-956d702e2fb4'}, {'abstract': 'The season for summer cherries is as brief as it is sweet. But if you find yourself with an abundance of cherries this month, Martha Rose Shulman offers five new ways to enjoy them.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/summer-cherry-season-short-and-sweet/', 'snippet': 'The season for summer cherries is as brief as it is sweet. But if you find yourself with an abundance of cherries this month, Martha Rose Shulman offers five new ways to enjoy them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The season for summer cherries is as brief as it is sweet. But if you find yourself with an abundance of cherries this month, Martha Rose Shulman offers five new ways to enjoy them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Summer Cherry Season, Short and Sweet', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cherries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-15T18:13:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Parker-Pope', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker-Pope', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84955d64-43fd-5c7f-a8ed-56fb09563837', 'word_count': 200, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84955d64-43fd-5c7f-a8ed-56fb09563837'}, {'abstract': 'Now five years into a campaign by the Council of Fashion Designers of America to enact some sort of protection for original designs, the proponents of such legislation say they have their best chance yet at seeing a bill become law.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/designers-revisit-copyright-protection/', 'snippet': 'Now five years into a campaign by the Council of Fashion Designers of America to enact some sort of protection for original designs, the proponents of such legislation say they have their best chance yet at seeing a bill become law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Let’s see here. On Wednesday, ABS by Allen Schwartz began selling a series of royal-wedding-inspired dresses that includes a fairly good copy of the Alexander McQueen gown worn by Catherine, Duchess of Cambridge, for $1,100. That same night, Representative Bob Goodlatte, a Virginia Republican, reintroduced legislation seeking to grant copyright protection to designers, presumably discouraging exactly that kind of knockoff fashion. And on Friday, the Proenza Schouler designers Jack McCollough and Lazaro Hernandez went to Washington to plead their case before Congress.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Designers Revisit Copyright Protection', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Copyrights and Copyright Violations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-15T18:14:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb05b3a7-6e4e-500e-acbb-3e829d21dd98', 'word_count': 616, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb05b3a7-6e4e-500e-acbb-3e829d21dd98'}, {'abstract': 'The Sablich Brothers have ranked the top fantasy players for each position, including PPR formats.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/complete-2011-fantasy-football-rankings/', 'snippet': 'The Sablich Brothers have ranked the top fantasy players for each position, including PPR formats.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jason and Justin Sablich are here to help you with your fantasy football draft. The Sablich brothers will provide fantasy football advice throughout the season on this blog and on Twitter (@5thDownFantasy).  ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Complete 2011 Fantasy Football Rankings', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fantasy Sports', 'rank':