84794faef26e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/a5085f15-3bf1-5f5f-8e08-84794faef26e'}, {'abstract': 'There’s major turnover on the manga list this week with eight new additions.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/graphic-books-best-sellers-ghost-stories/', 'snippet': 'There’s major turnover on the manga list this week with eight new additions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s major turnover on the manga list this week with eight new additions. Only Naruto, a regular of the list, and Vampire Knight, about an academy whose evening students are creatures of the night, remain from the previous week. I’ve had difficulty reading manga: the traditional right-to-left layouts often confuse me and many series that are at Volume 50 or higher make me feel late to the party. Of the new books this week, Dengeki Daisy has a “Ghost” or “Sixth Sense” vibe to it. The series is about Teru Kurebayashi, who after the death of her brother has been receiving comforting messages from the mysterious Daisy, who communicates through her brother’s cell phone. Spooky! Volume 5 enters our list at No. 8 this week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Graphic Books Best Sellers: Ghost Stories', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comic Books and Strips', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-15T18:30:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Gene Gustines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': 'Gene', 'lastname': 'Gustines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09b2c4e2-95a4-59fe-9674-0ccab9748383', 'word_count': 424, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09b2c4e2-95a4-59fe-9674-0ccab9748383'}, {'abstract': 'July 15, 2011