dline': 'Euro Zone Seeks Deal On Greece By Thursday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-15T18:57:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Castle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/247899c3-9525-52a7-8408-2eba1c72eaad', 'word_count': 540, 'uri': 'nyt://article/247899c3-9525-52a7-8408-2eba1c72eaad'}, {'abstract': 'A philanthropic group tries to marry financial capital with new energy technologies to introduce devices intended for the 1.4 billion people who live off the grid.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/if-everyone-lighted-one-little-led/', 'snippet': 'A philanthropic group tries to marry financial capital with new energy technologies to introduce devices intended for the 1.4 billion people who live off the grid.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From Lenin to Franklin Delano Roosevelt, 20th-century political leaders made the provision of universal electricity a centerpiece of their programs and oratory. “Communism is Soviet power plus the electrification of the whole country,” one slogan went. Or, in the case of F.D.R.’s Tennessee Valley Authority, “T.V.A.: Electricity For All.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lighting the Hopes of the Gridless', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Light-Emitting Diodes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lighting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Solar Energy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations Foundation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-15T18:59:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicity Barringer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicity', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barringer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41a829c2-9f66-5cd3-a736-8921c003bdad', 'word_count': 574, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41a829c2-9f66-5cd3-a736-8921c003bdad'}, {'abstract': 'Tom Watson, 61, is not at the British Open simply for the memories, as his ace at the par-3 sixth hole demonstrated.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/16/sports/golf/16iht-ARENA16.html', 'snippet': 'Tom Watson, 61, is not at the British Open simply for the memories, as his ace at the par-3 sixth hole demonstrated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SANDWICH, England — Enjoy Tom Watson while we have him: while he is still relevant, truly relevant, at the British Open instead of a ceremonial bauble; while he is still there to put the modern game in perspective with insight and eye contact; while he is still capable of mentoring the youngsters on a links course and beating most of them, too.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/16/sports/golf/golf-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 355, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/16/sports/golf/golf-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 355}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/16/sports/golf/golf-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 686, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/16/sports/golf/golf-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/16/sports/golf/golf-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Hole in One and Age Lines; Watson Has Both', 'kicker': 'In the Arena', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Hole in One, Watson Shows He’s Not Playing for Memories', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'British Open (Golf)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Watson, Tom', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-15T19:00:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Clarey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clarey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8db63724-7619-5b08-8105-848f862b89e1', 'word_count': 1076, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8db63724-7619-5b08-8105-848f862b89e1'}, {'abstract': 'Video posted online by Syrian activists appears to show more protests and violence across the country on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/videos-show-bloody-crackdown-in-syria/', 'snippet': 'Video posted online by Syrian activists appears to show more protests and violence across the country on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As my colleague Anthony Shadid reports, Syrian activists said tens of thousands of protesters took to the streets in Syria on Friday, and the government responded with sprays of gunfire that killed 19 people across the country.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Videos Show Bloody Crackdown in Syria', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-15T19:03:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth A. Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4fec2854-fdda-571c-b4d4-2d3e4c0436aa', 'word_count': 334, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4fec2854-fdda-571c-b4d4-2d3e4c0436aa'}, {'abstract': 'Thor Hushovd, who wore the yellow jersey for most of the first week of the Tour de France, then lost it, barreled down a mountain pass to win Stage 13.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/16/sports/cycling/16iht-CYCLING16.html', 'snippet': 'Thor Hushovd, who wore the yellow jersey for most of the first week of the Tour de France, then lost it, barreled down a mountain pass to win Stage 13.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOURDES, France — Thor Hushovd, who wore the yellow jersey of the Tour de France leader for most of the first week of the race, then lost it, barre