': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/bb15e18c-ac24-5a1e-b9e5-3be80abb7424', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/bb15e18c-ac24-5a1e-b9e5-3be80abb7424'}, {'abstract': 'Justin Timberlake has morphed from a boy-band singer to a solo pop star to a lead actor in two major screen comedies this summer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/17/movies/justin-timberlake-friends-with-benefits-bad-teacher.html', 'snippet': 'Justin Timberlake has morphed from a boy-band singer to a solo pop star to a lead actor in two major screen comedies this summer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN Justin Timberlake tried out for the role of Sean Parker in “The Social Network,” the director David Fincher had a particular line from Aaron Sorkin’s script in mind. Sean, the former Napster executive who schools Mark Zuckerberg in the ways of Silicon Valley, is a slick seducer: “He was described in the screenplay as moving through the room like Frank Sinatra,” Mr. Fincher recalled.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/arts/17TIMBERLAKE--span/17TIMBERLAKE--span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/17/arts/17TIMBERLAKE--span/17TIMBERLAKE--span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/arts/17TIMBERLAKE--span/TIMBERLAKE-Jp-5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/arts/17TIMBERLAKE--span/TIMBERLAKE-Jp-5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'th