, 'lead_paragraph': 'If you haven’t thought about cooking with sage since Thanksgiving, now is a good time to think again. Fresh sage is great in a lot of summer dishes, from pastas to vegetables. You can get it at the farmers’ market, or in the supermarket in those annoying little plastic clamshells. Or ask your friend with the garden for a little bunch. But a little pot of sage wouldn’t go amiss on a sunny city kitchen windowsill, along with a thyme plant and a pot of rosemary. For a small investment you’ll have the sprig or two you need when you need it, ready to snip.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Garlic and Sage Broth, Good for a Hangover or a Light Supper', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Garlic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Herbs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soups', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-15T21:12:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Tanis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tanis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d1d210b-c34f-5994-9d69-f56a36c5ab38', 'word_count': 260, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d1d210b-c34f-5994-9d69-f56a36c5ab38'}, {'abstract': 'New musical releases from the Norwegian singer Thomas Dybdahl, the drummer Eric Harland, the jazz drummer Terri Lyne Carrington, the band Erimaj and the indie-rock band Ursa Minor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/17/arts/music/new-music-from-thomas-dybdahl-and-ursa-minor.html', 'snippet': 'New musical releases from the Norwegian singer Thom