oration.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/law-surprise-news-corp-s-hiring-of-williams-connolly/', 'snippet': 'The move underscores the central role Joel I. Klein is playing in managing the company’s mounting legal problems, and also highlights the void in legal leadership that currently exists at the News Corporation.', 'lead_paragraph': '7:19 p.m. | Updated Over the last four decades, two large law firms — Hogan Lovells and Skadden, Arps, Slate, Meagher & Flom — have served as primary outside counsel to the News Corporation, the media conglomerate run by Rupert Murdoch.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Law Surprise: News Corp.’s Hiring of Williams & Connolly', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wiretapping and Other Eavesdropping Devices and Methods', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klein, Joel I', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sullivan, Brendan V Jr', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hogan Lovells', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NEWS CORP', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News of the World', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Skadden Arps Slate Meagher & Flom', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WILLIAMS & CONNOLLY', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-15T21:13:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/27e63668-2400-563e-886c-05fb63f707b4', 'word_count': 831, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27e63668-2400-563e-886c-05fb63f707b4'}, {'abstract': 'Each year, about one-third of the carbon dioxide released through the burning of fossil fuels is absorbed by the world’s forests, a new study says. But deforestation is having a devastating effect.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/as-carbon-sinks-forests-are-even-mightier-than-assumed/', 'snippet': 'Each year, about one-third of the carbon dioxide released through the burning of fossil fuels is absorbed by the world’s forests, a new study says. But deforestation is having a devastating effect.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The world’s forests are magnificent palaces of biodiversity, teeming with wacky and wonderful creatures and plants that seem otherworldly. But they’re also something far more mundane although useful: they’re giant sponges, soaking up vast amounts of carbon dioxide.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As ‘Sinks’ for Carbon, Forests Are Even Mightier Than Assumed', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carbon Dioxide', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forests and Forestry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Science (Journal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-15T21:15:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanna M. Foster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization