es.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mark Schmitt, left, of the Roosevelt Institute and Tim Carney of the Washington Examiner debate the politics of taxes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/opinion/video-bhobamataxes/video-bhobamataxes-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/15/opinion/video-bhobamataxes/video-bhobamataxes-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/15/opinion/video-bhobamataxes/video-bhobamataxes-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/15/opinion/video-bhobamataxes/video-bhobamataxes-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bloggingheads: Obama and Taxes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-15T23:40:35+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Opinion', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'None None', 'person': [{'firstname': 'None', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'None', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/a18a9800-ccd4-5da7-a908-61fe38ee6f63', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/a18a9800-ccd4-5da7-a908-61fe38ee6f63'}, {'abstract': 'CBS eked out a victory as the top-rated network on Thursday night as 6.5 million viewers tuned in to “Big Brother” at 9 p.m.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/16/arts/television/cbs-edges-rivals.html', 'snippet': 'CBS eked out a victory as the top-rated network on Thursday night as 6.5 million viewers tuned in to “Big Brother” at 9 p.m.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CBS eked out a victory as the top-rated network on Thursday night as 6.5 million viewers tuned in to “Big Brother” at 9 p.m., more than any other program on the night, according to Nielsen’s estimates. ABC’s “Wipeout” had an audience of 6.4 million at 8, but ABC was second for the night over all. CBS also drew 6.4 million viewers at 10 for a repeat of “The Mentalist,” while it broadcast back-to-back reruns of its sitcoms “The Big Bang Theory” (6.3 million) and “Rules of Engagement” (4.9 million). Fox was third with “So You Think You Can Dance” at 8 (5.2 million) followed by a repeat of “Glee” (2.9 million), and NBC finished fourth with low-rated comedy reruns and “Love Bites” at 10 (2 million).', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'CBS Edges Rivals', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'CBS Edges Rivals', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-15T23:47:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Toff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Toff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/881c7cf1-9c88-5077-a570-af255344ee9e', 'word_count': 126, 'uri': 'nyt://article/881c7cf1-9c88-5077-a570-af255344ee9e'}, {'abstract': 'The Republican presidential candidate had less than $500,000 on hand at the end of the first quarter.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/cain-raised-2-million-and-contributed-500000/', 'snippet': 'The Republican presidential candidate had less than $500,000 on hand at the end of the first quarter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Herman Cain raised $2 million during his first quarter as a presidential candidate, according to his campaign’s Federal Election Commission filing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cain Raised $2 Million and Contributed $500,000', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cain, Herman', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-15T23:48:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sean Collins Walsh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sean', 'middlename': 'Collins', 'lastname': 'Walsh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34f09e83-46f0-5658-b705-697cd51d9e5a', 'word_count': 135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34f09e83-46f0-5658-b705-697cd51d9e5a'}, {'abstract': 'Though there was broad bipartisan acceptance of the idea to keep Mr. Mueller in place, Senate Republicans have thrown up a series of roadblocks to approving that proposal swiftly.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/16/us/politics/16mueller.html', 'snippet': 'Though there was broad bipartisan acceptance of the idea to keep Mr. Mueller in place, Senate Republicans have thrown up a series of roadblocks to approving that proposal swiftly.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Obama administration’s plans for Congress to smoothly extend the t