ame': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55ff5925-730f-5240-9178-a4027543b884', 'word_count': 985, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55ff5925-730f-5240-9178-a4027543b884'}, {'abstract': 'In Karoline Leach’s “Tryst,” at the Irish Repertory Theater, a scam artist finds a mark, then a conscience. Is it love?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/16/theater/reviews/tryst-by-karoline-leach-at-the-irish-repertory-theater-review.html', 'snippet': 'In Karoline Leach’s “Tryst,” at the Irish Repertory Theater, a scam artist finds a mark, then a conscience. Is it love?', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are several plays battling it out in “Tryst,” at the Irish Repertory Theater. Trouble is, none have enough oomph to win the fight. Part melodrama, part thriller, part comedy and part romance, the script wanders through the genres, offering a story that’s frequently interesting yet ultimately unfocused. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/16/arts/Tryst/Tryst-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 876, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/16/arts/Tryst/Tryst-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/16/arts/Tryst/Tryst-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'He’s a Con Man With a Heart of Gold', 'kicker': "Theater Review | 'Tryst'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'He’s a Con Man With a Heart of Gold', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Irish Repertory Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-16T00:03:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Jaworowski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jaworowski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1cfc679-5c2e-500c-9eeb-e8b369280e41', 'word_count': 301, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1cfc679-5c2e-500c-9eeb-e8b369280e41'}, {'abstract': 'The first two saxophones of the Pitchfork Music Festival belonged to Merrill Garbus, a k a Tune-Yards. Her set began not long after the one by EMA finished.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/pitchfork-tune-yards-and-ema/', 'snippet': 'The first two saxophones of the Pitchfork Music Festival belonged to Merrill Garbus, a k a Tune-Yards. Her set began not long after the one by EMA finished.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — The first two saxophones of the Pitchfork Music Festival belonged to Merrill Garbus, a k a Tune-Yards. The sax matters now more than it has at any time since the recently departed Clarence Clemons was at his peak. But unlike some of her kitsch-minded contemporaries, who use the instrument to connote post-wink post-irony, Ms. Garbus makes her sax players work, using their meaty lines to thicken her one-woman ukulele-and-drums-and-howls cornucopia. Hers is hard, muscular, construction-site soul, and the frenzied saxophones behind her highlighted how much sweat making this music generates.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pitchfork: Tune-Yards and EMA', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garbus, Merrill', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tune-Yards', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-16T00:05:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b284393-5a5c-58dd-bbb0-ef17df63dc77', 'word_count': 207, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b284393-5a5c-58dd-bbb0-ef17df63dc77'}, {'abstract': 'A former National Security Agency official received a year’s probation and community service in a leak case that ended with the government dropping the major charges.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/16/us/16leak.html', 'snippet': 'A former National Security Agency official received a year’s probation and community service in a leak case that ended with the government dropping the major charges.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BALTIMORE — A former spy agency official accused of leaking classified information to a newspaper walked out of court a free man on Friday, sentenced to a year’s probation and community service, after hearing the judge excoriate the government for its handling of the case.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Jail Time in Trial Over N.S.A. Leak', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Jail Time in Trial Over N.S.A. Leak', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Security Agency', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baltimore Sun', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Drake, Thomas A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bennett, Richard D', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-16T00:06:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Shane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5bb97720-8888-54c2-b6de-340ba8b6a39a', 'word_count': 688, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5bb97720-8888-54c2-b6de-340ba8b6a39a'}, {'abstract': 'A sampling of some of the most quotable moments from Friday at Royal St. George’s.', 'web_url': 'https://onpar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/15/plenty-to-say-at-the-british-open/', 'snippet': 'A sampling of some of the most quotable moments from Friday at Royal St. George’s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SANDWICH, ENGLAND — They came in by the dozens to the press tent on Friday at the British Open. A sampling of what they said:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Plenty to Say at the British Open', 'kicker': 'On Par', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'British Open (Golf)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-16T00:20:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Clarey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clarey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b51924ee-cd53-5a3c-81cd-7a846b0f921e', 'word_count': 529, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b51924ee-cd53-5a3c-81cd-7a846b0f921e'}, {'abstract': 'Discussions have paired any increase in the debt limit with deep spending cuts that many governors fear will hurt their states as they are recovering from the Great Recession.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/16/us/politics/16governors.html', 'snippet': 'Discussions have paired any increase in the debt limit with deep spending cuts that many governors fear will hurt their states as they are recovering from the Great Recession.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SALT LAKE CITY — The rancorous debate in Washington over whether to raise the federal debt ceiling is alarming many of the nation’s governors from both parties, who fear that whatever the outcome, much-needed money will almost certainly be drained from their states.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/16/us/governors-1/governors-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/16/us/governors-1/governors-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/16/us/governors-1/governors-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'No Matter How Debt Debate Ends, Governors See More Cuts for States', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Matter How Debt Debate Ends, Governors See More Cuts for States', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Governors (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'orga