ttps://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/16/opinion/16sat1.html', 'snippet': 'Even if lawmakers raise the debt limit on time, the economy is weak and getting weaker.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Catastrophic.” “Calamitous.” “Major crisis.” “Self-inflicted wound.” Those are some of the ways Ben Bernanke, the chairman of the Federal Reserve, has described the fallout if Congress fails to raise the debt limit by the Aug. 2 deadline. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Blundering Toward Recession: Beyond the Debt Stalemate', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Blundering Toward Recession: The debt limit stalemate is just one of the problems', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bernanke, Ben S', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-16T00:52:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/bfdcf996-1cde-56a7-99a2-1d9e96439f6a', 'word_count': 588, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bfdcf996-1cde-56a7-99a2-1d9e96439f6a'}, {'abstract': 'The town government of Quartzsite is split by accusations of corruption on one side and intentional disruption on the other.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/16/us/16quartzsite.html', 'snippet': 'The town government of Quartzsite is split by accusations of corruption on one side and intentional disruption on the other.', 'lead_paragraph': 'QUARTZSITE, Ariz. — Like many folks in this blink-and-miss-it town on the western edge of the state, Ed Foster moved here to escape the hustle and bustle. He is delighted that the main drag is just a couple of miles long, bookended by gas stations. It doesn’t take much more than a working sewer and water hookup to make him happy. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/16/us/quartzsite-1/quartzsite-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 365, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/16/us/quartzsite-1/quartzsite-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 365}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/16/us/quartzsite-1/quartzsite-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 733, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/16/us/quartzsite-1/quartzsite-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/16/us/quartzsite-1/quartzsite-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Kicking Up the Dust in an Arizona Desert Town', 'kicker': 'Quartzsite Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Kicking Up the Dust in an Arizona Desert Town', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Quartzsite (Ariz)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mayors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Local Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-16T00:55:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Medina', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Medina', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d7bcbd7-0811-57dd-9c23-80da55b8f78c', 'word_count': 963, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d7bcbd7-0811-57dd-9c23-80da55b8f78c'}, {'abstract': 'House Republican leaders announced that they would waste precious days next week on spending caps and a balanced budget amendment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/16/opinion/16sat2.html', 'snippet': 'House Republican leaders announced that they would waste precious days next week on spending caps and a balanced budget amendment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The increasingly urgent cries to resolve the debt-ceiling stalemate — from Wall Street, bond rating companies, the Federal Reserve chairman, the White House, the Senate and pretty much everyone else — seem unable to penetrate the soundproof bunker built by House Republicans. Their leaders announced on Friday that they would waste precious days next week on a hopeless crusade for spending caps and a balanced budget amendment.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Blundering Toward Recession: Urgency and Sense Elude the House', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Blundering Toward Recession: Urgency and common sense don’t penetrate the House', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-16T00:55:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7d0de8d-9b3a-5a74-8f1b-c1a02fd1d819', 'word_count': 415, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7d0de8d-9b3a-5a74-8f1b-c1a02fd1d819'}, {'abstract': 'Dominique Strauss-Kahn turned up in another place many New Yorkers go to get away: the wide green lawn of the Boston Symphony’s summer home, Tanglewood, in Lenox, Mass.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/16/nyregion/strauss-kahn-attends-two-concerts-in-the-berkshires.html', 'snippet': 'Dominique Strauss-Kahn turned up in another place many New Yorkers go to get away: the wide green lawn of the Boston Symphony’s summer home, Tanglewood, in Lenox, Mass.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the day Dominique Strauss-Kahn was released from house arrest, the paparazzi followed him to an Upper East Side restaurant. (One tabloid said the bill for his party of four came to $700.) Later some tabloids, cable channels and Web sites said he was spending the Independence Day weekend in the Hamptons. (He wasn’t.) ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/16/nyregion/SUB-DSK/SUB-DSK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/16/nyregion/SUB-DSK/SUB-DSK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/16/nyregion/SUB-DSK/SUB-DSK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy'