ay-of-reckoning/', 'snippet': 'Resignations and apologies in the News Corporation’s phone hacking crisis have some guessing what may come next.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Never apologize. Never back down. Never lose.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Day of Reckoning', 'kicker': 'The Thread', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wiretapping and Other Eavesdropping Devices and Methods', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brooks, Rebekah', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hinton, Les', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, James R', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NEWS CORP', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wall Street Journal', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-16T01:01:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Catapano', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Catapano', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2af33800-bcef-5a73-a974-8088c5f00788', 'word_count': 1429, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2af33800-bcef-5a73-a974-8088c5f00788'}, {'abstract': 'The New York City Opera used to present as many as 20 productions in a season at Lincoln Center; now it will present four, staged at three other sites.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/16/opinion/16sat4.html', 'snippet': 'The New York City Opera used to present as many as 20 productions in a season at Lincoln Center; now it will present four, staged at three other sites.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York City Opera’s schedule for the coming season is not quite busking in the streets, but close. The company, which used to present as many as 20 productions in a season at Lincoln Center, will present four, which will be staged at BAM, El Museo del Barrio, and the Gerald W. Lynch Theater at John Jay College. If the opera management has its way, the chorus and the orchestra would be demoted from full-time employment to freelance status. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Opera on the Loose', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Opera on the Loose', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Opera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mortier, Gerard', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Steel, George', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kellogg, Paul', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-16T01:03:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/32f6ffdf-bcc8-557b-9242-c41640ee9e28', 'word_count': 306, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32f6ffdf-bcc8-557b-9242-c41640ee9e28'}, {'abstract': 'A torrent of posts on Twitter — about a sportswriter who may or may not have been suspended — displayed the raw influence of social media.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/16/sports/torrent-on-twitter-in-support-of-espns-bruce-feldman.html', 'snippet': 'A torrent of posts on Twitter — about a sportswriter who may or may not have been suspended — displayed the raw influence of social media.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For nearly 24 hours through Friday afternoon, a slice of the sports world was engaged in a Twitter uprising to force ESPN to end its reported suspension of Bruce Feldman, one of its college football writers. Thousands of Twitter posts were expended in the #freebruce campaign, which rose to No. 4 on Twitter’s trends list, a wild geyser of pro-Feldmanism.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/16/sports/feldman-1/feldman-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 859, 'width': 687, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/16/sports/feldman-1/feldman-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/16/sports/feldman-1/feldman-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Tip Becomes a Twitter Torrent', 'kicker': 'Sports Business', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Tip Becomes A Twitter Torrent', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leach, Mike', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blogs and Blogging (Internet)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, Adam', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feldman, Bruce', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 