ier from Hoboken, N.J., is accused of helping himself to the fine wine and fine art of others, like a Picasso drawing worth $30,000.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A man with a larcenous bent and modest means, eyeing some trifle in a shop, might just walk in, grab it and walk out. But if this thief has very refined, very expensive tastes, coveting something like, say, a Picasso, how does he manage to steal that?', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/16/nyregion/SOMMELIER1/SOMMELIER1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 692, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/16/nyregion/SOMMELIER1/SOMMELIER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/16/nyregion/SOMMELIER1/SOMMELIER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sommelier Stole Art Openly, Police Say', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sommelier Stole Art Openly, Police Say', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hoboken (NJ)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Picasso, Pablo', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-16T01:49:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rich