], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6be85336-a83e-51a8-8ea3-1dd80205c44d', 'word_count': 1148, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6be85336-a83e-51a8-8ea3-1dd80205c44d'}, {'abstract': 'For the star of the reality show “Staten Island Cakes,” Sunday is a day for horseback riding and an Italian feast with the family.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/17/nyregion/on-sundays-vincent-buzzetta-takes-a-break-from-cake.html', 'snippet': 'For the star of the reality show “Staten Island Cakes,” Sunday is a day for horseback riding and an Italian feast with the family.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Vincent Buzzetta’s parents wanted him to be a pharmacist or a doctor, but instead settled for watching their chocoholic son become a cake-baking prodigy with his own shop, the Cake Artist, in West Brighton on Staten Island. Mr. Buzzetta, 21, who graduated from the French Culinary Institute’s pastry program at 18, now also has his own reality series on WE tv, “Staten Island Cakes.” He lives in the Old Town neighborhood of Staten Island with his parents, brother and sister, all of whom weigh in loudly on the frenetic show. ROBIN FINN', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/nyregion/17routine_span/17routine_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 352, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/17/nyregion/17routine_span/17routine_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 352}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/nyregion/17routine_span/17routine_span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/nyr