e': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-16T03:20:55+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Sunday Review', 'section_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/5e491a92-c658-5adf-9a31-963981da67d1', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/5e491a92-c658-5adf-9a31-963981da67d1'}, {'abstract': 'No. 109 Cheese and Wine offers a wide variety of cheeses, as well as charcuterie, paté and wine.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/17/nyregion/no-109-cheese-and-wine-offers-more-than-cheese-and-wine.html', 'snippet': 'No. 109 Cheese and Wine offers a wide variety of cheeses, as well as charcuterie, paté and wine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Summer entertaining without having to use the oven or stove is much easier if you live in the vicinity of No. 109 Cheese and Wine. This handsome shop, with a stonework wall offset by a guacamole green color scheme, carries a wealth of gourmet treats in addition to some 150 varieties of cheese. ', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Than a Name Suggests', 'kicker': 'Quick Bite | Ridgefield', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'More Than a Name Suggests', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cheese', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-16T03:25:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Brooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/797e6785-f88d-5163-b785-89dc07248253', 'word_count': 292, 'uri': 'nyt://article/797e6785-f88d-5163-b785-89dc07248253'}, {'abstract': 'Turkey launched a military offensive in the predominantly Kurdish southeast in retaliation for an ambush by Kurdish separatists that killed 13 soldiers on Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/16/world/europe/16briefs-Turkey.html', 'snippet': 'Turkey launched a military offensive in the predominantly Kurdish southeast in retaliation for an ambush by Kurdish separatists that killed 13 soldiers on Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Turkey launched a military offensive in the predominantly Kurdish southeast in retaliation for an ambush by Kurdish separatists that killed 13 soldiers on Thursday. Army helicopters were joined by civilian village guards in the operation, the semiofficial Anatolian News Agency reported. The army provided no details on the number of troops involved. The attack on Thursday, near Diyarbakir, was the deadliest ambush by Kurdish separatists in recent years, and Prime Minister Tayyip Erdogan vowed that the rebels would pay a heavy price. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Turkey: Army Strikes Back at Rebels', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | EUROPE', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Turkey: Army Strikes Back at Rebels', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kurds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-16T03:27:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sebnem Arsu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sebnem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Arsu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/7aadf7ed-adc7-528c-9965-b8d480bf03bc', 'word_count': 82, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7aadf7ed-adc7-528c-9965-b8d480bf03bc'}, {'abstract': 'At the Watch Factory Restaurant in Cheshire, Austrian white wines are paired with lighter-than-usual fare.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/17/nyregion/watch-factory-brings-austrian-food-to-cheshire-conn.html', 'snippet': 'At the Watch Factory Restaurant in Cheshire, Austrian white wines are paired with lighter-than-usual fare.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AUSTRIAN restaurants, with their robust cuisine, don’t normally come to mind as good choices for summer dining. But Austria’s white wines — exquisitely refreshing in the warm weather — combined with lighter-than-usual fare make the Watch Factory Restaurant in Cheshire well worth a visit.', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/nyregion/17DINECT1/17DINECT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 688, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/nyregion/17DINECT1/17DINECT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/17/nyregion/17DINECT1/17DINECT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Austrian Cuisine, Ready for Summer', 'kicker': 'Connecticut Dining | Cheshire', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Austrian Cuisine, Ready for Summer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-16T03:32:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Lyness', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lyness', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e993be36-5494-5b54-a1ff-b1dd95c149e6', 'word_count': 746, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e993be36-5494-5b54-a1ff-b1dd95c149e6'}, {'abstract': 'President Hugo Chávez said Friday that he would return to Cuba to begin a new phase of cancer treatment including chemotherapy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/16/world/americas/16briefs-Venezuela.html', 'snippet': 'President Hugo Chávez said Friday that he would return to Cuba to begin a new phase of cancer treatment including chemotherapy.', 'lead_paragraph': ' President Hugo Chávez said Friday that he would return to Cuba to begin a new phase of cancer treatment including chemotherapy. Mr. Chávez, 56, said he would go to Havana on Saturday “to begin what we’ve called the second phase.” He had surgery in Cuba last month to remove a cancerous tumor from his pelvic region. He acknowledged Wednesday that he required further treatment for cancer but has not said what kind of cancer he has. On Friday, he said he was sending a letter to the president of the National Assembly to secure authorization for his trip, as required by the Constitution. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Venezuelan Leader to Return to Cuba for Next Phase of Cancer Treatment', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | THE AMERICAS', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Venezuelan Leader to Return to Cuba For Next Phase of Cancer Treatment', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chavez, Hugo', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cuba', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venezuela', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-16T03:35:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexei Barrionuevo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexei', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barrionuevo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5639fba-f80b-5d8f-9577-30c18fb0d8c2', 'word_count': 104, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5639fba-f80b-5d8f-9577-30c18fb0d8c2'}, {'abstract': 'Red Moon Pizza offers more than the usual shopping-mall fare: spot-on pizza and owners connected to their customers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/17/nyregion/red-moon-pizza-has-decor-and-prices-from-another-era.html', 'snippet': 'Red Moon Pizza offers more than the usual shopping-mall fare: spot-on pizza and owners connected to their customers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many of the food outlets in Lawrenceville’s Mercer Mall (Chevy’s, Arby’s, Hooters) can be found, duplicated, in malls across America. But Red Moon Pizza, which has been in business for more than 30 years, is related to no other pizza parlor of that name. ', 'print_section': 'NJ', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Pizzeria From Another Era', 'kicker': 'Quick Bite | Lawrenceville', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Pizzeria From Another Era', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subjec