ffect: using a bigger fork leads people to eat less.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Use a Bigger Fork and You’ll Eat Less', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Behavior', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-16T12:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b607163-d82d-599d-b3a1-8b61bde057a5', 'word_count': 276, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b607163-d82d-599d-b3a1-8b61bde057a5'}, {'abstract': 'Despite her concerns about detentions of journalists, Secretary of State Hillary Rodham Clinton said Turkey could serve as a model for Arab nations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/17/world/middleeast/17turkey.html', 'snippet': 'Despite her concerns about detentions of journalists, Secretary of State Hillary Rodham Clinton said Turkey could serve as a model for Arab nations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISTANBUL — In a series of pointed statements, Secretary of State Hillary Rodham Clinton criticized Turkey, a close NATO ally, on Saturday, for its mixed record on press and other freedoms.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/world/17turkey/17turkey-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/17/world/17turkey/17turkey-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'su