nization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1baec9e-77a9-560f-a23d-201e11d42d72', 'word_count': 1154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1baec9e-77a9-560f-a23d-201e11d42d72'}, {'abstract': 'It is unclear exactly how much Gov. Rick Perry’s extensive travels cost, who foots the bill and what part of the tab taxpayers pick up.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/17/us/17ttperry.html', 'snippet': 'It is unclear exactly how much Gov. Rick Perry’s extensive travels cost, who foots the bill and what part of the tab taxpayers pick up.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Rick Perry has been burning up the miles since he won re-election last year. He is on track to have made nearly 50 stops in 21 states by November.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Pays Rick Perry’s Travel Bill?', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Perry Racks Up Miles, and Costs, as He Travels the U.S. to Spread His Message', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-16T15:30:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thanh Tan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thanh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a0d6594c-f7dd-5fbd-854a-9ec9cd72d57c', 'word_count': 699, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a0d6594c-f7dd-5fbd-854a-9ec9cd72d57c'}, {'abstract': 'With as many as 500 free agents potentially available and with time short, a labor agreement would probably bring a gold rush.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/16/murky-waters-this-year-in-free-agent-pool/', 'snippet': 'With as many as 500 free agents potentially available and with time short, a labor agreement would probably bring a gold rush.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At some point, perhaps soon, the N.F.L. and its players will reach a new labor agreement, and the great free-agent gold rush of 2011 will begin. But for now, for as many as 500 free agents, there is no blueprint, no courting or being courted, only anticipation for what comes next and more labor pains induced in the form of unemployment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Murky Waters This Year in Free-Agent Pool', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Free Agents (Sports)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barber, Tiki', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burress, Plaxico', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holmes, Santonio', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Brad', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-16T15:37:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Greg Bishop', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Greg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bishop', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b869dac-67de-5c25-a90f-27dbd37b9033', 'word_count': 545, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b869dac-67de-5c25-a90f-27dbd37b9033'}, {'abstract': 'Jim Brown says ex-players appear to be gaining nothing despite progress in negotiations toward ending the N.F.L. lockout.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/17/sports/football/jim-brown-highlights-gap-between-current-and-retired-nfl-players.html', 'snippet': 'Jim Brown says ex-players appear to be gaining nothing despite progress in negotiations toward ending the N.F.L. lockout.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The N.F.L. legend Jim Brown added his voice to the growing chorus of retired players who feel that they have been discarded like worn tires. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Retired Players, No Seat at the Table', 'kicker': 'Sports of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Retired Players, No Seat at the Table', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Jim', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lockouts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-16T15:40:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By William C. Rhoden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Rhoden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d68f3fa5-0cb9-5b33-b688-ebce10fe2d27', 'word_count': 720, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d68f3fa5-0cb9-5b33-b688-ebce10fe2d27'}, {'abstract': 'As in N.C.A.A. football, colleges have been moving in and out of conferences, shrinking membership and prospects for some traditional powerhouses.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/17/sports/hockey/hockey-conferences-imperiled-by-reshuffling.html', 'snippet': 'As in N.C.A.A. football, colleges have been moving in and out of conferences, shrinking membership and prospects for some traditional powerhouses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Being the commissioner of the Central Collegiate Hockey Association, one of the nation’s leading conferences, is ordinarily a pretty good deal. The conference, which has existed since 1971, sends multiple teams to the N.C.A.A. men’s hockey tournament every year and has won 9 of the past 27 national championships.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reshuffling Blurs Picture, Jeopardizing Conferences', 'kicker': 'College Hockey', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Reshuffling Blurs Picture, Jeopardizing Conferences', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Collegiate Athletic Assn', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-16T15:56:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pat Borzi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pat', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borzi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/775202a1-1f5a-5de2-8b54-104d262a53fe', 'word_count': 763, 'uri': 'nyt://article/775202a1-1f5a-5de2-8b54-104d262a53fe'}, {'abstract': 'Emily Cox and Henry Rathvon remain fresh and relevant, while their puzzle describes something that is not.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/16/peak-acrostic/', 'snippet': 'Emily Cox and Henry Rathvon remain fresh and relevant, while their puzzle describes something that is not.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SECOND SUNDAY PUZZLE — If you watch a lot of television, there comes a point in most series where the entertainment level drops precipitously, and that is the point where the show is said to have “jumped the shark.” It might be a case of a specific character doing something that just strains viewers’ credulity, or the entire storyline might just lose its oomph. Either way, it’s a clear signal to everyone involved that it might be time to re-tool the show or pack up their toys and go home.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Variety: A Past-its-Peak Acrostic', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Acrostic Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-16T16:00:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac3df148-8781-51d4-8868-27768e854023', 'word_count': 343, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac3df148-8781-51d4-8868-27768e854023'}, {'abstract': 'I’m struck by how rapidly the women have improved, even since 2007 — and by a weird sensation of watching history in motion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/17/sports/soccer/womens-world-cup-this-time-a-show-worth-watching.html', 'snippet': 'I’m struck by how rapidly the women have improved, even since 2007 — and by a weird sensation of watching history in motion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the Women’s World Cup was played the United States in 1999, I went to the opening game at Giants Stadium, eager to be supportive. The atmosphere was great, the soccer dreadful. So slow, so clumsy — the women looked as if they were trying to play soccer under water. In 2003, and in 2007, I had trouble making myself watch on television. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Women’s World Cup: This Time, a Show Worth Watching', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'This Time, a Show Worth Watching', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wambach, Abby', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Solo, Hope', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's World Cup (Soccer)", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marta', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hamm, Mia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-16T16:05:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lawrie Mifflin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lawrie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mifflin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/445c41f5-601d-52e2-ad5c-61e8988001a6', 'word_count': 611, 'uri': 'nyt://article/445c41f5-601d-52e2-ad5c-61e8988001a6'}, {'abstract': 'Readers sound off on the latest headlines.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/17/sports/letters-to-the-editor.html', 'snippet': 'Readers sound off on the latest headlines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Sports Editor:', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Letters to the Editor', 'kicker': 'In-Box', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Player’s Worth Beyond the Field', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's World Cup (Soccer)", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jeter, Derek', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-16T16:06:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/a26af636-aab4-5dda-b1cd-45c4f5c079ac', 'word_count': 435, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a26af636-aab4-5dda-b1cd-45c4f5c079ac'}, {'abstract': 'Nobile, in his first full season of drag racing in the N.H.R.A., is not getting paid by his team, but he has won two of the last seven events in the pro stock class and has become a sensation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/17/sports/vincent-nobile-a-drag-racing-whiz-kid.html', 'snippet': 'Nobile, in his first full season of drag racing in the N.H.R.A., is not getting paid by his team, but he has won two of the last seven events in the pro stock class and has become a sensation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Vincent Nobile is 19 years old, just completed his first year as a business administration major at Adelphi University and lives with his parents in Dix Hills on Long Island. Nobile played shortstop in high school, and his bedroom is decorated with Yankees memorabilia.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/sports/dog-nobile-2/dog-nobile-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 870, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/sports/dog-nobile-2/dog-nobile-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/17/sports/dog-nobile-2/dog-nobile-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Vincent Nobile: A Drag-Racing Whiz Kid', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Drag-Racing Whiz Kid', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drag Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nobile, Vincent', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Racing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-16T16:12:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Caldwell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caldwell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6329ac3-baad-593c-830d-7aa8d7332f5c', 'word_count': 864, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6329ac3-baad-593c-830d-7aa8d7332f5c'}, {'abstract': 'Sim Bhullar, a 7-foot-4 teenager from Toronto, has a chance to be Asia’s next great basketball ambassador.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/17/sports/basketball/sim-bhullar-could-be-asias-next-basketball-superstar.html', 'snippet': 'Sim Bhullar, a 7-foot-4 teenager from Toronto, has a chance to be Asia’s next great basketball ambassador.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NORTH AUGUSTA, S.C. — When the 7-foot-4 center Sim Bhullar walks through airports, people flock to him and ask him to pose for pictures. When he recently visited India, where his parents were born, so many approached him at the Sikh shrine known as the Golden Temple that he was ushered into an office. People hung on the bars of the office windows to catch a glance. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/sports/YBHULLAR2/YBHULLAR2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 664, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/sports/YBHULLAR2/YBHULLAR2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/17/sports/YBHULLAR2/YBHULLAR2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'So Much Potential, So Far to Go for Young Basketball Prospect', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'So Much Potential, So Far to Go', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yao Ming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bhullar, Sim', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Toronto (Ontario)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-16T16:16:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pete Thamel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pete', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thamel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/993e6a5b-5c90-5dbf-a95b-f74559ed2fb7', 'word_count': 1172, 'uri': 'nyt://article/993e6a5b-5c90-5dbf-a95b-f74559ed2fb7'}, {'abstract': 'A confident Japanese team, with much of the world wishing it well, hopes to get its first victory over the United States in Sunday’s Women’s World Cup final.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/16/world-cup-finalists-size-up-their-opponents/', 'snippet': 'A confident Japanese team, with much of the world wishing it well, hopes to get its first victory over the United States in Sunday’s Women’s World Cup final.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRANKFURT, Germany — If it wasn’t yet apparent how confident Japan had grown after victories over Germany and Sweden in the Women’s World Cup, it became clear when Coach Norio Sasaki was asked about potential American vulnerability in Sunday’s final.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'World Cup Finalists Size Up Their Opponents', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's World Cup (Soccer)", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sundhage, Pia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-16T16:16:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeré Longman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeré', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Longman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1e74525-7f72-54ee-8e41-928dde02f332', 'word_count': 729, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1e74525-7f72-54ee-8e41-928dde02f332'}, {'abstract': 'The 5-foot-11 striker for the U.S. women’s national team has proved adept at scoring crucial goals with her head.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/17/sports/soccer/womens-world-cup-abby-wambach-stands-tall-for-us.html', 'snippet': 'The 5-foot-11 striker for the U.S. women’s national team has proved adept at scoring crucial goals with her head.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRANKFURT — Abby Wambach’s halftime instructions to a teammate were simple and insistent: Just put the ball on the back post. We’ll get a goal.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'cap