497, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1d1380e-82c9-58d0-b787-a4c4f46ba152'}, {'abstract': 'With an odd number of men, making the cut and pairings the format, someone was destined to not have a playing partner. Matt Millar was the odd man out.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/17/sports/golf/last-golfer-in-becomes-odd-one-out.html', 'snippet': 'With an odd number of men, making the cut and pairings the format, someone was destined to not have a playing partner. Matt Millar was the odd man out.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SANDWICH, England — Safely inside the interview tent with water still dripping off the bill of his cap, Matt Millar, the first man to finish on Saturday, looked over his shoulder toward the British Open course where he had just shot a 10-over-par 80.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/sports/subBUNKER/subBUNKER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/17/sports/subBUNKER/subBUNKER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/sports/subBUNKER/subBUNKER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 615, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Last Golfer in Becomes Odd One Out', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Last Golfer to Make Cut Becomes Odd One Out', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'British Open (Golf)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-16T16:31:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christop