oblem for baseball players competing during the day.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/17/sports/baseball/light-eyed-players-deal-with-glare-and-doubts.html', 'snippet': 'Light-colored eyes are believed to be more sensitive to bright sunlight, which can be a problem for baseball players competing during the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'During the third inning of a March 17 spring training game, Chicago White Sox shortstop Alexei Ramirez hit a soft fly ball to left field. Milwaukee Brewers outfielder Mark Kotsay had his sunglasses on, as he always does, but as he ran in toward the ball it disappeared into the glare of the harsh Arizona sun.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/sports/17blue2/17blue2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 694, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/sports/17blue2/17blue2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/17/sports/17blue2/17blue2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Light-Eyed Players Deal With Glare, and Doubts', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dealing With Glare, and Doubts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Eyes and Eyesight', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kotsay, Mark', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hamilton, Josh', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sunlight', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nevin, Phil', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date'