up.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alcatraz, the fog-shrouded rock transformed from an island prison into one of San Francisco’s most famous landmarks, is about to get a new identity — best seat in the house for the America’s Cup.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spectators Will Escape to Alcatraz for the Cup', 'kicker': 'The Bay Citizen', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spectators Will Escape To Alcatraz For the Cup', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALCATRAZ (SAN FRANCISCO)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "AMERICA'S CUP", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-16T20:43:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Upton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Upton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2aed2c9e-2a95-542e-9fb1-cb63e430bd42', 'word_count': 473, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2aed2c9e-2a95-542e-9fb1-cb63e430bd42'}, {'abstract': 'Sudden oak death, a killer disease, is attacking coastal oak trees. But scientists have found one healthy swath of forest that could be the perfect laboratory for a preventive treatment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/17/us/17bcoak.html', 'snippet': 'Sudden oak death, a killer disease, is attacking coastal oak trees. But scientists have found one healthy swath of forest that could be the perfect laboratory for a preventive treatment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a hot summer day in 2008, a pair of plant disease researchers made an extraordinary discovery as they toured a hillside forest in San Mateo County: a stand of trees that had not been infected by the killer disease known as sudden oak death.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/us/17BCOAK/17BCOAK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/17/us/17BCOAK/17BCOAK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/us/17BCOAK/17BCOAK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Scientists Fight a Deadly Oak-Tree Disease', 'kicker': 'The Bay Citizen', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Scientists Fight a Deadly Oak-Tree Disease', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trees and Shrubs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forests and Forestry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-16T20:48:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Upton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Upton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2b17a56-a6f4-54a3-97b0-bd360f9d4467', 'word_count': 723, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2b17a56-a6f4-54a3-97b0-bd360f9d4467'}, {'abstract': 'After a homeless man was killed by a transit officer this month, questions have been raised about whether BART is carrying out recommendations issued after the last shooting.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/17/us/17bcbart.html', 'snippet': 'After a homeless man was killed by a transit officer this month, questions have been raised about whether BART is carrying out recommendations issued after the last shooting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After a white BART police officer shot and killed an unarmed black man shortly after New Year’s 2009, the transit agency agreed to 127 policy changes recommended by an independent auditor. They included arming officers with Tasers and providing crisis-intervention training for the BART police force.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/us/17BCBART/17BCBART-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 365, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/17/us/17BCBART/17BCBART-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 365}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/us/17BCBART/17BCBART-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 686, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/us/17BCBART/17BCBART-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/17/us/17BCBART/17BCBART-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Latest BART Shooting Prompts New Discussion of Reforms', 'kicker': 'The Bay Citizen', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Latest BART Shooting Prompts New Discussion of Reforms', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transit Systems', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations',