zing through dark tunnels inside the jail in Odessa, they nearly succeeded, taking advantage of weaknesses in the West Texas facility. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/us/17TTJAILS1/17TTJAILS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/17/us/17TTJAILS1/17TTJAILS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/us/17TTJAILS1/17TTJAILS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 701, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/us/17TTJAILS1/17TTJAILS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/17/us/17TTJAILS1/17TTJAILS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jailbreaks Make for Good TV, but Remain Rare', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jailbreaks Make for Good TV, but Remain Rare', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prison Escapes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-16T21:29:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brandi Grissom', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brandi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grissom', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/212d94e0-8fd1-507c-869e-942e6f190e8d', 'word_count': 1122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/212d94e0-8fd1-507c-869e-942e6f190e8d'}, {'abstract': 'Some people may find Texas beaches underwhelming, but they have probably never been to. Surfside, Matagorda, Padre Island or St. Jo’s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/17/us/17tttravel.html', 'snippet': 'Some people may find Texas beaches underwhelming, but they have probably never been to. Surfside, Matagorda, Padre Island or St. Jo’s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tell someone you’re vacationing on the Texas coast, and you’ll probably get a sympathetic smile. This is a fair reaction in a state with more than 350 miles of coastline and, no offense to God’s country, a lot of underwhelming beaches. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21B', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/us/17TTTRAVEL/17TTTRAVEL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/17/us/17TTTRAVEL/17TTTRAVEL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/us/17TTTRAVEL/17TTTRAVEL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/us/17TTTRAVEL/17TTTRAVEL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/17/us/17TTTRAVEL/17TTTRAVEL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Four Hidden Beach Getaways, All Within State Lines', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Four Hidden Beach Getaways, All Within State Lines', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beaches', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-16T21:29:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stirling Kelso', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stirling', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kelso', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/31b3e953-8e15-5cdd-af14-2d77886148fd', 'word_count': 824, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31b3e953-8e15-5cdd-af14-2d77886148fd'}, {'abstract': 'Spooked by the specter of Islamic radicalism and the challenges posed by increasingly influential religious leaders, the Tajik authorities have been working fervently to curb religious expression.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/17/world/asia/17tajikistan.html', 'snippet': 'Spooked by the specter of Islamic radicalism and the challenges posed by increasingly influential religious leaders, the Tajik authorities have been working fervently to curb religious expression.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DUSHANBE, Tajikistan — Islam is blossoming in Tajikistan. Beards are in style. Headscarves, too. Bazaars are doing a booming trade in prayer rugs, religious audio recordings and gaudy clocks featuring Muslim holy sites.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/world/17tajikistan/17tajikistan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/17/world/17tajikistan/17tajikistan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/world/17tajikistan/TAJIKISTAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/world/17tajikistan/17tajikistan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/17/world/17tajikistan/17tajikistan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'On the Rise in Tajikistan, Islam Worries an Authoritarian Government', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On the Rise in Tajikistan, Islam Worries an Authoritarian Government', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tajikistan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rakhmon, Emomali', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tajiks (Ethnic Group)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-16T21:42:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Schwirtz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwirtz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d96c52d-2081-5a16-a944-3805d59a3238', 'word_count': 1059, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d96c52d-2081-5a16-a944-3805d59a3238'}, {'abstract': 'Daniel A. Finan just won’t let the fun end.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/16/sight/', 'snippet': 'Daniel A. Finan just won’t let the fun end.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SUNDAY’S PUZZLE — I really, really liked this one. Who knew there were so many familiar phrases that had a letter or letters within them that made the same sound as the last word in the phrase? Daniel A. Finan has found them for us, matched them up according to letter counts, and created a puzzle that just rocks, themewise. I would have liked it even more if there hadn’t been so much jumping around (“See X Down to get a hint to the answer to Y Across”), but all in all, I enjoyed myself.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sunday: The End Is in Sight', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-16T22:00:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/46dc9a9e-84ab-5b7a-9ea0-e3d001f5973c', 'word_count': 355, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46dc9a9e-84ab-5b7a-9ea0-e3d001f5973c'}, {'abstract': 'In a small hospital wing in Canandaigua, N.Y., the V.A. is mending its reputation for unresponsiveness.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/17/opinion/sunday/17sun4.html', 'snippet': 'In a small hospital wing in Canandaigua, N.Y., the V.A. is mending its reputation for unresponsiveness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Veterans Affairs Department says that it is not only making strides in treating post-traumatic stress disorder and brain injuries and in preventing suicides, but is also upending its reputation for bureaucratic delays and unresponsiveness.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/sunday-review/0717SReditorial/0717SReditorial-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 842, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/sunday-review/0717SReditorial/0717SReditorial-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/17/sunday-review/0717SReditorial/0717SReditorial-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The V.A. Tries to Get Beyond Its Culture of No', 'kicker': 'Editorial | Sunday Observer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The V.A. Tries to Get Beyond Its Culture of No', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Veterans Affairs Department', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-16T22:05:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lawrence Downes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lawrence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Downes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ab6285e-9bb0-5267-b0b3-2f760f4223b7', 'word_count': 778, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ab6285e-9bb0-5267-b0b3-2f760f4223b7'}, {'abstract': 'A new agreement between major Internet service providers and movie studios and record labels has some troubling elements.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/17/opinion/sunday/17sun3.html', 'snippet': 'A new agreement between major Internet service providers and movie studios and record labels has some troubling elements.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After years of trying to stop illegal downloading of music and videos by suing their fans, enticing them to pay through easier formats, and encrypting digital files, the music and movie industries hope they have found an effective approach to fighting copyright theft. This month, several major Internet service providers, including Verizon, Comcast, AT&T and Time Warner Cable, agreed to help movie studios and record labels identify Internet users who downloaded copyrighted content illicitly, warn them about the piracy and punish recalcitrant abusers. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Try at Curbing Piracy', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A New Try at Curbing Piracy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recordings and Downloads (Audio)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Copyrights and Copyright Violations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telephones and Telecommunications', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-16T22:05:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/889db381-9fa2-55c6-8774-504e96bfda7c', 'word_count': 508, 'uri': 'nyt://article/889db381-9fa2-55c6-8774-