opinion/sunday/17sun2.html', 'snippet': 'Rampant cheating by teachers in Atlanta’s schools hurts students and destroys trust.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A cheating scandal in which scores of teachers and principals in Atlanta’s public schools falsified student test results has thrown the system into chaos and made its name synonymous with fraud. This shameful episode has destroyed trust in the schools and made it impossible to determine how much students are learning and whether the system is doing its job. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Are They Learning?', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Are They Learning? Rampant cheating by teachers in Atlanta’s schools hurts students and destroys trust', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cheating', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests and Examinations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'No Child Left Behind Act', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hall, Beverly L', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Atlanta (Ga)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-16T22:05:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/cbb235cb-1121-5c4d-8136-adb09a5dfc6e', 'word_count': 486, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cbb235cb-1121-5c4d-8136-adb09a5dfc6e'}, {'abstract': 'Test your knowledge of recent events.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/17/opinion/sunday/17wait.html', 'snippet': 'Test your knowledge of recent events.', 'lead_pa