ded Red Bulls striker Juan Agudelo and Sporting Kansas City captain Omar Bravo to the league’s all-star team on Saturday.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/17/agudelo-and-bravo-added-to-m-l-s-all-star-team/', 'snippet': 'Major League Soccer Commissioner Don Garber added Red Bulls striker Juan Agudelo and Sporting Kansas City captain Omar Bravo to the league’s all-star team on Saturday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Major League Soccer Commissioner Don Garber added Red Bulls striker Juan Agudelo and Sporting Kansas City captain Omar Bravo to the league’s all-star team with his two picks Saturday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Agudelo and Bravo Added to M.L.S. All-Star Team', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Soccer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-17T06:11:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Das', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Das', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84e0fcad-8735-530f-b0d9-bad1c8907122', 'word_count': 288, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84e0fcad-8735-530f-b0d9-bad1c8907122'}, {'abstract': 'Jeré Longman looks at how Abby Wambach got so good at heading the ball, and how that skill has meant success for the United States women’s national team.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/17/abby-wambachs-head-for-the-game/', 'snippet': 'Jeré Longman looks at how Abby Wambach got so good at heading the ball, and how that skill has meant success for the United States women’s national team.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jeré Longman looks at how Abby Wambach got so good at heading the ball, and how that skill has meant success for the United States women’s national team. Read the article here — don’t miss the graphic charting how many of Wambach’s World Cup shots have come on headers — and come back to comment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Abby Wambach’s Head for the Game', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's World Cup (Soccer)", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-17T11:18:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/059e0c82-74ab-55af-a6f7-e4a39863a8ad', 'word_count': 55, 'uri': 'nyt://article/059e0c82-74ab-55af-a6f7-e4a39863a8ad'}, {'abstract': 'Britain’s most highly ranked police official resigned, and Rebekah Brooks, the former chief executive of News International, was arrested.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/world/europe/18hacking.html', 'snippet': 'Britain’s most highly ranked police official resigned, and Rebekah Brooks, the former chief executive of News International, was arrested.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Britain’s top police official resigned on Sunday, the latest casualty of the phone-hacking scandal engulfing British public life, just hours after Rebekah Brooks, the former chief executive of Rupert Murdoch’s News International, was arrested on suspicion of illegally intercepting phone calls and bribing the police. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/18/world/HACKING-1/HACKING-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/18/world/HACKING-1/HACKING-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/18/world/HACKING-1/HACKING-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Arrest and Scotland Yard Resignation Roil Britain', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tabloid Scandal Topples Leader at Scotland Yard', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stephenson, Paul Robert', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brooks, Rebekah', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News of the World', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Scotland Yard (Metropolitan Police Service)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wiretapping and Other Eavesdropping Devices and Methods', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News International Ltd', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-17T13:07:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Lyall and Don Van Natta Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lyall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Don', 'middlename': 'Van', 'lastname': 'Natta', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/829c2a11-5c96-571b-9401-4af60e41080e', 'word_count': 1396, 'uri': 'nyt://article/829c2a11-5c96-571b-9401-4af60e41080e'}, {'abstract': 'Darren Clarke of Northern Ireland fought off the winds as well as challenges from Phil Mickelson and Dustin Johnson to win his first major title at the British Open on Sunday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/sports/golf/2011-british-open-drama-unfolds-in-gusty-final-round.html', 'snippet': 'Darren Clarke of Northern Ireland fought off the winds as well as challenges from Phil Mickelson and Dustin Johnson to win his first major title at the British Open on Sunday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SANDWICH, England — On Sunday at Royal St. George’s, just before Darren Clarke tapped in the putt that would seal it all, the one that would mean the wait was over, that the British Open was his and the 20-year quest had come to an end, he stepped back, grinned, and spoke to himself.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/18/sports/golf/18open-pic4/18open-pic4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/18/sports/golf/18open-pic4/18open-pic4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/18/sports/golf/18open-pic4/18open-pic4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 723, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/18/sports/golf/18open-pic4/18open-pic4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/18/sports/golf/18open-pic4/18open-pic4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Holding Steady on Dreary Day, Clarke Captures His First Major', 'kicker': 'British Open | Royal St. Georges', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Steady Finish To Long Pursuit As Clarke Wins His First Major', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'British Open (Golf)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mickelson, Phil', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clarke, Darren', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Dustin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-17T13:57:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Dorman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dorman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/919b712e-e943-5791-8148-f5d406313e22', 'word_count': 1151, 'uri': 'nyt://article/919b712e-e943-5791-8148-f5d406313e22'}, {'abstract': 'The consequences of an inadequate stimulus.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/17/penny-wise-policy/', 'snippet': 'The consequences of an inadequate stimulus.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mark Thoma sends me to Jonathan Schwarz making the case that Obama knew perfectly well that the stimulus should have been bigger. I’m not sure that lets his advisers completely off the hook; there’s a big difference between saying, well, the macroeconomic case says this should be bigger, but smaller is OK, and saying — as they should have, and maybe some did — that a weak stimulus runs a large risk of setting us on a path toward a lost decade.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Penny-Wise Policy', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-17T14:03:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/75124357-a3a7-58d3-bed2-a36d46d6e14d', 'word_count': 274, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75124357-a3a7-58d3-bed2-a36d46d6e14d'}, {'abstract': 'Secretary of State Hillary Rodham Clinton on Sunday emphasized Washington’s “strong support” for Greece’s commitment to tough austerity measures.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/world/europe/18clinton.html', 'snippet': 'Secretary of State Hillary Rodham Clinton on Sunday emphasized Washington’s “strong support” for Greece’s commitment to tough austerity measures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATHENS — Secretary of State Hillary Rodham Clinton on Sunday emphasized Washington’s “strong support” for Greece’s commitment to right its debt-ridden economy through tough austerity measures, and she thanked the government for its contributions to NATO-led operations in Libya and\xa0diplomatic efforts in the Middle East. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/18/world/CLINTON/CLINTON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 709, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/18/world/CLINTON/CLINTON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/0