ned Out in Vancouver', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grass', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stillitano, Charlie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Soccer', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vancouver (British Columbia)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-17T14:29:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Bell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1dc198f-eab6-56bc-8aee-ef5cfaf13c46', 'word_count': 651, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1dc198f-eab6-56bc-8aee-ef5cfaf13c46'}, {'abstract': 'Despite a series of allegations of corruption, the 24-man executive committee of soccer’s governing body retains a culture of favors and perks, if not outright bribery.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/sports/soccer/18iht-fifa18.html', 'snippet': 'Despite a series of allegations of corruption, the 24-man executive committee of soccer’s governing body retains a culture of favors and perks, if not outright bribery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — The titans of international soccer are used to pampering. Motorcades. Police escorts. Five-star hotels. Lavish dinners. Cash allowances of $500 a day, and an additional $250 for their wives or girlfriends.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For FIFA Executives, Luxury and Favors', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For FIFA Executives, Luxury and Favors', 'name':