es and Japan from Frankfurt, Germany.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Japan won the Women’s World Cup for the first time on Sunday, stunning the United States in a penalty kick shootout after the teams played a pulsating 2-2 tie in Frankfurt, Germany.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Women’s World Cup Final: Japan Stuns U.S. in Shootout', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's World Cup (Soccer)", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-17T17:22:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Das', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Das', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e134ca6-1883-5c99-bc14-ccb58d482bb9', 'word_count': 4034, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e134ca6-1883-5c99-bc14-ccb58d482bb9'}, {'abstract': 'The group representing Greece’s private creditors said that progress was being made in talks on international banks’ involvement in the Greek bailout.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/business/global/creditors-see-talks-advancing-on-2nd-greek-rescue.html', 'snippet': 'The group representing Greece’s private creditors said that progress was being made in talks on international banks’ involvement in the Greek bailout.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The group representing Greece’s private creditors said Sunday that progress was being made in working out the involvement of international banks in the next Greek bailout.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2