rd-place team missing its four best hitters should look.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/18/sports/baseball/18mets-pic/18mets-pic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 967, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/18/sports/baseball/18mets-pic/18mets-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/18/sports/baseball/18mets-pic/18mets-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Reality Hits Hard, but the Short-Handed Mets Don’t, in a Sloppy Defeat', 'kicker': 'Phillies 8, Mets 5', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Reality Hits Hard, but the Short-Handed Mets Don’t, in a Sloppy Defeat', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bay, Jason', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reyes, Jose', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Philadelphia Phillies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pelfrey, Mike', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Howard, Ryan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rollins, Jimmy', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harris, Willie', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-17T21:18:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Keh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d65ccb8-3f01-5d80-809f-efab05e0fea6', 'word_count': 785, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d65ccb8-3f01-5d80-809f-efab05e0fea6'}, {'abstract': 'The Mariinsky Ballet’s season at the Metropolitan Opera House included three programs, two of ballets created in the 21st century, and the third a pair of ballets from 1947 and 1967.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/arts/dance/carmen-suite-from-mariinsky-ballet-review.html', 'snippet': 'The Mariinsky Ballet’s season at the Metropolitan Opera House included three programs, two of ballets created in the 21st century, and the third a pair of ballets from 1947 and 1967.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The most important feature of the Mariinsky Ballet’s season at the Metropolitan Opera House last week is what it didn’t contain. It’s 50 years since the company (then named Kirov) first danced in New York and the West. Hitherto its visits have featured a large proportion of the 19th-century ballet classics. Not so this time. Of its three recent programs in New York, two were of ballets created in the 21st century, while the third was a pair of ballets from 1947 and 1967.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/18/arts/BALLET/BALLET-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 278, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/18/arts/BALLET/BALLET-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 278}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/18/arts/BALLET/BALLET-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 475, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': N