d, the anti-domestic violence organization Between Friends has been onsite here, handing out fans to festivalgoers that read “Cool It. Don’t Be A Fan Of Violence.” The move was a protest against the presence on the bill of the foulmouthed, spiteful and fantastic Los Angeles rap collective Odd Future, whose appearance on this festival bill largely full of tasteful indie rock became a flashpoint for debates about violent and hateful imagery and messages in music. Rumors of a protest during the group’s performance swirled.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pitchfork: Odd Future Pushes Back on Protest', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Domestic Violence', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rap and Hip-Hop', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reggae Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Butler, Ishmael', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marley, Bob', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pitchfork Media', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-17T23:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a54a12c-f540-547e-a0b9-a3df6c4b2b64', 'word_count': 295, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a54a12c-f540-547e-a0b9-a3df6c4b2b64'}, {'abstract': 'Leaders of the antigovernment demonstrations named a transitional council as crowds returned to the streets in a “day of rage.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/world/middleeast/18yemen.html', 'snippet': 'Leaders of the antigovernment demonstrations named a transitional council as crowds returned to the streets in a “day of rage.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even as antigovernment protesters in Yemen struggled to revitalize their movement, sketching somewhat shaky plans over the weekend for a transitional government, they produced a show of their core strength, taking to the streets in huge numbers on Sunday to protest the rule of President Ali Abdullah Saleh.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/18/world/YEMEN/YEMEN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/18/world/YEMEN/YEMEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/18/world/YEMEN/YEMEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Yemenis Organize Shadow Government', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Yemenis Organize Shadow Government', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saleh, Ali Abdullah', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-17T23:32:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laura Kasinof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laura', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kasinof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/07de97d0-44c9-512a-8e6b-4a265599b29f', 'word_count': 747, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07de97d0-44c9-512a-8e6b-4a265599b29f'}, {'abstract': 'Greenhill & Company took the unusual step of announcing its earnings on a Sunday afternoon, saying profit exceeded analysts’ expectations, in an apparent attempt to bolster its sagging stock price.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/07/17/greenhill-reports-earnings-early/', 'snippet': 'Greenhill & Company took the unusual step of announcing its earnings on a Sunday afternoon, saying profit exceeded analysts’ expectations, in an apparent attempt to bolster its sagging stock price.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While many were transfixed by the women’s World Cup final on Sunday afternoon, Greenhill & Company was doing something different: releasing its latest quarterly earnings.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Greenhill’s Quarterly Earnings Rise 22%', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-17T23:32:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b221519-cd7c-57d1-ab45-38324fb26e60', 'word_count': 270, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b221519-cd7c-57d1-ab45-38324fb26e60'}, {'abstract': 'A NASA engineer who designed the flag planted on the moon by Neil Armstrong got $45,000 for his collector’s item, less than he had sought.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/science/space/18moon.html', 'snippet': 'A NASA engineer who designed the flag planted on the moon by Neil Armstrong got $45,000 for his collector’s item, less than he had sought.', 'lead_paragraph': 'They were three fabric scraps trimmed from the flag later planted on the moon by Neil Armstrong during the Apollo 11 mission. They never made it to the moon, but rather were discarded in a trash bin and recovered by Thomas Moser, a NASA engineer. And now — mounted to a poster with a nice photograph, and signed by Mr. Armstrong himself — they have sold for $45,000.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/18/science/space/moon/moon-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/18/science/space/moon/moon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/18/science/space/moon/moon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Flag Soared to the Moon, but Not Bids for 3 Scraps', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Flag Soared To the Moon, But Not Bids For 3 Scraps', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flags, Emblems and Insignia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collectors and Collections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ARMSTRONG, NEIL', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Aeronautics and Space Administration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Moon', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-17T23:39:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Space & Cosmos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Douglas Quenqua', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Douglas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Quenqua', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/174b0c06-a1fd-5050-8a11-c1707ca6ebb7', 'word_count': 335, 'uri': 'nyt://article/174b0c06-a1fd-5050-8a11-c1707ca6ebb7'}, {'abstract': 'At least 1,000 troops, some backed by tanks and others flown in on helicopters, descended on Albokamal, which is near the border with Iraq and that nation’s Sunni Muslim heartland.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/world/middleeast/18syria.html', 'snippet': 'At least 1,000 troops, some backed by tanks and others flown in on helicopters, descended on Albokamal, which is near the border with Iraq and that nation’s Sunni Muslim heartland.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — Security forces massed on Sunday near a key town in eastern Syria where dozens of soldiers have defected to join the four-month-old uprising against the government of President Bashar al-Assad, according to activists and residents there. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Syrian Forces Mass Near Town Where Many Soldiers Have Defected', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Syrian Forces Mass Near Town Where Many Soldiers Have Defected', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Governme