rker assistance program.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/opinion/18mon3.html', 'snippet': 'Republicans are refusing to approve trade agreements unless the White House decouples them from a bill to renew a worker assistance program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Republicans have said for years that passing trade pacts with South Korea, Colombia and Panama would increase American exports and cement relations with key allies. Yet they are now trying to undermine this goal.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yet Another Political Game', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Yet Another Political Game', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T01:37:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c347490-f2b9-5fe9-aeb8-f14014e8629b', 'word_count': 318, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c347490-f2b9-5fe9-aeb8-f14014e8629b'}, {'abstract': 'Plans are being made to redevelop an unlovely area near the Ronkonkoma train station and turn it into a cool destination.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/opinion/18mon4.html', 'snippet': 'Plans are being made to redevelop an unlovely area near the Ronkonkoma train station and turn it into a cool destination.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From high atop the five-story parking garage at Ronkonkoma’s Long Island Rail 