kelihood of less federal aid, considered the “new normal.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/us/18governors.html', 'snippet': 'At the National Governors Association meeting, state leaders talked of adjusting to the strong likelihood of less federal aid, considered the “new normal.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'SALT LAKE CITY —Arizona began cutting more than 100,000 people from its Medicaid rolls this month. Illinois, even after raising taxes, began the month with $3.8 billion worth of unpaid bills left over from last year. Connecticut sent layoff warnings last week to state troopers.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'States’ Money Woes Show No Favorites', 'kicker': 'Political Memo', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'States’ Money Woes Show No Favorites', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicaid', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Governors Assn', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal-State Relations (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T03:43:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3bb0c4f-05d6-52f5-b696-e696db4597a5', 'word_count': 928, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3bb0c4f-05d6-52f5-b696-e696db4597a5'}, {'abstract': 'Because on hot summer days, the human impulse to head for water still prevails.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/us/18outhere.html', 'snippet': 'Because on hot summer days, the human impulse to head for water still prevails.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No matter that this has been the summer of endless floods.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/18/us/Out-There/Out-There-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/18/us/Out-There/Out-There-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Summer Revelers Re-engage With Water, Its Transgressions Forgiven', 'kicker': 'Out Here | Lebanon, Mo.', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Summer Revelers Re-engage With Water, Its Transgressions Forgiven', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rivers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Missouri', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T03:49:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By A. G. Sulzberger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'Sulzberger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0165826-a82b-5744-9c7c-c00fe0489b21', 'word_count': 301, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0165826-a82b-5744-9c7c-c00fe0489b21'}, {'abstract': 'Rory McIlroy, who finished the British Open 12 shots off the lead, said the rainy, cool conditions simply did not suit his game.', 'web_url': 'https://onpar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/17/mcilroy-shrugs-off-rocky-performance/', 'snippet': 'Rory McIlroy, who finished the British Open 12 shots off the lead, said the rainy, cool conditions simply did not suit his game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SANDWICH, England — It was not as impolitic as his downplaying the Ryder Cup as an “exhibition”: a point of view that Rory McIlroy has since revised. But McIlroy did not exactly embrace the traditional challenge of the British Open after finishing 12 shots off the lead with a seven-over total of 287. Among his indignities on Sunday was the penalty stroke he was given after his ball moved on the seventh green in the strong winds after he had grounded his putter behind it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'McIlroy Shrugs Off Rocky Performance', 'kicker': 'On Par', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'British Open (Golf)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McIlroy, Rory', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T03:53:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Clarey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clarey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c4ad514d-24d7-5bed-9744-e6743afcc91b', 'word_count': 168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4ad514d-24d7-5bed-9744-e6743afcc91b'}, {'abstract': 'When Japan rallied to beat the United States in the World Cup final, bringing joy to a nation rocked by natural and nuclear disaster, even the members of the losing team took a moment to cheer inside.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/17/as-japan-celebrates-even-the-losers-cheer-inside/', 'snippet': 'When Japan rallied to beat the United States in the World Cup final, bringing joy to a nation rocked by natural and nuclear disaster, even the members of the losing team took a moment to cheer inside.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The undercurrent running through the entire Women’s World Cup for Japan was their hope that they could play well enough and long enough to bring joy and pride to their countrymen in the wake of this spring’s devastating earthquake and resulting nuclear disaster. As the Times reported last week:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Japan Celebrates, Even the Losers Cheer Inside', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Japan Earthquake and Tsunami (2011)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's World Cup (Soccer)", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T03:58:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Das', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Das', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b4222e7-71ba-5557-a5a2-d24d7e6c714b', 'word_count': 366, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b4222e7-71ba-5557-a5a2-d24d7e6c714b'}, {'abstract': 'Darren Clarke and his caddie, John Mulrooney, took it as a positive omen when officials gave Clarke the same locker that Greg Norman used in 1993, when he won in grand style.', 'web_url': 'https://onpar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/17/normans-lucky-locker/', 'snippet': 'Darren Clarke and his caddie, John Mulrooney, took it as a positive omen when officials gave Clarke the same locker that Greg Norman used in 1993, when he won in grand style.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SANDWICH, England —Greg Norman is not normally a source of good karma that players turn to when it comes to major championships.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Norman’s Lucky Locker', 'kicker': 'On Par', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clarke, Darren', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Norman, Greg', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T03:58:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Clarey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clarey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a468653d-aae8-5bed-a6b2-e4d2e181131a', 'word_count': 158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a468653d-aae8-5bed-a6b2-e4d2e181131a'}, {'abstract': 'This word has appeared in 50 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/word-of-the-day-carat/', 'snippet': 'This word has appeared in 50 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'carat •\\ˈker-ət, ˈka-rət\\• noun', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Word of the Day | carat', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T04:01:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/283c5388-4c0b-5de2-8497-4c8aeddaed4d', 'word_count': 238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/283c5388-4c0b-5de2-8497-4c8aeddaed4d'}, {'abstract': 'The Park Avenue Armory is announcing Aug. 15 as the on-sale date for the final six performances of the Merce Cunningham Dance Company.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/arts/dance/tickets-for-final-shows-by-cunningham-troupe.html', 'snippet': 'The Park Avenue Armory is announcing Aug. 15 as the on-sale date for the final six performances of the Merce Cunningham Dance Company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Park Avenue Armory is announcing Aug. 15 as the on-sale date for the final six performances of the Merce Cunningham Dance Company, along with world premieres by Shen Wei Dance Arts and Streb Extreme Action Company, completing the armory’s first full season of artistic programming. Tickets to all three can be can be purchased at armoryonpark.org. According to the last wishes of Mr. Cunningham, tickets to his company’s performances, which will be Dec. 29 to 31, are to cost $10. Announced before his death in 2009, the planned two-year legacy tour has traveled to more than 50 cities worldwide and signals an end to nearly 60 years of creativity from a master of modern dance and choreography. Rounding out the lineup, the new work by Shen Wei (Nov. 30 to Dec. 4), artist in residence at the armory, will combine digital projection with handmade scenic elements. Tickets will be $35. Streb (Dec. 14 to 22) will incorporate ziplines, bungee cords and trampolines for “Kiss the Air!,” a work that will make full use of the armory’s 55,000-square-foot performance hall. Tickets are to cost $30.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tickets for Final Shows by Cunningham Troupe', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tickets for Final Shows By Cunningham Troupe', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cunningham, Merce, Dance Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T04:03:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5622a9c-9803-5e2f-8a3e-0967dfa2b68d', 'word_count': 186, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5622a9c-9803-5e2f-8a3e-0967dfa2b68d'}, {'abstract': 'NYT: Front Page for 07/18/2011', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2011/07/18/multimedia/18frontpage.html', 'snippet': 'NYT: Front Page for 07/18/2011', 'lead_paragraph': 'NYT: Front Page for 07/18/2011', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'NYT: Front Page for 07/18/2011', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T04:10:49+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/45ed0dbc-4ea8-50ba-a581-eba6ae99e79f', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/45ed0dbc-4ea8-50ba-a581-eba6ae99e79f'}, {'abstract': 'In two weeks, all the madness and mayhem of the trade deadline season will be over. Some impact players will move, others will stay put. But into which category will the Rockies starter Ubaldo Jimenez fall?', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/the-ubaldo-jimenez-puzzle/', 'snippet': 'In two weeks, all the madness and mayhem of the trade deadline season will be over. Some impact players will move, others will stay put. But into which category will the Rockies starter Ubaldo Jimenez fall?', 'lead_paragraph': 'TORONTO – In two weeks, all the madness and mayhem of the trade deadline season will be over. Some impact players will move, but many others will stay put. Into which category will Ubaldo Jimenez fall? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Ubaldo Jimenez Puzzl