t://article/b69212a4-19f5-584e-8a45-3f8e96eed04d', 'word_count': 91, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b69212a4-19f5-584e-8a45-3f8e96eed04d'}, {'abstract': 'A group of friends in Britain will try this week to break the world record for the longest soccer game played, aiming for 72 hours of continuous play, in a charity fund-raiser that is already under way.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/a-four-day-game-chases-donations-and-a-world-record/', 'snippet': 'A group of friends in Britain will try this week to break the world record for the longest soccer game played, aiming for 72 hours of continuous play, in a charity fund-raiser that is already under way.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Teams and organizations always preach their efforts to “give something back,” whether it’s to the local community or further afield. But a group of friends from England are setting a new benchmark, pushing their own health and fitness to the limit to help those less fortunate than themselves.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Four-Day Game Chases Donations and a World Record', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T08:21:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Graham Ruthven', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Graham', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ruthven', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ea905a1-43e4-53bc-b37d-3d74007caca5', 'word_count': 466, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ea905a1-43e4-53bc-b37d-3d74007caca5'}, {'abstract': 'Gordon Parks worked for the Farm Security Administration before he gained fame. Now, the Library of Congress is making 50 of those pictures available in a little gem of a book.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/empathetic-portraits-of-a-segregated-nation/', 'snippet': 'Gordon Parks worked for the Farm Security Administration before he gained fame. Now, the Library of Congress is making 50 of those pictures available in a little gem of a book.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gordon Parks (1912-2006) is celebrated as a photographer, filmmaker, memoirist and breaker of color barriers. Before he was famous, however; before he was Gordon Parks, he had a one-year fellowship as a photographer at the Farm Security Administration. There, under the tutelage of Roy Stryker, he honed his skills.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Empathetic Portraits of a Segregated Nation', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T09:00:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Estrin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Estrin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7133864f-a29c-5631-b159-21ac096941a7', 'word_count': 489, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7133864f-a29c-5631-b159-21ac096941a7'}, {'abstract': 'TiVo’s Premiere service is much more than a standard DVR, but there are significant costs to the customer both in money and labor.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/tivo-nice-service-if-you-can-get-it/', 'snippet': 'TiVo’s Premiere service is much more than a standard DVR, but there are significant costs to the customer both in money and labor.', 'lead_paragraph': '9:44 p.m. | Updated  to clarify the pricing of Time Warner Cable’s DVR service.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'TiVo, Nice S