331-1121-57cd-b39c-2b05e47f84fe', 'word_count': 659, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd201331-1121-57cd-b39c-2b05e47f84fe'}, {'abstract': 'The Day: The same-sex marriage law is changing some lives significantly, and the change has nothing to do with those people getting married. Also, what City Room is reading in other papers and blogs.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/when-conscience-and-the-new-marriage-law-collide/', 'snippet': 'The Day: The same-sex marriage law is changing some lives significantly, and the change has nothing to do with those people getting married. Also, what City Room is reading in other papers and blogs.', 'lead_paragraph': ' As usual, Laura L. Fotusky attended Sunday morning services at Union Center Christian Church, which she described as “a nondenominational, Bible-preaching church” in Union Center, N.Y., a town about seven miles northwest of Binghamton. Her life is about to change significantly. But on Sunday Ms. Fotusky described herself as at peace. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Conscience and the New Marriage Law Collide', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T12:29:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clyde Haberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clyde', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/47654035-ccae-506d-bb8f-1c2c64c25524', 'word_count': 1078, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47654035-ccae-506d-bb8f-1c2c64c25524'}, {'abstract': 'American and European shares fell as investors took stock of the debt crisis in Europe and the deficit talks in the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/19/business/Daily-Stock-Market-Activity.html', 'snippet': 'American and European shares fell as investors took stock of the debt crisis in Europe and the deficit talks in the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Investors on Monday remained nervous about stress tests on European banks as well as the debt-ceiling talks in Washington, leading to a sell-off in stocks. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Markets Stumble on Debt and Deficit Worries', 'kicker': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Markets Stumble on Debt and Deficit Worries', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euro (Currency)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gold', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T12:35:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew Saltmarsh and Christine Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saltmarsh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6d3aa72-a9fb-536d-b619-7366272da8c7', 'word_count': 701, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6d3aa72-a9fb-536d-b619-7366272da8c7'}, {'abstract': 'Funds of funds with more than 20 underlying managers begin to lose the benefit of diversification, according to a study led by Stephen Brown at New York University’s Stern School of Business.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/funds-of-funds-may-actually-increase-risk-study-finds/', 'snippet': 'Funds of funds with more than 20 underlying managers begin to lose the benefit of diversification, according to a study led by Stephen Brown at New York University’s Stern School of Business.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ever since the financial crisis, the fund of hedge funds model has been under fire.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Funds of Funds May Actually Increase Risk, Study Finds', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hedge Funds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Stephen', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State University of New York', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T12:46:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Azam Ahmed', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Azam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ahmed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e99876c-f833-5692-bf38-310f0bd978a2', 'word_count': 435, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e99876c-f833-5692-bf38-310f0bd978a2'}, {'abstract': 'Cambodia and Thailand were ordered to withdraw troops from the area around a disputed temple and established a demilitarized zone along their mountainous border.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/19/world/asia/19temple.html', 'snippet': 'Cambodia and Thailand were ordered to withdraw troops from the area around a disputed temple and established a demilitarized zone along their mountainous border.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BANGKOK — The top judicial body of the United Nations on Monday sought to defuse tensions at a Southeast Asian flash point, ordering Cambodia and Thailand to withdraw troops from a disputed temple and establishing a demilitarized zone along their mountainous border.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/19/world/SUB-SUB-BRIEFS/SUB-SUB-BRIEFS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 745, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'U.N. Court Orders Troops From Temple on Thai-Cambodian Border', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Court Orders Thailand and Cambodia To Withdraw From Disputed Temple', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cambodia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Thailand', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T12:52:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Fuller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fuller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/49518276-b02d-5bf0-8b34-de59f151a03b', 'word_count': 586, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49518276-b02d-5bf0-8b34-de59f151a03b'}, {'abstract': 'A shopping tag-team sets upon AllSaints Spitalfields, in the meatpacking district.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/the-samurai-shopper-takes-a-pal/', 'snippet': 'A shopping tag-team sets upon AllSaints Spitalfields, in the meatpacking district.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a fledgling Samurai Shopper, I felt great empathy for the forlorn men I’d see, parked on department store settees, besieged by boredom as their wives inhabited nearby dressing rooms in nautical-striped whatnots or butterfly prints. Sometimes the wives stepped out to catwalk, sometimes not. It was then that I pledged never to drag anyone past the cordon sanitaire of ladies’ wear and make him sit like a cigar-store Indian while I swanned around in leather or lace, deciding what accentuated the positive and eliminated the muffin bloat around my belt.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Samurai Shopper Takes a Pal', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T13:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By S.S. Fair', 'person': [{'firstname': 'S.', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Fair', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c291c9cd-d928-5589-8ca8-b720e105db10', 'word_count': 772, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c291c9cd-d928-5589-8ca8-b720e105db10'}, {'abstract': 'Several people were reported injured when a thunderstorm struck during Cheap Trick’s performance on Sunday night at the Ottawa Bluesfest, but the band members were said to be unharmed.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/stage-collapses-during-cheap-trick-performance-in-ottawa/', 'snippet': 'Several people were reported injured when a thunderstorm struck during Cheap Trick’s performance on Sunday night at the Ottawa Bluesfest, but the band members were said to be unharmed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Several people were reported injured when a stage collapsed Sunday evening during a performance by Cheap Trick during the Ottawa Bluesfest, though the band members were said to be unharmed, according to The Associated Press. Canadian weather services had predicted a thunderstorm in Ottawa on Sunday night, which struck while Cheap Trick was performing on the festival’s main stage. This YouTube video posted by a user named gastorch997 shows the stage coming down in a matter of seconds as stunned onlookers scream. A concertgoer named Meghan Hurley wrote in The Ottawa Citizen that she “heard a loud bang,” after which “a frightened woman” told her “almost in tears that the stage had collapsed.” Ms. Hurley added, “I glanced over to where we had sat only moments before and all that remained was a heap of chairs that looked like a windswept pile of kindling for a bonfire.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stage Collapses During Cheap Trick Performance in Ottawa', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cheap Trick', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ottawa (Ontario)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T13:04:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/529072b4-efea-5167-adf8-a870c0784ac0', 'word_count': 234, 'uri': 'nyt://article/529072b4-efea-5167-adf8-a870c0784ac0'}, {'abstract': 'Budget trips for those who like to volunteer, grocery stores push big quantities to entice buyers, Virgin Mobile changes pricing on no-contract plans and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/monday-readingbudget-excursions-for-those-who-like-to-volunteer/', 'snippet': 'Budget trips for those who like to volunteer, grocery stores push big quantities to entice buyers, Virgin Mobile changes pricing on no-contract plans and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and online in our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Monday Reading:Budget Excursions for Those Who Like to Volunteer', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T13:08:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55c5b3df-165c-56e1-927b-31bdead3b638', 'word_count': 182, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55c5b3df-165c-56e1-927b-31bdead3b638'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/morning-take-out-287/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Obama Bypasses Warren in Pick for Consumer Post | President Obama has nominated Richard Cordray, the former attorney general of Ohio, to lead the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau, bypassing Elizabeth Warren, who pushed for the agency’s creation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Take-Out', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo'