ng', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T14:29:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Richards', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Richards', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b71868ef-e056-54f1-a051-dd6a9fadcb4a', 'word_count': 564, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b71868ef-e056-54f1-a051-dd6a9fadcb4a'}, {'abstract': 'Empellón Cocina, opening in the fall, will not have tacos and chips.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/alex-stupak-to-get-deeper-into-mexico/', 'snippet': 'Empellón Cocina, opening in the fall, will not have tacos and chips.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The success of Empellón, his taco-centric Mexican place in the West Village that opened earlier this year, has encouraged Alex Stupak, the former pastry chef at WD-50, to plan a second restaurant, Empellón Cocina, due in late fall.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Alex Stupak to Get Deeper Into Mexico', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T14:37:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06418092-d884-5bcc-a81c-1131cffb66fe', 'word_count': 152, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06418092-d884-5bcc-a81c-1131cffb66fe'}, {'abstract': 'As the Tour de France this week celebrates its 100th anniversary in t