ets, has filed for an initial public offering, providing a quick exit for its private equity owners.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/dave-busters-files-for-i-p-o/', 'snippet': 'Dave & Buster’s, the restaurant chain whose customers trade arcade tickets for stuffed animals, critter rings and other trinkets, has filed for an initial public offering, providing a quick exit for its private equity owners.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dave & Buster’s Entertainment, the restaurant chain whose customers exchange arcade tickets for stuffed animals, critter rings and other trinkets, filed on Monday for an initial public offering, providing a quick exit for the private equity firm Oak Hill Capital Partners. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dave & Buster’s Files For I.P.O.', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T14:57:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin Roose', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roose', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/061b29a6-49f2-55da-ad84-86a57f0b593e', 'word_count': 283, 'uri': 'nyt://article/061b29a6-49f2-55da-ad84-86a57f0b593e'}, {'abstract': 'The illustrator Olly Moss on his limited-edition “Captain America” posters, which resemble propaganda fliers from World War II.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/poster-boy-wonder/', 'snippet': 'The illustrator Olly Moss on his limited-edition “Captain America” posters, which resemble propaganda fliers from World War II.', 'lead_paragraph': ' NYTD.fullScreenSlideShowFactory.createSlideshow("#826", 592, 490, false, chameleonData);', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headl