lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — And so the sorry story continues, as people from the corridors of power confess their crimes and await their judgments. The glamorous favorite of the tyrant has fallen from her high perch, and it is rumored that further depths of corruption are waiting to be plumbed. Reputations everywhere are in tatters.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'London Theater Journal: Amoral Clarity', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Daniels, Ben', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grandage, Michael', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Felicity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Light, John', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Poulton, Mike', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schiller, Friedrich', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Donmar Warehouse Theater', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T15:23:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/296c850a-4e0b-59a1-ad9e-18df1b942f46', 'word_count': 663, 'uri': 'nyt://article/296c850a-4e0b-59a1-ad9e-18df1b942f46'}, {'abstract': 'Russian officials said that criminal cases have been launched against two former prison doctors over the death of Sergei L. Magnitsky, who died in detention after repeatedly requesting medical care.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes