d the new Consumer Financial Protection Bureau, is no stranger to Wall Street.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wall Street’s Newest Regulator a Longtime Foe', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T15:50:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6a03c3d-e3fe-54f9-ac51-e4a16e534f08', 'word_count': 726, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6a03c3d-e3fe-54f9-ac51-e4a16e534f08'}, {'abstract': 'Guided autobiography programs allow the elderly to revisit, and share, their lives.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/a-guided-tour-of-the-past/', 'snippet': 'Guided autobiography programs allow the elderly to revisit, and share, their lives.', 'lead_paragraph': '“A hot August day, opening day of school, 4th grade,” Elisabeth Park, 72, wrote for one of her assignments. “This is a dress-up occasion, and I know full well that my appearance is a disaster. To begin with, my dress looks like a nightgown….”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Guided Tour of the Past', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T15:57:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paula Span', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paula', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Span', 'qualifier':