fference between life and death. A new study suggests that being married is a significant factor in getting treatment faster — but only for men.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Patterns: Faster Treatment for the Married Man', 'kicker': 'Vital Signs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Patterns: Faster Treatment for the Married Man', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Heart', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T16:01:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Research', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Bakalar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakalar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2147a0d0-ba03-5443-aaeb-833d841e0c5a', 'word_count': 243, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2147a0d0-ba03-5443-aaeb-833d841e0c5a'}, {'abstract': 'An upturn in graffiti has renewed debates about whether it signifies alienation in struggling areas or whether its glorification contributes to urban blight.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/19/us/19graffiti.html', 'snippet': 'An upturn in graffiti has renewed debates about whether it signifies alienation in struggling areas or whether its glorification contributes to urban blight.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SANTA MONICA, Calif. — Fresh blotches of graffiti decorate the backs of street signs here near the ocean. Tags have popped up on guardrails along the dirt trails near Griffith Park across town. There are, almost daily, fresh splashes on walls in the San Fernando Valley, on downtown Los Angeles buildings and on billboards along the highways.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/19/us/19graffiti_cnd/19graffiti_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/19/us/19graffiti_cnd/19graffiti_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/19/us/19graffiti_cnd/19graffiti_cnd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/19/us/19graffiti_cnd/19graffiti_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/19/us/19graffiti_cnd/19graffiti_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cities Report Surge in Graffiti', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cities Large and Small Report an Upsurge in Graffiti', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Graffiti', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T16:10:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Nagourney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nagourney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c792958f-bd70-583e-9fac-23964f92cc2c', 'word_count': 1030, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c792958f-bd70-583e-9fac-23964f92cc2c'}, {'abstract': 'Representatives for the estate of Adrian Jacobs said that their plagiarism case against the “Harry Potter” author “was dead” after they failed to meet a Friday deadline to pay part of a security fund mandated by a British court.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/plagiarism-suit-against-j-k-rowling-is-really-truly-dead-for-now/', 'snippet': 'Representatives for the estate of Adrian Jacobs said that their plagiarism case against the “Harry Potter” author “was dead” after they failed to meet a Friday deadline to pay part of a security fund mandated by a British court.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While all those associated with the “Harry Potter” film franchise presumably spent the \xa0 weekend rolling around in their portions of the money minted by the record-breaking opening of “Harry Potter and the Deathly Hallows: Part 2,” a longstanding plagiarism case against the “Harry Potter” author J. K. Rowling has come to an end because of a shortage of funds.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Plagiarism Suit Against J. K. Rowling Is Really, Truly Dead (For Now)', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Plagiarism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rowling, J K', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T16:14:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': No