rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9235966a-32d4-5722-bdeb-73712cb0d4c8', 'word_count': 310, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9235966a-32d4-5722-bdeb-73712cb0d4c8'}, {'abstract': 'The underdog found a way to win the British Open and the Women’s World Cup, providing dramatic and heartwarming stories.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/19/sports/storybook-endings-in-british-open-and-womens-world-cup-leading-off.html', 'snippet': 'The underdog found a way to win the British Open and the Women’s World Cup, providing dramatic and heartwarming stories.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is hard to imagine two events stuffing two bigger heartwarming underdog stories into the span of a few hours than the Women’s World Cup and the British Open did Sunday. Before the day started, they had nothing in common beyond both involving sports — and with golf, some would even argue that point — but by the time they ended they were taxing our hankie supply and had fulfilled that oh-so-famous Yogi Berra quotation about it never being over until it’s over.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Storybook Endings', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Storybook Endings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's World Cup (Soccer)", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'British Open (Golf)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clarke, Darren', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Benson, Cedric', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Horton, Nathan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mickelson, Phil', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T16:21:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports'