article about it several years ago), but it was given new amplification and caused a new uproar when advocated in a commentary in the most recent Journal of the American Medical Association.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Removing  Obese Children From Their Parents', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Obesity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Obstetrics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T16:45:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Belkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/931365d7-19ff-543c-a53e-a2f75f783f86', 'word_count': 1199, 'uri': 'nyt://article/931365d7-19ff-543c-a53e-a2f75f783f86'}, {'abstract': "The champion swimmer Diana Nyad takes on a new challenge, Tara Parker Pope talks about a new study advocating aggressive treatment for chronic pain and Jim Gorman talks about the benefits of being a beta male -- especially if you're a baboon.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2011/07/18/science/science19.html', 'snippet': "The champion swimmer Diana Nyad takes on a new challenge, Tara Parker Pope talks about a new study advocating aggressive treatment for chronic pain and Jim Gorman talks about the benefits of being a beta male -- especially if you're a baboon.", 'lead_paragraph': "The champion swimmer Diana Nyad takes on a new challenge, Tara Parker Pope talks about a new study advocating aggressive treatment for chronic pain and Jim Gorman talks about the benefits of being a beta male -- especially if you're a baboon.", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The longest swim, stress and the alpha male (baboon), and treating chronic pain.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T16:45:47+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/f1ff0b48-44fb-58af-8ce2-d6ae04ca5bcd', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/f1ff0b48-44fb-58af-8ce2-d6ae04ca5bcd'}, {'abstract': 'Frank Langella, who has memorably played Richard Nixon in “Frost/Nixon” (and of course Count Dracula in “Dracula”), will write of his up-close-and-personal encounters with Elizabeth Taylor, Laurence Olivier, William Styron, Marilyn Monroe, Arthur Miller and Jacqueline Kennedy Onassis, among others, in a memoir entitled “Dropped Names.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/langella-to-drop-names-in-memoir/', 'snippet': 'Frank Langella, who has memorably played Richard Nixon in “Frost/Nixon” (and of course Count Dracula in “Dracula”), will write of his up-close-and-personal encounters with Elizabeth Taylor, Laurence Olivier, William Styron, Marilyn Monroe, Arthur ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Frank Langella, who has memorably played Richard Nixon on stage and screen in “Frost/Nixon” (and of course Count Dracula in the film “Dracula”), will write of his up-close-and-personal encounters with Elizabeth Taylor, Laurence Olivier, William Styron, Marilyn Monroe, Arthur Miller and Jacqueline Kennedy Onassis, among others, in a memoir to be released next year, his publisher said on Monday. HarperCollins acquired the rights to “Dropped Names,” Mr. Langella’s first book, said Jonathan Burnham, the publisher of the Harper imprint. “Mr. Langella is a razor sharp writer with a brilliantly perceptive eye and a remarkable gift for the telling detail,” Mr. Burnham said in a statement. Mr. Langella, whose long career has included films like “Dave,” “Starting Out in the Evening” and “The Ninth Gate,” is set to return to Broadway this fall in the Terence Rattigan drama “Man and Boy.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Langella to Drop Names in Memoir', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Langella, Frank', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T16:45:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e44e0427-f587-5fbb-8336-2e7dc0b19d70', 'word_count': 140, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e44e0427-f587-5fbb-8336-2e7dc0b19d70'}, {'abstract': 'BlackBerry users may want to know what navigation apps are available to them.  There aren’t many,  but users have a few options.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/app-smart-extra-blackberry-navigation-apps/', 'snippet': 'BlackBerry users may want to know what navigation apps are available to them.  There aren’t many,  but users have a few options.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My recent App Smart column recommends applications for audible turn-by-turn navigation. The best ones can replace those pricey personal navigation devices that are always getting stolen from cars.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'App Smart Extra: BlackBerry Navigators', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headli