 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T17:22:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c226636-a3d5-58e3-b100-0661c5d3ad29', 'word_count': 211, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c226636-a3d5-58e3-b100-0661c5d3ad29'}, {'abstract': 'The Environmental Working Group released “Meat Eater’s Guide to Climate Change and Health,” a comprehensive report which suggests that we all need to eat fewer animal products.', 'web_url': 'https://bittman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/more-weight-on-less-meat/', 'snippet': 'The Environmental Working Group released “Meat Eater’s Guide to Climate Change and Health,” a comprehensive report which suggests that we all need to eat fewer animal products.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Today the Environmental Working Group (EWG) released “Meat Eater’s Guide to Climate Change and Health,” a comprehensive report that suggests what’s become a common refrain here and elsewhere: we all need to eat fewer animal products – not just meat, but dairy as well. The guide tracks the lifecycle of the food we eat, from production and processing to consumption and waste disposal. It’s tricked out with enough features, graphics, and factoids to keep you busy – or equal parts hopeful and despondent – for a while. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Weight on Less Meat', 'kicker': 'Mark Bittman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Meat', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Working Group', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T17:29:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/43ac3a26-e3ed-53a7-9ad9-ea5d7ab5abae', 'word_count': 446, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43ac3a26-e3ed-53a7-9ad9-ea5d7ab5abae'}, {'abstract': 'Acorn TV, a new online offering from Acorn Media, will provide a concentrated dose of classic British dramas that are currently unavailable for free anywhere else in the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/watchlist-new-slate-of-british-tv-offerings-for-americans-online/', 'snippet': 'Acorn TV, a new online offering from Acorn Media, will provide a concentrated dose of classic British dramas that are currently unavailable for free anywhere else in the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If your taste in television runs toward British detectives — not to mention British soap operas, British literary classics and British colonial romances — then a new streaming video making its debut on Monday may be just your cup of tea.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Watchlist: New Online Slate of British TV Offerings for Americans', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T17:30:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Hale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f4c2282-f9e7-56e7-b7da-5b6684bc4d4f', 'word_count': 321, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f4c2282-f9e7-56e7-b7da-5b6684bc4d4f'}, {'abstract': 'On Monday, Emirates airlines introduced Destination Radio, a free app for the iPhone and iPod Touch.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/emirates-offers-radio-app-for-travelers/', 'snippet': 'On Monday, Emirates airlines introduced Destination Radio, a free app for the iPhone and iPod Touch.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Do you want to immerse yourself in a new culture? On Monday, Emirates airlines released a new radio app aimed at those who want to explore before traveling or simply want to discover new places. The new app, Destination Radio, is free and available for the iPhone and iPod Touch.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Emirates Offers Radio App for Travelers', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T17:33:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Danielle Belopotosky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Danielle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belopotosky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/414675ec-7447-5262-8566-691101cc5cb4', 'word_count': 243, 'uri': 'nyt://article/414675ec-7447-5262-8566-691101cc5cb4'}, {'abstract': 'In many buildings, fish tanks are a joy for young families, and meant to signal that services are a priority.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/19/nyregion/in-battery-park-the-fish-tank-is-the-new-public-square.html', 'snippet': 'In many buildings, fish tanks are a joy for young families, and meant to signal that services are a priority.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At some point every day, Amanda Beck’s 11-month-old daughter, Emmy, says, “B