19/health/nutrition/19swim.html', 'snippet': 'Diana Nyad, 61, aims to set a record by swimming across the shark-infested Straits of Florida in 60 hours.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KEY WEST, Fla. — Any day now, Diana Nyad will set out to do something no athlete has ever done: swim all day and all night, then all day and all night, then all day again.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/19/science/19SWIM1_SPAN/19SWIM1_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/19/science/19SWIM1_SPAN/19SWIM1_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/19/science/19SWIM1_SPAN/19SWIM1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/19/science/19SWIM1_SPAN/19SWIM1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/19/science/19SWIM1_SPAN/19SWIM1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ready to Swim 103 Miles With the Sharks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ready to Swim 103 Miles With the Sharks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Swimming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oceans and Seas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nyad, Diana', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T17:51:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Fitness & Nutrition', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lizette Alvarez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lizette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alvarez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8477ca7-5dd2-54c5-bdc7-a4da4622f816', 'word_count': 1682, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8477ca7-5dd2-54c5-bdc7-a4da4622f816'}, {'abstract': 'The most detailed long-term analysis of the factors that influence weight gain shows that conventional wisdom may not be the best approach.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/19/health/19brody.html', 'snippet': 'The most detailed long-term analysis of the factors that influence weight gain shows that conventional wisdom may not be the best approach.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s no secret that Americans are fatter today than ever before, and not just those unlucky people who are genetically inclined to gain weight or have been overweight all their lives. Many who were lean as young adults have put on lots of unhealthy pounds as they pass into middle age and beyond.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/19/science/19brod/19brod-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/19/science/19brod/19brod-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/19/science/19brod/19brod-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Still Counting Calories? Your Weight-Loss Plan May Be Outdated', 'kicker': 'Personal Health', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Still Counting Calories? Your Weight-Loss Plan May Be Outdated', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Obesity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weight', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T17:52:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane E. Brody', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Brody', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d81edad-64bf-5747-a579-068ca40a528c', 'word_count': 1444, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d81edad-64bf-5747-a579-068ca40a528c'}, {'abstract': '“Supergods,” by Grant Morrison, is an impressionistic overview of comic heroes and an attempt to rediscover the magical essence that inspired nearly 75 years’ worth of superhero storytelling.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/19/books/supergods-by-grant-morrison-book-review.html', 'snippet': '“Supergods,” by Grant Morrison, is an impressionistic overview of comic heroes and an attempt to rediscover the magical essence that inspired nearly 75 years’ worth of superhero storytelling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s nothing cool anymore about acknowledging the coolness of comic books. Popular culture is so far beyond that moment when comic characters — specifically those gifted, costumed adventurers known as superheroes — shed their reputation as fetish objects for children and marginalized adults and entered the mainstream. We’re now well into an era when every summer weekend brings the opening of an “X-Men” or “Green Lantern” movie. Colorful crime fighters’ vivid uniforms and rippling physiques are used to sell everything from pro football apparel to Broadway musicals, while the characters themselves, untethered from their decades-long narrative traditions, are reduced to mere commodities. Forget about rescuing Lois Lane or Aunt May — now it is the superhero himself who needs saving. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/19/arts/19book-web/19book-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/19/arts/19book-web/19book-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/19/arts/19book-web/19book-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Superheroes, Surveyed and Sized Up', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Comics Superheroes, Surveyed, Sized Up and Ready for Their Next Costume', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comic Books and Strips', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morrison, Grant', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T17:52:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/12864368-b634-5de2-99ea-f0ad4257af5c', 'word_count': 1084, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12864368-b634-5de2-99ea-f0ad4257af5c'}, {'abstract': 'Female cottony cushion scales tend to reproduce with their parasitic fathers rather than an outside male, resulting in a dwindling population, researchers report.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/19/science/19obinsect.html', 'snippet': 'Female cottony cushion scales tend to reproduce with their parasitic fathers rather than an outside male, resulting in a dwindling population, researchers report.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A small agricultural pest called the cottony cushion scale exhibits a bizarre form of hermaphroditism in which parasitic males infect their daughters at birth. This parasite lives in the daughter and fertilizes her eggs.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/19/science/19insect/19insect-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/19/science/19insect/19insect-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/19/science/19insect/19OBOX3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 863, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/19/science/19insect/19insect-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/19/science/19insect/19insect-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Male That May Mate Its Kind Into Extinction', 'kicker': 'Observatory', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Male That May Mate Its Kind Into Extinction', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insects', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parasites', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reproduction (Biological)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T17:57:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sindya N. Bhanoo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sindya', 'middlename': 'N.', 'lastname': 'Bhanoo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/15aac1d9-5584-59f1-9de8-4d5065076470', 'word_count': 252, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15aac1d9-5584-59f1-9de8-4d5065076470'}, {'abstract': 'NBC News and Facebook announce plans to host a “one-of-a-kind” debate for the Republican presidential candidates early next year in New Hampshire.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/facebook-and-nbc-to-host-republican-debate-in-n-h/', 'snippet': 'NBC News and Facebook announce plans to host a “one-of-a-kind” debate for the Republican presidential candidates early next year in New Hampshire.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Visit msnbc.com for breaking news, world news, and news about the economy', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Facebook and NBC to Host Republican Debate in N.H.', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gregory, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook.com', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NBC News', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Hampshire', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T17:57:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f2de973e-7d9e-5e6b-b298-a87baf4742d6', 'word_count': 114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f2de973e-7d9e-5e6b-b298-a87baf4742d6'}, {'abstract': 'Consumer spending, under the official government definition, still has a historically high share of gross domestic product. But that is misleading in several ways.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/looking-inside-the-consumer-bust/', 'snippet': 'Consumer spending, under the official government definition, still has a historically high share of gross domestic product. But that is misleading in several ways.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few commenters responded to my Sunday column by asking whether consumer spending had really declined all that much. A blog post by Jared Bernstein discusses this issue. The crux of the argument is this chart, showing that consumer spending does not make up a smaller share of gross domestic product than a few years ago:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Looking Inside the Consumer Bust', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Behavior', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gross Domestic Product', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T18:02:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David'