i': 'nyt://article/8e69856f-5d3d-55fa-a4b5-f13122273717'}, {'abstract': 'An exercise physiologist and other experts said that contrary to popular wisdom, they could find no scientific evidence that a softer surface is beneficial to runners.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/19/health/nutrition/19best.html', 'snippet': 'An exercise physiologist and other experts said that contrary to popular wisdom, they could find no scientific evidence that a softer surface is beneficial to runners.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hirofumi Tanaka, an exercise physiologist at the University of Texas at Austin, bristles when he sees dirt paths carved out of the grass along paved bicycling or running routes. The paths are created by runners who think softer ground protects them from injuries. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/19/science/19BEST/19BEST-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/19/science/19BEST/19BEST-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/19/science/19BEST/19BEST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 598, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/19/science/19BEST/19BEST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/19/science/19BEST/19BEST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Runners, Soft Ground Can Be Hard on the Body', 'kicker': 'Personal Best', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Runners, Soft Ground Can Be Hard on the Body', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Running', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Asphalt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shoes and Boots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T18:45:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Fitness & Nutrition', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gina Kolata', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kolata', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/036b7287-4f9a-5747-804f-6b0f242c72f3', 'word_count': 886, 'uri': 'nyt://article/036b7287-4f9a-5747-804f-6b0f242c72f3'}, {'abstract': 'A small group of executives at News Corporation pursued strategies for years that had the effect of obscuring the extent of wrongdoing in Britain’s best-selling tabloid.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/19/world/europe/19tactics.html', 'snippet': 'A small group of executives at News Corporation pursued strategies for years that had the effect of obscuring the extent of wrongdoing in Britain’s best-selling tabloid.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Two days before it emerged that The News of the World had hacked the cellphone of a murdered schoolgirl, igniting a scandal that has shaken the media empire of Rupert Murdoch, his son James told friends that he thought the worst of the troubles were behind him. And he was confident that the News Corporation’s $12 billion bid for the satellite company British Sky Broadcasting would go through, according to a person present. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/19/world/europe/TACTICS-1/TACTICS-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 648, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/19/world/europe/TACTICS-1/TACTICS-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/19/world/europe/TACTICS-1/TACTICS-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Murdoch Aides Long Tried to Blunt Scandal Over Hacking', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Murdoch Aides Long Obscured Scandal’s Scale', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NEWS CORP', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wiretapping and Other Eavesdropping Devices and Methods', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Scotland Yard (Metropolitan Police Service)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News of the World', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T18:59:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jo Becker and Ravi Somaiya', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jo', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Becker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ravi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Somaiya', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/151b35ff-7689-5fe7-b005-621bd3a93f17', 'word_count': 2415, 'uri': 'nyt://article/151b35ff-7689-5fe7-b005-621bd3a93f17'}, {'abstract': 'The Brooklyn-based artist Kenneth E. Parris III is on tour with members of the Merce Cunningham Dance Company, documenting their two-year Legacy Tour.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/drawing-dance-cunningham-at-dartmouth/', 'snippet': 'The Brooklyn-based artist Kenneth E. Parris III is on tour with members of the Merce Cunningham Dance Company, documenting their two-year Legacy Tour.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Brooklyn-based artist Kenneth E. Parris III is on tour with members of the Merce Cunningham Dance Company, documenting their two-year Legacy Tour through a series of drawings and paintings. After 58 years, the company is scheduled to disband on New Year’s Day 2012. This is the fifth in a series of graphite drawings he plans to create from the road, providing a front-row seat to the final weeks of the company’s journey. This week’s entry is from Dartmouth College.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Drawing Dance: Cunningham at Dartmouth', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T19:00:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e76b4f4-a630-5d26-b7cc-d8a20ce9293e', 'word_count': 133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e76b4f4-a630-5d26-b7cc-d8a20ce9293e'}, {'abstract': 'White Collar Watch looks at the laws that are likely to be the focus of investigations of the News Corporation and the potential problems that prosecutors would face in pursuing criminal charges.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/news-corp-braces-for-legal-trouble-in-the-u-s/', 'snippet': 'White Collar Watch looks at the laws that are likely to be the focus of investigations of the News Corporation and the potential problems that prosecutors would face in pursuing criminal charges.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The burgeoning scandal at the News Corporation has crossed over to the United States as federal investigations of the company’s conduct have started. There is no clearer sign of the seriousness of the company’s potential exposure to criminal prosecution than its hiring of Brendan V. Sullivan Jr. of Williams & Connolly, one of the most aggressive criminal defense lawyers in the country.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Corp. Braces for Legal Trouble in the U.S.', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Corrupt Practices Act (1977)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wiretapping and Other Eavesdropping Devices and Methods', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NEWS CORP', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WILLIAMS & CONNOLLY', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T19:02:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter J. Henning', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Henning', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2bc3e69-62e8-5242-b7c2-618c94de30a1', 'word_count': 1204, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2bc3e69-62e8-5242-b7c2-618c94de30a1'}, {'abstract': 'Some of these blended soups are elegant enough to serve not only as meals but also