ppet': 'More than eight million people in the United States have macular degeneration, here are two of their stories.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A man wakes up one morning to find that he cannot make out the details of a picture on the wall. His wife’s face, too, has become a blur. A trip to the ophthalmologist reveals he has macular degeneration.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/19/science/19VOIC2/19VOIC2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/19/science/19VOIC2/19VOIC2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/19/science/19VOIC2/19VOIC2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Adapting as Vision and Independence Ebb', 'kicker': 'Patient Voices', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Adapting as Vision and Independence Ebb', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Macular Degeneration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Eyes and Eyesight', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T19:15:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Views', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Barrow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barrow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/bde534c2-5a5f-5ed7-a3a8-2ad9fbd9a95f', 'word_count': 523, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bde534c2-5a5f-5ed7-a3a8-2ad9fbd9a95f'}, {'abstract': 'Despite a 13-month absence after an excruciatingly tense Season 3 cliffhanger, “Breaking Bad” set a ratings record in its return to AMC on Sunday night.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/breaking-bad-returns-with-record-numbers/', 'snippet': 'Despite a 13-month absence after an excruciatingly tense Season 3 cliffhanger, “Breaking Bad” set a ratings record in its return to AMC on Sunday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Despite a 13-month absence after an excruciatingly tense Season 3 cliffhanger, “Breaking Bad” set a ratings record in its return to AMC on Sunday night. According to Nielsen, an estimated 2.6 million people tuned in to witness the further misadventures of the meth dealers Walter White (Bryan Cranston) and Jesse Pinkman (Aaron Paul) and to learn whether Jesse actually killed a fellow meth cooker. That number was 32 percent greater than the viewership for last season’s premiere, and was the highest total in the series’ history.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Breaking Bad’ Cooks Up Record Numbers', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cranston, Bryan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMC (TV Network)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T19:15:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/559013a5-e12d-5bce-bb0b-38ae6cb42f3f', 'word_count': 170, 'uri': 'nyt://article/559013a5-e12d-5bce-bb0b-38ae6cb42f3f'}, {'abstract': 'Open-ended responses from 700 Americans surveyed by Gallup about why they think the debt ceiling should or should not be raised.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/what-americans-really-think-about-the-debt-ceiling/', 'snippet': 'Open-ended responses from 700 Americans surveyed by Gallup about why they think the debt ceiling should or should not be raised.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This month, a Gallup poll found that Americans are almost twice as likely to say they want their Congressional representative to vote against rather than for an increase in the debt ceiling (42 percent to 22 percent, with 35 percent saying they had no opinion).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Americans Really Think About the Debt Ceiling', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T19:22:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5a0f801-8abc-5f90-9169-66598a65e14e', 'word_count': 177, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5a0f801-8abc-5f90-9169-66598a65e14e'}, {'abstract': 'Meet winner #2 in our month-long New York Times as Your Summer Reading contest.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/student-reading-contest-winner-on-having-invasive-species-for-dinner/', 'snippet': 'Meet winner #2 in our month-long New York Times as Your Summer Reading contest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the second week of our Summer Reading Contest, we received 72 entries – many of which, we noticed, came from just three schools, identified by student writers as BSGE, VCHS and RHS. We’re grateful to the teachers and students from those schools for participating in the contest, and we hope more will join them. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Student Reading Contest Winner | On Having Invasive Species for Dinner', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T19:29:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holly Epstein Ojalvo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holly', 'middlename': 'Epstein', 'lastname': 'Ojalvo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4dff9474-abf7-50cf-9035-149783110190', 'word_count': 730, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4dff9474-abf7-50cf-9035-149783110190'}, {'abstract': 'Some of this week’s offerings in the popsicle matrix begin melting more quickly than others.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/ice-pop-update-the-meltiness-factor/', 'snippet': 'Some of this week’s offerings in the popsicle matrix begin melting more quickly than others.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One thing I didn’t have room to get into in the text accompanying this week’s popsicle matrix is what you might call the meltiness factor. Almost anything will freeze solid, but not everything will stay frozen for very long. Some of this week’s offerings begin melting more quickly than others.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ice Pop Update: The Meltiness Factor', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T19:34:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d9db510-48a5-5619-ab10-cb3b410e9675', 'word_count': 353, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d9db510-48a5-5619-ab10-cb3b410e9675'}, {'abstract': 'The show was particularly strong with viewers 18 to 49, beating AMC’s “Mad Men” in that group.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/return-of-breaking-bad-breaks-series-record/', 'snippet': 'The show was particularly strong with viewers 18 to 49, beating AMC’s “Mad Men” in that group.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The AMC drama “Breaking Bad” returned from a long hiatus – so long it missed out on this year’s Emmy nominations – with the strongest ratings the show has recorded.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Return of ‘Breaking Bad’ Breaks Series Record', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emmy Awards', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMC (TV Network)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T19:38:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84227200-e946-5d6f-b961-e614fe6334c7', 'word_count': 264, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84227200-e946-5d6f-b961-e614fe6334c7'}, {'abstract': 'Officials on Monday were discussing a proposal for a special levy to ensure that banks shared part of the cost of helping Greece a second time.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/19/business/global/european-governments-consider-a-bank-tax-to-finance-greek-bailout.html', 'snippet': 'Officials on Monday were discussing a proposal for a special levy to ensure that banks shared part of the cost of helping Greece a second time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRUSSELS — With European leaders poised to hold crucial talks Thursday in what one diplomat called “the euro zone’s ultimate Cinderella moment,” officials on Monday were discussing elements that might prove essential to a second bailout of Greece, including the new idea of a special levy to ensure that banks share part of the cost.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'European Governments Consider a Bank Tax to Finance Greek Bailout', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Levy on Banks Hangs Over Greek Bailout Talk', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trichet, Jean-Claude', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Central Bank', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T19:45:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Castle and Matthew Saltmarsh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saltmarsh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f08a098d-b073-5e55-853f-bf7163fa0574', 'word_count': 918, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f08a098d-b073-5e55-853f-bf7163fa0574'}, {'abstract': 'The interim military-led government replaced 14 of the 27 cabinet members in a concession to the protesters in Tahrir Square, drawing a mixed response.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/19/world/middleeast/19egypt.html', 'snippet': 'The interim military-led government replaced 14 of the 27 cabinet members in a concession to the protesters in Tahrir Square, drawing a mixed response.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — Egypt’s interim military government unveiled a promised cabinet shake-up on Monday aimed at mollifying a 10-day-old protest in Tahrir Square as the protesters themselves appeared for the first time to begin to lose some momentum.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt Revamps Cabinet as Protesters Seem to Lose Steam', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Egypt Revamps Cabinet as Protesters Seem to Lose Steam', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sharaf, Essam Adbel-Aziz', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T19:45:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By David D. Kirkpatrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/454c8049-5e23-5d94-b22a-406918de6595', 'word_count': 672, 'uri': 'nyt://article/454c8049-5e23-5d94-b22a-406918de6595'}, {'abstract': 'Ja Rule, the rapper and actor currently serving up to two years in prison on criminal weapon possession, was sentenced to 28 months for failing to file federal income tax returns over a five-year period.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/ja-rule-sentenced-for-failing-to-pay-taxes/', 'snippet': 'Ja Rule, the rapper and actor currently serving up to two years in prison on criminal weapon possession, was sentenced to 28 months for failing to file federal income tax returns over a five-year period.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ja Rule’s long fall from grace reached a new low in a New Jersey courtroom on Monday when the Queens-born rapper and actor was sentenced to 28 months in prison for failing to file federal income tax returns over a five-year period.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ja Rule Sentenced for Failing to Pay Taxes', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rap and Hip-Hop', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gotti, Irv', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ja Rule', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Murder Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oneida Correctional Facility', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T19:47:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f21592b-283b-52cf-bcce-67f4663e84ab', 'word_count': 532, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f21592b-283b-52cf-bcce-67f4663e84ab'}, {'abstract': '“The White Nile,” by Alan Moorehead, is a very readable tale of the 19th-century European intervention that ultimately led to the uneasy borders of Sudan, now redrawn.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/the-china-model-in-africa/', 'snippet': '“The White Nile,” by Alan Moorehead, is a very readable tale of the 19th-century European intervention that ultimately led to the uneasy borders of Sudan, now redrawn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A week ago a new country was created in Africa: South Sudan. By chance I had just finished reading “The White Nile,” by Alan Moorehead, which, despite some dated language, is a very readable tale of the 19th-century European intervention that ultimately led to the uneasy borders of Sudan, now redrawn.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The China Model in Africa', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giridharadas, Anand', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Aspen Institute', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T19:53:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vera Titunik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vera', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Titunik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/15e52c9d-3917-52d9-93f9-44757ac07c60', 'word_count': 296, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15e52c9d-3917-52d9-93f9-44757ac07c60'}, {'abstract': 'The S.E.C. obtained a freeze on the assets of three Swiss firms accused of illegal insider trading in Arch Chemicals ahead of the company’s $1.2 billion sale to the Lonza Group.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/s-e-c-freezes-assets-of-3-firms-accused-of-insider-trading/', 'snippet': 'The S.E.C. obtained a freeze on the assets of three Swiss firms accused of illegal insider trading in Arch Chemicals ahead of the company’s $1.2 billion sale to the Lonza Group.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Manhattan federal judge has frozen the assets of three Swiss asset managers accused of illegally profiting from trades made ahead of the $1.2 billion sale of Arch Chemicals to the Lonza Group, the Securities and Exchange Commission announced on Monday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'S.E.C. Freezes Assets of 3 Firms Accused of Insider Trading', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insider Trading', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Castel, P Kevin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khuzami, Robert', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARCH CHEMICALS INC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-18T19:57:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/292a9ba3-8735-587a-b551-a0123473e467', 'word_count': 258, 'uri': 'nyt://article/292a9ba3-8735-587a-b551-a0123473e467'}, {'abstract': 'Yao Ming’s retirement from the N.B.A. is forcing many Chinese to acknowledge that they have relied on him alone for national pride, ignoring shortcomings in the state sports system.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/19/sports/basketball/yaos-retirement-forces-china-to-rethink-basketball-system.html', 'snippet': 'Yao Ming’s retirement from the N.B.A. is forcing many Chinese to acknowledge that they have relied on him alone for national pride, ignoring shortcomings in the state sports system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — Nine seasons after Yao Ming walked onto a basketball court in Texas and inspired a generation of young Chinese to learn to dribble — or at least to watch until the final buzzer — his looming exit from professional basketball is being accompanied by nostalgia for the man who became a national hero. It is also triggering frustration over why no one in China, which has tens of millions of basketball players, appears capable of replacing him as an N.B.A. star.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/19/sports/YJPYAO/YJPYAO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 720, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/19/sports/YJPYAO/YJPYAO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/19/sports/YJPYAO/YJPYAO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'As Towering Star Retires, China Is Unprepared to Replace Him', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicke