tivities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The board of the News Corporation might as well be named “Friends of Rupert.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Murdoch’s Board Stands By as Scandal Widens', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Family Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NEWS CORP', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T01:21:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Ross Sorkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'Ross', 'lastname': 'Sorkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/95799e7b-aa39-5235-b36a-d8b85ed4e850', 'word_count': 1075, 'uri': 'nyt://article/95799e7b-aa39-5235-b36a-d8b85ed4e850'}, {'abstract': 'In brief sketches, three pairs of longtime partners discuss how they met, difficulties they endured and their joy at New York’s enactment of a law allowing same-sex marriage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/19/nyregion/same-sex-ny-couples-of-up-to-41-years-who-now-plan-to-marry.html', 'snippet': 'In brief sketches, three pairs of longtime partners discuss how they met, difficulties they endured and their joy at New York’s enactment of a law allowing same-sex marriage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Sunday, New York becomes the sixth and largest state with legalized same-sex marriage. Over the ensuing weeks and months, gay and lesbian couples from around the state, and beyond, are expected to descend on city and town clerks’ offices seeking marriage licenses, with the\xa0legal recognition, and rights, that marriage brings. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Three Same-Sex Couples, Together Many Years, the Wait Is About Over', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Three Same-Sex Couples, Together Many Years, the Wait Is About Over', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T01:21:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4869bb9-8c86-59d2-9ef5-94c7dec94ab8', 'word_count': 1120, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4869bb9-8c86-59d2-9ef5-94c7dec94ab8'}, {'abstract': 'Today’s television weather forecasters, increasingly called meteorologists, are going beyond simply telling people whether to carry an umbrella.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/19/us/19weatherman.html', 'snippet': 'Today’s television weather forecasters, increasingly called meteorologists, are going beyond simply telling people whether to carry an umbrella.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATLANTA — One evening in April, Tina Eller had the television on. Glenn Burns, the steely chief meteorologist for WSB-TV, said a tornado was three minutes away from slamming into her community. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/19/us/jp-WEATHERMAN/jp-WEATHERMAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/19/us/jp-WEATHERMAN/jp-WEATHERMAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/19/us/jp-WEATHERMAN/jp-WEATHERMAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/19/us/jp-WEATHERMAN/jp-WEATHERMAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/19/us/jp-WEATHERMAN/jp-WEATHERMAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'As Weather Becomes Big Story, TV Forecasters Play the Hero', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Weather Becomes Big Story, TV Forecasters Play the Hero', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radar', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tornadoes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T01:22:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kim Severson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Severson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fff93174-e2b3-5087-9618-ff601dbc9868', 'word_count': 1179, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fff93174-e2b3-5087-9618-ff601dbc9868'}, {'abstract': 'The Syrian opposition is not giving up, but they will need more support from the international community.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/19/opinion/19tue2.html', 'snippet': 'The Syrian opposition is not giving up, but they will need more support from the international community.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We are in awe at the courage of the Syrian people and disgusted by the brutality of President Bashar al-Assad and his henchmen. Mr. Assad has lost all legitimacy. The question now is what can the international community do to support the opposition and its demands for freedom? ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Syria’s Struggle', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Syria’s Struggle: The opposition isn’t giving up and needs clearer support from Washington and its allies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Security Council (UN)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARAB LEAGUE', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T01:24:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/7beee802-e454-5ab2-8c4e-5c5bbb996d22', 'word_count': 428, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7beee802-e454-5ab2-8c4e-5c5bbb996d22'}, {'abstract': 'New Yorkers have heard this before: officials said the system would not only locate tie-ups, but also alter traffic signals to ease them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/19/nyregion/a-new-high-tech-assault-on-midtown-traffic-jams.html', 'snippet': 'New Yorkers have heard this before: officials said the system would not only locate tie-ups, but also alter traffic signals to ease them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is an all-too-common sight in Midtown Manhattan: cars, taxis and trucks stacked behind one another, gridlock forming at intersections, horns blaring as pedestrians navigate the tight spaces between bumpers.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/19/nyregion/traffic/traffic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/19/nyregion/traffic/traffic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/19/nyregion/traffic/traffic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/19/nyregion/traffic/traffic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/19/nyregion/traffic/traffic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A New High-Tech Assault on Midtown Traffic Jams', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A New High-Tech Assault On Midtown Traffic Jams', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Midtown Area (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Signals and Signs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Delays (Transportation)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T01:35:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Haughney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haughney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce920249-b8d4-5727-9f11-24bff279d245', 'word_count': 702, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce920249-b8d4-5727-9f11-24bff279d245'}, {'abstract': 'A ruling on Chinese exports should also serve as a warning to others about protectionism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/19/opinion/19tue3.html', 'snippet': 'A ruling on Chinese exports should also serve as a warning to others about protectionism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The World Trade Organization’s ruling this month against China’s restrictions on the export of raw materials is a welcome decision that we hope will temper China’s mercantilistic strategy, in which every policy decision is designed to favor Chinese exporters. It also should serve as a warning to others about these protectionist tools. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nobody Should Be Fooled. It’s Protectionism.', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nobody Should Be Fooled. It&#8217;s Protectionism.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Protectionism (Trade)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Trade Organization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rare Earths', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T01:37:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/1824f8ed-89d5-56b5-be1e-70504373874a', 'word_count': 374, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1824f8ed-89d5-56b5-be1e-70504373874a'}, {'abstract': 'Is this payback for a media empire that took glee in the misery of others?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/19/opinion/19nocera.html', 'snippet': 'Is this payback for a media empire that took glee in the misery of others?', 'lead_paragraph': 'You have to love the fact that when John Yates resigned on Monday as the assistant commissioner of the Metropolitan Police in London — a k a Scotland Yard — he complained about the “huge amount of inaccurate, ill-informed and, on occasion, downright malicious gossip” that had finally forced his hand. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbLarge-v4.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Tables Are Turned on Murdoch', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Tables Are Turned On Murdoch', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News of the World', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wiretapping and Other Eavesdropping Devices and Methods', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wall Street Journal', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yates, John', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NEWS CORP', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T01:37:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Nocera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nocera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/dadfba88-4a0c-5c85-8f44-cdb7e3be3bab', 'word_count': 847, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dadfba88-4a0c-5c85-8f44-cdb7e3be3bab'}, {'abstract': 'Congress and regulators should address the future of the government mortgage finance companies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/19/business/economy/time-for-action-on-freddie-and-fannie-reuters-breakingviews.html', 'snippet': 'Congress and regulators should address the future of the government mortgage finance companies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A year after passage of the Dodd-Frank act, the $10.5 trillion American mortgage market remains in limbo. One big reason is that the law scarcely touches Fannie Mae, Freddie Mac and the Federal Housing Administration — the government-run lenders that dominate the home loan market.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/19/business/VIEWS/VIEWS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 973, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Time for Action on Freddie and Fannie', 'kicker': 'Reuters Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mortgage Market Due for Overhaul', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal National Mortgage Assn (Fannie Mae)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Home Loan Mortgage Corp (Freddie Mac)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgage-Backed Securities', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T01:39:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Agnes T. Crane, George Hay and Peter Thal Larsen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Agnes', 'middlename': 'T.', 'lastname': 'Crane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'Thal', 'lastname': 'Larsen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/240a704a-3952-5b30-b561-67d3baf9e4cd', 'word_count': 709, 'uri': 'nyt://article/240a704a-3952-5b30-b561-67d3baf9e4cd'}, {'abstract': 'The absence of top predators cascades through nature in surprisingly complex ways.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/19/opinion/19tue4.html', 'snippet': 'The absence of top predators cascades through nature in surprisingly complex ways.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A familiar metaphor for nature is the pyramid of life, with large predators living at the peak because they’re few in number and eat species lower on the pyramid. Like most simple metaphors, this one has a perceptual flaw. It creates the illusion that large predators have an effect only on the prey species immediately below them. The truth, as a growing body of scientific studies shows, is that the presence, and absence, of top predators cascades all through nature in surprisingly complex ways. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Peak and Life Below It', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Peak and Life Below It', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biodiversity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMALS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T01:42:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9398f81-6bb7-552b-addf-0e5bac817b00', 'word_count': 298, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9398f81-6bb7-552b-addf-0e5bac817b00'}, {'abstract': 'The six Episcopal bishops in New York decide individually whether a priest can officiate at a same-sex wedding, or even attend.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/19/nyregion/new-episcopal-split-priests-role-in-ny-gay-weddings.html', 'snippet': 'The six Episcopal bishops in New York decide individually whether a priest can officiate at a same-sex wedding, or even attend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Episcopal Church, which has been strained by gay-rights issues since the election of an openly gay bishop in New Hampshire eight years ago, is now divided over how to respond to the legalization of same-sex marriage in New York. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/19/nyregion/episcopal2/episcopal2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/19/nyregion/episcopal2/episcopal2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/19/nyregion/episcopal2/episcopal2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/19/nyregion/episcopal2/episcopal2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/19/nyregion/episcopal2/episcopal2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'True to Episcopal Church’s Past, Bishops Split on Gay Weddings', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'True to Episc