 and Alex Morgan will appear on several television programs.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/u-s-women-return-with-heads-held-high/', 'snippet': 'On Tuesday, Hope Solo, Abby Wambach, Christie Rampone and Alex Morgan will appear on several television programs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After their heartbreaking loss to Japan in the Women’s World Cup final, the players on the United States team were nevertheless treated to a hero’s welcome near Times Square on Monday. Onlookers gathered outside the W Hotel on 47th Street and Broadway like a flash mob, snapping photographs, seeking autographs and calling out “Hope!” at the popular goalkeeper Hope Solo.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Women Return With Heads Held High', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's World Cup (Soccer)", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Solo, Hope', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wambach, Abby', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T02:05:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Justin G. Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/045a7774-0490-547a-ac53-bb7406eef059', 'word_count': 584, 'uri': 'nyt://article/045a7774-0490-547a-ac53-bb7406eef059'}, {'abstract': 'Where were the practical conservatives when the spending cuts were on the table?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/19/opinion/19brooks.html', 'snippet': 'Where were the practical conservatives when the spending cuts were on the table?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the past months, Republicans enjoyed enormous advantages. Opinion polls showed that voters are eager to reduce the federal debt, and they want to do it mostly but not entirely through spending cuts. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-thumbLarge-v2.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Road Not Taken', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Road Not Taken', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservatism (US Politics)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T02:09:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Brooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/2152ef8f-b47e-5284-9c8d-d021ab6fdc03', 'word_count': 787, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2152ef8f-b47e-5284-9c8d-d021ab6fdc03'}, {'abstract': 'Health insurers continue to charge fees that make it difficult, and sometimes impossible, for women to prevent unintended pregnancy. That could soon change.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/19/opinion/19cullins.html', 'snippet': 'Health insurers continue to charge fees that make it difficult, and sometimes impossible, for women to prevent unintended pregnancy. That could soon change.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MY daughter, a divorced mother of three, called me recently to complain about the high cost of birth control. As a physician, I’m familiar with this problem, yet it never fails to frustrate me. Our health care system could save billions — and improve the health of women and families — by placing birth control within every woman’s reach. Instead, health insurers continue to charge fees that make it difficult, sometimes impossible, for women to prevent unintended pregnancy. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Make Birth Control Affordable', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Make Birth Control Affordable', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Preventive Medicine', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Obstetrics', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T02:15:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vanessa Cullins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vanessa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cullins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0b52d6e-03bb-505f-b1ca-e60ea5373e5c', 'word_count': 569, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0b52d6e-03bb-505f-b1ca-e60ea5373e5c'}, {'abstract': 'Rebels fire artillery guns outside of Ajdabiya.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/07/19/world/africa/20110719_LIBYA.html', 'snippet': 'Rebels fire artillery guns outside of Ajdabiya.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rebels fire artillery guns outside of Ajdabiya.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/19/world/africa/20110719_LIBYA-slide-J8PB/20110719_LIBYA-slide-J8PB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 665, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/19/world/africa/20110719_LIBYA-slide-J8PB/20110719_LIBYA-slide-J8PB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/19/world/africa/20110719_LIBYA-slide-J8PB/20110719_LIBYA-slide-J8PB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Battle for Libya | July 18, 2011', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T02:18:26+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'World', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/9d4a0d64-640c-5dba-9453-8618596a0a55', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/9d4a0d64-640c-5dba-9453-8618596a0a55'}, {'abstract': 'Rebecca Black has traded guileless, catchy awfulness for smug, catchy soullessness, a classic pop-culture progression.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/18/watchlist-rebecca-blacks-new-music-video/', 'snippet': 'Rebecca Black has traded guileless, catchy awfulness for smug, catchy soullessness, a classic pop-culture progression.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ah, Rebecca Black. As you sing in your new music video, “My Moment,” you’ve “waited for so long” for your moment to come. It’s been five whole months since your first music video, “Friday,” made you famous in not quite the way you expected and was watched 160 million times on YouTube. You even turned 14 in the meantime. Now you’re going to be famous on your own terms, at your own Web site, plus on your YouTube channel and, starting Tuesday, at iTunes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Watchlist: Rebecca Black’s New Music Video', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T02:19:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Hale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1de56c9e-b127-5f2e-8c6f-9e38bf4f003a', 'word_count': 441, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1de56c9e-b127-5f2e-8c6f-9e38bf4f003a'}, {'abstract': 'Members of Libya’s most prominent Islamist group are largely watching the civil conflict from exile, and officials are leery of the fighters’ former affiliation with Al Qaeda.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/19/world/africa/19rebel.html', 'snippet': 'Members of Libya’s most prominent Islamist group are largely watching the civil conflict from exile, and officials are leery of the fighters’ former affiliation with Al Qaeda.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Abu Sohaib spends most of his time online these days, following the news from his native Libya. He is in constant contact with friends on the ground there, helping them map out strategy to fight the rule of Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/19/world/REBEL/REBEL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/19/world/REBEL/REBEL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thu