 Internet search engine and long a haven for pirated music, will be able to download and stream songs legally.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/19/technology/baidu-chinas-search-giant-announces-music-licensing-deal.html', 'snippet': 'Users of Baidu, China’s dominant Internet search engine and long a haven for pirated music, will be able to download and stream songs legally.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — Baidu, the dominant Chinese Internet search engine, on Tuesday announced a major licensing deal with three of the world’s largest music companies that would allow Chinese Web users to legally download and stream hundreds of thousands of songs free.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/19/business/BAIDU/BAIDU-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 724, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'China’s Biggest Search Engine, Known for Illegal Downloads, Makes Music Deal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China’s Biggest Search Engine, Known for Illegal Downloads, Makes Music Deal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recordings and Downloads (Audio)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search Engines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Copyrights and Copyright Violations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baidu Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T04:06:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Levin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Levin', 'qualifier': None, 