': 'Central Park Chapels to ‘Pop Up’ for Gay Marriages', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Architizer', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Parks and Recreation Department (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TheKnot.com', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'CENTRAL PARK (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'COLUMBUS CIRCLE (NYC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T11:00:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9075e0d-0164-56de-9dcd-b61d77f46835', 'word_count': 638, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9075e0d-0164-56de-9dcd-b61d77f46835'}, {'abstract': 'My revelation started with a conversation among the owners in my business group.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/19/am-i-focusing-on-the-wrong-part-of-my-business/', 'snippet': 'My revelation started with a conversation among the owners in my business group.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is now more than three years since the economy took a nosedive. For most small businesses, this has been even more challenging than previous recessions because we have also had to deal with the real estate collapse, a credit crisis and changes in the marketplace brought on by the Internet and other forces. Not an easy time. And I don’t see much evidence of a bounce back coming soon. I have come to the conclusion that it is time to reassess.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Am I Focusing on the Wrong Part of My Business?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T11:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jay Goltz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goltz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d933e116-d231-5fb9-8138-8c80e7d028f0', 'word_count': 712, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d933e116-d231-5fb9-8138-8c80e7d028f0'}, {'abstract': 'The bank doled out huge payments to settle legal claims related to its troubled mortgage division. The loss was steep, but it was fully baked into expectations.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/07/19/bank-of-america-reports-loss-of-8-8-billion/', 'snippet': 'The bank doled out huge payments to settle legal claims related to its troubled mortgage division. The loss was steep, but it was fully baked into expectations.', 'lead_paragraph': '8:34 a.m. | Updated  Bank of America reported a loss of $8.8 billion in the second quarter as it doled out huge payments to settle legal claims related to its troubled mortgage division.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Bank of America, an $8.8 Billion Loss', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bank of America Corporation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T11:11:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f00430af-f040-5fdf-88ed-d85041b0ccdc', 'word_count': 693, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f00430af-f040-5fdf-88ed-d85041b0ccdc'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Rick Perry has promoted his economic record in Texas, but if he runs for president, it is clear that he plans to appeal to social conservatives.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/19/perry-takes-aim-at-religious-voters/', 'snippet': 'Gov. Rick Perry has promoted his economic record in Texas, but if he runs for president, it is clear that he plans to appeal to social conservatives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If Gov. Rick Perry of Texas runs for president, one thing seems clear: he plans to make a concerted appeal to the conservative Christians who make up a large block of Iowa’s Republican caucus voters.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Perry Eyes Religious Voters', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bachmann, Michele M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cain, Herman', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huckabee, Mike', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pawlenty, Tim', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': '