Reid maneuver a Republican retreat, or a conservative victory?', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/19/are-the-republicans-winning/', 'snippet': 'Is the McConnell-Reid maneuver a Republican retreat, or a conservative victory?', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a counterpoint to my column yesterday, which argued that Republicans have ceded the high ground in the debt-ceiling debate, I recommend Ezra Klein’s argument that the emerging Mitch McConnell-Harry Reid maneuver is actually a great deal for the right:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Are the Republicans Winning?', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T15:09:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f58d314b-f734-530d-9b7a-80af6d5abe4d', 'word_count': 755, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f58d314b-f734-530d-9b7a-80af6d5abe4d'}, {'abstract': 'This year the nominees include two past winners, P.J. Harvey and Elbow.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/19/adele-tops-shortlist-for-mercury-prize/', 'snippet': 'This year the nominees include two past winners, P.J. Harvey and Elbow.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Adele, the soulful British singer and songwriter who has dominated American and British charts this summer, was among the 12 artists nominated today for the Barclaycard Mercury Prize, along with the rapper Tinie Tempah and the electronic-music wunderkind James Blake.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Adele Tops Shortlist for Mercury Prize', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headli