lBook newsletter.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/07/19/morning-take-out-288/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOP STORIES', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Take-Out', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T15:25:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cdcfb00d-2395-5a39-97a7-9bb01e054fc8', 'word_count': 2162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cdcfb00d-2395-5a39-97a7-9bb01e054fc8'}, {'abstract': 'With a new N.F.L. collective bargaining agreement imminent, sportswriters examine what’s left to decide and the role some key figures played thus far.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/sports/sides-in-nfl-labor-dispute-anticipating-a-tentative-agreement.html', 'snippet': 'With a new N.F.L. collective bargaining agreement imminent, sportswriters examine what’s left to decide and the role some key figures played thus far.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We regret to inform you that all of the excitement of last weekend — those riveting soccer games and golf played for a while in a typhoon — has been replaced in the top sports news by lawyers in suits “anticipating a tentative agreement” to end the N.F.L. lockout. Yes, ladies and gentlemen, we are assured that an agreement is near. We think. Could get hung up, though. So check back when more lawyers in suits pony up to another microphone and we feel more of our brain cells sliding into a deep freeze.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Waiting for a Deal', 'kicker'