lue': 'Santa Barbara (Calif)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vancouver (British Columbia)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T17:47:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0035d3b9-33c0-542c-b37d-c70472ea9d7f', 'word_count': 197, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0035d3b9-33c0-542c-b37d-c70472ea9d7f'}, {'abstract': 'A New Jersey restaurant accidentally served a meat-filled dish to vegetarian Indian-Americans.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/19/court-permits-hindus-who-were-served-meat-to-sue-for-a-purifying-trip-to-india/', 'snippet': 'A New Jersey restaurant accidentally served a meat-filled dish to vegetarian Indian-Americans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A New Jersey appeals court has ruled that a group of Hindu diners can sue to be flown to India to resolve a dispute over an order of samosas, The Star-Ledger is reporting. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Court Permits Hindus Who Were Served Meat to Sue for a Purifying Trip to India', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T17:49:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Glenn Collins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Glenn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55270687-b2ad-5e10-a82d-a0af2f7fbf7e', 'word_count': 183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55270687-b2ad-5e10-a82d-a0af2f7fbf7e'}, {'abstract': 'Approached with sufficient caution, head-to-head polls can probably provide some insight as to how different types of Republican candidates would fare against President Obama.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/19/is-obama-against-romney-a-toss-up/', 'snippet': 'Approached with sufficient caution, head-to-head polls can probably provide some insight as to how different types of Republican candidates would fare against President Obama.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Looking at head-to-head polls can be treacherous so far in advance of a presidential election. Instead, I’d suggest that you devote most of your attention to President Obama’s approval ratings and perhaps the favorability ratings of the Republican candidates, as well as to things like economic forecasts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is Obama Against Romney a Toss-Up?', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T17:50:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/66629f2b-8ccf-51f7-90c6-3f35cde52269', 'word_count': 1040, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66629f2b-8ccf-51f7-90c6-3f35cde52269'}, {'ab