hout infecting others.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Regulators said on Tuesday that 28 of the world’s biggest and most interconnected banks would be required to hold more capital in reserve than less important banks would under proposals intended to keep the failure of one or two large institutions from causing a calamity. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Reserves May Be Asked of Top Banks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'More Reserves May Be Asked Of Top Banks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Basel Committee on Banking Supervision', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Group of Twenty', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Financial Stability Board', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T18:46:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Ewing', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ewing', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b8ff603-3d66-5113-83e6-ea36f77eba49', 'word_count': 300, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b8ff603-3d66-5113-83e6-ea36f77eba49'}, {'abstract': 'As Ashley Hebert met the families of her various suitors and whittled down her true love options to three from four, the audience actually grew over the course of the episode.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/19/a-growing-crowd-follows-the-bachelorette-and-her-search-for-love/', 'snippet': 'As Ashley Hebert met the families of her various suitors and whittled down her true love options to three from four, the audience actually grew over the course of the episode.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Reality programming once again dominated prime time as a two-hour version of “The Bachelorette” was the most-watched program on Monday evening, with an average of 7.7 million viewers tuning into ABC’s matchmaking show. As Ashley Hebert met the families of her various suitors and whittled down her true love options to three from four, the audience numbers actually grew over the course of the episode. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Growing Crowd Follows ‘The Bachelorette’ and Her Search for Love', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T18:59:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2efd06e-95d8-52eb-a244-21a9dbe0b95d', 'word_count': 159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2efd06e-95d8-52eb-a244-21a9dbe0b95d'}, {'abstract': 'Photographs of the newly refurbished dinosaur exhibition at the Natural History Museum of Los Angeles County, which opened this month.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/07/19/arts/20110720-DINO.html', 'snippet': 'Photographs of the newly refurbished dinosaur exhibition at the Natural History Museum of Los Angeles County, which opened this month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photographs of the newly refurbished dinosaur exhibition at the Natural History Museum of Los Angeles County, which opened this month.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credi