l': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/19/on-the-hunt-for-brooklyns-greenest/', 'snippet': 'Block associations have their checklists out and judges are on the streets in the 17th annual Greenest Block in Brooklyn contest. In early August, a winner will be chosen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'These days, Bee Atwell patrols her shaded block in the Bedford-Stuyvesant section of Brooklyn, horticultural checklist in hand. Are the stoops brightened by potted plants? Are the hydrangeas properly watered? Do the tree beds have signs warning dogs to lift their hind legs elsewhere?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On the Hunt for Brooklyn’s Greenest', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Contests and Prizes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flowers and Plants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gardens and Gardening', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Botanic Garden', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T19:07:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa W. Foderaro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Foderaro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3707ddb-5bcc-55d0-8086-da7d01d73b35', 'word_count': 842, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3707ddb-5bcc-55d0-8086-da7d01d73b35'}, {'abstract': 'The documentary will chronicle Mr. McCartney’s experiences in New York after the 9/11 terrorist attacks, including his preparation for and performance at the “Concert for New York City.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/19/paul-mccartney-documentary-the-love-we-make-coming-to-showtime/', 'snippet': 'The documentary will chronicle Mr. McCartney’s experiences in New York after the 9/11 terrorist attacks, including his preparation for and performance at the “Concert for New York City.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'No amount of coverage of the lives of the Beatles could make us say it’s all too much, and the cable networks are surely relieved to hear it. Following an announcement by HBO that it had acquired a documentary about George Harrison, Showtime said on Tuesday that it would broadcast a nonfiction feature about Paul McCartney and his experiences in New York after the 9/11 terrorist attacks. The film, “The Love We Make,” will chronicle Mr. McCartney’s journey from Sept. 11, 2001, when his plane was grounded on a New York tarmac, through his planning for and performance at the “Concert for New York City” at Madison Square Garden the next month. “The Love We Make” will feature footage from that concert as well as appearances by Mr. McCartney’s friends and colleagues, including David Bowie, Eric Clapton, Mick Jagger, Keith Richards and Pete Townshend, as well as his daughter Stella. It is directed by Bradley Kaplan and Albert Maysles, the venerated co-director of “Grey Gardens” and “Gimme Shelter,” as well as the 1964 documentary “What’s Happening! The Beatles in the U.S.A.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paul McCartney Documentary, ‘The Love We Make,’ Coming to Showtime', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bowie, David', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harrison, George', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jagger, Mick', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maysles, Albert', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCartney, Paul', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Beatles, The', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Showtime', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T19:15:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/630aae44-22c0-53b8-8d71-20164f36db5a', 'word_count': 279, 'uri': 'nyt://article/630aae44-22c0-53b8-8d71-20164f36db5a'}, {'abstract': 'Google is playing venture capitalist in the hottest market for technology start-up companies in over a decade.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/technology/google-spending-millions-to-find-the-next-google.html', 'snippet': 'Google is playing venture capitalist in the hottest market for technology start-up companies in over a decade.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOUNTAIN VIEW, Calif. — Google thinks it can be young and crazy again. And it is betting $200 million that it is right.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/20/technology/20googlePicA/20googlePicA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 335, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/20/technology/20googlePicA/20googlePicA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 335}}, {'rank': 0, 's