ear-long inquiry, please tell us what you’ll do — or have done — around this topic, and why. We hope to publish a variety of ideas from teachers across subject areas and levels.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Update, Aug. 12 |  Thank you to the many teachers who have written in so far — and please, keep those ideas coming! As we work behind the scenes to get ready for this anniversary, your creative and thoughtful responses have been enormously helpful. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Do You Teach About 9/11?', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T19:37:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09e444c1-4482-54d1-b985-4ebabef5d3fb', 'word_count': 253, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09e444c1-4482-54d1-b985-4ebabef5d3fb'}, {'abstract': 'Cadel Evans of Australia, who is second, and Alberto Contador of Spain, who is sixth, cut into Thomas Voeckler’s lead in the Tour de France, and Stage 16 went to Thor Hushovd of Norway.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/sports/cycling/2011-tour-de-france-as-contador-attacks-voeckler-feels-lead-slipping.html', 'snippet': 'Cadel Evans of Australia, who is second, and Alberto Contador of Spain, who is sixth, cut into Thomas Voeckler’s lead in the Tour de France, and Stage 16 went to Thor Hushovd of Norway.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GAP, France — Late Tuesday afternoon, in the capital of the Southern Alps, the French cyclist Thomas Voeckler wore both the yellow jersey and a frown. He led the Tour de France, still, for another day, maybe two, but almost certainly not for long.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/20/sports/cycling/20tour-pic/20tour-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/20/sports/cycling/20tour-pic/20tour-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/20/sports/cycling/20tour-pic/20tour-pic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/20/sports/cycling/20tour-pic/20tour-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/20/sports/cycling/20tour-pic/20tour-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Voeckler Feels Yellow Jersey Slipping Away', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Voeckler Feels the Yellow Jersey Slipping Away', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Contador, Alberto', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tour de France (Bicycle Race)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Voeckler, Thomas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Evans, Cadel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hushovd, Thor', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bicycles and Bicycling', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T19:39:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Cycling', 'byline': {'original':