liams Companies’ most recent $44 a share bid.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Locked in a bidding war for the Southern Union Company, Energy Transfer Equity said Tuesday that it would raise its bid for the pipeline operator to $5.9 billion, edging past a rival offer by the Williams Companies.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Energy Transfer Bumps Its Southern Union Bid', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Herschmann, Eric D', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Energy Transfer Equity LP', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Southern Union Company', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Williams Cos Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T20:11:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c826ae8-73aa-537c-93f2-0ff1dbb44bee', 'word_count': 329, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c826ae8-73aa-537c-93f2-0ff1dbb44bee'}, {'abstract': 'Representative Michele Bachmann’s presidential campaign denied a report that migraines at times left her “incapacitated,” saying they would not affect her ability to serve.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/us/politics/20bachmann.html', 'snippet': 'Representative Michele Bachmann’s presidential campaign denied a report that migraines at times left her “incapacitated,” saying they would not affect her ability to serve.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Representative Michele Bachmann suffers from migraine headaches so intense that she has sometimes sought emergency medical treatment, but the congresswoman said Tuesday that the condition would not preclude her from serving as president if elected.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/20/us/BACHMANN/BACHMANN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 709, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/20/us/BACHMANN/BACHMANN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/20/us/BACHMANN/BACHMANN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bachmann Says Migraines Won’t Be a Problem if She’s Elected President', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bachmann Says Severe Migraines Have Never Incapacitated Her', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bachmann, Michele M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Migraine Headaches', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T20:13:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sheryl Gay Stolberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sheryl', 'middlename': 'Gay', 'lastname': 'Stolberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0ce6c78-9b0b-5aa3-8978-2adfeadc9d5b', 'word_count': 635, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0ce6c78-9b0b-5aa3-8978-2adfeadc9d5b'}, {'abstract': 'It’s official: The anklet is once again de rigueur.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/19/the-chain-gang/', 'snippet': 'It’s official: The anklet is once again de rigueur.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We saw it first on the spring runways at Valentino and Chloé — models wearing delicate gold anklets with the daintiest flats. Then, for resort, the Row collaborated with the jewelry designer Ileana Makri on charmy versions of the accessory. And earlier this week the blogger Garance Doré confessed her love for the delicate adornment. It’s official: The anklet is de rigueur again. “I made one for myself last summer, and I absolutely love it,” the jewelry designer Irene Neuwirth\xa0says. “I don’t wear it every day, but I do find that once I put it on I don’t take it off.” Can’t wait until the Row’s resort version hits stores? Doré recommends doing it yourself. “I love the simple ones — tiny gold or silver bracelets will do, small beads I put on a string, or even just a piece of colored cord,” she says. “It’s charming when it feels easy.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Chain Gang', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T20:18:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ab5b1de-e85c-5284-9ec6-0d3ddce9ead7', 'word_count': 151, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ab5b1de-e85c-5284-9ec6-0d3ddce9ead7'}, {'abstract': 'After a weedkiller emerges as a leading suspect in the deaths of thousands of trees, property owners demand replacement trees and punitive damages.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/19/dupont-is-sued-over-new-herbicide/', 'snippet': 'After a weedkiller emerges as a leading suspect in the deaths of thousands of trees, property owners demand replacement trees and punitive damages.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Pennsylvania homeowner and an Indiana golf course company have filed a class-action lawsuit against DuPont charging that the chemical giant was either negligent or reckless in putting a new weedkiller on the market.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'DuPont Is Sued Over New Herbicide', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defoliants and Herbicides', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trees and Shrubs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'DuPont Company', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Michigan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T20:24:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanna M. Foster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18889fdd-3df4-5f33-8d5d-f08f4e94d66d', 'word_count': 535, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18889fdd-3df4-5f33-8d5d-f08f4e94d66d'}, {'abstract': 'The City Council Speaker on the lottery system that will determine which of those same-sex couple who wish to wed on June 24 will be married by the city.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/multimedia/100000000954199/christine-quinn-on-gay-marriage-lottery.html', 'snip