[{'firstname': 'Verne', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'Kopytoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0290f0c-72db-5156-bdb5-80628974d77b', 'word_count': 878, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0290f0c-72db-5156-bdb5-80628974d77b'}, {'abstract': 'An outbreak of bootlegging in New York reflects a change in immigration patterns from China.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/nyregion/sale-of-illegal-wine-flourishes-in-chinese-enclaves.html', 'snippet': 'An outbreak of bootlegging in New York reflects a change in immigration patterns from China.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The restaurant looks like so many others in the roiling heart of Chinatown, in Lower Manhattan: a garish sign in Chinese and English, slapdash photos of featured dishes taped to the windows, and extended Chinese families crowding around tables, digging into communal plates of steamed fish, fried tofu and sautéed watercress.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/20/nyregion/moonshine1/moonshine1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 372, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/20/nyregion/moonshine1/moonshine1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 372}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/20/nyregion/moonshine1/moonshine1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 701, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/20/nyregion/moonshine1/moonshine1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/20/nyregion/moonshine1/moonshine1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Illegal Sale of Rice Wine Thrives in Chinese Enclaves', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Illegal Sale of Rice Wine Thrives in Chinese Enclaves', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chinese-Americans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALCOHOLIC BEVERAGES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black Markets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chinatown (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Flushing (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'SUNSET PARK (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T21:09:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kirk Semple and Jeffrey E. Singer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kirk', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Semple', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jeffrey', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Singer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/23d40a78-bc22-5ea4-a9d7-9abaf8ff2a22', 'word_count': 1190, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23d40a78-bc22-5ea4-a9d7-9abaf8ff2a22'}, {'abstract': 'Finally, some not-dispiriting news from Washington. Who put forward the proposal that could help stave off economic catastrophe? A bipartisan group of seven senators called the Gang of Six.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/19/all-hail-the-gang-of-six-or-seven/', 'snippet': 'Finally, some not-dispiriting news from Washington. Who put forward the proposal that could help stave off economic catastrophe? A bipartisan group of seven senators called the Gang of Six.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Finally, some not-dispiriting news from Washington: President Obama has given his qualified support to a new plan to reduce the deficit, remarking that it “is broadly consistent with what we’ve been working on at the White House.” And who put forward this proposal that could help stave off economic catastrophe? A bipartisan group of seven senators called the Gang of Six. (Congress has never been good with numbers.) Earlier this year, Bill Keller wrote a column for the magazine praising the gang’s efforts, which he said proved that the word “politician” need not be a synonym for “craven,” and it’s certainly worth rereading now.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'All Hail the Gang of Six (or Seven)', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T21:13:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Greg Veis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Greg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Veis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2990602-0fd0-5856-9de0-aa735fe22eea', 'word_count': 104, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2990602-0fd0-5856-9de0-aa735fe22eea'}, {'abstract': 'Camille Strauss-Kahn was called to testify before investigators Monday as part of an investigation into accusations that her father attempted to rape a young writer, Tristane Banon, in 2003.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/world/europe/20france.html', 'snippet': 'Camille Strauss-Kahn was called to testify before investigators Monday as part of an investigation into accusations that her father attempted to rape a young writer, Tristane Banon, in 2003.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Investigators have questioned the daughter of Dominique Strauss-Kahn, the former head of the International Monetary Fund, as part of an investigation into accusations that he attempted to rape a young writer, Tristane Banon, in 2003, an official at the prosecutor’s office said on Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Daughter of Strauss-Kahn Is Questioned', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Daughter of Strauss-Kahn Is Questioned', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strauss-Kahn, Dominique', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Banon, Tristane', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T21:16:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maïa de la Baume', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maïa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'de la Baume', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/993c1ac3-add8-5baf-8b3f-4a8f9684e3a5', 'word_count': 451, 'uri': 'nyt://article/993c1ac3-add8-5baf-8b3f-4a8f9684e3a5'}, {'abstract': 'A. O. Scott looks back at Rob Reiner’s 1984 mockumentary.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/19/critics-picks-video-this-is-spinal-tap/', 'snippet': 'A. O. Scott looks back at Rob Reiner’s 1984 mockumentary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A. O. Scott turns his critical meter up to 11 when looking back at Rob Reiner‘s 1984 comedy “This Is Spinal Tap.” The film, which takes a “mockumentary” look inside the workings of the fictional rock band Spinal Tap, succeeds because it takes its characters seriously.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Critics’ Picks Video: ‘This is Spinal Tap’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Guest, Christopher', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McKean, Michael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reiner, Rob', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shearer, Harry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T21:20:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d040f0b-4bf3-546d-9a7c-ef566fe2acfa', 'word_count': 145, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d040f0b-4bf3-546d-9a7c-ef566fe2acfa'}, {'abstract': 'The company said enrollment rose and members were moderating their use of health care services.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/business/unitedhealth-groups-2nd-quarter-profit-jumps-13-percent.html', 'snippet': 'The company said enrollment rose and members were moderating their use of health care services.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The UnitedHealth Group, one of the nation’s largest health insurers, reported its second-quarter results on Tuesday, and the good news for the industry appeared likely to continue. UnitedHealth announced a double-digit increase in profits and raised its estimates for 2011 earnings, according to its news release. Its net income rose 13 percent, to $1.27 billion, or $1.16 a share, compared with $1.12 billion, or 99 cents a share, one year ago. And revenue increased 8 percent, to $25.23 billion. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Profit Up 13%, UnitedHealth Raises Outlook', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Profit Up 13%, UnitedHealth Raises Outlook', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'UnitedHealth Group Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T21:22:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Reed Abelson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Reed', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abelson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/038ee9c9-2d66-570a-b9d1-4a016c4411bc', 'word_count': 295, 'uri': 'nyt://article/038ee9c9-2d66-570a-b9d1-4a016c4411bc'}, {'abstract': 'After threatening a lockout, the Joffrey Ballet has reached a tentative settlement with its dancers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/arts/dance/joffrey-ballet-dancers-agree-to-tentative-deal.html', 'snippet': 'After threatening a lockout, the Joffrey Ballet has reached a tentative settlement with its dancers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After threatening a lockout, the Joffrey Ballet has reached a tentative settlement with its dancers, The Chicago Sun-Times reported. The company, based in Chicago, was in a contract dispute over salaries and rehearsal hours. The Joffrey wanted to increase the hours, to the chagrin of the American Guild of Musical Artists, the union representing the dancers and stage managers, who maintained they were not being compensated adequately for the extra time. This month the managers of the Joffrey sent a letter to its dancers, who were on a scheduled vacation, telling them that performances would be canceled unless a contract was signed. Christopher Clinton Conway, the Joffrey’s executive director, told The Sun-Times that, pending a vote by the dancers, a tentative agreement had been reached. The new contract, for five years instead of the previous contract’s three, includes a minimum 10 percent raise. “The dancers will be back in class on Monday, and rehearsals will begin, as planned, on July 25,” Mr. Conway said. Representatives for the guild could not be reached, The Sun-Times said.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Joffrey Ballet Dancers Agree to Tentative Deal', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Joffrey Ballet Dancers Agree to Tentative Deal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Joffrey Ballet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T21:22:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/a35659f8-6277-5c55-8b91-738398c39a15', 'word_count': 176, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a35659f8-6277-5c55-8b91-738398c39a15'}, {'abstract': "Since October 2009, no professional bull rider has been able to stay on Bushwacker for eight seconds. At a recent event in Pueblo, Colo., the riders explained why he's so tough to ride.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/sports/100000000954768/a-bull-named-bushwacker.html', 'snippet': "Since October 2009, no professional bull rider has been able to stay on Bushwacker for eight seconds. At a recent event in Pueblo, Colo., the riders explained why he's so tough to ride.", 'lead_paragraph': "Since October 2009, no professional bull rider has been able to stay on Bushwacker for eight seconds. At a recent event in Pueblo, Colo., the riders explained why he's so tough to ride.", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/19/sports/video-bushwacker/video-bushwacker-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/19/sports/video-bushwacker/video-bushwacker-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/19/sports/video-bushwacker/video-bushwacker-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/19/sports/video-bushwacker/video-bushwacker-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bushwacker Is a Tough Bull', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bull Riding', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Athletics and Sports', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T21:23:01+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'Joe Spring', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spring', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/413e63fa-1b17-5737-ba53-e1e30da241cb', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/413e63fa-1b17-5737-ba53-e1e30da241cb'}, {'abstract': 'Since October 2009, no cowboy has ridden Bushwacker, the toughest bull to ride on the Professional Bull Riders tour, for even eight seconds, the minimum needed to earn a score.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/sports/bushwacker-the-bucking-bull-confounds-the-cowboys.html', 'snippet': 'Since October 2009, no cowboy has ridden Bushwacker, the toughest bull to ride on the Professional Bull Riders tour, for even eight seconds, the minimum needed to earn a score.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dustin Elliott, a 145-pound professional cowboy, popped into the chute and felt energized by the lights above and the 1,600-pound bull beneath him. He wrapped a rope around his right hand, twisted right to left four times, then bounced up and down three times. The bull, meanwhile, looked casually to the left and waited.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/20/sports/20rodeo1/20rodeo1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/20/sports/20rodeo1/20rodeo1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/20/sports/20rodeo1/20rodeo1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/20/sports/20rodeo1/20rodeo1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/20/sports/20rodeo1/20rodeo1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jumping and Spinning, a Ballerina With Hooves', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jumping and Spinning, A Ballerina With Hooves', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rodeos', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bull Riding', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Professional Bull Riders Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T21:24:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Spring', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spring', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0855d4e7-a013-5452-87e3-59424b9c0ba9', 'word_count': 1302, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0855d4e7-a013-5452-87e3-59424b9c0ba9'}, {'abstract': 'Pakistan’s military has spent millions in a covert effort to tilt American policy against India’s control of Kashmir, including funneling campaign donations, the F.B.I. has claimed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/us/politics/20agent.html', 'snippet': 'Pakistan’s military has spent millions in a covert effort to tilt American policy against India’s control of Kashmir, including funneling campaign donations, the F.B.I. has claimed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Pakistan’s military, including its powerful spy agency, has spent $4 million over two decades in a covert attempt to tilt American policy against India’s control of much of Kashmir — including funneling campaign donations to members of Congress and presidential candidates, the F.B.I. claimed in court papers unsealed Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/20/world/AGENT-1/AGENT-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 301, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pakistan’s Military Plotted to Tilt U.S. Policy, F.B.I. Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'F.B.I. Points to Pakistan Military In a Long Plot to Tilt U.S. Policy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kashmiri American Council', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Inter-Services Intelligence', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T21:25:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage and Eric Schmitt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmitt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa632633-d30a-5466-be44-a48f5fd58757', 'word_count': 1130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa632633-d30a-5466-be44-a48f5fd58757'}, {'abstract': 'Janice Hahn took the oath of office one week after her special election victory to replace former Representative Jane Harman in California’s 36th Congressional District.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/19/hahn-sworn-in-to-house/', 'snippet': 'Janice Hahn took the oath of office one week after her special election victory to replace former Representative Jane Harman in California’s 36th Congressional District.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The House of Representatives welcomed its 433rd member on Tuesday when Janice Hahn was sworn in, one week after her special election victory to replace former Representative Jane Harman in California’s 36th Congressional District.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hahn Is Sworn In to House of Representatives', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hahn, Janice K', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T21:28:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f764c1b6-949a-5990-b4fb-505e6e211c99', 'word_count': 186, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f764c1b6-949a-5990-b4fb-505e6e211c99'}, {'abstract': 'A medical advisory panel suggested all health plans cover birth control under the new health care law.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/health/policy/20health.html', 'snippet': 'A medical advisory panel suggested all health plans cover birth control under the new health care law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — A leading medical advisory panel recommended on Tuesday that all insurers be required to cover contraceptives for women free of