sion in the British parliament was not Rupert Murdoch or his son James, but his wife, Wendi Deng Murdoch.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/world/europe/20wendi.html', 'snippet': 'The Murdoch who may have emerged best from the question-and-answer session in the British parliament was not Rupert Murdoch or his son James, but his wife, Wendi Deng Murdoch.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The Murdoch who may have emerged in the best light from the grueling question-and-answer session in the British Parliament on Tuesday was not Rupert Murdoch or his son James, but his wife, Wendi. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wendi Deng Murdoch Refuses to Pull a Punch', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Nimble Protector Strikes a Blow to Defend the Honor of an Empire', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Deng, Wendi', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News of the World', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NEWS CORP', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T22:50:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Graham Bowley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Graham', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bowley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/454327f6-1e35-53db-856f-c0e7fa0c0ce4', 'word_count': 593, 'uri': 'nyt://article/454327f6-1e35-53db-856f-c0e7fa0c0ce4'}, {'abstract': 'A documentary by Vadim Jendreyko about a translator and her eventful life.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/movies/dostoyevsky-translator-woman-with-the-5-elephants-film-review.html', 'snippet': 'A documentary by Vadim Jendreyko about a translator and her eventful life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s not apparent from the title, but Vadim Jendreyko’s elegant, slightly chilly documentary, “The Woman With the 5 Elephants,” is a profile of Svetlana Geier, a small and formidable woman who was the pre-eminent translator of Dostoyevsky’s novels into German. (The five elephants refer to her valedictory project, a 20-year effort to retranslate his five major novels, which she completed in 2007; she died, at 87, in 2010.)', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/20/arts/WOMAN/WOMAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/20/arts/WOMAN/WOMAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/20/arts/WOMAN/WOMAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 504, 'width': 831, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/20/arts/WOMAN/WOMAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/20/arts/WOMAN/WOMAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Diligently Turning Dostoyevsky German', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'The Woman With the 5 Elephants'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Diligently Turning Dostoyevsky German', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T22:52:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Hale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5be28adf-7de1-5d8c-8079-ae5be89dbee6', 'word_count': 428, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5be28adf-7de1-5d8c-8079-ae5be89dbee6'}, {'abstract': 'R. William Franklin is the third bishop, of the six in the state, to give full endorsement to same-sex marriages.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/19/episcopal-bishop-in-western-n-y-to-allow-priests-to-officiate-at-gay-marriages/', 'snippet': 'R. William Franklin is the third bishop, of the six in the state, to give full endorsement to same-sex marriages.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After much consultation, the Episcopal bishop in Western New York on Tuesday joined two of his peers in the state in allowing priests to officiate at same-sex weddings. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Episcopal Bishop in Western N.Y. to Allow Priests to Officiate at Gay Marriages', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Episcopal Church', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Franklin, R William', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T22:56:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shaila Dewan',