'abstract': 'Bluetooth speakerphones for smarphones are not usually a very noteworthy subject, but Jabra’s Freeway brings some worthwhile improvements to the category.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/19/jabras-speakerphone-is-exciting-because-its-useful/', 'snippet': 'Bluetooth speakerphones for smarphones are not usually a very noteworthy subject, but Jabra’s Freeway brings some worthwhile improvements to the category.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Getting excited about a Bluetooth car speakerphone is a tough business. First, it’s a Bluetooth device, so if you’ve seen one, you’ve seen them all. Second, it’s a device made for the car so it’s kind of useless for folks who spend time on the subway. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jabra’s Speakerphone Is Exciting Because It’s Useful', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bluetooth Wireless Technology', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speakers (Audio)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T23:17:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Biggs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Biggs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e53e7499-b92d-5932-a0d4-25185c5b0145', 'word_count': 325, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e53e7499-b92d-5932-a0d4-25185c5b0145'}, {'abstract': 'Long lines are part of the daily grind in Venezuela, but residents of the capital seem to accept them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/world/americas/20venezuela.html', 'snippet': 'Long lines are part of the daily grind in Venezuela, but residents of the capital seem to accept them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CARACAS, Venezuela —Revolutions come and go. Construction frenzies reshape this city’s skyline and then go bust, leaving white elephants as testament. Oil prices rise and fall, and rise again. But one thing, at least, endures: the lines. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/20/world/VENEZUELA-1/VENEZUELA-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/20/world/VENEZUELA-1/VENEZUELA-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/20/world/VENEZUELA-1/VENEZUELA-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 661, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/20/world/VENEZUELA-1/VENEZUELA-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/20/world/VENEZUELA-1/VENEZUELA-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'As Life Passes by, Venezuelans Are Always Standing in Line to Watch', 'kicker': 'Caracas Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Life Passes By, Venezuelans Are Always Standing in Line to Watch', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venezuela', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Supermarkets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-19T23:25:48+0000', 'document_ty