cker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T00:55:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Bornstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bornstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc2b3aad-6d81-5ce8-ab52-4b9480d1e5be', 'word_count': 1328, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc2b3aad-6d81-5ce8-ab52-4b9480d1e5be'}, {'abstract': 'Steve Garrison had just enough time to shower, pack a suitcase, grab his baseball gear and fly off to join the Yankees.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/19/the-call-comes-for-left-hander-garrison/', 'snippet': 'Steve Garrison had just enough time to shower, pack a suitcase, grab his baseball gear and fly off to join the Yankees.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ST. PETERSBURG, Fla. — When a player is promoted to the majors for the first time, the first person he tells is usually a parent. It was no different Tuesday for the left-hander Steve Garrison, who was recalled by the Yankees. Except that Garrison did not share the good news with his mother, Patty, over the phone. He just walked into the next room.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trenton Left-Hander Rushes to the Majors', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Girardi, Joe', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Robertson, Dave', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Soriano, Rafael', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T01:01:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6bcf65ff-27de-5c7d-9e0a-07a779ed55cf', 'word_count': 798, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6bcf65ff-27de-5c7d-9e0a-07a779ed55cf'}, {'abstract': 'Since last month, people have had to wait in jail for up to three days before being arraigned in Brooklyn Criminal Court and other city courts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/nyregion/new-york-budget-cuts-lead-to-longer-waits-for-arraignment.html', 'snippet': 'Since last month, people have had to wait in jail for up to three days before being arraigned in Brooklyn Criminal Court and other city courts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Brooklyn, a night in jail often lasts longer than one night. Sometimes it can drag out over two or even three nights. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/20/nyregion/arraign1/arraign1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/20/nyregion/arraign1/arraign1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/20/nyregion/arraign1/arraign1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo'