olving and see what he means.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wednesday: Limerick’s Land', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T02:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d66b52b-cba1-5e2e-83e0-68e79eb01547', 'word_count': 393, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d66b52b-cba1-5e2e-83e0-68e79eb01547'}, {'abstract': 'Under a plan called The Big Ask, officials from the city of Central Falls, which is facing the possibility of bankruptcy, asked employees to give up a portion of their pensions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/us/20centralfalls.html', 'snippet': 'Under a plan called The Big Ask, officials from the city of Central Falls, which is facing the possibility of bankruptcy, asked employees to give up a portion of their pensions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CENTRAL FALLS, R.I. — The retirees came from near and far, gathering in a muggy auditorium here to listen to an urgent pitch: give back a big chunk of your pension or risk losing it all. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/20/us/CENTRALFALLS-1/CENTRALFALLS-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/20/us/CENTRALFALLS-1/CENTRALFALLS-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype':