e and Separate People” addresses the struggle for many to accept their homosexuality while adhering to their religious beliefs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In his evocative 2009 docudrama, “The Temperamentals,” the playwright Jon Marans examined the stigma of being gay in pre-Stonewall America, when the threat of exposure could leave friendships, careers and even lives dangling by a thread. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/20/arts/SUB-strange/SUB-strange-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 985, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/20/arts/SUB-strange/SUB-strange-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/20/arts/SUB-strange/SUB-strange-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Gay Man Seeks a Place in an Orthodox World', 'kicker': "Theater Review | 'A Strange and Separate People'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Gay Man Seeks a Place In an Orthodox World', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paoluccio, Tricia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marans, Jon', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Calhoun, Jeff', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T02:01:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Rooney'