//article/889a8b3d-7c4a-5ddc-b4b4-e2b4e12e9238', 'word_count': 400, 'uri': 'nyt://article/889a8b3d-7c4a-5ddc-b4b4-e2b4e12e9238'}, {'abstract': 'Regulators are giving more scrutiny to real estate investment trusts that are not listed on exchanges but are sold by financial advisers, who get generous fees.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/realestate/commercial/nontraded-reits-face-increased-scrutiny.html', 'snippet': 'Regulators are giving more scrutiny to real estate investment trusts that are not listed on exchanges but are sold by financial advisers, who get generous fees.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last year, Cole Real Estate Investments of Phoenix, a sponsor of nontraded real estate investment trusts, refunded $3 million to the West Warwick, R.I., pension board, which had bought shares in one of its REITs despite strenuous objections from its investment adviser, who resigned in protest.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/20/business/Reits/Reits-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 705, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Closer, and Skeptical, Look at Nontraded REITs', 'kicker': 'Square Feet', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Closer, and Skeptical, Look at Nontraded REITs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate Investment Trusts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Office Buildings and Commercial Properties', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Financial Industry Regulatory Authority', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchan