un to help Syrians imagine life after the father-and-son dictatorship.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/07/20/world/middleeast/20110720hama-ss.html', 'snippet': 'In Hama, the revolt has begun to help Syrians imagine life after the father-and-son dictatorship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Hama, the revolt has begun to help Syrians imagine life after the father-and-son dictatorship.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/20/world/20110720_HAMA-slide-WMW1/20110720_HAMA-slide-WMW1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/20/world/20110720_HAMA-slide-WMW1/20110720_HAMA-slide-WMW1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/20/world/20110720_HAMA-slide-WMW1/20110720_HAMA-slide-WMW1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Is This Life After Assad?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T03:49:29+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'World', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/88ea38b6-9b8e-57aa-a8a4-41ab7bfa4553', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/88ea38b6-9b8e-57aa-a8a4-41ab7bfa4553'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on July 20, 2011.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/pageoneplus/corrections-july-20.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on July 20, 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRONT PAGE', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: July 20', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T03:52:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/671307f8-2d4e-56df-8cc7-6f1a034d4228', 'word_count': 680, 'uri': 'nyt://article/671307f8-2d4e-56df-8cc7-6f1a034d4228'}, {'abstract': 'Menstruation, with its accompanying fluctuating levels of the female sex hormone estrogen, can have a considerable effect on how a woman’s body responds to the demands of exercise and competition.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/athletic-performance-and-the-monthly-cycle/', 'snippet': 'Menstruation, with its accompanying fluctuating levels of the female sex hormone estrogen, can have a considerable effect on how a woman’s body responds to the demands of exercise and competition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What makes a female athlete different from a male athlete? Watching Abby Wambach leap above defenders in a World Cup soccer game to head the ball decisively into the net, or seeing her teammate Megan Rapinoe streak a pass down the pitch, the answer might seem to be: not much. As a group, female athletes, like their male counterparts, display coordination, strength, grace, speed, stamina and a bracing competitiveness.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Athletic Performance and the Monthly Cycle', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Estrogen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hormones', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Menstruation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T04:01:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gretchen Reynolds', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gretchen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reynolds', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd0388d9-829a-5e14-9038-6ba0f8a5ff3f', 'word_count': 801, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd0388d9-829a-5e14-9038-6ba0f8a5ff3f'}, {'abstract': 'The New York premiere of C.I.C.T./Théâtre des Bouffes du Nord’s production of Samuel Beckett’s “Fragments” is one of the highlights of the Baryshnikov Arts Center 2011 fall season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/arts/dance/baryshnikov-arts-center-announces-fall-season.html', 'snippet': 'The New York premiere of C.I.C.T./Théâtre des Bouffes du Nord’s production of Samuel Beckett’s “Fragments” is one of the highlights of the Baryshnikov Arts Center 2011 fall season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York premiere of C.I.C.T./Théâtre des Bouffes du Nord’s production of Samuel Beckett’s “Fragments” is one of the highlights of the Baryshnikov Arts Center 2011 fall season, which will run from Sept. 8 to Dec. 16. “Fragments” is the center’s second co-presentation with Theater for a New Audience. Three new dance pieces, by the choreographers Deganit Shemy and Liz Gerring and the Irish step dancer Colin Dunne, are also in the lineup. Musical offerings include a co-presentation with the Orchestra of St. Luke’s and two world premiere evening-length performances by the International Contemporary Ensemble.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Baryshnikov Arts Center  Announces Fall Season', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Baryshnikov Arts Center Announces Fall Season', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baryshnikov Arts Center', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T04:01:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bloom', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bloom', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/a28c67f3-e6b7-5ddd-b8d9-43d8a5239e79', 'word_count': 97, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a28c67f3-e6b7-5ddd-b8d9-43d8a5239e79'}, {'abstract': 'Analysts estimate that thousands of jobs will be eliminated with the federal government’s plan to shut 40 percent of its computer centers over the next four years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/technology/us-to-close-800-computer-data-centers.html', 'snippet': 'Analysts estimate that thousands of jobs will be eliminated with the federal government’s plan to shut 40 percent of its computer centers over the next four years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The federal government plans to shut 40 percent of its computer centers over the next four years to reduce its hefty technology budget and modernize the way it uses computers to manage data and provide services to citizens.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/20/business/Data/Data-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. to Close 800 Computer Data Centers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. to Close 800 Computer Data Centers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cloud Computing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Data Centers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Procurement', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kundra, Vivek', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T04:01:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Lohr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lohr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/931e59f7-202d-5918-b2dc-202e1f0cd3bb', 'word_count': 888, 'uri': 'nyt://article/931e59f7-202d-5918-b2dc-202e1f0cd3bb'}, {'abstract': 'Israeli naval forces boarded a French yacht off the Gaza coast on Tuesday, as the yacht tried to breach the Israeli maritime blockade of the Palestinian enclave.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/world/middleeast/20briefs-Israelbrf.html', 'snippet': 'Israeli naval forces boarded a French yacht off the Gaza coast on Tuesday, as the yacht tried to breach the Israeli maritime blockade of the Palestinian enclave.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Israeli naval forces boarded a French yacht off the Gaza coast on Tuesday, as the yacht tried to breach the Israeli maritime blockade of the Palestinian enclave. The forces met no resistance, Israeli military officials said, and steered the yacht toward the Israeli port of Ashdod. The yacht is a remnant of an international flotilla that had planned to challenge the blockade last month but was mostly thwarted. The military said that when the yacht reached Ashdod, the passengers would be questioned by the Israeli police and then turned over to immigration authorities. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Israelis Board Yacht Off Gaza', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Israelis Board Yacht Off Gaza', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gaza Strip', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T04:05:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Kershner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/17dda88e-3d1f-5382-bc8c-aef4a2ef4ef8', 'word_count': 93, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17dda88e-3d1f-5382-bc8c-aef4a2ef4ef8'}, {'abstract': 'President Nicolas Sarkozy presided over a ceremony in remembrance of the seven service members killed in Afghanistan last week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/world/europe/20briefs-francebrf.html', 'snippet': 'President Nicolas Sarkozy presided over a ceremony in remembrance of the seven service members killed in Afghanistan last week.', 'lead_paragraph': ' French President Nicolas Sarkozy on Tuesday presided over a national ceremony in remembrance of the seven service members who were killed in Afghanistan last week, the deadliest week for French troops there since 2008. “The entire country bows before your coffins,” Mr. Sarkozy said in a speech at the Hôtel des Invalides, where Napoleon is buried. Five of the troops died in a suicide attack in eastern Afghanistan, while a French Navy commando was killed by insurgents and a 22-year-old soldier was shot by friendly fire. The toll amplified the calls to speed up the withdrawal of French troops from the country. In a surprise visit to Afghanistan last week, Mr. Sarkozy said that France would withdraw 1,000 of its approximately 4,000 troops from Afghanistan by the end of 2012. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France: War Dead Are Honored', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France: War Dead Are Honored', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sarkozy, Nicolas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T04:07:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'Maïa de la Baume', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maïa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'de la Baume', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3147a0d-afc6-54ba-9d85-ddfb6b637c85', 'word_count': 130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3147a0d-afc6-54ba-9d85-ddfb6b637c85'}, {'abstract': 'This word has appeared in four New York Times articles in the past year.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/word-of-the-day-carouse/', 'snippet': 'This word has appeared in four New York Times articles in the past year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'carouse •\\kə-ˈrauz\\• verb/noun', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Word of the Day | carouse', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T04:07:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a05ca67d-340c-5305-80e6-7eb53f2dd911', 'word_count': 188, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a05ca67d-340c-5305-80e6-7eb53f2dd911'}, {'abstract': 'Secretary of State Hillary Rodham Clinton pressed India to open its markets further and to make it possible for American companies to bid for lucrative nuclear contracts there.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/world/asia/20briefs-Indiabrf.html', 'snippet': 'Secretary of State Hillary Rodham Clinton pressed India to open its markets further and to make it possible for American companies to bid for lucrative nuclear contracts there.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Secretary of State Hillary Rodham Clinton pressed India on Tuesday to open its markets further and to amend a crucial regulation that would make it possible for American companies to bid for lucrative nuclear contracts there. Mrs. Clinton, stopping in India for three days on a 12-country tour, also pledged the United States’ support in fighting terrorism. Her visit, her second as secretary of state, came a week after three bombs ripped through heavily populated areas of Mumbai, killing 19 people. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'India: Clinton Urges Open Markets', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'India: Clinton Urges Open Markets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Energy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T04:09:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lydia Polgreen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lydia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Polgreen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/6552cfcb-0568-59ce-8f33-d56583213c1f', 'word_count': 83, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6552cfcb-0568-59ce-8f33-d56583213c1f'}, {'abstract': 'One of China’s leading investigative reporting teams has been disbanded because it focused too much on social ills, reporters in the team say.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/world/asia/20briefs-Chinabrf.html', 'snippet': 'One of China’s leading investigative reporting teams has been disbanded because it focused too much on social ills, reporters in the team say.', 'lead_paragraph': ' One of China’s leading investigative reporting teams has been disbanded because it focused too much on social ills, reporters in the team say. The China Economic Times five-person team was a rarity in China. It had tackled a variety of social problems, most recently for exposing how officials had covered up the distribution of fake vaccinations that had led to children’s deaths. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China: Reporting Team Disbanded', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: Reporting Team Disbanded', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T04:16:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f3a2adc-cb67-5497-96b8-6d18243749f4', 'word_count': 63, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f3a2adc-cb67-5497-96b8-6d18243749f4'}, {'abstract': 'NYT: Front Page for 07/20/2011', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2011/07/20/multimedia/20frontpage.html', 'snippet': 'NYT: Front Page for 07/20/2011', 'lead_paragraph': 'NYT: Front Page for 07/20/2011', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'NYT: Front Page for 07/20/2011', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T04:45:08+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/f1bbf4a1-5220-5a9f-b058-ab3a64209984', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/f1bbf4a1-5220-5a9f-b058-ab3a64209984'}, {'abstract': 'There’s a lot of interest, but it probably won’t work, according to several tax and benefit lawyers.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/is-dividing-a-company-the-way-to-beat-the-affordable-care-act/', 'snippet': 'There’s a lot of interest, but it probably won’t work, according to several tax and benefit lawyers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'That’s one notion that seems to be circulating among small-business owners and their advisers lately. Consultants at McKinsey & Company floated the suggestion as part of their controversial report on employer views of health insurance. And in The Times’s coverage of that report, Milt Freudenheim interviewed a small-business owner who said he was hoping to “game the system.” The owner, Gerry Harkins, who is also chairman of the National Federation of Independent Business’s Georgia State Leadership Council, said he might split his Atlanta-based construction company into two smaller companies to evade the overhaul’s employer mandate, specifically the penalties on companies that fail to offer affordable health insurance to employees.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is Dividing a Company the Way to Beat the Affordable Care Act?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Federation of Independent Business', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T05:00:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robb Mandelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mandelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce5ba5f4-7b3a-5403-b589-0edc99184b8b', 'word_count': 981, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce5ba5f4-7b3a-5403-b589-0edc99184b8b'}, {'abstract': 'Taliban spokesmen denied reports sent through e-mail and text messages early Wednesday that their leader was dead, saying that their Web sites and telephones had been hacked.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/world/asia/20briefs-talibanbf.html', 'snippet': 'Taliban spokesmen denied reports sent through e-mail and text messages early Wednesday that their leader was dead, saying that their Web sites and telephones had been hacked.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Taliban spokesmen denied reports sent through their e-mail and in text messages early Wednesday that their movement’s leader, Mullah Muhammad Omar, was dead, saying that their Web sites and telephones had been hacked. Zabiullah Mujahid, one of the spokesmen, reached by telephone, said: “The enemy hijacked our telephone numbers and e-mails. They have sent out false texts and statements about death of Mullah Omar. In reality he is alive and in good condition.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Afghanistan: Taliban Deny Reports of Leader’s Death, Citing Hacking', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Afghanistan: Taliban Deny Reports Of Leader’s Death, Citing Hacking', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Omar, Muhammad (Taliban Leader)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T05:06:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alissa J. Rubin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alissa', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastn