esday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cnooc to Pay $2.1 Billion for Canadian Oil Sands Firm', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil Sands', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'China National Offshore Oil', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'OPTI Canada Incorporated', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALBERTA (CANADA)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T11:57:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris V. Nicholson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': 'V.', 'lastname': 'Nicholson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b8d0c06-f2e2-55e4-9812-9548f993cc9c', 'word_count': 493, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b8d0c06-f2e2-55e4-9812-9548f993cc9c'}, {'abstract': 'In Berlin, a palate-cleansing art installation for those suffering from aesthetic indigestion.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/now-showing-paul-thek-in-theory-and-practice/', 'snippet': 'In Berlin, a palate-cleansing art installation for those suffering from aesthetic indigestion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you’ve had your fill of glossy Pop Art and are suffering from aesthetic indigestion, “Prelude: Paul Thek in Process,” set to open this week in Berlin, is a wonderful palate cleanser — not to mention a poignant reminder that, when it comes to art, the means can be as, well, meaningful, as the ends. The curator Susanne Neubauer has focused on the ephemeral nature of a visionary artist’s practice, assembling rare slides, photographs, taped interviews, letters and other documents. The installation echoes Thek’s work, which, like his process, often reflected a sense of transience. A cascade of newspapers from walls to floor and pools of chicken wire are meant to evoke the spirit of his 1969 piece “Chicken Coop.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Now Showing | Paul Thek in Theory and Practice', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T12:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sameer Reddy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sameer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reddy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/159c8840-93e7-5426-a53c-5ce37c5e7c5c', 'word_count': 252, 'uri': 'nyt://article/159c8840-93e7-5426-a53c-5ce37c5e7c5c'}, {'abstract': 'If Ali Abdullah Saleh and his generals believe they can defeat protesters, they are taking an enormous risk.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/24/magazine/yemen-on-the-brink-of-hell.html', 'snippet': 'If Ali Abdullah Saleh and his generals believe they can defeat protesters, they are taking an enormous risk.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On May 29, a young woman named Bushra al- Maqtari joined a group of several thousand protesters marching down a trash-strewn boulevard in the Yemeni city of Taiz. The Arab world’s democratic uprising was five months old, and patience among the protesters in Taiz — Yemen’s second largest city — was wearing thin. Maqtari had been one of the first and most fearless leaders of the movement. She is a remarkable figure: a 31-year-old university administrator and fiction writer, she is also a childless divorcee who refused, until recently, to wear the abaya, the all-covering gown that is practically mandatory for women in Yemen. Tiny and frail, she has a round, lovely face, with level brows and tranquil brown eyes.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/magazine/24yemen3/24yemen3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/magazine/24yemen3/24yemen3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/24/magazine/24yemen3/24yemen3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Yemen on the Brink of Hell', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On the ground in Yemen.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'North Atlantic Treaty Organization', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Middle East', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T12:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert F. Worth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Worth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a7d2042-6700-5780-b79f-f791c5c9e39a', 'word_count': 8112, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a7d2042-6700-5780-b79f-f791c5c9e39a'}, {'abstract': 'As they traveled long distances to reach sea ice, 5 of 11 female bears swimming with their cubs lost the cubs along the way, and one bear swam 427 miles to reach the ice.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/the-perils-of-polar-bears-longer-swims/', 'snippet': 'As they traveled long distances to reach sea ice, 5 of 11 female bears swimming with their cubs lost the cubs along the way, and one bear swam 427 miles to reach the ice.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In arguments over the impact of climate change, some of the images commonly associated with those clashes have attracted skeptical critiques, perhaps none more so than those of polar bears forced to swim longer distances because their sea ice habitat is melting. Some skeptics point out that polar bears are born swimmers and that the worries of environmentalists are therefore overdone.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Perils of Polar Bears’ Longer Swims', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polar Bears', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Swimming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fish and Wildlife Service', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Geological Survey', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Wildlife Fund', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T12:05:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicity Barringer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicity', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barringer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5bd5a0cc-8e0b-5dbf-a74a-a5fe67ac3770', 'word_count': 373, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5bd5a0cc-8e0b-5dbf-a74a-a5fe67ac3770'}, {'abstract': 'Medical panel advises free contraceptive coverage, Nissan to raise the price of its electric car, nagging leads to better health for married men and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/wednesday-reading-medical-panel-recommends-free-contraceptive-coverage/', 'snippet': 'Medical panel advises free contraceptive coverage, Nissan to raise the price of its electric car, nagging leads to better health for married men and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and online in our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wednesday Reading: Medical Panel Recommends Free Contraceptive Coverage', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T12:30:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/64e8a622-5f10-5a83-aab2-96e998d2e967', 'word_count': 145, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64e8a622-5f10-5a83-aab2-96e998d2e967'}, {'abstract': 'The order from Boeing and Airbus, which hasn’t sold new planes to American for years, is worth over $38 billion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/business/global/american-places-record-order-with-2-jet-makers.html', 'snippet': 'The order from Boeing and Airbus, which hasn’t sold new planes to American for years, is worth over $38 billion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — American Airlines announced on Wednesday a record order for 460 single-aisle planes from Airbus and Boeing in a deal worth more than $38 billion. The order breaks the longstanding monopoly that Boeing has had with the airline and forced a significant shift in the company’s strategy.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/business/Air/Air-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/21/business/Air/Air-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 345}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/business/Air/Air-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 847, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jet Order by American Is a Coup for Boeing’s Rival', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'American Orders 460 Single-Aisle Jets From Boeing and Airbus', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Airlines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN AIRLINES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Continental Airlines', 'rank': 4,