 Services Group posted a second-quarter profit of $912 million, up 12 percent from the period a year earlier, benefiting from strong gains in retail banking and asset management as well as improving credit conditions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The PNC Financial Services Group on Wednesday reported a second-quarter profit of $912 million, up 12 percent from the period a year earlier, benefiting from strong gains in retail banking and asset management as well as improving credit conditions. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'PNC Profit Exceeds Expectations, Again', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'PNC Financial Services Group Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal Bank of Canada', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pittsburgh (Pa)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T12:51:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Owles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Owles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/519257a4-4338-5a3e-b8b8-de1ca859b18f', 'word_count': 223, 'uri': 'nyt://article/519257a4-4338-5a3e-b8b8-de1ca859b18f'}, {'abstract': 'Rihanna, who performed at Nassau Coliseum on Tuesday night, sings R&B songs with none of the DNA of rhythm or blues but plenty of carefully orchestrated pop.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/arts/music/rihanna-at-nassau-coliseum-music-review.html', 'snippet': 'Rihanna, who performed at Nassau Coliseum on Tuesday night, sings R&B songs with none of the DNA of rhythm or blues but plenty of carefully orchestrated pop.', 'lead_paragraph': 'UNIONDALE N.Y. — Rihanna isn’t cool because of her multitude of sexy, clever outfits; or her red hair, which sits flawless and immobile atop her head; or the ease with which she delivers a song, barely breaking a sweat, even on the most involved numbers.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/arts/Rihanna/Rihanna-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 827, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/arts/Rihanna/Rihanna-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/21/arts/Rihanna/Rihanna-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Star Who Clads Herself in Cool', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Star Who Clads Herself in Cool', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rihanna', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nassau Veterans Memorial Coliseum', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'West, Kanye', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Chris', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T12:54:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/3cf49d3c-e159-5172-aded-cb0a2ba87fd8', 'word_count': 762, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3cf49d3c-e159-5172-aded-cb0a2ba87fd8'}, {'abstract': 'The Day: Service has been reduced and fares have risen, but subway service is far better now than it was 30 or 40 years ago. Also, what City Room is reading in other papers and blogs.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/then-and-now-worrisome-times-in-the-subways/', 'snippet': 'The Day: Service has been reduced and fares have risen, but subway service is far better now than it was 30 or 40 years ago. Also, what City Room is reading in other papers and blogs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My candidate for the best New York film ever was shown on a cable channel the other day. This was the classic “Taking of Pelham One Two Three,” released in 1974. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Then and Now, Worrisome Times in the Subways', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subways', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transit Systems', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T12:56:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clyde Haberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clyde', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e8b4dde-1a6c-53ce-96ab-12fc2a8bb514', 'word_count': 929, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e8b4dde-1a6c-53ce-96ab-12fc2a8bb514'}, {'abstract': "The nation's battle with the mafia is seen as a test of whether E.U. membership can bring with it Western standards of justice.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/world/europe/20bulgaria.html', 'snippet': "The nation's battle with the mafia is seen as a test of whether E.U. membership can bring with it Western standards of justice.", 'lead_paragraph': 'SOFIA, Bulgaria — Arms pinned behind his back, Alexei “The Tractor” Petrov lay with his face pushed to the floor after heavily armed masked police commandos raided his home early last year. The police then hauled him off in one of Bulgaria’s most pronounced efforts to take on the godfathers of racketeering, kidnapping and prostitution who have eroded trust in the country’s institutions and day-to-day life.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/world/21bulgariaspan/21bulgaria-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/21/world/21bulgariaspan/21bulgaria-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/world/21bulgariaspan/21bulgaria-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/world/21bulgariaspan/21bulgaria-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/21/world/21bulgariaspan/21bulgaria-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Law and Order, Bulgarian Style', 'kicker': 'Sofia Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Batman’ Sets His Sights On Bulgaria’s Godfathers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bulgaria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Crime', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sofia (Bulgaria)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T13:05:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Castle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c5ec3874-2a0f-587b-9c7f-5cf3d1ba885a', 'word_count': 1232, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c5ec3874-2a0f-587b-9c7f-5cf3d1ba885a'}, {'abstract': 'In a letter to E*Trade, Citadel said the board had “squandered” a “phenomenal franchise” and it pressed the online brokerage company to put itself up for sale.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/citadel-slams-etrade-calling-for-a-sale/', 'snippet': 'In a letter to E*Trade, Citadel said the board had “squandered” a “phenomenal franchise” and it pressed the online brokerage company to put itself up for sale.', 'lead_paragraph': '8:05 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Citadel Assails E*Trade and Calls for Sale', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hedge Funds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citadel Investment Group', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'E TRADE Financial Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T13:14:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7075341-4d2b-5dea-8d42-00b984b59f5d', 'word_count': 342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7075341-4d2b-5dea-8d42-00b984b59f5d'}, {'abstract': 'The activist investor raised his bid for Clorox on Wednesday to $10.7 billion, two days after the detergents company spurned his takeover offer as “neither credible nor adequate.”', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/icahn-boosts-clorox-bid-to-10-7-billion/', 'snippet': 'The activist investor raised his bid for Clorox on Wednesday to $10.7 billion, two days after the detergents company spurned his takeover offer as “neither credible nor adequate.”', 'lead_paragraph': '8:27 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Icahn Raises Bid for Clorox and Scolds Managers', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Icahn, Carl C', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Clorox Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T13:22:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cfee3e50-9c0a-585a-9f49-6e91319d786f', 'word_count': 419, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cfee3e50-9c0a-585a-9f49-6e91319d786f'}, {'abstract': 'Less-is-more clutches modeled after the most ubiquitous strapless carrier of all: the lunch bag', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/takeout-totes/', 'snippet': 'Less-is-more clutches modeled after the most ubiquitous strapless carrier of all: the lunch bag', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is the season of the less-is-more clutch, with handfuls (pun intended) of designers offering palm-friendly options for girls on the go. Add to the list Beth Goodman, who in 2009 launched Marie Turnor Accessories, a collection of bags modeled after the most ubiquitous strapless carrier of all — the lunch bag. The idea came to her in Paris when she spotted a woman holding a perfect red paper bag. “I saw it as being a clutch,” Goodman explained. “It just looked to me like it should be,\xa0 it was such a chic and simple shape. I knew I had to create one in leather.” Her signature style, appropriately named the Picnic, is made of buttery-soft leather and comes in red, black, tan and white. For summer, Goodman is including a range of limited-edition colors — pale pink, purple, gold, bright turquoise and a sparkling aqua. Versatile, featherweight and with minimal hardware, they’re a welcome relief for our wardrobes and shoulders both.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Takeout Totes', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T13:30:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lily Miesmer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Miesmer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9dd136a9-4cc7-5e4e-acc4-9fb976f4ae3e', 'word_count': 162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9dd136a9-4cc7-5e4e-acc4-9fb976f4ae3e'}, {'abstract': 'A parliamentary panel investigating Britain’s hacking scandal accused the Murdoch empire on Wednesday of “deliberate attempts” to thwart its investigations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/world/europe/21yard.html', 'snippet': 'A parliamentary panel investigating Britain’s hacking scandal accused the Murdoch empire on Wednesday of “deliberate attempts” to thwart its investigations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — A parliamentary panel investigating Britain’s spreading phone hacking scandal accused the Murdoch empire on Wednesday of “deliberate attempts” to thwart various investigations into what had happened.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'British Panel Accuses Murdoch Company of Impeding Inquiries', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'British Panel Accuses Murdoch Company of Impeding Inquiries', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NEWS CORP', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Scotland Yard (Metropolitan Police Service)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wiretapping and Other Eavesdropping Devices and Methods', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News of the World', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T13:36:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Cowell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd2619fc-3569-53bb-ad25-0e1434560882', 'word_count': 855, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd2619fc-3569-53bb-ad25-0e1434560882'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Cooper, a star of the “Hangover” comedies, will play Lucifer in an adaptation of Milton’s epic of man’s first disobedience, to be filmed in Australia.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/bradley-cooper-going-down-under-way-down-under-for-paradise-lost-film/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Cooper, a star of the “Hangover” comedies, will play Lucifer in an adaptation of Milton’s epic of man’s first disobedience, to be filmed in Australia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Having returned from a humid if lucrative trip to Bangkok (to shoot the smash summer comedy “The Hangover Part II”) with all of his digits intact, Bradley Cooper is headed to another sweltering location for his next movie – and we don’t mean Australia.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bradley Cooper Going Down Under – Way Down Under – for ‘Paradise Lost’ Film', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cooper, Bradley', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Proyas, Alex', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Australia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bangkok (Thailand)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T13:37:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3715e9d-e739-54ac-8fd3-25a164747daf', 'word_count': 231, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3715e9d-e739-54ac-8fd3-25a164747daf'}, {'abstract': 'My husband and I are interested in taking our rudimentary textbook Spanish to another level by living and volunteering (or working) in a Spanish-speaking country for a year. Can you suggest a safe, beautiful area that allows Americans to live for up to a year where we would have access to language classes, meaningful activities (I am a psychologist; he is a lawyer) and interesting people? (Mountainous hiking opportunities would be a plus.)Dr. Valerie Salwen, Scarsdale, N.Y.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/qa-learn-spanish-and-do-some-good/', 'snippet': 'My husband and I are interested in taking our rudimentary textbook Spanish to another level by living and volunteering (or working) in a Spanish-speaking country for a year. Can you suggest a safe, beautiful area that allows Americans to live for ...', 'lead_paragraph': ' My husband and I are interested in taking our rudimentary textbook Spanish to another level by living and volunteering (or working) in a Spanish-speaking country for a year. Can you suggest a safe, beautiful area that allows Americans to live for up to a year where we would have access to language classes, meaningful activities (I am a psychologist; he is a lawyer) and interesting people? (Mountainous hiking opportunities would be a plus.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q&A: Learn Spanish and Do Some Good', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T13:39:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Lee Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': 'Lee', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/23dc633e-4ac8-5829-88e8-9627dfea78c0', 'word_count': 493, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23dc633e-4ac8-5829-88e8-9627dfea78c0'}, {'abstract': 'Representative Michele Bachmann continues to press her opposition to an increase in the debt ceiling as she runs another presidential campaign ad in Iowa this week.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/bachmann-reasserts-opposition-to-debt-limit-increase/', 'snippet': 'Representative Michele Bachmann continues to press her opposition to an increase in the debt ceiling as she runs another presidential campaign ad in Iowa this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Representative Michele Bachmann continues to press her opposition to an increase in the debt ceiling as she runs another presidential campaign ad in Iowa this week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bachmann Reasserts Opposition to Debt Limit Increase', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bachmann, Michele M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T13:57:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/22c77772-3742-51cb-9498-ca7128aae8be', 'word_count': 196, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22c77772-3742-51cb-9498-ca7128aae8be'}, {'abstract': 'Sluts, nuts and the clumsiness of reappropriation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/24/magazine/clumsy-young-feminists.html', 'snippet': 'Sluts, nuts and the clumsiness of reappropriation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I wanted to love SlutWalks, the viral protest movement that began this spring after a Toronto police officer told a group of college women that if they hoped to escape sexual assault, they should avoid dressing like “sluts.” In angry response, young women (and men) have marched in more than 70 cities around the world, often dressed in bras, halter tops and garter belts. ', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/magazine/24lede_span/mag-24lede-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/24/magazine/24lede_span/mag-24lede-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/magazine/24lede_span/mag-24lede-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/magazine/24lede_span/mag-24lede-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/24/magazine/24lede_span/mag-24lede-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ladies, We Have a Problem', 'kicker': 'First', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ladies, We Have a Problem', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sexual Harassment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Feminist Movement', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T14:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rebecca Traister', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rebecca', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Traister', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/01d6de01-c502-56