ender of unfettered scientific inquiry has been silent of late.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/calling-george-will-science-defender/', 'snippet': 'A conservative who claimed to be a defender of unfettered scientific inquiry has been silent of late.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I kind of figured that George Will’s January column urging Republican lawmakers to “rev the scientific engine” of America was a one-off.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Calling George Will, Science Defender', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservatism (US Politics)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Science Foundation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T14:21:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/87e3dd57-69cc-591b-9206-a52df4a1a934', 'word_count': 318, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87e3dd57-69cc-591b-9206-a52df4a1a934'}, {'abstract': 'The News Corporation said on Wednesday that it would no longer pay legal fees for Glenn Mulcaire, the private investigator who has been implicated in the phone hacking scandal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/world/europe/21mulcaire.html', 'snippet': 'The News Corporation said on Wednesday that it would no longer pay legal fees for Glenn Mulcaire, the private investigator who has been implicated in the phone hacking scandal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Under pressure in the widening phone hacking scandal, the News Corporation on Wednesday said that it would no longer pay the legal fees for the private investigator at the center of the hacking and partly lifted a confidentiality agreement on one of its law firms to allow the firm to give evidence to Parliament and to the police.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/world/21mulcaire/21mulcaire-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 678, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/world/21mulcaire/21mulcaire-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/21/world/21mulcaire/21mulcaire-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'News Corp. to Stop Paying Legal Fees of Key Figure in Hacking Case', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'News Corp. to Stop Paying Legal Fees of Key Figure in Hacking Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mulcaire, Glenn', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NEWS CORP', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wiretapping and Other Eavesdropping Devices and Methods', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News of the World', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T14:34:08+000