n Gray Blocked Protester First', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Unsung Woman in Gray Blocked Protester First', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News of the World', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'May-Bowles, Jonathan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NEWS CORP', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Deng, Wendi', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wiretapping and Other Eavesdropping Devices and Methods', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T16:57:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Graham Bowley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Graham', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bowley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/60049a0e-258d-554e-a708-68a6caedaae5', 'word_count': 414, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60049a0e-258d-554e-a708-68a6caedaae5'}, {'abstract': 'A sweaty summertime music festival that trades cheap beer and muddy tents for steak, spa treatments and luxe teepees.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/a-music-fest-for-grown-up-foodies/', 'snippet': 'A sweaty summertime music festival that trades cheap beer and muddy tents for steak, spa treatments and luxe teepees.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In early August, Patti Smith and Edward Sharpe, along with bands like Chairlift, Au Revoir Simone, Lissy Trulie and the Postelles, will play a new three-day rock festival called Escape to New York on the grounds of the Shinnecock Indian reservation in Southampton, N.Y. Though loud guitar, drinking and sunshine will be in plentiful supply, cheap beer, corndogs and funnel cake will not.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Music Festival for Grown-Up Foodies', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T17:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jacob Brown', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jacob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brown', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f16875ca-3d21-5935-a209-028a86b95d4a', 'word_count': 290, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f16875ca-3d21-5935-a209-028a86b95d4a'}, {'abstract': 'A credit union deposits money via online access before it has received customers’ checks.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/making-online-deposits-on-an-honor-system/', 'snippet': 'A credit union deposits money via online access before it has received customers’ checks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Go figure — it turns out that most people can be trusted not to lie about the amount of money they deposit in their bank account.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Making Online Deposits on an Honor System', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Honor System', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_da