erial': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d23729e-cc92-549d-97be-972cd9ee20e4', 'word_count': 1026, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d23729e-cc92-549d-97be-972cd9ee20e4'}, {'abstract': '“The Day Before You Came,” a compact show of modest prints in a project room of Andrea Rosen Gallery, is mostly about being a guy with a heat-seeking camera.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/artifacts-wolfgang-tillmans-male-genus/', 'snippet': '“The Day Before You Came,” a compact show of modest prints in a project room of Andrea Rosen Gallery, is mostly about being a guy with a heat-seeking camera.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s no secret that Wolfgang Tillmans has a special feeling for the men around him. In his portrait photographs, he examines them from every angle, indoors and out, in groups and alone, clothed and not. Sometimes he treats them as objects of desire and other times as simply as objects of curiosity. What’s strange is that, despite his camera’s studied distance from its subjects — friends in Tillman’s circle of acquaintance or landscapes, or rumpled clothing — his pictures read as very personal statements: Here are the people and the things I like and this is the way I like to see them. Which is part of their seduction.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Artifacts | Wolfgang Tillmans, Male Genus', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T18:46:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Linda Yablonsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Linda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yablonsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8a2727d-ffc2-5283-aa43-967df200682d', 'word_count': 569, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8a2727d-ffc2-5283-aa43-967df200682d'}, {'abstract': 'When the online real estate company Zillow went public, it joined a rarified group: corporations with single-letter ticker symbols. Zillow’s symbol is Z.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/for-zillow-a-single-letter-score/', 'snippet': 'When the online real estate company Zillow went public, it joined a rarified group: corporations with single-letter ticker symbols. Zillow’s symbol is Z.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David Paul Morris/Bloomberg NewsSpencer Rascoff, chief executive of Zillow.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Zillow, a Single-Letter Score', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Signs and Symbols', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nasdaq Stock Market', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Stock Exchange', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Zillow.com', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T18:47:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin Roose', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roose', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/66da4267-d292-584a-ba08-8b4968a2e298', 'word_count': 494, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66da4267-d292-584a-ba08-8b4968a2e298'}, {'abstract': 'Fugazi and Wu-Tang Clan together.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/the-latest-greatest-mash-up/', 'snippet': 'Fugazi and Wu-Tang Clan together.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Other than approving of its clever name — Wugazi is a much better choice than presumed runner-up, Fu-Tang — I didn’t react favorably to the news that someone mashed-up two of my favorite music entities, uncompromising D.C. post-punks Fugazi with lyrical superfriends and apparel licensors, the Wu-Tang Clan. Sure, the Dangermouse-Beatles mashup, “The Grey Album,” was an instant classic in 2004, but beyond that and a rare few others, the thought of a third-party recklessly commingling two bands’ copyrighted music has always made me queasy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Latest, Greatest Mash-Up', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T18:52:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tony Gervino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gervino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e0f0471-9f0e-553c-bab2-8792c91f5bf8', 'word_count': 201, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e0f0471-9f0e-553c-bab2-8792c91f5bf8'}, {'abstract': 'The new Ion Torrent machine costs $49,000 and takes just two hours to sequence DNA, but its inventor says it will take years to make sense of much of the data it reveals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/science/21genome.html', 'snippet': 'The new Ion Torrent machine costs $49,000 and takes just two hours to sequence DNA, but its inventor says it will take years to make sense of much of the data it reveals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The inventor of a new machine that decodes DNA with semiconductors has used it to sequence the genome of Gordon Moore, co-founder of Intel, a leading chip maker.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/us/GENOME/GENOME-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 354, 'width': 600, 'subType': 