', 'value': 'ADMISSIONS STANDARDS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T19:05:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'EdLife', 'section_name': 'Education', 'subsection_name': 'Education Life', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jacques Steinberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jacques', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/913ffb63-a477-56f6-a384-483d3085ddcf', 'word_count': 1008, 'uri': 'nyt://article/913ffb63-a477-56f6-a384-483d3085ddcf'}, {'abstract': 'History’s crossover event of “American Pickers,” “American Restoration” and “Pawn Stars” landed the network three shows in the Top 10 cable ratings last week.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/history-channel-turns-trash-into-ratings-gold/', 'snippet': 'History’s crossover event of “American Pickers,” “American Restoration” and “Pawn Stars” landed the network three shows in the Top 10 cable ratings last week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Trash really can be treasure, or least ratings gold, as History proved with its much-publicized cross-over event of three of its most popular shows last week. The gimmick, in which the stars of “American Pickers,” “American Restoration” and “Pawn Stars” joined forces to find, purchase and restore a 1957 Chevy 150 to pristine condition, worked, as the average 6.7 million total viewers tuning in made clear. But just how well became clearer with a look at the Top 10 list among basic cable shows for the week ending Sunday, according to Nielsen: the three shows all finished in the Top 10, with “Pawn Stars” second only to the Japan/U.S.A. final in the Women’s World Cup. “Pawn Stars,” in which viewers are privy to the haggling prowess of a family of pawnshop owners, has proved to be a major hit for History, as its ratings keep growing; the most recent episode, on Monday night, garnered 6.67 