del, became known for her brightly colored hair, which ranges from pale to neon pink, women in New York City were dousing their manes in Crayola hues. The coloring process has not changed much since the days of ’80s punk rockers and ’90s grunge enthusiasts (jars of Manic Panic dye are still a popular way to get the look), but the patterns, placement and mood of these “shock locks” have evolved.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/fashion/21SKIN-span/21zSKIN1A-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 192, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/21/fashion/21SKIN-span/21zSKIN1A-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 192}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/fashion/21SKIN-span/21zSKIN1A-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 328, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/fashion/21SKIN-span/21SKIN-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/21/fashion/21SKIN-span/21SKIN-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Shock Locks’ Leave Punk Behind', 'kicker': 'Skin Deep', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Shock Locks’ Leave Punk Behind', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hair', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Color', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dyes and Dyestuffs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T19:20:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_nam