at beer, which is growing in popularity in Russia, can be sold.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — The slow but steady gain of beer over vodka as the drink of choice among Russians suffered a setback on Wednesday when President Dmitri A. Medvedev signed a law restricting beer sales outdoors and late at night.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russian Law to Restrict Beer Sales', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russian Law to Restrict Beer Sales', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T20:55:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew E. Kramer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Kramer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe1192ea-6d3d-5cd0-8c9c-456cf39d0520', 'word_count': 311, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe1192ea-6d3d-5cd0-8c9c-456cf39d0520'}, {'abstract': 'France’s foreign minister said Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi would have to relinquish power as part of a larger deal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/world/europe/21france.html', 'snippet': 'France’s foreign minister said Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi would have to relinquish power as part of a larger deal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Foreign Minister Alain Juppé of France said Wednesday that the Libyan leader Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi could remain in Libya so long as he completely gave up power, as part of a larger political deal, including a cease-fire, on the future of the country.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France Says Qaddafi Can Stay in Libya if He Relinquishes Power', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France Says Qaddafi Can Stay in Libya if He Agrees to Give Up His Power', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qaddafi, Muammar el-', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T20:58:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Erlanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erlanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f0db331-fb1a-5bca-9ffa-dd461a8f2be8', 'word_count': 527, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f0db331-fb1a-5bca-9ffa-dd461a8f2be8'}, {'abstract': 'The company’s chief, Paul S. Otellini, attributed the results to strong corporate demand for Intel’s most advanced technology and the surge of mobile devices.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/technology/intel-posts-profit-that-beats-forecasts.html', 'snippet': 'The company’s chief, Paul S. Otellini, attributed the results to strong corporate demand for Intel’s most advanced technology and the surge of mobile devices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — Intel said that the modernization of data centers — the engines behind cloud computing — were responsible for the strong worldwide sales the chip maker reported Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Ti