rl': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/us/21hood.html', 'snippet': 'Maj. Nidal Malik Hasan, accused of 13 counts of premeditated murder, informed a judge before the proceeding in Texas that he had changed lawyers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FORT HOOD, Tex. — Wearing a camouflage Army uniform and sitting upright in a wheelchair, the military psychiatrist accused of killing 13 people in a shooting rampage here appeared in court on Wednesday at his arraignment, without the civilian lawyer who had been his lead defense attorney.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/us/HOOD/HOOD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 837, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/us/HOOD/HOOD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/21/us/HOOD/HOOD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Major Is Arraigned in Fort Hood Killings', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Major Is Arraigned In Fort Hood Killings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hasan, Nidal Malik', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fort Hood (Tex)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T21:13:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manny Fernandez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fernandez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ac8f9af-14cc-542f-b086-b30e624e866d', 'word_count': 829, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ac8f9af-14cc-542f-b086-b30e624e866d'}, {'abstract': '“Old Mel hired one of Da’s nephews — the slow-witted one with the dent in his forehead — to sink a well in his back acre.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/books/excerpt-killed-at-the-whim-of-a-hat-by-colin-cotterill.html', 'snippet': '“Old Mel hired one of Da’s nephews — the slow-witted one with the dent in his forehead — to sink a well in his back acre.”', 'lead_paragraph': '“Families is where our nation finds hope, where wings take dream.”— GEORGE W. BUSH, LACROSSE, WISCONSIN, 18 OCTOBER, 2000', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Killed at the Whim of a Hat’', 'kicker': 'Excerpt', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T21:14:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Colin Cotterill', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Colin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cotterill', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'First Chapter', '_id': 'nyt://article/332ca656-eecc-5c02-8131-8af12b7dffe6', 'word_count': 1638, 'uri': 'nyt://article/332ca656-eecc-5c02-8131-8af12b7dffe6'}, {'abstract': 'Colin Cotterill’s “Killed at the Whim of a Hat” starts off a new series set in Thailand and featuring the female crime reporter Jimm Juree.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/books/killed-at-the-whim-of-a-hat-by-colin-cotterill-book-review.html', 'snippet': 'Colin Cotterill’s “Killed at the Whim of a Hat” starts off a new series set in Thailand and featuring the female crime reporter Jimm Juree.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Colin Cotterill has been best known as the author of novels about Dr. Siri Paiboun, a septuagenarian Laotian coroner who is a much more lovable character than that description suggests. The Dr. Siri series, set in the 1970s, has been so popular that it once landed Mr. Cotterill on a slab in the Munich city morgue, where he was asked to pose for promotional photos. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/arts/book/book-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 975, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/arts/book/book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/21/arts/book/book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Murders to Unravel, Relatives to Endure', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Murders to Unravel, Relatives to Endure', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cotterill, Colin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Thailand', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T21:14:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Janet Maslin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Janet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Maslin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3813695-348f-52a4-90d9-94a5d59e94eb', 'word_count': 1021, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3813695-348f-52a4-90d9-94a5d59e94eb'}, {'abstract': 'A former tech entrepreneur turned photographer and feel-good missionary hopes to create awareness through his handmade books of images.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/fashion/joseph-peter-on-the-road-to-happiness-up-close.html', 'snippet': 'A former tech entrepreneur turned photographer and feel-good missionary hopes to create awareness through his handmade books of images.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NOT long after Joseph Peter, a tech entrepreneur turned photographer and feel-good missionary, took over the sixth floor of a triangle-shaped building at the intersection of Bleecker and Lafayette Streets in September, he hung a sign on the door. It read: “Warning: You are now entering an energy field of happiness. You will leave happier. We are not responsible for any loss of unhappiness.”', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/fashion/17CLOSE-span/17CLOSE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/21/fashion/17CLOSE-span/17CLOSE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/fashion/17CLOSE-span/17CLOSE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/fashion/17CLOSE-span/17CLOSE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/21/fashion/17CLOSE-span/17CLOSE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}]