tyle', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/a6e8e52d-854d-51db-b846-13622d31e344', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/a6e8e52d-854d-51db-b846-13622d31e344'}, {'abstract': 'The persistent inability of the United Nations to forge international consensus on climate change issues was on display at the Security Council.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/world/21nations.html', 'snippet': 'The persistent inability of the United Nations to forge international consensus on climate change issues was on display at the Security Council.', 'lead_paragraph': 'UNITED NATIONS — The persistent inability of the United Nations to forge international consensus on climate change issues was on display Wednesday, as Security Council members disagreed over whether they should address possible instability provoked by problems like rising sea levels or competition over water resources. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.N. Deadlock on Addressing Climate Shift', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Consensus On Addressing Climate Shift', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Security Council (UN)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T21:51:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil MacFarquhar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacFarquhar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc12cab0-9ee4-5abf-8ced-9c6df69e5894', 'word_count': 642, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc12cab0-9ee4-5abf-8ced-9c6df69e5894'}, {'abstract': 'The American striker Jozy Altidore is on the move again — signing a four-year contract with AZ in the Netherlands.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/20/altidore-is-the-cheese/', 'snippet': 'The American striker Jozy Altidore is on the move again — signing a four-year contract with AZ in the Netherlands.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Maybe it has been the language barrier: Spanish, Geordie English, Turkish. And now, Jozy Altidore faces the prospect of learning, or trying to learn, yet another European tongue — Dutch (though so many folks there learn English in elementary school). ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Altidore Is the Cheese', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Altidore, Jozy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Villarreal CF', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALKMAAR (NETHERLANDS)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T21:52:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Bell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1b9aabf-c5b8-5ff8-b4aa-1f691445904d', 'word_count': 366, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1b9aabf-c5b8-5ff8-b4aa-1f691445904d'}, {'abstract': 'For the first time in its illustrious past the Newport Folk Festival has sold out tickets for its two days of events in advance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/arts/music/a-first-in-long-history-of-newport-folk-festival.html', 'snippet': 'For the first time in its illustrious past the Newport Folk Festival has sold out tickets for its two days of events in advance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the first time in its illustrious past the Newport Folk Festival has sold out tickets for its two days of events in advance, partly because of a strong effort to promote the event through social networking sites, organizers said. The festival, which was started in 1959 and became famous in the 1960s during the heyday of protest songs, has sold out before, most recently in 2002, when Bob Dylan returned to perform there after an absence of many years. But in past years people could always get tickets at the gate, even on the last day of the festival, which is held at Fort Adams State Park on Narragansett Bay. This year, all 20,000 tickets were sold in advance. George Wein, the producer who founded the festival with Pete Seeger, said the Internet buzz was only a sign of something deeper: a resurgence of interest in folk music in recent years, as rising bands like Mumford & Sons have racked up hits on pop and rock charts using a folk template. Alongside established headliners like Emmylou Harris, left, and Elvis Costello, above left, the lineup this year includes hot indie-rock groups with folk-inflected styles, like the Decemberists and the Head and the Heart.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A First in Long History Of Newport Folk Festival', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A First in Long History Of Newport Folk Festival', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T21:52:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/71e1114e-634f-5db6-8a62-d9de9f318fa3', 'word_count': 208, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71e1114e-634f-5db6-8a62-d9de9f318fa3'}, {'abstract': 'The premiere of the final season of “Entourage” on Tuesday had the contemplative feel of a high school graduation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/fashion/at-entourage-premiere-dudes-at-the-end-of-an-era-scene-city.html', 'snippet': 'The premiere of the final season of “Entourage” on Tuesday had the contemplative feel of a high school graduation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE life-parodying-Hollywood scene at the “Entourage” premiere reached its self-referential height around the time Andrew Dice Clay lighted a cigarette just off the red carpet. Mr. Clay, who plays himself on the show (that is, an aging comic seeking a comeback), wore a sleeveless leather jacket with “Brooklyn” in rhinestones on the back, blue snakeskin boots and tinted glasses.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/fashion/17SCENE-span/17SCENE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/21/fashion/17SCENE-span/17SCENE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/fashion/17SCENE-span/17SCENE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 644, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/fashion/17SCENE-span/17SCENE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'im