red out-of-the-ordinary selections.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/arts/music/washington-square-music-festival-review.html', 'snippet': 'The Washington Square Music Festival offered out-of-the-ordinary selections.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The programming at free outdoor summer events often favors standard repertory, but the Washington Square Music Festival veered far off the beaten path with a concert called “The Joy of Unfamiliar Music” on Tuesday evening. A large crowd braved sweltering weather to hear the Festival Chamber Ensemble play works by Berio, Emmanuel Séjourné, Corrado Maria Saglietti and Vincenzo Gambaro.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/arts/SQUARE/SQUARE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 880, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Unusual Sounds to Play in a Park', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Unusual Sounds To Play In a Park', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington Square Park (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T22:11:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivien Schweitzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweitzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/09f88ad9-f8b6-5b05-a57f-9c960983e476', 'word_count': 359, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09f88ad9-f8b6-5b05-a57f-9c960983e476'}, {'abstract': "Is Twitter competing with outside developers who have created apps for it? Bettina Edelstein speaks with Times technology reporter Claire Cain Miller about strains between Twitter and third-party developers. The phone-hacking scandal in Britain may have you wondering about your own cellphone security. J.D. Biersdorfer has info and tips for keeping your voicemail secure. And speed demon Pedro Rafael Rosado takes a look at the Intel 320 Series 160 GB 2.5-inch SSD. The news roundup includes a Google+ iPhone app; William Shatner shaking up Google+; a Reddit founder charged with data theft; Amazon Kindle textbook rentals; and the Toshiba Thrive tablet. J.D.'s tip of the week: making shortcuts for Web apps in Chrome.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2011/07/20/technology/personaltech/20techtalk_pod.html', 'snippet': 'Is Twitter competing with outside developers who have created apps for it? Bettina Edelstein speaks with Times technology reporter Claire Cain Miller about strains between Twitter and third-party developers. The phone-hacking scandal in Britain ma...', 'lead_paragraph': "Is Twitter competing with outside developers who have created apps for it? Bettina Edelstein speaks with Times technology reporter Claire Cain Miller about strains between Twitter and third-party developers. The phone-hacking scandal in Britain may have you wondering about your own cellphone security. J.D. Biersdorfer has info and tips for keeping your voicemail secure. And speed demon Pedro Rafael Rosado takes a look at the Intel 320 Series 160 GB 2.5-inch SSD. The news roundup includes a Google+ iPhone app; William Shatner shaking up Google+; a Reddit founder charged with data theft; Amazon Kindle textbook rentals; and the Toshiba Thrive tablet. J.D.'s tip of the week: making shortcuts for Web apps in Chrome.", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': "Claire Cain Miller on tension over Twitter apps; safeguarding voicemail; Intel's 320 Series solid-state drive; news.", 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': No