imes.com/2011/07/20/electricity-demand-soars-in-mid-atlantic-states/', 'snippet': 'Grid operators in the mid-Atlantic region, New York State and New England predict that they can cope with the heat wave.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As millions of air conditioners sucked power, electricity consumption in the mid-Atlantic region soared on Wednesday beyond the level that planners had estimated would be the peak for this year. But grid operators in that region, and in New England and New York, said they were confident they could meet demand during the current heat wave.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Electricity Demand Soars in Mid-Atlantic States', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Conditioning', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Light and Power', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Delaware', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maryland', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New England States (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Carolina', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Virginia', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T22:22:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a85e9861-656b-54ce-9579-81db19c27f3f', 'word_count': 456, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a85e9861-656b-54ce-9579-81db19c27f3f'}, {'abstract': 'Howard Barker’s 1983 play “Victory: Choices in Reaction,” having its American premiere at the Atlantic Theater’s Stage 2, features Jan Maxwell in a tour de force performance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/theater/reviews/jan-maxwell-in-victory-choices-in-reaction-review.html', 'snippet': 'Howard Barker’s 1983 play “Victory: Choices in Reaction,” having its American premiere at the Atlantic Theater’s Stage 2, features Jan Maxwell in a tour de force performance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What is a lone Puritan widow in 1660s England to do when the Restoration government digs up her husband’s body, decapitates him posthumously and puts his head on a pike? If she is a character written by Howard Barker and played by the incomparable Jan Maxwell, she sets off on a journey to collect the pieces, no matter what that trip might do to her.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Puritan Widow Confronts a Randy, Profane King', 'kicker': "Theater Review | 'Victory: Choices in Reaction'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Puritan Widow Confronts A Randy, Profane King', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maxwell, Jan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romagnoli, Richard', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'PTP/NYC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T22:22:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anita Gates', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anita', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gates', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6da0a65-058e-57ed-8dd4-5b5659444bab', 'word_count': 409, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6da0a65-058e-57ed-8dd4-5b5659444bab'}, {'abstract': 'The New Albion label is running a series of performances at the Stone, a small concert hall owned by John Zorn.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/arts/music/jeffrey-roden-gyan-riley-and-wu-fei-at-the-stone-review.html', 'snippet': 'The New Albion label is running a series of performances at the Stone, a small concert hall owned by John Zorn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'How’s this for noncompetitive collegiality? You would think that John Zorn, the composer and saxophonist who also runs a new-music label, Tzadik, and an East Village performance space, the Stone, would use his small concert hall mainly as a showcase for his own music and for the works his label releases. He does some of that, but Mr. Zorn also regularly offers the Stone to other composers to do with as they please, often for weeks at a time, and they, in turn, present other composers. He also invites record labels that (in theory) compete with his own to offer showcases of their composers and performers. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/arts/STONE1/STONE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/21/arts/STONE1/STONE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/arts/STONE1/STONE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 836, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/arts/STONE1/STONE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 