 'value': 'Rent Control and Stabilization', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T23:05:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joyce Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joyce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af2f393b-43ba-50b5-b79c-3375757dcd0b', 'word_count': 157, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af2f393b-43ba-50b5-b79c-3375757dcd0b'}, {'abstract': 'The author tracks down those who helped rescue her father-in-law in France during World War II, and finds a substitute home.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/garden/bobbie-ann-mason-back-home-via-france.html', 'snippet': 'The author tracks down those who helped rescue her father-in-law in France during World War II, and finds a substitute home.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOR decades I knew where home was — the farm in Kentucky where I was raised. I was free to roam the world as long as my parents were still there. But now all that is gone, and in place of the family farm I have been going to France. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/20/garden/21domestic/21DOMESTIC1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/20/garden/21domestic/21domestic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/20/garden/21domestic/21domestic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Back Home, via France', 'kicker': 'Domestic Lives', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Back Home, Via France', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T23:05:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bobbie Ann Mason', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bobbie', 'middlename': 'Ann', 'lastname': 'Mason', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/caa6bf7a-941e-5082-85c9-106db014c844', 'word_count': 1449, 'uri': 'nyt://article/caa6bf7a-941e-5082-85c9-106db014c844'}, {'abstract': 'Steinway Lyngdorf’s S-Series promises unbelievably crisp sound in a package that’s portable.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/garden/steinway-lyngdorfs-22100-budget-stereo-system-audio.html', 'snippet': 'Steinway Lyngdorf’s S-Series promises unbelievably crisp sound in a package that’s portable.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It might seem like $22,100 is a fortune to pay for a stereo system, but Steinway Lyngdorf’s S-Series is actually a budget model; the company’s more established Model D starts at $188,000, with two 7-foot, 384-pound speaker towers and a tweeter trimmed in 24-karat gold.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/garden/21audio/21audio-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 777, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/garden/21audio/21audio-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, '