ween the Israelis and the Palestinians. But with talks at a standstill, the Obama administration now finds itself on the sidelines, and Europe is emerging as the key diplomatic actor.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/world/21mideast1/21mideast1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 806, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/world/21mideast1/21mideast1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/21/world/21mideast1/21mideast1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'As U.S. Steps Back, Europe Takes Bigger Role in Mideast Peace Push', 'kicker': 'Diplomatic Memo', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As U.S. Steps Back, Europe Takes Bigger Role in Mideast Peace Push', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Israeli Settlements', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-20T23:45:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/42be2881-026e-5bbe-ba4d-5ef701db4c76', 'word_count': 1012, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42be2881-026e-5bbe-ba4d-5ef701db4c76'}, {'abstract': 'Millions of people are on the brink of starvation and aid deliveries are complicated by the fact that militants control the famine zones.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/world/africa/21somalia.html', 'snippet': 'Millions of people are on the brink of starvation and aid deliveries are complicated by the fact that militants control the famine zones.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOMBASA, Kenya — The United Nations on Wednesday officially declared Somalia’s food crisis a famine in several parts of the country, with millions of people on the brink of starvation and aid deliveries complicated by the fact that Islamist militants aligned with Al Qaeda control the famine zones.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/world/21somalia_span/21somalia-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 355, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/21/world/21somalia_span/21somalia-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 355}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/world/21somalia_span/21somalia-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 716, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/world/21somalia_span/21somalia-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/21/world/21somalia_span/21somalia-thumbStand