 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/world/middleeast/21egypt.html', 'snippet': 'Egypt’s interim military rulers established a system for what is promised to be the first free and open elections in the country’s history.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — Egypt’s interim military rulers established a system on Wednesday for what is promised to be the first free and open elections in the country’s history, laying out a complicated plan evidently designed as a compromise between the competing demands of liberal and Islamist groups.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt Rulers Outline Plan for Elections', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Egypt Rulers Outline Plan For Elections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mubarak, Hosni', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-21T00:49:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By David D. Kirkpatrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f787d50b-baf7-5339-98e5-c140ec68448e', 'word_count': 334, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f787d50b-baf7-5339-98e5-c140ec68448e'}, {'abstract': 'A group of 75 retired players alleged that teams’ mismanagement of their concussions, and the league’s willful concealment of the effects of head injuries, led to the players’ current brain damage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/sports/football/retired-players-sue-nfl-over-treatment-of-concussions.html', 'snippet': 'A group of 75 retired players alleged that teams’ mismanagement of their concussions, and the league’s willful concealment of the effects of head injuries, led to the players’ current brain damage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A group of 75 retired N.F.L. veterans sued the league in a California court on Tuesday, alleging that N.F.L. teams’ mismanagement of their concussions, and the league’s willful concealment of evidence of the long-term effects of head injuries, led to the players’ current brain damage.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/sports/Y-SAFTEY/Y-SAFTEY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/21/sports/Y-SAFTEY/Y-SAFTEY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/sports/Y-SAFTEY/Y-SAFTEY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/sports/Y-SAFTEY/Y-SAFTEY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/21/sports/Y-SAFTEY/Y-SAFTEY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Concussion Treatment Cited in Suit Against N.F.L.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Concussion Treatment Cited in Suit Against N.F.L.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Concussions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dementia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-21T00:52:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson and Alan Schwarz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwarz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce3a3a16-a064-500b-a946-658403432526', 'word_count': 928, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce3a3a16-a064-500b-a946-658403432526'}, {'abstract': 'Among the issues still believed to be in play: the players’ demand for $320 million that owners did not have to pay in benefits during the 2010 season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/sports/football/in-a-surprising-turn-nfl-deal-doesnt-yet-get-final-approval.html', 'snippet': 'Among the issues still believed to be in play: the players’ demand for $320 million that owners did not have to pay in benefits during the 2010 season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATLANTA — The byzantine, often inscrutable negotiations toward a new N.F.L. labor agreement took another surprising turn on Wednesday when players, with a draft of the settlement in their hands in Washington, gave only a conditional recommendation for approval contingent on the negotiation of a few final terms, according to two people involved in the players’ actions.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 