'lead_paragraph': 'For the second time in a year, the State Department has issued an environmental impact statement about the proposed Keystone XL pipeline, which would carry diluted bitumen — an acidic crude oil — from the tar sands of northern Alberta to the Texas Gulf Coast. And for the second time in a year, the Environmental Protection Agency has excoriated the State Department for the inadequacy of its assessment.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wrong Pipeline, Wrong Assessment', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wrong Pipeline, Wrong Assessment: The State Department fails, again, to consider the risks of tar sands oil', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pipelines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil Sands', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TransCanada Corporation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-21T01:06:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/1eb5af63-4518-5cac-a8bf-fd093cc61953', 'word_count': 442, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1eb5af63-4518-5cac-a8bf-fd093cc61953'}, {'abstract': 'Chances may be remote, but News Corporation’s troubles in Britain could still reach the company’s television stations in the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/business/no-us-peril-for-news-corp-at-least-not-yet.html', 'snippet': 'Chances may be remote, but News Corporation’s troubles in Britain could still reach the company’s television stations in the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'News Corporation’s British static could yet hit American airwaves. Phone-hacking and bribery charges already threaten Rupert Murdoch’s hold on pay-TV company British Sky Broadcasting, known as BSkyB. But his ownership of 27 United States Fox Broadcasting stations, home to hit shows like “American Idol,” could also be in jeopardy if the accusations prove true.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No U.S. Peril for News Corp., at Least Not Yet', 'kicker': 'Reuters Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For News Corp., No U.S. Peril. Yet.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'British Sky Broadcasting Group (BSkyB)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NEWS CORP', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Communications Commission', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-21T01:06:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Reynolds Holding and Richard Beales', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Reynolds', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holding', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beales', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3507dfdc-a689-5392-a50a-b5e0b8ec526b', 'word_count': 723, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3507dfdc-a689-5392-a50a-b5e0b8ec526b'}, {'abstract': 'Lawyers for the actor Hugh Grant spoke of unspecified “other newspapers” in a small, nondescript courtroom on Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/world/europe/21london.html', 'snippet': 'Lawyers for the actor Hugh Grant spoke of unspecified “other newspapers” in a small, nondescript courtroom on Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Front pages across Britain featured pictures of Rupert Murdoch apologizing for phone hacking at The News of the World. But further suggestions that the practice spread beyond his newspaper emerged in a small, nondescript courtroom on Wednesday, even as Prime Minister David Cameron broadened an inquiry into the conduct of the British press.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/world/21london/21london-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 729, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/world/21london/21london-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/21/world/21london/21london-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Court, Suggestions of Hacking Beyond The News of the World', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Court, Suggestions of Hacking Beyond The N