/21/business/Anchor1/Anchor1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 710, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sharpton Appears to Win Anchor Spot on MSNBC', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sharpton Appears to Win Anchor Spot on MSNBC', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MSNBC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sharpton, Al', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-21T02:18:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/003fb072-9dca-5c00-a0cd-bb9008a81550', 'word_count': 563, 'uri': 'nyt://article/003fb072-9dca-5c00-a0cd-bb9008a81550'}, {'abstract': 'Virgin Mobile has kept unlimited data and messages on all tiers but raised the cost of voice minutes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/business/virgin-mobiles-new-rates-keep-data-plans-unlimited.html', 'snippet': 'Virgin Mobile has kept unlimited data and messages on all tiers but raised the cost of voice minutes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Into the summer squall of new phone plans, add the new no-contract plans from Virgin Mobile (owned by Sprint). The carrier is raising the prices of its bottom two tiers of service — to $35 from $25 for the 300-minute-a-month plan and to $45 from $40 for the 1,200-minute plan — but lowering the cost for the unlimited voice plan by $5, to $55. Data remains unlimited in all of the plans. The changes went into effect Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Virgin, Raising Revenue Without Raising Hackles', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At Virgin, Raising Revenue Without Raising Hackles', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Virgin Mobile', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cellular Telephones', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-21T02:19:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roy Furchgott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Furchgott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/868fda3b-799c-5a21-9d6a-57bf67b7c3ba', 'word_count': 332, 'uri': 'nyt://article/868fda3b-799c-5a21-9d6a-57bf67b7c3ba'}, {'abstract': 'Freddy Garcia, the Yankees’ 34-year-old starting pitcher, outdueled the Rays’ superb 25-year-old left-hander, David Price, holding Tampa Bay to eight hits in six and two-thirds innings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/sports/baseball/the-yankees-veteran-starter-freddy-garcia-outduels-the-rays.html', 'snippet': 'Freddy Garcia, the Yankees’ 34-year-old starting pitcher, outdueled the Rays’ superb 25-year-old left-hander, David Price, holding Tampa Bay to eight hits in six and two-thirds innings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ST. PETERSBURG, Fla. — The Tampa Bay Rays continued one of the more amazing streaks in modern baseball Wednesday night, starting a pitcher younger than 30 years old for the 698th consecutive game. Their ability to identify, draft and develop talent has helped them compete in a cutthroat division against the Boston Red Sox and the Yankees, who opted to assemble this year’s rotation through different means.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/sports/21yankees-1/21yankees-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 355, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/21/sports/21yankees-1/21yankees-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 355}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/sports/21yankees-1/21yankees-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/sports/21yankees-1/21yankees-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/21/sports/21yankees-1/21yankees-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Experience Tops Youth as Garcia Halts Rays', 'kicker': 'Yankees 4, Rays 0', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Experience Tops Youth As Garcia Halts Rays', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Granderson, Curtis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Price, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tampa Bay Rays', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garcia, Freddy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-21T02:21:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac852112-0c03-5c2e-aea7-b8669aaded5c', 'word_count': 888, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac852112-0c03-5c2e-aea7-b8669aaded5c'}, {'abstract': 'Elana Katz is a psychotherapist and mediator who specializes in helping couples through a collaborative, nonadversarial divorce process — and who teaches other therapists to do the same.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/nyregion/elana-katz-makes-divorce-less-adversarial.html', 'snippet': 'Elana Katz is a psychotherapist and mediator who specializes in helping couples through a collaborative, nonadversarial divorce process — and who teaches other therapists to do the same.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Elana Katz is director of the Family and Divorce Mediation Program at the Ackerman Institute for the Family in Manhattan, where she is also a senior faculty member, teaching and practicing collaborative divorce coaching. Originally from Peoria, Ill., she received a master’s degree in social work from Hunter College and also has a private practice in psychotherapy and mediation. Ms. Katz, 57, is divorced and lives on the Upper West Side; she has a daughter who is a teacher. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/nyregion/EXPERIENCE1/EXPERIENCE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/21/nyregion/EXPERIENCE1/EXPERIENCE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/nyregion/EXPERIENC