 multibillion-dollar secondary ticketing market.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/business/media/scalping-battle-putting-fans-in-the-middle.html', 'snippet': 'Ticket sellers are setting up nonprofit groups that claim they represent consumers, but are part of a lobbying fight over control of the multibillion-dollar secondary ticketing market.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s the summer concert season and, as usual, many fans are frustrated that rampant ticket scalping online has made seeing their favorite performer almost as much a frustration as a thrill. But now a new group says it wants to help.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/business/Tickets1/Tickets1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/21/business/Tickets1/Tickets1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/business/Tickets1/Tickets1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 642, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/business/Tickets1/Tickets1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/21/business/Tickets1/Tickets1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Scalping Battle Putting ‘Fans’ in the Middle', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Scalping Battle Led by ‘Fans’ In Name Only', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Live Nation Entertainment Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ticket Scalping', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'StubHub', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lobbying and Lobbyists', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nonprofit Organizations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ticketmaster', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-21T02:36:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab54b6c2-5a49-5068-b538-2cadaf71f3a9', 'word_count': 1159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab54b6c2-5a49-5068-b538-2cadaf71f3a9'}, {'abstract': 'The authorities have increased the death toll in a clash on Monday in the restive western border region of Xinjiang, saying now that 18 people died in the violence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/world/asia/21china.html', 'snippet': 'The authorities have increased the death toll in a clash on Monday in the restive western border region of Xinjiang, saying now that 18 people died in the violence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The authorities have increased the death toll in a clash on Monday in the restive western border region of Xinjiang, saying now that 18 people died in the violence. The state media reported on Monday that two police officers and two hostages had died in an attack on a police station in the city of Hotan. But state media said Wednesday that 14 others had also died in the attack. Exile groups representing the region’s largest minority, the Uighurs, said that the police had opened fired on unarmed demonstrators. But the state media said that protesters had attacked the station with grenades and explosives. Over the past two years, a series of riots and protests against the country’s majority ethnic group, the Han, has resulted in hundreds of deaths.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China: Death Toll Increases in Xinjiang', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: Death Toll in Clash Rises', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Xinjiang (China)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Uighurs (Chinese Ethnic Group)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-21T02:41:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/81bde91f-087e-5ff8-b544-f352ef5844c5', 'word_count': 130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81bde91f-087e-5ff8-b544-f352ef5844c5'}, {'abstract': 'Images from some of the films playing at NewFest, a New York film festival featuring movies with lesbian, gay, bisexual and transgender themes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/07/21/movies/newfest-2011.html', 'snippet': 'Images from some of the films playing at NewFest, a New York film festival featuring movies with lesbian, gay, bisexual and transgender themes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Images from some of the films playing at NewFest, a New York film festival featuring movies with lesbian, gay, bisexual and transgender themes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/movies/newfest-2011-slide-PCMH/newfest-2011-slide-PCMH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 735, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/movies/newfest-2011-slide-PCMH/newfest-2011-slide-PCMH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/21/movies/newfest-2011-slide-PCMH/newfest-2011-slide-PCMH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Films at NewFest', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-21T02:43:20+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Movies', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/aa61b95a-6ab1-5221-acf4-d7a71ae59824', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/aa61b95a-6ab1-5221-acf4-d7a71ae59824'}, {'abstract': 'Italy’s lower house of Parliament voted to lift the immunity of a lawmaker from Prime Minister Silvio Berlusconi’s People of Liberty party, allowing his arrest on corruption charges.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/world/europe/21briefs-Italy.html', 'snippet': 'Italy’s lower house of Parliament voted to lift the immunity of a lawmaker from Prime Minister Silvio Berlusconi’s People of Liberty party, allowing his arrest on corruption charges.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The lower house of Parliament on Wednesday voted to lift the immunity of a lawmaker from Prime Minister Silvio Berlusconi’s People of Liberty party, allowing his arrest on corruption charges. The vote, by a secret ballot, was a blow to Mr. Berlusconi, showing that factions within his center-right coalition had gone against his wishes and voted to allow the arrest of the lawmaker, Alfonso Papa. Prosecutors in Naples have charged Mr. Papa with corruption, including the illegal dissemination of information protected by state secrecy in a complex scandal involving the trading of favors by people who prosecutors say are close to members of Mr. Berlusconi’s cabinet. In another sign of government disarray, Mr. Berlusconi’s coalition lost a vote in Parliament on Wednesday on a plan to resolve a garbage crisis in Naples. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Italy: Two Setbacks for Belusconi', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | EUROPE', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Italy: Two Setbacks for Belusconi', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Naples (Italy)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berlusconi, Silvio', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-21T02:43:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Donadio', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Donadio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/450570e5-a399-53b0-b4aa-f4cabdba0963', 'word_count': 133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/450570e5-a399-53b0-b4aa-f4cabdba0963'}, {'abstract': 'Most of the city’s problems flow from a failed trash incinerator project that has saddled the city with $310 million in debt, causing residents to take a stand against deep sacrifices from taxpayers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/us/21harrisburg.html', 'snippet': 'Most of the city’s problems flow from a failed trash incinerator project that has saddled the city with $310 million in debt, causing residents to take a stand against deep sacrifices from taxpayers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HARRISBURG, Pa. — When officials here rejected a state-sponsored financial recovery plan on Tuesday night, the city was briefly transformed into the Greece of Pennsylvania, with residents taking a stand against fiscal austerity despite the risk to their own economy.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/us/HARRISBURG-2/HARRISBURG-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/us/HARRISBURG-2/HARRISBURG-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/21/us/HARRISBURG-2/HARRISBURG-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Harrisburg Finds Itself in Uncharted Financial Waters', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'City Finds Itself in Uncharted Financial Waters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Harrisburg (Pa)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-21T02:45:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name