they have found a potential cause for a number of otherwise unexplained cases of male infertility: the absence of a protein that coats sperm and allows them to reach an egg more easily.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Study Links Male Infertility to a Missing Protein', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Study Links Male Infertility to a Missing Protein', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infertility', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sperm', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reproduction (Biological)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-21T02:53:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pam Belluck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belluck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/508327ac-08dc-532a-babc-c12cbd784a17', 'word_count': 832, 'uri': 'nyt://article/508327ac-08dc-532a-babc-c12cbd784a17'}, {'abstract': 'Canada will revoke the Canadian citizenship of 1,800 people who the government believes used fraud to obtain their status.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/world/americas/21briefs-Canada.html', 'snippet': 'Canada will revoke the Canadian citizenship of 1,800 people who the government believes used fraud to obtain their status.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Canada will revoke the Canadian citizenship of 1,800 people who the government believes used fraud to obtain their status. Jason Kenney, the immigration minister, told a news conference on Wednesday that police and immigration investigators had found that most of the people had hired “crooked immigration consultants” to produce fake proof of residency in Canada. There has been a public debate about people who live in troubled parts of the world taking Canadian citizenship as a kind of insurance policy. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Canada: 1,800 Lose Citizenship', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | THE AMERICAS', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Canada: 1,800 Lose Citizenship', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizenship and Naturalization', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-21T03:03:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3f3f579-7ae2-5ed8-8617-693fcd51272d', 'word_count': 80, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3f3f579-7ae2-5ed8-8617-693fcd51272d'}, {'abstract': 'France’s main electricity company announced on Wednesday that it had delayed for another two years the completion of a third-generation nuclear power plant in northern France.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/world/europe/21briefs-France.html', 'snippet': 'France’s main electricity company announced on Wednesday that it had delayed for another two years the completion of a third-generation nuclear power plant in northern France.', 'lead_paragraph': ' France’s main electricity company announced on Wednesday that it had delayed for another two years the completion of a third-generation nuclear power plant in Flamanville, in northern France, citing structural problems, construction accidents and new tests for safety after the Fukushima nuclear accident in Japan. The European pressurized reactor, already delayed, is now expected to be finished in 2016, and the cost for the project is expected to rise to six billion euros. “This delay is linked to both structural and economic reasons,” the company, EDF, said in a statement. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France: Reactor Delayed Again', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | EUROPE', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France: Reactor Delayed Again', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Energy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-21T03:06:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Erlanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erlanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/813baa33-99c4-5bc3-ace8-7508b7ab9200', 'word_count': 92, 'uri': 'nyt://article/813baa33-99c4-5bc3-ace8-7508b7ab9200'}, {'abstract': 'A career military man, Mr. Gayler was also an ardent advocate of nuclear disarmament.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/us/21gayler.html', 'snippet': 'A career military man, Mr. Gayler was also an ardent advocate of nuclear disarmament.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Retired Adm. Noel Gayler, a highly decorated pilot who in the 1970s served as commander of American forces in the Pacific and director of the National Securi