opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/the-campbell-rangers-hit-bull-run/', 'snippet': 'A “gentleman officer” takes his Virginia cavalry into the Civil War’s first major battle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'John “Captain Jack” Alexander beamed with pride after the First Battle of Bull Run. His south central Virginia cavalry had distinguished itself in its first big fight, and his official report praised his men’s participation in the momentous engagement. “From the commencement of the action in the morning until late in the evening they were under the enemy’s fire,” he wrote. “They remained firm and unshaken, exhibiting an anxiety only to meet the enemy, and awaiting patiently an opportunity to strike an effective blow.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Campbell Rangers Hit Bull Run', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Farmers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-21T16:03:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ronald S. Coddington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ronald', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Coddington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a34841ee-38e4-50cc-83ea-2b7f0486da45', 'word_count': 1395, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a34841ee-38e4-50cc-83ea-2b7f0486da45'}, {'abstract': 'Andy Schleck of Luxembourg tried to wrest control of the Tour de France with a daring ride Thursday, but Thomas Voeckler of France would not yield his overall lead.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/22/sports/cycling/2011-tour-de-france-andy-schleck-surges-but-voeckler-holds-lead.html', 'snippet': 'Andy Schleck of Luxembourg tried to wrest control of the Tour de France with a daring ride Thursday, but Thomas Voeckler of France would not yield his overall lead.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GALIBIER SERRE-CHEVALIER, France — Andy Schleck of Luxembourg charged uphill, ahead, exhausted and alone.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/sports/ytour1/ytour1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/22/sports/ytour1/ytour1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/sports/ytour1/ytour1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 654, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/sports/ytour1/ytour1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/22/sports/ytour1/ytour1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Andy Schleck Charges in Tour; Voeckler Holds Lead', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After a Frenetic Ascent, Andy Schleck Sees Paris in the Distance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schleck, Andy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tour de France (Bicycle Race)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Voeckler, Thomas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bicycles and Bicycling', 'rank': 4, 'maj