s at Manhattan’s Trinity School were part of a research team that discovered that many herbal teas contain unlisted ingredients.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scientific Reports, a Nature journal, published research on Thursday showing that a significant percentage of herbal teas tested contained ingredients the tea manufacturers failed to list. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Young Sleuths’ Last Target: Sushi. This Time: Tea.', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DNA (Deoxyribonucleic Acid)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private and Sectarian Schools', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tea', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rockefeller University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Trinity School', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-21T16:59:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenny Anderson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Anderson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a21451c-903b-54cf-8e88-98dd86b52639', 'word_count': 695, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a21451c-903b-54cf-8e88-98dd86b52639'}, {'abstract': 'As news of the phone hacking scandal in Britain dominated the headlines this week, the editorial pages of two newspapers owned by Rupert Murdoch claimed that rival news organizations gave the story too much attention.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/cartoon-in-murdochs-paper-calls-hacking-inquiry-a