s', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/dfd2ab67-c90e-5113-94cd-b28d61f40427', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/dfd2ab67-c90e-5113-94cd-b28d61f40427'}, {'abstract': 'It’s entirely possible to go high-adrenaline by day and highbrow culture by night in this Colorado mountain town.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/07/24/travel/20110724-aspen.html', 'snippet': 'It’s entirely possible to go high-adrenaline by day and highbrow culture by night in this Colorado mountain town.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s entirely possible to go high-adrenaline by day and highbrow culture by night in this Colorado mountain town.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/travel/0724ASPEN-slide-FI8Q/0724ASPEN-slide-FI8Q-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/travel/0724ASPEN-slide-FI8Q/0724ASPEN-slide-FI8Q-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/24/travel/0724ASPEN-slide-FI8Q/0724ASPEN-slide-FI8Q-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '36 Hours in Aspen', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Aspen (Colo)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-21T19:09:44+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/06c5457e-aa92-5d21-b973-097e1910019f', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/06c5457e-aa92-5d21-b973-097e1910019f'}, {'abstract': 'Summer in Aspen brings fields of wildflowers framed by snow-capped peaks, a festival-rich arts scene, and myriad opportunities to hike, bike and mingle with the glitterati.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/24/travel/36-hours-in-aspen-colo.html', 'snippet': 'Summer in Aspen brings fields of wildflowers framed by snow-capped peaks, a festival-rich arts scene, and myriad opportunities to hike, bike and mingle with the glitterati.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT’S an open secret that Aspen isn’t just a glamorous winter resort. As the lineup of private jets at the tiny airport will attest, summer is when the mountain town’s festival scene brings in celebrities of almost every category — the likes of Yo-Yo Ma for the seasonlong Aspen Music Festival, Mario Batali for the Food & Wine Classic and Sandra Day O’Connor for the Ideas Festival. Along with them come classical-music fiends who carry their own scores and Food Network fans who go wild for live knife-skill demos from the stars of\xa0“Iron Chef.” Your seatmates on the puddle-jumper from Denver, however, are just as likely to be semi-pro cyclists or whitewater hounds sniffing out the best place to shoot the rapids. They know that summer in Aspen is when nature is in full swing, and the glowing fields of wild blue flax, prairie smoke and sunflowers, framed by snowcapped peaks and groves of aspen, do a fine job of wooing attention away from the glitterati. Not that you have to choose one world over the other. It’s entirely possible to go high-adrenaline by day and highbrow culture by night.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/travel/24HOURS_SPAN/24HOURS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 225, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/24/travel/24HOURS_SPAN/24HOURS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 225}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/travel/24HOURS_SPAN/24HOURS_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 225, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/travel/24HOURS_SPAN/24HOURS_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/24/travel/24HOURS_SPAN/24HOURS_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '36 Hours in Aspen, Colo.', 'kicker': '36 Hours', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Aspen, Colo.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Aspen (Colo)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-21T19:09:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bonnie Tsui', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bonnie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tsui', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/24bb2b54-643a-5109-9df2-2bb8a6e651dc', 'word_count': 1427, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24bb2b54-643a-5109-9df2-2bb8a6e651dc'}, {'abstract': 'The voice of a Syrian protest singer lives on in YouTube clips, even after his purported slaying.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/video-of-a-syrian-protest-anthem/', 'snippet': 'The voice of a Syrian protest singer lives on in YouTube clips, even after his purported slaying.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Reporting from the Syrian city of Hama, my colleague Anthony Shadid writes on Thursday about the danger of even singing a popular protest anthem, “Yalla Erhal Ya Bashar,” or “Come on Bashar, Leave,” which calls on President Bashar al-Assad to step down.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video of a Syrian Protest Anthem', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-21T19:12:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8cc4c72-f142-5211-84d5-988db0e81a6f', 'word_count': 314, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8cc4c72-f142-5211-84d5-988db0e81a6f'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Freud, a grandson of Sigmund Freud, was called “the greatest living realist painter” by one art critic in the late 1980s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/22/arts/lucian-freud-adept-portraiture-artist-dies-at-88.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Freud, a grandson of Sigmund Freud, was called “the greatest living realist painter” by one art critic in the late 1980s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lucian Freud, whose stark and revealing paintings of friends and intimates, splayed nude in his studio, recast the art of portraiture and offered a new approach to figurative art, died on Wednesday night at his home in London. He was 88. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/arts/design/Lucianfreudss-slide-A3YK/Lucianfreudss-slide-A3YK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 844, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/arts/design/Lucianfreudss-slide-A3YK/Lucianfreudss-slide-A3YK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/21/arts/design/Lucianfreudss-slide-A3YK/Lucianfreudss-slide-A3YK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lucian Freud, Figurative Painter Who Redefined Portraiture, Is Dead at 88', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lucian Freud, Figurative Painter Who Redefined Portraiture, Is Dead at 88', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Freud, Lucian', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-21T19:14:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Grimes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grimes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/0862b5a5-694f-50f6-a02f-d26933f33c23', 'word_count': 1383, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0862b5a5-694f-50f6-a02f-d26933f33c23'}, {'abstract': 'Teen drama, both real and fictional, continues to be a winning formula for MTV. The network’s new scripted comedy series “Awkward” made its debut to strong ratings Tuesday night, following the hit show “Teen Mom,” a reality series whose title needs no explanation.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/a-cool-debut-for-awkward/', 'snippet': 'Teen drama, both real and fictional, continues to be a winning formula for MTV. The network’s new scripted comedy series “Awkward” made its debut to strong ratings Tuesday night, following the hit show “Teen Mom,” a reality series whose title need...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Teen drama, both real and fictional, continues to be a winning formula for MTV. The network’s new scripted comedy series “Awkward” made its debut to strong ratings Tuesday night, following the hit show “Teen Mom,” a reality series whose title needs no explanation. Currently on its third season, “Teen Mom” drew 3.2 million viewers and was the most-watched cable show in the 18- to 49-year-old demographic for the night, a prize it has claimed each week since its season premiere on July 7, according to an analysis of Nielsen ratings data by TV by the Numbers. “Awkward,” which focuses on the teenage life of one Jenna Hamilton (Ashley Rickards), who wants nothing more than to fit in at her high school, picked up slightly more than 1.7 million viewers. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Cool Debut for ‘Awkward’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MTV Networks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-21T19:15:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac0c4b83-cdd4-5e44-aeea-725c93f09fd9', 'word_count': 226, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac0c4b83-cdd4-5e44-aeea-725c93f09fd9'}, {'abstract': 'Scenes of Doug Aitken\'s "Black Mirror Performance" (2011). (Video courtesy of Deste Foundation for Contemporary Art, Hellenic Festival, Burger Collection, 303 Gallery, Galerie Eva Presenhuber)', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/arts/design/100000000950083/aitken-excerpt.html', 'snippet': 'Scenes of Doug Aitken\'s "Black Mirror Performance" (2011). (Video courtesy of Deste Foundation for Contemporary Art, Hellenic Festival, Burger Collection, 303 Gallery, Galerie Eva Presenhuber)', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scenes of Doug Aitken\'s "Black Mirror Performance" (2011). (Video courtesy of Deste Foundation for Contemporary Art, Hellenic Festival, Burger Collection, 303 Gallery, Galerie Eva Presenhuber)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/multimedia/video-aitken/video-aitken-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/17/multimedia/video-aitken/video-aitken-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/multimedia/video-aitken/video-aitken-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/17/multimedia/video-aitken/video-aitken-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': "'Black Mirror Performance' (2011)", 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-21T19:17:20+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'None None', 'person': [{'firstname': 'None', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'None', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/b633c030-10e3-5797-8e8f-00d1b39cabad', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/b633c030-10e3-5797-8e8f-00d1b39cabad'}, {'abstract': 'A work by Amedeo Modigliani was believed to have figured in the arrest of a war-crimes suspect who spent seven years in hiding.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/22/world/europe/22iht-serbia22.html', 'snippet': 'A work by Amedeo Modigliani was believed to have figured in the arrest of a war-crimes suspect who spent seven years in hiding.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Questions arose on Thursday about the role of a stolen painting in the arrest of Goran Hadzic, the war crimes suspect who was apprehended near Belgrade, Serbia, this week after seven years in hiding.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/world/22serbia1/22serbia1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/world/22serbia1/22serbia1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/22/world/22serbia1/22serbia1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Authenticity of Painting Questioned in Capture of Serbian', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Modigliani Painting and the Fugitive', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Serbia', 'ran