as “mistaken” when he told a parliamentary committee investigating the phone hacking scandal at the newspaper that he was not aware of a key piece of evidence discovered in 2009.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/james-murdochs-evidence-was-mistaken-former-news-of-the-world-executives-say/', 'snippet': 'Two former executives of The News of the World released a statement on Thursday in which they said that James Murdoch was “mistaken” when he told a parliamentary committee investigating the phone hacking scandal at the newspaper that he was not aw...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two former executives who worked at The News of the World released a statement on Thursday in which they said James Murdoch was “mistaken” when he told a parliamentary committee investigating the phone hacking scandal at the newspaper that he was not aware of a key piece of evidence in 2008.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'James Murdoch’s Testimony Called Into Question by Former News of the World Executives', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wiretapping and Other Eavesdropping Devices and Methods', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, James R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Myler, Colin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taylor, Gordon', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thurlbeck, Neville', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NEWS CORP', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News International Ltd', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News of the World', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-21T20:37:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cfc60e25-a0be-52d9-ad87-fd9a7471e0c5', 'word_count': 540, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cfc60e25-a0be-52d9-ad87-fd9a7471e0c5'}, {'abstract': 'Photographs from Florida, Pakistan, China and Korea.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/07/21/blogs/20110721POD.html', 'snippet': 'Photographs from Florida, Pakistan, China and Korea.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photographs from Florida, Pakistan, China and Korea.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/blogs/20110721POD-slide-15TM/20110721POD-slide-15TM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pictures of the Day: Florida and Elsewhere', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-21T20:38:54+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Blogs', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/ba440ba7-10ae-5cfa-8215-f1d15a253e9f', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/ba440ba7-10ae-5cfa-8215-f1d15a253e9f'}, {'abstract': 'Egypt’s antiquities department has been downgraded from a ministry to a cabinet-affiliated office.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/eqypt-antiquities-department-downgraded/', 'snippet': 'Egypt’s antiquities department has been downgraded from a ministry to a cabinet-affiliated office.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Egypt’s antiquities department has been downgraded from a ministry to a cabinet-affiliated office, according to the Los Angeles Times, which cited an Egyptian cabinet spokesman Thursday. The announcement came after a new Cabinet was sworn in that did not include an antiquities minister. Egypt’s antiquities agency had been elevated to a ministry by the former president, Hosni Mubarak, in the last days of his rule; previously it had been under the Ministry of Culture. It still remained unclear, however, who the government intends to appoint to run the office. Last Sunday, officials said the prime minister, Essam Sharaf, planned to replace Zahi Hawass, the longtime antiquities chief, as part of a cabinet reshuffling aimed at appeasing protesters. Since the revolution, Mr. Hawass has come under fire for his ties to the Mubaraks and his financial relationships with American organizations like National Geographic. Mr. Sharaf at first said that he would appoint Abdel Fattah el Banna, a professor at the University of Cairo, as the new minister of antiquities, but he reversed himself after the choice drew protests from archeologists. In the meantime, Mr. Hawass said that Mr. Sharaf had asked him to continue to go to work, according to the Art Newspaper.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt Antiquities Department Downgraded', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hawass, Zahi', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-21T20:45:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc82cbe9-94c5-583f-a09e-9ad7796ce0c6', 'word_count': 203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc82cbe9-94c5-583f-a09e-9ad7796ce0c6'}, {'abstract': 'After the first two parts were presented at the Manhattan Theater Club, the last part will be at Atlantic Theater Company.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/shanleys-trilogy-finale-the-drama-behind-the-drama/', 'snippet': 'After the first two parts were presented at the Manhattan Theater Club, the last part will be at Atlantic Theater Company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The writer John Patrick Shanley won a Pulitzer Prize in drama and a Tony Award for best play for “Doubt” in 2005 at his longtime theatrical home, the Manhattan Theater Club, which began producing his work in the mid-1980s. “Doubt” was the first in a trilogy; the second play, “Defiance,” was mounted in 2006 at the club and was popular with audiences (it had a healthy three-month run) but a bit less so with critics.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shanley’s Trilogy Finale: The Drama Behind the Drama', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Edson, Margaret', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Meadow, Lynne', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shanley, John Patrick', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Atlantic Theater Co', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Manhattan Theater Club', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-21T20:45:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 't