y of the Brazilian rapper Marcelo D2 are more than decorations; they are also a statement of musical purpose and direction. One arm shows the image of the samba singer José Bezerra da Silva above the logo of the hardcore punk band Black Flag, while the face of Jimi Hendrix peeks out from the other. And on his neck is printed the title of John Coltrane’s most influential recording, “A Love Supreme.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/arts/22BRAZILspan/22BRAZIL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 351, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/22/arts/22BRAZILspan/22BRAZIL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 351}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/arts/22BRAZILspan/22BRAZIL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/arts/22BRAZILspan/22BRAZIL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/22/arts/22BRAZILspan/22BRAZIL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Showing Off Eclectic Tastes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Showing Off Eclectic Tastes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-21T22:17:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Rohter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65d6a54f-c4be-529b-9896-89dab7f38077', 'word_count': 1011, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65d6a54f-c4be-529b-9896-89dab7f38077'}, {'abstract': 'The Consumer Financial Protection Bureau has opened for business, and one of its first tasks may be to combine the Good Faith Estimate and Truth in Lending forms.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/24/realestate/sorting-through-lending-costs-mortgages.html', 'snippet': 'The Consumer Financial Protection Bureau has opened for business, and one of its first tasks may be to combine the Good Faith Estimate and Truth in Lending forms.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PLENTY of people have ideas about what you should be told when you’re shopping for a mortgage, but for now, that may not be much help.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/realestate/mort-graphic/mort-graphic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 309, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/21/realestate/mort-graphic/mort-graphic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 309}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/realestate/mort-graphic/mort-graphic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/21/realestate/mort-graphic/mort-graphic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sorting Through Lending Costs', 'kicker': 'Mortgages', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sorting Through Lending Costs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Financial Protection Bureau', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-21T22:17:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maryann Haggerty', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maryann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haggerty', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/147ec0bb-e427-548b-ab51-fd2d8cfb2db4', 'word_count': 648, 'uri': 'nyt://article/147ec0bb-e427-548b-ab51-fd2d8cfb2db4'}, {'abstract': 'An absorbing account of how cocaine affected the careers of Sigmund Freud and the pathbreaking American surgeon William Halsted.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/24/books/review/an-anatomy-of-addiction-by-howard-markel-book-review.html', 'snippet': 'An absorbing account of how cocaine affected the careers of Sigmund Freud and the pathbreaking American surgeon William Halsted.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On April 21, 1884, a 28-year-old researcher in the field now called neuroscience sat down at the cluttered desk of his cramped room in Vienna General Hospital and composed a letter to his fiancée, Martha Bernays, telling her of his recent studies: “I have been reading about cocaine, the effective ingredient of coca leaves,” Sigmund Freud wrote, “which some Indian tribes chew in order to make themselves resistant to privation and fatigue.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/books/review/Nuland/Nuland-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/books/review/Nuland/Nuland-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/24/books/review/Nuland/Nuland-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sigmund Freud’s Cocaine Years', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Blow to the Ego', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cocaine and Crack Cocaine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Freud, Sigmund', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Markel, Howard', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-21T22:17:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By SHERWIN NULAND', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sherwin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'NULAND', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d314ff63-4d8f-5811-aad7-1d68dcf8be60', 'word_count': 1331, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d314ff63-4d8f-5811-aad7-1d68dcf8be60'}, {'abstract': 'A coming-of-age story with a science-fiction angle, “Another Earth” explores unspeakable grief.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/22/movies/another-earth-with-brit-marling-review.html', 'snippet': 'A coming-of-age story with a science-fiction angle, “Another Earth” explores unspeakable grief.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At one point in “Another Earth,” a coming-of-adulthood story that improbably blends a plaintive drama with romantic longing and far-out science fiction, a young woman, Rhoda (Brit Marling), apprehensively moves through her old room in her family’s home as if she were a stranger. Once a bright 17-year-old bound for M.I.T., she had taken a calamitous turn while drinking and driving, a detour that sent her to prison. Booze, youth and stupidity led to the accident, as did her distracting long look at a newly discovered planet, the blue marble twin of our own that gives the movie its metaphorically resonant title.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/arts/ANOTHER/ANOTHER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/22/arts/ANOTHER/ANOTHER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/arts/ANOTHER/ANOTHER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 772, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/arts/ANOTHER/ANOTHER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/22/arts/ANOTHER/ANOTHER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Living in a Different World, Searching for a Second Chance', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Another Earth'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Living in a Different World, Searching for a Second Chance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marling, Brit', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cahill, Mike', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Another Earth (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-21T22:18:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b742f91-ee3a-58b2-84dc-4984adf79f44', 'word_count': 823, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b742f91-ee3a-58b2-84dc-4984adf79f44'}, {'abstract': 'Two new reality shows on CMT continue a trend among shows set in the South: urbanity is scarce, and a certain brand of womanhood is promoted.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/22/arts/television/sweet-home-alabama-and-texas-women-on-cmt.html', 'snippet': 'Two new reality shows on CMT continue a trend among shows set in the South: urbanity is scarce, and a certain brand of womanhood is promoted.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This month I had occasion to spend 10 days in rural Alabama, on a lake serving as a weekend redoubt for the swells of Birmingham to the north and Atlanta to the northeast. The local restaurant, elegantly rustic in the manner of a dining spot in Aspen or Jackson Hole, offered a hickory-grilled rib-eye for $38 and an appetizer constructed around heirloom figs. Not far away, the only grocery store in town carried farro, interesting cheeses and a line of artisanal pickles from a fashionable Brooklyn purveyor that I am unable to find at my own neighborhood supermarket in that very borough.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/arts/22SOUTHERNspan/22SOUTHERN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/22/arts/22SOUTHERNspan/22SOUTHERN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/arts/22SOUTHERNspan/22SOUTHERN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 578, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/arts/22SOUTHERNspan/22SOUTHERN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/22/arts/22SOUTHERNspan/22SOUTHERN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Down South, Where the Stereotypes Bloom', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Down South, Where the Stereotypes Bloom', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MTV Networks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Country Music Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALABAMA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tennessee', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-21T22:21:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ginia Bellafante', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ginia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bellafante', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/11d502e5-ac38-5d59-9940-9dfcb589962d', 'word_count': 905, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11d502e5-ac38-5d59-9940-9dfcb589962d'}, {'abstract': 'After abandoning a plan to merge with the London Stock Exchange, the parent of the Toronto Stock Exchange will begin talks with the investment group that made a hostile bid in May.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/toronto-exchange-owner-to-begin-deal-talks-with-maple-group/', 'snippet': 'After abandoning a plan to merge with the London Stock Exchange, the parent of the Toronto Stock Exchange will begin talks with the investment group that made a hostile bid in May.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OTTAWA — After abandoning a plan to merge with the London Stock Exchange, the parent of the Toronto Stock Exchange said Thursday that it will begin talks with the investment group that made a hostile bid in May.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Toronto Exchange Owner to Begin Talks With Maple Group', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'London Stock Exchange', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Maple Group Acquisition Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TMX Group', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toronto Stock Exchange', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-21T22:21:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9ddd386-d4dd-5bc0-8c16-a701139f6c9f', 'word_count': 318, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9ddd386-d4dd-5bc0-8c16-a701139f6c9f'}, {'abstract': 'When Zach Linder decided to rent an apartment of his own in Brooklyn, it occurred to him that it would not cost all that much more to buy a place.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/24/realestate/when-the-math-says-go-ahead-and-buy-the-hunt.html', 'snippet': 'When Zach Linder decided to rent an apartment of his own in Brooklyn, it occurred to him that it would not cost all that much more to buy a place.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ZACH LINDER, who had always shared an apartment, had every intention of renting a place of his own. Envisioning a small one-bedroom in a residential Brooklyn neighborhood, he drew up a budget: “$1,400 was my soft ceiling and $1,500 was my hard ceiling,” he said. “I thought I was being pretty reasonable and not tremendously overly neurotic and picky.”', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/realestate/Hunt4/Hunt4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 871, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/realestate/Hunt4/Hunt4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/24/realestate/Hunt4/Hunt4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Studio That Doesn’t Smack of a Dorm', 'kicker': 'The Hunt', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When the Math Says Go Ahead and Buy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-21T22:22:16+0000',