s, said he was cutting his ties to the team and the MSG Networks but would remain the lead N.H.L. announcer for NBC and Versus.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/emrick-voice-of-the-n-h-l-leaves-devils/', 'snippet': 'Mike Emrick, who broadcast Devils games for 21 seasons, said he was cutting his ties to the team and the MSG Networks but would remain the lead N.H.L. announcer for NBC and Versus.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The best local sports announcers are often as well known and as beloved as a team’s players. Think of Vin Scully and the Dodgers. Marv Albert and the Knicks. Mel Allen and the Yankees. Chick Hearn and the Lakers. Mike (Doc) Emrick became that distinctive figure for Devils fans for 21 seasons. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Emrick, Voice of the N.H.L, Leaves Devils', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Jersey Devils', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-21T22:58:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/29153736-2b4a-53b4-9c3c-4a928a0ce503', 'word_count': 554, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29153736-2b4a-53b4-9c3c-4a928a0ce503'}, {'abstract': 'The tight red-and-blue costume, which appears to be made from shiny rubber, may become a problem for Columbia Pictures and Marvel Studios.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/a-new-spider-man-suit-debuts-to-decidedly-mixed-reviews/', 'snippet': 'The tight red-and-blue costume, which appears to be made from shiny rubber, may become a problem for Columbia Pictures and Marvel Studios.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN DIEGO— Hollywood uses Comic-Con to introduce bits of upcoming films to the hardest of the hard-core fans, betting that the resulting frenzy will overflow into the mainstream. The risk is a negative reaction, which sends studios into crisis mode. Even lukewarm clapping can mean months of damage control.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New ‘Spider-Man’ Suit Debuts to Decidedly Mixed Reviews', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comic-Con (Convention)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garfield, Andrew', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Entertainment Weekly', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-21T23:00:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/907d77ad-06ac-5632-84b0-824de18adf05', 'word_count': 353, 'uri': 'nyt://article/907d77ad-06ac-5632-84b0-824de18adf05'}, {'abstract': 'Woodlawn has lots of trees and thickets of greenery around the low stoops of century-old houses. Yet the landscape feature that truly stands out is the bluestone in the sidewalks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/24/realestate/wearing-the-green-in-more-ways-than-one-living-inwoodlawn-the-bronx.html', 'snippet': 'Woodlawn has lots of trees and thickets of greenery around the low stoops of century-old houses. Yet the landscape feature that truly stands out is the bluestone in the sidewalks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WOODLAWN’S name is a pretty good example of truth in advertising: forested parks, lots of trees, thickets of greenery around the low stoops of century-old houses. Yet in this quiet corner of the Bronx along the Westchester border, the landscape feature that truly stands out is the bluestone in the sidewalks.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/realestate/24LIVING_SPAN/24LIVING_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/24/realestate/24LIVING_SPAN/24LIVING_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 340}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/realestate/24LIVING_SPAN/24LIVING_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/realestate/24LIVING_SPAN/24LIVING_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/24/realestate/24LIVING_SPAN/24LIVING_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Wearing the Green, in More Ways Than One', 'kicker': 'Living In | Woodlawn, the Bronx', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wearing the Green, in More Ways Than One', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Woodlawn (Bronx, NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-21T23:01:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk':