Rspan/22MISER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Weekend Miser', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Weekend Miser', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-21T23:04:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Lee Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': 'Lee', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/993ddb8a-fcdd-5543-8824-8ac68d8e9a45', 'word_count': 534, 'uri': 'nyt://article/993ddb8a-fcdd-5543-8824-8ac68d8e9a45'}, {'abstract': 'Other teams may have had more compelling narratives, but the defending American League champion Texas Rangers have the biggest division lead in the league.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/remember-the-rangers-theyre-winning-again/', 'snippet': 'Other teams may have had more compelling narratives, but the defending American League champion Texas Rangers have the biggest division lead in the league.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Major League Baseball, some teams’ narratives have an easier time grabbing headlines than others.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Remember the Rangers? They’re Winning Again', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN LEAGUE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Texas Rangers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-21T23:05:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By NEIL PAINE', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'PAINE', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/67fc3e90-c3b4-5d8b-b790-fe70a7ff2419', 'word_count': 678, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67fc3e90-c3b4-5d8b-b790-fe70a7ff2419'}, {'abstract': 'The singer is expected to cancel shows in Jamaica this weekend.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/r-kelly-back-at-home-after-throat-surgery/', 'snippet': 'The singer is expected to cancel shows in Jamaica this weekend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'R. Kelly, the rhythm and blues singer, was hospitalized briefly this week and underwent surgery to drain an abcess from one of his tonsils, his spokesman said. It is unclear when the 44-year-old Grammy award winning singer, known for his seductive vocals and lascivious lyrics, would be well enough to perform again. His appearance at a festival in Jamaica this weekend would likely be cancelled, the spokesman, Allan Mayer, said. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'R. Kelly Back at Home After Throat Surgery', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-21T23:12:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fecc8430-db5d-5760-9620-79ed79e3fa0b', 'word_count': 149, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fecc8430-db5d-5760-9620-79ed79e3fa0b'}, {'abstract': 'NASA may have closed one era in America’s human space flight program, but the arguments for bold and inspiring missions still hold.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/22/opinion/22fri1.html', 'snippet': 'NASA may have closed one era in America’s human space flight program, but the arguments for bold and inspiring missions still hold.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The smooth landing of the shuttle Atlantis on Thursday closed an era in America’s human space flight program that had triumphs and tragedies over the past three decades but was long overdue to end. The question now is whether the nation can summon the will to push hard for a far more ambitious set of manned voyages. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After the Space Shuttle', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After the Space Shuttle: The arguments for bold, and inspiring, missions still hold', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Aeronautics and Space Administration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'SPACE SHUTTLE', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'James Webb Space Telescope', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-21T23:18:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed1c4efd-d353-53e8-8aad-c3ef64984843', 'word_count': 567, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed1c4efd-d353-53e8-8aad-c3ef64984843'}, {'abstract': 'This open-plan house uses passive-house techniques to heat and cool the home not with technology, but with purposeful design.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/07/21/realestate/20110722_tour.html', 'snippet': 'This open-plan house uses passive-house techniques to heat and cool the home not with technology, but with purposeful desig