e life is deteriorating around her.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/22/movies/a-little-help-with-jenna-fischer-review.html', 'snippet': '“A Little Help” stars Jenna Fischer as a Long Island dental hygienist whose life is deteriorating around her.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a popular television actor, the leap to film can be dicey. Once the public has warmed to a specific persona, it can fiercely resist any dismantling of the illusion — which is why Steve Carell’s movie characters shrewdly retain the essence of his alter ego from “The Office,” Michael Scott.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/arts/ROUNDUP-1/ROUNDUP-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/22/arts/ROUNDUP-1/ROUNDUP-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/arts/ROUNDUP-1/ROUNDUP-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 876, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/arts/ROUNDUP-1/ROUNDUP-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/22/arts/ROUNDUP-1/ROUNDUP-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Unsatisfying Life', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': "Movie Review | 'A Little Help'", 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-21T23:26:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeannette Catsoulis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeannette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Catsoulis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c199990-ff7b-5c4f-80fe-82b198cd20e4', 'word_count': 372, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c199990-ff7b-5c4f-80fe-82b198cd20e4'}, {'abstract': '“At the Edge of the World,” at the Whitney, is an effective if incomplete reintroduction to the work of Lyonel Feininger, an American-born artist who was a major figure of the Bauhaus.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/22/arts/design/lyonel-feininger-show-at-the-whitney-review.html', 'snippet': '“At the Edge of the World,” at the Whitney, is an effective if incomplete reintroduction to the work of Lyonel Feininger, an American-born artist who was a major figure of the Bauhaus.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Talent moves in mysterious ways, often not according to the dictates of the artists who possess it or the art experts who seek to define and categorize it.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/arts/22FEININGER/22FEININGER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 817, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/arts/22FEININGER/22FEININGER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/22/arts/22FEININGER/22FEININGER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Modernist Who Thrived at the Margins of Painting', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Modernist Who Thrived At the Margins of Painting', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Whitney Museum of American Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feininger, Lyonel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-21T23:27:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roberta Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roberta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/52efb752-4af9-5ae3-b73a-8e79a64f3ff8', 'word_count': 1370, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52efb752-4af9-5ae3-b73a-8e79a64f3ff8'}, {'abstract': '“Fire in Babylon” is a history of the West Indies’ dominance of international cricket in the 1970s and ’80s and the symbolic weight its teams carried in a post-colonial era.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/22/movies/fire-in-babylon-on-west-indies-and-cricket-review.html', 'snippet': '“Fire in Babylon” is a history of the West Indies’ dominance of international cricket in the 1970s and ’80s and the symbolic weight its teams carried in a post-colonial era.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For his documentary “Fire in Babylon,” a history of the West Indian dominance of international cricket in the 1970s and ’80s and of the symbolic weight its teams carried in a post-colonial era, Stevan Riley makes use of a variety of beguiling components. There is archival match footage, unfamiliar and exotic to the American viewer. There is an unusually charismatic and authoritative group of talking heads, including former star players like Michael Holding, Gordon Greenidge and Vivian Richards. And there are breaks for cricket songs by reggae and calypso musicians, most notably Lord Short Shirt’s “Vivian Richards,” a lilting, evocative tribute to that legendary batsman.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/arts/BABYLON-4-SUB/BABYLON-4-SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/17/arts/BABYLON-4-SUB/BABYLON-4-SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/arts/BABYLON-4-SUB/BABYLON-4-SUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/17/arts/BABYLON-4-SUB/BABYLON-4-SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/17/arts/BABYLON-4-SUB/BABYLON-4-SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Look at West Indies Cricket', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': "Movie Review | 'Fire in Babylon'", 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cricket (Game)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-21T23:39:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Hale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/05ee4a39-f34c-5125-abb6-6dbf5edca05a', 'word_count': 339, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05ee4a39-f34c-5125-abb6-6dbf5edca05a'}, {'abstract': '“Singham” is about a super-tough village-born cop named Bajirao Singham, with bulging muscles and rock-hard morals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/22/movies/singham-a-bollywood-cop-film-review.html', 'snippet': '“Singham” is about a super-tough village-born cop named Bajirao Singham, with bulging muscles and rock-hard morals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'According to “Singham,” a fists-of-steel throwback of a Bollywood film, India suffers from three things: “pollution, population and corruption.” As for the first two, well, what to do? For corruption, though, the movie has a solution: Bajirao Singham (Ajay Devgn), a superman cop grown in village soil, with bulging muscles and rock-hard morals.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/movies/22singhamspan/22singhamspan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/22/movies/22singhamspan/22singhamspan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/movies/22singhamspan/22singham-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/movies/22singhamspan/22singhamspan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/22/movies/22singhamspan/22singhamspan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Cop Meets Bollywood', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': "Movie Review | 'Singham'", 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-21T23:48:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Saltz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saltz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b952691-8290-57bf-b45a-6b9dacc0c9d7', 'word_count': 339, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b952691-8290-57bf-b45a-6b9dacc0c9d7'}, {'abstract': 'More San Francisco property owners are turning their apartments and condos into short-term rentals for tourists.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/22/us/22bchomes.html', 'snippet': 'More San Francisco property owners are turning their apartments and condos into short-term rentals for tourists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last year, Pamela Kelley went to her landlord with a business proposition: She would move out of her rent-controlled apartment in the Russian Hill neighborhood of San Francisco if the owner agreed to turn the unit into a vacation rental and pay Ms. Kelley to manage it.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/us/22BCHOMES_span/22BCHOMES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/22/us/22BCHOMES_span/22BCHOMES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/us/22BCHOMES_span/22BCHOMES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'th