'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T00:15:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jesse Hirsch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jesse', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hirsch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0e2bf49-a876-5bd8-9546-acd4c7256484', 'word_count': 840, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0e2bf49-a876-5bd8-9546-acd4c7256484'}, {'abstract': '“The limestone and granite Church of Scientology in midtown Manhattan is located just northwest of Times Square, at 227 West 46th Street.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/22/books/review/excerpt-inside-scientology-by-janet-reitman.html', 'snippet': '“The limestone and granite Church of Scientology in midtown Manhattan is located just northwest of Times Square, at 227 West 46th Street.”', 'lead_paragraph': "Introduction: The World's Fastest-Growing Religion", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Inside Scientology’', 'kicker': 'Excerpt', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T00:20:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Janet Reitman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Janet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reitman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'First Chapter', '_id': 'nyt://article/76ca4c7d-30c3-5654-af7e-200fc3357958', 'word_count': 2564, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76ca4c7d-30c3-5654-af7e-200fc3357958'}, {'abstract': 'Two books examine the power that bountiful cash has bestowed on Scientology and the Roman Catholic Church.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/24/books/review/inside-scientology-and-render-unto-rome-book-review.html', 'snippet': 'Two books examine the power that bountiful cash has bestowed on Scientology and the Roman Catholic Church.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We do not need these books to tell us that money and religion make for a poisonous combination. But it is of some interest to see that ancient truth confirmed in both a church as relatively new as Scientology and one as ancient as Roman Catholicism. Even religious leaders develop a certain swagger when they know they are backed by bundles of cash. When a French court fined Scientology nearly a million dollars, one of its officials shrugged that off as “chump change.” And when the Vatican ran a deficit of nearly 2.4 million euros in 2007, an Italian journalist familiar with the church’s finances dismissed the debt as “chopped liver.” Chump change or chopped liver, both churches have bigger sums they can get to and use, and few outsiders are given a look at how they do it. These two books trace the cash source of theological confidence. ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/books/review/Wills-1/Wills-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 336, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/24/books/review/Wills-1/Wills-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 336}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/books/review/Wills-1/Wills-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/books/review/Wills-1/Wills-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/24/books/review/Wills-1/Wills-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Scientologists, Catholics and More Money Than God', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'More Money Than God', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hubbard, L Ron', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Church of Scientology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion-State Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T00:21:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Garry Wills', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Garry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wills', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/99bcab6d-afa4-504f-84b5-5fadc1445096', 'word_count': 2480, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99bcab6d-afa4-504f-84b5-5fadc1445096'}, {'abstract': 'A suit over a test to be marketed by 3M has escalated into a legal morass ensnaring 3M’s chief executive, Britain’s secretary of defense and a Washington lawyer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/22/business/in-3m-case-lawsuits-and-intrigue-over-a-medical-test.html', 'snippet': 'A suit over a test to be marketed by 3M has escalated into a legal morass ensnaring 3M’s chief executive, Britain’s secretary of defense and a Washington lawyer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is a legal scrap with tabloid sensibilities: extortion charges, libel claims, British royalty — and a prominent American protagonist, the 3M Corporation, purveyor of staples like Scotch tape and Post-it notes.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lawsuits and Intrigue Over 3M Diagnostic Test', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lawsuits and Intrigue Over 3M Diagnostic Test', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests (Medical)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Lanny J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Buckley, George W', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fox, Liam', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': '3M Company', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Methicillin-Resistant Staphylococcus Aureus', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T00:21:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Barry Meier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Barry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Meier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9fcd053-6d0e-5091-8650-f8558de89f67', 'word_count': 1111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9fcd053-6d0e-5091-8650-f8558de89f67'}, {'abstract': 'Senfronia Thompson has spent nearly 40 years in the Texas State House of Representatives fighting for the underserved, so her close ties to certain industries seem out of character.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/22/us/22ttthompson.html', 'snippet': 'Senfronia Thompson has spent nearly 40 years in the Texas State House of Representatives fighting for the underserved, so her close ties to certain industries seem out of character.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When a special interest group tried to defeat Representative Senfronia Thompson’s insurance bill this session with a flier condemning the “nanny state” and showing an infant suckling a woman’s breast, Ms. Thompson could not contain her outrage. In one of her famously impassioned speeches —\xa0between threats to bloody noses — she blasted what she called the objectification, disrespect and “violence” toward women, slamming her fist so hard against the lectern that her bracelet shattered. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/us/22TTTHOMPSON/22TTTHOMPSON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 611, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/us/22TTTHOMPSON/22TTTHOMPSON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/22/us/22TTTHOMPSON/22TTTHOMPSON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Defending ‘Little Dogs’ but Playing Both Sides', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Defending ‘Little Dogs’ But Playing Both Sides', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thompson, Senfronia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T00:26:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily Ramshaw', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ramshaw', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a667674-c92f-5ef5-938c-34104c29e703', 'word_count': 1404, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a667674-c92f-5ef5-938c-34104c29e703'}, {'abstract': 'What the citizens of Los Angeles discovered when they left their cars at home.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/carmageddons-big-surprise/', 'snippet': 'What the citizens of Los Angeles discovered when they left their cars at home.', 'lead_paragraph': 'So, they shut down a 10-mile stretch of one of the world’s busiest freeways for repair last weekend, in the nation’s most driver-stressed metropolis, and gave it a scary name — Carmageddon. Predictions were that Los Angeles would look like Mike Huckabee’s arteries before he lost a hundred pounds, and that chaos and road rage would reign under the tired sunlight of the Southland. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Carmageddon’s Big Surprise', 'kicker': 'Timothy Egan', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T00:30:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Timothy Egan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Timothy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Egan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5afd1a8-02d1-5325-9304-c5662864039b', 'word_count': 978, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5afd1a8-02d1-5325-9304-c5662864039b'}, {'abstract': 'After a series of embarrassing revelations about the prince, Buckingham Palace said he would “relinquish” his position promoting British businesses overseas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/22/world/europe/22britain.html', 'snippet': 'After a series of embarrassing revelations about the prince, Buckingham Palace said he would “relinquish” his position promoting British businesses overseas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Prince Andrew will resign as an ambassador for British businesses abroad, Buckingham Palace said Thursday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Prince Andrew Is Ending His Role as Business Envoy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Prince Andrew Is Ending His Role As Business Envoy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Royal Family', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Buckingham Palace', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Andrew, Duke of York', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nazarbayev, Nursultan A', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Epstein, Jeffrey E (1953- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T00:31:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e79f528-3d8c-5d01-922f-e76805b2f021', 'word_count': 201, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e79f528-3d8c-5d01-922f-e76805b2f021'}, {'abstract': 'The big drug maker Gilead Sciences has taken an important step in making AIDS drugs more available worldwide. But obstacles remain.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/21/sharing-patents-to-wipe-out-aids/', 'snippet': 'The big drug maker Gilead Sciences has taken an important step in making AIDS drugs more available worldwide. But obstacles remain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not since the announcement in 1996 that antiretroviral therapy could effectively control H.I.V. has there been a season of AIDS news as hopeful as this one.\xa0 Trials of a new microbicide have brought positive results; ongoing studies of circumcision are showing that it gives strong, lasting, protection; a man has been cured of H.I.V. infection  and new animal and clinical trials are raising hopes that he won’t be alone. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sharing Patents to Wipe Out AIDS', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Acquired Immune Deficiency Syndrome', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Generic Brands and Products', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inventions and Patents', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Third World and Developing Countries', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gilead Sciences Incorporated', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Medicines Patent Pool Foundation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Institutes of Health', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Unitaid', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T00:35:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tina Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6271c