e': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/324e9535-52fe-538a-bb6a-a99ced1e9a29', 'word_count': 296, 'uri': 'nyt://article/324e9535-52fe-538a-bb6a-a99ced1e9a29'}, {'abstract': 'Much of the country is in the throes of a heat wave, and the suffering is shared by humans, animals and crops alike.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/22/opinion/22fri4.html', 'snippet': 'Much of the country is in the throes of a heat wave, and the suffering is shared by humans, animals and crops alike.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Much of the country — and now the Northeast — is in the throes of an excessive heat alert. If a heat wave were a storm, like a blizzard or a hurricane, many people would have taken emergency measures, hunkering down, battening the hatches. But a heat wave comes with cloudless days, creating the illusion that it is merely a little more summer than they counted on. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Is It Called a Wave?', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Why Is It Called a Wave?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Northeastern States (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Temperature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T01:52:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d93e428-3e71-5314-bfd2-837deb2827b2', 'word_count': 292, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d93e428-3e71-5314-bfd2-837deb2827b2'}, {'abstract': 'Voters should pay close attention to how Representative Michele Bachmann deals with her migraines.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/22/opinion/22warner.html', 'snippet': 'Voters should pay close attention to how Representative Michele Bachmann deals with her migraines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Washington', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/opinion/22warner-oped/22warner-oped-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 482, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/22/opinion/22warner-oped/22warner-oped-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 482}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/opinion/22warner-oped/22warner-oped-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/opinion/22warner-oped/22warner-oped-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/22/opinion/22warner-oped/22warner-oped-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Me, Michele and Our Migraines', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Me, Michele and Our Migraines', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Migraine Headaches', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bachmann, Michele M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T01:58:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judith Warner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judith', '