'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T02:13:31+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/202cd239-d4cf-5cf8-b60e-d7ab6e2b4f1e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/202cd239-d4cf-5cf8-b60e-d7ab6e2b4f1e'}, {'abstract': 'A humorously intended campaign aimed at men on the soothing effects milk might have on PMS riffed on a similar campaign in 2005 — before social media flexed its muscle.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/22/business/media/milk-campaign-withdrawn-amid-charges-of-sexism.html', 'snippet': 'A humorously intended campaign aimed at men on the soothing effects milk might have on PMS riffed on a similar campaign in 2005 — before social media flexed its muscle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A\u2002CAMPAIGN by a milk marketer to address the serious subject of premenstrual syndrome in a humorous fashion — by focusing on how men purportedly suffer from its effects along with women — is being ended early after an outpouring of criticism and comments about the tone of the ads and even a parody on FunnyorDie.com.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/business/adco/adco-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 708, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/business/adco/adco-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/22/business/adco/adco-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Milk Campaign Ended Amid Social Media Firestorm', 'kicker': 'Advertising', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Milk Campaign Ended Amid Social Media Firestorm', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goodby, Silverstein & Partners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Milk', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T02:18:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/959a5d77-d600-5768-ace0-61303bbf0a8f', 'word_count': 974, 'uri': 'nyt://article/959a5d77-d600-5768-ace0-61303bbf0a8f'}, {'abstract': 'Even if Washington and Brussels succeed in avoiding immediate financial catastrophe, the deals being made will surely make the broader economic slump worse.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/22/opinion/22krugman.html', 'snippet': 'Even if Washington and Brussels succeed in avoiding immediate financial catastrophe, the deals being made will surely make the broader economic slump worse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'These are interesting times — and I mean that in the worst way. Right now we’re looking at not one but two looming crises, either of which could produce a global disaster. In the United States, right-wing fanatics in Congress may block a necessary rise in the debt ceiling, potentially wreaking havoc in world financial markets. Meanwhile, if the plan just agreed to by European heads of state fails to calm markets, we could see falling dominoes all across southern Europe — which would also wreak havoc in world financial markets.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Lesser Depression', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Lesser Depression', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T02:19:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f019fe5-0605-57ab-a453-655a4c2b64aa', 'word_count': 811, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f019fe5-0605-57ab-a453-655a4c2b64aa'}, {'abstract': 'Melvin Hershberger was seeking new ways to grow produce when a crash killed him and four other Amish farmers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/22/nyregion/among-victims-an-amish-farmer-quick-to-adapt.html', 'snippet': 'Melvin Hershberger was seeking new ways to grow produce when a crash killed him and four other Amish farmers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JASPER, N.Y. — For several golden years, Melvin Hershberger lived the Amish dream. He rose early with his wife and brood of children, who now number a dozen, to tend to the family’s goat herd, twice a day milking 70 goats by hand. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/nyregion/AMISH/AMISH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/nyregion/AMISH/AMISH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/22/nyregion/AMISH/AMISH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Among Victims, an Amish Farmer Quick to Adapt', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Among Victims, an Amish Farmer Quick to Adapt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hershberger, Melvin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AMISH', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Farmers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T02:22:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cara Buckley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f612ba19-8c33-5b2e-a6c3-14623200d971', 'word_count': 835, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f612ba19-8c33-5b2e-a6c3-14623200d971'}, {'abstract': 'Express Scripts’ offer for Medco Health Solutions has the potential for big savings and antitrust questions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/22/business/express-scripts-bid-for-medco-health-carries-risks.html', 'snippet': 'Express Scripts’ offer for Medco Health Solutions has the potential for big savings and antitrust questions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The $29.1 billion cash and stock offer by Express Scripts for Medco Health Solutions is not just one of the largest deals of the year. It is also a huge antitrust roll of the dice. The combination would create a behemoth in the pharmacy benefits management industry. So much so, it looks like a provocation to trustbusters.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/business/VIEWS/VIEWS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 973, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Express Scripts’ Bid for Medco Health Carries Risks', 'kicker': 'Reuters Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Merger Bid Raises Antitrust Issues', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Medco Health Solutions Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Express Scripts Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T02:25:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Cyran and Christopher Swann', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cyran', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Swann', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/670a76fd-85b2-5b05-bed4-3547570c7479', 'word_count': 767, 'uri': 'nyt://article/670a76fd-85b2-5b05-bed4-3547570c7479'}, {'abstract': 'Offense was in short supply as C. C. Sabathia stifled the Rays with his slider, and James Shields humbled the Yankees with his changeup in the finale of their four-game series.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/22/sports/baseball/rays-edge-yankees-in-duel-between-sabathia-and-shields.html', 'snippet': 'Offense was in short supply as C. C. Sabathia stifled the Rays with his slider, and James Shields humbled the Yankees with his changeup in the finale of their four-game series.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ST. PETERSBURG, Fla. — From C. C. Sabathia’s vacation in the Bahamas to James Shields’s sojourn to the All-Star Game in Arizona, there exists plenty of evidence that confirms that they have, in fact, left Yankee Stadium, where on July 10 they engaged in a captivating battle, each pitching a complete game without allowing an earned run. Playing on synthetic turf, not grass, and under a dome, not a bright sky, they reunited for a duel Thursday night at Tropicana Field, and it was as if they had never taken off their uniforms.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/sports/yankees/yankees-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 408, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/22/sports/yankees/yankees-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 408}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/sports/yankees/yankees-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 839, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/sports/yankees/yankees-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/22/sports/yankees/yankees-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rays Find Extra Ounce of Offense to Escape Pitching Duel', 'kicker': 'Rays 2, Yankees 1 ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rays Find Extra Ounce of Offense to Escape Pitching Duel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tampa Bay Rays', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shields, James', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sabathia, C C', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T02:25:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df97e093-d826-5c6c-9e07-082b4b612602', 'word_count': 909, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df97e093-d826-5c6c-9e07-082b4b612602'}, {'abstract': 'Lawmakers’ deficit-reduction proposals and the eventual failure of a bipartisan committee created to identify $1.2 trillion in deficit reductions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/07/22/us/politics/20110722-comparing-deficit-reduction-plans.html', 'snippet': 'Lawmakers’ deficit-reduction proposals and the eventual failure of a bipartisan committee created to identify $1.2 trillion in deficit reductions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lawmakers’ deficit-reduction proposals and the eventual failure of a bipartisan committee created to identify $1.2 trillion in deficit reductions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Plans for Reducing the Deficit', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reid, Harry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McConnell, Mitch', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T02:40:47+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/3de664ea-596a-5ace-bc12-f6ea6e3c7280', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/3de664ea-596a-5ace-bc12-f6ea6e3c7280'}, {'abstract': 'Canada’s former military commander in Afghanistan pleaded guilty to having had a sexual relationship with a subordinate and for trying to block an investigation of the affair.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/22/world/americas/22briefs-commander.html', 'snippet': 'Canada’s former military commander in Afghanistan pleaded guilty to having had a sexual relationship with a subordinate and for trying to block an investigation of the affair.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Canada’s former military commander in Afghanistan was fined about $7,400 and given a symbolic reduction in rank after pleading guilty to having had a sexual relationship with a subordinate and for trying to block an investigation of the affair. The former commander, Daniel Ménard, 45, a brigadier general, had his rank reduced to colonel by a military judge in Montreal on Thursday. But because he has retired from the military, he will retain his former rank. General Ménard had the relationship with a female master corporal under his command in Afghanistan.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/world/22briefs-menard/22briefs-menard-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 817, 'width': 496, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Canada: Penalties for Ex-Commander', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | THE AMERICAS', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Canada: Penalties for Ex-Commander', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T03:15:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d57b9ce-0dc2-51e1-b1f7-7ed2e73d2b03', 'word_count': 92, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d57b9ce-0dc2-51e1-b1f7-7ed2e73d2b03'}, {'abstract': 'As a heat wave moved east on Thursday, life around the country became an improvisation, particularly for those who toil in the heat each day, whether by choice or circumstance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/22/us/22heatintro.html', 'snippet': 'As a heat wave moved east on Thursday, life around the country became an improvisation, particularly for those who toil in the heat each day, whether by choice or circumstance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WICHITA FALLS, Tex. — The guys who cut the grass at the parks in this north central Texas city, which has endured 30 consecutive days of triple-digit heat, stuff ice packs into their bright orange vests. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/us/Weather/Weather-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/22/us/Weather/Weather-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/us/Weather/Weather-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/us/Weather/Weather-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/22/us/Weather/Weather-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Soldiering On When the Job Is White Hot', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Frozen Bananas to Tank Tops, Heat Wave Turns Work Into Improv', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Atlanta (Ga)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kansas City (Mo)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T03:24:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manny Fernandez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fernandez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/377c476c-a4d5-5ee9-a919-137d452e7928', 'word_count': 558, 'uri': 'nyt://article/377c476c-a4d5-5ee9-a919-137d452e7928'}, {'abstract': 'For the Grant Park Orchestra, there is a certain stoic pride to having played in pounding rains, peculiar fogs, tornado scares, sudden swarms of bugs and, yes, brutal, crushing heat.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/22/us/22heatchicago.html', 'snippet': 'For the Grant Park Orchestra, there is a certain stoic pride to having played in pounding rains, peculiar fogs, tornado scares, sudden swarms of bugs and, yes, brutal, crushing heat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — When the enormous stage doors roll open for the Grant Park Orchestra’s performance, a rush of hot air surges in among the musicians. The humid heat tends to send the instruments out of tune — and in unhappily assorted directions (the metal instruments’ notes may go sharp even as the woodwinds’ go flat). And there have been moments when Mary Stolper’s flute suddenly seemed to wish, in all the sweat, to “slide right off” her face.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sweating Through Flats and Sharps', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sweating Through Flats And Sharps', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T03:24:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Monica Davey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Monica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa64d0b2-c1cd-51e7-ad06-7c151a0ed251', 'word_count': 328, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa64d0b2-c1cd-51e7-ad06-7c151a0ed251'}, {'abstract': 'The heat wasn’t enough to deter Rezwan Jahengir, a Pakistan native, from toiling away in his kebab truck in Washington. His customers, on the other hand, were not so courageous.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/22/us/22heatdc.html', 'snippet': 'The heat wasn’t enough to deter Rezwan Jahengir, a Pakistan native, from toiling away in his kebab truck in Washington. His customers, on the other hand, were not so courageous.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — When Washingtonians, hungry and drooping these days, walk up to Rezwan Jahengir’s kebab truck, they see a man who seems at home in the heat. \xa0', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/us/HEATDC/HEATDC-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/22/us/HEATDC/HEATDC-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/us/HEATDC/HEATDC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/us/HEATDC/HEATDC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/22/us/HEATDC/HEATDC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hot? Back Home, They Call This Balmy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hot? Back Home, They Call This Balmy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and C