 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T12:59:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed41869e-0678-5986-aaee-58d10fccbad0', 'word_count': 1408, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed41869e-0678-5986-aaee-58d10fccbad0'}, {'abstract': 'After nearly drowning, Cullen Jones has set his mind to conquering the water.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/24/magazine/cullen-jones-sprinter-in-a-speedo.html', 'snippet': 'After nearly drowning, Cullen Jones has set his mind to conquering the water.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The night before the men’s 4x100-meter freestyle relay at the 2008 Olympics in Beijing, Cullen Jones was in bed, not sleeping, when Michael Phelps, his megastar teammate, knocked on the door. “Michael’s like, ‘LeBron and all the N.B.A. guys are downstairs, and they want to say hi to us,’ ” Jones recalled. “I’m half asleep. I say, ‘What!?’ This is huge for me. Huge.” A group of N.B.A. players’ calling on a bunch of relay swimmers is equivalent to Obama’s dropping by a state assemblyman’s home. “So I pull on clothes and run downstairs,” Jones, who is 27, told me as he recovered after a practice on the black leather couch in his apartment in Charlotte, N.C. “Le-Bron is talking to Michael, saying: ‘Good luck. Trying to get eight gold medals? That’s crazy.’ And here I come racing in, I’m shaking guys’ hands. Then I hear LeBron go, ‘Wait, you got a brother on the team?’ ”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/magazine/24jones_span/24jones_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 378, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/24/magazine/24jones_span/24jones_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 378}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/magazine/24jones_span/mag-24jones-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/magazine/24jones_span/24jones_span-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/24/magazine/24jones_span/24jones_span-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sink and Swim', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sink and Swim', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Cullen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Swimming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T13:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth Weil', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weil', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6751c29-302f-5a14-9bb7-426ade1b665e', 'word_count': 904, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6751c29-302f-5a14-9bb7-426ade1b665e'}, {'abstract': 'In Lee Tamahori’s “Devil’s Double,” Dominic Cooper plays Saddam Hussein’s nihilistic son, Uday, as well as Latif Yahia, who served as his body double.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/24/movies/the-devils-double-the-shoes-of-a-psychopath.html', 'snippet': 'In Lee Tamahori’s “Devil’s Double,” Dominic Cooper plays Saddam Hussein’s nihilistic son, Uday, as well as Latif Yahia, who served as his body double.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT’S hard to conceive of too many narratives in which Saddam Hussein might emerge as a second-tier villain. But in “The Devil’s Double” he is portrayed as a man who at least operated according to his own narrow code of loyalty and warped ethical compass, while his nihilistic son Uday is pure, unchecked evil.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/arts/24DEVIL1/24DEVIL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/24/arts/24DEVIL1/24DEVIL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/arts/24DEVIL1/24DEVIL1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/arts/24DEVIL1/24DEVIL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/24/arts/24DEVIL1/24DEVIL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Stepping Into the Shoes of a Psychopath', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stepping Into