ideo/5ff7d54b-e54a-5325-b891-4c4a16014a9e'}, {'abstract': 'In “Rise of the Planet of the Apes,” Fox revisits a theme that has generally been good to the studio: the vengeance of nature against perfidious man.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/22/in-man-vs-nature-fox-sides-with-the-furry-guys/', 'snippet': 'In “Rise of the Planet of the Apes,” Fox revisits a theme that has generally been good to the studio: the vengeance of nature against perfidious man.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN DIEGO — “We’re rooting for the apes here,” noted Damon Lindelof, the co-creator of “Lost,” but employed on Thursday as the host of 20th Century Fox’s presentation to the Comic-Con crowd of some upcoming films. Mr. Lindelof, who voiced the usual nostalgia about his visits to Comic-Con back in the old days — that would be the mid-1990s — was referring to the distinctly pro-simian sentiment underlying “Rise of the Planet of the Apes,” which is set to open early next month.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Man Vs. Nature, Fox Sides With the Furry Guys', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comic-Con (Convention)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Franco, James', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lindelof, Damon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Serkis, Andy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twentieth Century Fox', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T14:45:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cieply', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cieply', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68db785d-478c-5cbb-a70c-d1d092f7fdaf', 'word_count': 285, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68db785d-478c-5cbb-a70c-d1d092f7fdaf'}, {'abstract': 'The safety agency said that owners reported leaks that caused oil to coat their cars’ tires.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/22/n-h-t-s-a-investigates-4400-lotus-elises-for-oil-cooler-leaks/', 'snippet': 'The safety agency said that owners reported leaks that caused oil to coat their cars’ tires.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The National Highway Traffic Safety Administration is investigating oil-cooler leaks on 4,400 Lotus Elise sports cars from the 2005-6 model years after receiving complaints from owners saying that a tire became coated with oil, causing handling problems.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'N.H.T.S.A. Investigates 4,400 Lotus Elises for Oil-Cooler Leaks', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recalls and Bans of Products', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Highway Traffic Safety Administration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T14:52:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/658156c6-ce87-51cf-9428-fc245fec017a', 'word_count': 525, 'uri': 'nyt://article/658156c6-ce87-51cf-9428-fc245fec017a'}, {'abstract': 'As of April, new New York City heating oil regulations require that by 2015 the buildings switch from No. 6 oil, the cheapest and dirtiest fuel available, to No. 4.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/24/realestate/10000-buildings-get-the-word-on-dirty-fuel.html', 'snippet': 'As of April, new New York City heating oil regulations require that by 2015 the buildings switch from No. 6 oil, the cheapest and dirtiest fuel available, to No. 4.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT was the sight of apartment buildings in New York City belching plumes of black smoke into the sky that spurred Diane Nardone into action.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/realestate/24COVER_SPAN/24COVER_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/24/realestate/24COVER_SPAN/24COVER_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/realestate/24COVER_SPAN/24COVER_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/realestate/24COVER_SPAN/24COVER_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/24/realestate/24COVER_SPAN/24COVER_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Going Green in New York: One Co-op’s Story', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '10,000 Buildings Get the Word', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Heating', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T14:58:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivian S. Toy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivian', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Toy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/551ea0b8-760a-5a25-a3db-06a619580d98', 'word_count': 1980, 'uri': 'nyt://article/551ea0b8-760a-5a25-a3db-06a619580d98'}, {'abstract': 'The plan to slash the budget of the Office of Congressional Ethics failed Friday by a 302-to-102 vote.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/22/plan-to-cut-budget-of-ethics-office-fails-house-vote/', 'snippet': 'The plan to slash the budget of the Office of Congressional Ethics failed Friday by a 302-to-102 vote.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The plan to slash the budget of the Office of Congressional Ethics failed Friday by a 302-to-102 vote, after House members were forced to go on the record instead of deciding the matter more anonymously by a voice vote. But the proposal still gave critics of the three-year-old office an opportunity to air their grievances on the House floor.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Plan to Cut Budget of Ethics Office Fails House Vote', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Institutional)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Watt, Melvin L', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T