to benefit Slow Food. Tickets are $25 for Slow Food members and $35 for others.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Weekend Fare', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T16:06:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bao Ong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bao', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f7de3b3-8394-5c28-b3d9-7dcfb2b282e7', 'word_count': 519, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f7de3b3-8394-5c28-b3d9-7dcfb2b282e7'}, {'abstract': 'An interactive family tree covering 15 generations of the Van Dusen family, among the earliest Europeans to settle in New York City.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/07/22/nyregion/20110722-family-tree.html', 'snippet': 'An interactive family tree covering 15 generations of the Van Dusen family, among the earliest Europeans to settle in New York City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An interactive family tree covering 15 generations of the Van Dusen family, among the earliest Europeans to settle in New York City.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Van Dusens Through History', 'kicker': 'In the Family', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genealogy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Van Dusen Family', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T16:13:47+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'New York', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/07b9bf7c-d4c3-5506-bf10-a6a7a2c2f0f4', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/07b9bf7c-d4c3-5506-bf10-a6a7a2c2f0f4'}, {'abstract': 'On the brutal climb to Alpe d’Huez, Andy Schleck of Luxembourg battled his way into the Tour de France lead, despite Alberto Contador’s desperate attempt to challenge him.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/23/sports/2011-tour-de-france-andy-schleck-grabs-overall-lead.html', 'snippet': 'On the brutal climb to Alpe d’Huez, Andy Schleck of Luxembourg battled his way into the Tour de France lead, despite Alberto Contador’s desperate attempt to challenge him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALPE d’HUEZ, France — After 2,105 miles and nearly three weeks of racing, through three perilously steep climbs into the Alps, the Tour de France will be decided Saturday in a 26-mile sprint through Grenoble. This is like deciding a marathon with a 100-meter dash.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/23/sports/TOUR/TOUR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 365, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/23/sports/TOUR/TOUR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 365}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/23/sports/TOUR/TOUR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 736, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/23/sports/TOUR/TOUR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/23/sports/TOUR/TOUR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Afte