y.html', 'snippet': 'Struggling countries in the euro zone need to become competitive with Germany, the bloc’s powerhouse, but progress is slow.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IF the economies of the bailed-out countries in the euro zone are ever going to prosper again, they will have to somehow regain competitiveness with Germany, the dominant economy in the zone.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Striving for Productivity, Chasing Germany', 'kicker': 'Off the Charts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Striving for Productivity, Chasing Germany', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Productivity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T17:35:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Floyd Norris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Norris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/30748bd4-4801-55f7-808c-2fea52818686', 'word_count': 455, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30748bd4-4801-55f7-808c-2fea52818686'}, {'abstract': 'The charitable lead trust is a tool used by the rich to pass on money to heirs while avoiding certain taxes, but establishing such a trust is complicated.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/23/your-money/estate-planning/charitable-lead-trusts-draw-renewed-interest.html', 'snippet': 'The charitable lead trust is a tool used by the rich to pass on money to heirs while avoiding certain taxes, but establishing such a trust is complicated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JACQUELINE KENNEDY ONASSIS is remembered for many things — as a first lady, a preservationist, a fashion icon. But her legend stands tall in a far more esoteric realm: her will is revered in the world of trusts and estates, too. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/23/your-money/estate-planning/23wealth-image/23wealth-image-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Trust Surges, Heirs and Taxes in Mind, but Mind the Details', 'kicker': 'Wealth Matters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Trust Surges, Heirs and Taxes in Mind, but Mind the Details', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wills and Estates', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'High Net Worth Individuals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Financial Planners', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T17:37:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'subsection_name': 'Estate Planning', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af3ca42f-d988-55c4-8963-099ec1325d14', 'word_count': 1309, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af3ca42f-d988-55c4-8963-099ec1325d14'}, {'abstract': 'The designer-turned-artist talks about the emotions and commitments behind his shocking new installation, “Make It Hard.”', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/22/asked-answered-helmut-lang/', 'snippet': 'The designer-turned-artist talks about the emotions and commitments behind his shocking new installation, “Make It Hard.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Back in 2008, when Helmut Lang installed a busted up disco ball on the floor of the Journal Gallery in Brooklyn, he explained that, in his mind anyway, the piece related to the Janus mythology — looking back and moving forward. “It’s also about transitions and new beginnings, representing time as one half respects the past and the other one looks into the future,” he said. But with his new installation at the Fireplace Project in East Hampton, N.Y., it appears that the past is no longer an issue for the designer who took what turned out to be a permanent hiatus from fashion in 2005 and has been working full time as an artist pretty much ever since. “Make It Hard,” as the show is called, comprises about 20 pillar-like sculptures, which Lang created after he shredded the thousands of pieces that remained in his archive. Sad as it may be to think about all of those wasted moleskin coats, lace and rubber dresses and motocross pants, “Make It Hard” is a poignant realization of Lang’s long-held conviction that fashion and art have become one. On the eve of the opening, Lang talked to The Moment about art, the passage of time and why there will never be another Helmut Lang sample sale ever again.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Asked & Answered | Helmut Lang', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T17:38:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alix Browne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alix', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Browne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a105b035-2f6a-502d-ab5b-7fc342819e83', 'word_count': 989, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a105b035-2f6a-502d-ab5b-7fc342819e83'}, {'abstract': 'The ruling was the third time in six years that a court threw out a new S.E.C. rule because the agency failed to adequately assess its economic effects.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/23/business/appeals-court-rules-against-sec-on-proxy-materials.html', 'snippet': 'The ruling was the third time in six years that a court threw out a new S.E.C. rule because the agency failed to adequately assess its economic effects.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — A federal appeals court panel on Friday delivered a sharp rebuke to the Securities and Exchange Commission by throwing out a recently approved regulation that would have made it easier for shareholders to oust corporate directors.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Appeals Court Rejects S.E.C. Rule on Access to Proxy Materials', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Appeals Court Rejects S.E.C. Rule on Access to Proxy Materials', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boards of Directors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T17:38:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wyatt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wyatt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/905f25ef-dc71-5974-8ff7-71ad18434b45', 'word_count': 706, 'uri': 'nyt://article/905f25ef-dc71-5974-8ff7-71ad18434b45'}, {'abstract': 'Lexus will unveil the next generation of its GS midsize luxury sedan at Pebble Beach, on the Monterey Peninsula, during the collector car festivities there next month.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/22/wheelies-the-midsize-on-monterey-edition/', 'snippet': 'Lexus will unveil the next generation of its GS midsize luxury sedan at Pebble Beach, on the Monterey Peninsula, during the collector car festivities there next month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In which we bring you motoring news from around the Web:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wheelies: The Midsize-on-Monterey Edition', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marchionne, Sergio', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chrysler LLC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Daimler AG', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fiat SpA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'LEXUS DIVISION OF TOYOTA MOTOR SALES USA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mercedes-Benz', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toyota Motor Corp', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Volkswagen AG', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pebble Beach (Calif)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T17:41:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2bb568fa-8962-579c-840e-14f401f26404', 'word_count': 388, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2bb568fa-8962-579c-840e-14f401f26404'}, {'abstract': 'For Rachel Shteir, author of “The Steal: A Cultural History of Shoplifting,” the object of her desire was a 1950s-style wallet from Pier 1 Imports.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/24/fashion/author-rachel-shteirs-clamshell-wallet-possessed.html', 'snippet': 'For Rachel Shteir, author of “The Steal: A Cultural History of Shoplifting,” the object of her desire was a 1950s-style wallet from Pier 1 Imports.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THIS may surprise you (or not, given the mercury’s recent leaps), but in the United States, the weather disasters that take the biggest toll on human life are not hurricanes, tornadoes, floods or blizzards. They are heat waves: slow, steady and quiet, wreaking havoc under the cover of a cheery blue sky.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/fashion/24POSSESSED_SPAN/24POSSESSED_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/24/fashion/24POSSESSED_SPAN/24POSSESSED_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/fashion/24POSSESSED_SPAN/24POSSESSED-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 723, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/fashion/24POSSESSED_SPAN/24POSSESSED_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'t