s Confirms Diesel-Powered Chevrolet Cruze for 2013', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Cars (Compact, Subcompact and Microcars)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chevrolet Division of General Motors Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North America', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T17:49:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Stenquist', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stenquist', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4d66596-4d76-50c0-b9b3-fca5a6d7374b', 'word_count': 170, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4d66596-4d76-50c0-b9b3-fca5a6d7374b'}, {'abstract': "Scenes from along West 52nd Street in Hell's Kitchen include horses at rest, kids and dogs at play and men at work.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/realestate/100000000960665/west-52nd-street.html', 'snippet': "Scenes from along West 52nd Street in Hell's Kitchen include horses at rest, kids and dogs at play and men at work.", 'lead_paragraph': "Scenes from along West 52nd Street in Hell's Kitchen include horses at rest, kids and dogs at play and men at work.", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/realestate/video-blocks52/video-blocks52-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/22/realestate/video-blocks52/video-blocks52-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/realestate/video-blocks52/video-blocks52-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/22/realestate/video-blocks52/video-blocks52-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Block by Block: West 52nd Street', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T17:49:37+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'Judy Tong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/7d3cc66e-6c91-5660-82b1-db5c2f3ef654', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/7d3cc66e-6c91-5660-82b1-db5c2f3ef654'}, {'abstract': 'It seems not a week goes by without some presence of vampires on the graphic books list.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/22/graphic-books-best-sellers-more-vampires/', 'snippet': 'It seems not a week goes by without some presence of vampires on the graphic books list.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It seems not a week goes by without some presence of vampires on the graphic books lists. The manga list has three titles, Volume 5 of Rosario + Vampire: Season Two, about a school filled with creates of the night (bloodsuckers and werewolves), Volume 12 of Vampire Knight (about an academy whose night students are Dracula-wannabes) and Volume 10 of Dance in the Vampire Bund (about a once safe haven for vampires off the coast of Japan). Another variation of these vampire chronicles comes in “Blood Work,” which enters our hardcover list at No. 1 this week. The book is by Kim Harrison, whose “Hollows” novels are about a vampire and a witch who solve crimes. This original graphic novel delves into the early days of their partnership. Could this be the next AMC original series?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Graphic Books Best Sellers: More Vampires', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Graphic Novels', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T17:53:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Gene Gustines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': 'Gene', 'lastname': 'Gustines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/47ca8139-8f3a-54e7-bd58-045e7c2ce879', 'word_count': 154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47ca8139-8f3a-54e7-bd58-045e7c2ce879'}, {'abstract': 'A model vindicated.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/22/this-age-of-hicks/', 'snippet': 'A model vindicated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Matt Yglesias links to a libertarian blogger admitting some self-doubt after the failure of high inflation to materialize as predicted. I would offer a friendly word of caution to Mr. Lee: once he starts admitting the existence of contrary evidence, he’s on the road to becoming another Bruce Bartlett, who has become a moderate Democrat in all but name.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'This Age of Hicks', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T17:53:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c13b7b7f-55ff-576c-8325-fec9ff375f6f', 'word_count': 368, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c13b7b7f-55ff-576c-8325-fec9ff375f6f'}, {'abstract': 'Worlds collide between Eighth and 12th Avenues: art and commerce, rich and poor, high and low, Stiles Farmers Market and Starbucks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/24/realestate/the-grit-and-glamour-of-west-52nd-street-block-by-block.html', 'snippet': 'Worlds collide between Eighth and 12th Avenues: art and commerce, rich and poor, high and low, Stiles Farmers Market and Starbucks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AT quitting time one recent Wednesday just before the afternoon commuter rush, the clip-clop of hooves came lazily up the West Side Highway. Without direction from his driver, the carriage horse turned right on West 52nd Street. He was heading back to the barn.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/realestate/24BLOCK_SPAN/24BLOCK_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 375, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/24/realestate/24BLOCK_SPAN/24BLOCK_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 375}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/realestate/24BLOCK_SPAN/24BLOCK_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 375, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/realestate/24BLOCK_SPAN/24BLOCK_SPA