ng ready. But for those of us who routinely travel with our same-sex partners (legal or otherwise), the law, which goes into effect today, won’t automatically eradicate awkward moments on those occasions when you’d hope to be treated just like every other married couple.", 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/travel/24SUBPERSONALJOURNEYS/24SUBPERSONALJOURNEYS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 942, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/travel/24SUBPERSONALJOURNEYS/24SUBPERSONALJOURNEYS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/24/travel/24SUBPERSONALJOURNEYS/24SUBPERSONALJOURNEYS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After Gay Marriage, the Check-In Dance', 'kicker': 'Personal Journeys', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Gay Marriage, the Check-In Dance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'HOTELS AND MOTELS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T18:55:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Marcus', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Marcus', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b7da424-87b2-57c1-a3e8-11cf4b43a7a8', 'word_count': 1289, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b7da424-87b2-57c1-a3e8-11cf4b43a7a8'}, {'abstract': 'Guimarães, a 2012 European Capital of Culture, is being reborn as a locus of youth and contemporary arts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/24/travel/guimaraes-becoming-a-cultural-center-of-portugal.html', 'snippet': 'Guimarães, a 2012 European Capital of Culture, is being reborn as a locus of youth and contemporary arts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE earthy appeal of Guimarães, Portugal, was plentifully evident during a recent visit to Adega dos Caquinhos, a small, family-run restaurant in the city center. Profanity, served up in the warm, open-throated intonations of this region of northern Portugal, is as much a part of the menu as the veal chop or tripe stew. The matronly but sharp-tongued owner, Augusta Ribeiro, routinely dresses down customers for refusing wine, and once, I was told, she called a man impotent for asking for hot sauce. When I stopped in for lunch with Rui Torrinha, a local cultural organizer, it wasn’t long before he was being harangued for his vegetarianism.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/travel/24NEXT1_span/24NEXT1_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/24/travel/24NEXT1_span/24NEXT1_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/travel/24NEXT1_span/Next-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/travel/24NEXT1_span/24NEXT1_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/24/travel/24NEXT1_span/24NEXT1_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Arts Take Root in Portugal’s ‘Cradle City’', 'kicker': 'Next Stop', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Arts Take Root in Portugal’s ‘Cradle City’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guimaraes (Portugal)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T18:55:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charly Wilder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charly', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0cf160e9-18d7-5aca-8670-2c86c902e984', 'word_count': 1543, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0cf160e9-18d7-5aca-8670-2c86c902e984'}, {'abstract': 'A retro bing sutt, or traditional cafe that serves Western-style breakfast dishes and drinks all day.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/24/travel/restaurant-report-capital-cafe-hong-kong.html', 'snippet': 'A retro bing sutt, or traditional cafe that serves Western-style breakfast dishes and drinks all day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No one comes to Hong Kong for eggs and French toast. But one of the most memorable Hong Kong experiences is dining at a bing sutt (literally, “ice room”), a traditional cafe that serves Western-style breakfast dishes and drinks all day.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/travel/24BITES_SPAN/24BITES_SPAN-articleLa