'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cricket (Game)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rugby (Game)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weight Lifting', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T19:09:14+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/cccdb4cf-493d-5098-bae2-b49eb3cc2297', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/cccdb4cf-493d-5098-bae2-b49eb3cc2297'}, {'abstract': 'Retired racecar transporters, with their connection to famous marques, have begun to spur more collector interest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/24/automobiles/collecting-racing-transporters.html', 'snippet': 'Retired racecar transporters, with their connection to famous marques, have begun to spur more collector interest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MILLION-DOLLAR Duesenbergs and vintage Italian racecars crossing the auction block will hardly be surprising sights at the sales scheduled to take place in conjunction with the Pebble Beach Concours d’Élégance on the Monterey Peninsula of California next month. ', 'print_section': 'AU', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/automobiles/24TRAN1/24TRAN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 320, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/24/automobiles/24TRAN1/24TRAN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 320}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/automobiles/24TRAN1/24TRAN1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 514, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/automobiles/24TRAN1/24TRAN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/24/automobiles/24TRAN1/24TRAN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Supporting Acts Making a Move to Center Stage', 'kicker': 'Collecting', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Supporting Acts Making a Move To Center Stage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antique and Classic Cars', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collectors and Collections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Racing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T19:09:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Automobiles', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Donald Osborne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Donald', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Osborne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f420fa62-fa2e-5c99-bbfb-16abbcf320d9', 'word_count': 1246, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f420fa62-fa2e-5c99-bbfb-16abbcf320d9'}, {'abstract': 'It’s perfectly legitimate for voters to consider where politicians like Chris Christie and Rahm Emanuel send their children to school.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/22/on-their-childrens-schools-politicians-should-save-the-outrage/', 'snippet': 'It’s perfectly legitimate for voters to consider where politicians like Chris Christie and Rahm Emanuel send their children to school.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you’re a politician who has all kinds of things to say about public education, do voters have the right to know where you send your children to school?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Their Children’s Schools, Politicians Should Save the Outrage', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T19:11:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Bai', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bai', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1d816d8-b4a8-5374-bd5a-ab91baa98938', 'word_count': 770, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1d816d8-b4a8-5374-bd5a-ab91baa98938'}, {'abstract': 'The 8th Annual Youth Awards show, “Premios Juventud,” attracted the largest number of viewers in the demographic most coveted by advertisers.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/22/univision-triumphs-on-a-barren-night-of-broadcast-tv/', 'snippet': 'The 8th Annual Youth Awards show, “Premios Juventud,” attracted the largest number of viewers in the demographic most coveted by advertisers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A relatively barren television landscape on Thursday night — with the big four networks running either comedy repeats or reality shows — allowed the Spanish-language Univision to score a ratings victory in the category advertiser-coveted demographic of 18- to 49-year-olds with its 8th Annual Youth Awards show, “Premios Juventud.” The three-hour ceremony, which featured performances from Ricky Martin and Pitbull, averaged 4.1 million total viewers. The winners were determined by online vote at univision.com. CBS had the most total viewers on the night thanks to a live eviction episode of “Big Brother” (6.7 million viewers). “Love Bites,” the sole NBC series not in repeats, fell to just under 1.8 million viewers for its (unplanned) final episode. The show was canceled earlier this week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Univision Triumphs on a Barren Night of Broadcast TV', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Univision', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T19:15:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0da3db03-24bb-5f9a-8b2e-79f221a8dbd5', 'word_count': 124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0da3db03-24bb-5f9a-8b2e-79f221a8dbd5'}, {'abstract': 'Courthouse Confidential: The national executives of Tau Epsilon Phi have stepped down and allowed interim leaders to come in and run the fraternity while elections are organized.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/22/settlement-ends-bitter-infighting-at-a-fraternity/', 'snippet': 'Courthouse Confidential: The national executives of Tau Epsilon Phi have stepped down and allowed interim leaders to come in and run the fraternity while elections are organized.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A century-old fraternity that was recently embroiled in internal strife between the national executives and members of several local chapters has reached a resolution to end the bitter infighting.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Settlement Ends Bitter Infighting at a Fraternity', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fraternities and Sororities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tau Epsilon Phi', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T19