— the artful combination of dolphin gray, navy and orange in this tea-length dress is optimized by the unexpected addition of red accessories.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Look of The Moment | Carey Mulligan', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T19:26:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/96df5ea2-ba89-5e5c-9391-cec886c4fcae', 'word_count': 66, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96df5ea2-ba89-5e5c-9391-cec886c4fcae'}, {'abstract': 'With same-sex marriage now legal in New York, some gay sons and daughters are starting to feel the same heat from parents as their straight siblings do.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/24/fashion/weddings/some-parents-of-gay-children-push-for-marriage.html', 'snippet': 'With same-sex marriage now legal in New York, some gay sons and daughters are starting to feel the same heat from parents as their straight siblings do.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOR the last year, Aaron Breslow, 23, an H.I.V. project coordinator, has been dating Dan Scudellari, 26, an advertising executive. They have spent holidays with each other’s families, and enjoy searing scallops and making kale salads in their apartments in Brooklyn.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/fashion/24MOMS1_SPAN/24MOMS1_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'i