lly elsewhere, they are thinking about marrying again — in their home state.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THEY’VE already exchanged vows and rings once before, say George W. Slowik Jr. and Patrick Turner. But that time, at a 2002 civil union ceremony in Vermont with four friends as witnesses, the festivities were limited to a luncheon followed by a round of facials.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/fashion/24FIELDNOTES/24FIELDNOTES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 986, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/fashion/24FIELDNOTES/24FIELDNOTES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/24/fashion/24FIELDNOTES/24FIELDNOTES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Walking Miles of Aisles', 'kicker': 'With This Ring . . . | Field Notes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Walking Miles of Aisles', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T20:18:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Society', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': 'Weddings', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tatiana Boncompagni', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tatiana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Boncompagni', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/790951c2-37cf-5db8-8f9f-e2ad9eaef75a', 'word_count': 1144, 'uri': 'nyt://article/790951c2-37cf-5db8-8f9f-e2ad9eaef75a'}, {'abstract': 'Mark Bittman makes his favorite easy jam, which is fruitier, and less cloying, than its grocery store counterparts.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/22/the-minimalist-fast-blueberry-jam/', 'snippet': 'Mark Bittman makes his favorite easy jam, which is fruitier, and less cloying, than its grocery store counterparts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you’re a gardener, a farmers’ market enthusiast, or a member of a community-supported agriculture group, there will probably come a point in the summer when you will find yourself overwhelmed with fresh berries, which seem like a ticking time bomb as they begin to soften and rot. When that point comes, don’t think — just make jam. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Minimalist: Fast Blueberry Jam', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blueberries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jams and Jellies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T20:19:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d8259fa-3a72-5842-9467-e934daefac57', 'word_count': 335, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d8259fa-3a72-5842-9467-e934daefac57'}, {'abstract': 'If Congress won’t deal with him, President Obama should raise the debt ceiling unilaterally.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/22/opinion/22posner.html', 'snippet': 'If Congress won’t deal with him, President Obama should raise the debt ceiling unilaterally.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PRESIDENT OBAMA should announce that he will raise the debt ceiling unilaterally if he cannot reach a deal with Congress. Constitutionally, he would be on solid ground. Politically, he can’t lose. The public wants a deal. The threat to act unilaterally will only strengthen his bargaining power if Republicans don’t want to be frozen out; if they defy him, the public will throw their support to the president. Either way, Republicans look like the obstructionists and will pay a price.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Should Raise the Debt Ceiling on His Own', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributors', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama Should Raise the Debt Ceiling on His Own', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fourteenth Amendment (US Constitution)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitution (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T20:21:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By ERIC A. POSNER and ADRIAN VERMEULE', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'POSNER', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Adrian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'VERMEULE', 