But our sister online publication The Local East Village blog found the zippier version of the drink on the shelves of five bodegas in the East Village in recent days. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In East Village, a Suspect Drink Can Still Be Found', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALCOHOLIC BEVERAGES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Caffeine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Village (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-22T21:47:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b6d8050-f28b-5c31-83a2-0fc6dbe2bf80', 'word_count': 127, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b6d8050-f28b-5c31-83a2-0fc6dbe2bf80'}, {'abstract': 'This sprawling tale of madness, based on a 1956 novel by Yukio Mishima, never really earns the crazy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/23/theater/reviews/the-temple-of-the-golden-pavilion-at-the-rose-theater-review.html', 'snippet': 'This sprawling tale of madness, based on a 1956 novel by Yukio Mishima, never really earns the crazy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a three-hour-long production, “The Temple of the Golden Pavilion” sure does use a lot of shorthand.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/23/arts/Sub-Temple/Sub-Temple-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/23/arts/Sub-Temple/Sub-Temple-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo