desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09da9cb4-15ae-5476-a356-b2c68a7690c2', 'word_count': 13, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09da9cb4-15ae-5476-a356-b2c68a7690c2'}, {'abstract': '“Malcolm X: A Life of Reinvention,” by Manning Marable, is at the center of a renewed effort that may well gain traction because the legal environment has changed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/23/nyregion/biography-helps-renew-calls-to-investigate-malcolm-x-assassination.html', 'snippet': '“Malcolm X: A Life of Reinvention,” by Manning Marable, is at the center of a renewed effort that may well gain traction because the legal environment has changed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The death of Malcolm X, shot dead at the Audubon Ballroom in Upper Manhattan in 1965, never inflamed the public imagination in the same way the assassinations of John F. Kennedy and the Rev. Dr. Martin Luther King Jr. did. But scholars have long believed that a bungled investigation resulted in the imprisonment of the innocent and allowed some of those responsible to go free. Over the decades, efforts to reopen the case have failed.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/nyregion/20110723-malcolmxA/20110723-malcolmxA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 992, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/nyregion/20110723-malcolmxA/20110723-malcolmxA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/22/nyregion/20110723-malcolmxA/20110723-malcolmxA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheig