ain other people are not living acceptable lives and must be reformed. I’m all for the concept, so long as I’m the one deciding what’s acceptable and doing the reforming. And I have something that most of the other self-appointed judges don’t: the Putt-Putt System of Personal Redemption.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/nyregion/24CRITIC_SPAN/24CRITIC_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/24/nyregion/24CRITIC_SPAN/24CRITIC_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/nyregion/24CRITIC_SPAN/24CRITIC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/nyregion/24CRITIC_SPAN/24CRITIC_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/24/nyregion/24CRITIC_SPAN/24CRITIC_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'No Windmill, but Still a Cure for the Wicked', 'kicker': 'City Critic', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Windmill, But Still a Cure For the Wicked', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'TriBeCa (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Miniature Golf', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-23T01:34:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename