f Southern arms at the Battle of Bull Run, the first train crowded with Union prisoners of war rolled into Richmond, Va. A motley crew of bedraggled federals poured out of the cars. Curious citizens buzzed with excitement as guards marched the men through the Confederate capital.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Private Conant and the First Bull Run Prisoners', 'kicker': 'disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisoners of War', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lincoln, Abraham', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-23T01:47:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ronald S. Coddington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ronald', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Coddington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9568f7a4-1d23-5cd5-bc68-94323c07d316', 'word_count': 1632, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9568f7a4-1d23-5cd5-bc68-94323c07d316'}, {'abstract': 'The avant-garde artist Robert Wilson spends part of his Sundays reading alone or gardening, but he still keeps to an hour-by-hour work calendar.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/24/nyregion/for-robert-wilson-work-rarely-stops.html', 'snippet': 'The avant-garde artist Robert Wilson spends part of his Sundays reading alone or gardening, but he still keeps to an hour-by-hour work calendar.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Robert Wilson, the multifaceted artist and the director of avant-garde creations like “Einstein on the Beach,” is one cosmic cat. Mr. Wilson is as likely to collaborate with Lou Reed and Laurie Anderson as with members of the local Shinnecock Indian tribe. He established the Watermill Center on Long Island, a cultural think tank for young artists and scholars, in 1992 and acknowledges it as his legacy; its annual benefit gala is July 30. Mr. Wilson’s 70th birthday is being celebrated Oct. 4 at the Brooklyn Academy of Music with the opening of his production of Bertolt Brecht and Kurt Weill’s “Threepenny Opera.” He keeps to a daily work regimen, but on Sundays allows himself time to relax and smell the roses on his six-acre retreat.  ROBIN FINN', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/nyregion/24ROUTINE_SPAN/24ROUTINE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 352, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/24/nyregion/24ROUTINE_SPAN/24ROUTINE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 352}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/nyregion/24ROUTINE_SPAN/24ROUTINE_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/nyregion/24ROUTINE_SPAN/24ROUTINE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/24/nyregion/24ROUTINE_SPAN/24ROUTINE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Working as a Way of Living', 'kicker': 'Sunday Routine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Working as a Way of Living', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, Robert', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, '