in exchange for a deal to raise the debt ceiling and prevent default. But it was never enough, and, on Friday evening, it became clear that it may never be enough. Speaker John Boehner again walked away from the “grand bargain” he had been negotiating with President Obama, leaving the country teetering on the brink of another economic collapse.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Party That Can’t Say Yes', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Party That Can’t Say Yes: Once again, Republicans walk away from an overly generous debt-limit offer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-23T02:02:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/71364d1b-8e93-5c0f-b1bf-5c7f69a446b9', 'word_count': 579, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71364d1b-8e93-5c0f-b1bf-5c7f69a446b9'}, {'abstract': 'A Bronx policeman found glass in his McDonald’s burger in 2005; an employee confessed but was acquitted and sued the officer and the city.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/23/nyregion/policemans-stop-at-mcdonalds-produces-years-of-court-cases.html', 'snippet': 'A Bronx policeman found glass in his McDonald’s burger in 2005; an employee confessed but was acquitted and sued the officer and the city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The police officer, recalling that night, sounds like an actor in a fast-food commercial: “At some point, something told me, grab a Big Mac.” And so on a freezing January night in 2005, the officer, John Florio, then 39, stopped at the drive-through window of a McDonald’s in the Hunts Point section of the Bronx. He ordered the combo, a Big Mac with fries and a Coke. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/23/nyregion/ALT-CRIMESCENE/ALT-CRIMESCENE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tale of Glass in Burger Lingers', 'kicker': 'Crime Scene', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tale of Glass In Burger Lingers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Confessions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "McDonald's Corporation", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-23T02:02:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/96892ee1-1828-5075-9b11-dd7782eaa36f', 'word_count': 990, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96892ee1-1828-5075-9b11-dd7782eaa36f'}, {'abstract': 'The European Union leaders have finally approved a bailout loan for Greece and others, but the economic crisis is far from over.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/23/opinion/23sat2.html', 'snippet': 'The European Union leaders have finally approved a bailout loan for Greece and others, but the economic crisis is far from over.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Europe’s leaders finally woke up — and not a moment too soon. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Some Sense in Europe', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Some Sense in Europe: New lending terms for Greece and others will buy time, but the crisis isn’t over', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-23T02:03:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/d24060e2-63eb-5801-a6e0-622834b66688', 'word_count': 426, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d24060e2-63eb-5801-a6e0-622834b66688'}, {'abstract': 'Excerpts from a conversation between Roger Cohen, the Op-Ed columnist for International Herald Tribune, and Gen. David Petraeus.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/opinion/100000000961858/roger-cohen-speaks-to-gen-petraeus.html', 'snippet': 'Excerpts from a conversation between Roger Cohen, the Op-Ed columnist for International Herald Tribune, and Gen. David Petraeus.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Excerpts from a conversation between Roger Cohen, the Op-Ed columnist for International Herald Tribune, and Gen. David Petraeus.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/opinion/video-patraeus/video-patraeus-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/22/opinion/video-patraeus/video-patraeus-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/22/opinion/video-patraeus/video-patraeus-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/22/opinion/video-patraeus/video-patraeus-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Roger Cohen Speaks to Gen. Petraeus', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Petraeus, David H', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-23T02:03:17+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Opinion', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'Diego Laje', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Diego', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Laje', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/f44d81a1-7148-5f9b-b691-a1b731065db0', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/f44d81a1-7148-5f9b-b691-a1b731065db0'}, {'abstract': 'Union leaders in New York and Connecticut are encouraged to approve the new and fairly negotiated contracts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/23/opinion/23sat3.html', 'snippet': 'Union leaders in New York and Connecticut are encouraged to approve the new and fairly negotiated contracts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are now thousands of workers in New York and Connecticut whose jobs depend on the good sense of their fellow union members. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fair Deals in New York and Connecticut', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fair Deals in New York and Connecticut', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Malloy, Dannel P', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Employees', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-23T02:03:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/3673f835-2aa7-5abd-9008-ef2149110165', 'word_count': 340, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3673f835-2aa7-5abd-9008-ef2149110165'}, {'abstract': 'The International Maritime Organization has introduced important, but limited, rules to reduce emissions from large cargo ships.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/23/opinion/23sat4.html', 'snippet': 'The International Maritime Organization has introduced important, but limited, rules to reduce emissions from large cargo ships.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The International Maritime Organization, an agency of the United Nations, has introduced important, if still too limited, rules to reduce emissions from large cargo ships. Tankers, container ships and other freighters, most of which burn a coarse petroleum sludge called bunker fuel, now contribute about 3.3 percent of global carbon dioxide emissions, though some analysts argue the figure may be considerably higher. Without new restrictions, emissions from increased shipping could nearly triple by 2050. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Changing Course', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Changing Course', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ships and Shipping', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Energy Efficiency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Maritime Organization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lobbying and Lobbyists', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-23T02:04:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/075641e5-de3e-5955-bd82-c42e159e9125', 'word_count': 237, 'uri': 'nyt://article/075641e5-de3e-5955-bd82-c42e159e9125'}, {'abstract': 'Can Apple retain its dominance after ending the iPhone’s exclusivity to AT&T? A Verizon subscriber compares the packaging and content of rival devices.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/23/business/testing-iphone-buying-the-android.html', 'snippet': 'Can Apple retain its dominance after ending the iPhone’s exclusivity to AT&T? A Verizon subscriber compares the packaging and content of rival devices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'First sold to the public just four years ago, the Apple iPhone melded the vast potential of the Internet with a multimedia player, a still and video camera, e-mail, texting, instant messaging, social networking and other applications — now 425,000 and counting — into one elegant, easy-to-use touch-screen package. And it makes voice calls. Rarely has one device so upended a market.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/business/james-stewart/james-stewart-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/25/business/james-stewart/james-stewart-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/business/james-stewart/james-stewart-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/business/james-stewart/james-stewart-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1333, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/business/james-stewart/james-stewart-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/25/business/james-stewart/james-stewart-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': N