lice ceremony came after two days of unrest that left 18 people dead and many more hospitalized.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAPE TOWN — Facing international condemnation for his government’s use of force against peaceful demonstrators, Malawi’s president defiantly blamed protest organizers and political opponents on Friday for the violence that left 18 people dead this week. And he warned them against a return to the streets.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Malawi President Blames Protesters for Violence', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Malawi President Blames Protesters for Violence', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Malawi', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mutharika, Bingu wa', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Millennium Challenge Corp', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-23T02:05:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Celia W. Dugger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Celia', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Dugger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc0f76bf-49c0-5a6a-a978-7a4d7aaf9419', 'word_count': 910, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc0f76bf-49c0-5a6a-a978-7a4d7aaf9419'}, {'abstract': 'For N.F.L. Commissioner Roger Goodell and DeMaurice Smith, the head of the players union, a possible labor agreement will probably define their legacies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/23/sports/football/for-roger-goodell-and-demaurice-smith-nfl-labor-peace-w