https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/23/business/new-mccafe-beverages-lift-results-at-mcdonalds.html', 'snippet': 'McDonald’s said second-quarter profit rose 15 percent, topping analysts’ estimates, as more consumers ate out and McCafé beverages raised sales.', 'lead_paragraph': 'McDonald’s said second-quarter profit rose 15 percent, topping analysts’ estimates, as more consumers ate out and McCafé beverages raised sales. Net income climbed to $1.41 billion, or $1.35 a share, from $1.23 billion, or $1.13 a share, a year earlier, McDonald’s said in a statement Friday. The average estimate of 22 analysts surveyed by Bloomberg was $1.28 a share. Sales rose 16 percent to $6.91 billion. Stock in McDonald’s, which is based in Oak Brook, Ill., rose $2.02, to $88.56 a share. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New McCafé Beverages Lift Results at McDonald’s', 'kicker': 'Business Briefing | EARNINGS', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New McCafé Beverages Lift Results at McDonald’s', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': "McDonald's Corporation", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-23T02:17:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bloomberg News', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bloomberg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'News', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/89a45a9e-bdb5-54a4-a697-d55fd027bd14', 'word_count': 82, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89a45a9e-bdb5-54a4-a697-d55fd027bd14'}, {'abstract': 'A plea bargain agreement ends a case that had drawn angry criticism from journalists and others.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/23/world/europe/23georgia.html', 'snippet': 'A plea bargain agreement ends a case that had drawn angry criticism from journalists and others.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TBILISI, Georgia — Four Georgian photographers accused of spying for Russia were released from custody on Friday as part of a plea bargain agreement, hastily resolving a case that had drawn angry criticism from fellow journalists and media watchdog groups.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Georgia Frees 4 Photographers Held as Spies for Russia', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Georgia Frees Photographers Accused of Spying for Russia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia (Georgian Republic)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abdaladze, Giorgi', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gedenidze, Irakli', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-23T02:19:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mzia Kupunia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mzia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kupunia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/90c4ae8f-96dc-535f-a8c1-b6d45c103719', 'word_count': 424, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90c4ae8f-96dc-535f-a8c1-b6d45c103719'}, {'abstract': 'The MTK: Music to Know festival will pair acts like Vampire Weekend and Ellie Goulding with tents selling clothing from labels including Topshop and Tory Burch.', 'we