bles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Larchmont enjoys a luxury of good little restaurants, but Vintage 1891, open since March, brings something new to town: nightlife. In a historic brick building, this wine lounge offers beautifully plated food and a svelte refuge from the heat. The wine list is first-class; the rosemary popcorn ($4) is addictive. ', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Pour and a Plate', 'kicker': 'Quick Bite | Larchmont', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Pour and a Plate', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Westchester County (NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-23T03:01:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alice Gabriel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alice', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/35a2017d-375c-55c8-9d94-4c619e0259cb', 'word_count': 313, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35a2017d-375c-55c8-9d94-4c619e0259cb'}, {'abstract': 'The menu at Scalini Osteria in downtown Bronxville, N.Y., features the classic regional fare of Italy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/24/nyregion/scalini-osteria-in-bronxville-ny-restaurant-review.html', 'snippet': 'The menu at Scalini Osteria in downtown Bronxville, N.Y., features the classic regional fare of Italy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FEW restaurants in the county will offer one cuisine exclusively. Scalini Osteria, however, not only has embraced the cooking of Italy, but also has created a menu of memorable dishes simply by featuring the country’s classic regional fare.', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/nyregion/24SUBDINEWE1/24SUBDINEWE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/nyregion/24SUBDINEWE1/24SUBDINEWE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/24/nyregion/24SUBDINEWE1/24SUBDINEWE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Exclusively Italian, and Adriatic to Boot', 'kicker': 'Westchester Dining | Bronxville', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Exclusively Italian, And Adriatic to Boot', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Westchester County (NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-23T03:04:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By M. H. Reed', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/259d2b86-c11c-5601-a679-a40055312570', 'word_count': 803, 'uri': 'nyt://article/259d2b86-c11c-5601-a679-a40055312570'}, {'abstract': 'The 2009 vintage pinot blanc is one of a number of appealing new releases from the Lieb Family Cellars.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/24/nyregion/lieb-family-cellars-offers-appealing-pinot-blanc.html', 'snippet': 'The 2009 vintage pinot blanc is one of a number of appealing new releases from the Lieb Family Cellars.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lieb Family Cellars, in Cutchogue, has become synonymous with both dry and sparkling pinot blanc on Long Island. Its dry version, a perennial favorite of consumers and restaurants, mimics the pinot blanc of Alsace. ', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Welcome Picnic Guest', 'kicker': 'Long Island Vines ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Welcome Picnic Guest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lieb Family Cellars', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-23T03:08:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Howard G. Goldberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Howard', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'Goldberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/91b09eaf-c63b-57e0-9640-248f57dce522', 'word_count': 324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91b09eaf-c63b-57e0-9640-248f57dce522'}, {'abstract': 'The ambience at South Edison is casual, but the food and prices are more on par with restaurants in the Hamptons.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/24/nyregion/south-edison-brings-upscale-food-to-montauk.html', 'snippet': 'The ambience at South Edison is casual, but the food and prices are more on par with restaurants in the Hamptons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SOUTH Edison has the look of Montauk but the food and prices of the Hamptons. The year-old restaurant serves exciting fare created by the chef Todd Mitgang, the former executive chef and co-owner of Crave Ceviche Bar in Manhattan. Steven Kristel is his partner in this venture.', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/nyregion/24DINELI1/24DINELI1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/nyregion/24DINELI1/24DINELI1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/24/nyregion/24DINELI1/24DINELI1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hamptons Fare With Informal Feel', 'kicker': 'Long Island Dining | Montauk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hamptons Fare With Informal Feel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-23T03:09:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanne Starkey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Starkey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a2706c9-6e21-5bb9-84c8-aaf9b2968bbf', 'word_count': 854, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a2706c9-6e21-5bb9-84c8-aaf9b2968bbf'}, {'abstract': 'Paul’s and Sandy’s Too, in East Hampton, combines an array of locally grown fruits and vegetables with a hardware store.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/24/nyregion/local-produce-at-pauls-and-sandys-too.html', 'snippet': 'Paul’s and Sandy’s Too, in East Hampton, combines an array of locally grown fruits and vegetables with a hardware store.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of Connecticut’s more reliable produce stands is by the entrance to Paul’s and Sandy’s Too in East Hampton. The sprawling garden center and hardware store maintains 15 greenhouses filled with plants, but it does not grow any of its own fruits and vegetables. Instead, a broad array of produce is trucked in daily, largely from area farms. ', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hardware and Produce', 'kicker': 'Quick Bite | Connecticut', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hardware and Produce', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Farmers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-23T03:13:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Brooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1014ef11-fac9-508f-8531-bcc4bff61337', 'word_count': 317, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1014ef11-fac9-508f-8531-bcc4bff61337'}, {'abstract': 'Bar Rosso in Stamford, Conn., has an impressive wine list, Italian dishes like a marinated lamb chop with a Catalan-inspired romesco sauce, and irresistible basil gelato.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/24/nyregion/bar-rosso-in-stamford-conn-for-after-work-or-film-review.html', 'snippet': 'Bar Rosso in Stamford, Conn., has an impressive wine list, Italian dishes like a marinated lamb chop with a Catalan-inspired romesco sauce, and irresistible basil gelato.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHAT makes Bar Rosso, a clubby cafe in downtown Stamford, such a magnet for those under 40 is partly its location: half a block from the lively outdoor happy-hour scene on Bedford Street across from the Avon Theater Film Center.', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/nyregion/24DINECT1/24DINECT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/nyregion/24DINECT1/24DINECT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/24/nyregion/24DINECT1/24DINECT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Clubby, for After Work or a Movie', 'kicker': 'Connecticut Dining | Stamford', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Clubby, for After Work Or a Movie', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Stamford (Conn)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-23T03:14:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Brooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/08ca80b7-33c1-51b9-8d87-3621923dbbb5', 'word_count': 733, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08ca80b7-33c1-51b9-8d87-3621923dbbb5'}, {'abstract': 'A teenage girl, whose kidnapping on Sunday from a park captivated France, was found unharmed on Friday, apparently taken by her fiancé’s family as part of a premarriage ritual, the police said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/23/world/europe/23briefs-France.html', 'snippet': 'A teenage girl, whose kidnapping on Sunday from a park captivated France, was found unharmed on Friday, apparently taken by her fiancé’s family as part of a premarriage ritual, the police said.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A teenage girl, whose kidnapping on Sunday from a park in Privas, in southeast France, riveted the country, was found unharmed on Friday, apparently taken by her fiancé’s family as part of a Chechen premarriage ritual, the police said. The girl, who was not named and who was thought to be 16 or 17, was found by the police in the southwestern Haute-Garonne region with the family of her fiancé, said a spokeswoman for the Privas police. The family said they were simply following an old North Caucasus tradition, like others in the Chechen diaspora. The kidnapping originates as a response by a man when a young woman’s family refuses a marriage. After the abduction and a night spent away from home, the young women is considered “soiled,” and the family would then consent to the union. Religious leaders among the Chechens, who are mostly Muslim, are trying to put an end to the tradition. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France: Kidnapping Was Part of Ritual', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | EUROPE', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France: Kidnapping Was Part of Ritual', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kidnapping', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-23T03:14:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Erlanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erlanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ab8a3c4-2cca-5d32-be7c-b78a948d569a', 'word_count': 156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ab8a3c4-2cca-5d32-be7c-b78a948d569a'}, {'abstract': 'The shuttering of The News of the World due to the phone-hacking scandal may leave Rupert Murdoch’s other British newspapers without exclusive access to the country’s Olympians.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/23/sports/olympics/murdoch-newspapers-may-lose-exclusive-access-to-2012-british-olympians.html', 'snippet': 'The shuttering of The News of the World due to the phone-hacking scandal may leave Rupert Murdoch’s other British newspapers without exclusive access to the country’s Olympians.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rupert Murdoch’s British newspapers could lose exclusive access to the country’s athletes as they prepare for next year’s Summer Games in London because of the phone-hacking scandal that led to the closing of the tabloid The News of the World and testimony before Parliament by Murdoch and his son James.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Murdoch Papers Could Lose Special Access to 2012 Athletes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Murdoch Papers May Lose Exclusive Access to 2012 Athletes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News of the World', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News International Ltd', 'ra