ers with nature that sustain her.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a sunny July afternoon, a dirt road tucked inside the Delaware Water Gap National Recreation Area near Blairstown, N.J., was calm and serene. A deer, uninterested in the sight of a man eating a peanut butter sandwich while leaning against his car, strolled across the road and disappeared into the woods. A few yards away, a stream tumbled under a wooden footbridge.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/sports/dog-trail-1/dog-trail-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/24/sports/dog-trail-1/dog-trail-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/sports/dog-trail-1/dog-trail-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/sports/dog-trail-1/dog-trail-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/24/sports/dog-trail-1/dog-trail-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Speed Hiker Thrives on Natural Rhythms of the Appalachian Trail', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Speed Hiker Thrives on Natural Rhythms of the Appalachian Trail', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hikes and Hiking', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'APPALACHIAN TRAIL', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-23T13:46:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Keith Mulvihill', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Keith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mulvihill', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/13289cdd-134c-50e9-9250-eb6c6d44b105', 'word_count': 1195, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13289cdd-134c-50e9-9250-eb6c6d44b105'}, {'abstract': 'Shaun White, the snowboarder and skateboarder, is looking forward to the 2014 Olympics, which will include a new event: slopestyle snowboarding.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/24/sports/30-seconds-with-shaun-white.html', 'snippet': 'Shaun White, the snowboarder and skateboarder, is looking forward to the 2014 Olympics, which will include a new event: slopestyle snowboarding.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Shaun White, the professional snowboarder and skateboarder, competed this weekend in skate vert at the Dew Tour season opener in Ocean City, Md. At the Winter X Games, White, a two-time Olympic gold medalist in the halfpipe, has dominated slopestyle snowboarding, which involves performing tricks in the air as well as on rails and boxes. This month the International Olympic Committee approved the inclusion of men’s and women’s slopestyle, and freestyle skiing for the 2014 Games in Sochi, Russia. White, 24, visited Manhattan recently to promote his signature line of Oakley sunglasses. VINCENT M. MALLOZZI', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/sports/seconds/seconds-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 659, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/sports/seconds/seconds-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'sub