inal': 'By Randall Stross', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randall', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stross', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ccc6aa97-df52-5043-a822-1feb7e2e5ce1', 'word_count': 899, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ccc6aa97-df52-5043-a822-1feb7e2e5ce1'}, {'abstract': 'The police said that the death of the Grammy-award winning singer Amy Winehouse, who battled addiction problems for years, was being treated as “unexplained.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/24/world/europe/24amy.html', 'snippet': 'The police said that the death of the Grammy-award winning singer Amy Winehouse, who battled addiction problems for years, was being treated as “unexplained.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Amy Winehouse, the Grammy-award winning singer who has battled addiction problems for years, was found dead on Saturday at her apartment in London, the police said. She was 27.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Amy Winehouse Found Dead in London, Police Say', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Amy Winehouse Found Dead in London, Police Say', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-23T17:13:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Werdigier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werdigier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b57e317-ba45-542c-b4a0-18f400ac443f', 'word_count': 430, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b57e317-ba45-542c-b4a0-18f400ac443f'}, {'abstract': 'Think Quarterly, a business-to-business marketing tool from Google, will make its debut this week. But it’s being promoted with a retro technique: snail mail.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/24/business/google-tries-an-online-publication-for-marketing-itself.html', 'snippet': 'Think Quarterly, a business-to-business marketing tool from Google, will make its debut this week. But it’s being promoted with a retro technique: snail mail.', 'lead_paragraph': '“DATA beats opinion” has long been a mantra at Google, where evidence-based research tends to rule. But now the company is showing its softer side with Think Quarterly, a business-to-business publication whose first United States issue is to make its debut online this week.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/business/Stream-4/Stream-4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/24/business/Stream-4/Stream-4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Slowing Down to Savor the Data', 'kicker': 'Slipstream', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Slowing Down To Savor the Data', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-23T17:14:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'NAT', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Natasha Singer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Natasha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Singer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff2a070e-7ff2-5dbc-9c4c-e36673a6e0a1', 'word_count': 969, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff2a070e-7ff2-5dbc-9c4c-e36673a6e0a1'}, {'abstract': 'Increased public spending, matched by tax increases, would offer balanced support of the economy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/24/business/economy/tax-and-spend-but-keep-your-balance-economic-view.html', 'snippet': 'Increased public spending, matched by tax increases, would offer balanced support of the economy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE fight over the debt ceiling has deflected attention from the serious problems of fixing the economy and finding jobs for the 14 million unemployed. Worse, it has created strong negative feelings about fiscal policy, just when other policy measures seem incapable of restoring economic health.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/business/VIEW/VIEW-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 823, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/business/VIEW/VIEW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/24/business/VIEW/VIEW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Taxing and Spending, in Balance', 'kicker': 'Economic View', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Taxing And Spending, In Balance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infrastructure (Public Works)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'American Recovery and Reinvestment Act (2009)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-23T17:15:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'NAT', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert J. Shiller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Shiller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0b03450-6a5d-5703-87c6-4850b0b9c154', 'word_count': 1058, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0b03450-6a5d-5703-87c6-4850b0b9c154'}, {'abstract': 'As gold’s value surges, asset managers and others are revisiting its merits.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/24/your-money/in-golds-popularity-shades-of-1980-strategies.html', 'snippet': 'As gold’s value surges, asset managers and others are revisiting its merits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE worse things get, the better it looks for gold. That’s been the pattern this summer.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/business/STRAT/STRAT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 578, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/business/STRAT/STRAT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/24/business/STRAT/STRAT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In a Gold Lovefest, Shades of 1980', 'kicker': 'Strategies', 'content_kicker': None, 'p