word_count': 486, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70597089-f24a-57e9-899b-24e891a9050d'}, {'abstract': 'The wife of the Patriots owner Robert K. Kraft died this week after a long battle with cancer and was a beloved fixture around the team.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/23/remembering-myra-kraft/', 'snippet': 'The wife of the Patriots owner Robert K. Kraft died this week after a long battle with cancer and was a beloved fixture around the team.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The best story about Myra Kraft to emerge among the touching remembrances following her death this week after a long battle with cancer came from her son Jonathan. He recalled how his mom, during a family trip to South Africa in the era of apartheid, demanded that a white police officer who was taking black men into custody arrest her, too. Jonathan remembered his dad, the Patriots owner Robert K. Kraft, telling him not to let his mother get in trouble. So he threw his mom, a petite woman, over his shoulder and hauled her away.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Remembering Myra Kraft', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kraft, Robert K', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Patriots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-23T21:29:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judy Battista', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Battista', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd289a06-81ed-5191-a752-abf938a93f0a', 'word_count': 430, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd289a06-81ed-5191-a752-abf938a93f0a'}, {'abstract': 