s been found at the Comic-Con International convention, perhaps farther up the river than even Kurtz dared to tread.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN DIEGO—Werner Herzog has been found, here at the Comic-Con International convention, perhaps farther up the river than even Kurtz dared to tread.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Herzog Found at Comic-Con', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comic-Con (Convention)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Herzog, Werner', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-23T22:59:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cieply', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cieply', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c2cd1bf-6700-587e-8bf9-1b6dc5b73541', 'word_count': 253, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c2cd1bf-6700-587e-8bf9-1b6dc5b73541'}, {'abstract': 'With continuing population growth, water-supply constraints and drought, low-cost reclaimed wastewater is in greater and greater demand.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/24/us/24ttsewage.html', 'snippet': 'With continuing population growth, water-supply constraints and drought, low-cost reclaimed wastewater is in greater and greater demand.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FORT WORTH — At the plant that treats most of this city’s sewage, water sloshes and foams within giant concrete walls. This is cleaned-up sewage, made even purer by processes the plant expanded just a few months ago. Now some treated water runs through specially labeled, purple-colored pipes to irrigate nearby golf courses and a park, instead of just being dumped into the nearby Trinity River, as it had for decades.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/us/24TTSEWAGE/24TTSEWAGE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 662, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/us/24TTSEWAGE/24TTSEWAGE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/24/us/24TTSEWAGE/24TTSEWAGE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Adversity Creates a Boom for ‘Reclaimed Water’', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Adversity Creates a Boom for ‘Reclaimed Water’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drought', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recycling of Waste Materials', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-23T23:05:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Galbraith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Galbraith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/191fa27c-095c-54dd-a7e0-3feca2baf17d', 'word_count': 1032, 'uri': 'nyt://article/191fa27c-095c-54dd-a7e0-3feca2baf17d'}, {'abstract': 'Readers comment on my column arguing that the debt ceiling mess is becoming a threat to American national security', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/23/readers-comment-on-my-budget-column/', 'snippet': 'Readers comment on my column arguing that the debt ceiling mess is becoming a threat to American national security', 'lead_paragraph': 'My Sunday column argues that we usually think of national security challenges coming from terrorists or enemy countries, but one major challenge to American national security right now comes from the grotesque mishandling of the Washington budget battle. A default would do enormous damage to American interests, and some of the Republican budget cuts — particularly in education — have already done the same. I wish we were as vigorous in standing up to domestic threats to national security as foreign ones, but we’re not. Read the column and post your thoughts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Readers Comment on My Budget Column', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-23T23:18:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a716396-b818-525e-b039-aa9c9ce989f2', 'word_count': 92, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a716396-b818-525e-b039-aa9c9ce989f2'}, {'abstract': 'Conditions for writers who refuse to conform to government restrictions in China have worsened since February, when the Communist Party began a wide-ranging crackdown on dissent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/24/world/asia/24beijing.html', 'snippet': 'Conditions for writers who refuse to conform to government restrictions in China have worsened since February, when the Communist Party began a wide-ranging crackdown on dissent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — For Chinese authors who join the international writers’ organization PEN, membership would appear to have very few privileges. Many of its members are subjected to frequent harassment; four of them are currently in prison, including one of its founders, Liu Xiaobo, the essayist and Nobel Peace Prize laureate serving 11 years for subversion. All told, the group counts 40 journalists, novelists and historians imprisoned because of their writings.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Beijing Bars Writers From a Literary Celebration, Continuing a Crackdown', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Beijing Bars Writers From a Literary Celebration, Continuing a Crackdown', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'PEN American Center', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ai Weiwei', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-23T23:21:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Jacobs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jacobs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cadcdf7a-e3c3-52ad-b8c5-6be7df2905d2', 'word_count': 719, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cadcdf7a-e3c3-52ad-b8c5-6be7df2905d2'}, {'abstract': 'In a sign of the times in Philadelphia, the fans seemed to prefer water to beer.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/23/in-the-city-of-brotherly-heat/', 'snippet': 'In a sign of the times in Philadelphia, the fans seemed to prefer water to beer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHILADELPHIA — In Citizens Bank Park in Philadelphia, the temperature was 100 degrees when Kyle Kendrick threw the first pitch against the San Diego Padres at 4:12 p.m., but the heat didn’t dampen the spirits of the officially sold-out crowd.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In the City of Brotherly Heat', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizens Bank Park (Philadelphia, Pa)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Philadelphia Phillies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philadelphia (Pa)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-24T00:01:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Hurdle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hurdle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/370614f4-f525-5003-b1ad-e932e5844bb8', 'word_count': 506, 'uri': 'nyt://article/370614f4-f525-5003-b1ad-e932e5844bb8'}, {'abstract': 'The annual accountability ratings for Texas’ school districts are coming out soon, but a change in the ratings formula will surely cause grief in numerous districts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/24/us/24ttaccountable.html', 'snippet': 'The annual accountability ratings for Texas’ school districts are coming out soon, but a change in the ratings formula will surely cause grief in numerous districts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Friday, the Texas Education Agency will publicly release its annual accountability ratings for the state’s 1,000-plus school districts. School officials always eye this day with nervous anticipation, but this year many are feeling more than a twinge of dread. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Change in Rating Formula Creates Anxiety in Schools', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Change in Rating Formula Creates Anxiety in Schools', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests and Examinations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ratings and Rating Systems', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-24T00:02:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Morgan Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Morgan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e51bf2b8-b824-5c30-a8ac-837d6e353aff', 'word_count': 650, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e51bf2b8-b824-5c30-a8ac-837d6e353aff'}, {'abstract': 'Formula One isn’t the kind of car racing that Texas fans are used to, but well-heeled locals and visitors from abroad could make the new course in Austin a big success.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/24/us/24ttsports.html', 'snippet': 'Formula One isn’t the kind of car racing that Texas fans are used to, but well-heeled locals and visitors from abroad could make the new course in Austin a big success.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sebastian Vettel of Germany is dominating Formula One again this season, building on his 2010 championship with six wins in nine races. But that’s nothing compared with the underdog triumph that Formula One itself just pulled: getting money from the state of Texas.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21B', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/us/24TTSPORTS/24TTSPORTS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 662, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/us/24TTSPORTS/24TTSPORTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/24/us/24TTSPORTS/24TTSPORTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'With Some Rich Car Fans, Formula One Could Work', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Some Rich Car Fans, Formula One Could Work', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Austin (Tex)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Racing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Formula One', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-24T00:02:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e657fe2-017d-5e8b-a7aa-0fe2fd60170d', 'word_count': 895, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e657fe2-017d-5e8b-a7aa-0fe2fd60170d'}, {'abstract': 'After some hiccups, Sony Pictures Entertainment and its coming reboot of the “Spider-Man” series won the battle for fans’ hearts and minds at Comic-Con on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/23/tension-among-spider-man-fans-at-comic-con/', 'snippet': 'After some hiccups, Sony Pictures Entertainment and its coming reboot of the “Spider-Man” series won the battle for fans’ hearts and minds at Comic-Con on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN DIEGO — They came, they saw and some walked — several hundred Comic-Con attendees poured out of the giant Hall H about halfway through the “Amazing Spider-Man” presentation. But Sony Pictures Entertainment and its coming reboot of the “Spider-Man” series won the battle for fans’ hearts and minds at the fan convention on Friday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tension Turns Into Approval Among ‘Spider-Man’ Fans at Comic-Con', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comic-Con (Convention)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-24T00:15:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cieply', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cieply', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0122a3b-1c4d-513f-9a04-7c96ebcba7e5', 'word_count': 294, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0122a3b-1c4d-513f-9a04-7c96ebcba7e5'}, {'abstract': 'Lanham Lyne, one of the newest members of the Texas House, is seriously reconsidering his decision to work in the Capitol, and that says a lot about how the Legislature works.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/24/us/24ttramsey.html', 'snippet': 'Lanham Lyne, one of the newest members of the Texas House, is seriously reconsidering his decision to work in the Capitol, and that says a lot about how the Legislature works.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ross Ramsey, the managing editor at The Texas Tribune, writes a column for The Tribune.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/us/sub24TTRAMSEY/sub24TTRAMSEY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 611, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/us/sub24TTRAMSEY/sub24TTRAMSEY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/24/us/sub24TTRAMSEY/sub24TTRAMSEY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Neophyte in the House, but Not in Politics, Sours on the Experience', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Neophyte in the House, but Not in Politics, Sours on the Experience', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-24T00:15:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Ramsey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ramsey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7709b6f7-ac7d-5781-83ed-c200f7c4b077', 'word_count': 821, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7709b6f7-ac7d-5781-83ed-c200f7c4b077'}, {'abstract': 'The lockout would only end after the full union votes in favor of the collective bargaining agreement, although the doors of N.F.L. facilities could open conditionally before then.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/24/sports/football/vote-to-ratify-nfl-labor-agreement-is-expected-monday.html', 'snippet': 'The lockout would only end after the full union votes in favor of the collective bargaining agreement, although the doors of N.F.L. facilities could open conditionally before then.', 'lead_paragraph': 'N.F.L. players and owners made such significant progress on their remaining differences Saturday that tentative plans were being made for the players’ executive committee to meet in Washington on Monday. The hope is that they will vote to ratify the agreement that will end the lockout after more than four months. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Players Committee Expected to Ratify N.F.L. Labor Agreement on Monday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Players Committee Expected to Ratify N.F.L. Labor Agreement on Monday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collective Bargaining', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League Players Assn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lockouts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-24T00:16:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judy Battista', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Battista', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3763cba0-d1fa-5752-98ef-66c4847476ae', 'word_count': 822, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3763cba0-d1fa-5752-98ef-66c4847476ae'}, {'abstract': 'General Shalikashvili was the first foreign-born soldier to become the chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/24/us/24Shalikashvili.html', 'snippet': 'General Shalikashvili was the first foreign-born soldier to become the chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gen. John M. Shalikashvili, the first foreign-born soldier to become the chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff, died Saturday morning at an Army hospital in Washington State of complications after a stroke. He was 75.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/us/OBIT-SHALIKASHVILI/OBIT-SHALIKASHVILI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 614, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/us/OBIT-SHALIKASHVILI/OBIT-SHALIKASHVILI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/24/us/OBIT-SHALIKASHVILI/OBIT-SHALIKASHVILI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Gen. John M. Shalikashvili, Military Chief in 1990s, Dies at 75', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gen. John M. Shalikashvili, 75, Military Chief in 1990s', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shalikashvili, John M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'