times.com/2011/07/24/us/politics/24molloy.html', 'snippet': 'Five presidents — from Gerald R. Ford to Bill Clinton — were trumpeted into the House by Mr. Molloy to deliver State of the Union addresses in the years that he was doorkeeper.', 'lead_paragraph': 'James T. Molloy, the 34th and last doorkeeper of the House of Representatives, known for heralding the opening of joint sessions of Congress by bellowing “Mr. Speaker, the president of the United States!” from the rear of the House chamber, died on Tuesday in Rochester. He was 75.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/us/dogMOLLOY/dogMOLLOY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/us/dogMOLLOY/dogMOLLOY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/24/us/dogMOLLOY/dogMOLLOY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'James T. Molloy, Last Doorkeeper of the House, Is Dead at 75', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'James T. Molloy, 75, Final Doorkeeper of House', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-24T00:42:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dennis Hevesi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dennis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hevesi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/b28cf723-b347-5dcb-9493-8ae839d5f260', 'word_count': 576, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b28cf723-b347-5dcb-9493-8ae839d5f260'}, {'abstract': 'In a book that came out four months after the assassination of President John F. Kennedy, Mr. Leslie wrote that a climate of right-wing extremism had primed Dallas to become the scene of a national tragedy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/24/us/24leslie.html', 'snippet': 'In a book that came out four months after the assassination of President John F. Kennedy, Mr. Leslie wrote that a climate of right-wing extremism had primed Dallas to become the scene of a national tragedy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Warren Leslie, who in 1964 raised hackles in Dallas, his adopted hometown, when he contended in a book that a climate of right-wing extremism had primed the city to become the scene of a national tragedy — the assassination of President John F. Kennedy — died on July 6 at his home in Chicago. He was 84.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/us/doLESLIE1-obit/doLESLIE1-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 708, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/us/doLESLIE1-obit/doLESLIE1-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/24/us/doLESLIE1-obit/doLESLIE1-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Warren Leslie Dies at 84; Wrote