y Council, witnessed the marriage of Justin Daniel, 32, right, and Joshua Cogswell, 35, in Brooklyn. The couple have been together for 10 years. When Mr. Daniel had trouble removing his ring so that Mr. Cogswell could put it back on for the ceremony — he had had it on for so long — Ms. Quinn unleashed one of her trademark belly laughs, joking that it reminded her of an “I Love Lucy” episode. Mr. Cogswell said that the couple had not expected the council speaker to attend their wedding, but that having the surprise guest “was awesome.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gay Marriage | Downtown Brooklyn, 10:40 A.M.', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-24T17:23:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e954897-da00-5106-a511-7ab66c2e99da', 'word_count': 105, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e954897-da00-5106-a511-7ab66c2e99da'}, {'abstract': 'A Civil War-era provision in the 14th Amendment makes for an interesting discussion on whether President Obama could use it to unilaterally raise the debt ceiling.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/us/politics/25legal.html', 'snippet': 'A Civil War-era provision in the 14th Amendment makes for an interesting discussion on whether President Obama could use it to unilaterally raise the debt ceiling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — A few days ago, former President Bill Clinton identified a constitutional escape hatch should President Obama and Congress fail to come to terms on a deficit reduction plan before the government hits its borrowing ceiling.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The 14th Amendment, the Debt Ceiling and a Way Out', 'kicker': 'Legal Memo', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The 14th Amendment, the Debt Ceiling and a Way Out', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fourteenth Amendment (US Constitution)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Bill', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-24T17:26:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Liptak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liptak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4f770bd-c111-5ec6-a18b-e02c9c677061', 'word_count': 777, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4f770bd-c111-5ec6-a18b-e02c9c677061'}, {'abstract': 'Esmeralda Santiago’s latest work is a sweeping historical novel set on a plantation in her native Puerto Rico.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/books/esmeralda-santiagos-conquistadora-is-a-puerto-rican-epic.html', 'snippet': 'Esmeralda Santiago’s latest work is a sweeping historical novel set on a plantation in her native Puerto Rico.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KATONAH, N.Y. — On a cold, clear January day in 2008 Esmeralda Santiago walked downstairs to her office in her hilltop home here to immerse herself in writing the final pages of “Conquistadora,” her new novel. She was a week away from the deadline for this epic about her beloved Puerto Rico featuring a big cast of characters that includes the slave-driving, sugar plantation queen of the title, one Ana Cubillas. But when Ms. Santiago opened the computer document of her manuscript that day, the words looked something like this: Agttt Higg Bowq Sm. Pvxef byiz alwb.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/25/books/25esmeralda-web/25esmeralda-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/25/books/25esmeralda-web/25esmeralda-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/25/books/25esmeralda-web/25esmeralda-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Puerto Rico in History, Imagined and Real', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Puerto Rico In History, Imagined And Real', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santiago, Esmeralda', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Puerto Rico', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-24T17:41:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicia R. Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicia', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/39c78ab1-b5ce-5e73-a3a7-170264ca53cc', 'word_count': 1119, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39c78ab1-b5ce-5e73-a3a7-170264ca53cc'}, {'abstract': 'The question of whether to combine last names had not come up before in 19 years for one couple, but on a historic day, they had to decide.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/24/gay-marriage-to-hyphenate-or-not-to-hyphenate/', 'snippet': 'The question of whether to combine last names had not come up before in 19 years for one couple, but on a historic day, they had to decide.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BUFFALO — The issue was names. Last names. Would they be adopting each other’s? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gay Marriage | To Hyphenate, or Not to Hyphenate?', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-24T17:45:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Javier C. Hernández', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Javier', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Hernández', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df5794fc-84b4-539f-b252-444151a6e810', 'word_count': 365, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df5794fc-84b4-539f-b252-444151a6e810'}, {'abstract': 'For one volunteer, Judge Joseph Dawson, the first day of same-sex marriage in New York was bittersweet. His husband, whom he married in Connecticut, died of cancer in 2009.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/24/gay-marriage-for-many-judges-its-personal/', 'snippet': 'For one volunteer, Judge Joseph Dawson, the first day of same-sex marriage in New York was bittersweet. His husband, whom he married in Connecticut, died of cancer in 2009.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Of the fourteen judges who volunteered to marry gay and lesbian couples in the Bronx, many had come forward for a reason. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gay Marriage | For Many Judges, It’s Personal', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klein, Gerald', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-24T18:05:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adriane Quinlan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adriane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Quinlan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/10ac1031-78ce-5a4c-8930-e7ac087fe983', 'word_count': 204, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10ac1031-78ce-5a4c-8930-e7ac087fe983'}, {'abstract': 'Italy and Spain are major guarantors, but they may be next in line for aid if Europe’s debt crisis deepens.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/business/global/europes-troubled-countries-become-part-of-the-rescue-team.html', 'snippet': 'Italy and Spain are major guarantors, but they may be next in line for aid if Europe’s debt crisis deepens.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Can a bailout fund whose backers include some of the countries it may be called upon to bail out really succeed? That’s the question being asked by skeptical investors about the European Financial Stability Facility — the rescue fund of 440 billion euros, or $632 billion, that is being given new, 