W ORLEANS — At midnight last Saturday, friends and well-wishers sang “Happy Birthday” to the trumpet player who led the band that night at the Palm Court Jazz Cafe. When they finished, the trumpet player turned to a few young women sitting behind him.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/25/us/ORLEANS/ORLEANS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/25/us/ORLEANS/ORLEANS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/25/us/ORLEANS/ORLEANS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 696, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/25/us/ORLEANS/ORLEANS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/25/us/ORLEANS/ORLEANS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At 100, Still Keeping Time as the Leader of the Band', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At 100, Still Keeping Time as the Leader of the Band', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Orleans (La)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T00:02:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By DAVE THIER', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'THIER', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6af0f37a-4fbc-5e35-b1cc-7580bcebd179', 'word_count': 553, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6af0f37a-4fbc-5e35-b1cc-7580bcebd179'}, {'abstract': 'In western Libya, a deep and sometimes agonized frustration at the pace and target selection of air support from NATO is growing among members of the Transitional National Council and residents who live in harm’s way.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/24/in-libyas-west-signs-of-growing-frustration-with-nato/', 'snippet': 'In western Libya, a deep and sometimes agonized frustration at the pace and target selection of air support from NATO is growing among members of the Transitional National Council and residents who live in harm’s way.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the consistent experiences of reporting alongside opposition fighters in Libya is feeling the delineation between what the rank and file have to say of the NATO bombing campaign and the statements of the officials in the Transitional National Council, the de facto rebel authority.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Libya’s West, Signs of Growing Frustration With NATO', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qaddafi, Muammar el-', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'North Atlantic Treaty Organization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transitional National Council (Libya)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T00:04:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By C.J. Chivers', 'per