most scholars of the Civil War asks, what did the First Battle of Bull Run mean to American history?', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a hot July morning, exactly 150 years ago, the armies of the barely born Confederacy and the badly shaken United States surrounded the town of Manassas, not far from a creek called Bull Run, for miles around, in every direction. It was a Sunday. Some people thought one major battle would be the very war itself, the beginning and the end, the resolution of decades of arguing over the place of slavery in the future of the United States. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Meaning of Bull Run', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Slavery', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lincoln, Abraham', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T01:15:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward L. Ayers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Ayers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fa03783-c645-5178-b9e4-e5941f30c26a', 'word_count': 2178, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fa03783-c645-5178-b9e4-e5941f30c26a'}, {'abstract': 'As the league’s new collective bargaining agreement was worked out Sunday night, it was hoped that a vote could be held Monday so the players union could begin their own ratification process.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/sports/football/nfl-lockout-approaches-end-but-timetable-still-vague.html', 'snippet': 'As the league’s new collective bargaining agreement was worked out Sunday night, it was hoped that a vote could be held Monday so the players union could begin their own ratification process.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the executive committee of the N.F.L. Players Association preparing to gather in Washington, a late request by players to have an opt-out clause inserted into the new collective bargaining agreement was the last loose end to be settled before a vote could be taken that would lead to the end of the lockout. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/25/sports/YNFL/YNFL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 737, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/25/sports/YNFL/YNFL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/25/sports/YNFL/YNFL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'End of N.F.L. Lockout Is Imminent, if Elusive', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'End of N.F.L. Lockout Is Imminent, if Elusive', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collective Bargaining', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League Players Assn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lockouts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T01:24:19+0000', 'document_t