58-2410-5c27-976c-e1cc88c89b92', 'word_count': 693, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8dc3458-2410-5c27-976c-e1cc88c89b92'}, {'abstract': 'The Murdoch hacking scandal, as explained by Shakespeare.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/opinion/25marche.html', 'snippet': 'The Murdoch hacking scandal, as explained by Shakespeare.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AT the hearing into the News of the World phone hacking scandal in London this past Tuesday, the commissioner of Scotland Yard did something unusual for a policeman. He quoted Shakespeare. Explaining the swiftness of his resignation, he mangled a bit of Macbeth: “If ’twere best it were done, ’twere well it were done quickly.” The reference was perfectly fitting for a scandal whose defining adjective is coming to be “Shakespearean.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/opinion/0725oped-art2/0725oped-art2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/24/opinion/0725oped-art2/0725oped-art2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/24/opinion/0725oped-art2/0725oped-art2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'More Than Kin, and Less Than Kind', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'More Than Kin, and Less Than Kind', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wiretapping and Other Eavesdropping Devices and Methods', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News of the World', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 3, 'major'