longside wine and food pairing sessions, cooking classes for children, and stalls selling fresh local produce. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'London Food Festival Hits Fifth Year', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T10:00:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claudia Barbieri', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claudia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barbieri', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8dda490a-78aa-5033-b005-f0d740c7d0e2', 'word_count': 277, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8dda490a-78aa-5033-b005-f0d740c7d0e2'}, {'abstract': 'Secretary of State Hillary Rodham Clinton clearly aimed her remarks in Hong Kong on Monday at Beijing’s leaders without explicitly criticizing China.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/26/business/global/clinton-urges-asian-nations-to-compete-fairly-in-world-markets.html', 'snippet': 'Secretary of State Hillary Rodham Clinton clearly aimed her remarks in Hong Kong on Monday at Beijing’s leaders without explicitly criticizing China.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — Secretary of State Hillary Rodham Clinton on Monday laid out an American economic agenda in Asia that emphasized broad international agreements over bilateral pacts, part of a wider theme of preserving American involvement in Europe and Asia.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/world/CLINTON/CLINTON-jumbo.jpg', 'heigh