isory practice.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/perella-weinberg-hires-jpmorgan-health-care-banker/', 'snippet': 'Perella Weinberg Partners has hired Christopher O’Connor, a health care banker at JPMorgan Chase, to help the boutique investment bank build out its medical devices advisory practice.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Perella Weinberg Partners has hired Christopher O’Connor, a health care banker at JPMorgan Chase, to help it build out its medical devices advisory practice.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Perella Weinberg Hires JPMorgan Health Care Banker', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JPMorgan Chase & Company', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Perella Weinberg Partners', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T10:57:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09fb45e9-3a8a-5073-a79e-29371ac41363', 'word_count': 151, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09fb45e9-3a8a-5073-a79e-29371ac41363'}, {'abstract': 'Can you match the promise to the person who made it at the 2011 Comic-Con in San Diego?', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/oaths-of-oddness-the-surprising-pledges-of-comic-con/', 'snippet': 'Can you match the promise to the person who made it at the 2011 Comic-Con in San Diego?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In pop culture as in politics, there are consumers so discerning that they will not commit disposable income or cast votes unless they know in advance exactly what they’re getting from a blockbuster movie or a candidate for office, and these people want their commitments up front – preferably in the form of a verbal oath or written pledge. If you make such a declaration as an election contender, you might be abdicating your “governing responsibilities in a period of incredibly rapid change and financial stress,” as Thomas Friedman has written, but if you do so as the star or creator of a forthcoming fantasy-themed work, you might just be participating in Comic-Con International, which wrapped up in San Diego over the weekend. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Oaths of Oddness: The Surprising Pledges of Comic-Con', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comic-Con (Convention)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ball, Alan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Del Toro, Guillermo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garfield, Andrew', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Groening, Matt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lorre, Chuck', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stewart, Kristen', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T11:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/30ca947c-2f3e-5405-8950-54332c04a838', 'word_count': 449, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30ca947c-2f3e-5405-8950-54332c04a838'}, {'abstract': 'Forrest Blue, one of the N.F.L.’s best centers of the early 1970s, died last week.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/forrest-blue-and-giving-offensive-linemen-their-due/', 'snippet': 'Forrest Blue, one of the N.F.L.’s best centers of the early 1970s, died last week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few thoughts about Forrest Blue, one of the N.F.L.’s best centers of the early 1970s. Blue was residing at an assisted-living facility in Carmichael, Calif., when he died last week at age 65 or 66 (There is some discrepancy as to whether he was born in 1944 or in 1945.) According to his daughter, Blue began exhibiting symptoms of dementia about 15 years ago. His brain will be sent to Boston University for further study. Andy Barall writes about pro football history for The Fifth Down.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Forrest Blue, and Giving Offensive Linemen Their Due', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco 49ers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T11:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Barall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6672a25-4e6e-52da-8408-e31cbd01f393', 'word_count': 807, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6672a25-4e6e-52da-8408-e31cbd01f393'}, {'abstract': 'In this week’s Complaint Box: People who refer to themselves in the third person are called “illeists,” from the Latin meaning “that man.” And they must stop.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/complaint-box-third-person-epidemic/', 'snippet': 'In this week’s Complaint Box: People who refer to themselves in the third person are called “illeists,” from the Latin meaning “that man.” And they must stop.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I sat next to two teenagers on the subway a couple of weeks ago and cringed as one of them repeatedly referred to herself in the third person: “Jessie so doesn’t wear Converse” and “Jessie’s sister? Freak show!” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Complaint Box | Third-Person Epidemic', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook.com', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T11:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rebecca Bazell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rebecca', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bazell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/98e16871-29a9-55ac-98de-675e496f45c3', 'word_count': 644, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98e16871-29a9-55ac-98de-675e496f45c3'}, {'abstract': 'Plus: Does technology sometimes make you less productive?', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/this-week-in-small-business-are-small-businesses-the-answer/', 'snippet': 'Plus: Does technology sometimes make you less productive?', 'lead_paragraph': 'What’s affecting me, my clients and other small-business owners this week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'This Week in Small Business: Are Small Businesses the Answer?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T11:00:41+0000', 'document_type