ors focused on the debt ceiling talks in Washington.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/26/business/Daily-Stock-Market-Activity.html', 'snippet': 'Stocks closed lower, but not at their lowest point of the day, as investors focused on the debt ceiling talks in Washington.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The lack of a deal to raise the debt limit in the United States hung over the financial markets on Monday, unsettling investors because of the uncertainty but not provoking a major reaction in bond or stock prices.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shares Down Moderately on U.S. Debt Talks', 'kicker': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Shares Down Moderately on U.S. Debt Talks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T13:11:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f002bacb-b2ac-5d8b-8ba9-b0b00dd424f0', 'word_count': 672, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f002bacb-b2ac-5d8b-8ba9-b0b00dd424f0'}, {'abstract': 'Brad Falchuk, a creator and producer of “Glee,” said that Lea Michele, Chris Colfer and Cory Monteith will remain with the series in Season 4, following remarks by Ryan Murphy, a fellow creator and producer, were interpreted to mean that those actors were departing after Season 3.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/glee-stars-wont-leave-series-after-graduation-producers-say/', 'snippet': 'Brad Falchuk, a creator and producer of “Glee,” said that Lea Michele, Chris Colfer and Cory Monteith will remain with the series in Season 4, following remarks by Ryan Murphy, a fellow creator and producer, were interpreted to mean that those act...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Which “Glee” stars will still be with the cast of that hit Fox musical comedy at this time next year? The answer seems to depend on whom you ask and when you ask it. In the most recent response to that question, Brad Falchuk, a creator and executive producer of “Glee,” said on Sunday that the lead actors Lea Michele, Chris Colfer and Cory Monteith will remain with the series in Season 4, days after remarks by Ryan Murphy, a fellow creator and executive producer, were interpreted to mean that those actors were departing after Season 3.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Glee’ Stars Won’t Leave Series After Graduation, Producers Say', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T13:18:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c82b224a-dd62-548d-bf47-133980140d19', 'word_count': 449, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c82b224a-dd62-548d-bf47-133980140d19'}, {'abstract': 'Wealthy families charter planes to fly their children to summer camp, same-sex couples marry in New York, the gold lovefest continues and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/monday-reading-traveling-to-summer-camp-via-private-jets/', 'snippet': 'Wealthy families charter planes to fly their children to summer camp, same-sex couples marry in New York, the gold lovefest continues and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and online in our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Monday Reading: Traveling to Summer Camp Via Private Jets', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T13:30:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Siegel Bernard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': 'Siegel', 'lastname': 'Bernard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6bfd02e-61c9-5adc-9ba5-814da254a615', 'word_count': 200, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6bfd02e-61c9-5adc-9ba5-814da254a615'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/morning-take-out-291/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Writing Again, Third Point’s Loeb Takes Swipe at Obama | Daniel S. Loeb, the founder of Third Point, isn’t shy about speaking his mind.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Take-Out', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T13:37:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': No