e death toll at 39, including two Americans. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/world/26wreck1_span/26wreck1_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/26/world/26wreck1_span/26wreck1_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/world/26wreck1_span/26wreck1_span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 689, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/world/26wreck1_span/26wreck1_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/26/world/26wreck1_span/26wreck1_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'China Finds More Bodies, and a Survivor, in Trains’ Wreckage', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China Finds More Bodies, and a Survivor, in Trains’ Wreckage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Railroads', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Railroad Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transit Systems', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T16:09:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sharon LaFraniere', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sharon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'LaFraniere', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5118be9a-6996-55c2-8269-e7f8fdf2fb84', 'word_count': 553, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5118be9a-6996-55c2-8269-e7f8fdf2fb84'}, {'abstract': 'A small but growing number of field biologists study urban evolution — the biological changes that cities bring to the wildlife that inhabits them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/26/science/26evolve.html', 'snippet': 'A small but growing number of field biologists study urban evolution — the biological changes that cities bring to the wildlife that inhabits them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To study evolution, Jason Munshi-South has tracked elephants in central Africa and proboscis monkeys in the wilds of Borneo. But for his most recent expedition, he took the A train.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/science/26EVOL_337/26EVOL_337-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 250, 'width': 337, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/science/26EVOL_337/26EVOL_337-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/26/science/26EVOL_337/26EVOL_337-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Evolution Right Under Our Noses', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Evolution Right Under Our Noses', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Urban Areas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evolution', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mice', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insects', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bacteria', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T16:15:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Zimmer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zimmer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/753516b0-339c-5dbc-ae5f-37702a7db190', 'word_count': 2434, 'uri': 'nyt://article/753516b0-339c-5dbc-ae5f-37702a7db190'}, {'abstract': 'After years of development, Michael Murphy’s “Golf in the Kingdom” has been turned into a film by the director Susan Streitfeld and the producer Mindy Affrime.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/26/movies/the-novel-golf-in-the-kingdom-is-now-a-film.html', 'snippet': 'After years of development, Michael Murphy’s “Golf in the Kingdom” has been turned into a film by the director Susan Streitfeld and the producer Mindy Affrime.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For many golfers Michael Murphy’s 1972 novel, “Golf in the Kingdom,” is practically a sacred text. It’s about a young man, modeled on Mr. Murphy himself, who on his way to an ashram in India stops off in Scotland, where his life is transformed by an encounter with a golf pro and mystic named Shivas Irons, who knows as much about Pythagoras and the Hindu scriptures as he does about hitting a high fade. Several filmmakers have felt similarly transported by reading the book, and “Golf in the Kingdom” has been optioned or in development since before it was even published. Gus Van Sant was interested for a while. Sean Connery was approached about playing Shivas. Clint Eastwood fell in love with the book and clung to the rights for a decade or so before giving up. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/arts/KINGDOM/KINGDOM-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/26/arts/KINGDOM/KINGDOM-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/arts/KINGDOM/KINGDOM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/arts/KINGDOM/KINGDOM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/26/arts/KINGDOM/KINGDOM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Mystical Tale, From Tee to Green', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Mystical Tale, From Tee to Green', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murphy, Michael', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Streitfeld, Susan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T16:29:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles McGrath', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGrath', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/11d8831a-8db0-56ef-a1b4-daf7f7f18c55', 'word_count': 1172, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11d8831a-8db0-56ef-a1b4-daf7f7f18c55'}, {'abstract': 'How would you grade President Obama’s approach to environmental and energy issues?', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/varied-views-of-obamas-environmental-record/', 'snippet': 'How would you grade President Obama’s approach to environmental and energy issues?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yale Environment 360, an online publication of the university’s school of forestry and environmental studies, has rounded up some assessments of President Obama’s performance on environment and energy issues as his first term shifts into its home stretch. The commentary comes from people as varied as Joe Romm of the liberal Center for American Progress, who gives the president an “F,” to Kenneth Green of the libertarian American Enterprise Institute, who criticizes the president for letting the Environmental Protection Agency overstep its bounds.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Varied Views of Obama’s Environmental Record', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidents and Presidency (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ENVIRONMENT', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T16:38:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ab17569-f481-5ade-a106-6efa1e48a4f8', 'word_count': 267, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ab17569-f481-5ade-a106-6efa1e48a4f8'}, {'abstract': 'Philadelphia’s bar scene is flourishing thanks to a focus on local brews and a community of excellent taprooms, pubs and bars.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/drink-up-north-philly-beer-part-1/', 'snippet': 'Philadelphia’s bar scene is flourishing thanks to a focus on local brews and a community of excellent taprooms, pubs and bars.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Poplar Street, between Second and Third Street in the Northern Liberties neighborhood of Philadelphia, there sits a placard placed by the Pennsylvania Historical and Museum Commission. It reads, “AMERICA’S FIRST LAGER: In 1840, John Wagner brought lager yeast from his native Bavaria and brewed the nation’s first lager beer. Later, other German immigrants began brewing lagers, which soon became popular & promoted growth of America’s brewing industry.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Drink Up | North Philly Beer, Part 1', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T16:42:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jordan Michelman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jordan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Michelman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f54495f-8cde-5dee-b8ea-c0b911e6737d', 'word_count': 1197, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f54495f-8cde-5dee-b8ea-c0b911e6737d'}, {'abstract': 'Plenty of people wake up at 40 having saved nothing or having spent their savings because of lack of discipline or economic necessity.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/to-the-people-who-havent-saved-anything-yet/', 'snippet': 'Plenty of people wake up at 40 having saved nothing or having spent their savings because of lack of discipline or economic necessity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carl Richards is a certified financial planner in Park City, Utah. His sketches are archived here on the Bucks blog and on his personal Web site, BehaviorGap.com.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'To the People Who Haven’t Saved Anything Yet', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Savings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T16:45:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Richards', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Richards', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4562ec03-a13c-554d-9754-bf99e65a59ac', 'word_count': 637, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4562ec03-a13c-554d-9754-bf99e65a59ac'}, {'abstract': 'Fans of Wall Street intern blogs have reason to cheer: an anonymous blogger has begun chronicling his 10-week banking internship, warts and all.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/the-intern-blogger-returns/', 'snippet': 'Fans of Wall Street intern blogs have reason to cheer: an anonymous blogger has begun chronicling his 10-week banking internship, warts and all.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good news for those who mourned the disappearance of Mumbles, the banking intern who began blogging pseudonymously this summer and promptly quit after two posts: a new Wall Street intern blogger has made his debut.', '