dth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Perfect Vinaigrette', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Salads', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Salad Dressings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T16:52:32+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'David Frank', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Frank', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/6ad6d51b-8930-5405-97ca-0eb4d75dc3ad', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/6ad6d51b-8930-5405-97ca-0eb4d75dc3ad'}, {'abstract': 'Nashi, a pro-Kremlin organization, and Prime Minister Vladimir V. Putin were both positively referenced in the manifesto written by Anders Behring Breivik.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/26/world/europe/26russia.html', 'snippet': 'Nashi, a pro-Kremlin organization, and Prime Minister Vladimir V. Putin were both positively referenced in the manifesto written by Anders Behring Breivik.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — A Russian youth group and Prime Minister Vladimir V. Putin strove on Monday to distance themselves from positive references to them in the manifesto written by Anders Behring Breivik, the avowed anti-immigrant extremist who is the lone suspect in the mass killings in Norway.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia Youth Group and Putin Distance Themselves From Killer’s Compliments', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia Youth Group and Putin Distance Themselves from Killer’s Compliments', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nashi', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Breivik, Anders Behring', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Norway', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T16:55:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew E. Kramer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Kramer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e85ea1c-7eb7-5377-9850-530c9959bfad', 'word_count': 336, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e85ea1c-7eb7-5377-9850-530c9959bfad'}, {'abstract': 'Vinaigrette is easy, but there are a few little tricks involved. Learn them in this video.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/what-the-well-dressed-salad-is-wearing-this-summer/', 'snippet': 'Vinaigrette is easy, but there are a few little tricks involved. Learn them in this video.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Are you wilting faster than an overdressed salad? I am. It’s hot out, and to me that’s salad weather. (Actually, every season is salad weather to me, but I crave it more as the temperature rises.) The best-tasting salads rely on good greens lightly coated in a well-made vinaigrette, which is a snap to make once you know a few little tricks. The first is to always dissolve the salt in the acid before adding the oil. Then give it a good whisking or, even easier, shake, shake, shake it up in a jar. To see it all come together, watch my latest video.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What the Well-Dressed Salad Is Wearing This Summer', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Salad Dressings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Salads', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T16:55:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18ed6c8e-54bd-572f-8569-52ad50658b77', 'word_count': 167, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18ed6c8e-54bd-572f-8569-52ad50658b77'}, {'abstract': 'Following the release of a new Irish government report criticizing the Vatican’s response to the sexual abuse of children by Irish priests, Prime Minister Enda Kenny denounced the church in an impassioned speech.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/video-of-irish-leaders-speech-attacking-the-vatican/', 'snippet': 'Following the release of a new Irish government report criticizing the Vatican’s response to the sexual abuse of children by Irish priests, Prime Minister Enda Kenny denounced the church in an impassioned speech.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As my colleague Rachel Donadio reports, “the Vatican has recalled its ambassador to Ireland following the release of an Irish government report that the Vatican had discouraged efforts by bishops to report cases of sex abuse to the police.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video of Irish Leader’s Speech Attacking the Vatican', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Clergy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Priests', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kenny, Enda', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ireland', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T16:57:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7af6d631-c175-50cb-936d-c8c7ee8b14e6', 'word_count': 327, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7af6d631-c175-50cb-936d-c8c7ee8b14e6'}, {'abstract': 'The first season of Joe Mauer’s eight-year, $184 million contract has been perhaps the most trying of his career.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/26/sports/baseball/grumbles-mix-with-cheers-for-mauer-a-hometown-hero.html', 'snippet': 'The first season of Joe Mauer’s eight-year, $184 million contract has been perhaps the most trying of his career.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MINNEAPOLIS — The limestone that covers the outer walls of Target Field is said to be 450 million years old. It was quarried in Mankato, Minn., and gives the park a warm kind of glow, not only from the outside but also from the dugout roofs, the backstop and the corner walls, near the foul poles. It is local, enduring and appealing.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/sports/baseball/26mauer1/26mauer1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/26/sports/baseball/26mauer1/26mauer1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/sports/baseball/26mauer1/26mauer1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/sports/baseball/26mauer1/26mauer1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/26/sports/baseball/26mauer1/26mauer1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Booing the Boy Next Door', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Booing the Boy Next Door', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mauer, Joe', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gardenhire, Ron', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Minnesota Twins', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T17:01:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/530c4ddf-4e69-54af-b32d-18186a94f38c', 'word_count': 1297, 'uri': 'nyt://article/530c4ddf-4e69-54af-b32d-18186a94f38c'}, {'abstract': 'Whatever happens this week with Washington’s debt talks, the economy will likely be worse off.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/on-debt-talks-a-lose-lose-lose-lose-situation/', 'snippet': 'Whatever happens this week with Washington’s debt talks, the economy will likely be worse off.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Endemol/NBC Universal Sorry, Howie Mandel: Deal or no deal, the American economy probably still loses.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Debt Talks, a Lose-Lose-Lose-Lose Situation', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interest Rates', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T17:04:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b7b65f9-4fcb-5b5c-b0ad-f8c3abf784f7', 'word_count': 858, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b7b65f9-4fcb-5b5c-b0ad-f8c3abf784f7'}, {'abstract': 'Does anything stand out when you compare the following passages, the first from Raymond Chandler’s “Farewell, My Lovely,” the second from John Buchan’s “The 39 Steps”?', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/two-shots-of-hooch/', 'snippet': 'Does anything stand out when you compare the following passages, the first from Raymond Chandler’s “Farewell, My Lovely,” the second from John Buchan’s “The 39 Steps”?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Does anything stand out when you compare the following passages, the first from Raymond Chandler’s “Farewell, My Lovely,” the second from John Buchan’s “The 39 Steps”?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Shots of Hooch', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker'