,000 employees, 10.5 percent of its work force.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As it struggles with the declining popularity of the BlackBerry line of smartphones, Research In Motion said on Monday that it would begin laying off about 2,000 employees, 10.5 percent of its work force, this week.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With BlackBerry in Decline, RIM Will Shed 2,000 Jobs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With BlackBerry in Decline, RIM Will Shed 2,000 Jobs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Research In Motion Ltd', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T17:41:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/51b4747b-5777-5084-b7ee-53376473ce94', 'word_count': 592, 'uri': 'nyt://article/51b4747b-5777-5084-b7ee-53376473ce94'}, {'abstract': 'Urk. And I mean that.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/moderation-fails-blog-issues/', 'snippet': 'Urk. And I mean that.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Times comment moderation software, which works badly even when it’s working well, is currently not working at all. I’ll come back to your comments later today, maybe.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Moderation Fails (Blog Issues)', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T17:42:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bbf687e0-d342-5e53-8aed-29ea339a5e9d', 'word_count': 34, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bbf687e0-d342-5e53-8aed-29ea339a5e9d'}, {'abstract': 'The Democratic House leader requested an investigation after a newspaper reported allegations of inappropriate sexual behavior by Representative David Wu, Democrat of Oregon.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/pelosi-seeks-ethics-investigation-of-wus-conduct/', 'snippet': 'The Democratic House leader requested an investigation after a newspaper reported allegations of inappropriate sexual behavior by Representative David Wu, Democrat of Oregon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Democratic leaders in the House have called for an immediate ethics investigation into allegations that Representative David Wu, a Democrat from Oregon, engaged in unwanted sexual activity with a teenage daughter of a donor.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pelosi Seeks Ethics Investigation of Wu’s Conduct', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pelosi, Nancy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wu, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House Committee on Ethics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oregon', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T17:53:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/64ea22ca-1d82-51e1-a67c-c5eac9fb1e45', 'word_count': 427, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64ea22ca-1d82-51e1-a67c-c5eac9fb1e45'}, {'abstract': 'The study could be foreshadowing the effect of climate change on Earth, its lead author says.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/26/science/26obearth.html', 'snippet': 'The study could be foreshadowing the effect of climate change on Earth, its lead author says.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two hundred million years ago, at the end of the Triassic period, a mass extinction, often attributed to major volcanic activity, wiped out half of all marine life on Earth. But new research published in the journal Science suggests that the extinction was more likely to have been caused by the release of at least 12,000 gigatons of methane from the seafloor into the atmosphere. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/science/26OBEXTINCT/26OBEXTINCT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 415, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/26/science/26OBEXTINCT/26OBEXTINCT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 415}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/science/26OBEXTINCT/26OBOX3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 757, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/science/26OBEXTINCT/26OBEXTINCT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name'