tection Bureau has ignited fear on Wall Street. But many banks may eventually benefit from the regulator’s careful watch, according to a new report by Moody’s Investors Service.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Moody’s Sees Benefits for Banks From Consumer Bureau', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cordray, Richard', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Financial Protection Bureau', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Moody's Investors Service Inc", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T18:15:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55544db2-4b1d-5982-81ad-b7bd39e8d494', 'word_count': 347, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55544db2-4b1d-5982-81ad-b7bd39e8d494'}, {'abstract': 'The Norway-based manufacturer of the Think City, which filed for bankruptcy in June, was purchased by a Russian investor.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/think-global-gets-a-russian-lifeline/', 'snippet': 'The Norway-based manufacturer of the Think City, which filed for bankruptcy in June, was purchased by a Russian investor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A month after filing for bankruptcy, which marked the fourth time in the company’s history that it suffered a financial collapse, Think Global AS has been saved, again.', 'source': 'The New York Ti