e chief executive duties starting next year.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/deutsche-bank-taps-co-ceos-to-replace-ackermann/', 'snippet': 'Deutsche Bank resolved a leadership crisis, saying that Anshu Jain and Jürgen Fitschen will share chief executive duties starting next year.', 'lead_paragraph': '7:45 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Deutsche Bank Names Co-C.E.O.’s to Succeed Ackermann', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ACKERMANN, JOSEF', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jain, Anshu', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deutsche Bank AG', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T18:32:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Ewing', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ewing', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7bc7d7d2-98cd-5275-98f3-70851e850149', 'word_count': 870, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7bc7d7d2-98cd-5275-98f3-70851e850149'}, {'abstract': 'In a speech, the mayor will indirectly criticize President Obama and Congressional leaders, suggesting they have behaved irresponsibly and irrationally.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/debt-crisis-has-already-hurt-economy-bloomberg-says/', 'snippet': 'In a speech, the mayor will indirectly criticize President Obama and Congressional leaders, suggesting they have behaved irresponsibly and irrationally.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg, in a blistering critique of Washington politics, will argue on Monday that the failure of national leaders to reach an agreement on the debt ceiling has already done damage to the economy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Debt Crisis Has Already Hurt Economy, Bloomberg Says', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T18:33:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Javier C. Hernández', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Javier', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Hernández', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ed1c6fe-d72f-5db2-bdf8-2031950da2cb', 'word_count': 315, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ed1c6fe-d72f-5db2-bdf8-2031950da2cb'}, {'abstract': '“When I started spending time with the man who would be my husband, I began to notice a strong and pleasing odor of coffee wafting up from his feet.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/26/books/excerpt-the-memory-of-all-that-by-katharine-weber.html', 'snippet': '“When I started spending time with the man who would be my husband, I began to notice a strong and pleasing odor of coffee wafting up from his feet.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I started spending time with the man who would be my husband, I began to notice a strong and pleasing odor of coffee wafting up from his feet. Not only did his shoes smell good, they also occasionally contained a few grains of actual coffee grounds. This was, I soon discovered, the consequence of Nick having purchased an enormous and ancient coffee grinder from a defunct A&P in Vermont for eight dollars. In his tiny makeshift cabin on the edge of a forest in rural Connecticut there was only one electrical outlet wired seriously enough not to blow all the fuses every time he ground coffee, and it was in the back of his only closet. How could I not fall in love with a man whose feet smelled of freshly ground coffee?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘The Memory of All That’', 'kicker': 'Excerpt', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T18:39:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katharine Weber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katharine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'First Chapter', '_id': 'nyt://article/808c6903-c258-5b1b-987a-243d75b9c6bd', 'word_count': 3625, 'uri': 'nyt://article/808c6903-c258-5b1b-987a-243d75b9c6bd'}, {'abstract': 'The novelist Katharine Weber brings many famous and glamorous names to her memoir, including that of her grandmother’s lover, George Gershwin.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/26/books/the-memory-of-all-that-by-katharine-weber-book-review.html', 'snippet': 'The novelist Katharine Weber brings many famous and glamorous names to her memoir, including that of her grandmother’s lover, George Gershwin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By all descriptions, the 1926 musical “Oh, Kay!” qualifies as light entertainment. But when the novelist Katharine Weber saw a 1989 revival, at the Goodspeed Opera House in Connecticut, the show came with weight attached. Its music was written by George Gershwin, who had been the lover of Kay Swift, Ms. Weber’s maternal grandmother, who may have inspired the show’s title character. In any case, one of Ms. Weber’s theatergoing companions, an old friend of the family, told her that Ms. Weber’s father had once been a beau of Ms. Swift, who had subsequently introduced him to her daughter, who became Ms. Weber’s mother. If that were true, then her father would have been her grandmother’s lover. The mind reels before this erotically annotated genealogy.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/arts/JPBOOK/JPBOOK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 680, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/arts/JPBOOK/JPBOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/26/arts/JPBOOK/JPBOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When Granny Met Gershwin, and Other Gossip', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Granny Met Gershwin, and Other Gossip', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Swift, Kay', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADULTERY', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weber, Katharine', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gershwin, George', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T18:39:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/bfebabcb-13f8-533a-912b-a091e1faa85a', 'word_count': 1124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bfebabcb-13f8-533a-912b-a091e1faa85a'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama urged “a balanced approach” that would include higher tax revenues as well as cuts. Speaker John A. Boehner accused Mr. Obama of asking for “a blank check.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/26/us/politics/26fiscal.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama urged “a balanced approach” that would include higher tax revenues as well as cuts. Speaker John A. Boehner accused Mr. Obama of asking for “a blank check.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Democratic-led Senate and Republican-led House on Monday barreled toward a showdown on competing plans to cut spending and raise the debt limit as a resolution to the intensifying crisis remained farther from sight just one week before a possible federal default.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/us/26fiscal2_span/26fiscal2_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/26/us/26fiscal2_span/26fiscal2_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/us/26fiscal2_span/26fiscal2_span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/us/26fiscal2_span/26fiscal2_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/26/us/26fiscal2_span/26fiscal2_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Showdown Nears on Debt as Obama Warns of ‘Crisis’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Congress Heads For Showdown On Debt Plans', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reid, Harry', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T18:40:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Hulse and Jackie Calmes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hulse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jackie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Calmes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/79ded1d6-6da6-5a50-9f13-d16cb2e2132b', 'word_count': 1211, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79ded1d6-6da6-5a50-9f13-d16cb2e2132b'}, {'abstract': '“Watch the Throne,” which has been touted on Facebook by the rappers, will initially only be available on iTunes.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/highly-anticipated-kanye-west-and-jay-z-album-set-for-release/', 'snippet': '“Watch the Throne,” which has been touted on Facebook by the rappers, will initially only be available on iTunes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After months of speculation on hip-hop blogs and in publications, Kanye West and Jay-Z announced on Monday that they would release their first album together, titled “Watch the Throne,” (Roc-A-Fella. Roc Nation/ Def Jam) on Aug. 8. But the record will initially only be available through iTunes. The album will go on sale in record stores and on Internet outlets four days later.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Highly Anticipated Kanye West and Jay-Z Album Set for Release', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jay-Z', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mayfield, Curtis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ocean, Frank', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Redding, Otis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'West, Kanye', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Def Jam', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook.com', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'iTunes', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T18:54:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/026ac7a1-85b0-5f6a-8ea5-153a494e5fe4', 'word_count': 220, 'uri': 'nyt://article/026ac7a1-85b0-5f6a-8ea5-153a494e5fe4'}, {'abstract': 'Dr. David A. Ansell writes about his years working at Cook County Hospital in Chicago, where treating patients was often a medical and political struggle.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/26/health/views/26zuger.html', 'snippet': 'Dr. David A. Ansell writes about his years working at Cook County Hospital in Chicago, where treating patients was often a medical and political struggle.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Man down in the men’s washroom!” This cry is not part of the usual hospital soundtrack, but when Dr. David A. Ansell heard it as he sped down a corridor in the old Cook County Hospital in Chicago, he barely broke stride. He veered into the men’s room, tried the locked door of the stall where a crumpled body lay, hoisted himself up over the fetid contents of the adjacent toilet, balanced on the metal divider and prepared to descend and administer CPR. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/science/26ZUGE/26ZUGE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 760, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/science/26ZUGE/26ZUGE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/26/science/26ZUGE/26ZUGE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Their Zeal Changed Lives, if Not the System', 'kicker': 'Books', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Their Zeal Changed Lives, if Not The System', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emergency Medical Treatment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3,