'nyt://article/1e158604-1e0f-5b41-a5a6-b3651f3cb13b'}, {'abstract': 'The Brooklyn-based artist Kenneth E. Parris III is on tour with members of the Merce Cunningham Dance Company, documenting their two-year Legacy Tour.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/drawing-dance-the-cunningham-company-at-lincoln-center/', 'snippet': 'The Brooklyn-based artist Kenneth E. Parris III is on tour with members of the Merce Cunningham Dance Company, documenting their two-year Legacy Tour.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Brooklyn-based artist Kenneth E. Parris III is on tour with members of the Merce Cunningham Dance Company, documenting their two-year Legacy Tour through a series of drawings and paintings. After 58 years, the company is scheduled to disband on New Year’s Day 2012. This is the sixth in a series of graphite drawings he plans to create from the road, providing a front-row seat to the final weeks of the company’s journey. This week’s entry is from Lincoln Center.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Drawing Dance: The Cunningham Company at Lincoln Center', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cunningham, Merce, Dance Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T19:30:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc182ab1-0cb4-5ee1-b1b1-36083f329890', 'word_count': 133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc182ab1-0cb4-5ee1-b1b1-36083f329890'}, {'abstract': 'Some dolphins use marine basket sponges to forage for food because it allows them to uncover prey undiscoverable by echolocation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/26/science/26obdolphin.html', 'snippet': 'Some dolphins use marine basket sponges to forage for food because it allows them to uncover prey undiscoverable by echolocation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the 1980s it was discovered that some bottlenose dolphins in Shark Bay, Australia, rip up marine basket sponges from the seafloor and place them on their beaks for protection as they forage for food along rocky substrate. It is the only known instance of tool use by dolphins in the wild.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/science/26OBDOLPHIN/26OBDOLPHIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 375, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/26/science/26OBDOLPHIN/26OBDOLPHIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 375}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/science/26OBDOLPHIN/26OBOX2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/science/26OBDOLPHIN/26OBDOLPHIN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/26/science/26OBDOLPHIN/26OBDOLPHIN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dolphin Tool Helps to Find Fare on Seafloor', 'kicker': 'Observatory', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dolphin Tool Helps To Find Fare on Seafloor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dolphins and Porpoises', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tools', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T19:35:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sindya N. Bhanoo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sindya', 'middlename': 'N.', 'lastname': 'Bhanoo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd2eea9e-d7a8-5e19-ab5e-2997ad2ea1c0', 'word_count': 317, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd2eea9e-d7a8-5e19-ab5e-2997ad2ea1c0'}, {'abstract': 'The autopsy of Amy Winehouse was inconclusive Monday, and family and fans will have to wait weeks for toxicology reports.  Meanwhile, sales of the singer’s records online continued to surge after her death Saturday.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/sales-for-amy-winehouses-music-spike-after-her-death/', 'snippet': 'The autopsy of Amy Winehouse was inconclusive Monday, and family and fans will have to wait weeks for toxicology reports.  Meanwhile, sales of the singer’s records online continued to surge after her death Saturday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Medical examiners in London were unable Monday to pinpoint what killed Amy Winehouse, the 27-year-old pop singer found dead in her home Saturday, and it will take at least two weeks before toxicology tests are completed, the Metropolitan Police said, according to the Associated Press.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Winehouse Autopsy Inconclusive; Sales of Singer’s Records Increase Online', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winehouse, Amy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'iTunes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nielsen SoundScan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TMZ.com', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T19:35:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr. and Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr.', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/96267db4-748d-558e-b3e7-d9e21ade387e', 'word_count': 549, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96267db4-748d-558e-b3e7-d9e21ade387e'}, {'abstract': 'Letter in response to Jeffrey Rosen’s review of James B. Stewart’s “Tangled Webs.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/31/books/review/the-nature-of-a-lie.html', 'snippet': 'Letter in response to Jeffrey Rosen’s review of James B. Stewart’s “Tangled Webs.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Nature of a Lie', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Nature of a Lie', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T19:37:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/92ed5239-98cf-5864-82a2-b8bc200f3661', 'word_count': 190, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92ed5239-98cf-5864-82a2-b8bc200f3661'}, {'abstract': 'Like most news these days, I found out that singer Amy Winehouse had died via Twitter. Immediately, my feed was filled up with heartfelt condolences from friends, fans and other musicians, M.I.A. even released a demo, as a tribute to Winehouse.I wish I were surprised by the tragic development. The news stories of Winehouse’s deterioration and death confirmed that she was not long for the world.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/catching-amy-winehouse/', 'snippet': 'Like most news these days, I found out that singer Amy Winehouse had died via Twitter. Immediately, my feed was filled up with heartfelt condolences from friends, fans and other musicians, M.I.A. even released a demo, as a tribute to Winehouse.I w...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like most of the media world, I learned that Amy Winehouse had died via Twitter, as my\xa0timeline filled up with heartfelt condolences from friends, fans and other musicians. M.I.A. even released a tribute demo.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Catching Amy Winehouse', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T19:41:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tony Gervino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gervino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41b017f1-e010-5f92-a093-e508b1e86e2c', 'word_count': 358, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41b017f1-e010-5f92-a093-e508b1e86e2c'}, {'abstract': 'Nick Davies, a journalist who has covered the hacking scandal in Britain extensively for the Guardian, has sold a book about the scandal titled “Hack Attack.”', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/british-journalist-sells-book-on-hacking-scandal/', 'snippet': 'Nick Davies, a journalist who has covered the hacking scandal in Britain extensively for the Guardian, has sold a book about the scandal titled “Hack Attack.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The hacking scandal in Britain has caught the attention of the publishing industry.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'British Journalist Sells Book on Hacking Scandal', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wiretapping and Other Eavesdropping Devices and Methods', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News of the World', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T19:54:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2aba8e1b-4cc9-5ae6-a869-1fc5d1dc5508', 'word_count': 112, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2aba8e1b-4cc9-5ae6-a869-1fc5d1dc5508'}, {'abstract': 'The Norway attack suspect appears in court; Democrats and Republicans offer different approaches to raising the debt ceiling; and the N.F.L. lockout ends.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/multimedia/100000000964720/timescast--july-25-2011.html', 'snippet': 'The Norway attack suspect appears in court; Democrats and Republicans offer different approaches to raising the debt ceiling; and the N.F.L. lockout ends.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Norway attack suspect appears in court; Democrats and Republicans offer different approaches to raising the debt ceiling; and the N.F.L. lockout ends.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/25/multimedia/video-tc-110725/video-tc-110725-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/25/multimedia/video-tc-110725/video-tc-110725-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/25/multimedia/video-tc-110725/video-tc-110725-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/25/multimedia/video-tc-110725/video-tc-110725-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'TimesCast | July 25, 2011', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Norway', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T19:55:19+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'ContinuousNews', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'Zena Barakat|Ben Solomon|Vijai Singh|Channon Hodge', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zena', 'middlename': 'Barakat', 'lastname': 'Ben', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/cb1b5fe1-38e1-5854-aaf8-daaa73e840a4', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/cb1b5fe1-38e1-5854-aaf8-daaa73e840a4'}, {'abstract': 'In the latest round of endorsements, Emily’s List endorses candidates who are trying to topple Republicans backed by the Tea Party.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/womens-committee-backs-3-democrats-for-house/', 'snippet': 'In the latest round of endorsements, Emily’s List endorses candidates who are trying to topple Republicans backed by the Tea Party.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Taking action against what it calls Republicans’ “war on women,” a political action committee that backs the candidacies of women who support abortion rights endorsed three Democrats on Monday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Women’s Committee Backs 3 Democrats for House', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T19:56:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Southall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Southall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/91abbd3d-6fe9-5615-9832-c8435892532f', 'word_count': 333, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91abbd3d-6fe9-5615-9832-c8435892532f'}, {'abstract': 'For years, contraception has been mostly a woman’s responsibility. But now scientists are studying treatments that may help men control fertility.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/putting-men-on-the-pill/', 'snippet': 'For years, contraception has been mostly a woman’s responsibility. But now scientists are studying treatments that may help men control fertility.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For years, contraception has been mostly a woman’s responsibility. But now scientists are studying new treatments that may help men control fertility.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Putting Men on the Pill', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T19:59:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Parker-Pope', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker-Pope', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3fcca8f2-6e97-5b12-8097-6782b6328d1f', 'word_count': 114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3fcca8f2-6e97-5b12-8097-6782b6328d1f'}, {'abstract': 'Between 1980 and 2000, the share of adults working was on average about 10 percentage points higher in the United States than in Europe. But that gap is closing.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/on-jobs-the-u-s-is-turning-into-europe/', 'snippet': 'Between 1980 and 2000, the share of adults working was on average about 10 percentage points higher in the United States than in Europe. But that gap is closing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hide your kids, and hide your wives. Economists’ worse fears have come true: The United States has been slowly turning into Europe.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Jobs, the U.S. Is Turning Into Europe', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Western Europe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T20:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/67a55f09-b13c-5b34-a1c0-8cec9cb6346f', 'word_count': 508, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67a55f09-b13c-5b34-a1c0-8cec9cb6346f'}, {'abstract': 'Are strict parental attitudes hurting or helping our kids?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/allowing-teen-sex-in-your-house/', 'snippet': 'Are strict parental attitudes hurting or helping our kids?', 'lead_paragraph': 'I have written here about the work of Amy Schalet, who has studied the divergent ways that Dutch and American parents talk to their children about sex (the Dutch are more accepting), and the apparent effects on teen pregnancy and sexually transmitted diseases in both countries (they are higher in the United States). ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Allowing Teenage Sex in Your House', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Youth', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T20:00:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Belkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca355c74-197a-5d40-bb8f-40c3fabee09a', 'word_count': 223, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca355c74-197a-5d40-bb8f-40c3fabee09a'}, {'abstract': 'Alia Penner brings her psychedelic brand of California color down to the clothing racks.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/shes-a-rainbow/', 'snippet': 'Alia Penner brings her psychedelic brand of California color down to the clothing racks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the artist Alia Penner’s eyes, everything looks better covered in rainbows. Not girly, pastel rainbows, but brilliant acid hues that bring to mind Peter Max and Sonia Delaunay. When the California-born artist isn’t painting rainbow-framed portals into alternate universes, she brings her pop psychedelic sensibility to album covers and posters for L.A. bands and happenings, helping to define the contemporary look of the city. Now, after dipping her toes into fashion with illustrations for Erin Wasson’s RVCA ad campaign and the hand-lettered titles for a Missoni film by Kenneth Anger, Penner, the former fashion editor of Arthur magazine, has introduced Mombi, a line of dresses named for a witch in Frank L. Baum’s Oz series, at Colette in Paris.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'She’s a Rainbow', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T20:00:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steffie Nelson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steffie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nelson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/635e132e-c1c6-576c-abed-08b3e82f67ea', 'word_count': 252, 'uri': 'nyt://article/635e132e-c1c6-576c-abed-08b3e82f67ea'}, {'abstract': 'The concept, which teases the successor for the brand’s compact S.U.V., is more aggressively styled than the current generation of the mini-ute.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/2012-honda-cr-v-concept-makes-web-debut/', 'snippet': 'The concept, which teases the successor for the brand’s compact S.U.V., is more aggressively styled than the current generation of the mini-ute.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The fourth generation of the CR-V, Honda’s bread-and-butter mini-ute, is officially on track to reach showrooms by the end of this year, with a revised interior, some flashy new bodywork and a more fuel-efficient 2.4-liter engine.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '2012 Honda CR-V Concept Makes Web Debut', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Honda Motor Co Ltd', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T20:00:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a32b02d5-4cbe-5dfa-ae21-6a4ee5a38a73', 'word_count': 243, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a32b02d5-4cbe-5dfa-ae21-6a4ee5a38a73'}, {'abstract': 'Bactrim, a commonly used medication, is more effective than cranberry at controlling infections, but it encourages the development of resistant strains of bacteria.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/26/health/research/26regimens.html', 'snippet': 'Bactrim, a commonly used medication, is more effective than cranberry at controlling infections, but it encourages the development of resistant strains of bacteria.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Women with recurrent urinary tract infections sometimes must take low-dose antibiotics for months to control the problem. Many prefer to try something less onerous, like cranberry extract or juice, which several studies have suggested can prevent these infections.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Regimens: Downside for a Urinary