dies has found, but it does not reduce the number of Caesarean sections or forceps deliveries.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Childbirth: A Drug Shortens Labor but Does Little Else', 'kicker': 'Vital Signs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Childbirth: A Drug Shortens Labor but Does Little Else', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Obstetrics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T20:44:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Research', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Bakalar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakalar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2c4ddf1-c156-56f1-8047-b731ea6d5c0f', 'word_count': 233, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2c4ddf1-c156-56f1-8047-b731ea6d5c0f'}, {'abstract': 'A quaint term has become code for an underground space that is not legally a bedroom, although many people may choose to use it that way.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/26/nyregion/a-rec-room-is-the-new-way-to-expand-an-apartment.html', 'snippet': 'A quaint term has become code for an underground space that is not legally a bedroom, although many people may choose to use it that way.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Selling real estate in New York has long involved its own sort of code. “Quiet” means dark, back-of-the-building; “cozy” means small; and “flexible” means “not really,” as in the “flex 1BR” that is actually a studio with a nook. But as developers seek to wring every last bit of space out of their projects, another term has cropped up more and more: “rec room,” meaning an underground space that is not legally a bedroom, although many people use it that way.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/nyregion/26appraisal/26appraisal-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/26/nyregion/26appraisal/26appraisal-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/nyregion/26appraisal/26appraisal-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/nyregion/26appraisal/26appraisal-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/26/nyregion/26appraisal/26appraisal-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Rec Room’ Is the New Way to Expand an Apartment', 'kicker': 'The Appraisal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'That Extra Underground Space? Call It a Rec Room', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basements and Cellars', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Buildings Department (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T20:45:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Diane Cardwell', 'person': [{'firstname