razzi and film crews, corporations and private citizens compete for space over the city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Helicopters swooped low over the Sepulveda Pass the weekend of July 16 to monitor the shutdown of Interstate 405. The week before, paparazzi helicopters hovered as Prince William and his wife, the Duchess of Cambridge, settled into Hancock Park. Indeed, every day brings a steady swarm of buzzing copters crisscrossing the vast Southern California sprawl in what many officials say are greater numbers than ever before.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/us/CHOPPERS-1/CHOPPERS-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/26/us/CHOPPERS-1/CHOPPERS-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/us/CHOPPERS-1/CHOPPERS-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 709, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/us/CHOPPERS-1/CHOPPERS-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/26/us/CHOPPERS-1/CHOPPERS-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Helicopters Jam the Skies Above Los Angeles', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Helicopter Traffic Jams the Skies Over Los Angeles', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Helicopters', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T21:27:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Nagourney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nagourney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed05dfa8-4304-53b6-afff-96c88c17f0e0', 'word_count': 972, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed05dfa8-4304-53b6-afff-96c88c17f0e0'}, {'abstract': 'A. O. Scott explores the existential predicaments that arise in Robert Zemeckis’s 1985 time-travel adventure.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/critics-picks-video-back-to-the-future/', 'snippet': 'A. O. Scott explores the existential predicaments that arise in Robert Zemeckis’s 1985 time-travel adventure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week, A. O. Scott remembers the ’80s and the ’50s with the high-energy Robert Zemeckis comedy/adventure “Back to the Future.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Critics’ Picks Video: ‘Back to the Future’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fox, Michael J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'LLOYD, CHRISTOPHER', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zemeckis, Robert', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T21:30:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72aa2e90-5bf6-5ffa-ada8-c59ca77951a9', 'word_count': 154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72aa2e90-5bf6-5ffa-ada8-c59ca77951a9'}, {'abstract': 'A new handbag line from designer Victoria Horning has no where to go but up.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/intern-rising-victoria-horning-handbags/', 'snippet': 'A new handbag line from designer Victoria Horning has no where to go but up.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I never carried a real handbag until I started designing them,” says the debutante accessories designer Victoria Horning. “But now, every morning I take the bag I choose to wear so seriously!” Horning, a 24-year-old Manhattanite who graduated from some of fashion’s most prestigious prep schools (read: internships at Vogue, Alexander Wang and Nina Ricci), had terrific experience and no place to tote it. So, she started a label, making bags and cummerbunds out of calf hair, leather, alligator and stingray. It was a relatively modest project — that is, until word got out and her girlfriends wanted in. Today, the made-in-New York collection features six handbags, including the off-white lambskin one that Horning chose for her appointment with T (above). “I just hope to see lots of girls wearing them, especially the Kates,” she says. “You know, Bosworth and Moss.” Oh, yes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Intern Rising | Victoria Horning Handbags', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T21:30:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8812a817-fc36-552f-9292-8c2be9564aca', 'word_count': 153, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8812a817-fc36-552f-9292-8c2be9564aca'}, {'abstract': 'Multiple universes are all the rage these days, and the new film “Another Earth” explores those crisscrossing worlds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/26/science/26view.html', 'snippet': 'Multiple universes are all the rage these days, and the new film “Another Earth” explores those crisscrossing worlds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The thing about parallel universes — which may be great or terrible — is that in theory they don’t collide.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/science/26VIEW/26VIEW-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/26/science/26VIEW/26VIEW-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 340}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/science/26VIEW/26VIEW-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/science/26VIEW/26VIEW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/26/science/26VIEW/26VIEW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'It’s Fashionable to Take a Trip to Another Universe', 'kicker': 'On View', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'It’s Fashionable to Take a Trip to Another Universe', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Physics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science Fiction', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cahill, Mike', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T21:33:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dennis Overbye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dennis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Overbye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e875e073-03c9-53bf-84d0-a7e3fa616d4b', 'word_count': 1129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e875e073-03c9-53bf-84d0-a7e3fa616d4b'}, {'abstract': 'Research increasingly suggests that men and women experience grief in different ways, and the realization has bolstered a nascent movement of bereavement groups geared to men throughout the country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/26/health/26grief.html', 'snippet': 'Research increasingly suggests that men and women experience grief in different ways, and the realization has bolstered a nascent movement of bereavement groups geared to men throughout the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1990, Sam and Gretchen Feldman cashed out on their share of a national chain of men’s apparel stores and retired to Martha’s Vineyard, Mass. There, they devoted their time to volunteer work and an active social calendar. The following years were golden ones for the Feldmans, but in 2007 Mrs. Feldman learned she had cancer. She died a year later. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/science/26GRIE1/26GRIE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/science/26GRIE1/26GRIE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy'