ip-hop of New York City. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/arts/marcelo-1/marcelo-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/arts/marcelo-1/marcelo-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/26/arts/marcelo-1/marcelo-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Paying Tribute to New York, by Way of Brazil', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Paying Tribute to New York, by Way of Brazil', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marcelo D2', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T21:43:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/363d2c36-b3f1-5611-8450-33c4d9822311', 'word_count': 435, 'uri': 'nyt://article/363d2c36-b3f1-5611-8450-33c4d9822311'}, {'abstract': 'After long hours policing financial firms, officials at Wall Street regulators duke it out on the diamonds of the National Mall with fellow overseers, local businesses and big corporations.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/on-this-field-regulators-find-no-one-is-too-big-to-fail/', 'snippet': 'After long hours policing financial firms, officials at Wall Street regulators duke it out on the diamonds of the National Mall with fellow overseers, local businesses and big corporations.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Too big to fail” is something to be feared and loathed in Washington — except on the softball field.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On This Field, Regulators Find No One Is Too Big to Fail', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Softball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Financial Protection Bureau', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Deposit Insurance Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Treasury Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T21:44:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess and Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/faab28a2-b077-521b-8e02-7a16f0d33532', 'word_count': 678, 'uri': 'nyt://article/faab28a2-b077-521b-8e02-7a16f0d33532'}, {'abstract': 'In the heat of summer, tomatoes, a rich source of vitamin A and vitamin C, are ripening in gardens everywhere. Today: a tomato, spelt and herb salad.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/health/nutrition/25recipehealth.html', 'snippet': 'In the heat of summer, tomatoes, a rich source of vitamin A and vitamin C, are ripening in gardens everywhere. Today: a tomato, spelt and herb salad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Elizabeth Eckholt, a chef in Northern California who specializes in “healing” foods, believes that greens, cucumbers, celery and seaweeds help maintain health by preventing the body from becoming overly acidic. This notion gives me pause, and for one big reason: I love tomatoes, and they are notoriously acidic.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/25/health/25recipehealth/25recipehealth-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/25/health/25recipehealth/25recipehealth-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/25/health/25recipehealth/25recipehealth-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/25/health/25recipehealth/25recipehealth-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/25/health/25recipehealth/25recipehealth-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/25/health/25recipehealth/25recipehealth-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/25/health/25recipehealth/25recipehealth-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Summer’s Treasure: Tomatoes', 'kicker': 'Recipes for Health', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Summer&#8217;s Treasure: Tomatoes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tomatoes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Salads', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T21:55:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Fitness & Nutrition', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Rose Shulman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': 'Rose', 'lastname': 'Shulman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'recipe', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d5d07b6-143c-5e37-9880-cafb1c57932f', 'word_count': 415, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d5d07b6-143c-5e37-9880-cafb1c57932f'}, {'abstract': 'In “Red Cloud Rising: The Fifth Wall,” participants must separate fact from fiction as they scour Lower Manhattan for clues to a feared force in international commerce.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/26/theater/red-cloud-rising-is-theater-on-lower-manhattan-streets.html', 'snippet': 'In “Red Cloud Rising: The Fifth Wall,” participants must separate fact from fiction as they scour Lower Manhattan for clues to a feared force in international commerce.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For 250 years Bydder Financial has been one of the most powerful forces in the global economy. It has underwritten the expansion of American multinational corporations, shaping the destiny of smaller countries to suit the priorities of the United States and of Bydder itself. From its august headquarters on Broad Street, barely a block from the New York Stock Exchange, Bydder stands astride international commerce like a colossus (or perhaps Croesus).', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/arts/REDCLOUD/REDCLOUD-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 358, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/26/arts/REDCLOUD/REDCLOUD-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 358}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/arts/REDCLOUD/REDCLOUD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 616, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/arts/REDCLOUD/REDCLOUD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/26/arts/REDCLOUD/REDCLOUD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'You Pursue a Wall Street Cabal. Or Do You?', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'You Pursue a Wall Street Cabal. Or Do You?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Arber, Gyda', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T22:00:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Seth Schiesel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schiesel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6879995-3be7-5ae0-95df-7b75aab17a77', 'word_count': 862, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6879995-3be7-5ae0-95df-7b75aab17a77'}, {'abstract': 'Survivors of the Utoya Island attack and those close to them expressed a mixture of guilt, anger, stoicism and confusion about Friday’s events.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/26/world/europe/26survivors.html', 'snippet': 'Survivors of the Utoya Island attack and those close to them expressed a mixture of guilt, anger, stoicism and confusion about Friday’s events.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OSLO — Tore Sinding Bekkedal cowered in a bathroom for most of the 90 minutes during which a Norwegian gunman unleashed his carnage on Friday on the island of Utoya, a sanctuary for center-left political debate among Norwegian youth.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Survivor Describes Moments of Terror in Attack in Norway', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Survivor Describes Moments of Terror in Attack in Norway', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Breivik, Anders Behring', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Utoya (Norway)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oslo (Norway)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T22:06:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew Saltmarsh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saltmarsh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ba1d1c5-1612-5801-a030-24a953574de0', 'word_count': 990, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ba1d1c5-1612-5801-a030-24a953574de0'}, {'abstract': 'Events in Europe, Washington and three Canadian cities last week honored the centennial of Marshall McLuhan, who introduced ideas like “the medium is the message” and “the global village” into everyday use.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/26/books/marshall-mcluhan-media-theorist-is-celebrated.html', 'snippet': 'Events in Europe, Washington and three Canadian cities last week honored the centennial of Marshall McLuhan, who introduced ideas like “the medium is the message” and “the global village” into everyday use.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OTTAWA — By the time Marshall McLuhan died in 1980, the once provocative voice that had propelled him to international stardom rare for an academic had been silenced by a stroke. In his home country, Canada, he had become something of a national embarrassment, often seen as an eccentric at best, a charlatan at worst. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/arts/JPMCLUHAN/JPMCLUHAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 739, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/arts/JPMCLUHAN/JPMCLUHAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/26/arts/JPMCLUHAN/JPMCLUHAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Early Media Prophet Is Now Getting His Due', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Early Media Prophet Is Now Getting His Due', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McLuhan, Marshall', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Toronto', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T22:13:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bbf7f089-2939-5cc7-91c6-544f2df4f8f9', 'word_count': 778, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bbf7f089-2939-5cc7-91c6-544f2df4f8f9'}, {'abstract': 'Several members of the family announced plans for a tribute concert in October. But Jackson’s estate said it had not authorized the event.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/michael-jackson-tribute-is-announced-then-questioned/', 'snippet': 'Several members of the family announced plans for a tribute concert in October. But Jackson’s estate said it had not authorized the event.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Several members of Michael Jackson’s family announced plans on Monday for a grand tribute concert in October. But those plans were immediately called into question when Jackson’s estate said it had not authorized the event, and two of Jackson’s brothers said they would not support it because the event was scheduled to take place during the criminal trial of Jackson’s doctor.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Michael Jackson Tribute Is Announced, Then Questioned', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jackson, Michael', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T22:17:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'repo