'snippet': 'The fiercest debate over an appropriations bill seemed to center on 39 riders that would hobble the regulation of big polluters and prevent the Department of Interior from listing new endangered species.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The House of Representatives began heated debate on Monday on an appropriations bill for the Department of Interior and Environmental Protection Agency that pits Republican critics of environmental regulation against Democrats who fear that landmark protections could be gutted. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Volleys Fly in House Debate on E.P.A. and Interior', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bishop, Tim', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCollum, Betty', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Simpson, Mike', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fish and Wildlife Service', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Interior Department', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T22:21:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanna M. Foster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported