6-a160-523d-a86e-ace7b6b34c05'}, {'abstract': 'Slide Show: A selection of readers’ photos from the weekend when New York legalized same-sex marriage.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/gay-marriage-a-reader-submitted-photo-album/', 'snippet': 'Slide Show: A selection of readers’ photos from the weekend when New York legalized same-sex marriage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Sunday, July 24, hundreds of gay and lesbian couples said “I do” on the first day of same-sex marriage in New York. To document the occasion, we asked readers to help us to create a wedding album. The above photo was submitted by Ruti Smithline, who took it in Brooklyn and wrote: ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gay Marriage | A Reader-Submitted Photo Album', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T22:27:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/196c7743-45bc-5159-85c9-87da696d67b1', 'word_count': 94, 'uri': 'nyt://article/196c7743-45bc-5159-85c9-87da696d67b1'}, {'abstract': 'Apple reveals its plans for a store in Grand Central Terminal.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/city-room-apples-plans-for-grand-central-terminal/', 'snippet': 'Apple reveals its plans for a store in Grand Central Terminal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Metropolitan Transportation Authority is gearing up to face a new challenge in traffic control: managing the masses of people lining up at Grand Central for the latest Apple release or Shake Shack burgers. At the transportation authority’s committee hearings Monday, the agency’s director of real estate, Jeffrey Rosen, confirmed that in the coming months Apple will open a store wrapping around the east side of the balcony at Grand Central terminal and a Shake Shack restaurant will open up in the basement, around the corner from the Oyster Bar. Read the entire blog post on City Room. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'City Room: Apple’s Plans for Grand Central Terminal', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grand Central Terminal (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T22:31:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce3ea8dd-8e42-5e94-b767-1f6f2c0d857c', 'word_count': 99, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce3ea8dd-8e42-5e94-b767-1f6f2c0d857c'}, {'abstract': 'Plans to move ABC’s “All My Children” to the Web after it ends its run in on the network may be delayed by a contractual roadblock.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/contract-talks-may-delay-soaps-move-to-the-web/', 'snippet': 'Plans to move ABC’s “All My Children” to the Web after it ends its run in on the network may be delayed by a contractual roadblock.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Prospect Park, a production company that plans to shift the soap operas “All My Children” and “One Life To Live” to the Web from television, has run into a contractual roadblock.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Contract Talks May Delay Soap’s Move to the Web', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None,