'abstract': 'As various federal taxes expired, most airlines lifted prices by an amount equal to the customer’s savings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/26/business/airlines-raise-fares-as-federal-taxes-expire.html', 'snippet': 'As various federal taxes expired, most airlines lifted prices by an amount equal to the customer’s savings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Let’s talk about taxes. Wait a second, come back here! I mean airfare taxes.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/business/Roadjp/Roadjp-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 870, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Bonanza for Airlines as Taxes End', 'kicker': 'On the Road', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Bonanza For Airlines As Taxes End', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-25T23:58:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Sharkey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sharkey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ded3025-3f9b-55f2-97b4-aca014b41a09', 'word_count': 930, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ded3025-3f9b-55f2-97b4-aca014b41a09'}, {'abstract': 'Readers’ accounts of their own survivor guilt illuminate an often ignored cost of war.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/shame-and-responsibility-a-response/', 'snippet': 'Readers’ accounts of their own survivor guilt illuminate an often ignored cost of war.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Writing about guilt feelings can open the floodgates to readers’ own painful and unresolved guilt, but also to outrage at those who should feel guilt, but don’t.\xa0 The probing and rich comments I received online and by e-mail about my essay, “The Moral Logic of Survivor Guilt,” touched on both responses and set me thinking more about the appropriateness of various guilt feelings.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shame and Responsibility: A Response', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-26T00:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nancy Sherman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nancy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sherman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/85e54c39-7732-5843-8b7e-b2b43625807a', 'word_count': 1374, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85e54c39-7732-5843-8b7e-b2b43625807a'}, {'abstract': 'The former defense editor writes that though the newspaper has become a punch line, he grew up with it, and loved it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/31/magazine/news-of-the-worlds-desperate-final-hours.html', 'snippet': 'The former defense editor writes that though the newspaper has become a punch line, he grew up with it, and loved it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As day broke over Libya a few weeks ago, so did reports that News of the World hacked the phones of a murdered teenager, the victims of the 7/7 London bombings and possibly soldiers killed in Iraq and Afghanistan. I was on a 410-foot-long British Navy warship that was firing missiles into Libya, covering the war for News of the World. I called my boss. “It couldn’t be much worse, son,” he said. “Get home.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/31/magazine/31dismissal/31dismissal-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 332, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/31/magazine/31dismissal/31dismissal-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/31/magazine/31dismissal/31dismissal-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'News of the World’s Desperate Final Hours', 'kicker': 'Dismissals', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘It Couldn’t Be Much Worse, Son’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News of the World', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wiretapping and Other Eavesdropping Devices and Methods', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brooks, Rebekah', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-26T00:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul McNamara', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McNamara', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c504f84c-269b-54b5-8ec2-7ade6d935cc7', 'word_count': 862, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c504f84c-269b-54b5-8ec2-7ade6d935cc7'}, {'abstract': 'After Friday’s deadly attacks in Norway, questions are growing about whether the police are equipped to deal with violent crime.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/26/world/europe/26police.html', 'snippet': 'After Friday’s deadly attacks in Norway, questions are growing about whether the police are equipped to deal with violent crime.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OSLO — When a man dressed in a police uniform began slaughtering young people at a Norwegian summer camp last week, one of the first to be killed was a real police officer named Trond Berntsen, who for years had worked in security at the camp. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/world/POLICE/POLICE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/26/world/POLICE/POLICE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 345}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/world/POLICE/POLICE-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/world/POLICE/POLICE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/26/world/POLICE/POLICE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Unsettling Wariness in Norway, Where Police Are Rarely Armed', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Where Police Are Rarely Armed, Norway Is Tense After Slaughter', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords':