-f48a0fc2b5ab'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Jerry Brown signed into law Monday legislation that would allow illegal immigrants to receive privately financed scholarships for state universities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/26/us/26brfs-HALFOFDREAMA_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Jerry Brown signed into law Monday legislation that would allow illegal immigrants to receive privately financed scholarships for state universities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Jerry Brown signed into law Monday legislation that would allow illegal immigrants to receive privately financed scholarships for state universities. The bill is part of package known as the California Dream Act, which would entitle those students to the same kind of state aid that American citizens and legal residents can receive. That bill has passed the state Assembly, but has not come to the floor for a vote in the Senate. The Democratic-controlled Legislature has passed similar bills in the past, but they were vetoed by then-Gov. Arnold Schwarzenegger, a Republican. Mr. Brown is a Democrat. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California: Half of ‘Dream’ Act Signed', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | WEST', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'California: Half of ‘Dream’ Act Signed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Development, Relief, and Education for Alien Minors Act', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigrants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Scholarships and Fellowships', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Edmund G Jr', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-26T00:58:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Medina', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Medina', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/5cdbcf15-b0ff-532f-a830-a7746146372d', 'word_count': 99, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5cdbcf15-b0ff-532f-a830-a7746146372d'}, {'abstract': 'The Mariners extended a franchise-record losing streak to 16 games with a 10-3 loss to the Yankees Monday night.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/26/sports/baseball/for-mariners-wins-and-answers-remain-out-of-reach.html', 'snippet': 'The Mariners extended a franchise-record losing streak to 16 games with a 10-3 loss to the Yankees Monday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The expansion Mariners pulled on their trident caps in 1977, and the logo choice might have angered Poseidon: fourteen consecutive losing seasons followed. They once employed a player whose surname came to epitomize offensive futility. Only one of the 28 cities that currently boast major league teams has never hosted a World Series game. That would be Seattle, and there seems a better chance of Starbucks banning coffee than that streak ending this October. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/sports/subMARINERS/subMARINERS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/sports/subMARINERS/subMARINERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/26/sports/subMARINERS/subMARINERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'h