, 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — It was the political scoop of the year, a damning, serialized exposé in The Daily Telegraph about how British politicians were abusing their parliamentary expense accounts to pay for things like moat-cleaning and wisteria-trimming. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/world/JP-MURDOCH/JP-MURDOCH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/26/world/JP-MURDOCH/JP-MURDOCH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/world/JP-MURDOCH/JP-MURDOCH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/world/JP-MURDOCH/JP-MURDOCH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/26/world/JP-MURDOCH/JP-MURDOCH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Murdoch Veterans Portray an Engaged Boss', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Murdoch Newspaper Veterans Portray a Fully Engaged Boss', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News of the World', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Times of London', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NEWS CORP', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sun, The (British Newspaper)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-26T02:36:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Lyall and Graham Bowley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lyall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Graham', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bowley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e60ce1e-d340-550f-b6da-841234747a8b', 'word_count': 1993, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e60ce1e-d340-550f-b6da-841234747a8b'}, {'abstract': 'Four Yankees took the stage at a Broadway theater to support a organization that provides musical instruction to individuals with disabilities.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/yankees-jump-on-stage-for-charity/', 'snippet': 'Four Yankees took the stage at a Broadway theater to support a organization that provides musical instruction to individuals with disabilities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It appeared as if the Yankees’ game Monday night in the Bronx could be rained out, but that did not stop some players from putting on a matinee performance on Broadway, with Nick Swisher belting out a Backstreet Boys song and Russell Martin playing bongo drums on stage.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yankees Jump on Stage for Charity', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cervelli, Francisco', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dickerson, Chris', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Russell', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'val