'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-26T02:38:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Money & Policy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Pear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pear', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f19435ef-3bef-5200-9e7a-791a18305fb0', 'word_count': 836, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f19435ef-3bef-5200-9e7a-791a18305fb0'}, {'abstract': 'Lawyers suing BP over last year’s oil spill in the Gulf of Mexico have filed a brief asking a federal judge to take over the $20 billion fund that the company established to compensate victims.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/26/us/26brfs-JUDGEISASKED_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'Lawyers suing BP over last year’s oil spill in the Gulf of Mexico have filed a brief asking a federal judge to take over the $20 billion fund that the company established to compensate victims.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lawyers suing BP over last year’s oil spill in the Gulf of Mexico have filed a brief asking a federal judge in New Orleans to take over the $20 billion fund that the company established to compensate victims. The lawyers argue that the fund has only paid some 16 percent of “interim” claims from people with continuing damage, calling it an “abject failure.” The fund, administered by Kenneth R. Feinberg, has paid $4.8 billion so far in emergency and final claims, including hundreds of millions of dollars in interim claims. Mr. Feinberg has argued that many claims are presented with inadequate documentation, and said, “20,000 interim claims and the payment of over $250 million is not exactly evidence of failure.” The brief also called for Judge Carl J. Barbier of Federal District Court to declare invalid the final settlements’ provisions releasing BP and other companies involved with the spill from further suits. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Louisiana: Judge Is Asked to Provide New Oversight for BP Fund', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | SOUTH', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Louisiana: Judge Is Asked to Provide New Oversight for BP Fund', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barbier, Carl J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feinberg, Kenneth R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Offshore Drilling and Exploration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BP Plc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gulf of Mexico', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-26T02:58:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Schwartz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwartz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/3bbbf61a-cf34-5bc0-8cfa-0522f7e499cd', 'word_count': 153, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3bbbf61a-cf34-5bc0-8cfa-0522f7e499cd'}, {'abstract': 'The Lincoln Center Dialogue series will be held at the David Rubenstein Atrium.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/lincoln-center-announces-new-discussion-series/', 'snippet': 'The Lincoln Center Dialogue series will be held at the David Rubenstein Atrium.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Business, not cultural affairs, will be on the breakfast menu at Lincoln Center this fall as the Center begins a morning series where leaders will “discuss significant issues facing American society.” Reynold Levy, the center’s president is to announce the breakfast series on Tuesday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lincoln Center Announces New Discussion Series', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brokaw, Tom', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-26T03:01:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Pogrebin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogrebin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/922bd392-090f-5b81-ae3b-97e38e8e6a12', 'word_count': 264, 'uri': 'nyt://article/922bd392-090f-5b81-ae3b-97e38e8e6a12'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Cacoyannis, most famous for “Zorba the Greek” with Anthony Quinn, also brought Greek drama to the stage and screen, including “Electra” with Irene Papas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/26/movies/michael-cacoyannis-director-of-zorba-the-greek-dies-at-90.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Cacoyannis, most famous for “Zorba the Greek” with Anthony Quinn, also brought Greek drama to the stage and screen, including “Electra” with Irene Papas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Michael Cacoyannis, a Greek filmmaker whose art-house films and adaptations of Euripides for\xa0stage and screen were critically acclaimed, but who was best known as the director of the 1964 Hollywood hit “Zorba the Greek,” died on Monday in Athens. He was 90.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/arts/obit-cavoyannis/obit-cavoyannis-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/26/arts/obit-cavoyannis/obit-cavoyannis-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/26/arts/obit-cavoyannis/obit-cavoyannis-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Michael Cacoyannis, Director of ‘Zorba the Greek,’ Dies at 90', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Michael Cacoyannis, Director of ‘Zorba,’ Dies at 90', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-26T03:04:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Vitello', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vitello', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/23a51bbe-86c9-5793-aa61-746adf0d50af', 'word_count': 665, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23a51bbe-86c9-5793-aa61-746adf0d50af'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on July 26, 2011.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/26/pageoneplus/corrections-july-26.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on July 26, 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': 'INTERNATIONAL', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: July 26', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-26T03:18:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/1fdafc8e-4b44-563a-a686-715b1846831f', 'word_count': 471, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1fdafc8e-4b44-563a-a686-715b1846831f'}, {'abstract': 'The risk of a default starts to increase exponentially as we get nearer to the deadline for raising the debt limit, but Wall Street may not be getting that message.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/25/washington-is-out-of-touch-how-about-wall-street/', 'snippet': 'The risk of a default starts to increase exponentially as we get nearer to the deadline for raising the debt limit, but Wall Street may not be getting that message.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The stock market, digesting Friday afternoon’s news of a breakdown in negotiations between President Obama and the House speaker, John A. Boehner, on plans to raise the federal debt limit, behaved relatively calmly today, with the Dow Jones shedding 0.7 percent to close at 12,593 points.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Washington Is Out of Touch. How About Wall Street?', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dow Jones Stock Average', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-26T03:37:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a261ec2-9ff1-5b0c-a14e-68055bbf58fa', 'word_count': 1107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a261ec2-9ff1-5b0c-a14e-68055bbf58fa'}, {'abstract': 'The latest actions by House Republicans push the nation to the brink of ruinous default.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/26/opinion/26tue1.html', 'snippet': 'The latest actions by House Republicans push the nation to the brink of ruinous default.', 'lead_paragraph': 'House Republicans have lost sight of the country’s welfare. It’s hard to conclude anything else from their latest actions, including the House speaker’s dismissal of President Obama’s plea for compromise Monday night. They have largely succeeded in their campaign to ransom America’s economy for the biggest spending cuts in a generation. They have warped an exercise in paying off current debt into an argument about future spending. Yet, when they win another concession, they walk away.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Republican Wreckage', 'kicker