was charged with crimes relating to the fatal overdose of Derek Boogaard of the Rangers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MINNEAPOLIS — The family of the late Derek Boogaard came to the defense of Aaron Boogaard, who faces charges of drug distribution and tampering in connection with the fatal overdose of his brother, a former enforcer for the Minnesota Wild and Rangers. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Boogaard Charges Are ‘Just Plain Wrong,’ Family Says', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boogaard, Aaron', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boogaard, Derek', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Rangers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-26T14:49:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Branch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Branch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bcf3856d-aca3-501b-9e56-6b68ab6e1bc2', 'word_count': 731, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bcf3856d-aca3-501b-9e56-6b68ab6e1bc2'}, {'abstract': 'McLaren sends three racecars to Spa-Forchamps, Fiat sets a show date for its 500 Abarth and Mercedes squeezes 510 horsepower from its 6.3-liter V-8.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/26/wheelies-the-highly-attuned-edition/', 'snippet': 'McLaren sends three racecars to Spa-Forchamps, Fiat sets a show date for its 500 Abarth and Mercedes squeezes 510 horsepower from its 6.3-liter V-8.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In which we bring you motoring news from around the Web:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wheelies: The Highly Attuned Edition', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fiat SpA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ford Motor Company', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Infiniti Division of Nissan Motor Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mercedes-Benz', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-26T15:17:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fea4ec5c-e685-5930-b9c7-1d3dec75f52c', 'word_count': 394, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fea4ec5c-e685-5930-b9c7-1d3dec75f52c'}, {'abstract': '“From the Sky Down,” directed by Davis Guggenheim and charting the creation and legacy of the album “Achtung Baby,” will make its debut at a gala presentation on Sept. 8.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/26/u2-documentary-will-open-toronto-film-festival/', 'snippet': '“From the Sky Down,” directed by Davis Guggenheim and charting the creation and legacy of the album “Achtung Baby,” will make its debut at a gala presentation on Sept. 8.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Long before Bono and the Edge were best known as the composers of the Broadway musical “Spider-Man: Turn Off the Dark,” they and their U2 band mates Adam Clayton and Larry Mullen Jr. were more immediately associated with best-selling rock albums like “Achtung Baby.” It is this more felicitous time in the band’s history that is revisited in Davis Guggenheim’s documentary “From the Sky Down,” which will open the 2011 Toronto International Film Festival, the festival’s organizers said on Tuesday. The new film from Mr. Guggenheim, the director of “An Inconvenient Truth” and “Waiting for Superman,” will chronicle the creation and legacy of “Achtung Baby,” the 1991 U2 album that included hits like “One” and “Mysterious Ways,” using archival footage and new interviews. It will make its debut at a gala presentation on Sept. 8.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U2 Documentary Will Open Toronto Film Festival', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Toronto International Film Festival', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Aung San Suu Kyi, Daw', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bono', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clayton, Adam', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cronenberg, David', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Edge, The', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Emmerich, Roland', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Freud, Sigmund', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Friedkin, William', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Guggenheim, Davis', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jung, Carl Gustav', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Madonna', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Meirelles, Fernando', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Payne, Alexander', 'rank': 18, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oakland Athletics', 'rank': 19, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'U2', 'rank': 20, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-26T15:20:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c541b831-cff9-518f-b9d4-ad818f09d629', 'word_count': 253, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c541b831-cff9-518f-b9d4-ad818f09d629'}, {'abstract': 'Is there a place for empathy in the judicial system?  How much should jurists identify with litigants in a case when determining the extent of damage done in a case?', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/26/thinking-cap-legal-empathy/', 'snippet': 'Is there a place for empathy in the judicial system?  How much should jurists identify with litigants in a case when determining the extent of damage done in a case?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thinking Cap is about work in progress in the world of ideas.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thinking Cap: Legal Empathy', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Georgetown University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-26T15:30:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a95c9cf-42af-533c-bede-a846044d3574', 'word_count': 526, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a95c9cf-42af-533c-bede-a846044d3574'}, {'abstract': 'Well, recent Japanese economic history, anyway.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/26/everyone-should-learn-japanese/', 'snippet': 'Well, recent Japanese economic history, anyway.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OK, maybe not. But you really shouldn’t be commenting on current economic events unless you’ve studied the last time a major economy found itself up against the zero lower bound on interest rates. Those of us who had paid attention to Japan knew that large increases in the monetary base wouldn’t be inflationary and that large government borrowing wouldn’t drive up interest rates. Those who hadn’t got it completely wrong.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Everyone Should Learn Japanese', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-26T15:41:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac325580-6ccb-5793-9bba-bcbc1e6fcaf7', 'word_count': 225, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac325580-6ccb-5793-9bba-bcbc1e6fcaf7'}, {'abstract': 'A lawyer for the man charged in Friday’s attacks in Norway told reporters on Tuesday that his client appeared to be insane. The day before, the suspect’s estranged father told Norwegian television his son should have killed himself.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/26/video-of-remarks-by-oslo-suspects-lawyer-and-his-estranged-fathers-response/', 'snippet': 'A lawyer for the man charged in Friday’s attacks in Norway told reporters on Tuesday that his client appeared to be insane. The day before, the suspect’s estranged father told Norwegian television his son should have killed himself.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At a news conference in Oslo on Tuesday, Geir Lippestad, a lawyer acting for Anders Behring Breivik, the anti-Muslim extremist who carried out Friday’s massacre in Norway, told reporters that his client said “he’s in a war, and he believes that when you are in a war you can do things like that without pleading guilty.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video of Remarks by Oslo Suspect’s Lawyer and His Estranged Father’s Response', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Breivik, Anders Behring', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Norway', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oslo (Norway)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-26T15:41:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2f40c2d-432c-5191-86c2-13e62ec9eaf5', 'word_count': 240, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2f40c2d-432c-5191-86c2-13e62ec9eaf5'}, {'abstract': 'Crime Scene Extra: A woman cannot bring herself to look at a mural of her brother, who was shot to death.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/26/a-killer-is-sentenced-but-the-heartache-remains/', 'snippet': 'Crime Scene Extra: A woman cannot bring herself to look at a mural of her brother, who was shot to death.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Elena Lopez, 68, came home from church that day two summers ago to a surprise. Several friends and family members were at her apartment in the Lower East Side.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Killer Is Sentenced, but the Heartache Remains', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Forbidden City (NYC Nightclub)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Village (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-26T15:42:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/11277f83-34b2-50c7-a419-7a648340833e', 'word_count': 596, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11277f83-34b2-50c7-a419-7a648340833e'}, {'abstract': 'She is the second person in New York City whose death on Saturday has been linked to the heat wave.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/26/brooklyn-girl-10-dies-from-heat/', 'snippet': 'She is the second person in New York City whose death on Saturday has been linked to the heat wave.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A 10-year-old Brooklyn girl died on Saturday from the heat, combined with an underlying medical condition, the medical examiner’s office said. She is the second person in the city whose death that day has been linked to the heat wave. Medical examiners released no information about the girl other than the time of death, 6:25 p.m. The high temperature on Saturday was 100 degrees. A 94-year-old woman also died Saturday of the heat, combined with an underlying disease. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Brooklyn Girl, 10, Dies From Heat', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Temperature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Office of the Chief Medical Examiner of the City of New York', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-26T15:50:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8175eb5-dcee-5809-a760-fd888bd0e431', 'word_count': 79, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8175eb5-dcee-5809-a760-fd888bd0e431'}, {'abstract': 'The lockout ends and free-agency mayhem begins as the N.F.L. tries to stuff an off-season of business into a few days.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/26/leading-off-plan-your-post-lockout-party-or-dont/', 'snippet': 'The lockout ends and free-agency mayhem begins as the N.F.L. tries to stuff an off-season of business into a few days.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Considering how long and ridiculous the N.F.L. lockout was, you might think a little elation would break out when it finally ended Monday. But if it weren’t for the hyperventilating television types proclaiming their long nightmare over, the reaction would have been a sea of rolled eyeballs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Leading Off: Plan Your Post-Lockout Party, or Don’t', 'kicker': 'The Fifth 