therine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/adafb445-2a2a-5fb5-acdc-7a59121fc39f', 'word_count': 261, 'uri': 'nyt://article/adafb445-2a2a-5fb5-acdc-7a59121fc39f'}, {'abstract': 'Brooklyn’s butchers travel north with a pig, some wine and a gaggle of hungry students.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/26/maine-course-gastronomy-in-the-great-outdoors/', 'snippet': 'Brooklyn’s butchers travel north with a pig, some wine and a gaggle of hungry students.', 'lead_paragraph': '“We don’t have preset menus, or really plan ahead. We drive to Maine a couple days in advance with salt, olive oil, butter, a pig, knives and, oh yeah, wine,” says Tom Mylan of the Meat Hook, Brooklyn’s buzziest butcher shop. “When we arrive on the coast, we look at what’s fresh and plentiful, and take it from there.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Maine Course | Gastronomy in the Great Outdoors', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-26T16:00:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katie Chang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/350500eb-3e11-553e-944d-14f088aa666b', 'word_count': 331, 'uri': 'nyt://article/350500eb-3e11-553e-944d-14f088aa666b'}, {'abstract': 'The longlist of 13 will be shortened to 6 in September, with the winner to be announced on Oct. 18.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/26/man-booker-prize-list-ranges-far-and-wide/', 'snippet': 'The longlist of 13 will be shortened to 6 in September, with the winner to be announced on Oct. 18.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An eclectic group of 13 writers was chosen on Tuesday for the longlist of this year’s Man Booker Prize, considered the most prestigious award for fiction in the English-speaking world. Stella Rimington, the chairwoman of the judges, said in a statement: “We are delighted by the quality and breadth of our longlist, which emerged from an impassioned discussion. The list ranges from the Wild West to multiethnic London via post-cold war Moscow and Bucharest, and includes four first novels.” The prize honors what the judges deem to be the best novel of the year by an author in the former British Commonwealth, Ireland or Zimbabwe.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Man Booker Prize List Ranges Far and Wide', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Man Booker Prize', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barnes, Julian', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barry, Sebastian', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DeWitt, Patrick', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hollinghurst, Alan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rimington, Stella', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rogers, Jane', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Granta', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jonathan Cape', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-26T16:02:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 