ight Cosmos Copa NYC title on Sunday, a uniquely New York event with a mini-World Cup feel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the final whistle sounded at Flushing Meadows on Sunday, the NYC Poland bench players rushed the field and a wild celebration ensued among the Polish supporters. With a 3-1 victory over NYC Senegal in the Cosmos Copa NYC final match, Poland had reclaimed its spot atop New York’s soccer elite and brought the title back to Greenpoint for the second consecutive year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For NYC Poland, Second Copa Title Doubly Sweet', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-26T17:54:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Belac', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belac', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b5989ae-81eb-56b9-998f-f913defe0873', 'word_count': 644, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b5989ae-81eb-56b9-998f-f913defe0873'}, {'abstract': 'Raúl Castro left the speeches to his vice president at a revolutionary hospital, another sign of the new tone he has adopted since taking over power from his brother Fidel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/27/world/americas/27cuba.html', 'snippet': 'Raúl Castro left the speeches to his vice president at a revolutionary hospital, another sign of the new tone he has adopted since taking over power from his brother Fidel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CIEGO DE ÁVILA, Cuba — For the second year in a row, Raúl Castro left the rhetoric to his vice president. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit'