count shopping, and a lot of what we pay (or don’t pay) for clothes comes down to timing. Missing those perfect loafers on eBay by mere seconds or logging on to a Gilt sale after it’s already been ravaged by the hungriest shoppers can be a major letdown. So, T editors scoured the Internet and designed a foolproof guide to shopping the best discount sites. Happy clicking!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Online Shopping | Time Zones', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-26T20:39:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lily Miesmer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Miesmer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a0e1e6e-5965-5611-95c1-609895ad855e', 'word_count': 516, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a0e1e6e-5965-5611-95c1-609895ad855e'}, {'abstract': 'The train crash that killed 39 people last week is part of a much broader pattern of transport safety problems, particularly on China’s roads.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/27/world/asia/27rail.html', 'snippet': 'The train crash that killed 39 people last week is part of a much broader pattern of transport safety problems, particularly on China’s roads.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — The high-speed train crash that killed 39 people last week has captured public attention in China, but it is part of a much broader pattern of transport safety problems, particularly on the country’s roads.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Road Safety Problems Pose Dire Threat in China', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Road Safety Problems Pose Dire Threat in China', 'name': None, 'seo': Non