now a part of our online lives.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/27/books/microstyle-by-christopher-johnson-review.html', 'snippet': 'The branding consultant Christopher Johnson explains how to think big and write small when we compose all those little bits that are now a part of our online lives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The mischievous Web site Gawker has marketed a T-shirt, aimed, you assume, at especially odious young people, that reads: “Yes, I am quietly judging you.” If there is to be a Second Coming, I hope Jesus will be good-humored enough to wear his.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/27/arts/BOOK/BOOK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 946, 'width': 666, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/27/arts/BOOK/BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/27/arts/BOOK/BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Wooing With Words in the Age of the Incredible Shrinking Message', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wooing With Words in the Age of the Incredible Shrinking Message', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'English Language', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-26T21:03:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dwight Garn