ell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/635f3809-5745-50e8-8478-cd02eb54cadd', 'word_count': 187, 'uri': 'nyt://article/635f3809-5745-50e8-8478-cd02eb54cadd'}, {'abstract': 'The House speaker vowed to tweak the legislation after the Congressional Budget Office estimated that his proposal would cut the deficit by about $850 billion, not $1 trillion.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/26/boehner-plan-falls-short-of-advertised-cuts-says-budget-agency/', 'snippet': 'The House speaker vowed to tweak the legislation after the Congressional Budget Office estimated that his proposal would cut the deficit by about $850 billion, not $1 trillion.', 'lead_paragraph': '6:49 p.m. | Updated The debt plan being pushed by House Speaker John A. Boehner would not meet a key demand by conservatives to cut spending by as much as the debt ceiling would be increased, the official budget agency for Congress said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Boehner Plan Falls Short of Advertised Cuts, Says Budget Agency', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Congressional Budget Office', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-26T22:38:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization'