recipe', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd6a60de-735d-5ef1-b596-2eb86d49aa9b', 'word_count': 226, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd6a60de-735d-5ef1-b596-2eb86d49aa9b'}, {'abstract': 'Anne Saxelby has drawn raves and an award in Manhattan for her work at Saxelby Cheesemongers in the Essex Street Market.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/27/dining/anne-saxelby-making-new-yorkers-say-cheese-feed-me.html', 'snippet': 'Anne Saxelby has drawn raves and an award in Manhattan for her work at Saxelby Cheesemongers in the Essex Street Market.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ANNE SAXELBY was having quite a day on the day I met with her this month. She was headed to Gracie Mansion for the city’s Neighborhood Achievement Awards, where Saxelby Cheesemongers, her five-year-old shop in the Essex Street Market, was named Manhattan’s Small Business of the Year. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/27/dining/27FEED1_SPAN/27FEED1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 332, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/27/dining/27FEED1_SPAN/27FEED1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 332}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/27/dining/27FEED1_SPAN/27FEED1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/27/dining/27FEED1_SPAN/27FEED1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/27/dining/27FEED1_SPAN/27FEED1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Making New Yorkers Say Cheese, Smile or No', 'kicker': 'Feed Me', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Making New Yorkers Say Cheese, Smile or No', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cheese', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-26T22:49:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Witchel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Witchel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/22244d0a-040e-5aa5-9268-574cdd59816a', 'word_count': 1040, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22244d0a-040e-5aa5-9268-574cdd59816a'}, {'abstract': 'Sky Foods, a new 36,000-square-foot supermarket in Flushing, Queens, stocks 30 kinds of live fish and shellfish, as well as Asian produce and other staples.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/27/dining/sky-foods-an-asian-supermarket-opens-in-flushing-food-stuff.html', 'snippet': 'Sky Foods, a new 36,000-square-foot supermarket in Flushing, Queens, stocks 30 kinds of live fish and shellfish, as well as Asian produce and other staples.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The choices are almost mind-boggling at Sky Foods, a 36,000-square-foot supermarket in a new shopping mall in Flushing, Queens. The seafood department stocks 30 kinds of live fish and shellfish, including Dungeness crabs for around $7.99 a pound, a nasty-looking freshwater fish called marble goby and, soon, live frogs. Meats have a vast counter and are also sold precut in packages, like fresh beef tendon, whole partridges and elegant rounds of sliced duck gizzards. The owner, Chung Fat Supermarket Group, which has other markets in the borough, and Ed Wu, the manager, have made a particular effort to stock organic Asian produce. Dried noodles line both sides of a 60-foot aisle. “Some of these noodles I can’t even name,” Mr. Wu said.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/27/dining/27STUF_MARKET/27STUF_MARKET-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/27/dining/27STUF_MARKET/27STUF_MARKET-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/27/dining/27STUF_MARKET/27STUFF2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/27/dining/27STUF_MARKET/27STUF_MARKET-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/27/dining/27STUF_MARKET/27STUF_MARKET-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lots of Fish Swim at Huge Asian Store', 'kicker': 'Food Stuff', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lots of Fish Swim at Huge Asian Store', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Supermarkets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-26T22:49:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b97322e0-7e84-5b40-afff-a9644fa44412', 'word_count': 225, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b97322e0-7e84-5b40-afff-a9644fa44412'}, {'abstract': 'Peels, stalks, rinds, stems — if home cooks reconsidered what should go into the pot, and what into the trash, what would they find?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/27/dining/thats-not-trash-thats-dinner.html', 'snippet': 'Peels, stalks, rinds, stems — if home cooks reconsidered what should go into the pot, and what into the trash, what would they find?', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAST week in Chelsea, Mich., as people wilted and vegetables flourished in the intense heat, Anne Elder ran through some of her favorite summer ingredients: pearly garlic “rounds” that flower at the top of the plant in hot weather, the spreading leaves of the broccoli plant, yellow dandelion flowers that she dips whole into batter and deep fries.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/27/dining/27SCRAPS_SPAN/27SCRAPS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/27/dining/27SCRAPS_SPAN/27SCRAPS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/27/dining/27SCRAPS_SPAN/27SCRAPS_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 712, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/27/dining/27SCRAPS_SPAN/27SCRAPS_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/27/dining/27SCRAPS_SPAN/27SCRAPS_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'That’s Not Trash, That’s Dinner', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'That’s Not Trash, That’s Dinner', 'name': None, 'seo': None, '