create time for Congress to raise the debt ceiling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — It turns out the federal government is sitting on some extra cash.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. May Have Way to Cover Bills After Deadline, for Week', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Analysts Unsure of Date U.S. Would Reach Debt Limit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Treasury Department', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-26T22:51:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Binyamin Appelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Binyamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Appelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c271c60-05df-56ec-8fb9-879c7b223c06', 'word_count': 520, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c271c60-05df-56ec-8fb9-879c7b223c06'}, {'abstract': 'East End Kitchen opens on the Upper East Side; Hotel Chantelle opens in a Ludlow Street rooftop garden; and other new restaurants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/27/dining/east-end-kitchen-hotel-chantelle-open-off-the-menu.html', 'snippet': 'East End Kitchen opens on the Upper East Side; Hotel Chantelle opens in a Ludlow Street rooftop garden; and other new restaurants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Opening', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Off the Menu', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Off the Menu', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-26T22:52:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e3fe4387-8b9c-52c0-b0ff-f7e732c38d13', 'word_count': 462, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3fe4387-8b9c-52c0-b0ff-f7e732c38d13'}, {'abstract': 'The Metropolitan Opera and the union representing choristers, stage managers, dancers and staff directors have reached an agreement on a new three-year contract, officials said on Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/27/arts/music/met-and-chorus-union-agree-on-contract.html', 'snippet': 'The Metropolitan Opera and the union representing choristers, stage managers, dancers and staff directors have reached an agreement on a new three-year contract, officials said on Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Metropolitan Opera and the union representing choristers, stage managers, dancers and staff directors have reached an agreement on a new three-year contract, officials said on Tuesday. Talks were continuing with the other two major unions at the Met, those representing the stagehands and orchestra. The agreement with the American Guild of Musical Artists, which covers the chorus, was reached in May and ratified on June 19 during the Met’s tour of Japan. Met officials wanted to hold off on the announcement until the other two contracts were settled. The chorus agreement was to have expired on Sunday, the same day that the other two agreements end: with the orchestra, represented by Local 802 of the American Federation of Musicians; and the stagehands, represented by Local 1 of the International Alliance of Theatrical Stage Employees. The guild employees received 2 percent raises for each year. The talks are being led by Joseph Volpe, the former general manager, who was succeeded by Peter Gelb. Mr. Volpe himself is a former stagehand and is considered well versed in labor matters at the Met. The Met finished this year without a deficit but has an accumulated deficit of $51 million, Mr. Gelb said. Pension funds are $78 million underfunded, and the endowment is $243 million, more than $100 million off its peak before the recession. “We have large financial weights hanging on our backs that we are constantly reminded of,” he said.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Met and Chorus Union Agree on Contract', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Met and Chorus Union Agree on Contract', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Alliance of Theatrical Stage Employees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN GUILD OF MUSICAL ARTISTS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN FEDERATION OF MUSICIANS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-26T22:55:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/51334633-7b81-513d-a65d-9bc5f3aee387', 'word_count': 243, 'uri': 'nyt://article/51334633-7b81-513d-a65d-9bc5f3aee387'}, {'abstract': 'A tasting of Italian dishes; a Friends of the Farmer tasting in Copake, N.Y.; a benefit for Jeff’s Kitchen and scholarships in Bridgehampton, N.Y.; and other events this wee