urrealist. Look at the morning’s home page or front page headlines: The world appears to be nothing but a series of nonsequiturs, bizarre conjunctions at every turn, a bundle of isolated phenomena with no apparent meaning or connection. Take two very recent events, each of them entirely singular, extraordinary, and in their different ways tragic. Just a few days ago, I read about them on the same page of a newspaper, immediately adjacent to one another, separated only by a thin black line. I was shocked by the proximity. It was like an oxymoron, or a Zen koan, I couldn’t make any sense of it. Amy Winehouse and Anders Behring Breivik.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Winehouse, Breivik and Deadly Ideals', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suicides and Suicide Attempts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Breivik, Anders Behring', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winehouse, Amy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Norway', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T00:10:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4df9ad0-cd64-5cd6-b8f7-3f7ef1b62f93', 'word_count': 1240, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4df9ad0-cd64-5cd6-b8f7-3f7ef1b62f93'}, {'abstract': 'Eric Chavez started at third for the Yankees on Tuesday, ending an 82-day stay on the disabled list that began when he broke a bone in his foot May 5.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/26/chavez-comes-off-the-disabled-list-and-into-the-yankees-lineup/', 'snippet': 'Eric Chavez started at third for the Yankees on Tuesday, ending an 82-day stay on the disabled list that began when he broke a bone in his foot May 5.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It had been so long since Eric Chavez saw his name on the Yankees lineup card that as he got dressed Tuesday afternoon, he admitted he was not sure when he had last played in a major league game.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chavez Comes Off the Disabled List and Into the Yankees’ Lineup', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chavez, Eric', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Girardi, Joe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Soriano, Rafael', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wedge, Eric', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Seattle Mariners', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T00:13:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Borden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f891d3c8-b1b7-5409-978a-2975a5ffdb91', 'word_count': 756, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f891d3c8-b1b7-5409-978a-2975a5ffdb91'}, {'abstract': 'Gen. Martin E. Dempsey, President Obama’s nominee to be chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff, warned that proposed cuts in the military budget would be “extraordinarily difficult.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/27/us/27military.html', 'snippet': 'Gen. Martin E. Dempsey, President Obama’s nominee to be chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff, warned that proposed cuts in the military budget would be “extraordinarily difficult.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Gen. Martin E. Dempsey, President Obama’s nominee to be chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff, warned on Tuesday that proposed cuts in the military budget of up to $1 trillion would be “extraordinarily difficult and very high risk.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/27/us/MILITARY/MILITARY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 639, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/27/us/MILITARY/MILITARY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/27/us/MILITARY/MILITARY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nominee to Lead Joint Chiefs Warns Against Deep Cuts', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nominee to Lead Joint Chiefs Warns Against Deep Cuts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dempsey, Martin E', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Joint Chiefs of Staff', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T00:21:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name