k': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa56947f-e3c2-549a-a385-a230ed2ba91f', 'word_count': 1128, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa56947f-e3c2-549a-a385-a230ed2ba91f'}, {'abstract': 'Relegated five years ago in the Calciopoli scandal, Juventus sees itself as resilient and resurgent, and hopes new leadership and a new stadium might pave the way back to the top of Serie A.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/26/pride-in-black-and-white/', 'snippet': 'Relegated five years ago in the Calciopoli scandal, Juventus sees itself as resilient and resurgent, and hopes new leadership and a new stadium might pave the way back to the top of Serie A.', 'lead_paragraph': 'George Vecsey writes about Juventus, Italian soccer’s Old Lady. Relegated five years ago in the Calciopoli scandal, it sees itself as resilient and resurgent, and hopes new leadership and a new stadium might pave the way back to the top of Serie A. Read the article here, and come back to comment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pride in Black and White', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T00:36:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f5bd61d-d2c4-5b5d-af16-2c7c007f2c10', 'word_count': 52, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f5bd61d-d2c4-5b5d-af16-2c7c007f2c10'}, {'abstract': 'With the lockout over, the frenzy of assembling 32 rosters begins. One agent said it was “like New Year’s Eve and the new millennium all rolled into one.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/27/sports/football/nfl-begins-a-really-short-off-season.html', 'snippet': 'With the lockout over, the frenzy of assembling 32 rosters begins. One agent said it was “like New Year’s Eve and the new millennium all rolled into one.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The madness really began Monday night, when the N.F.L. e-mailed a memo to all 32 teams at 6:20 p.m. telling them they were allowed to start negotiating contracts with rookies in 40 minutes. That was a change from the timeline the league had set out earlier in the day the lockout was put to rest, and it was so unexpected that at least one team told an agent it did not see the note for several hours after it was sent. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/27/sports/NFL3/NFL3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 976, 'width': 878, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/27/sports/NFL3/NFL3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/27/sports/NFL3/NFL3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'N.F.L. Begins Very Short Off-Season', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'It’s All a Blur as the N.F.L. Kicks Off an Unusually Short Off-Season', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Draft and Recruitment (Sports)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Palmer, Carson', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Free Agents (Sports)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lockouts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'va