s transparency and accountability and that its monitoring and enforcement is seriously inadequate.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/26/group-skewers-sustainable-logging-effort/', 'snippet': 'A World Wildlife Fund seeks to protect vulnerable forests by promoting global trade in sustainable timber.  But an investigative group says that the effort lacks transparency and accountability and that its monitoring and enforcement is seriously ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Less than one-fifth of the world’s forests are intact, and every year about 30 million acres are destroyed. With pressure on forests only expected to increase, the race is on to find a balancing point between commercial and conservation interests. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Group Skewers Sustainable Logging Effort', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biodiversity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Logging Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wood and Wood Products', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Global Witness', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Wildlife Fund', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T00:43:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanna M. Foster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1902378b-bac8-55de-a155-dd05c51d986b', 'word_count': 641, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1902378b-bac8-55de-a155-dd05c51d986b'}, {'abstract': 'George Osborne, the chancellor of the Exchequer, had extensive meetings with Rupert and James Murdoch.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/27/world/europe/27hacking.html', 'snippet': 'George Osborne, the chancellor of the Exchequer, had extensive meetings with Rupert and James Murdoch.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — As the phone hacking scandal struck the heart of British politics in recent weeks, one figure has been notably silent: the chancellor of the Exchequer, George Osborne, who, by several accounts, played a decisive role in bringing the former News of the World editor Andy Coulson into 10 Downing Street as a senior adviser. That move has deeply embarrassed the British government.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/27/world/HACKING/HACKING-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/27/world/HACKING/HACKING-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/27/world/HACKING/HACKING-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Meetings Indicate British Officials’ Links to Murdochs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Meetings Indicate British Officials’ Links to Murdochs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'British Sky Broadcasting Group (BSkyB)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News of the World', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Osborne, George', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocat