 network that has long been the centerpiece of Rupert Murdoch’s European ambitions.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'James Murdoch’s Future at Stake as BSkyB Board Meets', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'James Murdoch’s Future at Stake as BSkyB Board Meets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wiretapping and Other Eavesdropping Devices and Methods', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'British Sky Broadcasting Group (BSkyB)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NEWS CORP', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, James R', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T00:45:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Werdigier and Graham Bowley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werdigier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Graham', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bowley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2cfcfc0-dcf0-5f49-9263-e26dd5e76efa', 'word_count': 884, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2cfcfc0-dcf0-5f49-9263-e26dd5e76efa'}, {'abstract': 'A report from a federal agency said there was not enough evidence or research to say 9/11 had caused cancer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/27/nyregion/not-enough-evidence-to-link-911-and-cancer-report-finds.html', 'snippet': 'A report from a federal agency said there was not enough evidence or research to say 9/11 had caused cancer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is not enough evidence yet to say whether the dust and smoke cloud produced by the terrorist attack on the World Trade Center caused cancer, federal officials concluded in a report released on Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Scant Evidence to Link 9/11 to Cancer, U.S. Report Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Not Enough Evidence to Link 9/11 and Cancer, a Federal Report Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cancer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'James Zadroga 9-11 Health and Compensation Act', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Institute for Occupational Safety and Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T00:45:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anemona Hartocollis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anemona', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hartocollis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c06777c5-a7cd-5439-a550-fc8da31c0403', 'word_count': 916, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c06777c5-a7cd-5439-a550-fc8da31c0403'}, {'abstract': 'Removing Jeff Hathaway could cost the university more than $3 million.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/27/sports/ncaabasketball/uconn-said-to-be-pursuing-buyout-of-athletic-director.html', 'snippet': 'Removing Jeff Hathaway could cost the university more than $3 million.', 'lead_paragraph': 'These should be heady times for the University of Connecticut. The men’s basketball team won the national title in April, the football team played in its first Bowl Championship Series game in January and the women’s basketball program is widely considered the country’s premier program. Few athletic departments can compare with UConn’s recent accomplishments. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'UConn Said to Be Pursuing Buyout of Athletic Director', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'UConn Said to Be Pursuing Buyout of Athletic Director', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hathaway, Jeff', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Calhoun, Jim', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Connecticut', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Herbst, Susan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T00:48:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pete Thamel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pete', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thamel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c61bf9d3-2c50-57b9-9650-4e98c39e0387', 'word_count': 583, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c61bf9d3-2c50-57b9-9650-4e98c39e0387'}, {'abstract': 'Representative Luis V. Gutierrez, a Democrat from Illinois, said he decided to participate in the protest after President