s and even movie theaters to promote its new products.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/27/business/media/sharpie-aims-a-new-campaign-at-teenagers.html', 'snippet': 'Sharpie, the maker of pens and markers, is using social media, television, magazines and even movie theaters to promote its new products.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SHARPIE, whose permanent markers were immortalized by NFL receiver Terrell Owens when he pulled a Sharpie out of his sock to sign a football after scoring a touchdown, is turning to more minor celebrities to promote its products.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/27/business/Adco2/Adco2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/27/business/Adco2/Adco2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/27/business/Adco2/Adco2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Sharpie Campaign, Aimed at Teenagers, Urges Self-Expression', 'kicker': 'Advertising', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Sharpie Campaign, Aimed at Teenagers, Urges Self-Expression', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Online Advertising', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teenagers and Adolescence', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T01:37:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane L. Levere', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Levere', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/370c6148-4298-574c-98cf-bafe5e9a8fbd', 'word_count': 1002, 'uri': 'nyt://article/370c6148-4298-574c-98cf-bafe5e9a8fbd'}, {'abstract': 'A small water utility in California sued to challenge the wealthy farming interests that dominate two of the country’s largest water banks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/27/science/earth/27waterbank.html', 'snippet': 'A small water utility in California sued to challenge the wealthy farming interests that dominate two of the country’s largest water banks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BAKERSFIELD, Calif. — Peter Key knew something was strange when the water levels in his tropical fish tank began to go down last summer. Then the washing machine took 40 minutes to fill, and the toilets would not flush.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/27/us/27waterbank2_span/27waterbank2_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/27/us/27waterbank2_span/27waterbank2_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/27/us/27waterbank2_span/27waterbank2_span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/27/us/27waterbank2_span/27waterbank2_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/27/us/27waterbank2_span/27waterbank2_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Storing Water for a Dry Day Leads to Suits', 'kicker': 'Precious Waters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Storing Water For a Dry Day Leads to Suits', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AGRICULTURE', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T01:40:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicity Barringer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicity', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barringer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5dc27d4b-b5a9-5c61-b786-7f2389326012', 'word_count': 1208, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5dc27d4b-b5a9-5c61-b786-7f2389326012'}, {'abstract': 'Why middle income countries like Egypt and China are being hard hit by trade policies on AIDS drugs.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/26/a-trade-barrier-to-defeating-aids/', 'snippet': 'Why middle income countries like Egypt and China are being hard hit by trade policies on AIDS drugs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Friday’s Fixes column, I wrote about the Medicines Patent Pool, a new organization trying to make AIDS drugs better, cheaper and available sooner to people who need them in poor countries.\xa0\xa0 It relies on voluntary donations of rights by patent holders, most of them pharmaceutical companies.\xa0\xa0 Its success is crucial;\xa0 new research shows that if we can dramatically increase the n