-term debt compare with some other countries', 'lead_paragraph': 'How the AAA rating of the United States and the current interest rate on long-term debt compare with some other countries', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Consequence of Lower Ratings', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T02:33:27+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/4d0fd939-db56-5405-83df-87c3469a4861', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/4d0fd939-db56-5405-83df-87c3469a4861'}, {'abstract': 'Federal prosecutors in Manhattan announced Tuesday that they had charged four men from other nations, including Iran and Lebanon, in connection with sting operations run by the Drug Enforcement Administration.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/27/us/27briefs-Drugbrf.html', 'snippet': 'Federal prosecutors in Manhattan announced Tuesday that they had charged four men from other nations, including Iran and Lebanon, in connection with sting operations run by the Drug Enforcement Administration.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Federal prosecutors in Manhattan announced Tuesday that they had charged four men from other nations, including Iran and Lebanon, in connection with sting operations run by the Drug Enforcement Administration. Two men were charged with conspiring to provide material support to Hezbollah, which the United States considers a terrorist organization. Officials said they sought to buy surface-to-air missiles from informants working for the D.E.A. One of the men, along with a third defendant, was also accused in a heroin conspiracy to benefit Hezbollah. Another man, an Afghan, was charged with narcoterrorism conspiracy in a s