 retrial to a woman who was sentenced to probation for her role in her 4-year-old son’s death in a street-crossing accident.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/27/us/27brfs-MOTHERGETSRE_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'A judge on Tuesday granted a retrial to a woman who was sentenced to probation for her role in her 4-year-old son’s death in a street-crossing accident.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A judge on Tuesday granted a retrial to a woman who was sentenced to probation for her role in her 4-year-old son’s death in a street-crossing accident. The case of Raquel Nelson, 30, has prompted a national outcry from parents and lawyers who argue that it would be unfair to make her spend up to three years in jail because she allowed her young son, A. J., to cross the street outside of a crosswalk. He was killed in an Atlanta suburb in a hit-and-run accident in October. Before the judge granted the retrial, a jury had sentenced Ms. Nelson to a year of probation on a misdemeanor charge of vehicular homicide. The driver served six months in jail for the crime. Ms. Nelson’s lawyer said she would probably accept the retrial in order to disprove her guilt, even though that would reopen the possibility of jail time. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Georgia: Mother Gets Retrial in Jaywalking Death', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | SOUTH', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Georgia: Mother Gets Retrial in Jaywalking Death', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hit-and-Run Drivers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Atlanta (Ga)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T02:45:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robbie Brown', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robbie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brown', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role