ntences. When he returns from Japan, he will select a sentence of the week from among your contributions. Please write in with the very best sentence you read this week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bring It, Readers: Sentence of the Week Needs You', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Anderson, Sam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Blondie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T10:15:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Staff', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Staff'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2a2c3ab-d056-5a33-98e5-2dcd4faefe9e', 'word_count': 1123, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2a2c3ab-d056-5a33-98e5-2dcd4faefe9e'}, {'abstract': 'The Libyan leader, under siege for months, shows no signs so far of yielding to Western demands.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/world/africa/28libya.html', 'snippet': 'The Libyan leader, under siege for months, shows no signs so far of yielding to Western demands.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — With Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi showing no signs, so far, of yielding to Western demands, diplomats from the United States, Britain and France have adopted a new tactic in recent days: offering the besieged leader the opportunity to remain in Libya if he dissolves the government and steps aside.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/world/28libya-1311804600220/28libya-1311804600220-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/28/world/28libya-1311804600220/28libya-1311804600220-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/world/28libya-1311804600220/28libya-1311804600220-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Plan Would Keep Qaddafi in Libya, but Out of Power', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Plan Would Keep Qaddafi In Libya, but Out of Power', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transitional National Council (Libya)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qaddafi, Muammar el-', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hague, William', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T10:36:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Helene Cooper and John F. Burns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Helene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Burns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cbe37736-b584-5cec-ae93-5dcd17b545f2', 'word_count': 917, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cbe37736-b584-5cec-ae93-5dcd17b545f2'}, {'abstract': 'I imagine that everyone has experienced a version of this moment. I was trapped — no matter what I said, it was going to sound bad, because the real explanation was that the work simply wasn’t perfect.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/27/the-very-picky-customer/', 'snippet': 'I imagine that everyone has experienced a version of this moment. I was trapped — no matter what I said, it was going to sound bad, because the real explanation was that the work simply wasn’t perfect.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We got a call from a potential client a week ago Monday, which isn’t unusual. We get two or three calls every day. Our phones are set up so that they all ring whenever a call comes in. I sit within a couple of feet of my other two salesmen, Don and Nathan, and whoever is free grabs the call. I happened to be in the middle of writing an e-mail that day, so I let it ring and Don picked up. He answered: “Paul Downs Cabinetmakers, Don speaking, can I help you?”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Very Picky Customer', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tables', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T11:00:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Downs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Downs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b03b56f-ef39-5a91-907f-d57b540cd708', 'word_count': 1746, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b03b56f-ef39-5a91-907f-d57b540cd708'}, {'abstract': 'An iconic New York bar and restaurant is closing, though the Plaza says it is in negotiations “with a noted New York restaurant operator” to move in.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/27/oak-room/', 'snippet': 'An iconic New York bar and restaurant is closing, though the Plaza says it is in negotiations “with a noted New York restaurant operator” to move in.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every time Jaelin Sarper, a teacher from Singapore, visits New York, she makes sure to spend time savoring one of her favorite local icons. It’s not the Statue of Liberty or a trip to Magnolia Bakery for cupcakes. She makes her way to the Oak Room at the Plaza Hotel where she had her first martini, bought by her father.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Last Call at the Oak Room at the Plaza', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bars', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shinn, Everett', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oak Room', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Plaza Hotel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T11:11:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Haughney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haughney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dfbcefad-7033-52ca-a3f9-f20417a9a324', 'word_count': 425, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dfbcefad-7033-52ca-a3f9-f20417a9a324'}, {'abstract': 'To celebrate the resurgence of British golf is to ignore that the women are lagging far behind their male counterparts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/sports/golf/28iht-SRWOISLES28.html', 'snippet': 'To celebrate the resurgence of British golf is to ignore that the women are lagging far behind their male counterparts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No amount of sideways rain at Royal St. George’s could obscure the view that the sun is shining on the British empire. The British Open began with three men from the British Isles among the top four golfers in the world and ended with a fourth, Darren Clarke of Northern Ireland, clasping the claret jug. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/27/sports/srwoisles27/srwoisles27-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 709, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/27/sports/srwoisles27/srwoisles27-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/27/sports/srwoisles27/srwoisles27-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'British Women Face Hurdles and Indifference', 'kicker': "Special Report: Women's British Open", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'British Women Face Hurdles And Indifference', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Scotland', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ladies Professional Golf Assn', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T11:20:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Special Report', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b70f785-de80-5a56-8fde-c564751e6832', 'word_count': 1019, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b70f785-de80-5a56-8fde-c564751e6832'}, {'abstract': 'Republicans — and outside groups that often support them — have had to choose sides on the bill on the debt ceiling put forward by House Speaker John A. Boehner.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/27/scorecard-republican-supporters-and-opponents-of-boehner-plan/', 'snippet': 'Republicans — and outside groups that often support them — have had to choose sides on the bill on the debt ceiling put forward by House Speaker John A. Boehner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A debt plan by Speaker John A. Boehner has forced the nation’s Republicans — and outside groups that often support them — to choose sides.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Scorecard: Republican Supporters and Opponents of Boehner Plan', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cantor, Eric', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jordan, Jim', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pawlenty, Tim', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'West, Allen B', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'or