", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Caitlin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Connell-Rodwell", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e86ce16d-7e15-542c-a03b-0475daf92c09', 'word_count': 899, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e86ce16d-7e15-542c-a03b-0475daf92c09'}, {'abstract': 'Seth Kugel reports on his summer projects of getting more exercise and learning to love (or, at least, like) olives.', 'web_url': 'https://frugaltraveler.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/27/olives-and-exercise-the-upshot/', 'snippet': 'Seth Kugel reports on his summer projects of getting more exercise and learning to love (or, at least, like) olives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I set out for my Mediterranean trip this summer with two self-improvement goals: to get regular exercise (by running or doing the equivalent three times a week) and to learn to like olives (by eating every one that came my way, which in this part of the world, was a lot).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Olives and Exercise: The Upshot', 'kicker': 'Frugal Traveler', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mediterranean Sea', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T16:05:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Seth Kugel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kugel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a755f581-a79c-5188-8b14-53fbbab96326', 'word_count': 318, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a755f581-a79c-5188-8b14-53fbbab96326'}, {'abstract': 'A top official from one of the largest rating agencies told a House panel the American credit rating could be lowered.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/business/bank-examiner-testifies-on-credit-downgrade.html', 'snippet': 'A top official from one of the largest rating agencies told a House panel the American credit rating could be lowered.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The United States is unlikely to default on its debt obligations but its credit rating could still be lowered if it doesn’t come up with an adequate plan to address spending and its soaring budget deficit, an official from one of the country’s largest credit rating agencies told a House panel Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/business/28ratingPicB/28ratingPicB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Credit Agency Tells Congress a Default Is Unlikely', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Unlikely to Default, S.&P. Chief Tells Panel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ratings and Rating Systems', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T16:08:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wyatt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wyatt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e2cd245-746d-5a95-9d9e-b57129a967cc', 'word_c