'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/27/now-selling-textfield-titles-at-creatures-of-comfort/', 'snippet': 'The SoHo shop unveils a temporary bookstore and exhibition that includes names like Phil Chang and Arthur Ou.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For its fifth in-store project, the SoHo shop Creatures of Comfort collaborated with the publishing and distribution company Textfield Inc. on “No More Reality,” a temporary bookstore and exhibition. Through Aug. 25, works by the artists Phil Chang, Arthur Ou, Eduardo Sarabia and Anna Sew Hoy — all Textfield Inc. favorites — play a supporting role to the printing house founder Jonathan Maghen’s curiously obscure and graphic selection of paperbacks and monographs. No book costs more than $100 (not even the artist Jennifer Doyle’s lovingly compiled “Municipal du Futbol,” about amateur soccer in Los Angeles, which includes two clothbound books, a jersey, nine artist lithographs and a poster). Pick up “The Portable John Latham” or the hilarious “Hippie Photos and Surfer Man” by the photographer Doniella Davy while you shop for Maison Martin Margiela clothes and Robert Clergerie shoes (fall’s tassel-top loafers and embossed leather wedges just arrived, p.s.).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Now Selling | Textfield Titles at Creatures of Comfort', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T17:00:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane Herman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Herman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2aa9bcb0-c064-5be0-a87f-bdfa514fed34', 'word_count': 157, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2aa9bcb0-c064-5be0-a87f-bdfa514fed34'}, {'abstract': 'Afghans have been advised to stand by for the debut next month of a new comedy series, “The Ministry,” which appears to be a version of “The Office” in all but name.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/27/afghan-deadpan-kabul-gets-its-version-of-the-office/', 'snippet': 'Afghans have been advised to stand by for the debut next month of a new comedy series, “The Ministry,” which appears to be a version of “The Office” in all but name.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Saad Mohseni, an Afghan media mogul who owns the popular Tolo TV network, has alerted his Twitter followers to stand by for the debut next month of a new comedy series, “The Ministry,” which appears to be an Afghan version of “The Office” in all but name.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Afghan Deadpan: Kabul Gets Its Version of ‘The Office’', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption in Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gervais, Ricky', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mohseni, Saad', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T17:00:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7a9a835-2511-52f6-b4e9-654ed80dcb8f', 'word_count': 477, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7a9a835-2511-52f6-b4e9-654ed80dcb8f'}, {'abstract': 'The private-equity firm Permira is in negotiations to sell its 45 percent ownership in Proenza Schouler to a group of New York investors with ties to Theory and Helmut Lang.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/27/a-proenza-schouler-deal-is-near/', 'snippet': 'The private-equity firm Permira is in negotiations to sell its 45 percent ownership in Proenza Schouler to a group of New York investors with ties to Theory and Helmut Lang.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A European private-equity firm is expected to sell its shares in the design house Proenza Schouler to a group of New York investors led by John Howard, the chief executive of Irving Place Capital, and Andrew Rosen, a seasoned garment industry executive behind Theory and Helmut Lang.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Proenza Schouler Deal Is Near', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T17:03:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a72abd4-244f-5a9e-ab7f-aee29c4bcb45', 'word_count': 454, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a72abd4-244f-5a9e-ab7f-aee29c4bcb45'}, {'abstract': 'On Bard College’s campus, a free summer camp for low-income students who excel in mathematics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/07/28/nyregion/20110728MATHCAMP.html', 'snippet': 'On Bard College’s campus, a free summer camp for low-income students who excel in mathematics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Bard College’s campus, a free summer camp for low-income students who excel in mathematics.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': No