ng standoff. Also, John Harwood reports from inside Mitt Romney’s campaign in New Hampshire.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Caucus Video: Speaker Boehner’s Perilous Moment; Mitt Romney in New Hampshire', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Hampshire', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T17:08:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Werschkul', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werschkul', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5bdd0f5-f87a-5a3a-bf24-25ea9500c004', 'word_count': 36, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5bdd0f5-f87a-5a3a-bf24-25ea9500c004'}, {'abstract': 'Daniel F. Akerson, the chief executive, appeared to put to rest recent speculation about a possible sale of European unit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/business/gm-ceo-squelches-opel-rumors.html', 'snippet': 'Daniel F. Akerson, the chief executive, appeared to put to rest recent speculation about a possible sale of European unit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DETROIT — General Motors is not interested in selling its European unit, Adam Opel, the carmaker’s chief executive said Wednesday, countering widespread speculation.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'G.M. Says Opel Unit Not for Sale', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'G.M. Says Opel Unit Not for Sale', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Opel, Adam, AG', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T17:09:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bunkley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bunkley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3817598d-3d89-5111-91d1-7f8a1b28332e', 'word_count': 361, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3817598d-3d89-5111-91d1-7f8a1b28332e'}, {'abstract': 'A report finds that the jobs lost in the recession were largely in the middle tier of wages, but most of the jobs created in the recovery have been low-wage positions.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/27/where-the-job-growth-is-at-the-low-end/', 'snippet': 'A report finds that the jobs lost in the recession were largely in the middle tier of wages, but most of the jobs created in the recovery have been low-wage positions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s more unhappy news for the millions of Americans hoping for a surge in the number of good, high-paying jobs — a new report concludes that the great bulk of new jobs created since the economic recovery began are in lower-wage occupations, paying $13.52 or less an hour. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Where the Job Growth Is: At the Low End', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T17:10:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Greenhouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenhouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cefb2ada-f110-5fee-8901-51afd80bc13f', 'word_count': 571, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cefb2ada-f110-5fee-8901-51afd80bc13f'}, {'abstract': 'Many small businesses have combined timing, willingness to pay cash and market savvy to negotiate lower rents or to move into better spaces.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/business/smallbusiness/capitalizing-on-a-weak-commercial-real-estate-market.html', 'snippet': 'Many small businesses have combined timing, willingness to pay cash and market savvy to negotiate lower rents or to move into better spaces.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From 2009 to 2010, the commercial real estate market in the United States seemed bottomless. Whether seeking manufacturing, office or retail space, those looking to lease or buy were in the driver’s seat, said Fred Schmidt, president and chief operating officer for Coldwell Banker Commercial in Parsippany, N.J. After the supply of space hit a peak in the fourth quarter of 2010, he said, the market began a slow recovery — “but it’s definitely still a tenant’s and buyer’s market.” ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/business/smallbusiness/28sbiz/28sbiz-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Capitalizing on a Weak Commercial Real Estate Market', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Saving on Real Estate In a Down Economy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Office Buildings and Commercial Properties', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Relocation of Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Small Business Administration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T17:12:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eilene Zimmerman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eilene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zimmerman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5be3fc70-8ba2-5c99-b282-923e21226868', 'word_count': 1262, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5be3fc70-8ba2-5c99-b282-923e21226868'}, {'abstract': 'The N.F.L. followed its lockout with rules of engagement for signing free agents that were confusing, at best.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/sports/nfl-off-season-promises-to-be-short-but-wild.html', 'snippet': 'The N.F.L. followed its lockout with rules of engagement for signing free agents that were confusing, at best.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While everyone seemed to predict that the end of the N.F.L. lockout would result in a free agency free-for-all, no one stepped forward with a properly absurd proposal for how it should be handled. We like the idea of putting all players’ names on Ping-Pong balls and have them spit out of a lottery hopper. Or perhaps the whole thing should be handled like Bingo. Auction paddles, anyone? No, wait, let’s just play it all as a big video game. Or maybe Bob Barker has some time on his hands. “Plaxico Burress, come on down!”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'N.F.L.’s Game of Catch-Up', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'N.F.L. Off-Season Promises to Be Short but Wild', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pryor, Terrelle', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McNabb, Donovan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Palmer, Carson', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sabathia, C C', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burress, Plaxico', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T17:13:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb05c46e-a1fb-56f6-a6cc-6324fdf84620', 'word_count': 677, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb05c46e-a1fb-56f6-a6cc-6324fdf84620'}, {'abstract': 'On August 6 and 7th, for the last two days of its blockbuster exhibition “Alexander McQueen: Savage Beauty,’’ the Metropolitan Museum of Art will keep the show open until midnight.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/27/met-museum-to-stay-open-later-than-ever-before-for-mcqueen-show/', 'snippet': 'On August 6 and 7th, for the last two days of its blockbuster exhibition “Alexander McQueen: Savage Beauty,’’ the Metropolitan Museum of Art will keep the show open until midnight.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Metropolitan Museum of Art has never catered to the late-night crowd, but on Aug. 6 and 7, the last two days of its blockbuster exhibition “Alexander McQueen: Savage Beauty,’’ it will keep the show open until midnight. Having combed through the museum’s records, officials there said they believed that this would be the first time the Met has stayed open so late. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Met Museum to Stay Open for McQueen Show Later Than Ever Before', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McQueen, Alexander', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Museum of Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T17:15:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Vogel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vogel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 