'uri': 'nyt://article/c94e4108-b4bf-5f61-ac1f-14d97780204c'}, {'abstract': 'Ludwig Willisch will replace Jim O’Donnell, inheriting a region with sales momentum that could lead the brand past Lexus by year’s end.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/27/bmw-group-appoints-new-president-for-north-american-region/', 'snippet': 'Ludwig Willisch will replace Jim O’Donnell, inheriting a region with sales momentum that could lead the brand past Lexus by year’s end.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jim O’Donnell, the president of BMW of North America, is retiring on a high note, with the company entertaining realistic notions of becoming the No. 1 luxury automotive brand in the United States. The executive will be succeeded in October by Ludwig Willisch, who oversaw BMW’s M performance division before being promoted to head European sales.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'BMW Group Appoints New President for North American Region', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Donnell, Jim", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Audi Division of Volkswagen AG', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bayerische Motorenwerke AG', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'LEXUS DIVISION OF TOYOTA MOTOR SALES USA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mercedes-Benz', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toyota Motor Corp', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North America', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T17:51:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew DeBord', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname'