cle/8040266f-fc36-5b61-8994-98799c736b83'}, {'abstract': 'A 108-year-old water main burst, and the water damaged two gas mains. At 177th Street, near Jerome Avenue, the water was about a foot and a half deep.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/27/jerome-ave-becomes-river-after-a-water-main-bursts/', 'snippet': 'A 108-year-old water main burst, and the water damaged two gas mains. At 177th Street, near Jerome Avenue, the water was about a foot and a half deep.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A major water supply line in the Bronx burst on Wednesday morning, flooding Jerome Avenue for several blocks near 177th Street, halting traffic, disrupting subway and bus service and damaging two nearby gas mains.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Flooding in Bronx After Water Line Breaks', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Office of Emergency Management (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T18:07:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e20e97dd-2a98-5990-a807-4220b2733cab', 'word_count': 507, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e20e97dd-2a98-5990-a807-4220b2733cab'}, {'abstract': 'The beard has become a symbol of youthful rebellion (and a different sort of conformity) for the first time since the heyday of Fillmore East.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/07/28/fashion/20110728-BEARD.html', 'snippet': 'The beard has become a symbol of youthful rebellion (and a different sort of conformity) for the first time since the heyday of Fillmore East.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The beard has become a symbol of youthful rebellion (and a different sort of conformity) for the first time since the heyday of Fillmore East.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/20110728-BEARD-slide-HL97/20110728-BEARD-slide-HL97-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/20110728-BEARD-slide-HL97/20110728-BEARD-slide-HL97-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/20110728-BEARD-slide-HL97/20110728-BEARD-slide-HL97-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Beards: Rugged? Trendy? Or Unreliable?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hair', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T18:10:45+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Fashion & Style', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/b150ee87-638b-545d-817a-88126864bee7', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/b150ee87-638b-545d-817a-88126864bee7'}, {'abstract': 'A beard can be many things: a signifier of age and wisdom; a symbol of rebellious youth; or, as uncool as it may be, a result of being too sick from the flu to even shave.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/fashion/what-your-beard-says-about-you-the-mirror.html', 'snippet': 'A beard can be many things: a signifier of age and wisdom; a symbol of rebellious youth; or, as uncool as it may be, a result of being too sick from the flu to even shave.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOUR years ago, I grew the first full beard of my adult life on a whim. I was 41, and it was neither a fashion statement nor a midlife crisis, but it came at a fortuitous time: the style world just happened to be entering the Postmillennial He-Man Beard Epoch.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/20110728-BEARD-slide-HL97/20110728-BEARD-slide-HL97-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/20110728-BEARD-slide-HL97/20110728-BEARD-slide-HL97-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/20110728-BEARD-slide-HL97/20110728-BEARD-slide-HL97-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Your Beard Says About You', 'kicker': 'The Mirror', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Younger, Stronger, Cooler. And All by Not Shaving.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hair', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T18:13:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa5af645-2e2d-5558-9b4c-eef8a4d865e5', 'word_count': 1386, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa5af645-2e2d-5558-9b4c-eef8a4d865e5'}, {'abstract': 'One blog posits that the move could be an attempt by the hotel’s new owner to break a union.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/27/chelsea-hotel-to-stop-taking-reservations/', 'snippet': 'One blog posits that the move could be an attempt by the hotel’s new owner to break a union.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The legendary Chelsea Hotel will stop taking reservations next Tuesday, Curbed reports. Living With Legends: Hotel Chelsea Blog reports that the news “could mean many things,” including the chance to do construction under reduced scrutiny or challenge the union.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chelsea Hotel to Stop Taking Reservations', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'HOTELS AND MOTELS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Curbed.com', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HOTEL CHELSEA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T18:25:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4775e986-e61c-5001-bbe0-95111dbc3b5c', 'word_count': 39, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4775e986-e61c-5001-bbe0-95111dbc3b5c'}, {'abstract': 'As some consumers rip out designers’ itchy ID tags, there’s been a move toward subtlety and comfort in attaching logos.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/fashion/snipping-out-annoying-clothing-labels.html', 'snippet': 'As some consumers rip out designers’ itchy ID tags, there’s been a move toward subtlety and comfort in attaching logos.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LEAH MISSBACH DAY, 52, a photojournalist in Chicago, likes designer labels like Balenciaga, Alexander Wang and Dries Van Noten. But not next to her skin. “I cut them out because they’re scratchy and they bug me,” she said. “I’ve got a whole drawer full of tags.” ', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/28labels3/28LABELS3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/28labels3/28labels3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/28labels3/28labels3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Taking the Scissors to Annoying Labels', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Taking the Scissors To Annoying Labels', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labeling and Labels', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T18:33:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e6a25ea-3748-5dcc-b3b1-822c62bff1f5', 'word_count': 1085, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e6a25ea-3748-5dcc-b3b1-822c62bff1f5'}, {'abstract': 'The expected trade of Carlos Beltran would bring back a top pitching prospect from the Giants.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/27/mets-set-to-send-beltran-to-giants/', 'snippet': 'The expected trade of Carlos Beltran would bring back a top pitching prospect from the Giants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Mets and the San Francisco Giants are on the verge of completing a trade that would send Carlos Beltran to the Giants in exchange for a top prospect who is likely to be Zack Wheeler, a right-handed pitcher taken in the first round of the 2009 draft. The pending deal was confirmed by a person in baseball with knowledge of the talks. More details here, with updates to follow. Are the Mets on the right path, and should more big names be following Beltran out of town?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mets Set to Send Beltran to Giants', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beltran, Carlos', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco Giants', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T18:33:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41bde9ec-c52c-594d-aadd-11bcd64c692f', 'word_count': 88, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41bde9ec-c52c-594d-aadd-11bcd64c692f'}, {'abstract': 'NBC News cameras filming a Brian Williams special added to the reality show vibe on Capitol Hill.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/27/a-hectic-and-often-hidden-day-in-the-life/', 'snippet': 'NBC News cameras filming a Brian Williams special added to the reality show vibe on Capitol Hill.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As if there wasn’t enough going on at the United States Capitol on Wednesday, it was all happening with cameras rolling.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Hectic, and Often Hidden, Day in the Life', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capitol Building (Washington, DC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Brian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NBC News', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T18:33:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d92b0c3d-b6b4-5416-9d82-5b0efc77a3c3', 'word_count': 197, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d92b0c3d-b6b4-5416-9d82-5b0efc77a3c3'}, {'abstract': 'The day in N.F.L. transactions, rumored transactions and other happenings in the league’s abbreviated player-movement period.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/27/n-f-l-free-for-all-central/', 'snippet': 'The day in N.F.L. transactions, rumored transactions and other happenings in the league’s abbreviated player-movement period.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Big signing news of the day, so farThe Titans added a bit of stability with the signing of former Seahawks quarterback Matt Hasselbeck on Monday, although that is sort of like saying you’ve added some fresh water to the Atlantic Ocean. But after sending Vince Young into exile and having Kerry Collins retire instead of dive into this reclamation project, the Titans desperately needed not to throw their first-round draft pick Jake Locker straight into the lion pit. They put out a call for a veteran stop-gap and Hasselbeck, 35, answered, to the tune of $21 million over three years, the Tennessean reported.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'N.F.L. Free-for-All Central', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T18:36:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd2b0c40-2ae6-510f-a20c-c9b7d4c99acc', 'word_count': 452, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd2b0c40-2ae6-510f-a20c-c9b7d4c99acc'}, {'abstract': 'The Textile Museum will move to George Washington University’s Foggy Bottom campus and become part of a new museum scheduled to open in 2014, the two institutions announced on Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/27/textile-museum-to-move-to-george-washington-university/', 'snippet': 'The Textile Museum will move to George Washington University’s Foggy Bottom campus and become part of a new museum scheduled to open in 2014, the two institutions announced on Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Textile Museum  will move to George Washington University’s Foggy Bottom campus and become part of a new museum scheduled to open in 2014, the two institutions announced on Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Textile Museum to Move to George Washington University', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': No