ures and design changes. J.D. Biersdorfer chats with Jack Welde, the CEO of Smartling (http://www.smartling.com), about website translation and how his company uses the cloud and the crowd (-sourcing) to offer different language options. Freshly rickrolled, Pedro Rafael Rosado has something to say about that old prank. The news roundup includes YouTube taking up 22 percent of all mobile bandwidth; Walmart giving its Vudu video service an extra push; a new Mozilla mobile platform project; the resignation of a top U.S. cyber official; release of the Samsung Galaxy Tab 10.1 tablet with 4G service; and an Apple security update. J.D.'s tip of the week: a feature in Microsoft Office 2010 and 2007 for Windows called KeyTips, which lets you jump into ribbon menus with just a few keystrokes and shows you what to press.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2011/07/27/technology/personaltech/27techtalk_pod.html', 'snippet': "Alan Yacavone, an Apple expert from the Times's News Technology team, stops by to discuss Lion and its new features and design changes. J.D. Biersdorfer chats with Jack Welde, the CEO of Smartling (http://www.smartling.com), about website translat...", 'lead_paragraph': "Alan Yacavone, an Apple expert from the Times's News Technology team, stops by to discuss Lion and its new features and design changes. J.D. Biersdorfer chats with Jack Welde, the CEO of Smartling (http://www.smartling.com), about website translation and how his company uses the cloud and the crowd (-sourcing) to offer different language options. Freshly rickrolled, Pedro Rafael Rosado has something to say about that old prank. The news roundup includes YouTube taking up 22 percent of all mobile bandwidth; Walmart giving its Vudu video service an extra push; a new Mozilla mobile platform project; the resignation of a top U.S. cyber official; release of the Samsung Galaxy Tab 10.1 tablet with 4G service; and an Apple security update. J.D.'s tip of the week: a feature in Microsoft Office 2010 and 2007 for Windows called KeyTips, which lets you jump into ribbon menus with just a few keystrokes and shows you what to press.", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A closer look at Lion, the new version of Mac OS X; website translation; the term "rickrolling;" news.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T21:39:20+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/c178d750-c639-5857-9125-3fe007b2496e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/c178d750-c639-5857-9125-3fe007b2496e'}, {'abstract': 'A look at six rehearsals at the 42nd Street Studios in Times Square.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/07/31/theater/20110731-rehearse.html', 'snippet': 'A look at six rehearsals at the 42nd Street Studios in Times Square.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A look at six rehearsals at the 42nd Street Studios in Times Square.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fine Tuning Behind Closed Doors', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T21:42:12+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Theater', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/fd8b457c-be63-5512-9a6e-056b495267da', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/fd8b457c-be63-5512-9a6e-056b495267da'}, {'abstract': 'A day in the life of the New 42nd Street Studios, a 10-story building in Times Square.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/31/theater/rehearsals-side-by-side-and-glorified.html', 'snippet': 'A day in the life of the New 42nd Street Studios, a 10-story building in Times Square.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FORTY-SECOND STREET has long catered to the needs of New Yorkers, tourists, theater lovers, moviegoers, small-time hustlers, global corporations, shoppers, restaurateurs, news hounds, thrill seekers, hopefuls and has-beens. But until the New 42nd Street Studios was completed in 2000, there was precious little space for performing artists to rehearse.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/31/arts/31REHEARSE5-1311368880185/31REHEARSE5-1311368880185-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/31/arts/31REHEARSE5-1311368880185/31REHEARSE5-1311368880185-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/31/arts/31REHEARSE5-1311368880185/31REHEARSE5-1311368880185-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/31/arts/31REHEARSE5-1311368880185/31REHEARSE5-1311368880185-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/31/arts/31REHEARSE5-1311368880185/31REHEARSE5-1311368880185-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rehearsals, Side by Side and Glorified', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rehearsals, Side by Side And Glorified', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords':