nyt://interactive/739284f7-c95d-5f99-bc4d-a65baa3fd64b'}, {'abstract': 'Charles Bradley erased the line between showmanship and sentiment at a performance in Fort Greene Park.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/arts/music/charles-bradley-at-fort-greene-park-review.html', 'snippet': 'Charles Bradley erased the line between showmanship and sentiment at a performance in Fort Greene Park.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The line between showmanship and sentiment is often thick and impermeable, but midway through his Tuesday evening performance in Fort Greene Park in Brooklyn, Charles Bradley obliterated it.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/arts/bradley/bradley-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Journeyman Soul Singer Embraces His Audience in Word and in Deed', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Journeyman Soul Singer Embraces His Audience in Word and in Deed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T21:53:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/58668ab8-793a-5ff6-b4d8-2378b9ae2f56', 'word_count': 682, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58668ab8-793a-5ff6-b4d8-2378b9ae2f56'}, {'abstract': 'Play continues at the summer championships in Toronto.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/crosswords/bridge/von-zedtwitz-title-at-north-american-championships-bridge.html', 'snippet': 'Play continues at the summer championships in Toronto.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TORONTO — At the American Contract Bridge League’s Summer North America Championships here on Sunday the Von Zedtwitz Life Master Pairs was won by Peter Bertheau and Per-Olla Cullin from Sweden. They finished less than a board ahead of Tarek Sadek from Egypt and Zia Mahmood of New York. Third were Jan Jansma from the Netherlands and Jay Borker of Greenwich, Conn. Bertheau and Cullin will play for Sweden in this year’s Bermuda Bowl world team championship, but not as partners.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Swedish Pair Wins Von Zedtwitz Title by Less Than a Board', 'kicker': 'Bridge', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Swedish Pair Wins Von Zedtwitz Title by Less Than a Board', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cards and Card Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bridge (Card Game)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T21:55:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'subsection_name': 'Bridge', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phillip Alder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phillip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5534bfcf-46da-5bd3-9219-0b5a374357a1', 'word_count': 511, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5534bfcf-46da-5bd3-9219-0b5a374357a1'}, {'abstract': 'Senators kept an eye on history while working out a way to make an exception to a 10-year term limit.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/27/senate-extends-term-of-f-b-i-director/', 'snippet': 'Senators kept an eye on history while working out a way to make an exception to a 10-year term limit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Senate on Wednesday voted unanimously to extend the tenure of Robert S. Mueller III as director of the Federal Bureau of Investigation, allowing him to serve for two more years.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Senate Extends Term of F.B.I. Director', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T21:57:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee3fd2f3-93f9-581f-a76b-2815970f6530', 'word_count': 282, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee3fd2f3-93f9-581f-a76b-2815970f6530'}, {'abstract': 'Images from a new exhibition of “Art, Science, and Invention in the 19th Century.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/07/27/arts/design/Smithsonian-American-Art-.html', 'snippet': 'Images from a new exhibition of “Art, Science, and Invention in the 19th Century.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Images from a new exhibition of “Art, Science, and Invention in the 19th Century.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/27/arts/design/Smithsonian-American-Art--slide-WRJR/Smithsonian-American-Art--slide-WRJR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 783, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/27/arts/design/Smithsonian-American-Art--slide-WRJR/Smithsonian-American-Art--slide-WRJR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/27/arts/design/Smithsonian-American-Art--slide-WRJR/Smithsonian-American-Art--slide-WRJR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘The Great American Hall of Wonders’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Smithsonian Institution', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T21:58:07+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Arts', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/12bb5291-3295-50d3-ae21-7c054364612a', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/12bb5291-3295-50d3-ae21-7c054364612a'}, {'abstract': 'Two books about Joseph Heller, by his daughter, Erica Heller (“Yossarian Slept Here”) and Tracy Daugherty (“Just One Catch”).', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/books/books-about-joseph-heller-by-erica-heller-and-tracy-daugherty-review.html', 'snippet': 'Two books about Joseph Heller, by his daughter, Erica Heller (“Yossarian Slept Here”) and Tracy Daugherty (“Just One Catch”).', 'lead_paragraph': '“Just One Catch” is a soup-to-nuts chronicle of the life of  Joseph Heller. It is by Tracy Daugherty, who should not be confused with Mr. Heller’s daughter. Erica Heller’s own book about her father is “Yossarian Slept Here,” and there are many places where Heller’s daughter and Mr. Daugherty overlap. This situation is so jarring that it has driven Christopher Buckley, not ordinarily known for cornball silliness, to two giddy attacks of wordplay. About the biography he blurbs, “A major achievement, or should I say major major major?” in honor of Major Major, a major character in Heller’s “Catch-22.” His blurb for Ms. Heller: “I think this is going to be one hell(er) of a memoir.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/arts/JPBOOK1/JPBOOK1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 672, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/arts/JPBOOK1/JPBOOK1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/28/arts/JPBOOK1/JPBOOK1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Catching of Two Joseph Hellers', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Catching Of Two Joseph Hellers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Heller, Joseph', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Heller, Erica', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apthorp (Manhattan, NY, Apartments)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Daugherty, Tracy (1955- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Yossarian Slept Here (Book)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Just One Catch (Book)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T22:07:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Janet Maslin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Janet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Maslin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b930617-a9a9-532c-a96c-3b0ff6e285c1', 'word_count': 1266, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b930617-a9a9-532c-a96c-3b0ff6e285c1'}, {'abstract': '“The Great American Hall of Wonders” exhibition at the Smithsonian American Art Museum in is a curiosity cabinet shaped by the American innovations in the 19th century.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/arts/design/smithsonian-art-museums-american-hall-of-wonders-review.html', 'snippet': '“The Great American Hall of Wonders” exhibition at the Smithsonian American Art Museum in is a curiosity cabinet shaped by the American innovations in the 19th century.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The first thing we see on entering the new exhibition at the Smithsonian American Art Museum here is a life-size painting of a formally dressed, graciously welcoming, aged gentleman. He is lifting a heavy red drape and gesturing as if inviting us to visit the marvels within. Beyond the curtain we glimpse walls lined with hundreds of glass cases, each containing stuffed birds. We see visitors strolling past, engaged in contemplation or struck with amazement. We also spot part of a mastodon skeleton, discovered in 1801 by the same man who lifts the curtain.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/arts/Wonders-1/Wonders-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 393, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/28/arts/Wonders-1/Wonders-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 393}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/arts/Wonders-1/Wonders-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 671, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/arts/Wonders-1/Wonders-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/28/arts/Wonders-1/Wonders-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The World as America Dreamed It', 'kicker': 'Exhibition Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The World as America Dreamed It', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inventions and Patents', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Smithsonian American Art Museum', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Smithsonian Institution', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T22:13:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Rothstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rothstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/77688e1a-32de-50ae-b78f-f65ea3fbbad6', 'word_count': 1472, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77688e1a-32de-50ae-b78f-f65ea3fbbad6'}, {'abstract': 'The first day of Nickelodeon’s rebroadcast of 1990s shows on TeenNick doubled the channel’s prior ratings in the midnight to 2 a.m. time slot.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/27/teennick-finds-success-in-the-nostalgic-90s/', 'snippet': 'The first day of Nickelodeon’s rebroadcast of 1990s shows on TeenNick doubled the channel’s prior ratings in the midnight to 2 a.m. time slot.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Viacom’s research appears to have been proved right: twenty-somethings do want their old Nickelodeon shows back.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'TeenNick Finds Success in the Nostalgic ’90s', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nickelodeon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T22:13:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e25a4b2-fb96-54ba-8f3c-551b8821406a', 'word_count': 379, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e25a4b2-fb96-54ba-8f3c-551b8821406a'}, {'abstract': 'Really truly.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/27/obama-the-moderate-conservative/', 'snippet': 'Really truly.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No time to do any original posting tonight. But for those who missed the first time I linked to it, here’s Bruce Bartlett — an economic adviser to Ronald Reagan — explaining why Obama is indeed a moderate conservative in practical terms.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama the Moderate Conservative', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T22:16:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/08fefe2b-1345-5904-bb0e-acceceb844bf', 'word_count': 46, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08fefe2b-1345-5904-bb0e-acceceb844bf'}, {'abstract': '“The Optimists” consists of five vignettes, each of whose cynical stories of humble people embracing absurd illusions illustrate the universal impulse to believe in a better future, no matter what.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/movies/the-optimists-by-goran-paskaljevic-review.html', 'snippet': '“The Optimists” consists of five vignettes, each of whose cynical stories of humble people embracing absurd illusions illustrate the universal impulse to believe in a better future, no matter what.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It would be comforting to imagine that “The Optimists,” Goran Paskaljevic’s viciously funny gloss of Voltaire’s “Candide,” was a site-specific satire of this Serbian director’s homeland in the post-Milosevic era. The film’s five vignettes, whose characters cling to irrational optimism in the face of poverty, injustice and hatred, are all set in an unidentified Eastern European wasteland of bleak farming villages, one of which has been inundated by a flood.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/arts/OPTIMISTS/OPTIMISTS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/28/arts/OPTIMISTS/OPTIMISTS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 390}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/arts/OPTIMISTS/OPTIMISTS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 790, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/arts/OPTIMISTS/OPTIMISTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/28/arts/OPTIMISTS/OPTIMISTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Best of All Possible Worlds: When Life Gives You Mud, Take a Mud Bath', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'The Optimists'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Best of All Possible Worlds: When Life Gives You Mud, Take a Mud Bath', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paskaljevic, Goran', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T22:21:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf59bd03-a031-5580-91f7-e778dc108e32', 'word_count': 722, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf59bd03-a031-5580-91f7-e778dc108e32'}, {'abstract': 'The Justice Department has asked Google for more information and time to investigate its acquisition of Admeld, a display advertising company.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/27/government-seeks-more-information-on-googles-admeld-acquisition/', 'snippet': 'The Justice Department has asked Google for more information and time to investigate its acquisition of Admeld, a display advertising company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Justice Department has asked Google for more information and time as it investigates the search giant’s $400 million acquisition of Admeld, a display advertising company, Google said on Wednesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Government Seeks More Information on Google’s Admeld Acquisition', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antitrust Laws and Competition Issues', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T22:23:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claire Cain Miller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claire', 'middlename': 'Cain', 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b32594aa-dedd-59f8-b995-7f5e1a2e171a', 'word_count': 212, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b32594aa-dedd-59f8-b995-7f5e1a2e171a'}, {'abstract': 'Bookstore buyers are in the dark as Little, Brown & Company coyly offers the fall release “Untitled” by Anonymous, marketed as “the inside story of life with one of the most controversial figures of our time.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/books/little-brown-offers-untitled-by-anonymous.html', 'snippet': 'Bookstore buyers are in the dark as Little, Brown & Company coyly offers the fall release “Untitled” by Anonymous, marketed as “the inside story of life with one of the most controversial figures of our time.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the last few days buyers for bookstores around the country have opened their e-mail to find a mysterious last-minute addition to the Little, Brown & Company fall lineup. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/arts/ANON2/ANON2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 621, 'width': 745, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/arts/ANON2/ANON2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/28/arts/ANON2/ANON2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Publisher Plays Coy With Book Release', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Publisher Plays Coy With Book Release', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'LITTLE BROWN & CO', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Madoff, Bernard L', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hachette Book Group', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Madoff, Andrew', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hooper, Catherine', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Book Trade and Publishing', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T22:25:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e79ca95-fd7d-5009-981a-b9ba1c4c516c', 'word_count': 640, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e79ca95-fd7d-5009-981a-b9ba1c4c516c'}, {'abstract': 'A short course of Dwarf Fortress basics.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/27/its-never-too-late-to-learn-how-to-succeed-while-in-fortress-mode/', 'snippet': 'A short course of Dwarf Fortress basics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you enjoyed Jonah Weiner’s article on Tarn and Zach Adams and the brilliance of their computer game, Dwarf Fortress, then you will likely also enjoy this interview with Wiener over on the excellent Boing Boing podcast Gweek 010. And if at some point during your reading of the story you thought to yourself, with some small amount of melancholy, I would like to learn how to plant crops and forge weapons and protect myself against vampire dwarves, but I am not the kind of person who even knows how to distinguish the military from the nobles, then you are in luck. At the University of Reddit, starting Aug. 3, there’s a class being offered on Dwarf Fortress basics. So go forth and remember, the hippos like the sewers!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'It’s Never Too Late to Learn How to Succeed While in Fortress Mode', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T22:31:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joel Lovell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lovell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/40bb3123-ef6f-5b5d-a284-7ffd49c5526a', 'word_count': 129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40bb3123-ef6f-5b5d-a284-7ffd49c5526a'}, {'abstract': 'Republicans have loaded a House appropriations bill with provisions to severely curtail environmental oversight.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/science/earth/28enviro.html', 'snippet': 'Republicans have loaded a House appropriations bill with provisions to severely curtail environmental oversight.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the nation’s attention diverted by the drama over the debt ceiling, Republicans in the House of Representatives are loading up an appropriations bill with 39 ways — and counting — to significantly curtail environmental regulation.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/us/ENVIRO/ENVIRO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 688, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Republicans Seek Big Cuts in Environmental Rules', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'House Republicans Try to Curb Environmental Rules', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wilderness Areas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bureau of Land Management', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Interior Department', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Grand Canyon (Ariz)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fish and Wildlife Service', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T22:31:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Leslie Kaufman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Leslie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaufman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/387428ff-a8bd-546e-96df-2937524d4514', 'word_count': 925, 'uri': 'nyt://article/387428ff-a8bd-546e-96df-2937524d4514'}, {'abstract': 'A report from the Congressional Budget Office could help Speaker John A. Boehner sell his debt-ceiling legislation to conservatives in his party.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/27/boehners-bill-gets-a-boost/', 'snippet': 'A report from the Congressional Budget Office could help Speaker John A. Boehner sell his debt-ceiling legislation to conservatives in his party.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new version of Speaker John A. Boehner’s House debt-ceiling bill would cut spending by $917 billion over 10 years, according to the Congressional Budget Office, giving the speaker’s legislation a fresh boost in advance of a possible vote on Thursday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Boehner’s Bill Gets a Boost', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reid, Harry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T22:31:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Micahel D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Micahel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8a89150-2717-5e92-bcc6-5597239192f9', 'word_count': 269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8a89150-2717-5e92-bcc6-5597239192f9'}, {'abstract': 'Manchester United striker Javier Hernández sustained a concussion during training Tuesday night and spent the night in a local hospital in New Jersey.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/27/chicharito-sustains-concussion/', 'snippet': 'Manchester United striker Javier Hernández sustained a concussion during training Tuesday night and spent the night in a local hospital in New Jersey.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HARRISON, N.J. — Manchester United’s fabled cone of silence was activated Tuesday night when the team’s young Mexican star, Javier Hernández, known as Chicharito, was injured during an evening training session. But the club kept the news under wraps until only hours before the start of its match against the Major League Soccer all-stars.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chicharito Sustains Concussion', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hernandez, Javier', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Soccer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Manchester United', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T22:34:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Bell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/95ba5e07-158b-5781-94b6-96736cffdae5', 'word_count': 299, 'uri': 'nyt://article/95ba5e07-158b-5781-94b6-96736cffdae5'}, {'abstract': 'Even if he can get his debt ceiling bill through the House, 53 Democratic senators tell John A. Boehner, it will die in the Senate.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/27/senate-democrats-promise-to-reject-boehner-plan/', 'snippet': 'Even if he can get his debt ceiling bill through the House, 53 Democratic senators tell John A. Boehner, it will die in the Senate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fifty-three De