Topsy, works with popular Twitter posts, selecting those that are from a particular time period, have certain terms or contain links.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/business/topsy-a-search-engine-sorts-out-whats-popular-on-twitter.html', 'snippet': 'A search engine, Topsy, works with popular Twitter posts, selecting those that are from a particular time period, have certain terms or contain links.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you’ve tried to search for posts on Twitter’s built-in search box, you know it can be frustrating.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Better Way to Sort Out What’s Hot on Twitter', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Better Way to Sort Out What’s Hot on Twitter', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search Engines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T22:52:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Boutin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Boutin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2dbc2314-ea54-5871-a390-933b09e99669', 'word_count': 297, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2dbc2314-ea54-5871-a390-933b09e99669'}, {'abstract': 'Amid serious discussions about averting economic catastrophe, the White House rolls out a prank that never gets old.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/27/rick-astley-will-save-us-all/', 'snippet': 'Amid serious discussions about averting economic catastrophe, the White House rolls out a prank that never gets old.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the country — maybe the world — on the edge of economic Armageddon and the parties seemingly incapable of cooperating even in the direst of circumstances, the White House has a message of unity.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rick Astley Will Save Us All', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Astley, Rick', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T22:54:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Wheaton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wheaton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b67cfdf3-3ac0-562f-83b2-3d9dc539a06a', 'word_count': 154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b67cfdf3-3ac0-562f-83b2-3d9dc539a06a'}, {'abstract': 'The keys to taking summer photos are to avoid harsh midday light and spread light around the subject. A flash and sunscreen can help.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/business/summer-photos-without-grimaces.html', 'snippet': 'The keys to taking summer photos are to avoid harsh midday light and spread light around the subject. A flash and sunscreen can help.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ah, summer: the time for sun, sand and harshly lighted photos of the family grimacing into the sun.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For a Day at the Beach, Take Sunscreen and a Flash', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For a Day at the Beach, Take Sunscreen and a Flash', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T22:58:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roy Furchgott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Furchgott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/01137c52-928c-5c05-bc17-8fa176545237', 'word_count': 304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01137c52-928c-5c05-bc17-8fa176545237'}, {'abstract': 'Wesco Aircraft Holdings, a plane equipment service provider owned by the Carlyle Group, priced its initial public offering at $15 a share.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/07/27/carlyles-wesco-prices-its-i-p-o-below-expectations/', 'snippet': 'Wesco Aircraft Holdings, a plane equipment service provider owned by the Carlyle Group, priced its initial public offering at $15 a share.', 'lead_paragraph': '11:26 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Carlyle’s Plane Unit I.P.O. Priced Below Expected Range', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carlyle Group', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T23:02:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d12f1098-cccb-57d6-8d67-9a5a913a93b7', 'word_count': 263, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d12f1098-cccb-57d6-8d67-9a5a913a93b7'}, {'abstract': 'The eco-ideology known as permaculture has entered the mainstream.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/garden/permaculture-emerges-from-the-underground.html', 'snippet': 'The eco-ideology known as permaculture has entered the mainstream.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AS a way to save the world, digging a ditch next to a hillock of sheep dung would seem to be a modest start. Granted, the ditch was not just a ditch. It was meant to be a “swale,” an earthwork for slowing the flow of water down a slope on a hobby farm in western Wisconsin.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/garden/28garden-span/28garden-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 371, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/28/garden/28garden-span/28garden-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 371}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/garden/28garden-span/28GARDEN6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/garden/28garden-span/28garden-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/28/garden/28garden-span/28garden-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Permaculture Movement Grows From Underground', 'kicker': 'In the Garden', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Growing From Underground', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gardens and Gardening', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AGRICULTURE', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sustainable Living', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T23:07:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Tortorello', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tortorello', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71715345-d7c6-57f6-a583-2b8103eef247', 'word_count': 2668, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71715345-d7c6-57f6-a583-2b8103eef247'}, {'abstract': 'Easily cut your boot time in half using solid-state drives, and open applications in a blink.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/technology/personaltech/solid-state-drives-get-you-to-work-faster.html', 'snippet': 'Easily cut your boot time in half using solid-state drives, and open applications in a blink.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For many people, waiting for their computers to boot up is time passed drumming their fingers, making a cup of coffee or watching the grass grow. The delay is because of starting the hard drive, which has to awaken and rev up to retrieve stored data.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/business/28BASICS1/28BASICS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/28/business/28BASICS1/28BASICS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/business/28BASICS1/28BASICS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 623, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/business/28BASICS1/28BASICS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/28/business/28BASICS1/28BASICS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Computer Drives to Start Your Day Quicker', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Computer Drives To Start Your Day Quicker', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Data Storage', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T23:16:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/980256e0-a5e8-5bfe-9ab3-8ef36b8a032a', 'word_count': 1202, 'uri': 'nyt://article/980256e0-a5e8-5bfe-9ab3-8ef36b8a032a'}, {'abstract': 'The designer Steven Sclaroff, who likes to meld disparate styles with a touch of humor, shops for interesting footstools.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/garden/footstools-shopping-with-steven-sclaroff.html', 'snippet': 'The designer Steven Sclaroff, who likes to meld disparate styles with a touch of humor, shops for interesting footstools.', 'lead_paragraph': 'STEVEN SCLAROFF is a big fan of footstools, “both for their intended use and as extra pull-up seating,” he said. “I have them all over my house, and if a lot of people are coming over, I just herd them all into the living room.”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/garden/21shop-span/21shop-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 373, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/21/garden/21shop-span/21shop-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 373}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/garden/21shop-span/21SHOP-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/21/garden/21shop-span/21shop-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/21/garden/21shop-span/21shop-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Footstools', 'kicker': 'Shopping With Steven Sclaroff', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Knocked Off His Feet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Furniture', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T23:24:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rima Suqi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rima', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Suqi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62a19a25-9a8e-5fb8-bc17-824bac9be0b2', 'word_count': 371, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62a19a25-9a8e-5fb8-bc17-824bac9be0b2'}, {'abstract': 'Todd Forrest of the New York Botanical Garden offers tips for saving plants from triple-digit temperatures.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/garden/a-professional-gardener-on-shielding-plants-from-heat-qa.html', 'snippet': 'Todd Forrest of the New York Botanical Garden offers tips for saving plants from triple-digit temperatures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gardeners often think Mother Nature has it in for them, and they may not be far off-base this summer. Triple-digit temperatures and severe droughts in many parts of the country have made the act of gardening borderline Sisyphean, if not a health risk. Just ask the country singer Loretta Lynn: she was hospitalized earlier this month for heat exhaustion after spending time in her Tennessee garden. (“There ain’t a tomato worth it,” Ms. Lynn was quoted as saying in an Associated Press article.)', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/garden/28qna1/28SUBQA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 681, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/garden/28qna1/28qna1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/28/garden/28qna1/28qna1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Professional Gardener on Shielding Plants From Stifling Heat', 'kicker': 'Currents | Q&A', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Professional Gardener on Shielding Plants From Stifling Heat', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gardens and Gardening', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-27T23:24:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Kurutz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kurutz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d08dd92-5208-5dbd-91b6-8c0bc820d2b2', 'word_count': 854, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d08dd92-5208-5dbd-91b6-8c0bc820d2b2'}, {'abstract': 'The ceramicist Jim Schatz set up a studio in Greene, N.Y., and now spends a good part of his time making things for birds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/garden/a-hummingbird-feeder-that-floats-on-the-breeze-outdoors.html', 'snippet': 'The ceramicist Jim Schatz set up a studio in Greene, N.Y., and now spends a good part of his time making things for birds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2004, the ceramicist Jim Schatz left Manhattan to set up a studio in Greene, N.Y., near Binghamton. “Living here, on a creek, exposed me to the birds,” Mr. Schatz said. “And the birds led me to thinking about bird products.”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/garden/28outdoors-span/28outdoors-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/28/garden/28outdoors-span/28outdoors-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/garden/28outdoors-span/28CURRENTS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/garden/28outdoors-span/28outdoors-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumb