ions of salmon in Chile and ravaged the fish farming industry there was probably brought over from Norway, a major salmon producer has acknowledged.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/world/28chile-inline1/28chile-inline1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/world/28chile-inline1/28chile-inline1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/28/world/28chile-inline1/28chile-inline1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Norwegians Concede a Role in Chilean Salmon Virus', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Norwegians Concede a Role In Chilean Salmon Virus', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Salmon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chile', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Norway', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish Farming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-28T00:59:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexei Barrionuevo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexei', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barrionuevo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a51ca61a-104a-5f04-8dc4-bdf8c81f0a98', 'word_count': 841, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a51ca61a-104a-5f04-8dc4-bdf8c81f0a98'}, {'abstract': 'A family’s wrongful-death lawsuit against United Airlines would be the first such case from the World Trade Center attack to go to trial.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/nyregion/family-in-911-suit-may-be-able-to-seek-damages-for-suffering.html', 'snippet': 'A family’s wrongful-death lawsuit against United Airlines would be the first such case from the World Trade Center attack to go to trial.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The final minutes of the passengers on United Airlines Flight 175, the second plane to strike the World Trade Center, were sheer horror, as reported in calls to the ground. The hijackers used pepper spray and knives. A flight attendant had been stabbed; both pilots had been killed.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Judge May Let 9/11 Lawsuit Pursue Damages for Suffering on Doomed Flight', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Judge May Let 9/11 Lawsuit Pursue Damages for Suffering on Doomed Flight', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Trade Center (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bavis, Mark', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hellerstein, Alvin K', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Airlines', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-28T01:03:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Weiser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weiser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e2f3173-cbd4-5d85-b73a-d74dd52fefb7', 'word_count': 815, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e2f3173-cbd4-5d85-b73a-d74dd52fefb7'}, {'abstract': 'Though the withdrawal of American military forces from Iraq and Afghanistan will save the nation billions of dollars, the cost of caring for veterans is projected to grow for decades to come.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/us/28veterans.html', 'snippet': 'Though the withdrawal of American military forces from Iraq and Afghanistan will save the nation billions of dollars, the cost of caring for veterans is projected to grow for decades to come.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Though the withdrawal of American military forces from Iraq and Afghanistan will save the nation billions of dollars a year, another cost of war is projected to continue rising for decades to come: caring for the veterans.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/us/VETERANS/VETERANS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/us/VETERANS/VETERANS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/28/us/VETERANS/VETERANS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cost of Treating Veterans Will Rise Long Past Wars', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A New Chapter in Providing Care for Those Who Serve: Cost of Treating Veterans Will Rise Long Past Wars', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-28T01:04:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Dao', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dao', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2836ac4e-60c2-51c0-8ead-33ce9d99205b', 'word_count': 1014, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2836ac4e-60c2-51c0-8ead-33ce9d99205b'}, {'abstract': 'The Russian government cautioned in a statement issued that it would “not leave unanswered the unfriendly steps” taken by the United States in barring several dozen Russian officials from receiving American visas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/world/europe/28briefs-USISWARNEDON_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'The Russian government cautioned in a statement issued that it would “not leave unanswered the unfriendly steps” taken by the United States in barring several dozen Russian officials from receiving American visas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Russian government cautioned in a statement issued Wednesday that it would “not leave unanswered the unfriendly steps” taken by the United States in barring several dozen Russian officials from receiving American visas over their involvement in the detention and death of the Russian lawyer Sergei L. Magnitsky two years ago. It was one of the Obama administration’s sharpest responses yet to human rights abuses in Russia. The Russian Foreign Ministry said in its statement that the visa ban, coming into force despite the thaw in the two countries’ relations, represented “an instrument of the past.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia: U.S. Is Warned on Visas', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | EUROPE', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia: U.S. Is Warned on Visas', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Visas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-28T01:05:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew E. Kramer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Kramer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/eca93536-b4a0-5b6a-b67e-9be0be477203', 'word_count': 97, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eca93536-b4a0-5b6a-b67e-9be0be477203'}, {'abstract': 'Dunkin’ Brands received a market reception to its debut worthy of a sizzling Internet company, as the fast-food chain’s shares surged 46.6 percent.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/07/27/an-i-p-o-built-on-the-basics-sugar-and-coffee/', 'snippet': 'Dunkin’ Brands received a market reception to its debut worthy of a sizzling Internet company, as the fast-food chain’s shares surged 46.6 percent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The latest splashy stock debut had all the markings of a sizzling technology start-up company: a better-than-expected offering price, a swarm of investors clamoring for shares and a first-day pop that defied a broader market drop.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An I.P.O. Built on the Basics: Sugar and Coffee', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo':