edc3a', 'word_count': 212, 'uri': 'nyt://article/728ba793-b90d-500a-9e78-731cdf7edc3a'}, {'abstract': 'In Norway, a 21-year prison term doesn’t seem long enough to avenge the deaths of 76 people.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/opinion/28rosenbaum.html', 'snippet': 'In Norway, a 21-year prison term doesn’t seem long enough to avenge the deaths of 76 people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NORWAY, a nation far removed from the wickedness of the world, is now facing one of its greatest moral challenges: What to do with Anders Behring Breivik, the man who has confessed to massacring 76 people, many of them children. Norway does not allow for capital punishment, and the longest prison sentence a killer can usually receive there is 21 years. A country of such otherwise good fortune and peaceful intention is now unprepared — legally and morally —to deal with such a monstrous atrocity. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Justice? Vengeance? You Need Both', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Justice? Vengeance? You Need Both', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Breivik, Anders Behring', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Norway', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Anthony, Casey', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Foreman, John', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-28T01:21:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thane Rosenbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/276b5fe1-87d2-52fc-aaca-a07b79b6f249', 'word_count': 918, 'uri': 'nyt://article/276b5fe1-87d2-52fc-aaca-a07b79b6f249'}, {'abstract': 'How John Parker, a slave, found liberty at Manassas.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/27/slavery-and-freedom-at-bull-run/', 'snippet': 'How John Parker, a slave, found liberty at Manassas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the morning of Sunday, July 21, 1861, John Parker and three other men opened fire on Union forces. In the chaos of the Civil War’s first major battle, the group, which was operating a cannon, “couldn’t see the Yankees at all and only fired at random.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Slavery and Freedom at Bull Run', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Slavery', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-28T01:30:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Masur', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Masur', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c5ea932-59d0-5bda-9769-3467c3350582', 'word_count': 1398, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c5ea932-59d0-5bda-9769-3467c3350582'}, {'abstract': 'I have never been ghost hunting before. I have also never been to Staten Island. Now a silent battle rages within me as to which of these firsts is more exciting.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/27/over-the-verrazano-into-the-shadows/', 'snippet': 'I have never been ghost hunting before. I have also never been to Staten Island. Now a silent battle rages within me as to which of these firsts is more exciting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Ghost Hunter has Louis Vuitton floor mats, and this I did not expect. He arrives at my building in a customized white Mitsubishi Eclipse with a sound system that’s Madison-Square-Garden-loud and a TV hidden in the dash. It’s less Ghostmobile, more getaway car. I’d forgotten that, esoteric hobbies aside, the Ghost Hunter was born and raised in Brooklyn. And like a lot of guys from Bergen Beach, he loves his car.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Over the Verrazano, Into the Shadows', 'kicker': 'Townies', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ghosts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Staten Island (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-28T01:30:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alina Simone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Simone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65ff0f36-60a8-5164-b06d-0cc97e6e01f1', 'word_count': 2023, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65ff0f36-60a8-5164-b06d-0cc97e6e01f1'}, {'abstract': 'Questions surround an effort by Essex County to hire a company to run a 450-bed immigrant detention center through a bidding process the county says has been open.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/nyregion/political-links-seen-behind-essex-county-detention-center-bid.html', 'snippet': 'Questions surround an effort by Essex County to hire a company to run a 450-bed immigrant detention center through a bidding process the county says has been open.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Three weeks ago, Essex County, N.J., announced that it was seeking a company to run a 450-bed immigrant detention center, hoping to take advantage of a federally financed initiative to set up such facilities with better supervision and medical care.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/nyregion/Y-IMMIG1/Y-IMMIG1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 356, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/28/nyregion/Y-IMMIG1/Y-IMMIG1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 356}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/nyregion/Y-IMMIG1/Y-IMMIG1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/nyregion/Y-IMMIG1/Y-IMMIG1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/28/nyregion/Y-IMMIG1/Y-IMMIG1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Political Links Seen Behind New Jersey Detention Center Bid', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Political Links And a Jail Bid In North Jersey', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration Detention', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DiVincenzo, Joseph N Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Immigration and Customs Enforcement (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privatization', 'rank': 5, 'major'