es, but a far more crucial issue is the continuing surge in health-care costs, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/which-is-in-worse-shape-u-s-or-europe/', 'snippet': 'All eyes may be on the debt limit in the United States, but a far more crucial issue is the continuing surge in health-care costs, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Simon Johnson, the former chief economist at the International Monetary Fund, is the co-author of “13 Bankers.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Which Is in Worse Shape, U.S. or Europe?', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-28T09:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simon Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f65a6e1-b022-564d-958b-1c68e389645a', 'word_count': 982, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f65a6e1-b022-564d-958b-1c68e389645a'}, {'abstract': 'It dawned on Times editors that they had a photographer in place at Walter Reed who could cover the hospital’s closing. It turned out that he was already on the job.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/back-in-action-and-back-on-page-1/', 'snippet': 'It dawned on Times editors that they had a photographer in place at Walter Reed who could cover the hospital’s closing. It turned out that he was already on the job.', 'lead_paragraph': '“He will be missed until — as I have no doubt he will — he returns to action, cameras blazing.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headl