 Revel Casino, wh...', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you want to revisit some memory lanes, at least of the Parker Brothers sort, from back when you were pretty sure you would make a great real estate tycoon when you grew up, then go to Google Maps and plug in the address for the Revel Casino, which was featured in last weekend’s Look essay. There it is: 500 Boardwalk, Atlantic City, right around the corner from the original Vermont and Oriental Avenues. (Somehow it seems fitting that Morgan Stanley, which lost around a billion dollars on its Revel investment, failed to put the casino on one of the farther-off orange properties, particularly New York Avenue, which, if I read this and this right, is the optimal Monopoly strategy.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Here Comes the Neighborhood', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-28T14:39:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dean Robinson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dean', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robinson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e2ea86e-9721-5600-8c37-46b74d69d668', 'word_count': 274, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e2ea86e-9721-5600-8c37-46b74d69d668'}, {'abstract': 'N.F.L. free agency and trade mania includes the Patriots dealing for Albert Haynesworth, the Dolphins trading for Reggie Bush and the Seahawks signing Sidney Rice.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/n-f-l-free-for-all-central-starring-haynesworth-and-rice/', 'snippet': 'N.F.L. free agency and trade mania includes the Patriots dealing for Albert Haynesworth, the Dolphins trading for Reggie Bush and the Seahawks signing Sidney Rice.', 'lead_paragraph': '4:50 p.m. | Updated While