n capital and exploration expenditures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HOUSTON — Exxon Mobil and Royal Dutch Shell reported large increases in second-quarter profits on Thursday, benefiting from oil and gasoline prices that have been propelled upward by political turbulence in the Middle East and North Africa. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Higher Prices Buoy Profits as Oil Companies Scramble for New Fields', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Higher Prices Buoy Profits as Oil Companies Scramble for New Fields', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Exxon Mobil Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal Dutch Shell Plc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-28T15:12:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clifford Krauss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clifford', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krauss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/395a15c2-b310-5a53-9428-d002ade663e2', 'word_count': 957, 'uri': 'nyt://article/395a15c2-b310-5a53-9428-d002ade663e2'}, {'abstract': 'Advice on handling dinner guests who want to bring extra friends along, restaurants that offer unwanted after-dinner drinks,', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/dear-flofab-my-dinner-guests-invite-their-own-guests/', 'snippet': 'Advice on handling dinner guests who want to bring extra friends along, restaurants that offer unwanted after-dinner drinks,', 'lead_paragraph': 'Each week, Florence Fabricant gives advice on the fine points of entertaining at home and eating in restaurants. Have a dining dilemma? Ask FloFab.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dear FloFab: My Dinner Guests Invite Their Own Guests', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs, Etiquette and Manners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-28T15:24:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ebdd278-1549-52d6-a19d-97ea250f4a6a', 'word_count': 676, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ebdd278-1549-52d6-a19d-97ea250f4a6a'}, {'abstract': 'The price will rise to $25 from $20.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/museum-of-modern-art-raising-admission-and-membership-fees/', 'snippet': 'The price will rise to $25 from $20.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The Museum of Modern Art, faced with what it calls “escalating costs in virtually all aspects of operating the museum,’’ is raising its admission price to $25 for adults from $20, where it has been since 2004. The change takes effect on Sept. 1. Admission will remain free for children 16 and under; the charge for full-time students will rise to $14 from $12.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Museum of Modern Art Raising Admission and Membership Fees', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major'