xpected transformation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this video Sam Grobart, an iPhone user, and Andrew Ross Sorkin, who uses a BlackBerry, decide to swap phones. The change leads to a larger-than-expected transformation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video: A Smartphone Showdown', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'BlackBerry (Handheld Device)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-28T15:37:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/809f1e1c-6dab-58d3-b506-016e0faf02ed', 'word_count': 27, 'uri': 'nyt://article/809f1e1c-6dab-58d3-b506-016e0faf02ed'}, {'abstract': 'The judge accused Ford of concealing documents that may have changed the outcome of a 2010 court case decided in the automaker’s favor.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/florida-judge-throws-out-verdict-in-ford-unintended-acceleration-case/', 'snippet': 'The judge accused Ford of concealing documents that may have changed the outcome of a 2010 court case decided in the automaker’s favor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Florida judge on July 20 said Ford misled the court and federal safety investigators by concealing documents in a case decided in Ford’s favor in 2010. According to the judge, the documents proved that unintended acceleration in certain vehicles could have been caused by electromagnetic interference with those vehicles’ cruise control systems.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Florida Judge Throws Out Verdict in Ford Unintended-Acceleration Case', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Highway Traffic Safety Administration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-28T15:44:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c09599ba-2967-5d41-9201-264daceb9c8f', 'word_count': 612, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c09599ba-2967-5d41-9201-264daceb9c8f'}, {'abstract': 'This week’s pairing: the poem “Lone Egret” by Kathleen M. McCann, and a City Room blog post by Andy Newman about the Harlem Meer.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/poetry-pairing-july-28-2011/', 'snippet': 'This week’s pairing: the poem “Lone Egret” by Kathleen M. McCann, and a City Room blog post by Andy Newman about the Harlem Meer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In our weekly “Poetry Pairing” series, we collaborate with the Poetry Foundation to feature a work from its American Life in Poetry project alongside content from The Times that somehow echoes, extends or challenges the poem’s themes. Each poem is introduced briefly by Ted Kooser, a former United States poet laureate.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Poetry Pairing | July 28, 2011', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-28T15:46:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holly Epstein Ojalvo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holly', 'middlename': 'Epstein', 'lastname': 'Ojalvo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/487eb3f0-fdb5-5e2e-8f58-a7b8fba82bb9', 'word_count': 417, 'uri': 'nyt://article/487eb3f0-fdb5-5e2e-8f58-a7b8fba82bb9'}, {'abstract': 'Taking the blog on the road, and giving it a rest.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/motherlode-and-vacation/', 'snippet': 'Taking the blog on the road, and giving it a rest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As those of you who follow me on Twitter or Facebook already know, I am out of town.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Motherlode, and Vacation', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blogs and Blogging (Internet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Text Messaging', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-28T15:46:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Belkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a41d14c1-77d2-51bc-8228-40089e69299c', 'word_count': 692, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a41d14c1-77d2-51bc-8228-40089e69299c'}, {'abstract': 'Several of Germany’s largest companies reported underwhelming earnings in the second quarter, suggesting a decline in confidence even in Europe’s strongest economies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/business/global/reports-heighten-concerns-about-german-economy.html', 'snippet': 'Several of Germany’s largest companies reported underwhelming earnings in the second quarter, suggesting a decline in confidence even in Europe’s strongest economies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRANKFURT — Underwhelming earnings reports Thursday from several of Germany’s largest companies, along with a report showing a slump in confidence among European business and consumers, raised concerns that growth could be slowing even in the Continent’s strongest economies.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/29/business/Gcon/Gcon-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Weak Earnings in Germany Raise Concerns of Slowing Growth', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Weak Earnings in Germany Raise Concerns of Slowing Growth', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Siemens AG', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Volkswagen AG', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euro (Currency)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-28T15:53:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Ewing', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ewing', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/102d5b2e-ef88-500d-98c2-0c8deff67012', 'word_count': 790, 'uri': 'nyt://article/102d5b2e-ef88-500d-98c2-0c8deff67012'}, {'abstract': 'AMC confirmed widespread reports that the “Walking Dead” producer Frank Darabont had been replaced by Glen Mazzara, effective immediately.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/new-blood-for-the-walking-dead-amc-replaces-producer/', 'snippet': 'AMC confirmed widespread reports that the “Walking Dead” producer Frank Darabont had been replaced by Glen Mazzara, effective immediately.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the middle of production of its highly anticipated second season, “The Walking Dead,” AMC’s much-talked-about drama about the survivors of a zombie infestation, has replaced its show runner. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': "New Blood for ‘The Walking Dead': AMC Replaces Producer", 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Darabont, Frank', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kirkman, Robert', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Centers for Disease Control and Prevention', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Atlanta (Ga)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-28T15:55:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c76f67df-fbc6-5af3-8fad-486b472f734b', 'word_count': 234, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c76f67df-fbc6-5af3-8fad-486b472f734b'}, {'abstract': 'Nicolas Dumit Estevez, an artist transplanted from Manhattan, spent six months creating an exhibit that tries to map the complex personality of the Bronx.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/reborn-in-the-bronx-and-celebrating-its-identity/', 'snippet': 'Nicolas Dumit Estevez, an artist transplanted from Manhattan, spent six months creating an exhibit that tries to map the complex personality of the Bronx.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In April, along a grassy bank in a garden preserve in the Bronx neighborhood known as West Farms, Nicolas Dumit Estevez, clothed in white robe, head nearly shaven, was baptized with the not-so-pure water of the Bronx River. Not as a Christian — as a Bronxite.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reborn in the Bronx, and Celebrating Its Identity', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-28T16:02:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Boryga', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Boryga', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/16a7c9ce-a214-5070-a17a-d5c8c2183584', 'word_count': 627, 'uri': 'nyt://article/16a7c9ce-a214-5070-a17a-d5c8c2183584'}, {'abstract': 'New tools adopted by ecologists from other fields are adding fresh perspectives to old questions, like “Why do pollinators visit certain flowers?”', 'web_url': 'https://scientistatwork.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/the-puzzle-of-plant-pollinator-interactions/', 'snippet': 'New tools adopted by ecologists from other fields are adding fresh perspectives to old questions, like “Why do pollinators visit certain flowers?”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Daniel Song, a doctoral student at the University of Pennsylvania, writes from Hovsgol National Park, Mongolia, where he is studying how plants and pollinators form interaction networks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Puzzle of Plant-Pollinator Interactions', 'kicker': 'Scientist at Work', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flowers and Plants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insects', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Pennsylvania', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mongolia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-28T16:08:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel S. Song', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Song', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/73a34551-c862-5660-8a1b-08ffff9b700f', 'word_count': 519, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73a34551-c862-5660-8a1b-08ffff9b700f'}, {'abstract': 'Though still in their infancy, cardiovascular exercise machines that enable users to generate electricity are growing in popularity at gyms and sports clubs.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/pedaling-your-way-to-environmental-nirvana/', 'snippet': 'Though still in their infancy, cardiovascular exercise machines that enable users to generate electricity are growing in popularity at gyms and sports clubs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Another lunchtime spin class had recently been added by popular demand. But since it was new on the schedule, the session at the New York Sports Club at 23rd Street and Eighth Avenue in Manhattan wasn’t crowded when I arrived on a recent Wednesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pedaling Your Way to Environmental Nirvana', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bicycles and Bicycling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Light and Power', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Clubs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consolidated Edison Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Sports Club', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chelsea (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-28T16:10:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dorothy Spears', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dorothy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spears', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00c4ef8f-d972-5c67-9711-d0529f33b47f', 'word_count': 912, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00c4ef8f-d972-5c67-9711-d0529f33b47f'}, {'abstract': 'Your hint: This repurposed factory now houses artists and studios in a former industrial city that has become a design hub.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/guess-where-this-is-25/', 'snippet': 'Your hint: This repurposed factory now houses artists and studios in a former indu