ns, Verizon Workers Vote to Authorize Strike', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communications Workers of America', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Verizon Communications Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Strikes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telephones and Telecommunications', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Brotherhood of Electrical Workers', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-28T17:20:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Greenhouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenhouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5089ddeb-1b4d-5085-8259-ca9ba4970346', 'word_count': 915, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5089ddeb-1b4d-5085-8259-ca9ba4970346'}, {'abstract': 'The long-rumored Maserati S.U.V., which could be unveiled at the Frankfurt auto show in September, may share fundamental pieces with its Fiat Group brethren, Dodge and Jeep.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/the-maser-ango-italian-s-u-v-might-use-chrysler-platform-from-durango-and-grand-cherokee/', 'snippet': 'The long-rumored Maserati S.U.V., which could be unveiled at the Frankfurt auto show in September, may share fundamental pieces with its Fiat Group brethren, Dodge and Jeep.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The history of crossbred cars is filled with hits and misses. You might end up with the McLaren F1, arguably the best application ever of a BMW engine, or you might end up with the Chrysler TC by Maserati. If you don’t recall the TC, it was a mid-’80s Chrysler LeBaron with a Maserati trident. That mongrel gave opera windows a bad name, which is saying something.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Maser-ango? Italian S.U.V. Might Use Chrysler Platform From Durango and Grand Cherokee', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frankfurt Auto Show', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chrysler LLC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fiat SpA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jeep Division of Chrysler', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Maserati SpA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Porsche AG', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Volkswagen AG', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-28T17:24:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ezra Dyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ezra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6451adb2-9c17-5fbf-a39b-de8cbec38357', 'word_count': 500, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6451adb2-9c17-5fbf-a39b-de8cbec38357'}, {'abstract': 'Officials provided few details as they imposed financial sanctions on six people believed to be Qaeda operatives.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/world/29terror.html', 'snippet': 'Officials provided few details as they imposed financial sanctions on six people believed to be Qaeda operatives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Treasury Department on Thursday accused the Iranian authorities of aiding Al Qaeda and said it was imposing financial sanctions on six people believed to be Qaeda operatives in Iran, Kuwait, Qatar and Pakistan. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Treasury Accuses Iran of Aiding Al Qaeda', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Treasury Dept., Citing Six People as Operatives, Accuses Iran of Aiding Al Qaeda', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-28T17:24:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Helene Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Helene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0084f703-0717-59a6-b9ad-eda7d57bd5fb', 'word_count': 677, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0084f703-0717-59a6-b9ad-eda7d57bd5fb'}, {'abstract': 'Fortune magazine reports on the downfall of Jeff Kindler, and the internal struggles over steering the company forward.', 'web_url': 'https://prescriptions.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/a-new-take-on-pfizers-former-c-e-o/', 'snippet': 'Fortune magazine reports on the downfall of Jeff Kindler, and the internal struggles over steering the company forward.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Jeffrey B. Kindler resigned abruptly on a weekend last December from his post as chief executive of Pfizer, the move startled many people in the pharmaceutical world and raised questions about Mr. Kindler’s stewardship of the company.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Take on Pfizer’s Former C.E.O.', 'kicker': 'Prescriptions', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kindler, Jeffre