ame': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-28T17:31:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ef562d9-3f5b-560c-8ab1-9ffd2d0c201c', 'word_count': 301, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ef562d9-3f5b-560c-8ab1-9ffd2d0c201c'}, {'abstract': 'A report from the Department of Homeland Security gave an indication of the poor state of federal records almost a decade after the Sept. 11, 2001, attacks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/us/29pilot.html', 'snippet': 'A report from the Department of Homeland Security gave an indication of the poor state of federal records almost a decade after the Sept. 11, 2001, attacks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Transportation Security Administration cannot determine the real identities of thousands of the people to whom the Federal Aviation Administration has issued licenses as pilots and aircraft mechanics, but has located an additional 27 who should not have held them because of terrorist connections, according to an internal report by the Department of Homeland Security.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '27 Deemed to Be Threats Held Aviation Licenses', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '27 Deemed to Be Threats Held Aviation Licenses', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Security and Warning Systems', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Aviation Administration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-28T17:41:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4eec3fd9-092f-55b8-9bcc-755a8665f3c7', 'word_count': 708, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4eec3fd9-092f-55b8-9bcc-755a8665f3c7'}, {'abstract': 'Hours after officially announcing they had traded Carlos Beltran to the Giants, the Mets scored nine runs off Reds starter Homer Bailey.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/sports/baseball/mets-complete-trade-of-beltran-to-giants.html', 'snippet': 'Hours after officially announcing they had traded Carlos Beltran to the Giants, the Mets scored nine runs off Reds starter Homer Bailey.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CINCINNATI — Time and again this season, the Mets have found a way to steady themselves in the midst of turbulence.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/29/sports/mets/mets-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 374, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/29/sports/mets/mets-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 374}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/29/sports/mets/mets-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/29/sports/mets/mets-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/29/sports/mets/mets-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mets Complete Beltran Trade and a Four-Game Sweep of the Reds', 'kicker': 'Mets 10, Reds 9', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mets Complete Beltran Trade and a Four-Game Sweep of the Reds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cincinnati Reds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trades (Sports)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco Giants', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beltran, Carlos', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-28T17:43:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Keh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf743bd1-ca17-520d-909d-96b81ed55ca7', 'word_count': 763, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf743bd1-ca17-520d-909d-96b81ed55ca7'}, {'abstract': 'At 14, Sam Ferlo is spending the summer as a clown in a traveling youth circus, putting his father’s lessons to good use.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/us/29land.html', 'snippet': 'At 14, Sam Ferlo is spending the summer as a clown in a traveling youth circus, putting his father’s lessons to good use.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRATTLEBORO, Vt. — Down Clown Alley, in the backstage tent for Circus Smirkus, a slight boy of 14 studies his clown self in a jagged piece of mirror. This is Sam Ferlo, the son of a former circus clown and a former circus showgirl, and the godson of a man once known as the Human Cannonball.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/29/us/29land/29land-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/29/us/29land/29land-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/29/us/29land/29land-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Young Clown Follows in a Father’s Giant Footsteps', 'kicker': 'This Land', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Son Follows Giant Footsteps Into the Big Tent', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Circuses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Clowns', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-28T17:49:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Barry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee79ebba-dfbb-55a7-9e34-7c01acc1b012', 'word_count': 1271, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee79ebba-dfbb-55a7-9e34-7c01acc1b012'}, {'abstract': 'Defensive end Mathias Kiwanuka re-signs with the Giants on Thursday, reversing the team’s string of departures on defense.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/kiwanuka-re-signs-with-giants/', 'snippet': 'Defensive end Mathias Kiwanuka re-signs with the Giants on Thursday, reversing the team’s string of departures on defense.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Giants have agreed to terms with defensive end Mathias Kiwanuka, who missed all but three games last season with a neck injury.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kiwanuka Re-Signs With Giants', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Free Agents (Sports)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lockouts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kiwanuka, Mathias', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-28T18:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Tanier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tanier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5fc9b938-178c-542c-9fbd-e71cffb69b6f', 'word_count': 203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5fc9b938-178c-542c-9fbd-e71cffb69b6f'}, {'abstract': 'Adam Dunn of the White Sox was hitting .161 through Wednesday, putting him on a pace for the lowest batting average by a player who qualified for a batting title since 1910.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/keeping-score-adam-dunns-historically-bad-season/', 'snippet': 'Adam Dunn of the White Sox was hitting .161 through Wednesday, putting him on a pace for the lowest batting average by a player who qualified for a batting title since 1910.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This generation of baseball fans has grown accustomed to records falling, both at the plate and on the mound, but this season the Chicago White Sox slugger Adam Dunn is quietly making history of a different sort. With a batting average of .161, he is on track to put up the lowest single-season batting average by any player qualified for a batting title since 1910.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Keeping Score: Adam Dunn’s Historically Bad Season', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago White Sox', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-28T18:00:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By NEIL PAINE', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'PAINE', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c078fe6a-70e3-50f8-9896-a878d32aae30', 'word_count': 743, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c078fe6a-70e3-50f8-9896-a878d32aae30'}, {'abstract': 'The rationale for the reduced pay for rookies in the new labor deal is that they should prove themselves before being showered with money.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/sports/football/nfl-veterans-sold-out-rookies-in-labor-deal.html', 'snippet': 'The rationale for the reduced pay for rookies in the new labor deal is that they should prove themselves before being showered with money.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The empty feeling some players may have in their hearts this week is a sense of guilt that comes from betrayal. To achieve a deal, top N.F.L. rookies were sacrificed. They will receive less so veteran players and retired players can receive more. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit'