pt', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-28T20:47:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By JOHN BURNHAM SCHWARTZ', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'Burnham', 'lastname': 'SCHWARTZ', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'First Chapter', '_id': 'nyt://article/231aacd3-e91e-5438-a8ca-a3453fc7394e', 'word_count': 908, 'uri': 'nyt://article/231aacd3-e91e-5438-a8ca-a3453fc7394e'}, {'abstract': 'In “Northwest Corner,” John Burnham Schwartz picks up the story of his novel “Reservation Road” 12 years later.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/books/northwest-corner-by-john-burnham-schwartz-book-review.html', 'snippet': 'In “Northwest Corner,” John Burnham Schwartz picks up the story of his novel “Reservation Road” 12 years later.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Humpty-Dumpty of families, the Arnos seem irreparably broken apart. We first came to know them in John Burnham Schwartz’s 1998 novel, “Reservation Road.” Eloquently told but brutal, the story follows the Arnos and another family as they collide in a horrific car accident and shatter.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/29/arts/29BOOK-AUTHOR/BOOK-AUTHOR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 682, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/29/arts/29BOOK-AUTHOR/29BOOK-AUTHOR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': '