s of three to six months in jail.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SERANG, Indonesia — Twelve members of a mob that set upon adherents of an Islamic sect, killing three of them, received sentences of three to six months in jail on Thursday. Rights advocates criticized the ruling as an example of growing impunity for violence against religious minorities in Indonesia. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/29/world/29indonesia/29indonesia-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 745, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/29/world/29indonesia/29indonesia-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/29/world/29indonesia/29indonesia-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rights Advocates Criticize Light Sentences in Sectarian Killings in Indonesia', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rights Advocates Criticize Light Sentences in Sectarian Killings in Indonesia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indonesia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ahmadiyya (Muslim Sect)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Human Rights Watch', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yudhoyono, Susilo Bambang', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-28T21:01:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Aubrey Belford', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Aubrey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09f61232-0b94-5c60-8de8-0970118cda46', 'word_count': 476, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09f61232-0b94-5c60-8de8-0970118cda46'}, {'abstract': 'A temporary rink opened on Thursday at 30th Street and 10th Avenue, giving something new for people on the restored elevated railroad track to look down on.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/below-the-high-line-spiraling-roller-skaters/', 'snippet': 'A temporary rink opened on Thursday at 30th Street and 10th Avenue, giving something new for people on the restored elevated railroad track to look down on.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The man was an island of bliss in the midst of chaos. He twirled, spinning on roller skates under the High Line, balanced and composed. Around him, people were falling. Legs splayed. Wrists buckled. An ankle was sprained.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Below the High Line, Spiraling Roller Skaters', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'High Line (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roller Skating', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Friends of the High Line', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-28T21:02:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, '