ney properly in reducing crowded classrooms. On Thursday, the Appellate Division backed up the city.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/city-wins-appeal-of-law-suit-over-class-size/', 'snippet': 'A group of plaintiffs, including the teachers’ union, contended that the city didn’t spend state money properly in reducing crowded classrooms. On Thursday, the Appellate Division backed up the city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A lawsuit claiming that the city misused millions of dollars in state money earmarked to reduce class sizes was dismissed Thursday by an appeals court.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'City Wins Appeal of Law Suit Over Class Size', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mulgrew, Michael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walcott, Dennis M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Federation of Teachers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-28T21:36:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sharon Otterman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sharon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Otterman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/31112fc9-9369-5ecb-91fc-0e0104994981', 'word_count': 289, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31112fc9-9369-5ecb-91fc-0e0104994981'}, {'abstract': 'If you have ever dreamed of entering a boxing ring with Mike Tyson, the former heavyweight champion, an update and contest added to the boxer’s iOS game could make that happen.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/boxing-mike-tyson-on-an-iphone-and-in-real-life/', 'snippet': 'If you have ever dreamed of entering a boxing ring with Mike Tyson, the former heavyweight champion, an update and contest added to the boxer’s iOS game could make that happen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most people would not be too excited about the idea of entering a boxing ring with Mike Tyson, the former heavyweight champion. But for those who find the prospect appealing, here’s your opportunity.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Boxing Mike Tyson on an iPhone, and in Real Life', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boxing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tyson, Mike', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Las Vegas (Nev)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nevada', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-28T21:38:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a92b545-537f-55ee-8002-c4ca00d898c2', 'word_count': 273, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a92b545-537f-55ee-8002-c4ca00d898c2'}, {'abstract': 'Mark Duplass stars in Craig Johnson’s film “True Adolescents,” which explores the sexual discomfort of boys and men not entirely secure in their masculinity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/movies/mark-duplass-in-craig-johnsons-true-adolescents-review.html', 'snippet': 'Mark Duplass stars in Craig Johnson’s film “True Adolescents,” which explores the sexual discomfort of boys and men not entirely secure in their masculinity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Craig Johnson’s tender indie comedy, “True Adolescents,” examines the interim passages of male lives when time is nervously frittered away and the future looms through the mist like a giant scary question mark.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/29/arts/29TRUE/TRUE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 614, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/29/arts/29TRUE/29TRUE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/29/arts/29TRUE/29TRUE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Great Outdoors Beckons as a Test of Manhood', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'True Adolescents'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Great Outdoors Beckons As a Test of Manhood', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duplass, Mark', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leo, Melissa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Craig', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-28T21:43:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba8bbf41-6697-5326-804b-ed39ef155489', 'word_count': 748, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba8bbf41-6697-5326-804b-ed39ef155489'}, {'abstract': 'With a baby on the way, Katie and Kevin Hogan made a nursery in a corner of their one-bedroom on East 72nd Street.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/31/realestate/an-apartment-with-a-little-give-habitatsupper-east-side.html', 'snippet': 'With a baby on the way, Katie and Kevin Hogan made a nursery in a corner of their one-bedroom on East 72nd Street.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KATIE WADE, a copywriter for a pharmaceutical advertising agency who grew up in New Jersey, moved to New York in 2003 after graduating from Georgetown. She did the usual bouncing around — living in one apartment after another with various friends from high school and college. But after a few years, she decided it was finally time to acquire a place of her own.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/31/realestate/31HABI3/31HABI3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/31/realestate/31HABI3/31HABI3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/31/realestate/31HABI3/31HABI3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Apartment With a Little Give', 'kicker': 'Habitats | Upper East Side', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Apartment With a Little Give', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Upper East Side (NYC)', 'r