 lover’s mistreatment — was a fine match for the expressive bigness of her voice. Its sound, more distractingly, was pure Strokes: strobing guitar chords, peppy bass line, terse drumming. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/29/arts/29SIA_SPAN/SIA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/29/arts/29SIA_SPAN/SIA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 340}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/29/arts/29SIA_SPAN/SIA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 587, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/29/arts/29SIA_SPAN/SIA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/29/arts/29SIA_SPAN/SIA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Big-Voiced Singer Takes Off In Several Directions at Once', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Big-Voiced Singer Takes Off In Several Directions at Once', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Webster Hall', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-28T22:09:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac082d1b-ced9-5435-9c1b-0a5d16ff4af0', 'word_count': 583, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac082d1b-ced9-5435-9c1b-0a5d16ff4af0'}, {'abstract': 'The 17th-century Dutch painter Frans Hals is the focus of a small exhibition at the Met.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/arts/design/frans-hals-at-metropolitan-museum-review.html', 'snippet': 'The 17th-century Dutch painter Frans Hals is the focus of a small exhibition at the Met.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The most useful knowledge we have about the great 17th-century Dutch painter Frans Hals is what we glean from the vibrant, shimmering surfaces of his art. He was an amazingly gifted technician, capable of defining the human face in passages of seemingly quick, vivacious brush strokes that convey both physical solidity and expressive fluidity. He was also something of an empath, intuitively alert, it would seem, to what was going on behind those faces. He approached his subjects with an open, nonjudgmental equanimity, whether he depicted them singly or in groups, in dignified repose or unbridled revelry. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/29/arts/20110729-hals-ss-slide-M5XH/20110729-hals-ss-slide-M5XH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 827, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/29/arts/20110729-hals-ss-slide-M5XH/20110729-hals-ss-slide-M5XH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/29/arts/20110729-hals-ss-slide-M5XH/20110729-hals-ss-slide-M5XH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Faces Still Alive, Centuries Later', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Faces Still Alive, Centuries Later', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hals, Frans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Museum of Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-28T22:11:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roberta Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roberta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/49708f66-1d34-5962-bcd8-9f09d64e0a87', 'word_count': 1481, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49708f66-1d34-5962-bcd8-9f09d64e0a87'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Livingston is the president of the Tishman Construction Corporation and the chief executive of construction services for the Aecom Technology Corporation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/31/realestate/john-t-livingston.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Livingston is the president of the Tishman Construction Corporation and the chief executive of construction services for the Aecom Technology Corporation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mr. Livingston, 58, is the president of the Tishman Construction Corporation and the chief executive of construction services for the Aecom Technology Corporation, which acquired Tishman in July 2010 for $245 million in cash and stock. Tishman is the construction manager for several ground-zero projects, including 1 World Trade Center and the PATH Terminal Hub.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/31/realestate/SUB-SqFt/SUB-SqFt-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 6