, a Democrat — would affect the economy over the next decade.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Debt Fixes’ Drag on the Economy', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gross National Product (GNP)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-28T22:20:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd749636-7804-5c32-a693-cb71d8dfa82e', 'word_count': 324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd749636-7804-5c32-a693-cb71d8dfa82e'}, {'abstract': 'A selection of rock and pop listings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/arts/music/rock-and-pop-listings-july-29-aug-4.html', 'snippet': 'A selection of rock and pop listings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pop', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rock and Pop Listings July 29 — Aug. 4', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Listings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-28T22:21:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article