erest, or revealed any noteworthy evidence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/sports/basketball/still-seeking-answers-family-sues-in-wrights-death.html', 'snippet': 'Since the murder, the police have not made any arrests, named any suspects or persons of interest, or revealed any noteworthy evidence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MEMPHIS — A year after the body of the veteran N.B.A. player Lorenzen Wright was discovered in a wooded area in this city’s southeast suburbs, family and friends gathered Thursday for a candlelight vigil outside the FedEx Forum to draw attention to the still-unsolved killing.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/29/sports/sub-wright/sub-wright-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 333, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/29/sports/sub-wright/sub-wright-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 333}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/29/sports/sub-wright/sub-wright-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/29/sports/sub-wright/sub-wright-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/29/sports/sub-wright/sub-wright-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After a Year, No Answers in N.B.A. Player’s Death', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Looking for Answers In a Player’s Death', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wright, Lorenzen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Memphis (Tenn)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T00:06:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Card', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Card', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4cb328ba-355f-5d00-be40-4e9b7d40d360', 'word_count': 808, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4cb328ba-355f-5d00-be40-4e9b7d40d360'}, {'abstract': 'The police said they found a military uniform with Fort Hood patches, a pistol, shotgun shells and an article on “how to make a bomb in your kitchen” in the suspect’s motel room.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/us/29awol.html', 'snippet': 'The police said they found a military uniform with Fort Hood patches, a pistol, shotgun shells and an article on “how to make a bomb in your kitchen” in the suspect’s motel room.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An Army private who had been absent without leave since earlier this month was arrested this week near Fort Hood with a gun and suspicious materials in what local law enforcement officials described on Thursday as a “terror plot” to kill other soldiers.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/29/us/AWOL/AWOL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 670, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/29/us/AWOL/AWOL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/29/us/AWOL/AWOL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Soldier Held Amid Claim of Terror Plot at Fort Hood', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Soldier Held Amid Claim Of Terror Plot At Fort Hood', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fort Hood (Tex)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hasan, Nidal Malik', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T00:07:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4857891-0104-59ac-9e8c-fb440fe5e24e', 'word_count': 627, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4857891-0104-59ac-9e8c-fb440fe5e24e'}, {'abstract': '“The Devil’s Double,” a slick, English-language excursion into Saddam Hussein’s Iraq, might seem either timely or insensitive, given the uprisings in the Middle East.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/movies/the-devils-double-a-look-at-iraq-review.html', 'snippet': '“The Devil’s Double,” a slick, English-language excursion into Saddam Hussein’s Iraq, might seem either timely or insensitive, given the uprisings in the Middle East.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As people across the Arab world struggle to shake off the burdens of dictatorship, the release of “The Devil’s Double,” a slick English-language excursion into Saddam Hussein’s Iraq, might seem either timely or insensitive. Shot in lurid, gilded tones; pulsing with pop decadence, the film is less an anatomy of authoritarian politics than a gangster movie. Mercedes-Benz sedans hurtle through the streets; men in dark suits and sunglasses share the screen with women in lingerie; guns are drawn and fired; and life is either a nonstop war or an endless party, or both.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/29/arts/29DEVIL_SPAN/29DEVIL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/29/arts/29DEVIL_SPAN/29DEVIL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 340}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/29/arts/29DEVIL_SPAN/29DEVIL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/29/arts/29DEVIL_SPAN/29DEVIL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/29/arts/29DEVIL_SPAN/29DEVIL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Straight From Uday Hussein’s Inner Circle', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'The Devil’s Double'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Straight From Uday Hussein’s Inner Circle', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cooper, Dominic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tamahori, Lee', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T00:16:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [