ract': 'Data from 2009, 2010 and 2011 show that spring was a frustrating season in the combat zones.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/opinion/states-of-conflict-an-update.html', 'snippet': 'Data from 2009, 2010 and 2011 show that spring was a frustrating season in the combat zones.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE spring of 2011 brought perhaps the single biggest highlight in the war on terrorism since 9/11: the killing of Osama bin Laden in Pakistan. Generally, however, it was a frustrating season in the combat zones, as shown below in data from April 1 to June 30 of 2009, 2010 and 2011.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'States of Conflict: An Update', 'kicker': 'Op-Chart', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'States of Conflict: An Update', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T01:10:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': "By IAN LIVINGSTON and MICHAEL E. O'HANLON", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'LIVINGSTON', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': "O'HANLON", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/9af90e11-80c1-590c-90c1-97cf31106c8e', 'word_count': 344, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9af90e11-80c1-590c-90c1-97cf31106c8e'}, {'abstract': 'The Campaign Against Marijuana Planting, whose costs are shared by the State of California and the federal government, is endangered because of California budget cuts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/us/29bccamp.html', 'snippet': 'The Campaign Against Marijuana Planting, whose costs are shared by the State of California and the federal government, is endangered because of California budget cuts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Wednesday, a helicopter buzzed over the rugged hills of Mendocino National Forest and lowered five narcotics agents dressed in green fatigues and armed with guns, clippers and machetes. Under the bright blue sky, the crew began to cut down thousands of marijuana plants that were flourishing with the help of an irrigation system in a remote section of the forest in Tehama County.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/29/us/29bccamp/29bccamp-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/29/us/29bccamp/29bccamp-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/29/us/29bccamp/29bccamp-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/29/us/29bccamp/29bccamp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/29/us/29bccamp/29bccamp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Budget Cuts Endanger State’s Marijuana Eradication Program', 'kicker': 'The Bay Citizen', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Budget Cuts Endanger State’s Marijuana Eradication Program', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marijuana', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parks and Other Recreation Areas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T01:14:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zusha Elinson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zusha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elinson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e19c48d-691d-5f90-a4b4-f06fa389dcd0', 'word_count': 1157, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e19c48d-691d-5f90-a4b4-f06fa389dcd0'}, {'abstract': 'Irabu, a star pitcher in Japan who died on Thursday, burst on the scene with the Yankees in July 1997.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/sports/baseball/irabu-baseball-rock-star-played-yankee-stadium.html', 'snippet': 'Irabu, a star pitcher in Japan who died on Thursday, burst on the scene with the Yankees in July 1997.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the night Hideki Irabu first pitched in New York City, 51,901 fans squeezed into old Yankee Stadium along with a news media contingent of almost 300, at least a third of which were Japanese. In Japan, the morning television audience exceeded 30 million.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/29/sports/ARATON2/ARATON2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 682, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/29/sports/ARATON2/ARATON2-thumbStand