 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/29/nyregion/ALT-ABOUT/ALT-ABOUT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/29/nyregion/ALT-ABOUT/ALT-ABOUT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/29/nyregion/ALT-ABOUT/ALT-ABOUT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/29/nyregion/ALT-ABOUT/ALT-ABOUT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Accuser Gets Her Day, Though Not in Court', 'kicker': 'About New York', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For an Accuser, Getting the Day, But Not in Court', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Diallo, Nafissatou', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strauss-Kahn, Dominique', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vance, Cyrus R Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T01:46:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Dwyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dwyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fee2c8e7-0f11-5ff8-aae6-ecc4eab8bdcd', 'word_count': 812, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fee2c8e7-0f11-5ff8-aae6-ecc4eab8bdcd'}, {'abstract': 'The numbers of Hispanic and Asian New Yorkers grew more slowly, the black population fell and the shrinking of the non-Hispanic white population eased.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/nyregion/census-finds-slight-stabilizing-in-new-york-city-racial-makeup.html', 'snippet': 'The numbers of Hispanic and Asian New Yorkers grew more slowly, the black population fell and the shrinking of the non-Hispanic white population eased.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York City edged a baby step closer to racial equilibrium in the last decade, according to census results released this month. Compared with the 1990s, the numbers of Hispanic and Asian New Yorkers grew more slowly; blacks recorded their first population loss since the Civil War; and non-Hispanic whites, who registered their smallest population loss in decades, also logged the biggest gains of any group among young children. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Slower Racial Change Found in Census of City', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Slower Racial Change Found in Census of City', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Census', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T01:50:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Roberts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roberts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6bd4a29-440e-5278-be8a-e309db06dbbb', 'word_count': 799, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6bd4a29-440e-5278-be8a-e309db06dbbb'}, {'abstract': 'In “All She Can” a young woman seeks a way out from her small Texas town through sports.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/movies/all-she-can-review.html', 'snippet': 'In “All She Can” a young woman seeks a way out from her small Texas town through sports.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Perched somewhere between hard-luck tale and inspirational story, “All She Can,” about a high school girl trying to win a scholarship to the University of Texas, mostly feels as ponderous as the sport that might be her ticket out: powerlifting.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/29/arts/29ROUNDUP_ALL/29ROUNDUP_ALL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/29/arts/29ROUNDUP_ALL/29ROUNDUP_ALL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 340}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/29/arts/29ROUNDUP_ALL/29ROUNDUP_ALL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/29/arts/29ROUNDUP_ALL/29ROUNDUP_ALL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/29/arts/29ROUNDUP_ALL/29ROUNDUP_ALL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Powerlifting as Escape', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': "Movie Review | 'All She Can'", 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T01:52:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Saltz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saltz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e387085-cc6f-5160-b6fe-f5e1b5094a07', 'word_count': 351, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e387085-cc6f-5160-b6fe-f5e1b5094a07'}, {'abstract': 'With his photographs, Mr. Liebling brought about a deep awareness of the personal in the political, and influenced a generation of photographers and documentary filmmakers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/arts/design/jerome-liebling-photographer-and-mentor-is-dead-at-87.html', 'snippet': 'With his photographs, Mr. Liebling brought about a deep awareness of the personal in the political, and influenced a generation of photographers and documentary filmmakers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jerome Liebling, whose subtly powerful pictures and the lessons he drew from them influenced a generation of socially minded photographers and documentary filmmakers, died on Wednesday in Northampton, Mass. He was 87. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/02/arts/design/2liebling/2liebling-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 742, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/02/arts/design/2liebling/2liebling-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/08/02/arts/design/2liebling/2liebling-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jerome Liebling, Socially Minded Photographer, Dies at 87', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jerome Liebling, 87, Realist Photographer and Teacher', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Liebling, Jerome', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hampshire College', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T01:56:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randy Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kennedy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/345fa980-0738-55ce-b84c-aba9161d2395', 'word_count': 785, 'uri': 'nyt://article/345fa980-0738-55ce-b84c-aba9161d2395'}, {'abstract': '“Sleep Furiously,” Gideon Koppel’s documentary, tracks how time passes in a Welsh farming community.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/movies/sleep-furiously-review.html', 'snippet': '“Sleep Furiously,” Gideon Koppel’s documentary, tracks how time passes in a Welsh farming community.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not much happens in Gideon Koppel’s film “Sleep Furiously,” an impressionistic documentary about Trefeurig, a farming community in Wales. A calf is born; a choir sings; a cake is baked. The action heats up a bit when the film checks in with a yellow library van, manned by a kindly fellow who chats with the villagers about books and the town.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/29/arts/29ROUNDUP_SLEEP/29ROUNDUP_SLEEP-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/29/arts/29ROUNDUP_SLEEP/29ROUNDUP_SLEEP-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 340}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption':