f feasting with a visit to mosques for prayers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — The relentless cycle of protest and crackdown in Syria over the last four months appears poised to enter a new phase in the coming Muslim holy month of Ramadan, with activists planning to capitalize on religious rhythms to hold nightly demonstrations despite fears of an even harsher government reaction.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Syrians Planning for Stepped Up Protests During Ramadan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Syrians Planning for Stepped-Up Protests During Ramadan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ramadan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mosques', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T02:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nada Bakri', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nada', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakri', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1797f937-1f7c-53f5-8470-d864dc58fe42', 'word_count': 761, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1797f937-1f7c-53f5-8470-d864dc58fe42'}, {'abstract': 'An interesting-looking grid from Paula Gamache.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/deflation/', 'snippet': 'An interesting-looking grid from Paula Gamache.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRIDAY’S PUZZLE — Well. This is an interesting-looking grid. And it’s not meant to represent anything other than your standard Friday crossword grid. It’s certainly not implying that it’s anything else, unlike a certain Sunday puzzle from not too long ago that I am still getting mail about, by the way. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Friday: They’re Subject to Inflation and Deflation', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T02:00:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a714a266-3bbf-5ade-9eab-2f362410273c', 'word_count': 233, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a714a266-3bbf-5ade-9eab-2f362410273c'}, {'abstract': 'A hike in government fuel rules to 54.5 miles per gallon by 2025 is being meekly accepted by the car industry.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/business/carmakers-back-strict-new-rules-for-gas-mileage.html', 'snippet': 'A hike in government fuel rules to 54.5 miles per gallon by 2025 is being meekly accepted by the car industry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DETROIT — Four years ago, the American auto industry was so opposed to higher fuel economy standards that executives of Detroit camped out in Washington in an unsuccessful bid to undercut them.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/29/business/29cafePicA/29cafePi