embers of Congress, who are concerned with the clawback lawsuits filed by the trustee, Irving H. Picard.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Government Accountability Office, the investigative arm of Congress, will evaluate the actions of the trustee for the victims of Bernard L. Madoff’s fraud; the Securities Investor Protection Corporation, which appointed the trustee; and the Securities and Exchange Commission, in the liquidation of Madoff’s firm.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Actions of Madoff Victims’ Trustee Will Be Reviewed', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Actions of Madoff Victims’ Trustee Will Be Reviewed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Picard, Irving H', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Madoff, Bernard L', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ponzi and Pyramid Schemes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilpon, Fred', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities Investor Protection Corp', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T02:34:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e93dd3a-2225-5ec0-8c90-db012a151f75', 'word_count': 277, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e93dd3a-2225-5ec0-8c90-db012a151f75'}, {'abstract': 'Hours of arm-twisting do not produce enough vote for Speaker John A. Boehner to pass his legislation.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/28/no-vote-thursday-night-on-debt-plan/', 'snippet': 'Hours of arm-twisting do not produce enough vote for Speaker John A. Boehner to pass his legislation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Republican leaders in the House have announced that there will be no vote on the debt ceiling bill Thursday night, an indication that Speaker John A. Boehner remains short of the votes necessary to pass his legislation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Vote Thursday Night on Debt Plan', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T02:40:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84ee5a3e-76e8-58fc-944d-079585b14170', 'word_count': 140, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84ee5a3e-76e8-58fc-944d-079585b14170'}, {'abstract': 'The conference has added Nebraska, divisional play and a championship game, but the troubles faced by some of its marquee teams still dominate the conversation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/sports/despite-changes-scandal-remains-hot-topic-for-big-ten.html', 'snippet': 'The conference has added Nebraska, divisional play and a championship game, but the troubles faced by some of its marquee teams still dominate the conversation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — With Nebraska joining the Big Ten and the addition of divisional play and a championship game, the conference is anticipating a historic season. But scandal was an unavoidable topic of discussion Thursday as coaches and conference officials addressed reporters on Big Ten media day at a downtown hotel here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Despite Changes, Scandal Remains Hot Topic for Big Ten', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Despite Changes, Scandal Remains Hot Topic for Big Ten', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Collegiate Athletic Assn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Big Ten Conference', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Nebraska', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T02:52:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan McGrath', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGrath', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fe723cb-0a34-5cef-812f-d31654feb925', 'word_count': 464, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fe723cb-0a34-5cef-812f-d31654feb925'}, {'abstract': 'In Scottsdale, Ariz., a conservative place in a conservative state, many golfers expressed dismay at Democrats and at a dearth of politicians with integrity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/us/politics/29gopdistrict.html', 'snippet': 'In Scottsdale, Ariz., a conservative place in a conservative state, many golfers expressed dismay at Democrats and at a dearth of politicians with integrity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SCOTTSDALE, Ariz. — Keith Tassio was steaming, and the fierce summer sun was only partly to blame. Golfers view their game as a respite from life’s frustrations, and here he was, about to putt on the ninth hole of one of Scottsdale’s many, many golf courses, being asked about Washington, of all things.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Time