new stimulant drug known as bath salts passed the Senate Judiciary Committee unanimously Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A bill that would ban the new stimulant drug known as bath salts passed the Senate Judiciary Committee unanimously Thursday. The bill, which was sponsored by Senator Charles E. Schumer, Democrat of New York, would make mephedrone and methylenedioxypyrovalerone illegal to possess or sell. Both would be added to the list of controlled Schedule I substances. Bath salts are typically sold online or in convenience stores or head shops, and doctors report seeing agitated, violent behavior in some users. At least 29 states have banned bath salts, which are sold under names including Ivory Wave and Vanilla Sky and are typically injected, smoked or snorted. The bill will go to the Senate floor. \xa0 ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bill to Ban Stimulant Drug Advances in Senate', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | WASHINGTON', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bill to Ban Stimulant Drug Advances in Senate', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schumer, Charles E', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T03:43:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katie Zezima', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zezima', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/89b8c2c0-71bf-51b2-9a63-428b5a0b8b99', 'word_count': 114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89b8c2c0-71bf-51b2-9a63-428b5a0b8b99'}, {'abstract': 'Barry H. Landau, a New York-based historian and writer, was indicted Thursday by a federal grand jury on charges of conspiring to steal historical documents and sell them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/us/29brfs-HISTORIANISI_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'Barry H. Landau, a New York-based historian and writer, was indicted Thursday by a federal grand jury on charges of conspiring to steal historical documents and sell them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Barry H. Landau, a New York-based presidential historian and writer, was indicted Thursday by a federal grand jury on charges of conspiring to steal historical documents and sell them, according to the United States attorney’s office in Baltimore. Mr. Landau, 63, and Jason Savedoff, 24, his colleague, who was also charged, could face up to 10 years in prison if convicted of theft of documents, which federal prosecutors say include a letter from Benjamin Franklin to John Paul Jones taken from the New-York Historical Society. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Maryland: Historian Is Indicted in Theft of Documents', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | MID-ATLANTIC', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Maryland: Historian Is Indicted in Theft of Documents', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Landau, Barry H', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maryland', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T03:44:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sabrina Tavernise', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sabrina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tavernise', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '