Ms. Platt, who was nominated for an Oscar, collaborated with her ex-husband Peter Bogdanovich on films like “The Last Picture Show.” She was also a screenwriter and producer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Polly Platt, a Hollywood producer, designer and screenwriter who was responsible for the aesthetic of several of Peter Bogdanovich’s early films, died on Wednesday at her home in Brooklyn. She was 72.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/29/obituaries/29platt-pic/29platt-pic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 776, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/29/obituaries/29platt-pic/29platt-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/29/obituaries/29platt-pic/29platt-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Polly Platt, Producer and Production Designer, Dies at 72', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Polly Platt, Film Producer and Designer, Dies at 72', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T04:54:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margalit Fox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margalit', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fox', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/c32eeef7-16e3-5bbd-8493-3445708a8a67', 'word_count': 636, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c32eeef7-16e3-5bbd-8493-3445708a8a67'}, {'abstract': '“Betty Blue Eyes,” the musical at the Ivor Novello Theater based on the 1984 film “A Private Function,” captures the the writer Alan Bennett’s sensibility in its portrayal of the age of austerity in postwar Britain.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/london-theater-journal-a-pig-that-would-make-a-playwright-proud/', 'snippet': '“Betty Blue Eyes,” the musical at the Ivor Novello Theater based on the 1984 film “A Private Function,” captures the the writer Alan Bennett’s sensibility in its portrayal of the age of austerity in postwar Britain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – Never let it be said that the pig is not a lady. Yes, the title character of “Betty Blue Eyes,” the slyly winning new musical at the Ivor Novello Theater, is irrefutably porcine. She emits odors that cause everyone around her to gag, and you do need to watch where you step after she’s been in the room. Yet this over-size porker has a shy, persuasive charm that can only be described as genteel. The same may be said of the show in which she appears.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'London Theater Journal: A Pig That Would Make a Playwright Proud', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bennett, Alan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Drewe, Anthony', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eyre, Richard', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mackintosh, Cameron', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mear, Stephen', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shearsmith, Reece', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stiles, George', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T05:00:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/532229cc-c13e-5c4d-b619-4ef00e4225e5', 'word_count': 923, 'uri': 'nyt://article/532229cc-c13e-5c4d-b619-4ef00e4225e5'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on July 29, 2011.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/pageoneplus/corrections-july-29.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on July 29, 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRONT PAGE', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: July 29', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T06:35:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e854362-5c06-5a7b-a496-b8712eb460b6', 'word_count': 479, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e854362-5c06-5a7b-a496-b8712eb460b6'}, {'abstract': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/news-quiz-july-29-2011/', 'snippet': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'See what you know about the news below. To prepare, you might scan the articles or summaries on today’s paper.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Quiz | July 29, 2011', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date