made public so people can see what is being done in their name and with their tax dollars.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/31/opinion/sunday/executions-should-be-televised.html', 'snippet': 'Executions ought to be made public so people can see what is being done in their name and with their tax dollars.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mr. Shemtob is an assistant professor of criminal justice at Central Connecticut State University. Mr. Lat, a former federal prosecutor, is the founder of Above the Law, a legal blog. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/31/opinion/sunday/31executions/31executions-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/31/opinion/sunday/31executions/31executions-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/31/opinion/sunday/31executions/31executions-jumbo-v2.gif', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/31/opinion/sunday/31executions/31executions-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/31/opinion/sunday/31executions/31executions-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Executions Should Be Televised', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Executions Should Be Televised', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recordings and Downloads (Video)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grant, Andrew', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T14:31:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By ZACHARY B. SHEMTOB and DAVID LAT', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zachary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/c43ea659-eb12-5a56-ad4a-120808e1fae4', 'word_count': 816, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c43ea659-eb12-5a56-ad4a-120808e1fae4'}, {'abstract': 'Why the Republican Party might be better off if the Boehner bill fails in the House.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/crisis-of-the-house-divided/', 'snippet': 'Why the Republican Party might be better off if the Boehner bill fails in the House.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jonah Goldberg, on the ongoing agony of the House Republican caucus:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Crisis of the House Divided', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T14:32:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a2aba17-14cc-51ca-9b60-e9212697e216', 'word_count': 526, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a2aba17-14cc-51ca-9b60-e9212697e216'}, {'abstract': 'Activity on the nest is a sign that Bobby intends to return to breed there come winter.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/hawk-cam-bobby-visits-nest-as-pip-explores-union-square/', 'snippet': 'Activity on the nest is a sign that Bobby intends to return to breed there come winter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Things have been quiet indeed up on the red-tailed hawk nest above Washington Square Park. But on Thursday afternoon at about 2:45, Bobby, father of Pip, came back to do a little ritualistic tidying. John Blakeman, hawk expert and nest watcher, said that the visit means that Bobby has every intention of returning to the nest to breed again. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hawk Cam | Bobby Visits Nest as Pip Explores Union Square', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hawks (Birds)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington Square Park (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T14:39:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman and Emily S. Rueb', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Rueb', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1c1ad01-0e54-58ad-8d91-7a90e2cce279', 'word_count': 213, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1c1ad01-0e54-58ad-8d91-7a90e2cce279'}, {'abstract': 'Online video requires drastically different media skills because it is consumed in a highly specific way.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/when-shilling-on-the-web-think-small/', 'snippet': 'Online video requires drastically different media skills because it is consumed in a highly specific way.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mariah Carey and Barack Obama each had something to sell this week, and they made live videos to do it. Both videos bombed. Ms. Carey’s pitch on HSN, for tracksuits and other sundries from her fashion label, was too weird. Mr. Obama’s pitch on the networks for Congressional compromise wasn’t nearly weird enough.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Shilling on the Web, Think Small', 'kicker': 'Virginia Heffernan', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carey, Mariah', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'YouTube.com', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T14:40:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Virginia Heffernan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Virginia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Heffernan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2c4b39b-cbe5-591d-9856-72c48d91097b', 'word_count': 915, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2c4b39b-cbe5-591d-9856-72c48d91097b'}, {'abstract': 'Unlike other purely electric cars, the subbrand’s runabout, scheduled for production in 2013, will offer an optional gasoline-burning range extender.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/range-extending-option-for-electric-bmw-i3-a-smart-hedge/', 'snippet': 'Unlike other purely electric cars, the subbrand’s runabout, scheduled for production in 2013, will offer an optional gasoline-burning range extender.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Friday in Frankfurt, BMW showed working prototypes of its i3 electric runabout and i8 plug-in hybrid sports coupe. The carbon-fiber-reinforced concepts were relatively faithful to the renderings that accompanied the launch of the German automaker’s “i” subbrand in February. A new wrinkle, however, is the addition of an optional gasoline-burning range extender for the i3, an otherwise purely electric car.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Range-Extending Option for Electric BMW i3: a Smart Hedge?', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Vehicles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Engines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bayerische Motorenwerke AG', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Frankfurt (Germany)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T14:42:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Schultz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schultz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6eced78b-1bf7-51cc-a8f3-cbc2b72a7bee', 'word_count': 314, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6eced78b-1bf7-51cc-a8f3-cbc2b72a7bee'}, {'abstract': 'We’ll be busy working behind the scenes to get the blog ready for the next academic year. Meanwhile, however, here are some things to do while we’re gone.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/the-learning-network-is-on-hiatus-next-week/', 'snippet': 'We’ll be busy working behind the scenes to get the blog ready for the next academic year. Meanwhile, however, here are some things to do while we’re gone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We’re busy working behind the scenes these days, including helping our Newspaper in Education colleagues with their annual series of teacher workshops (PDF), which this year we’ve enjoyed presenting out at The New York Times printing plant in Queens. (Please note: all workshops are now closed.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Learning Network Is on Hiatus Next Week', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T14:46:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8f7c230-a56c-510f-b315-dfac176f2a30', 'word_count': 237, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8f7c230-a56c-510f-b315-dfac176f2a30'}, {'abstract': 'July 28, 2011 - The hotel maid accusing Dominique Straus-Kahn of sexual assault, speaks out again at a Brooklyn press conference.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/multimedia/100000000971678/timescast--nafissatou-diallo-speaks.html', 'snippet': 'July 28, 2011 - The hotel maid accusing Dominique Straus-Kahn of sexual assault, speaks out again at a Brooklyn press conference.', 'lead_paragraph': 'July 28, 2011 - The hotel maid accusing Dominique Straus-Kahn of sexual assault, speaks out again at a Brooklyn press conference.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/multimedia/video-tc-110728-accuser/video-tc-110728-accuser-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/28/multimedia/video-tc-110728-accuser/video-tc-110728-accuser-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlarge