minee to the White House.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISLESBORO, Maine — President Obama on Thursday afternoon nominated Ronnie Abrams, a lawyer at Davis Polk & Wardwell, to serve as a judge in Federal District Court in Manhattan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Davis Polk Lawyer Nominated for Federal Bench', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Courts (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gillibrand, Kirsten E', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Davis Polk & Wardwell', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T14:59:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/26cb99c6-53fa-5f19-bb22-6d2ea52010ac', 'word_count': 499, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26cb99c6-53fa-5f19-bb22-6d2ea52010ac'}, {'abstract': 'Senator Harry Reid of Nevada, the majority leader, said he would move ahead on Friday with a Democratic plan to increase the debt limit.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/reid-says-he-will-move-ahead-with-his-bill/', 'snippet': 'Senator Harry Reid of Nevada, the majority leader, said he would move ahead on Friday with a Democratic plan to increase the debt limit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Senator Harry Reid of Nevada, the majority leader, said he would move ahead on Friday with a Democratic plan to increase the debt limit, saying he could no longer wait for House Republicans to complete their version.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reid Says He Will Move Ahead With His Bill', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T15:07:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D.Shear and Robert Pear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/530eff34-c6c4-5dbe-ba47-eb39d1ff1db3', 'word_count': 298, 'uri': 'nyt://article/530eff34-c6c4-5dbe-ba47-eb39d1ff1db3'}, {'abstract': 'Despite its expense, Medicare remains quite popular, researchers find.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/how-do-you-feel-about-medicare/', 'snippet': 'Despite its expense, Medicare remains quite popular, researchers find.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What Americans really think about Medicare: They like it. They don’t want to see it significantly changed. But they’re conscious of the federal deficit and willing to consider a number of strategies to reduce the gap, including raising taxes on high earners, spending less on foreign aid and overseas military commitments, and limiting tax deductions for large corporations. They’re even amenable to certain cost-cutting measures in Medicare itself.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Do You Feel About Medicare?', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T15:09:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paula Span', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paula', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Span', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a5efe97-65b0-531e-9335-bdb52287b8da', 'word_count': 203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a5efe97-65b0-531e-9335-bdb52287b8da'}, {'abstract': 'How will climate change affect the diverse plant community that feeds the inhabitants of the northern Mongolian steppe?', 'web_url': 'https://scientistatwork.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/plants-climate-and-a-midsummer-festival/', 'snippet': 'How will climate change affect the diverse plant community that feeds the inhabitants of the northern Mongolian steppe?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Laura Fox, a postdoctoral researcher with the University of Pennsylvania, writes from Mongolia, where she is studying the effects of climatic warming on steppe vegetation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Plants, Climate and a Midsummer Festival', 'kicker': 'Scientist at Work', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flowers and Plants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Pennsylvania', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mongolia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T15:11:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laura Fox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laura', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fox', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/86398fd5-02de-5be6-897d-f2655d838d00', 'word_count': 607, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86398fd5-02de-5be6-897d-f2655d838d00'}, {'abstract': 'Now that a sewage discharge caused by a fire has passed, officials call their attention to a perennial cause of contamination: storm water that overwhelms the treatment system.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/on-hudson-pollution-back-to-routine-worries/', 'snippet': 'Now that a sewage discharge caused by a fire has passed, officials call their attention to a perennial cause of contamination: storm water that overwhelms the treatment system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Water tests along the Hudson River show that bacteria levels are falling near the North River Wastewater Treatment Plant in Harlem, which stopped treating sewage for a few days last week because of a fire.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Hudson Pollution, Back to Routine Worries', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T15:12:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mireya Navarro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mireya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Navarro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d634538-339b-5ccb-854f-b578a8d0c0de', 'word_count': 457, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d634538-339b-5ccb-854f-b578a8d0c0de'}, {'abstract': 'The book is tentatively scheduled to come out in 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/linda-ronstadt-writing-a-memoir/', 'snippet': 'The book is tentatively scheduled to come out in 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Linda Ronstadt is joining the music memoir club with her own book, “Heart Like a Wheel,” said her publisher, Simon & Schuster. The memoir, titled after her hit 1974 album, will focus on her long career, during which she has sold more than 100 million records. “Few singers have been as wide-ranging or as distinctive in their artistry,” Jonathan Karp, the publisher of Simon & Schuster, said in a statement. “Linda Ronstadt has a singular voice, and that is true on the page as well.” The book is tentatively scheduled for publication in 2013.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Linda Ronstadt Writing a Memoir', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Book Trade and Publishing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karp, Jonathan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ronstadt, Linda', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Simon & Schuster Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T15:26:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d3c4a44-ef30-55b5-9948-19062847ae5d', 'word_count': 95, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d3c4a44-ef30-55b5-9948-19062847ae5d'}, {'abstract': 'With the city pushing relentlessly against Jamaica Bay, advocates are toiling to keep the 20,000-acre wildlife haven vital.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/31/nyregion/jamaica-bay-a-wild-place-on-the-edge-of-change.html', 'snippet': 'With the city pushing relentlessly against Jamaica Bay, advocates are toiling to keep the 20,000-acre wildlife haven vital.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OF all the ways to describe Jamaica Bay — it is the city’s largest open space, it is a perch of choice for more than 300 species of birds, it is that wetland thing you fly above while landing at (or leaving) Kennedy Airport — the most suggestive of its singularity is that it sits within the only national park in the United States you can reach by subway. ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/31/nyregion/31JAMAICA1/31JAMAICA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 369, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/31/nyregion/31JAMAICA1/31JAMAICA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 369}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/31/nyregion/31JAMAICA1/31JAMAICA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 706, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/31/nyregion/31JAMAICA1/31JAMAICA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/31/nyregion/31JAMAICA1/31JAMAICA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jamaica Bay: Wilderness on the Edge', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jamaica Bay: Wilderness On the Edge', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jamaica Bay (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T15:27:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Feuer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Feuer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/54b28c74-708c-574e-84f8-cdb896066845', 'word_count': 2469, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54b28c74-708c-574e-84f8-cdb896066845'}, {'abstract': 'Susana Baca, the acclaimed singer and soul of Afro-Peruano music, became on Thursday the first black cabinet minister of independent Peru.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/heart-and-soul/', 'snippet': 'Susana Baca, the acclaimed singer and soul of Afro-Peruano music, became on Thursday the first black cabinet minister of independent Peru.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Susana Baca, the acclaimed singer and soul of Afro-Peruano music, became the first black cabinet minister of independent Peru when she was sworn in as minister of culture on Thursday by the country’s new president, Ollanta Humala. Baca, 67, is revered for mixing Andean and African rhythms and has played a key role in the revival of Afro-Peruano music and dance — folkloric traditions long sidelined in Peru.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Heart and Soul', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T15:30:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abby Aguirre', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Aguirre', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5efd9f8-ee33-5dd8-8e48-03154189b01f', 'word_count': 185, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5efd9f8-ee33-5dd8-8e48-03154189b01f'}, {'abstract': 'The political insurgency that put Republicans into power in the House also has the potential to leave the party divided.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/30/us/politics/30assess.html', 'snippet': 'The political insurgency that put Republicans into power in the House also has the potential to leave the party divided.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — There is an old Texas saying often applied to politics that you need to “dance with the one that brung you.” But many of the Tea Party-infused freshmen who helped the Republican Party take control of the House last November are here to polka while their leadership is begging them to waltz.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'G.O.P. Fervor Cuts 2 Ways for Boehner', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Bid to Conquer Debt, G.O.P. Faces a Divide', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T15:39:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/666b3db3-aa69-5dac-9988-244bd0f94d4a', 'word_count': 1093, 'uri': 'nyt://article/666b3db3-aa69-5dac-9988-244bd0f94d4a'}, {'abstract': 'This week, Helen Schulman on her new novel, "The Beautiful Life"; the linguist Ben Zimmer explains how computers reveal the jargon of fiction; Julie Bosman has notes from the field; and Jennifer Schuessler has best-seller news. Sam Tanenhaus is the host.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2011/07/29/books/booksupdate/29bookreview_pod.html', 'snippet': 'This week, Helen Schulman on her new novel, "The Beautiful Life"; the linguist Ben Zimmer explains how computers reveal the jargon of fiction; Julie Bosman has notes from the field; and Jennifer Schuessler has best-seller news. Sam Tanenhaus is th...', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week, Helen Schulman on her new novel, "The Beautiful Life"; the linguist Ben Zimmer explains how computers reveal the jargon of fiction; Julie Bosman has notes from the field; and Jennifer Schuessler has best-seller news. Sam Tanenhaus is the host.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Helen Schulman on her novel, "The Beautiful Life"; how computers reveal the jargon of fiction; best-seller news.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T15:44:25+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Books Update', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/81530cc6-4082-533b-99e7-cfd0adc38965', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/81530cc6-4082-533b-99e7-cfd0adc38965'}, {'abstract': 'In its report to the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration, the automaker said that it was not aware of any accidents related to the steering problem.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/8400-volvo-s80-sedans-recalled-for-sudden-loss-of-power-assist/', 'snippet': 'In its report to the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration, the automaker said that it was not aware of any accidents related to the steering problem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Volvo is recalling about 8,400 of its S80 sedans from 2007 for possible steering problems.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '8,400 Volvo S80 Sedans Recalled for Sudden Loss of Power Assist', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobi