mon misunderstanding: yes, MTV still plays music videos. Honest. Watch in the early morning for an hour or two under the “AMTV” tag — I’ve seen them only when awake for a doctor’s appointment or, more likely, up late for an overnight deadline, but they’re there, you naysayers. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/29/arts/television/minutes-span/minutes-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/29/arts/television/minutes-span/minutes-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/29/arts/television/minutes-span/minutes-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 976, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/29/arts/television/minutes-span/minutes-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/29/arts/television/minutes-span/minutes-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tuning in to Nostalgia (and Even Videos) on MTV', 'kicker': "Critic's Notebook", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Nod to Past, A Few Videos', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MTV Networks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T16:56:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8eb78abe-afa6-5729-93eb-76b3e4a53287', 'word_count': 724, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8eb78abe-afa6-5729-93eb-76b3e4a53287'}, {'abstract': 'Few foods are as versatile as the tomato, as Martha Rose Shulman demonstrates in this week’s Recipes for Health. She offers tomatoes that are Sicilian and stuffed, slow roasted, sweet and sour, souped up or succulent in salad.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/cooking-with-summer-tomatoes/', 'snippet': 'Few foods are as versatile as the tomato, as Martha Rose Shulman demonstrates in this week’s Recipes for Health. She offers tomatoes that are Sicilian and stuffed, slow roasted, sweet and sour, souped up or succulent in salad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Few foods are as versatile as the tomato, as Martha Rose Shulman demonstrates in this week’s Recipes for Health. She offers tomatoes that are Sicilian and stuffed, slow roasted, sweet and sour, souped up or succulent in salad.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Summer Tomatoes: Stuffed, Sweet and Souped Up', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T17:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Parker-Pope', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker-Pope', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aefacff9-713b-5037-9174-6de2277e04bc', 'word_count': 135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aefacff9-713b-5037-9174-6de2277e04bc'}, {'abstract': 'With federal fuel-economy standards rising, it is little wonder that automakers are expanding the search for simple ways to squeeze more energy from petroleum fuels.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/31/automobiles/latest-out-of-tailpipes-electricity-with-exhaust.html', 'snippet': 'With federal fuel-economy standards rising, it is little wonder that automakers are expanding the search for simple ways to squeeze more energy from petroleum fuels.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EVEN the most efficient of modern cars has a wasteful streak: only about a quarter of the energy contained in the fuel the engine burns is converted to motion. Much of the lost energy flows out of the tailpipe in the form of hot exhaust gases, researchers at General Motors say. ', 'print_section': 'AU', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/31/automobiles/31WAST/31WAST-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/31/automobiles/31WAST/31WAST-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/31/automobiles/31WAST/31WAST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 603, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/31/automobiles/31WAST/31WAST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/31/automobiles/31WAST/31WAST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Latest Out of Tailpipes: Electricity With Exhaust', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Latest Out of Tailpipes: Electricity With Exhaust', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fuel Efficiency', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Energy Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bayerische Motorenwerke AG', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T17:01:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Automobiles', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Ashley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ashley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/947f1789-e7b4-5764-a59b-d77648f67fa0', 'word_count': 484, 'uri': 'nyt://article/947f1789-e7b4-5764-a59b-d77648f67fa0'}, {'abstract': 'European countries offer a variety of incentives to nudge their residents into electric and hybrid vehicles. Here’s a breakdown.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/31/automobiles/europes-incentive-plans-for-spurring-ev-sales.html', 'snippet': 'European countries offer a variety of incentives to nudge their residents into electric and hybrid vehicles. Here’s a breakdown.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EUROPEAN governments are reaching deep into their pockets and plumbing the depths of their imaginations to get electric vehicles out of showrooms and onto the highway. Though the goals of the individual countries are mostly similar — carbon-free fleets in pollution-free cities — many different approaches to making it happen are in place. ', 'print_section': 'AU', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia'