pending/', 'snippet': 'Dwindling government spending was one of the factors holding back growth in the second quarter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Congress continues to wrangle over a debt reduction bill that will inevitably cut government spending, Friday’s estimates of second-quarter gross domestic product provided a sobering look at how a decline in public spending and investment can restrain growth.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Role of Government Spending', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gross Domestic Product', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T17:04:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Motoko Rich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Motoko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8380cef0-19b4-5b5f-a789-a1b742127f9d', 'word_count': 371, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8380cef0-19b4-5b5f-a789-a1b742127f9d'}, {'abstract': 'A recipe for Vietnamese Grilled Duck Salad With Cucumber, Radishes and Peanuts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/08/03/dining/vietnamese-grilled-duck-salad-with-cucumber-radishes-and-peanuts-recipes.html', 'snippet': 'A recipe for Vietnamese Grilled Duck Salad With Cucumber, Radishes and Peanuts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Time: 40 minutes plus at least 90 minutes’ marinating', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/03/dining/APPE/APPE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 385, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/08/03/dining/APPE/APPE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 385}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/03/dining/APPE/APPE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/03/dining/APPE/APPE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/08/03/dining/APPE/APPE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Vietnamese Grilled Duck Salad With Cucumber, Radishes and Peanuts', 'kicker': 'Recipe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Vietnamese Grilled Duck Salad with Cucumber, Radishes and Peanuts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Salads', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poultry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grilling (Cooking)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T17:05:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'recipe', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae2afe28-ba91-5213-a03f-baab81a66827', 'word_count': 392, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae2afe28-ba91-5213-a03f-baab81a66827'}, {'abstract': 'A grilled duck salad with Vietnamese seasonings is zesty, cool and satisfying on a steamy summer night, and the rendered fat from the meat can be stored for later.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/08/03/dining/duck-fat-for-later-a-salad-for-now-a-good-appetite.html', 'snippet': 'A grilled duck salad with Vietnamese seasonings is zesty, cool and satisfying on a steamy summer night, and the rendered fat from the meat can be stored for later.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN I cook duck, it’s just as often for the rendered fat as it is for the meat. As much as I love the gamy, sweet flesh, it’s the fat that I really crave. I keep a jar of the heady stuff in the fridge, pulling it out when I want to sauté fish or potatoes or kale, or pop a vat of popcorn. I use it to make pie crusts and biscuits, and to fry chicken. When my supplies run low, I simply cook up some more duck to replenish it.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/03/dining/APPE/APPE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 385, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/08/03/dining/APPE/APPE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 385}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/03/dining/APPE/APPE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/03/dining/APPE/APPE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/08/03/dining/APPE/APPE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Duck Fat for Later, a Salad for Now', 'kicker': 'A Good Appetite', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Duck Fat For Later, A Salad For Now', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'valu