', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good tomatoes are in, finally. Real, farm-grown meaty tomatoes, like classic Beefsteak and Brandywine and Lemon Boy, and sweet cherry tomatoes of different colors. So a fine tomato salad comes to mind, but what about a sandwich? Not a BLT; not tomato, avocado and sprouts. Rather, a Mediterranean sandwich of tomatoes with capers, anchovy and basil, piled into a freshly baked roll. A little bit soggy, completely heavenly. And no need to turn on the oven. Read about it, along with a few other sandwich reveries, in this week’s City Kitchen.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Little More Than Great Tomatoes and Bread', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sandwiches', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tomatoes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T17:34:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Tanis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tanis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0979bf20-e1b7-5c64-923f-c9d2dc371170', 'word_count': 161, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0979bf20-e1b7-5c64-923f-c9d2dc371170'}, {'abstract': 'Toyota has taken its popular Prius hybrid and made it more big-box friendly. The car is longer, roomier and has much more trunk space.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/31/automobiles/autoreviews/the-toyota-prius-v-a-hybrid-that-hauls-more-stuff.html', 'snippet': 'Toyota has taken its popular Prius hybrid and made it more big-box friendly. The car is longer, roomier and has much more trunk space.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TESTED 2012 P