ate': '2011-07-29T21:19:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Society', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': 'Weddings', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9be0513-c887-561d-9461-99ebc51f93fc', 'word_count': 230, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9be0513-c887-561d-9461-99ebc51f93fc'}, {'abstract': 'A research scientist and an investment banker, both graduates of Emory University, marry in Rye, N.Y.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/31/fashion/weddings/katharine-mccarthy-william-rosener-weddings.html', 'snippet': 'A research scientist and an investment banker, both graduates of Emory University, marry in Rye, N.Y.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Katharine Joy McCarthy and William Lincoln Rosener were married Saturday in Rye, N.Y. Carol A. Fabietti, an aunt of the bridegroom who became a Universal Life minister for the occasion, officiated at the Wainwright House, an event space. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/31/fashion/weddings/31MCCARTHYjpg/31MCCARTHYjpg-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 612, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/31/fashion/weddings/31MCCARTHYjpg/31MCCARTHYjpg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/31/fashion/weddings/31MCCARTHYjpg/31MCCARTHYjpg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Katharine McCarthy, William Rosener', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Katharine McCarthy, William Rosener', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T21:19:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Society', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': 'Weddings', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0a2ece7-00f6-58c6-8dde-05441ab095c6', 'word_count': 219, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0a2ece7-00f6-58c6-8dde-05441ab095c6'}, {'abstract': 'Under the speaker’s plan,  the debt limit could be raised by $1.6 trillion in February — but only if the nation’s archivist reports that a balanced budget amendment has been sent to the states for ratification.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/boehners-bill-and-the-balanced-budget-amendment/', 'snippet': 'Under the speaker’s plan,  the debt limit could be raised by $1.6 trillion in February — but only if the nation’s archivist reports that a balanced budget amendment has been sent to the states for ratification.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Speaker John A. Boehner’s debt ceiling bill would essentially require a two-thirds vote in both chambers of Congress before the nation’s debt ceiling could be raised next year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Boehner’s Bill and the Balanced Budget Amendment', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T21:25:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36864241-1b81-56a2-9339-bda780b44a6f', 'word_count': 236, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36864241-1b81-56a2-9339-bda780b44a6f'}, {'abstract': 'A total unknown, a 24-year-old Army medic from Shreveport, La., has been signed to a Givenchy exclusive by the label’s designer Riccardo Tisci.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/caesar-stovall-army-medic-turned-givenchy-model/', 'snippet': 'A total unknown, a 24-year-old Army medic from Shreveport, La., has been signed to a Givenchy exclusive by the label’s designer Riccardo Tisci.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE military trains its personnel to do battle, and so does fashion. The techniques and methods may differ, but the core precepts are the same.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Caesar Stovall, Army Medic Turned Givenchy Model', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Models (Professional)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T21:27:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Guy Trebay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Guy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Trebay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/66bbc883-433d-5874-bf84-454f5f139a4a', 'word_count': 568, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66bbc883-433d-5874-bf84-454f5f139a4a'}, {'abstract': 'As part of the “Celebrate Brooklyn!” festival, the Mark Morris Dance Group performed three works on Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/30/arts/dance/mark-morris-dance-at-prospect-park-bandshell-review.html', 'snippet': 'As part of the “Celebrate Brooklyn!” festival, the Mark Morris Dance Group performed three works on Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No choreographer alive is more bewildering than Mark Morris. Much of his work is strikingly cerebral and schematic, and yet its main effect tends to be the direct opposite. His dancers exude a visceral urgency, an innocent charm and a “you could do this too” simplicity of style that turn the connection between them and the audience into a bond of love and recognition. On one level, his dances are all about the raw stuff of dance itself. On another, they plainly have much to say. They are about the multiple layers of their music, and yet, in terms of timing, imagery and structure, their fit to the score is frequently — deliberately — disconcerting. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/30/arts/morris/morris-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 311, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/30/arts/morris/morris-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 311}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/30/arts/morris/morris-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 531, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/30/arts/morris/morris-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/30/arts/morris/morris-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Some Death, Some Struggle, Some Strain, Yet So Much Still Is Joyful', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Some Death, Some Struggle, Some Strain, Yet So Much Still Is Joyful', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Morris, Mark, Dance Group', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Philharmonic', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morris, Mark', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T21:34:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/218f68a3-eba8-58af-af3a-6ebe02eb859e', 'word_count': 1022, 'uri': 'nyt://article/218f68a3-eba8-58af-af3a-6ebe02eb859e'}, {'abstract': 'The bands Weezer and the Flaming Lips appeared together at the PNC Bank Arts Center on Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/30/arts/music/weezer-and-the-flaming-lips-in-concert-review.html', 'snippet': 'The bands Weezer and the Flaming Lips appeared together at the PNC Bank Arts Center on Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HOLMDEL, N.J. — Weezer, established in 1992, and the Flaming Lips, established in 1983, have both had multiple-act, hill-and-dale careers in what used to be called alternative rock. Presumably, so have their listeners, some of whom are closing in on 50. But they don’t have much else in common, and that’s partly why their collaboration on Thursday at PNC Bank Arts Center here — repeated on Friday at Jones Beach — felt like a bright idea. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/30/arts/30WEEZER/30WEEZER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 666, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/30/arts/30WEEZER/30WEEZER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/30/arts/30WEEZER/30WEEZER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Team of Introvert and Extrovert', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Team of Introvert and Extrovert', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Weezer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Rivers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T21:35:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Ratliff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ratliff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f8d849c-9d7e-5cc9-80e8-e91449b1a9ef', 'word_count': 799, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f8d849c-9d7e-5cc9-80e8-e91449b1a9ef'}, {'abstract': 'Along with the work of the Danish composer Carl Nielsen, the Royal Danish Orchestra presented Stravinsky’s complete ballet music for “Pulcinella” at the Lincoln Center Festival on Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/30/arts/music/royal-danish-orchestra-at-lincoln-center-festival-review.html', 'snippet': 'Along with the work of the Danish composer Carl Nielsen, the Royal Danish Orchestra presented Stravinsky’s complete ballet music for “Pulcinella” at the Lincoln Center Festival on Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The official biography of the Royal Danish Orchestra does not mince words: this, we are told, is “the oldest orchestral institution in the world,” tracing its origin to the trumpet corps in the court of King Christian I and dating from 1448. To put that date into perspective, the institution was founded 100 years before the Dresden Staatskapelle, often cited as one of the world’s oldest orchestras; 435 years before the Norwegian composer Johan Svendsen inaugurated the Danish orchestra’s symphonic concert series; and 441 years before the Danish composer Carl Nielsen took his position among its second violins.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/30/arts/royal/royal-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/30/arts/royal/royal-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/30/arts/royal/royal-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Danes Deliver Rare Works by a Native Son', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Danes Deliver Rare Works by a Native Son', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nielsen, Carl', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T21:37:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb86c928-9b35-5305-8841-9b224812ba5b', 'word_count': 411, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb86c928-9b35-5305-8841-9b224812ba5b'}, {