 the Motherlode book club book, and Fetal Origins Research.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Annie Murphy Paul came to visit me at The Times earlier this week, and we chatted in front of some cameras about her book “Origins: How the\xa0 Nine Months Before Birth Shape the Rest of Our Lives.” Much of our conversation was about the potential use and misuse of fetal origins research: Would it be a trigger for greater resources toward helping pregnant women be healthy? To reduce their stress, improve their nutrition, and clean their environments? Or would it become just one more way to blame the mother?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Will Fetal Science Lead to Lawsuits?', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Obstetrics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T21:53:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Belkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c7d9c9c6-c107-5c66-85a7-b19404e294e5', 'word_count': 1048, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c7d9c9c6-c107-5c66-85a7-b19404e294e5'}, {'abstract': 'New bells and whistles aren’t the only reason to upgrade to Lion. The new version of Apple’s operating system for the Mac also includes updated security features.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/lions-upgraded-robust-security-features/', 'snippet': 'New bells and whistles aren’t the only reason to upgrade to Lion. The 