ough environments. And, as the work of Times photographers shows through the decades, they always have.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/a-citys-hard-edges-softened-by-joy/', 'snippet': 'Children in New York can make the best of tough environments. And, as the work of Times photographers shows through the decades, they always have.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Is there a creature as imaginative or as indefatigable as the city child in search of a place to play? New York would seem to have been designed for everything but youthful frolic. And, to be sure, it can hold great perils. Yet from generation to generation — ever since the kids sang “Ring Around the Rosie” and “London Bridge Is Falling Down” — the sidewalks of New York have yielded to youngsters’ inexhaustible need to frisk, exult, screech, plot and plunge.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A City’s Hard Edges, Softened by Joy', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Youth', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T23:15:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Dunlap and Darcy Eveleigh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Dunlap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Darcy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eveleigh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e28cf5e3-d13f-5a43-9ac1-368a68737b24', 'word_count': 275, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e28cf5e3-d13f-5a43-9ac1-368a68737b24'}, {'abstract