d in Southern California, where predawn interruptions usually come from car alarms, it took some time to realize he was hearing the muezzin’s call to prayer.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/30/us/RELIGION/RELIGION-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 863, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/30/us/RELIGION/RELIGION-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/30/us/RELIGION/RELIGION-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A War-Hardened Filmmaker Delves Into Islam', 'kicker': 'On Religion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A War-Hardened Filmmaker Delves Into Islam', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Koran', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T23:38:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Samuel G. Freedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Samuel', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'Freedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a41fe548-080a-552b-84a6-3bb354940eab', 'word_count': 999, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a41fe548-080a-552b-84a6-3bb354940eab'}, {'abstract': 'A blue-ribbon commission recommends a new process for choosing a permanent repository for the nation’s nuclear waste based on sound science and local consent.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/how-to-pick-a-site-for-a-nuclear-waste-dump/', 'snippet': 'A blue-ribbon commission recommends a new process for choosing a permanent repository for the nation’s nuclear waste based on sound science and local consent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The United States can find a way to dispose of its nuclear waste, even if the current program is at an impasse, according to the blue-ribbon commission established by President Obama after he ended the government’s planning for making Yucca Mountain in Nevada the nation’s nuclear waste repository.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Pick a Site for a Nuclear Waste Dump', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Wastes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chu, Steven', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Makhijani, Arjun', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Energy Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yucca Mountain (Nev)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-29T23:39:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8bba99e-b289-52bf-b9f0-f933d3100731', 'word_count': 610, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8bba99e-b289-52bf-b9f0-f933d3100731'}, {'abstract': 'A look at the latest Weekend Business podcast, and a listen.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/podcast-g-d-p-european-stocks-