url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/senate-tables-boehner-bill/', 'snippet': 'Less than two hours after the House approved its debt-limit measure, the Democratic leaders in the Senate followed through on their promise to kill the  legislation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The United States Senate quickly dispatched the debt ceiling bill passed by the House Friday evening, tabling the Republican bill indefinitely and moving quickly to start consideration of a Democratic plan that would avoid default on Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Senate Tables Boehner Bill', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-30T00:28:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/573303b2-0c30-5214-9e92-c03ab4cf555e', 'word_count': 161, 'uri': 'nyt://article/573303b2-0c30-5214-9e92-c03ab4cf555e'}, {'abstract': 'At a number of Manhattan restaurants, the draft wine comes from the Gotham Project, which extols benefits like freshness and convenience.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/31/nyregion/gotham-project-pushes-a-tap-wine-manifesto.html', 'snippet': 'At a number of Manhattan restaurants, the draft wine comes from the Gotham Project, which extols benefits like freshness and convenience.', 'lead_paragraph': '“WARNING: Wine Not Beer,” reads the disclaimer on the draft handle behind the bar at Terroir Tribeca, a wine bar on Harrison Street in Manhattan. You’ll find the same thing at the restaurants Buttermilk Channel and Colicchio & Sons, where the taps dispense red, white and rosé, all from a keg-wine company known as the Gotham Project. ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/31/nyregion/31GOTHAM1-SPAN/31GOTHAM1-SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/31/nyregion/31GOTHAM1-SPAN/31GOTHAM1-SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/31/nyregion/31GOTHAM1-SPAN/31GOTHAM1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/31/nyregion/31GOTHAM1-SPAN/31GOTHAM1-SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/31/nyregion/31GOTHAM1-SPAN/31GOTHAM1-SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Partners Push a Tap Wine Manifesto', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Partners Push a Tap Wine Manifesto', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Colicchio & Sons', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Red Rooster (NYC Restaurant)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'DBGB (NYC Restaurant)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'City Winery', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-30T00:28:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/33187e85-3a69-5f63-80f8-fe5338c3cc50', 'word_count': 799, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33187e85-3a69-5f63-80f8-fe5338c3cc50'}, {'abstract': 'As a witness in a nonfatal Manhattan shootout in which he was among the injured, a boy helped bring the killer in a different shooting to justice.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/30/nyregion/young-witness-to-a-new-york-shooting-helps-convict-a-killer.html', 'snippet': 'As a witness in a nonfatal Manhattan shootout in which he was among the injured, a boy helped bring the killer in a different shooting to justice.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The boy is 13 now, whip-thin and taller than he was two years ago, but after what happened then, not as quick. He opened the door of his family’s 14th-floor apartment in a Bronx project on Thursday morning and said no, he could not talk right now, because his parents were not home. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/30/nyregion/CRIMESCENE/CRIMESCENE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/30/nyregion/CRIMESCENE/CRIMESCENE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/30/nyregion/CRIMESCENE/CRIMESCENE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Courage to Testify, but No Desire to Elaborate', 'kicker': 'Crime 