t', 'value': 'Flags, Emblems and Insignia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-30T00:30:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Terry L. Jones', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Terry', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Jones', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae8f010a-e41e-597a-9978-ad8e1820bf08', 'word_count': 1489, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae8f010a-e41e-597a-9978-ad8e1820bf08'}, {'abstract': 'Black Swan Records, founded in the 1920s by a disciple of W. E. B. Du Bois, was the first major black-owned record company, starting the careers of performers like Ethel Waters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/31/nyregion/answers-to-questions-about-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'Black Swan Records, founded in the 1920s by a disciple of W. E. B. Du Bois, was the first major black-owned record company, starting the careers of performers like Ethel Waters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q. The liner notes for one of my albums mentions a Black Swan Records in New York. It sounds interesting. Could you tell me about the company?', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/31/nyregion/31FYI/31FYI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1009, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/31/nyregion/31FYI/31FYI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/31/nyregion/31FYI/31FYI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnail