o played a role.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jay H. Walder, chairman of the embattled Metropolitan Transportation Authority, traveled to Albany earlier this year seeking help for a transit system in peril. Mr. Walder, a kid from Queens who rose to the top of his field and harbored big ambitions for his state, was not unlike the man he had hoped to see: Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/30/nyregion/WALDER/WALDER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 722, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/30/nyregion/WALDER/WALDER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/30/nyregion/WALDER/WALDER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Governor Said to Have Irked Transit Leader Who Is Leaving', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cuomo Is Said To Have Irked Exiting Leader Of the M.T.A.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walder, Jay H', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Transportation Authority', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-30T00:52:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael M. Grynbaum and Christine Haughney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6a6ece0-0372-53d1-974d-1b7148ac465f', 'word_count': 1262, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6a6ece0-0372-53d1-974d-1b7148ac465f'}, {'abstract': 'Radio talk show host Jonathan Schwartz scans the computer for Red Sox news on Sunday mornings before heading to the studio at WNYC.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/31/nyregion/for-jonathan-schwartz-sundays-are-for-spinning-cds.html', 'snippet': 'Radio talk show host Jonathan Schwartz scans the computer for Red Sox news on Sunday mornings before heading to the studio at WNYC.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Sunday afternoons for the past four decades, Jonathan Schwartz has been spinning the wax and waxing poetic on all things Sinatra and American standard. Now 72, Mr. Schwartz can be heard every day of the week on Sirius Satellite Radio — Channel 71 — but weekends still find him at his longtime home on the FM dial, WNYC. He lives in Midtown Manhattan with the actress  Zohra Lampert, whom he married last year. Mr. Schwartz’s daughter, Casey, 28, and son, Adam, 24, often join them for dinner. ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/31/nyregion/31ROUTINE_SPAN/31ROUTINE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 352, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/31/nyregion/31ROUTINE_SPAN/31ROUTINE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 352}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/31/nyregion/31ROUTINE_SPAN/31ROUTINE_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy':