 None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b7b5c26-52f1-5be6-9563-1697b7089f16', 'word_count': 605, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b7b5c26-52f1-5be6-9563-1697b7089f16'}, {'abstract': 'There’s a surprising pleasure in the absence of a fence that has stood for more than a decade.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/30/opinion/mending-fences.html', 'snippet': 'There’s a surprising pleasure in the absence of a fence that has stood for more than a decade.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While the horses have been on vacation across the road in a neighbor’s pasture, my own pastures have grown into what looks like the first stage of abandonment. The grass is high, and so are the thistles and burdock. Here and there, sumac is trying to grow unnoticed. Several of the fences are down — intentionally — and in two of the pastures lie the trunks of dead sugar maples, cut into log lengths. They remind me of whale bones I once saw on an island off the coast of southern Chile.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mending Fences', 'kicker': 'Editorial | The Rural Life', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mending Fences', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fences', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-30T01:26:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Verlyn Klinkenborg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Verlyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Klinkenborg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/e60acefe-c13a-56de-8890-0ffaf7c294a5', 'word_count': 336, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e60acefe-c13a-56de-8890-0ffaf7c294a5'}, {'abstract': 'Since the end of the lockout, a high-stakes, almost drunken shopping spree is under way in an extraordinary talent bazaar.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/30/sports/football/off-season-reduced-to-days-nfl-runs-through-millions.html', 'snippet': 'Since the end of the lockout, a high-stakes, almost drunken shopping spree is under way in an extraordinary talent bazaar.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After more than four months of fighting over money, the National Football League has proved — in four of the most frenetic and expensive days in its history — that it did not forget how to spend it. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/30/sports/y-nfl-1/y-nfl-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 357, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/30/sports/y-nfl-1/y-nfl-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 357}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/30/sports/y-nfl-1/y-nfl-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 698, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/30/sports/y-nfl-1/y-nfl-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/30/sports/y-nfl-1/y-nfl-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Off-Season Reduced, N.F.L. Runs Through Millions', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Off-Season Reduced to Days, N.F.L. Runs Through Millions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Draft and Recruitment (Sports)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Free Agents (Sports)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lockouts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Asomugha, Nnamdi', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kolb, Kevin', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Haynesworth, Albert', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ochocinco, Chad', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-30T01:26:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judy Battista', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Battista', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/caf5cddd-1b53-569b-833a-cfeff779eeec', 'word_count': 1154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/caf5cddd-1b53-569b-833a-cfeff779eeec'}, {'abstract': 'The undefeated See You at Peelers won her division of Yonkers Raceway’s $233,230 New York Sire Stakes Rye Pace on Thursday, her 21st lifetime victory and eighth as a 3-year-old.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/30/sports/filly-remains-undefeated.html', 'snippet': 'The undefeated See You at Peelers won her division of Yonkers Raceway’s $233,230 New York Sire Stakes Rye Pace on Thursday, her 21st lifetime victory and eighth as a 3-year-old.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The undefeated See You at Peelers won her division of Yonkers Raceway’s $233,230 New York Sire Stakes Rye Pace on Thursday, her 21st lifetime victory and eighth as a 3-year-old. An easy two-and-a-half-length victor, she completed the mile in 1 minute 52.2 seconds, a track record for her 3-year-old filly weight class. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Filly Remains Undefeated', 'kicker': 'Sports Briefing | Harness Racing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Filly Remains Undefeated', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Harness Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yonkers Raceway', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-30T01:30:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Drape', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Drape', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ebfb9e0-43f8-5270-bb85-3d8527a19b43', 'word_count': 52, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ebfb9e0-43f8-5270-bb85-3d8527a19b43'}, {'abstract': 'Dr. Marburger maintained the respect of most colleagues even as many of them were harshly critical of the Bush White House.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/30/us/30marburger.html', 'snippet': 'Dr. Marburger maintained the respect of most colleagues even as many of them were harshly critical of the Bush White House.', 'lead_paragraph': 'John H. Marburger III, a physicist, former college president and Democrat who served as science adviser to President George W. Bush and was frequently called on to defend his policies on birth control, stem cell research and climate change, died Thursday at his home in Port Jefferson, Long Island. He was 70.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/30/us/MARBURGER-obit/MARBURGER-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/30/us/MARBU