s but offers a variety of rotating daily specials.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/31/nyregion/at-cod-almighty-chippery-fish-and-chips-and-more.html', 'snippet': 'Cod Almighty Chippery, a new fast-casual restaurant, specializes in fish and chips but offers a variety of rotating daily specials.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fish and chips are the headliner at Cod Almighty Chippery. But at this fast-casual restaurant, which opened last August in a strip mall in Westfield, there are also other catches: “po’ boy” sandwiches with fried clams ($8.25), fish tacos ($7) and steamed mussels ($7.95), to name a few. ', 'print_section': 'NJ', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From the Sea to Your Plate', 'kicker': 'Quick Bite | Westfield', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From the Sea to Your Plate', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-30T02:52:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kelly Feeney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kelly', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Feeney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/82f3bf08-9a77-5fea-b71e-57d46f196f21', 'word_count': 285, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82f3bf08-9a77-5fea-b71e-57d46f196f21'}, {'abstract': 'At Luchento’s, the drapes are heavy, the lighting low and the air chilly, and the portions are prehistorically large.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/31/nyregion/luchentos-ristorante-in-millstone-township-nj-review.html', 'snippet': 'At Luchento’s, the drapes are heavy, the lighting low and the air chilly, and the portions are prehistorically large.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE crowd of cars around Luchento’s Ristorante had long intrigued me, but it was a recent facade renovation that propelled me through the doors. Once there, I found a dining style evocative of scenes in vintage photographs or films.', 'print_section': 'NJ', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/31/nyregion/31DINENJ1/31DINENJ1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/31/nyregion/31DINENJ1/31DINENJ1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/31/nyregion/31DINENJ1/31DINENJ1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Local Italian Staple, Back to Its Family Roots', 'kicker': 'New Jersey Dining | Millstone Township', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Local Italian Staple, Back to Its Family Roots', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-30T02:53:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karla Cook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cook', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/67d1b235-c6b8-5cc3-8021-40047706548c', 'word_count': 825, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67d1b235-c6b8-5cc3-8021-40047706548c'}, {'abstract': 'Thousands of mourners attended the funeral of top rebel military commander, Gen. Abdul Fattah Younes, in Benghazi on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/07/29/world/africa/20110730_LIBYA.html', 'snippet': 'Thousands of mourners attended the funeral of top rebel military commander, Gen. Abdul Fattah Younes, in Benghazi on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thousands of mourners attended the funeral of top rebel military commander, Gen. Abdul Fattah Younes, in Benghazi on Friday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/29/world/africa/20110730_LIBYA-slide-2ONK/20110730_LIBYA-slide-2ONK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Battle for Libya | July 29, 2011', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-30T02:59:32+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'World', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/1b31e1e5-b069-5c3e-a096-858a45df6cb1', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/1b31e1e5-b069-5c3e-a096-858a45df6cb1'}, {'abstract': 'The president’s re-election struggle blends strains of the crises that his three predecessors faced.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/30/us/politics/30obama.html', 'snippet': 'The president’s re-election struggle blends strains of the crises that his three predecessors faced.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — It was a day that brought fresh evidence of all the forces converging on President Obama in the latter half of his term: a weakened economy he cannot lift, a deeply divided Congress he cannot move and, as a result, a level of political risk he seems hard-pressed to control.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/30/us/OBAMA/OBAMA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/30/us/OBAMA/OBAMA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/30/us/OBAMA/OBAMA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 688, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/30/us/OBAMA/OBAMA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/30/us/OBAMA/OBAMA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama’s Crucible Moment at Intersection of Politics and the Economy', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama’s Crucible Moment at Intersection of Politics and the Economy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-30T03:02:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Harwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/1946678a-d71f-56eb-9f80-068ee6c48df3', 'word_count': 977, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1946678a-d71f-56eb-9f80-068ee6c48df3'}, {'abstract': 'Officials denied that Charles Monnett, a wildlife biologist, was suspended because of possible misconduct involving his scientific reports on dead polar bears in the Beaufort Sea.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/30/science/earth/30brfs-BIOLOGISTSSU_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'Officials denied that Charles Monnett, a wildlife biologist, was suspended because of possible misconduct involving his scientific reports on dead polar bears in the Beaufort Sea.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A spokeswoman for the federal Bureau of Ocean Energy Management, Regulation and Enforcement issued a brief statement on Friday denying that Charles Monnett, a wildlife biologist and manager of scientific contracts, was suspended because of possible misconduct involving his scientific reports on dead polar bears in the Beaufort Sea. Melissa Schwartz, the bureau’s deputy chief of staff and communications director, wrote in an e-mail, “The agency placed Mr. Monnett on administrative leave for reasons having nothing to do with scientific integrity, his 2006 journal article or issues related to permitting,” a reference to the bureau’s role in permitting offshore drilling. “Any suggestions or speculation to the contrary are wrong,” Ms. Schwartz concluded. Dr. Monnett was told of the leave in an official letter on July 18, which referred to a continuing investigation by the department’s inspector general into “integrity issues.” A few days before his suspension, a long-running contract involving polar bear research by scientists at the University of Alberta was abruptly put on hold. It is not clear whether the action involving that contract is connected to Dr. Monnett’s suspension. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Biologist’s Suspension Is Not Related to Scientific Integrity, Bureau Official Says', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | SCIENCE', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Biologist’s Suspension Is Not Related To Scientific Integrity, Bureau Official Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Monnett, Charles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polar Bears', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bureau of Ocean Energy Management, Regulation and Enforcement', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-30T03:08:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicity Barringer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicity', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barringer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3061cdb-594f-5e87-9a43-5956606d5e87', 'word_count': 182, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3061cdb-594f-5e87-9a43-5956606d5e87'}, {'abstract': 'A federal judge in Washington has ordered the release of hundreds of pages of President Richard M. Nixon’s 1975 testimony about Watergate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/30/us/30brfs-JUDGEORDERSR_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'A federal judge in Washington has ordered the release of hundreds of pages of President Richard M. Nixon’s 1975 testimony about Watergate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A federal judge in Washington has ordered the release of hundreds of pages of President Richard M. Nixon’s 1975 testimony about Watergate. The judge, Royce C. Lamberth III of the Federal District Court for the District of Columbia, wrote in a decision issued Friday that “nearly 40 years later, Watergate continues to capture both scholarly and public interest.” The Obama administration objected to the release, citing the privacy of people mentioned in the testimony. But Judge Lamberth wrote that the “undisputed historical interest” in the testimony, among other factors, far outweighed “the need to maintain the secrecy of the records.” The transcripts will not be released right away; the government can appeal the decision. Stanley I. Kutler, a leading Watergate historian who filed suit to get the documents last year, said that Nixon’s grand jury testimony was “a rare opportunity to hear him — what should I say? — unplugged. There are no aides, there are no lawyers, there are no spin doctors.” With the possible penalty of perjury over his head, Professor Kutler said, “My guess is he told those people the truth.” A spokesman for the Department of Justice, Charles S. Miller, said the agency was reviewing the judge’s decision and had not determined its next step. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Judge Orders Release of Nixon’s Watergate Testimony', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | WASHINGTON', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Judge Orders Release of Nixon’s Watergate Testimony', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Watergate Affair', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nixon, Richard Milhous', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-30T03:11:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Schwartz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwartz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/782f2784-f18e-50f2-b5e0-4a711c007afa', 'word_count': 211, 'uri': 'nyt://article/782f2784-f18e-50f2-b5e0-4a711c007afa'}, {'abstract': 'Phillies general manager Ruben Amaro makes a significant trade — again. With the Houston Astros — again.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/29/ruthless-and-relentless-phillies-amaro-strikes-again/', 'snippet': 'Phillies general manager Ruben Amaro makes a significant trade — again. With the Houston Astros — again.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Which adjective best describes Ruben Amaro, the general manager of the Philadelphia Phillies. Ruthless? Relentless? Both work pretty well. Amaro made another significant trade on Friday, acquiring the two-time All-Star outfielder Hunter Pence from the Houston Astros for three minor leaguers and a player to be named later.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ruthless and Relentless, Phillies’ Amaro Strikes Again', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pence, Hunter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Houston Astros', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Philadelphia Phillies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Houston (Tex)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philadelphia (Pa)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-30T03:13:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/141db5b0-73bf-55d3-bc8d-5e4f1ed32a7a', 'word_count': 441, 'uri': 'nyt://article/141db5b0-73bf-55d3-bc8d-5e4f1ed32a7a'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print