 problems we don’t have, worsening the ones we do.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just worth reminding everyone: We have a deeply depressed economy — more deeply than we realized, according to the GDP revisions — which is clearly suffering from a lack of demand. Meanwhile, the government is able to borrow at very low interest rates:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Warped Discourse, Again', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-30T13:42:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d751f57b-7120-5cb8-b00a-49b5e4644d3c', 'word_count': 70, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d751f57b-7120-5cb8-b00a-49b5e4644d3c'}, {'abstract': 'Greenspan, still doing damage.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/30/the-malevolent-ex-maestro/', 'snippet': 'Greenspan, still doing damage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After playing a key role in creating the greatest economic disaster in three generations, you might have expected Alan Greenspan to lie low. But no, he’s out there issuing opinions, which for some reason still get listened to. Worse: he keeps calling for a return to the very regime he favored before, the regime that led to disaster.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Malevolent Ex-Maestro', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-07-30T14:05:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a5f8931-983a-53b3-9515-4d72125eaed4', 'word_count': 296, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a5f8931-983a-53b3-9515-4d72125eaed4'}, {'abstract': 'In a season twice interrupted by stints on the disabled list, Jim Thome creaks along in his pursuit of his 600th home run.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/31/sports/baseball/thome-battles-age-in-pursuit-of-no-600.html', 'snippet': 'In a season twice interrupted by stints on the disabled list, Jim Thome creaks along in his pursuit of his 600th home run.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MINNEAPOLIS — Jim Thome’s two lockers at Target Field contain the usual trappings of a veteran player: workout T-shirts of various designs, multiple pairs of cleats and assorted knick-knacks. But the one visible concession to Thome’s age — he turns 41 on Aug. 27 — was the hand-held muscle stimulator, about the size of a hair dryer, plugged in and ready for use.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/31/sports/dog-thome/dog-thome-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/31/sports/dog-thome/dog-thome-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/31/sports/dog-thome/dog-thome-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 739, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/31/sports/dog-thome/dog-thome-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/31/sports/dog-thome/dog-thome-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Thome’s Pursuit of 600 Interrupted by Aches', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pursuit of 600 Interrupted by Aches', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thome, Jim', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Minnesota Twins', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-30T14:11:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pat Borzi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pat', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borzi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1527ed8b-6089-5509-a6c0-86ee21bbe74c', 'word_count': 1092, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1527ed8b-6089-5509-a6c0-86ee21bbe74c'}, {'abstract': 'The most important thing to know about baseball trades made in July is that most of them do not amount to much.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/31/sports/baseball/mlb-trade-deadline-can-be-great-deal-of-trouble.html', 'snippet': 'The most important thing to know about baseball trades made in July is that most of them do not amount to much.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The most important thing to know about baseball trades made in July is that most of them do not amount to much. Few of the stars traded to contenders will be the difference between winning and losing, and few of the young prospects traded for stars will become stars. Still, we have had a flurry of activity leading to Sunday’s deadline for nonwaiver trades (don’t ask), with stars like Carlos Beltran and numerous lesser lights changing teams and kindling hope 