humbnail': 'images/2011/07/31/us/31cnckotlowitz/31cnckotlowitz-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Writer Gets New Vision From Film', 'kicker': 'Chicago News Cooperative', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Writer Gets New Vision From Film', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kotlowitz, Alex', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, Steve (1954- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-30T20:19:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jessica Reaves', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jessica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reaves', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/418ec5f9-bc50-5728-ad69-2aff2670a295', 'word_count': 518, 'uri': 'nyt://article/418ec5f9-bc50-5728-ad69-2aff2670a295'}, {'abstract': 'Osi Umenyiora, a Pro Bowl defensive end who is seeking a trade or a new contract that he claims General Manager Jerry Reese promised him, ended his holdout on Saturday.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/30/giants-back-at-camp-again-minus-umenyiora/', 'snippet': 'Osi Umenyiora, a Pro Bowl defensive end who is seeking a trade or a new contract that he claims General Manager Jerry Reese promised him, ended his holdout on Saturday.', 'lead_paragraph': '6:54 p.m. | Updated EAST RUTHERFORD, N.J. — The Giants had their first walkthrough of training camp Saturday morning and Osi Umenyiora, as expected, was nowhere to be found at the Timex Performance Center. Umenyiora, unhappy with his contract, seemingly decided to hold out for a second day and pay the consequences — $30,000 worth.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Umenyiora Ends Holdout and Reports to Giants Camp', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Umenyiora, Osi', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-30T20:19:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By JORGE CASTILLO', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jorge', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'CASTILLO', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e89d73e-5630-50e4-9859-ebd5840d7970', 'word_count': 387, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e89d73e-5630-50e4-9859-ebd5840d7970'}, {'abstract': 'The members of Kids These Days, a very young band, may not fit into a genre, but they definitely have a sound and, maybe more important, a business plan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/31/us/31cnckids.html', 'snippet': 'The members of Kids These Days, a very young band, may not fit into a genre, but they definitely have a sound and, maybe more important, a business plan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Vic Mensa was so determined to get into Lollapalooza last year that he tried jumping a fence near some downtown train tracks, brushed against an electrical transformer powering the trains, fell 25 feet to the ground and wound up in the hospital. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23B', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/31/us/31cnc-kids/31cnc-kids-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 3