ng number of abandoned pets, especially the old and the sick.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/31/us/31bcshelter.html', 'snippet': 'As difficult economic times continue, East Bay animal shelters are receiving a growing number of abandoned pets, especially the old and the sick.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Pit Bull puppy with Parvovirus and a Shih Tzu that had been hit by a car are just two examples of pets that have been abandoned by their owners at East Bay animal shelters in recent months. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/31/us/31shelter/31shelter-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/31/us/31shelter/31shelter-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/31/us/31shelter/31shelter-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 655, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/31/us/31shelter/31shelter-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/31/us/31shelter/31shelter-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Owners Abandoning Ill and Aging Pets in Hard Times', 'kicker': 'The Bay Citizen', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Owners Abandoning Ill and Aging Pets in Hard Times', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco Bay Area (Calif)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-30T21:01:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jamie Hansen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jamie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hansen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3804bf54-3594-50b5-bb82-43371d1b3678', 'word_count': 516, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3804bf54-3594-50b5-bb82-43371d1b3678'}, {'abstract': 'At a time when tax policy is atop the national political agenda, some are looking anew at proposals of the 19th-century political economist Henry George.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/31/us/31bcstevens.html', 'snippet': 'At a time when tax policy is atop the national political agenda, some are looking anew at proposals of the 19th-century political economist Henry George.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Elizabeth Lesly Stevens writes a column for The Bay Citizen.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Tax Policy With San Francisco Roots', 'kicker': 'The Bay Citizen', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Tax Policy With San Francisco Roots', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'George, Henry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-30T21:02:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth Lesly Stevens', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': 'Lesly', 'lastname': 'Stevens', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a3f9ba7-805f-5f2e-b543-526b2cb72f4f', 'word_count': 738, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a3f9ba7-805f-5f2e-b543-526b2cb72f4f'}, {'abstract': 'The bomb attack occurred in an impoverished part of eastern Afghanistan that had been relatively quiet until recently.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/31/world/asia/31afghanistan.html', 'snippet': 'The bomb attack occurred in an impoverished part of eastern Afghanistan that had been relatively quiet until recently.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — A bomb attack on a patrol killed two NATO soldiers and five Afghan soldiers on Friday evening, in an impoverished area of eastern Afghanistan where the Afghan government has little presence and where there have not previously been many lethal attacks on soldiers. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Attack on a Patrol in Afghanistan Kills Seven', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Deadly Attack on a Patrol in Afghanistan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'North Atlantic Treaty Organization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-30T21:08:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sharifullah Sahak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sharifullah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sahak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef0be052-c1da-53ae-9e73-1794e0eb64e0', 'word_count': 328, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef0be052-c1da-53ae-9e73-1794e0eb64e0'}, {'abstract': 'Peyton Manning’s new contract, for five years and $90 million, will pay him an average of $18 million per year, the same as Patriots quarterback Tom Brady.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/31/sports/football/manning-agrees-to-90-million-contract-with-colts.html', 'snippet': 'Peyton Manning’s new contract, for five years and $90 million, will pay him an average of $18 million per year, the same as Patriots quarterback Tom Brady.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In one of the oddest negotiations in the N.F.L.’s current free-agency frenzy, Indianapolis Colts quarterback Peyton Manning agreed to a contract Saturday that will not give him the highest annual salary in the game — even though his team owner vowed more than a year ago to give him a deal that would make him the highest paid player in N.F.L. history. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Manning’s $90 Million Deal Gives the Colts Flexibility', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Manning’s $90 Million Deal Gives the Colts Flexibility', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manning, Peyton', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indianapolis Colts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-30T21:16:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judy Battista', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Battista', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4888944-c1a9-51d6-aa85-129bee49f5f5', 'word_count': 603, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4888944-c1a9-51d6-aa85-129bee49f5f5'}, {'abstract': 'If Gov. Rick Perry decides to seek the presidency, he will be relying heavily on an inner circle of confidants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/31/us/31ttperryweb.html', 'snippet': 'If Gov. Rick Perry decides to seek the presidency, he will be relying heavily on an inner circle of confidants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Rick Perry’s inner circle has evolved significantly since he was first elected to the Texas House in 1984. He changed parties, for one thing, becoming a Republican and shucking one political infrastructure for another. And he changed offices, moving from the House to the Texas Department of Agriculture, from there to the lieutenant governorship and from there, with the election of George W. Bush to the presidency in 2000, into the office he holds today. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/31/us/31ttperryweb-span/31ttperryweb-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/31/us/31ttperryweb-span/31ttperryweb-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/31/us/31ttperryweb-span/31ttperryweb-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/31/us/31ttperryweb-span/31ttperryweb-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/31/us/31ttperryweb-span/31ttperryweb-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Perry’s Legion: The Folks Behind the Man', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Perry’s Legion: The Folks Behind, Beside and Around the Man', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-30T21:17:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Ramsey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ramsey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/66aa2f1a-3492-5200-94c9-a0c56f66a213', 'word_count': 1069, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66aa2f1a-3492-5200-94c9-a0c56f66a213'}, {'abstract': 'The American Wind Power Center in Lubbock bills itself as the world’s largest windmill museum, fittingly because Texas is the nation’s leader in supplying wind-generated power.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/31/us/31ttwindmill.html', 'snippet': 'The American Wind Power Center in Lubbock bills itself as the world’s largest windmill museum, fittingly because Texas is the nation’s leader in supplying wind-generated power.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LUBBOCK — A century ago, Texas was covered with windmills, which pumped water from aquifers so cattle could drink and gardens could grow. Thousands of these old-style models still exist in remote pastures, but in recent years far taller and more powerful turbines have sprouted atop western mesas, transforming this oil and gas state into the national leader in wind-generated electrical power.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23B', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/31/us/31tt-windmill/31tt-windmill-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/31/us/31tt-windmill/31tt-windmill-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/31/us/31tt-windmill/31tt-windmill-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 701, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/31/us/31tt-windmill/31tt-windmill-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/31/us/31tt-windmill/31tt-windmill-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Museum Shows History and Power of Wind Energy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Museum Shows History and Power of Wind Energy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Windmills', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wind Power', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-30T21:19:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Galbraith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Galbraith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3929c1