wn some cash, hotels are one option, and there are a few cheaper ones offered by the city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'During the Roman summer, oppressive heat waves are common, leaving captive tourists to bake in museum halls lacking air conditioning or roast on cobblestone streets. Few hotels in town offer swimming pools — and those that do charge a premium to nonguests who wish to take a dip. But if you are willing to plunk down some cash, there are options, as well as a few cheaper ones offered by the city. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cooling Dips for the Roman Summer', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'HOTELS AND MOTELS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Swimming Pools', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rome (Italy)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-31T10:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katie Parla', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parla', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1521ec32-fc3a-53c0-90d8-ca9f3d5c8268', 'word_count': 263, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1521ec32-fc3a-53c0-90d8-ca9f3d5c8268'}, {'abstract': 'Money for nothing and your jobs from free — but we say no.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/31/when-people-pay-you-to-take-their-money/', 'snippet': 'Money for nothing and your jobs from free — but we say no.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Look at the rates on inflation-protected US bonds:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When People Pay You To Take Their Money', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo