 members who care for him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the journalist David Whitehouse began circulating the first few chapters of his debut novel, “Bed,” he soon found himself picked up as a London client of the William Morris Agency. He was amazed at this good fortune. “Suddenly, I was walking around like Charlie Big Potatoes, thinking all sorts of good things were going to happen to me,” he has told interviewers. “But what actually did happen was, well, nothing.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/01/arts/BOOK/BOOK-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 636, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/01/arts/BOOK/BOOK-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/08/01/arts/BOOK/BOOK-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Very Big Man and the Brother Who Resents Him', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Very Big Man and the Brother Who Resents Him', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-31T21:15:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Janet Maslin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Janet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Maslin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/78721ad2-e1f6-5177-9985-1e908a2075c5', 'word_count': 979, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78721ad2-e1f6-5177-9985-1e908a2075c5'}, {'abstract': 'A spokesman for Senator Harry Reid said the Senate majority leader has “signed off on the debt-ceiling agreement pending caucus approval,” but Pentagon funding was a potential snag', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/31/reid-hopes-for-sunday-night-debt-vote/', 'snippet': 'A spokesman for Senator Harry Reid said the Senate majority leader has “signed off on the debt-ceiling agreement pending caucus approval,” but Pentagon funding was a potential snag', 'lead_paragraph': '5:29 p.m. | Updated A spokesman for Senator Harry Reid said the Senate majority leader has “signed off on the debt-ceiling agreement pending caucus approval.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reid Backs Debt Deal and Hopes for Sunday Night Debt Vote', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reid, Harry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-31T21:19:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/607c3354-0412-5a47-9069-17df23ca2b91', 'word_count': 348, 'uri': 'nyt://article/607c3354-0412-5a47-9069-17df23ca2b91'}, {'abstract': 'Poul Ruders’s adaptation of “Dancer in the Dark,” the 2000 Lars von Trier film musical, fails to persuade you to consider it on its own terms.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/08/01/arts/music/poul-ruderss-selma-jezkova-at-lincoln-center-review.html', 'snippet': 'Poul Ruders’s adaptation of “Dancer in the Dark,” the 2000 Lars von Trier film musical, fails to persuade you to consider it on its own terms.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If Sarah Bernhardt’s definitive performance in Victorien Sardou’s 1887 play “La Tosca” had been available through Netflix, would Puccini ever have based an opera on it? Would his “Tosca” have stood a chance?', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/01/arts/SELMA/SELMA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 779, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/01/arts/SELMA/SELMA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/08/01/arts/SELMA/SELMA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A von Trier Tragedy, Recast as Opera', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A von Trier Tragedy, Recast as Opera', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lincoln Center Festival', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'von Trier, Lars', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ruders, Poul', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-31T21:41:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zachary Woolfe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zachary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Woolfe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b22e341f-512a-5a49-8d19-e973700d9fa6', 'word_count': 755, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b22e341f-512a-5a49-8d19-e973700d9fa6'}, {'abstract': '“The Harvest/La Cosecha,” a documentary by U. Roberto Romano, tracks three child migrant farmworkers and the grinding cycle of their seasons.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/08/01/movies/the-harvestla-cosecha-review.html', 'snippet': '“The Harvest/La Cosecha,” a documentary by U. Roberto Romano, tracks three child migrant farmworkers and the grinding cycle of their seasons.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The Harvest/La Cosecha,” an earnest documentary about child migrant farmworkers in the United States, has a muckraking agenda but a melancholy soul. As it follows a 16-year-old boy and two girls, 12 and 14, through one harvest cycle, it depicts their lives as a more or less voluntary indentured servitude and provides a detailed, sometimes heartbreaking, mostly hopeless portrait of a permanent American underclass. But the tone is never angry; resignation is the primary note, and an ability to endure that isn’t so much resilience as stubbornness.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/01/arts/SUBHARVEST/SUBHARVEST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 640, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/01/arts/SUBHARVEST/SUBHARVEST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/08/01/arts/SUBHARVEST/SUBHARVEST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Children in the Fields, but Not at Play', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'The Harvest' ", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Children in the Fields, but Not at Play', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Migrant and Foreign Workers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-31T21:45:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Hale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/eede08e6-9134-5c6f-b6ed-23516ea5f771', 'word_count': 330, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eede08e6-9134-5c6f-b6ed-23516ea5f771'}, {'abstract': 'An eight-hour battle overnight and Sunday morning raised fresh questions about divisions, distrust and deception.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/08/01/world/africa/01libya.html', 'snippet': 'An eight-hour battle overnight and Sunday morning raised fresh questions about divisions, distrust and deception.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BENGHAZI, Libya — Rebel fighters challenging the rule of Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi waged an eight-hour gunfight here in their de facto capital on Sunday, against what their leaders called a “fifth column” of Qaddafi loyalists who had posed as a rebel brigade. It was the latest sign of discord and trickery in the rebel ranks to emerge in the four days since the killing of the rebels’ top military leader, Gen. Abdul Fattah Younes, a former Qaddafi confidant who had defected to their side. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/01/world/africa/LIBYA/LIBYA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'art