eb_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/08/01/arts/music/voigt-lessons-deborah-voigt-at-glimmerglass-review.html', 'snippet': 'Deborah Voigt spoke of her relationships, her alcoholism and her battles with weight in a one-woman concert at the Glimmerglass Festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'COOPERSTOWN, N.Y. — Opera singers have written their share of celebrity tell-all memoirs. The soprano Deborah Voigt recently sold her autobiography to HarperCollins, scheduled for release in two years. She has already gone public about her struggles with obesity, which led her to undergo gastric bypass surgery in 2004.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/01/arts/DEBORAH/DEBORAH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/08/01/arts/DEBORAH/DEBORAH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/01/arts/DEBORAH/DEBORAH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 747, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Diva’s Struggles and Songs, Shared With Candor', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Diva’s Struggles and Songs, Shared With Candor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Voigt, Deborah', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-31T21:55:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Tommasini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tommasini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/921b16c7-c6dc-5f87-9683-49fc23d6e65d', 'word_count': 994, 'uri': 'nyt://article/921b16c7-c6dc-5f87-9683-49fc23d6e65d'}, {'abstract': 'A concert focused on Biber in the 4x4 Baroque Music Festival featured the violinist Robert Mealy and the harpsichordist Avi Stein at St. Peter’s Lutheran Church on Saturday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/08/01/arts/music/4x4-baroque-music-festival-review.html', 'snippet': 'A concert focused on Biber in the 4x4 Baroque Music Festival featured the violinist Robert Mealy and the harpsichordist Avi Stein at St. Peter’s Lutheran Church on Saturday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 4x4 Baroque Music Festival began as an early-music fan’s farewell to the summer, with four free concerts offered around Labor Day. This year the festival’s players — a core of early-music stars, including the harpsichordist Avi Stein and the violinist Robert Mealy — have moved it to midsummer: the series began on Friday evening and runs through Wednesday at St. Peter’s Lutheran Church. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/01/arts/BAROQUE/BAROQUE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Exploring the Intricacies of the 17th Century', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Exploring the Intricacies of the 17th Century', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stein, Avi', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-31T21:56:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/37b13fe7-1bf7-5ba7-9f9a-bf00e0309358', 'word_count': 436, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37b13fe7-1bf7-5ba7-9f9a-bf00e0309358'}, {'abstract': 'In which we manage to make some headway in a puzzle by Joel Fagliano.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/07/31/mental/', 'snippet': 'In which we manage to make some headway in a puzzle by Joel Fagliano.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Administrivial Tournament “Save the Date” Alert! Will Shortz has announced the date of the 2011 Westchester Crossword Puzzle Tournament, the proceeds of which benefit the Pleasantville Fund for Learning. Save Oct. 21 (exact starting time to be determined) if you will be in the area and would like to have a fun, low-key tournament experience, meet some of your favorite constructors and help raise money for a great cause. Plus, if history holds, the desserts provided are not to be believed. The location will be Will’s brand-new table tennis club — the Westchester Table Tennis Center, located at 175 Tompkins Ave., in Pleasantville, N.Y. It’s three and a half blocks from the Pleasantville train station on MetroNorth. I’m told that the space is twice as large as the former location, which should nicely accommodate the growing legions of tournament fans, and you can even arrive early and play some table tennis! You can read more about the club here, and registration for the tournament is accepted at the door.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Monday: Whacked-Out Mental State', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-31T22:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b60537c-3d4d-5cc2-9ab8-6c22f48d9008', 'word_count': 497, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b60537c-3d4d-5cc2-9ab8-6c22f48d9008'}, {'abstract': 'A new ad campaign for the New York International Latino Film Festival makes fun of stereotypes to attract attendees while drawing attention to the problem.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/08/01/business/media/ad-campaign-pokes-fun-at-latino-stereotypes.html', 'snippet': 'A new ad campaign for the New York International Latino Film Festival makes fun of stereotypes to attract attendees while drawing attention to the problem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOR some Hollywood movies, clichés are everything. An asteroid destroys a major city. A shadowy figure appears behind someone in the reflection of medicine cabinet mirror. A Latina maid marries a successful businessman and lives happily ever after. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/01/business/sub-ADCO/sub-ADCO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 835, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/01/business/sub-ADCO/sub-ADCO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/08/01/business/sub-ADCO/sub-ADCO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Flaunting Latino Clichés in Effort to Defuse Them', 'kicker': 'Advertising', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Flaunting Latino Clichés in Effort to Defuse Them', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York International Latino Film Festival', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-31T22:02:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tanzina Vega', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tanzina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vega', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5af9f864-1a69-58b9-8617-9f60f9a4dd37', 'word_count': 793, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5af9f864-1a69-58b9-8617-9f60f9a4dd37'}, {'abstract': 'The Cro-Mags and Screaming Females were among the performers in the latest free show at the House of Vans skate park.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/08/01/arts/music/cro-mags-and-screaming-females-at-house-of-vans-review.html', 'snippet': 'The Cro-Mags and Screaming Females were among the performers in the latest free show at the House of Vans skate park.', 'lead_paragraph': 'People straighten up around John Joseph, the singer for the Cro-Mags. He reminds you that the best of his music, New York hardcore, has a history and a set of standards, musical and ethical; he has no time for what people choose to do outside of those standards. He’s not hectoring you, exactly, about punk and veganism and the economy and your ability to rise to the occasion; he’s making strong recommendations and asking withering questions. Like “What are you, tired?” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/01/arts/MAGS/MAGS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/08/01/arts/MAGS/MAGS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/01/arts/MAGS/MAGS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 663, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/01/arts/MAGS/MAGS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/08/01/arts/MAGS/MAGS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Muscling Through a Murky, Hardcore Night in a Box', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Muscling Through a Murky, Hardcore Night in a Box', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Screaming Females', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-31T22:03:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Ratliff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ratliff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c8caf9a-f629-5285-bef9-4a2cb2b1a319', 'word_count': 825, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c8caf9a-f629-5285-bef9-4a2cb2b1a319'}, {'abstract': 'The pianist Marc-André Hamelin took on a daunting program of Berg, Stockhausen, Ravel and Liszt at the International Keyboard Institute and Festival on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/08/01/arts/music/marc-andre-hamelin-at-international-keyboard-festival-review.html', 'snippet': 'The pianist Marc-André Hamelin took on a daunting program of Berg, Stockhausen, Ravel and Liszt at the International Keyboard Institute and Festival on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The pianist Marc-André Hamelin is fearless. No successful performer can afford to show fear from the stage, but with Mr. Hamelin, fearlessness is something more: a positive attribute, a confident calm that he exudes even while unleashing volcanic eruptions of sound and emotion.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/01/arts/MARC/MARC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 803, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Romantic Temperament Applied to Monuments', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Romantic Temperament Applied to Monuments', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hamelin, Marc-Andre', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-31T22:03:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By James R. Oestreich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Oestreich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5266643e-bd86-5c95-896c-15785da3eeb1', 'word_count': 433, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5266643e-bd86-5c95-896c-15785da3eeb1'}, {'abstract': 'Oumou Sangare commanded the stage at the Celebrate Brooklyn! festival on Friday night, delivering her praise and admonitions with a modern kick.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/08/01/arts/music/oumou-sangare-at-celebrate-brooklyn-review.html', 'snippet': 'Oumou Sangare commanded the stage at the Celebrate Brooklyn! festival on Friday night, delivering her praise and admonitions with a modern kick.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Regal, righteous and funky, the Malian singer and songwriter Oumou Sangare commanded the stage of Celebrate Brooklyn! on Friday night at the Prospect Park Bandshell. Wearing a white caftan, a red necklace and a white headscarf that her movements kept shaking loose, Ms. Sangare praised and admonished: End forced child marriage, share good fortune, seek wisdom, don’t waste your youth. She was taking on the traditional West African singer’s role as community conscience while delivering her messages with a modern kick.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/01/arts/SANGARE/SANGARE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 732, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/01/arts/SANGARE/SANGARE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/08/01/arts/SANGARE/SANGARE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Malian Singer Sets Her West African Message to a Dance Beat', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Malian Singer Sets Her West African Message to a Dance Beat', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sangare, Oumou', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-31T22:06:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/79fc93a4-5495-5888-b83f-c13c0fa8d370', 'word_count': 563, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79fc93a4-5495-5888-b83f-c13c0fa8d370'}, {'abstract': 'In a financial market not usually known for excitement, stability has been replaced with concern, reflected in falling prices for short-term offerings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/08/01/business/uncertainty-driving-treasury-bill-fluctuations.html', 'snippet': 'In a financial market not usually known for excitement, stability has been replaced with concern, reflected in falling prices for short-term offerings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In normal times, it is hard to find a financial market that is more boring than the one where short-term Treasury bills are traded. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Uncertainty Driving Treasury Bill Fluctuations', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Uncertainty Driving Treasury Bill Fluctuations', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Treasury Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-31T22:13:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Floyd Norris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Norris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/38cc1277-7977-50c6-b364-984d179eb2ae', 'word_count': 640, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38cc1277-7977-50c6-b364-984d179eb2ae'}, {'abstract': 'At Lincoln Center on Saturday afternoon “She’s Got the Power!” presented a four-hour marathon of girl-group songs from the 1960s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/08/01/arts/music/shes-got-the-power-at-lincoln-center-review.html', 'snippet': 'At Lincoln Center on Saturday afternoon “She’s Got the Power!” presented a four-hour marathon of girl-group songs from the 1960s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was all about love. Waiting for it, finding it, showing it, fearing for it, fighting for it, sometimes losing it, sometimes taking it all the way to happy-ever-after marriage. On Saturday afternoon the rock archivists of the Ponderosa Stomp and Lincoln Center Out of Doors presented a fond four-hour marathon of girl-group songs from the early 1960s, sung by the women who made them. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/01/arts/STOMP/STOMP-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/08/01/arts/STOMP/STOMP-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/01/arts/STOMP/STOMP-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 654, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/01/arts/STOMP/STOMP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/08/01/arts/STOMP/STOMP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Girl-Group Hits From Rock’s Women', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Girl-Group Hits From Rock’s Women', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lincoln Center Out of Doors Festival', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ponderosa Stomp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spector, Ronnie', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gore, Lesley', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-31T22:13:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea0ba398-7e4b-57a9-9bb4-cf0abed9f402', 'word_count': 680, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea0ba398-7e4b-57a9-9bb4-cf0abed9f402'}, {'abstract': 'Eiko & Koma’s performance piece “Water” made use of that element at the Lincoln Center Out of Doors festival.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/08/01/arts/dance/eiko-koma-at-lincoln-center-out-of-doors-review.html', 'snippet': 'Eiko & Koma’s performance piece “Water” made use of that element at the Lincoln Center Out of Doors festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Forty years after they began to collaborate, the performance duo Eiko & Koma remain among New York’s greatest and most extraordinary performers. Their particular secret is that, while moving with extreme slowness, they are masters of suspense. Watching, you’re kept on tenterhooks: what will happen next? ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'Th