mily back story for Captain Ahab.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some people argue passionately over which is the Great American Novel, “Moby-Dick” or “The Adventures of Huckleberry Finn.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/01/arts/MOBY1/MOBY1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 791, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ahab Has a Wife and a Heart. Oh, and a Whale.', 'kicker': 'Television Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ahab Has a Wife and a Heart. Oh, and a Whale.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANDERSON, GILLIAN', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Melville, Herman', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hurt, William', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hawke, Ethan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sutherland, Donald', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-07-31T22:18:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alessandra Stanley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alessandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stanley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/2bea697b-1882-572f-beb8-a84d8811f5b0', 'word_count': 1113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2bea697b-1882-572f-beb8-a84d8811f5b0'}, {'abstract': '“Magic Trip: Ken Kesey’s Search for a Kool Place,” a film by Alex Gibney and Alison Ellwood, reconstructs footage of Kesey’s 1964 cross-country bus trip.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/08/01/movies/magic-trip-reconstructs-footage-from-ken-keseys-bus-trip.html', 'snippet': '“Magic Trip: Ken Kesey’s Search for a Kool Place,” a film by Alex Gibney and Alison Ellwood, reconstructs footage of Kesey’s 1964 cross-country bus trip.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Magic Trip: Ken Kesey’s Search for a Kool Place,” a film by Alex Gibney and Alison Ellwood that opens on Friday, is an exercise in what they call “archival vérité.” It’s a documentary that uses old footage to recreate a documentary that Kesey intended to make about his 1964 cross-country bus trip — the one so memorably chronicled in Tom Wolfe’s account, “The Electric Kool-Aid Acid Test.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/01/arts/MAGIC1/MAGIC1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 739, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/01/arts/MAGIC1/MAGIC1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/08/01/arts/MAGIC1/MAGIC1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Film Hitches a Weird Ride on Kesey’s Bus', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Film Hitches A Weird Ride On Kesey’s Bus', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kesey, Ken', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'LSD (Lysergic Acid Diethylamide)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nineteen Hundred Sixties', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gibney, Alex', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cassady, Neal', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_dat